window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_YOU_PROMISED_TO_BE_AN_IDLE_SON_IN_LAW_HOW_COULD_YOU_BECOME_A_LAND_IMMORTAL_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101 - 102: Why is Shu State a Little Chilly in June?","paragraphs":["The very next morning, Xiao Wan’er finalized the partnership with Hundred Herbs Hall.","Wang Ji was relieved when he heard the news. He personally brought the contract over, accompanied by the vice president of the Medicine Hall Guild, Liu Liming.","Liu Liming, of course, did not dare to be negligent. He and several guild members reviewed the contract’s contents, one by one.","Once all matters were settled, both parties affixed their seals and signed their names.","Only then was the matter finally settled.","Naturally, Xiao Wan’er didn’t see them far, merely having the Armored Warriors in the mansion escort them out.","Wang Ji took his leave respectfully, but his eyes drifted toward the nearby Spring Lotus Garden. He could faintly hear Chen Yi’s cheerful voice from within, and couldn’t help but feel a surge of emotion.","’If the young miss knew what the master did behind the scenes, I wonder how she would react.’","The contract established between Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall this time was not as simple as just buying medicinal ingredients based on prescriptions.","It also included a new clause: the Xiao Family Medicine Hall would act as a vendor for five types of tea drinks produced by Hundred Herbs Hall.","Specifically, Wangji Tea, Divine Bull Tea, Old Platinum Tea, Mushroom Tea, and Beauty Tea.","Furthermore, Chen Yi had given special instructions that because Hundred Herbs Hall was newly selling these tea drinks, fifty percent of the profits would be shared with the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","One must remember that under the original agreement, Hundred Herbs Hall was only supposed to share ten percent of the profits.","From this, it wasn’t hard for Wang Ji to see Chen Yi’s attitude toward the Xiao Family. He was being incredibly considerate.","But that wasn’t all.","What was more important were the prescriptions the master had provided.","Those were prescriptions written by a Medical Master from a previous dynasty!","Forget a thick volume containing a total of thirty-two prescriptions; even a single one would be enough to sustain a Medicine Hall.","That alone showed how precious they were.","Yet the master had given them to the Xiao Family without batting an eye, even sending along those few Quack Doctors who had received his guidance...","It made Wang Ji, who had witnessed it all, ache with regret.","But Chen Yi didn’t see it that way.","’Never mind that those prescriptions weren’t written by some so-called Medical Master from a past dynasty, but were just some of my own research. Even if they were real, so what?’","’How could a few external possessions compare to the peace and harmony of the Xiao Mansion?’","Just after the contract was signed, Xiao Wan’er came to the Spring Lotus Garden. A pink cloak enveloped her body, making her delicate, beautiful face appear even more stunning.","Hearing her approach, Chen Yi looked up from the game board. Seeing the joyful expression on her face, he already knew the outcome and said with a smile:","\"The magpies have been chirping on the eaves all morning. I just knew something good was going to happen in the mansion today.\"","Xiao Wan’er walked over gracefully and sat down at the stone table, her face still holding a relaxed smile.","\"You guessed right. I just finalized the contract with Wang Ji.\"","\"Now, our Medicine Halls not only have renowned doctors presiding over them and prescriptions to support them, but we also have a supply of ingredients from Hundred Herbs Hall. You could say we killed three birds with one stone.\"","Chen Yi blinked. \"Three birds?\"","His reminder made Xiao Wan’er think of something. She quickly waved Shen Huatang and Cui’er over. \"And there’s one more.\"","\"The tea drinks that Hundred Herbs Hall used to give away as gifts are now going to be sold.\"","\"Wang Ji sent some over. The taste is said to be quite good. I brought a few, so everyone, have a try.\"","Chen Yi had already noticed the tea drinks Shen Huatang was carrying. He didn’t refuse, signaling for Xiaodie to take them.","They each got a bottle of Wangji Tea.","Xiao Wuge, however, curiously opened a bottle of Mushroom Tea. He took a sip, and his little face immediately scrunched up. \"Sour! Sour! So sour!\"","\"Is it sour?\"","Xiao Wan’er had Shen Huatang open a bottle for her. She took a small sip, and a faint smile appeared on her face. \"It’s delicious.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi looked at her, and strands of crystalline light reflected in the depths of his pupils.","He saw a faint blue aura emanating from around Xiao Wan’er’s body, with faint traces of black mixed within.","That black aura was as dark as ink.","Chen Yi frowned to himself and said, \"This tea is a bit cold and chilling. It would be good for relieving summer heat.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded with a smile and was about to take another sip when Shen Huatang stepped forward. \"Miss, let me have a taste.\"","Before she could respond, Shen Huatang had already taken the bottle of Mushroom Tea from her hand, drained it in one go, and wiped her mouth. \"The taste... is indeed pretty good.\"","\"...\"","Xiao Wan’er was stunned for a moment, then understood her attendant’s intention and sighed softly with a hint of regret.","A brief silence fell.","Xiao Wan’er changed the subject. \"I wonder where Wang Ji found the recipe. Judging by the taste, this tea should sell well.\"","Chen Yi’s eyes remained fixed on her, using his Qi Observation Skill to inspect her illness. Hearing her words, he replied casually, \"Probably.\"","Xiao Wan’er noticed his stare and shot him a playful glare.","\"Tomorrow, Wang Ji will bring a Physician to Jishi Medicine Hall. Don’t forget to go and take a look.\"","After saying this, she stood up. \"And don’t forget to write a reply to Second Sister. I’ll have someone deliver them together this afternoon.\"","Chen Yi smiled, nodded, and stood up to see her off.","He didn’t retract his gaze until Xiao Wan’er had returned to Jiaxing Garden.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wuge, who was still hugging the bottle of Mushroom Tea and drinking, and asked pensively:","\"Wuge, what month does your sister go to the Wumeng Mountain Dojo each year?\"","Suspecting nothing, Xiao Wuge recalled, \"Last year she went in the ninth month. She even brought me back a lot of tasty treats when she returned.\"","The ninth month.","In Shu State, it was the transition from late summer to early autumn, and the lingering heat was still strong.","These details surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind. Combining them with the Profound Mysteries of the Great Success Medical Dao, the principles of yin-yang balance, and the Five Qi and Six Cycles, he deduced:","’Xiao Wan’er doesn’t have a simple cold-yin illness. She must have the legendary Supreme Yin Body. She was born with extreme yin cold that dominates and freezes her meridians, leading to qi stagnation in the meridians and the decline of her life gate’s fire.’","’Her visits to that dojo must be to supplement her yang fire and slow the advance of the cold poison toward her heart.’","But this only treated the symptoms, not the root cause.","As Chen Yi thought, various pathologies and prescriptions swirled through his mind.","A moment later, he shook his head to himself. ’Even with my current Great Success Medical Dao, I can only delay it, not eradicate it completely.’","Chen Yi looked up at the bright sun in the sky and let out a long breath.","Why did Shu State in the sixth month feel a little chilly?","...","「Ten days later, on the ninth day of the seventh month.」","The weather went from hot to hotter.","But within Shu State Prefecture City, a wave of refreshing coolness washed over the hearts of all who toiled outdoors.","—It was the Wangji Tea and Mushroom Tea sold by Hundred Herbs Hall.","Each bottle of Wangji Tea was priced at ten copper coins.","Each bottle of Mushroom Tea was priced at twenty copper coins.","Each bottle of Beauty Tea was priced at one hundred copper coins.","Was it expensive?","Of course, it was.","But don’t be hasty. A notice specially posted by Hundred Herbs Hall clearly stated that they would buy back the porcelain bottles.","Each porcelain bottle for eight copper coins.","With that factored in, the Wangji Tea was no longer so expensive.","Even a laborer at the Wharf who earned around thirty copper coins a day carrying sacks could afford a bottle of Wangji Tea to quench their thirst.","As for the Mushroom Tea and Beauty Tea, made especially for women, they caused a stir as soon as they went on sale, with countless young ladies scrambling to buy them.","This was especially true in the brothels of South City’s Yanhua Lane.","The reason was simple: Jishi Medicine Hall also sold these tea drinks.","If nothing else, those few Qin Buildings certainly knew how to do business.","Just because the Shopkeeper of Jishi Medicine Hall was Chen Yi—Chen Qingzhou—they hauled back cart after cart of assorted tea drinks, then sent back cart after cart of empty porcelain bottles.","The teas they bought were not only liked by the girls, but also by their clients.","It was just that they each had their own favorites.","The girls preferred the Mushroom Tea and Beauty Tea, which were not only sweet and sour but could also enhance their complexion.","Meanwhile, the clients who frequented Yanhua Lane were more fond of the Divine Bull Tea.","Despite its vulgar-sounding name, its effects made the carousing scholars and wealthy gentry who stayed up all night drink it endlessly.","With this multi-pronged approach, the five tea drinks made Hundred Herbs Hall famous throughout Shu State Prefecture City.","And as a result, the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, which also sold the teas, benefited as well.","The shared profits from the tea sales greatly alleviated the Xiao Mansion’s shortage of silver coins.","Jishi Medicine Hall alone brought in three hundred taels daily, with a net profit of one hundred taels.","Although the other four branches didn’t do as well, they still brought in thirty to fifty taels of silver daily.","As a result, Xiao Wan’er had a constant smile on her face lately.","In her delight, she didn’t forget to return the favor.","She not only had her Third Grand-uncle, Xiao Shen, inform the Prefectural Yamen to increase the patrols of government officials around Hundred Herbs Hall, but also ordered Wang Lixing and Liu Si’er to lead men to patrol their own Medicine Halls.","Chen Yi saw all of this.","But his first thought wasn’t one of joy; instead, his attention turned to Linglan Pavilion.","Many things can’t be judged by their glamorous surface; a crisis is often hidden within.","’If I were the one who stole the medicinal ingredients and set up Linglan Pavilion, seeing the Xiao Family’s current success, I probably wouldn’t be able to sit still any longer.’"]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102 - 103: Nine of Eleven","paragraphs":["BOOM.","RUMBLE...","After the scorching heat of June and early July, a storm that had been brewing for days finally burst forth in a torrential downpour.","The oppressive heat that had suffocated Shu State City was instantly extinguished by the rain. Even the residual warmth lingering on the stone slabs quickly dissipated.","A cool, comfortable breeze allowed the city’s residents to finally slow their pace.","Even the laborers who had toiled all day and the government officials and City Guard Army soldiers who had run about tirelessly could now stroll through the streets and alleys with ease.","However, under the heavy rain, many craftsmen trying to make a living found it difficult to smile.","After all, no one was going to watch someone break a stone slab on their chest in a downpour.","Wudong Street, just outside the East Market, at the Jishi Medicine Hall.","The Medicine Hall, which had managed to revive its business thanks to Hundred Herbs Hall’s tea drinks, was now filled with people.","The vast majority were not patients, but craftsmen from the East Market.","There were burly men who performed feats of strength, acrobats, and even some fortune-tellers who read futures and romantic destinies.","They gathered in small groups inside the Medicine Hall, both to shelter from the rain and to enjoy a cup of the tea drink.","Although they earned little from their hard work each day, they could still afford a cup of Wangji Tea for two copper coins.","\"I wonder what kind of recipe Hundred Herbs Hall uses. This drink tastes a bit like tea, but not quite. One cup cools you right down to the bone.\"","\"Even on the hottest days, it can keep the heat off you for half the day.\"","A man in a short-sleeved linen shirt and shorts held a porcelain bottle, taking small sips, clearly reluctant to finish it all at once.","Beside him, a fortune-teller carrying a cloth bag embroidered with the words \"Marriage & Future\" shook his head knowingly and said:","\"You think they’d let you in on the secret to their cash cow?\"","\"I was just making an observation.\"","\"What are you worried about that for? A guy who can’t even make fifty copper coins a day, worrying about big shots like Hundred Herbs Hall who haul their gold and silver around by the cartload?\"","\"Hauling silver coins by the cartload? Are their tea drinks really that profitable?\"","\"Of course. It’s not just Hundred Herbs Hall. Take this Jishi Medicine Hall, for example. Before, this place was so deserted you could catch sparrows at the door. But look at it now...\"","Before he could finish, Liu Quan, who had long since grown tired of these craftsmen, slammed his abacus shut. \"If you’re here to drink tea, then drink your tea. What’s with all the chatter?\"","The fortune-teller paused mid-sentence. He glanced at Liu Quan, but instead of getting annoyed, he turned to Chen Yi, who was sitting near the Physician.","\"Shopkeeper Chen, your accountant is a rather fierce one.\"","Liu Quan’s eyes widened in a glare, but with Chen Yi present, he swallowed the retort on the tip of his tongue. \"Shopkeeper, look at them...\"","Chen Yi had been watching the new Physician apply acupuncture needles. He turned at the sound of their voices and said with a smile:","\"There’s nothing that can’t be said openly. Besides, it’s true that Jishi Medicine Hall’s business is booming again thanks to Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Liu Quan sullenly shut his mouth, lowered his head to his ledger, and went back to clacking away on his abacus.","The fortune-teller chuckled. \"As expected of Shu State’s famous scholar. Your words are a pleasure to hear.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"The principles of life are the same, whether you’ve read books or not.\"","\"It’s just that, today, Jishi Medicine Hall is able to offer you all some convenience. If our business isn’t doing so well in the future, I hope you’ll all remember to give us some of your patronage.\"","At these words, the craftsmen, who were naturally skilled at reading people, all nodded in agreement.","The fortune-teller, being a man of impulse, immediately offered to give Chen Yi a free reading.","\"Shopkeeper, I see you have a rosy complexion, like the auspicious purple qi flowing from the east. You are destined for great wealth and status in the future.\"","Chen Yi looked at him, a faint glow flashing in his eyes, and said with a smile, \"Let’s not talk about my fortune for now. If you don’t have a Physician check your pulse soon, I’m afraid you don’t have many days left.\"","\"Er...\"","The fortune-teller’s face darkened. \"Are you cursing me, Shopkeeper?\"","Chen Yi didn’t answer, instead gesturing for him to come closer. \"If I’m wrong, I’ll give you a bottle of Divine Bull Tea.\"","The people in the Medicine Hall immediately started hooting and hollering.","The fortune-teller was a decisive man. A bottle of Divine Bull Tea sold for thirty copper coins in the Medicine Hall, but it could fetch a hundred in South City’s Yanhua Lane.","Even if he didn’t drink it, reselling it would be enough to cover his food and drink for half a month.","The fortune-teller sat down.","Chen Yi had the new, limping Physician, Ma Liangcai, check his pulse.","Ma Liangcai dutifully did as he was told, placing three fingers on the fortune-teller’s wrist and concentrating on his examination.","After a moment, he paused.","Then he pressed a little harder, feeling for the deep pulse.","After a few moments, Ma Liangcai suddenly sighed. \"The Shopkeeper was right. Your illness is already in its final stages.\"","The fortune-teller looked at him doubtfully. \"Are you sure?\"","He wasn’t old, only forty, and in the prime of his life.","He traveled all over and had never noticed anything wrong with his body.","Naturally, he didn’t believe it now.","\"Let me ask you, do you usually have trouble with cold drinks?\"","\"I suppose so...\"","\"When it rains, do you feel a chill?\"","\"Yeah.\"","\"And...\"","As Ma Liangcai went through a few more questions, details the fortune-teller had never paid attention to were confirmed one by one. His face instantly turned deathly pale. \"Can... can I be saved?\"","\"Yes.\"","Before Ma Liangcai could speak, Chen Yi grabbed a bottle of Divine Bull Tea from nearby, stuffed it into the man’s hand, and said with a smile:","\"One bottle of Divine Bull Tea a day, and I guarantee you’ll be cured. Today’s bottle is on the house.\"","The fortune-teller looked at the tea drink in his hand, then at Chen Yi, then at Ma Liangcai, who was trying to stifle his laughter. It took him a long moment to realize what was happening. \"Hey, you... you shopkeeper!\"","\"Haha...\"","Instantly, the Jishi Medicine Hall erupted with endless laughter.","\"Shopkeeper Chen, you said it so convincingly, I really thought Old Ji only had a few days left! I was already wondering how we’d handle his body.\"","\"Haha... Old Ji cons people left and right, but today he’s the one who got conned by Shopkeeper Chen.\"","The fortune-teller, Old Ji, shook his head with a wry smile. \"Forgive my bluntness, Shopkeeper Chen, but please don’t scare a man like that again.\"","Chen Yi chuckled and exchanged a few more jokes with the crowd. Then he instructed Liu Quan and the others to look after the Medicine Hall and, as usual, prepared to head home around mid-afternoon.","The craftsmen laughingly said their goodbyes, finding him to be an interesting character.","Stepping outside, Chen Yi glanced at Linglan Pavilion. He saw its shopkeeper, Qian Kuan, offer a forced smile and a nod. Chen Yi simply nodded back before walking toward the carriage driven by Ge the Third.","Qian Kuan watched him disappear into the rain, his gaze shifting to the Jishi Medicine Hall, still ringing with boisterous laughter. His expression grew increasingly foul.","’How could the Xiao Family Medicine Hall make a comeback even from this?’","’Hundred Herbs Hall!’","Though Chen Yi hadn’t seen Qian Kuan’s reaction, he had made a few observations from spending the last several days at the Jishi Medicine Hall.","For instance, Qian Kuan, while seemingly busy with his own customers, paid an inordinate amount of attention to Jishi Medicine Hall.","He seemed to be keeping track of the people coming and going from Jishi Medicine Hall each day, and even estimating their revenue.","And then there was the way Qian Kuan looked at him.","Since beginning his study of Martial Arts, Chen Yi had naturally become more perceptive of such things.","Combined with the snippets of conversation his enhanced hearing picked up, he could confirm that Linglan Pavilion was indeed targeting the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","It hadn’t been obvious before, but now that the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s business was improving, the people at Linglan Pavilion had grown somewhat restless.","Their words were no longer so guarded.","Chen Yi watched the downpour outside the carriage window. In his mind, a white stone landed on a Go board.","The center point, ten-ten.","But he took this white stone, named \"Hundred Herbs Hall,\" and placed it at nine-eleven.","—Once Hundred Herbs Hall gained momentum, it was bound to draw some people out.","...","「Night fell, and the downpour continued.」","Through the curtain of rain, in the western part of the city near the West Market, lay the residential manors of Shu State’s high officials and dignitaries.","Unlike the North City, where Duke Dingyuan resided, the manors around the West Market were at most three courtyards deep.","Such were the building regulations, a line these wealthy gentry could not cross.","At this moment, in a manor not far from Hundred Herbs Hall, the main hall of the central courtyard was brightly lit.","Outside the hall, dozens of guards stood watch, clad in raincoats with long blades hanging at their waists.","Faintly, a loud CRASH echoed from within.","\"Under these circumstances, you still allowed the Xiao Family Medicine Hall to survive? What have you all been doing these past days?\"","\"Young Master, we... we did everything according to your instructions regarding the Physicians, the medicinal ingredients, and the treatments...\"","\"Then how do you explain today’s outcome?\"","\"Young Master, it’s not that we weren’t diligent. It’s that the Xiao Family Medicine Hall relied on Hundred Herbs Hall to regain its footing.\"","\"Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","A clear, cold voice spoke.","\"The same Hundred Herbs Hall that made a name for itself in South City’s Yanhua Lane?\"","\"The very same.\"","A moment of silence.","\"What is their connection to the Xiao Family?\"","\"Hundred Herbs Hall’s shopkeeper, Wang Ji, was previously the shopkeeper of the Xiao Family’s Jishi Medicine Hall—the same one where the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law is now.\"","\"Ever since Wang Ji left Jishi Medicine Hall, he started Hundred Herbs Hall with someone else. It’s said there’s another owner behind him, but we haven’t been able to find out who it is.\"","The cold voice spoke again. \"Another owner? Heh. There must be. Otherwise, where would a mere shopkeeper get the recipe for such a tea drink?\"","\"Old Fifth, have you been to Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","\"Reporting to the Young Master, this subordinate went at noon today, but... but only a Steward came out. I did not see Wang Ji.\"","CRACK!","A porcelain bottle shattered.","The cold voice became even colder, squeezing the words out from between clenched teeth: \"Truly courting death!\"","\"Old Third, inform the members of the Illusory Sound Sect. Have them make a move and burn down Hundred Herbs Hall!\"","Another person hesitated. \"Young Master, the people from the Illusory Sound Sect are still being tracked by the Prefectural Yamen and the Xiao Family Punishment Hall. If they show themselves now, I’m afraid...\"","\"Afraid? My Liu Family has spent so many silver coins to support them precisely for moments like this! Otherwise, what’s the use of keeping them around?\"","\"And the ’Sword Madman,’ where is he now? If he hasn’t left Shu State, have him make a move as well.\"","\"Reporting to the Young Master, the ’Sword Madman’ has supposedly gone to the Mountain Race.\"","The cold voice paused. \"What is he doing with the Mountain Race? There’s no one there for him to test his blade on.\"","\"Xiao Jinghong...\"","The cold voice paused, then broke into a laugh.","\"Good, good, good. The ’Sword Madman’ is certainly mad enough, daring to provoke that lunatic Xiao Jinghong. Can his blade stand up to Xiao Jinghong’s long spear?\"","\"Young Master, Black Tooth tried to persuade him, but he wouldn’t listen.\"","At these words, the main hall fell silent.","In the flickering candlelight, a handsome young man with refined features, dressed in purple brocade and sitting with a ramrod-straight posture, finally spoke:","\"Then we’ll ignore him for now.\"","\"First, have the Illusory Sound Sect deal with Hundred Herbs Hall. Find the person backing him and... kill them.\"","\"Also, get your hands on the recipes for those tea drinks.\"","As his voice faded, the five figures around him responded in unison. Then, one of them spoke up:","\"Young Master, if the Xiao Family notices, what should we do?\"","The young man rose to his feet and snorted coldly. \"Someone else will be there to take the fall!\"","Not long after, the manor fell quiet as the people in the main hall dispersed.","Faintly, a dark figure slipped out and, using the curtain of rain as cover, flitted toward another manor.","’If the Liu Family makes another move, they’ll inevitably draw the attention of the Xiao Family Punishment Hall.’","’It’s time... to get *that* person to make a move, too...’"]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103 - 104: An Elder Brother Is Like a Father","paragraphs":["Tingyu Pavilion was the study Chen Yunfan had specially set up in this three-courtyard residence after arriving in Shu State.","The name was elegant, the decor was elegant, and the style was very refined.","This was especially true on rainy days.","When rainwater slid down the roof tiles, it would strike the bamboo chimes under the eaves, creating a series of crisp sounds.","In his own words, if his scholarship was lacking, he had to make up for it in other areas.","However, while it certainly had style...","...when the rain actually came, the sound of the bamboo chimes outside the study was incessant.","Never mind Chen Yunfan; even the calm and steady Chun Ying found it noisy.","This was especially true when she was handling official Government Office business for Chen Yunfan. Listening to the bamboo chimes outside while seeing Chen Yunfan lying on a daybed on the other side of the room, reading a play, her face immediately filled with resentment.","\"Young Master, could you at least glance at some of these official documents and decrees?\"","Without lifting his head, Chen Yunfan slowly turned a page and said in a lazy tone:","\"You’re the ’White-robed Minister.’ You can even make sense of the situation in Great Wei. Handling a little official business like this is naturally no problem for you.\"","That might be true, but things couldn’t go on like this forever.","Chun Ying helplessly picked up the register she had just finished with, walked over, and said:","\"Young Master, you can ignore the others, but this one, you really must take a look.\"","Chen Yunfan glanced sideways at her. Seeing her serious expression, he took it with one hand. \"The Dingyuan Army’s summer harvest has been stored. The Three Towns yielded a total of 2,130,000 shi of grain.\"","\"This year’s harvest is pretty good. Based on the standard of one shi of grain per month, the Dingyuan Soldiers will have enough to last until the end of the year.\"","Chun Ying said, \"The Governor’s Office needs to supervise the Commandant’s Office in allocating the grain and have two hundred thousand shi delivered to Shu State Prefecture City for storage.\"","Chen Yunfan tossed the register aside and pouted. \"What does that have to do with me? It’s a thankless job. Whoever wants to do it can go ahead.\"","Chun Ying started to speak, then hesitated. \"Young Master, you are the Assistant Governor now. This is your responsibility.\"","Chen Yunfan turned his head away. \"I’m not going. The Xiao Family submitted twelve memorials to the Imperial Court this year requesting grain, and the court didn’t give them any.\"","\"Now that they finally have grain, they’re definitely not going to hand it over. Why would I go looking for trouble with them? Am I that bored?\"","\"But...\"","\"No buts. The way I got this Assistant Governor position was fishy. It’s better to be low-key and cautious.\"","Seeing that he wouldn’t budge, Chun Ying stopped trying to persuade him. She took the register and returned to her desk to handle other official matters.","Chen Yunfan, on the other hand, went back to his play, letting out a few laughs from time to time, clearly having reached an amusing part.","Just then, a sharp thwack echoed through the room.","THWACK.","The two turned to look and saw an arrow stuck quivering in the wall.","Chen Yunfan looked outside, frowning slightly, and cursed under his breath, \"These gutter-dwelling Hidden Guards really think my place is their own backyard.\"","Hearing this, Chun Ying walked over, removed the arrow, and took out a slip of paper from it. After a glance, she said, \"Young Master, it’s a message from the Hawk.\"","Chen Yunfan looked away from the window and took the note. \"The Illusory Sound Sect has reappeared. The Shu State Liu Family intends to move against Hundred Herbs Hall to suppress the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.\"","A single sentence, with a start and a finish.","And yet, it had neither.","Chen Yunfan thought for a moment, then started cursing. \"Why the hell are they giving me this information?\"","\"If they want to deal with the Xiao Family, they should just let the Illusory Sound Sect make their move.\"","\"And if they don’t, are they planning to use me to pass the message to the Xiao Family?\"","Upon hearing this, Chun Ying’s expression shifted slightly. \"The Liu Family of Shu State is a branch of the Liu Clan of Jing State.\"","\"But because of Liu Hong, the Left Envoy of the Governor’s Office, the Jing State Liu Clan is subtly losing control over this branch...\"","Chen Yunfan interrupted, \"And? So the Hidden Guard is also unhappy with the Shu State Liu?\"","Chun Ying analyzed, \"They likely hope to use the Xiao Family to weaken the Shu State Liu Family.\"","After a pause, she continued, \"Young Master, the Xiao Family actually suspected long ago that the Illusory Sound Sect, which stole the medicinal ingredients, was connected to several of the Noble Families in Shu State.\"","\"On top of that, Liu Jing—Liu Huanzhi—the legitimate Sixth Young Master of the Jing State Liu Clan, opened Linglan Pavilion right next to several of the Xiao Family’s Medicine Halls.\"","\"The Xiao Family Punishment Hall must be watching the Shu State Liu, Liu Jing, and the others.\"","\"I just don’t understand Elder Master Xiao’s plan. He doesn’t seem to be in a hurry to make a move.\"","After listening, Chen Yunfan said thoughtfully, \"Given the Xiao Family’s current situation, I guess the Old Marquis wants to see just who all is involved.\"","\"It wasn’t hard to see from his previous birthday banquet. The Old Marquis has already prepared to be the Xiao Family’s final line of defense.\"","\"For a man like him who has spent his life on horseback, his final counterattack before death will surely be earth-shattering. Naturally, he needs to find a suitable target.\"","Chun Ying seemed to have a realization. \"The people in Shu State must be worried about that too.\"","Chen Yunfan nodded. \"But it seems the Hidden Guard’s ambitions in Shu State are not small, either.\"","Chun Ying had come to the same conclusion.","If they were only targeting the Xiao Family, the Hidden Guard would have chosen to sit on the mountain and watch the tigers fight, not to stick their oar in.","\"What do you plan to do, Young Master?\"","\"Nothing. Let them fight their battles. I’ll mind my own business.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yunfan’s palm trembled slightly, and the slip of paper disintegrated into tiny fragments, which were then blown out of the study by the wind.","He looked out at the rainy night and snorted. \"As if the Hidden Guard is worthy of ordering me around.\"","Chun Ying opened her mouth but was speechless for a moment.","The words of persuasion she was about to say died on her lips.","Chen Yunfan didn’t care what she thought. Now that he had a grasp of the situation, he lay back down and continued reading his play.","He would let out a chuckle or two from time to time.","After a moment of thought, Chun Ying tried a new approach. \"Young Master, Young Master Yi is now the Shopkeeper of Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","\"I heard that most of the tea drinks that Hundred Herbs Hall supplies to the Xiao Family Medicine Hall are sold through Young Master Yi.\"","\"If something happens to Hundred Herbs Hall, I’m afraid it will affect Young Master Yi as well.\"","Chen Yunfan’s smile froze. He fell silent for a moment, then abruptly sat up, his expression turning serious.","\"Chun Ying, you have a point. I really shouldn’t just do nothing.\"","Chun Ying was just starting to feel pleased when she heard him say, \"How about we go rescue Hundred Herbs Hall in secret?\"","\"Er...\"","\"Think about it. If Brother Yi finds out in the future that it was me who rescued Hundred Herbs Hall, allowing him, the Shopkeeper, to continue his business peacefully, won’t he be grateful to me?\"","\"He should be...\"","Chen Yunfan raised an eyebrow. \"You think so too, right? Then it’s decided.\"","\"For the next two days, have those bastards keep an eye on the Liu Family and see when they make their move.\"","Chen Yunfan muttered to himself for a bit, then chuckled. \"As expected of me.\"","\"Just you wait. I will reassert my authority as the elder brother and let Brother Yi know what ’an elder brother is like a father’ truly means!\"","\"...As long as you’re happy, Young Master.\"","’As expected,’ Chun Ying thought, ’when it comes to Young Master Yi, the Young Master is always very attentive.’","...","「Xiao Family, Spring Lotus Garden.」","\"The rain keeps falling, the atmosphere isn’t exactly harmonious...\"","Having finished his Cultivation, Chen Yi stood in a pavilion in a good mood, watching the rain strike the pond and willows.","Although he still hadn’t obtained a suitable True Essence Cultivation technique, by relying on his Mastery Level Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, his Cultivation had reached the Middle Eighth Grade.","Of the twelve main meridians in his body, besides the four in his hands and feet, he had opened another four in succession, causing the True Essence within the two great Seas of Qi—his Dantian and his chest—to become much more abundant.","Not only had his Punch, Step, and Spear Techniques benefited, but his Medical Dao, Calligraphy Dao, and Chess Dao had also improved.","For example, the Acupuncture Skills \"Controlling Needle with Qi\" and \"Meridian Continuation\" both required True Essence to support them.","The same was true for the Calligraphy Dao Realm of Beauty and Grace.","Even the Evolutionary Chess Game in the Way of Chess Dao had become clearer and more distinct.","The effects of True Essence were truly profound.","’But not having a True Essence Cultivation technique isn’t a long-term solution.’","With this in mind, Chen Yi planned to have Wang Ji acquire a manual from other channels tomorrow and start practicing with it.","Martial Arts may have been popular in the Great Wei Dynasty, but top-tier Martial Arts—that is, Cultivation Techniques of Earth Level and above—were rarely seen.","They were mostly controlled by the Imperial Court, Noble Families, and Sects.","The Cultivation Techniques that circulated among the public were either incomplete or of a lower grade, making cultivation inefficient.","This was why Chen Yi had been waiting patiently.","He was hoping for a Celestial Level or Earth Level intelligence report that would reward him with a True Essence Cultivation technique.","One and done.","Unfortunately, all the intelligence reports these past few days had been Yellow Level; he hadn’t even seen a single Profound Level one.","He sat for a while, until the hour of Zi—","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Top Grade: Half past the hour of Zi, Hidden Guards are discussing important matters inside Four Directions Hall. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","A fluorescent light flashed and disappeared.","After reading it, Chen Yi shot to his feet and looked in the direction of Jiaxing Garden.","’Half past the hour of Zi... that’s in an hour.’","’Hidden Guards discussing important matters in Four Directions Hall... Xiao Dongchen?’","’Who’s the other person?’","’But Four Directions Hall...’","’It wasn’t a problem that Jiaxing Garden was between it and my Spring Lotus Garden. The issue was that Shen Huatang was in the residence now, so he couldn’t just hop over the wall like last time.’","’But he didn’t want to give up on a Profound Level intelligence report he had waited so long for.’","’Even just a few glances from afar could yield a significant reward.’","With that in mind, Chen Yi called up his panel.","[Opportunity: 147]","After a moment’s thought, Chen Yi added the Opportunity points to his \"Martial Arts Step,\" raising it to the Great Success Realm.","’To get past Jiaxing Garden silently, even the powder Miss Pei gave me would be useless. My only chance is to improve my Body Technique as much as possible.’","’And if I’m unlucky enough to be discovered... well, it’s a long night, and I can’t sleep. There’s nothing wrong with taking a walk, right?’","With his previous experiences, he suppressed the Profound Mysteries of the Great Success \"Martial Arts Step\" in his mind before they could even make a splash.","Immediately after, Chen Yi began practicing the Meteor Butterfly Step inside the pavilion, absorbing the Profound Mysteries of the \"Martial Arts Step\" at the same time.","His figure flickered unpredictably, like a black butterfly flitting about under the cover of the rainy night.","A quarter of an hour later.","[Successfully practiced Step Technique · Meteor Butterfly Step (Earth Tier). Level: Mastery]","Chen Yi stopped and slowly calmed the True Essence in his body.","He glanced at the falling rain, then at his clothes, and immediately returned to his room to change into a long black robe.","Without a moment’s delay, Chen Yi used the Meteor Butterfly Step to flit away from Spring Lotus Garden like a phantom, heading toward Four Directions Hall.","To avoid Shen Huatang, whose Cultivation had reached the Fifth Grade, he even took a deliberate detour.","He also dodged every one of the Xiao Family Armored Warriors he encountered along the way.","After about a quarter of an hour, Chen Yi finally arrived outside Four Directions Hall.","He listened intently for a moment. Following his memory from his previous visit, he leaped to another spot that was not illuminated by the lights of Four Directions Hall.","Seeing no one around, he let out a long breath.","Then, Chen Yi observed his surroundings.","Fortunately, the rain provided cover, and the shadows in the courtyard were blurry and indistinct.","’But obviously, in this kind of environment, the Hidden Guards wouldn’t be having their discussion outside.’","Who would have thought that just as this idea crossed his mind, he would see Xiao Dongchen walk out of the wooden building.","Following behind him was one of the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard, clad in armor.","Chen Yi froze for a second, then quickly hid himself and used the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to conceal his aura, fixing his gaze on them.","’Liu Si’er?’"]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104 - 105: Secrets, Four Symbols","paragraphs":["It wasn’t Liu Si’er.","The build and gait were wrong.","Chen Yi stared intently at the Armored Warrior standing beside Xiao Dongchen, a faint sense of familiarity washing over him.","It had to be an Armored Warrior he had seen and interacted with a few times.","Besides Liu Si’er, there was only Wang Lixing, Ge the Third, Yan Hong...","One by one, their images overlapped with the person before him.","Finally, it settled on one man.","Chen Yi froze, barely managing to hold back a curse.","’Damn it—Ge the Third!’","’How could it be Ge the Third?’","Over the past few days, he had suspected many people around him, even those newly hired Quack Physicians.","But he had never once suspected Ge the Third.","That bastard was usually so big and burly, with a boisterous personality that made it seem like he couldn’t keep a secret to save his life...","’To think he was a Hidden Guard, concealing his true identity so deeply.’","’You bastard. Just you wait!’","Chen Yi cursed under his breath, the composure he had cultivated over the past few days shattering completely.","Then, he pricked up his ears and listened carefully to their conversation.","With his current Middle Eighth Grade Cultivation, his hearing was several times sharper than an ordinary person’s, allowing him to catch snippets of sound even through the curtain of rain.","\"...The Dingyuan Army has stored as much as two million stones of grain. It’s too much.\"","\"Even if the Governor’s Office confiscates a portion of it, when you factor in the grain acquired through the salt and iron monopoly, the Dingyuan Army will still have enough to last half a year without worry.\"","\"For me, this is an out-and-out disaster.\"","Xiao Dongchen’s voice was crystal clear, making Chen Yi’s heart stir.","He had, of course, heard about the summer harvest from the three military garrisons over the past few days. The Old Master had been delighted by the news for a long time.","Recalling the words \"Mutual Market\" from Xiao Dongchen’s previous secret letter, Chen Yi could vaguely guess what the two were meeting to discuss today.","Just then, he heard Ge the Third lower his voice. \"Master Chen, it’s no use coming to me about this.\"","\"Although we are both Silver Banner Officers, our missions are different. The Iron Banner Officers and members of the White Tiger Group we can mobilize are also different.\"","\"Even if I did as you ask, I could only round up some local thugs or Wandering Martial Artists. They’d be useless for the ’Mutual Market matter’.\"","\"You can’t possibly expect them to take care of Granny Shan and the Second Miss, can you?\"","A moment of silence passed.","Xiao Dongchen paced over to the pavilion in the courtyard. He looked up at the rainy night sky and said in a low voice:","\"I will handle the Mutual Market myself. But that grain... I need you to take care of it.\"","\"Are you thinking...\"","Ge the Third seemed to swear. \"Are you out of your mind?\"","Xiao Dongchen shook his head. \"We both know that if the Mutual Market succeeds, the Xiao Family’s troubles will vanish in an instant.\"","\"You can see it from the Liu Family’s recent probing.\"","\"Even with the Old Master gravely ill, Wuge still young, and the Xiao Family barely holding on, they are still extremely cautious, terrified of drawing the Old Master’s attention.\"","\"If we can’t throw the Xiao Family into chaos now, the other Noble Families of Shu State will never make a move.\"","\"Once the Xiao Family escapes its predicament, even if the Old Master is gone, the members of the first branch will still be able to protect the entire family.\"","Xiao Dongchen paused and turned his head to look at him, his tone serious. \"Hawk, our missions may be different, but our objectives are the same.\"","\"If my second branch can’t gain control of the Xiao Family, what chance does your ’Fledgling’ have?\"","Hearing this, Ge the Third’s eyes turned sinister under his helmet. \"His business has nothing to do with you. I advise you to pay less attention to him.\"","Xiao Dongchen chuckled. \"I’m afraid you don’t know yet, do you? Liu Jing is already planning to move against the Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Once they succeed and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s business suffers, with the ’Fledgling’s’ personality, he’ll definitely just stay put in the Spring Lotus Garden.\"","\"When that happens, how will you force him to submit?\"","Ge the Third snorted. \"That’s not your concern. I have my own methods.\"","\"Going to find more thugs and hooligans?\"","\"You’re pushing me to kill you!\"","Xiao Dongchen shook his head, then leaned in and whispered a few words. \"Helping me is helping yourself. Besides, ’Lady Tiger’ also needs Shu State to fall into chaos.\"","Ge the Third frowned at him. \"Lady Tiger? You’re in contact with her too? I think you’ve really lost your mind.\"","Chen Yi listened intently but couldn’t make out what Xiao Dongchen had whispered.","However, judging from Ge the Third’s reaction, it wasn’t hard to deduce that this \"Lady Tiger\" was a Hidden Guard with the same status as them.","’A Silver Banner Officer?’","’It does fit the structure of the Imperial Court’s forces.’","Over there, Ge the Third was silent for a long time before nodding slightly. \"What do you want me to do?\"","A smile spread across Xiao Dongchen’s face. \"Exactly as you guessed—burn the grain.\"","Ge the Third immediately cursed again. His eyes scanned the surroundings, and instead of replying directly, he raised his voice and said:","\"As Master Chen commands. This subordinate will go to the Hundred Herbs Hall tomorrow to fetch some tea.\"","After speaking, he turned and vanished into the rain, striding out of the Four Directions Hall with purpose.","Xiao Dongchen didn’t try to stop him. After watching him leave, he glanced toward Jiaxing Garden and muttered:","\"Shen Huatang left the mansion late at night. I wonder if it’s to deal with the people from the Illusory Sound Sect.\"","\"But everything is ready, so it doesn’t matter... Heh heh...\"","Muttering to himself, he slowly paced toward the wooden building.","With a CREAK, the door closed.","[You have witnessed the hidden ways of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion’s Hidden Guards and overheard their secret council. Reward: Four Symbols Skill (Profound Tier), Opportunity +30.]","[Evaluation: Subject arrived, sounds heard, scene witnessed. However, the eavesdropping is excessive. A natural-born sneak.]","Seeing this, Chen Yi knew their discussion was over and both had left, so he carefully got to his feet.","This time, however, he didn’t walk through the outer courtyard. Using the rain as cover, he executed the Meteor Butterfly Step, crossing nearly seventy yards in just two breaths and vaulting over the wall into Jiaxing Garden on the other side.","’If I had known Shen Huatang wasn’t in the mansion, why would I have bothered upgrading my Martial Arts Step?’","’I hope this won’t affect my progress with the Heart Method I just obtained, the Four Symbols Skill for cultivating True Essence.’","Still, this incident made it easy for Chen Yi to see the extent of the Hidden Guards’—or rather, Xiao Dongchen’s—control over the Xiao Family.","’Besides the Personal Guards Liu Si’er and Ge the Third, there are probably other Hidden Guards hiding in the mansion.’","’Perhaps even here, in Jiaxing Garden?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing, but in any case, he would have to be more careful from now on.","Who would have thought that just as he landed, he would see Xiao Wan’er in the distance, standing by her window and staring blankly into the rain.","Fortunately, she hadn’t noticed him, so it wouldn’t be a repeat of last time.","Chen Yi carefully hid behind a tree, quietly waiting for Xiao Wan’er to close her window.","After waiting for a moment, he still saw no movement from her.","Chen Yi peeked his head out, looked at the beautiful silhouette in the building above, and muttered in annoyance:","\"I really don’t know what to say about her. Her body is so sensitive to the cold, yet she keeps the window wide open. Isn’t she afraid of her illness acting up?\"","Others might not know, but Chen Yi, who had practiced his Qi Observation Skill on Xiao Wan’er many times, was keenly aware of her physical condition.","To say she had a \"Supreme Yin Body\" was an understatement. Besides the yin coldness, her yang fire was also faintly dissipating.","It was just like the \"Detachment Syndrome\" of the short man who died at the Prefectural Yamen.","’Once her yang fire dissipates to a certain point, she could perish at any moment.’","Just as Chen Yi was thinking about this, he heard Xiao Wan’er’s voice from the wooden building.","It wasn’t speech, but the sound of her humming a song:","\"Snowy soul spun from clouds to form her hair, icy silk rinsed in moonlight for her eyes, the Kui Gorge at night overflows with a river of stars... Jade Steps and Jade Trees, a beauty like you, is rarely seen in this world...\"","Chen Yi paused, watching her silhouette and listening intently to her song.","At this moment, under the cover of night, the wind whistled and the rain pattered down. The flowers, grass, and trees seemed to sway back and forth in accompaniment.","Even with the sound of the rain and the fragrant scents wafting through the air, nothing could mask her song.","It was as if Jiaxing Garden itself had become more vibrant, more radiant, like a painted scroll.","A short while later.","Xiao Wan’er’s voice faded, and a faint blush appeared on her pale face.","She gazed at the rain outside, listened to the pattering sound, then pulled her cloak tighter around herself and gently closed the window.","Not long after, the candlelight in her room was extinguished.","Faintly, the sound of a sigh seemed to drift out.","Chen Yi watched quietly for a moment, a complex expression on his face.","’It seems that poem I wrote back then was indeed a bit too forward.’"]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105 - 106: Accomplishment and Breakthrough","paragraphs":["Moments later, Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden.","He fetched a basin of hot water and quickly washed up in his room. Changing into a fresh robe, he finally felt much more refreshed.","This downpour was even more ferocious than the ones from early summer.","If not for his proficiency in Martial Arts, he would have surely caught a chill from walking for over an hour in the rainy night.","After a brief rest, Chen Yi went to his study. He lit the two candles in the room, used their flames to light the oil lamp on his desk, and then sat down.","He poured water and ground the ink.","The night was deep outside the window, while the room was cast in a dim, yellow glow.","Although the rain pattered ceaselessly against the roof tiles, Chen Yi’s mood remained unaffected.","Moreover, as he ground the ink, his mind grew increasingly tranquil and serene.","Everything he had seen and heard tonight—some of it with his eyes, some with his ears, and some of it had settled deep in his heart.","He needed to quiet his mind and focus to sort through it all.","Moments later, the ink in the inkstone was smooth and evenly mixed.","Chen Yi pulled out a sheet of Yunsong Paper, selected a small wolf-hair brush from the holder, dipped it in ink, and began to write.","\"Four Hidden Guards identified within the Xiao Mansion. Two groups, different missions.\"","\"First group: Ge the Third, Liu Si’er, Uncle Gui. Priority: the ’Fledgling’ mission.\"","\"Second group: Xiao Dongchen and his subordinate Hidden Guards. Goal: ’seize the Xiao Family’.\"","\"Also involved: the Liu Clan of Shu State, the Liu Clan of Jing State, the Illusory Sound Sect...\"","The first group didn’t require much thought.","Even setting aside his naturally detached temperament, he would never let them get what they wanted.","The latter group’s ambition and threat, however, were far greater.","Xiao Dongchen currently wanted to \"throw the Xiao Family and Shu State into chaos,\" with his sights set squarely on the \"Mutual Market.\"","To achieve his goal, he couldn’t allow the Dingyuan Army to remain stable, which was why he had been so anxious for Ge the Third to go discuss important matters with him tonight.","Chen Yi thought, ’Burning the granaries of the Three Towns... a truly vicious plan.’","With this thought, he used his brush to circle the name \"Xiao Dongchen\" and draw an \"X\" over it.","Next, Chen Yi wrote down the three words \"Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","’This chess piece, now that it’s gained some momentum, has certainly flushed a few people out.’","Whether it was the Liu Clan of Jing State or the Liu Clan of Shu State, their ultimate goal was to ensure the Xiao Family didn’t prosper.","And from what the two Silver Banner Officers of the Hidden Guard had said, it wasn’t just the Liu Clan in Shu State; other Noble Families felt the same way.","That was why Xiao Dongchen hoped to throw the Xiao Family into chaos, inciting the Hidden Guard, the Noble Families, and others to rise up and attack them.","As Chen Yi gazed at the words on the Yunsong Paper, several more pieces materialized on the chessboard in his mind.","Xiao Dongchen, Ge the Third, and the others were the traitors within.","The Liu of Shu State should be Liu Hong, the Left Envoy of the Shu State Governor’s Office. This piece was the head of a small dragon among the black pieces.","Behind him were the Liu Clan of Jing State and other Noble Families.","But as for the white pieces representing the Xiao Family...","After a moment of quiet thought, Chen Yi still hesitated to place a single piece on his mental \"chessboard.\"","A game of the Chess Dao was just like two armies clashing in battle.","The white pieces were currently a lone pillar, unable to support the structure, yet he couldn’t even find a supporting piece to form a pincer?","The only ones he could think of were \"Zhang Xuan, Duke Qian of Guangyue Prefecture,\" and the soldiers of the three military towns.","But clearly, these pieces were either too far away or carried too much \"weight.\" It wasn’t yet time to play them.","’At the birthday banquet, all those guests seemed to hold the Old Marquis in high esteem.’","’But in the end, are they all just going to sit on the sidelines?’","’On second thought, that’s probably not it.’","’Perhaps Xiao Dongchen and Ge the Third were right earlier. The Old Marquis is waiting.’","’He’s waiting for them all to reveal themselves so he can finish the job in one fell swoop.’","’When the tree falls, the monkeys scatter.’","’The Old Marquis is gambling on human nature.’","As these thoughts ran through his mind, Chen Yi’s focus returned to the chessboard within.","At present, the black pieces were forming an encirclement around the white.","However, the white pieces also had a chance to bite off a corner from the black.","But if he failed to find that crucial supporting piece soon, defeat would only be a matter of time.","For the moment, he could see no hope of turning the tables.","Chen Yi shook his head. He tore the sheet of Yunsong Paper to shreds, then held the pieces over the oil lamp, burning them to ash bit by bit.","He was now left with one final question.","Why was the Imperial Court secretly moving against the Xiao Family?","Or rather, why did the Imperial Court want chaos in Shu State and the power of its various noble families to decline?","Xiao Dongchen, Ge the Third, and the \"Lady Tiger\" they spoke of all shared this goal.","But what was the reason?","To weaken the border towns and reclaim military authority?","But if that was the case, was it necessary to take down all the Noble Families of Shu State along with them?","’It feels like doing so is no different from cutting off one’s own arm.’","Chen Yi tidied up his desk, his mind churning with these thoughts.","There had to be a reason he hadn’t yet discovered; the whole affair felt strange.","Having tidied up, Chen Yi rose and walked to the window, gazing out at the wind-battered Qinghe Garden.","In the gloom, everything was reduced to hazy, indistinct shapes.","Only the lantern hanging from the eaves swung in the wind, its dim light unable to reach very far.","Much like the Xiao Family at this very moment.","As he gazed out, the faces of several people around him surfaced in his mind.","Xiao Jinghong, Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, Xiaodie, the Old Marquis...","The longer he stayed with the Xiao Family, the more his initial resolution—to be able to cut ties and leave at any time—gradually faded.","After all, he was not a cold-blooded, heartless man.","After a long silence, Chen Yi uttered a single word: \"Troublesome.\"","He immediately did a few chest-expanding stretches, inhaling and exhaling as his expression grew serious.","’First things first, I need to improve my Martial Arts.’","He hadn’t forgotten that the Illusory Sound Sect was planning to make a move against Hundred Herbs Hall.","’I wonder if those Jianghu people I had Wang Ji find have arrived yet. They can’t possibly expect a scholar like me to handle it, can they?’","After letting a few stray thoughts drift through his mind, Chen Yi sat down in his chair and focused his attention on the newly acquired *Four Symbols Skill*.","\"The Four Symbols—Cyan Dragon, Black Tortoise, Vermilion Bird, and White Tiger—represent the Spiritual Qi of the four cardinal directions, which are Wood, Water, Fire, and Metal...\"","\"Guide the Spiritual Qi of the Four Directions to merge into the Sea of Qi, opening the Four Divine Positions...\"","As the cultivation mantra surfaced in his mind, Chen Yi sensed something odd about the *Four Symbols Skill*.","’For a summary this grandiose to belong to a mere Profound-rank Technique, just how powerful must Earth Tier and the even higher Celestial Tier techniques be?’","But he soon understood why.","This version of the *Four Symbols Skill* was actually a \"Lesser\" version.","The general principles were lofty, but the actual content could only support his cultivation up to the Fifth Grade Realm. To progress further, he would need to find the rest of the technique.","Chen Yi grimaced inwardly, but he knew the problem wasn’t with the reward itself. This was likely the limit of what either Xiao Dongchen or Ge the Third had learned.","After reading it through once, Chen Yi relaxed his mind. As he began to circulate his energy according to the mantra, the Profound Mysteries of his Great Success \"Martial Arts Body\" unexpectedly surfaced in his mind.","It was the very last bit of information on the \"Martial Arts Body,\" which had been buried beneath countless other Profound Mysteries.","He instantly realized that both the External Refining Pile Skill and the method for True Essence Cultivation were hidden within the physical body.","The former was merely the exterior and the latter the interior. When combined, they could unlock the secret potential of the human body.","As Chen Yi came to this realization, his understanding of the *Four Symbols Skill* deepened, and the True Essence within him began to travel along the designated route, flowing through his Sea of Qi and meridians.","At first, it only circulated through the meridians in his limbs and organs that he had already fully opened.","Faintly, he could feel wisps of Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi surging toward him.","It was no longer entering his body in mere slivers as before, but in full-on \"wisps.\"","Clearly, a technique that specialized in True Essence Cultivation was stronger than the *Black Tortoise Concealment Technique* by a significant margin.","Before long.","Chen Yi’s mind became completely immersed in his cultivation. He followed the technique, devouring wisps of Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi into his Dantian and the Sea of Qi in his Chest.","They were then all converted into True Essence.","[Successfully learned Cultivation Technique: *Four Symbols Skill* (Profound-rank). Level: Initial Insight]","[Gains from Cultivation: Two more Main Meridians opened. Cultivation has broken through to: Eighth Grade, Upper.]","The downpour raged on outside, but not a single sound reached his ears.","Chen Yi felt his consciousness drift into a sea of cotton. He was in a hazy trance, yet it was a state of pure bliss.","The sensation was something that could not be described to an outsider."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106 - 107: Eighth Grade Upper Stage","paragraphs":["The next morning.","The rain had lightened considerably.","Beneath the gloomy sky, a layer of mist shrouded the lush vegetation of the Spring Lotus Garden, obscuring the view in a hazy blur.","It was impossible to see clearly.","Weather like this, however, brought Xiaodie a little joy.","It wasn’t because Chen Yi hadn’t left early, but because he was still resting in the study.","By the candlelight, she could see his figure sitting cross-legged on a chair.","His face was calm, his eyes closed.","He was clearly sleeping soundly.","Xiaodie took a quiet peek, then tiptoed out of the study, covering her mouth with her hand to stifle a smile.","She had woken up even earlier today than yesterday; thankfully, her efforts had not been in vain.","With that thought, she ran upstairs to tidy up the room.","\"Huh?\"","Xiaodie tilted her head in confusion as she looked at the damp long robe and undergarments hanging on the rack, her twin hair buns tilting to one side along with her head.","’Did Master Chen go out last night?’","Xiaodie couldn’t figure it out, so she didn’t dwell on it. She tidied up the room and carried the wet clothes downstairs.","After taking them to the laundry room and washing them with floral water and soap beans, she shook out the long robe and strenuously stood on her tiptoes to hang it on the clothesline.","\"Phew...\"","Xiaodie looked down at her own short legs and pouted.","’If only I were as tall as the Eldest Miss and the Second Miss, at least hanging laundry wouldn’t be such a struggle.’","A young maid who rarely went out was bound to have some strange little worries.","Fortunately, Xiaodie never let her worries linger. Once she thought about them, she forgot them.","She then ran to fetch water and bring breakfast, trip after trip, moving quite quickly.","Once everything was ready,","Xiaodie wiped the sweat from her forehead and let out a long sigh, a relieved smile gracing her small face.","She was like a flower bud waiting to bloom, pure and elegant.","’Time to wake the Young Master, and Master Chen.’","Xiaodie muttered to herself, counting on her fingers the things she had to do today.","’I need to prepare tea. If Master Chen isn’t going to the Medicine Hall, he’ll definitely be playing chess in the pavilion.’","’I’ll need to get two cups ready; Grandpa Sun will probably come too.’","’I have to get the small shovel to dig for earthworms for the Young Master’s fishing.’","’I also need to remind the kitchen to cook according to Master Chen’s tastes for lunch, and specifically tell them to use less spice.’","Shu State was humid, so people there ate a lot of spicy food.","But Xiaodie always remembered that Master Chen was from Jiangnan Prefecture and wasn’t accustomed to the cuisine of Shu State.","So, from the moment she became Chen Yi’s personal maid, she couldn’t afford to overlook these small details.","She was, after all, a maid who aspired to become a \"head maid.\"","It had to be said... her ambition was quite grand.","Just as Xiaodie ran upstairs to help Xiao Wuge get dressed, Chen Yi slowly concluded his cultivation.","He slowly opened his eyes and exhaled a breath of turbid air.","The long stream of air was a murky white, faintly dotted with specks of black.","Chen Yi knew these were impurities that had accumulated in his meridians, flesh, and organs from long periods of cultivation.","Now that he had achieved success in his Four Symbols Skill cultivation, these impurities were being expelled by the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi, making his body purer.","Chen Yi looked around, then stood up and stretched.","Not only did he not feel tired, but he felt refreshed and clear-headed. His mind was clearer than ever before, and his five senses were much sharper.","Needless to say, the True Essence within him had more than doubled compared to last night.","’My cultivation has reached the Upper Stage of the Eighth Grade Realm. Not bad.’","He took a moment to carefully experience the changes.","Chen Yi grinned. ’But the path of Martial Arts has its price.’","What price?","The fact that he could no longer sleep, of course.","Cultivating the Four Symbols Skill could replace sleep, which meant he couldn’t sleep at noon or at night anymore.","To sleep even once would be a sign of disrespect to his cultivation of the Martial Dao.","’It’s just that now I’ve lost another \"hobby.\"’","A happy problem to have.","Chen Yi shook his head, walked out of the study, and sat down at the living room table to slowly eat his breakfast.","Even without trying to listen, Xiaodie’s voice clearly reached his ears.","\"Young Master, Master Chen isn’t going to the Medicine Hall today!\"","\"Really? Then I’m going to learn chess from Brother-in-law today.\"","\"Then the Young Master will definitely be as amazing as Master Chen in the future.\"","\"I think so too, hehe...\"","Listening to the conversation upstairs, Chen Yi naturally felt lighthearted and cheerful.","’Looks like I’ll have to disappoint them. I can’t just relax in the mansion today.’","Before, when many things were still unclear, Chen Yi could remain patient, focusing on his cultivation, chess, and the Medical Dao.","But now that he had a general grasp of the Xiao Family’s situation, the sooner he resolved it, the better.","’It’s a shame my wife isn’t here. Otherwise, how would this riffraff dare to show their faces?’","With that thought, Chen Yi finished breakfast with Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie.","Then, under their disappointed gazes, he told them he had some matters to attend to and would be back soon.","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"I’m the Shopkeeper of the Medicine Hall now, after all. If I don’t go, Eldest Sister will have something to say about it.\"","Disappointed as they were,","Both Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie were sensible. \"Brother-in-law, then you have to teach me chess next time you’re resting.\"","Xiaodie chimed in, \"Master Chen, teach me too, teach me!\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, naturally not refusing.","’Although my Chess Dao is only at the Minor Success Realm, it’s more than enough to teach a few beginners.’","After a short rest,","Chen Yi changed into a set of green robes, opened an oil-paper umbrella, and walked out of the Spring Lotus Garden.","He was currently using the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to hide his aura. Walking alone in the rain, he looked no different from an ordinary person.","But the sight of his figure made Xiaodie a little worried.","Xiaodie glanced at the sky. ’Master Chen is dressed so lightly. He can’t catch a cold.’","With that thought, she made a mental note to prepare ginger tea for Master Chen.","Xiao Wuge came out and looked at where Chen Yi had already disappeared. He could only say, \"Looks like I’ll have to go stay with Eldest Sister today.\"","Xiaodie snapped back to reality and quickly opened an umbrella for him. \"It’s livelier over at the Eldest Miss’s place.\"","Xiao Wuge walked beside her, muttering, \"But I have to read...\"","Xiaodie smiled but didn’t say anything.","She didn’t dare comment on the arrangements made by the mansion’s Eldest Miss.","If someone overheard, they would think she was ill-mannered.","...","Chen Yi arrived at the front courtyard with his umbrella and called out to an Armored Warrior, \"Is Ge the Third around?\"","The Armored Warrior replied, \"Master Chen, Ge the Third went out early this morning. He said Old Master Chen ordered him to go to the Medicine Hall to pick up some tea.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"What about Brother Xing and Brother Si?\"","The words had just left his mouth when he remembered that Xiao Wan’er had sent those two to inspect the Xiao Family’s various medicine halls.","\"Never mind. No need to prepare a carriage today.\"","Chen Yi said, not asking the Armored Warrior to prepare a carriage or follow him, and walked out of the mansion on foot.","Just then, a carriage approached from outside the gate, driven by Yan Hong, whom he had met a few times.","\"Master Chen, heading out?\"","Chen Yi smiled warmly and nodded, stepping aside to let the carriage pass before continuing on his way.","But he could still hear the voices from behind him.","\"The son-in-law? Junior Sister, is that General Jinghong’s husband?\"","\"Yes.\"","’Shen Huatang? Her senior sister...’","’So she wasn’t in Jiaxing Garden last night because she went to pick up someone from her Sect.’","Chen Yi’s heart stirred slightly, and he slowed his pace. The voices from the mansion grounds carried over:","\"He certainly looks like a scholar, so frail and weak. I really don’t know why General Jinghong agreed to marry him into the family.\"","\"Senior Sister, now that we’re at the Marquis’s Mansion, it’s best not to say such things.\"","\"I know, I know. I get the rules. Can’t gossip about the masters and mistresses of the mansion, right?\"","\"General Jinghong cares for Master Chen a great deal, as does the Eldest Miss.\"","\"Is that so? Then he must have some extraordinary qualities, right? Tell me about them.\"","\"Um... his calligraphy is quite good.\"","\"That’s it?\"","As the distance grew, Chen Yi stopped listening.","’Still, \"That’s it?\"’","’Even if Shen Huatang’s senior sister had a high cultivation, she was clearly uneducated and ill-mannered.’","Chen Yi grumbled internally as he walked farther and farther away.","About an hour later, he finally arrived at the West Market, his eyes sweeping a glance around.","For a fleeting moment, he deactivated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique within him, allowing all the surrounding sounds to enter his ears.","Instantly, he had a complete grasp of the situation within a twenty-zhang radius.","Pedestrians hurrying by: thirty-two.","People inside the shops along the street: forty-three.","Martial Artists with deep, steady breathing indicating they had cultivation: eight.","And two whose sounds were indistinct.","’If there are no other Martial Artists skilled in techniques similar to the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, then this is the situation.’","As he thought, Chen Yi walked straight toward Hundred Herbs Hall.","Wang Ji was inside the shop. Upon seeing him, he greeted him with a normal-looking smile, \"Shopkeeper Chen, what a rare sight! What brings you to Hundred Herbs Hall today?\"","Chen Yi glanced around and saw quite a few people inside buying tea and medicinal herbs. He smiled and nodded.","\"I have some matters to discuss with Boss Wang. Shall we speak inside?\"","\"Please.\"","Chen Yi followed him inside, but as he did, he raised his hand and made a prearranged signal.","Wang Ji paused for a moment, then nodded with a serious expression. Verbally, he said, \"Shopkeeper Chen, I wonder how the Eldest Miss has been recently?\"","\"Thanks to your good wishes, Boss Wang, Eldest Sister has been in a good mood lately...\""]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107 - 108: Which Son of a Bitch Is Watching Me?","paragraphs":["Ever since the tea beverages became a roaring success in Shu State Prefecture City, the layout of Hundred Herbs Hall had also changed.","The front hall still sold a variety of low-priced medicinal herbs and the five types of tea beverages, but the back hall had been converted into an accounting office where dedicated staff handled the books.","Because profits had to be shared with the various medicine halls throughout Shu State, the account books had to be kept meticulously.","For this reason, Wang Ji had specifically hired ten experienced accountants.","At this moment, the sound of abacuses clacking filled the air.","On the second floor, as before, were two rooms used for receiving visitors.","One was for business, the other for honored guests.","Chen Yi followed Wang Ji into the innermost room.","After taking a seat, he casually surveyed his surroundings. Circulating the True Essence in his body, he deactivated the effects of the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","In an instant, the sounds of dripping rain, footsteps, breathing, and the voices of all sorts of people flooded his senses.","It was a bit noisy, but it also put him more at ease.","’The two people with faint breathing likely had a Cultivation not exceeding the Seventh Grade Realm.’","After listening for a moment, Chen Yi now had a good sense of the few Martial Artists outside Hundred Herbs Hall. Aloud, he said,","\"Thanks to your care, Boss Wang, business at the Xiao Family’s several medicine halls has improved considerably.\"","His finger, however, was dipped in tea water, writing on the table: \"Someone wants to eliminate Hundred Herbs Hall. Make preparations.\"","Wang Ji read it, his expression changing slightly, but he smiled naturally and replied, \"You’re too kind, Shopkeeper Chen.\"","\"Previously, the Young Miss was gracious enough to have me serve as the shopkeeper at Jishi Medicine Hall. Now that circumstances have improved, I naturally wouldn’t dare forget my roots.\"","As he spoke, he also used his finger to write on the table: \"My lord, what do you need me to do?\"","While speaking, Chen Yi wrote in reply, \"Have those Jianghu People arrived in Shu State? What is their strength?\"","\"Most are only at the level of mansion guards. Only two are swordsmen who have roamed the Jianghu for years; their Cultivation is said to be in the Seventh Grade Realm.\"","\"Too weak.\"","\"Then I’ll look for more later.\"","Chen Yi shook his head, writing, \"It’s too late. Those people are practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Illusory Sound Sect.\"","After Wang Ji finished reading, his expression turned grim.","Who in Shu State didn’t know the name of the Illusory Sound Sect these days?","That group had dared to rob even the Xiao Family, and their methods were brutal. Slaughtering his Hundred Herbs Hall, which was just starting to see success, would be child’s play for them.","\"My lord, I’ll do whatever you say.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. After a moment of thought, he wrote on the table, \"Go to the Xiao Family.\"","Wang Ji froze for a second. \"My lord, you mean...?\"","Chen Yi nodded and continued writing, \"Tell Xiao Wan’er that the Illusory Sound Sect plans to move against Hundred Herbs Hall. Seek her protection.\"","\"Also, bring all the silver you took previously.\"","’If he hadn’t just happened to see Shen Huatang arrive with a senior sister from her Sect, he never would have told Wang Ji to do this.’","’The Xiao Family’s current situation was so precarious that one wrong move could bring down the whole enterprise.’","’Even the Old Master was being so cautious, to say nothing of Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wang, and the others.’","’But with Shen Huatang and her senior sister of a higher Cultivation level present, they would stand a chance against the Illusory Sound Sect.’","’According to his deductions, the visitor from the Celestial Sect was likely here for matters concerning the Illusory Sound Sect and the \"Sword Madman,\" Liu Lang.’","’It wasn’t that he was intentionally scheming, either.’","’As for that sum of silver coins...’","’He figured that if Wang Ji didn’t send the money to Xiao Wan’er soon, Ge the Third and Liu Si’er would start getting suspicious.’","’Or perhaps they already suspected his connection to Hundred Herbs Hall.’","After reading, Wang Ji nodded at once. \"I’ll have someone get the silver coins and take them over immediately.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and said aloud,","\"These days, the tea beverages from Hundred Herbs Hall are famous throughout Shu State. We get a lot of customers every day, especially from those few brothels in South City.\"","\"I came today to discuss with you, Boss Wang, whether you might be able to spare some more of those tea beverages for Jishi Medicine Hall in the future.\"","Wang Ji relaxed and replied with a smile, \"I’m afraid I’ll have to disappoint you, Shopkeeper Chen. Forgive me, but my hands are tied.\"","This wasn’t just an excuse.","They had truly reached their limit.","Ever since the tea beverages gained fame in Shu State, dozens of workers packing and shipping them day and night still couldn’t produce enough to supply Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Halls.","Wang Ji was just about to discuss with Yan Hai the possibility of hiring more workers, acquiring a residential compound, and increasing the tea’s production output.","Chen Yi was well aware of Hundred Herbs Hall’s situation, but he said, \"You can save that for the Young Miss, Boss Wang.\"","Wang Ji understood. He cupped his hands and said, \"I will lead a party to pay her a visit shortly. I hope Shopkeeper Chen will help put in a good word for me...\"","The back-and-forth was perfectly coordinated.","Lately, Chen Yi had been quite satisfied with Wang Ji’s performance.","’It was just that his past experiences made it difficult for him to trust anyone completely.’","’He always held something back.’","After their business was concluded, Chen Yi exchanged a few pleasantries before rising to leave.","However, upon reaching the front hall, he paused to pick up some medicinal herbs before opening his umbrella and leisurely strolling toward the East Market.","「Not long after.」","Wang Ji, carrying the silver notes, boarded a carriage and headed straight for the Xiao Family.","Seeing this, a few of the seemingly ordinary passersby and stall vendors who had been hiding nearby glanced around before getting up and walking away.","But just as they left, two more figures appeared in a corner, staring at their retreating backs.","A coarse voice spoke up. \"Brother Ning, why d’you think the Young Master wants us watchin’ this Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","\"How should I know? But Young Master Yi just passed by. I figure the Young Master wants to get his ’revenge’ on him.\"","\"The Young Master is gonna kill Young Master Yi?\"","\"Are you an idiot? I’m sayin’ the Young Master wants to *help* Young Master Yi. Didn’t you hear him say their medicine hall needs tea from Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","\"Oh.\"","\"And next time, just call me ’Brother Ning.’ Don’t copy your Sister Xiu, it sounds so girly.\"","\"Got it, Brother Ning... I mean, Brother Ning.\"","...","「Just before noon.」","Wang Ji left Jiaxing Garden with a relaxed expression.","Not only had a great weight been lifted from his mind, but he had also secured Xiao Wan’er’s promise, so he no longer had to worry about the Illusory Sound Sect for the time being.","With that, he had completed the task Chen Yi had assigned him.","What he didn’t know, however, was that as he was pleading his case to Xiao Wan’er, a woman in a long white dress was in an adjacent room, cracking melon seeds and listening intently.","She was prettier than Shen Huatang, with an oval face, fair skin, and a voluptuous figure.","However, she had a habit of sitting with one foot propped up on the stool, while the other swung back and forth.","Clearly, she was someone who didn’t stand on ceremony.","\"Well, what a coincidence.\"","\"I just get to the Xiao Family, and news of the Illusory Sound Sect shows up... Don’t tell me some son of a turtle’s been tailin’ me?\"","Just then, Shen Huatang entered the room. Seeing her sister’s rough-and-tumble posture, she immediately frowned.","\"Xie Tingyun, this is the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion...\"","Before she could finish, the woman in white had already straightened up, puffing her chest out proudly and glancing sideways at her. \"How’s this?\"","A look of resignation appeared on Shen Huatang’s face. \"Senior Sister, Master’s letter specifically instructed me to teach you some etiquette.\"","The woman named Xie Tingyun waved her hand dismissively. \"I know, I know.\"","\"Let’s go. The Young Miss has sent for you.\"","\"Let’s get a move on...\"","...","「In the afternoon, the sky over Shu State City grew dim.」","The rain, far from letting up, returned to yesterday’s intensity.","As it poured, Jishi Medicine Hall filled with artisans from the East Market.","They all chattered away, trading idle gossip.","Some of it was worth hearing; some was best ignored.","For instance, the local anecdotes and rumors from the Jianghu were worth a listen.","Chen Yi found this quite interesting and would occasionally ask a question or two.","For example, who in the Jianghu had the highest Cultivation.","Nine out of ten would say, \"If you’re talking about the most powerful, it has to be Immortal Bai of the Wind and Rain Tower.\"","\"Listening to the rain from the eaves of the Wind and Rain Tower, he looks upon a Jianghu where he has no equal.\"","\"Immortal Bai has an undefeated record. Even when the Sword Master himself challenged him, they fought for three straight days, and Immortal Bai won by a single move.\"","\"But ever since thirty years ago, when Immortal Bai sealed his ’Mirror Platform,’ no one has heard of him fighting anyone else.\"","Chen Yi found this fascinating and chimed in with a question, \"Is his real name actually Immortal Bai?\"","His question prompted a roar of laughter in Jishi Medicine Hall.","\"Shopkeeper Chen, you don’t follow Jianghu affairs much, do you?\"","\"Are you stupid? Shopkeeper Chen is a scholar. He’s probably one of those who ’only reads the books of sages.’\"","After some joking and teasing, someone finally explained, \"Senior Immortal Bai’s real name is Gongye Bai.\"","\"He got the moniker ’Immortal’ because when he was young, he often dressed up as a fortune-teller and read people’s fates.\"","\"It’s just that, the people whose fortunes he told are all said to have met rather miserable ends.\"","Chen Yi asked curiously, \"How so?\"","\"The better the fortune, the worse the outcome. If he told someone they were destined for ’wealth and honor,’ that person would be reporting to the Underworld within three days, guaranteed.\"","\"The worst case was Fairy Lian Yue. He told her, ’Your marriage is destined by the heavens; a happy event is just around the corner.’ HAHA... She’s still single to this day.\"","\"Then there was the old Daoist of Mang Mountain. His fortune was supposedly ’the descent of the Emperor Star.’ The very next day, his entire Daoist temple on Mang Mountain was massacred...\"","Listening to these amusing anecdotes about Immortal Bai’s fortune-telling, Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh.","’The strange tales of the Jianghu were truly strange in their own way.’","「As evening approached.」","Chen Yi tidied up, took some more herbs from the counter, and was about to leave with his umbrella when he saw Ge the Third arriving in the carriage.","He gave a nod of greeting and climbed into the carriage, his expression natural.","Ge the Third glanced at Jishi Medicine Hall. \"Young Master, why are there so many people inside?\"","\"They’re all taking shelter from the rain,\" Chen Yi said casually.","’He watched the pedestrians on the rain-slicked road outside the carriage, his mind already churning with plots to entrap the blockhead driving the carriage—the one with the thick eyebrows and big eyes, but a heart as black as his methods were ruthless.’","’In any case, he couldn’t possibly let Ge the Third stay idle.’"]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108 - 109: Ah, Earth Level...","paragraphs":["At dinner, Chen Yi met Shen Huatang’s senior martial sister, Xie Tingyun.","Her name was rather elegant.","But she certainly didn’t understand etiquette.","During the meal, she would subconsciously wolf down her food, her eyes fixed on the meat dishes.","Then, after a discreet kick from Shen Huatang, she would put on a reluctant expression, sit up straight, and start taking smaller bites.","Chen Yi wasn’t the only one who noticed; Xiao Wan’er saw it too.","But perhaps because she had interacted with Xie Tingyun during the day, she already had a general impression and found it somewhat amusing.","Of course, this was just an insignificant interlude.","The main topic of conversation during the meal was the Medicine Hall’s business.","Ever since signing the contract with Hundred Herbs Hall, the Xiao Family’s several Medicine Halls had gotten back on track.","Xiao Wan’er had been in a good mood ever since.","The last few times they had eaten together, she had always found a few things to say to Chen Yi.","She would either talk about the Medicine Halls’ recent earnings or how the other Shopkeepers were managing things.","Chen Yi naturally understood her intentions. He knew she wanted to share some of her experience and methods to help him adapt to his new role as a Medicine Hall Shopkeeper as quickly as possible.","Perhaps she also hoped he would manage Jishi Medicine Hall well, which would bring him—and by extension, her—some prestige in front of the Xiao Family.","Most people within the Xiao Family didn’t think highly of Chen Yi. They felt that a scholar like him, serving as a Medicine Hall Shopkeeper, wouldn’t be able to lower himself to cater to customers.","It was a stereotype.","Scholars, farmers, artisans, and merchants—merchants were always looked down upon.","Therefore, Chen Yi wasn’t surprised that the Xiao Family and others who knew his situation would think this way.","Tonight, however, Xiao Wan’er didn’t talk about any of that.","\"Have you noticed anything unusual at Jishi Medicine Hall recently?\" Xiao Wan’er asked while sipping a ginseng soup meant to nourish one’s ’yang fire’.","Chen Yi pretended to think for a moment before shaking his head. \"Nothing unusual. It’s been raining for days, so the shop has been mostly filled with artisans taking shelter.\"","He smiled and changed the subject to an interesting story he had heard that afternoon. \"I heard them say that the most formidable person in the Jianghu is called ’Immortal Bai’.\"","\"He’s known by the saying, ’Listening to the misty rain in the Wind and Rain Tower, he looks up to find himself unrivaled in the Jianghu.’ Eldest Sister, have you heard of him?\"","Xiao Wan’er seemed taken aback by the sudden change of topic. After a slight pause, she said she hadn’t.","Then she looked at Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun. \"Do you two know of him?\"","\"Immortal Bai? How could any Jianghu person not know ’im?\"","Xie Tingyun subconsciously slipped into her Shu State dialect. She glanced at the silent Shen Huatang, then continued in a more proper tone:","\"Immortal Bai is a senior of the Jianghu. He became famous fifty years ago and has always been a legendary figure. I heard he stepped into the Land Immortal Realm long ago.\"","\"With a wave of his hand, he can summon clouds and rain. He has the power to move mountains and fill seas.\"","\"But in recent decades, few have seen him, and there have been no stories of him dueling with anyone in Martial Arts.\"","At this, Xie Tingyun looked at Chen Yi. \"Young Master, you... you’re interested in Jianghu affairs?\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"The artisans were talking about how he reads people’s fortunes. It sounded interesting.\"","Xie Tingyun’s eyebrows shot up, a hint of delight on her face. She was about to speak when she felt a kick under the table and could only clear her throat. \"Mm... it is indeed interesting.\"","She shot Shen Huatang a resentful look and mouthed what seemed to be a few words.","Shen Huatang ignored her and said gravely, \"Miss, what Wang Ji said during the day might be true. We must be on our guard.\"","Xiao Wan’er already had this in mind and nodded. \"Starting tomorrow, you will lead a team to patrol the Medicine Halls.\"","As if feeling her statement was too abrupt, she explained to Chen Yi:","\"Around noon, Wang Ji came to the manor to ask for help. He said the Illusory Sound Sect is planning to make a move on Hundred Herbs Hall and hoped our family could lend a hand.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"No wonder Eldest Sister asked that earlier. But I truly haven’t noticed anything unusual at Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Xie Tingyun was heard muttering under her breath, \"If a scholar like you could notice them, the Illusory Sound Sect would have been wiped out long ago.\"","...","’This woman really is blunt,’ Chen Yi chuckled to himself.","Xiao Wan’er heard her too and said with a smile, \"My brother-in-law is indeed not skilled in Martial Arts.\"","Realizing she had misspoken, Xie Tingyun grimaced. Enduring Shen Huatang’s exasperated gaze, she stood up and bowed.","\"Um, I’ll take a walk around the city tonight and check on the situation around Hundred Herbs Hall and the other Medicine Halls.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded. \"Very well. We are grateful to Fairy Tingyun for traveling a thousand li to be here.\"","\"It’s nothin’, it’s nothin’.\"","Xie Tingyun waved her hand, then paused. After a glance at Shen Huatang, she properly excused herself and left.","Before she left, she also snatched a roasted chicken leg.","Shen Huatang watched her go, then stood up as well. \"Miss, I’ll take some men and go check on her.\"","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment, then nodded. \"In that case, go ahead and notify the Punishment Hall. Tell them to be on alert as well.\"","Shen Huatang bowed and turned to leave.","Chen Yi just watched quietly, finishing the soup in his bowl.","After a moment of silence, he asked, \"The Illusory Sound Sect has reappeared, and they’re targeting Hundred Herbs Hall again. Does this mean someone from the Shu State region is pulling the strings?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement but said vaguely, \"I’m not clear on the specifics. Grandfather and Second Grand-uncle are handling it with the Punishment Hall.\"","\"Brother-in-law, you don’t need to worry about it. Just stay in the manor for the next few days. It won’t be too late to go to the Medicine Hall after everything has calmed down.\"","Chen Yi had planned to do just that. He mimicked Shen Huatang, standing up and bowing. \"I shall obey the Eldest Miss’s command. I will return to Spring Lotus Garden now.\"","Seeing his antics, Xiao Wan’er chided him playfully, \"Even if you don’t leave the manor, you should still pay attention to the Medicine Hall’s business. It’s not like Liu Quan can’t come here to report.\"","Chen Yi nodded with a smile and led Xiao Wuge back to Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wan’er quietly watched the pair, one tall and one small, depart, the smile on her face gradually fading.","She silently lowered her head and drank her ginseng soup, an inexplicable bitterness in her mouth.","「Back at Spring Lotus Garden.」","Xiao Wuge glanced around before whispering, \"Brother-in-law, I’ll tell you a secret.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Sister Xie Tingyun, Sister Huatang’s senior martial sister, she’s really good at martial arts.\"","Chen Yi had long suspected that Xie Tingyun’s Martial Arts were formidable, but he didn’t know the specifics. He asked with a smile, \"You saw?\"","Xiao Wuge nodded repeatedly. \"She can retrieve objects from a distance.\"","As he spoke, he mimed a ’dragon claw’ snatching motion. \"Like this, WHOOSH, and the thing is in her hand.\"","’This seems to be a clever application of True Essence,’ Chen Yi thought pensively.","’Externalizing True Essence? That doesn’t seem to require an exceptionally high level of Cultivation.’","Xiao Wuge, however, was very interested in this. He continued to mime the motion as he followed Chen Yi back to the wooden building. \"It would be great if I were that powerful too.\"","Chen Yi patted his head. \"Once you undergo Bone Marrow Cleansing and Foundation Establishment at age six, you’ll be able to do it too.\"","Xiao Wuge giggled, but his smile soon faded into gloom.","\"When I turn six, I won’t be able to stay in Shu State anymore. I’ll have to go to Jinling.\"","He brought up the old topic again, looking at Chen Yi with hope in his eyes. \"Brother-in-law, are you really not planning to go to Jinling with me?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. Instead of rejecting him outright, he just smiled and said they would see how things were at the manor next year.","It was a rather perfunctory answer, but it still made Xiao Wuge overjoyed.","Chen Yi smiled and asked Xiaodie to take him to wash up.","To his surprise, Xiaodie first brought him a bowl of ginger tea, saying, \"Young Master, the humidity is heavy on rainy days...\"","Chen Yi looked at the steaming ginger tea, didn’t refuse, and drank it all in one go.","Xiaodie happily took the bowl and scurried upstairs with Xiao Wuge.","Chen Yi watched them go, then touched his stomach. His True Essence circulated halfway from his Elixir Field and Sea of Qi, dispelling the warmth of the ginger tea.","’Now that I’m accomplished in Martial Arts, eating too much of certain things is actually detrimental.’","’Especially since I’m skilled not only in Martial Arts, but also the Medical Dao.’","’The yin and yang in the human body must be balanced.’","’Any increase or decrease in yang qi or yin qi will affect the body. One must always be mindful.’","After Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge had gone to bed,","Chen Yi got up and began his Cultivation as usual.","However, he temporarily stopped practicing his Punch, Step, and Spear techniques, dedicating all his time to cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","He didn’t stop until the hour of Zi, late at night, after circulating his energy for a full six cycles.","After carefully comprehending the Profound Mysteries of the Martial Arts Body in his mind, Chen Yi rose to his full height and walked to the window.","By now, the downpour had subsided, leaving only a drizzle.","But the wind was still quite strong, and he could see the blurry silhouette of the distant bamboo forest swaying back and forth.","’The Eighth Grade Realm requires opening the Eight Main Meridians and the Ren and Du Meridians.’","’Now, only the Ren and Du Meridians are left.’","In the two short days since acquiring the Four Symbols Skill, Chen Yi’s Cultivation had progressed by leaps and bounds.","He had gone from the Middle Stage of the Eighth Grade straight to the Upper Stage, and now he was on the verge of Perfection. His progress could only be described as astonishingly fast.","’Once I reach the Seventh Grade, I should be able to unleash the power of the Dragon-slaying Spear.’","As Chen Yi thought this, he made a mental note to find a suitable weapon in the future—preferably something inconspicuous that could be easily concealed.","Before long, the hour of Zi arrived—","[Daily Intelligence · Earth-level Middle Grade: At the first quarter of the hour of Xu, Hundred Herbs Hall was attacked. Significant Opportunities can be obtained.]","Chen Yi glanced at it. \"Earth Level...\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109 - 110: Immortal Drunk","paragraphs":["’Earth Level, huh? Then I have no choice but to go.’","Chen Yi had thought the mastermind behind the Illusory Sound Sect would be more cautious and slow their pace.","He hadn’t expected them to be in such a hurry.","It had been twenty days at most since Hundred Herbs Hall had taken off, and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s business had only been booming again for just over ten days.","Not even a full month had passed, and it wasn’t yet time for Hundred Herbs Hall to share its profits of silver coins with the Xiao Family Medicine Hall. Yet, those people were already itching to cut off the Xiao Family’s source of wealth.","It just went to show how domineering they were.","’The person behind the Illusory Sound Sect... a Liu from Jing State? Or a Liu from Shu State?’","As he thought about it, a slight smile touched Chen Yi’s lips. ’Either way, the name is Liu.’","He glanced at the night outside, took a brief rest, and then got to work.","No matter how much his Cultivation improved in a single day, he would be no match for those Evil Demons from the Illusory Sound Sect.","Rather than waste time on Cultivation, it was better to make thorough preparations to protect himself.","Xie Tingyun, Shen Huatang, and the Xiao Family Punishment Hall would be the ones to intercept the Evil Demons from the Illusory Sound Sect.","’I’m just going to watch the show. I have no intention of revealing myself.’","Fortunately, Chen Yi had made some preparations in advance, so he wasn’t panicking now.","He then took out the medicinal herbs he had brought back from Jishi Medicine Hall and Hundred Herbs Hall. Using the scale, pestle, and other tools kept in the study, he began to process them.","He meticulously ground the herbs into fine powders, carefully placing each one on a separate sheet of Yunsong Paper.","Pile after pile.","It took him a full hour to finish his preparations.","And now for the most crucial step—compounding the drug.","Chen Yi found a cloth to cover his mouth and nose. He then held his breath with the Breath Concealment Technique and sealed his airways with True Essence.","It was no wonder he was being so cautious.","The formula he was about to concoct was one he had spent the last several days specifically researching.","Due to its overwhelming potency, he had named it \"Immortal Drunk.\"","It wasn’t a Poison, but it was more effective than one.","Following the recipe, Chen Yi weighed out each powder and carefully poured them into a clean porcelain basin.","There were thirteen herbs in total. Though they were all common, when combined with the right catalyst, their explosive potency was enough to knock out a Middle Third-Grade Martial Artist.","Whether that meant Sixth Grade, Fifth Grade, or Fourth Grade remained to be seen until he actually used it.","Once all the herbs were in the porcelain basin, Chen Yi took a porcelain vial from his robes and slowly tapped the powder within into the mixture.","This was the very same Knockout Drug he had gotten from Pei Guanli—and the catalyst for his Immortal Drunk.","Instantly, a hazy, pinkish dust that was neither mist nor smoke began to rise.","’It’s done.’","This strange phenomenon matched exactly what Chen Yi had envisioned when he designed the drug.","Without a moment’s hesitation, he poured all the powder from the basin into the porcelain vials he had prepared.","In total, he had produced five vials of Immortal Drunk.","Once he was finished, Chen Yi opened the window, letting the residual powder in the room disperse on the wind. Only then did he let out a long sigh of relief.","He looked at the five porcelain vials on the table, a smile spreading across his face.","Even though he could only use it five times, he was eagerly anticipating the effects of Immortal Drunk.","’Immortal Drunk... Its true power is that it can bypass the protection of True Essence.’","Seeing that it was nearly three in the morning, Chen Yi put away the vials, sat back on his bed, and began cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","Soon, his mind once again entered that profound and mysterious state of chaos.","「The next day」","The two-day downpour finally ceased.","However, the sky remained a hazy gray, showing no signs of clearing.","The evaporating moisture made Shu State City feel faintly hot and muggy.","Some people broke out in a sweat just sitting still, to say nothing of those who were out working.","Thus, after a busy morning, Xiaodie returned to her room to wash up and change into a fresh, dry set of clothes.","She even wrapped cotton bands around her two hair buns to absorb sweat.","She then woke up Xiao Wuge and Chen Yi as usual, and the three of them had breakfast together in the living room.","They had simple but delicious wonton noodles with chili oil.","When Xiaodie saw Chen Yi finish two bowls, both doused in chili oil, she asked in surprise, \"Young Master, you like spicy food?\"","Chen Yi nodded with a smile. \"Shu State’s cuisine is famous throughout the Great Wei. Of course I like it.\"","’Especially hot pot.’","It was just that the Xiao Mansion, being a prominent household, had its own dedicated kitchen that focused mainly on stir-fried and braised dishes.","Breakfast might be simple, but lunch and dinner were extravagant affairs of rare delicacies or exquisite, ornate dishes. There was never anything as simple as hot pot, which couldn’t showcase the chefs’ skills.","Xiaodie studied him skeptically. When she was sure he was serious, she broke into a laugh. \"Young Master, if you like spicy food, you should have told me sooner.\"","\"I thought since you’re from Jiangnan Prefecture, you wouldn’t be used to spicy food.\"","Chen Yi smiled. Thinking of hot pot, an idea struck him. \"At noon, go to the kitchen and have them...\"","’Since I don’t have to go to the Medicine Hall today, I might as well eat something special right here in the mansion.’","He gave her detailed instructions, having Xiaodie write them all down.","Chen Yi then took Xiao Wuge to the pavilion, brought out a chessboard, and prepared to teach him how to play.","He hadn’t even finished explaining the rules when he saw Xiao Wan’er approaching with Cui’er and Juan’er, carrying account books and an abacus.","Xiao Wan’er glanced at them and said with a gentle smile, \"Playing chess? Have I come at a bad time?\"","Xiao Wuge pouted at the sight of her. \"Sister, please, have a seat.\"","Xiao Wan’er patted his head affectionately. \"Jiaxing Garden felt a little deserted today. I hope I’m not bothering you.\"","\"Not at all, not at all...\"","Chen Yi chuckled, placed the chessboard on a nearby bench, and motioned for Xiao Wuge to continue their game there.","He was a little surprised to see Xiao Wan’er, but he didn’t feel she was an intrusion.","After all...","Chen Yi thought of the melody he had heard two nights before. He collected himself and focused on teaching Xiao Wuge chess.","\"The Chess Dao has three great Realms: seeing the game as just a game, seeing the game as more than a game, and finally, seeing the game as just a game again...\"","He wasn’t trying to be profound; this was a genuine insight he’d gained after reaching Minor Success in the Chess Dao.","He himself, however, had only reached the second Realm: ’seeing the game as more than a game.’","His earlier mental exercise of using Shu State as a chessboard was one of the applications of this Realm.","Xiao Wuge took his words to heart without fully understanding them, and then began to familiarize himself with the rules of the game.","The one taught with focus, and the other learned with diligence, making Xiao Wan’er, who was watching from the side, feel a little out of place.","She hadn’t come over simply because \"Jiaxing Garden felt deserted.\"","For some reason, she had felt uneasy all day, as if something momentous was about to happen.","Strangely, however, after coming to Spring Lotus Garden and watching Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge play, her unease had subsided, replaced by a sense of peace.","Xiao Wan’er didn’t understand why, attributing it simply to the garden’s elegant atmosphere.","「As noon approached.」","Xiaodie bustled about, bringing out the hot pot base and having the kitchen staff deliver various ingredients and dipping sauces.","The group gathered around and began to enjoy hot pot right there in the pavilion.","Xiao Wan’er and her maids had never eaten like this before. They found it novel and ate with delight.","\"Is this how they eat in Jiangnan Prefecture?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"This is an authentic Shu State dish. I heard about it from the artisans in the East Market.\"","He wasn’t lying. While hot pot was a rare sight in Shu State Prefecture City, it was quite common in the more remote towns and counties.","It was a convenient way of eating favored by Pullers and Boatmen who were in a hurry to get to work.","Xiao Wan’er nodded as she took small bites. \"It’s delicious.\"","Xiao Wuge was sweating profusely, panting and hissing from the spice.","\"Sister, Brother-in-law, I think my lips are swollen...\"","His complaint made everyone burst out laughing, and the atmosphere was warm and pleasant.","But hearing Xiao Wuge’s casual address, Xiao Wan’er’s face, illuminated by the glow of the pot’s burner, took on a slight blush.","’It should be Eldest Sister and Second Brother-in-law.’","Xiao Wan’er and her party didn’t get up to leave until evening.","Before she left, she specifically warned Chen Yi not to go out for the next few days, lest those villains find an opportunity to harm him.","Chen Yi, of course, nodded obediently, looking the very picture of compliance.","But shortly after nightfall, he feigned exhaustion and sent Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge to their rooms to rest.","He waited until their breathing grew slow and steady.","Chen Yi changed into a long black robe and put on a simple disguise, adding a small mustache.","He checked his reflection in a copper mirror. After confirming that he wouldn’t be recognized at a glance, he took the five vials of Immortal Drunk and slipped out of Spring Lotus Garden.","However, Chen Yi didn’t attempt to cross the middle and front courtyards.","Instead, he cut through the Purple Bamboo Forest and took a detour over a small hill on the other side, heading toward Hundred Herbs Hall.","Though some of the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard were stationed there, the woods were dense.","Under the cover of night, with his current Realm in the Meteor Butterfly Step, he was confident he could sneak out of the Xiao Mansion if he was careful.","About an hour later, Chen Yi arrived at Hundred Herbs Hall.","Following his memory, he walked nonchalantly to a tavern on the edge of the West Market.","It was not yet curfew, and the tavern was bustling with diners, full of life and the smell of cooking.","\"A private room upstairs.\"","\"This way, sir.\"","Chen Yi went to a private room on the third floor overlooking the street. He sat down leisurely, gazed at Hundred Herbs Hall in the distance, and muttered to himself:","’When you’re watching a show, it’s always better to have some peanuts and melon seeds.’"]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110 - 111: Fairy Tingyun","paragraphs":["Shu State City at night possessed a unique beauty.","Especially the bustling West Market.","As the dark clouds gradually dispersed, a full moon hung in the night sky, accompanied by the sparkle of brilliant stars.","The wooden buildings with their flying eaves, built along the streets in and around the West Market, stood in tight, orderly rows like two long dragons stretching for miles.","Lanterns hanging from the eaves cast candlelight of various colors, illuminating the night and making the liveliness of the entire street clearly visible.","Passersby gathered in twos and threes.","There were scholars in long robes with a refined air, portly merchants, and a few Wandering Martial Artists in short tunics carrying weapons.","Ultimately, no one was paying attention to the finer details of their surroundings.","It was Chen Yi, looking down from his high vantage point, who observed every street and alley while sipping his tea.","Even without deactivating his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, he could spot several suspicious individuals lurking around Hundred Herbs Hall with his keen eyesight alone.","For instance, there was an old man running a stall closest to Hundred Herbs Hall.","Although his face was weathered by time, his eyes were exceptionally bright, not at all like those of an old man struggling to get by.","Or the vendor selling candied haws on the street corner, whose gaze was too shifty and body too tense, as if he were ready to strike at any moment.","Then there were the two men hidden in the shadows, one short and stout, the other tall and thin, dressed like beggars.","Their words and actions were indeed convincing, with very few flaws.","It was just that their pairing was far too conspicuous.","Especially the short, stout man, whose complexion was ruddy and radiant.","It was hard for Chen Yi to believe they were real beggars.","But after watching for a long time, he still hadn’t seen any of the Evil Demonic Dao from the Illusory Sound Sect.","He hadn’t spotted Xie Tingyun from the Celestial Sect, or anyone from the Xiao Family Punishment Hall, either.","Seeing that the Hour of the Dog was approaching, Chen Yi focused his attention on the shops near Hundred Herbs Hall.","There was a tailor shop, a rice merchant, an inn, and a place with a sign outside that read: \"Fang Family Water Escort Agency.\"","Upon closer inspection, he noticed something unusual.","To be precise, it was the horse-drawn carriages entering and exiting the Escort Agency.","He could faintly hear the sound of long, deep breaths coming from within the carriages.","The inn also seemed strange, but he couldn’t tell if it was just out-of-town guests or members of the Evil Demonic Dao.","As for whether there were any Martial Arts practitioners whose breathing he couldn’t even detect, that was impossible to determine for now.","Just then, he heard some hushed conversation from the street corner.","The short, stout man said, \"Brother Ning, something’s not right tonight.\"","The tall, thin man, his head drooping, replied, \"Huh?\"","\"Why is everyone walking around carrying packets of meat?\"","\"...Get lost. If you want to eat, we can talk about it when we get back.\"","\"Oh.\"","The short, stout man paused, then added, \"Brother Ning, the smell of that meat isn’t right.\"","Hearing this, the tall, thin man impatiently lifted his head. \"What’s not right about it?\"","\"It stinks of Knockout Drug...\"","At these words, Chen Yi’s expression flickered. He quickly wet a piece of his clothing with water, covered his nose and mouth, and held his breath.","He then saw plumes of white smoke rising from the oil-paper packets carried by the passersby.","It wasn’t just one person or one packet, but a hundred or more of them.","He didn’t know what method they used, but the smoke spread in an instant, blanketing the entire street like a thick fog.","The real pedestrians passing by collapsed to the ground, unconscious.","Even from inside the restaurant where Chen Yi was, he could hear a series of THUDS, mingled with the crisp sound of bowls and chopsticks falling to the floor.","Clearly, many people had fallen for the trick.","Faintly, a curse came from the street corner: \"Dammit, why didn’t you say so sooner?\"","\"Quick, blow the whistle!\"","\"PHEW—\"","As the sharp whistle sounded, Chen Yi stuffed the cotton he had prepared earlier into his ears. He feigned unconsciousness, slumping over the windowsill with his eyes half-open to watch the show.","’I thought those from the Evil Demonic Dao were just brainless thugs who fought head-on. I didn’t expect them to have this kind of plan and preparation.’","’It shows they have some respect for the Shu State Prefecture’s Imprisonment Department and the City Guard Army, fearing them at least a little.’","Then, the sound of a bizarre zither melody, with a strange, winding tune, began to play.","At first, it sounded like the wailing of ghosts and howling of wolves. Upon a second listen...","He wasn’t going to listen a second time. Chen Yi not only had cotton in his ears but had also sealed his ear-related acupoints with True Essence, blocking out most of the sound.","He had heard more than once about the strange methods of the Illusory Sound Sect. He knew those Evil Demons were experts at using melodies to control others, so he had to be on guard.","Next, he saw four figures completely shrouded in black robes rushing over, moving from far to near at high speed.","Their speed was more than double his own Meteor Butterfly Step. Clearly, their Martial Arts Cultivation was higher than his.","In the blink of an eye, the four of them arrived before the entrance of Hundred Herbs Hall.","They held four different musical instruments: a zither, a pipa, a long flute, and a gong.","It was a motley collection, but they were without a doubt deadly weapons.","The zither music was played by one of the black-robed figures. Like the Knockout Drug, it had an effect that could make one drowsy.","Chen Yi watched as they surveyed their surroundings before brazenly walking into Hundred Herbs Hall, and he couldn’t help but sweat for Wang Ji, Yan Sea, and the others.","’I’ve already done what I can. Whether they live or die now depends on the strength of Xie Tingyun and her people.’","Just then, a hoarse voice came from within Hundred Herbs Hall. \"Who goes there?\"","It was followed by a woman’s voice: \"Xie Tingyun of the Celestial Sect.\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. ’So she was already inside Hundred Herbs Hall.’","’She’s reasonably attentive, I suppose.’","’Looks like Wang Ji and the others should be fine then.’","Just as he was thinking this, it seemed Xie Tingyun had already started fighting the people from the Illusory Sound Sect over there.","Amidst crisp whistling sounds, all kinds of melodies filled the air as the zither, flute, gong, and pipa clashed.","\"You sons of bitches from the Illusory Sound Sect, stop playing your damn ghost tunes.\"","\"Keep playing, and believe me, I’ll string your heads together on my sword!\"","The words had barely faded when Chen Yi saw the four black-robed figures who had previously run into Hundred Herbs Hall fleeing in panic.","A Qi Blade followed close behind. With a SWISH, it sliced through one of the black-robed figures, severing his leg.","Blood splattered on the ground, and a row of bluestone pavers was sliced cleanly in two.","Chen Yi’s eyes twitched. He widened them slightly as he stared at the power of that Qi Blade, thinking, ’So this is a Martial Arts Powerhouse? Sword Qi?’","After being in Great Wei for so long, he had finally seen one of the legendary powerhouses of the Jianghu.","Before he could think any further, he saw Xie Tingyun drift out, clad in a long white dress and holding a long sword.","Her feet didn’t touch the ground. As her figure flickered, her long sword traced two \"sword flowers\" in the air.","Several streaks of Sword Qi flew out in succession. Even in the dark of night, the shape of the Qi Blades was clearly visible.","Amidst a series of SWISHES, wherever the Sword Qi passed, everything within ten zhang was cut down.","\"It’s the head disciple of the Celestial Sect, Fairy Tingyun! Retreat!\"","\"Don’t you run now! I have questions for you.\"","\"Did your Illusory Sound Sect’s Elder, Elder Demon Jia, come to Shu State or not? I have a score to settle with him!\"","The Illusory Sound Sect Evil Demons didn’t respond. They fought as they retreated, luring Xie Tingyun further and further away.","Seeing this, Chen Yi was left speechless.","’How could she be so unreliable? Getting led away by such an obvious \"lure the tiger from the mountain\" ploy?’","The person behind all this had deployed so much stupefying smoke; they had clearly come prepared.","Aside from those four Illusory Sound Sect Evil Demons, Chen Yi was certain there were others waiting to deal with Hundred Herbs Hall.","Sure enough, it wasn’t long before...","Another group of people appeared on the street. They were the Wandering Martial Artists who had emerged from the nearby inn.","Judging by their builds, none of them seemed to be weak.","At the very least, Chen Yi hadn’t heard their breathing earlier.","After gathering at the street corner, they charged into Hundred Herbs Hall once more.","But soon after, a group of people also emerged from the other Escort Agency.","\"Take them all down!\"","Chen Yi stared at the person who spoke, slightly stunned. It was his Second Uncle Xiao, Xiao Xuanshuo.","Among the several Armored Warriors behind him were many familiar faces, including Liu Si’er and Wang Lixing.","Hearing this, the Wandering Martial Artists who had entered Hundred Herbs Hall seemed to become alert. \"Careful, it’s an ambush!\"","Immediately, he saw the Xiao Family’s group begin to fight with those Wandering Martial Artists.","But it was clear that Wang Lixing and the others were no match for the Wandering Martial Artists.","Before ten breaths had passed, some were already injured and had fallen to the ground.","\"Useless!\"","The voice rang out, and Second Uncle Xiao was seen slapping his wheelchair. His entire body launched into the air, a long sword already in his other hand as he charged straight into the fray.","Amidst the CLANGING of colliding weapons, his Sword Qi reached a distance of three zhang.","Coordinating with Wang Lixing and the others, Second Uncle Xiao and the few Wandering Martial Artists actually fought to a standstill.","Just as Chen Yi was getting absorbed in the spectacle, his earlobes twitched, and he suddenly half-closed his eyes.","Sometime, without him noticing, two people had come up behind him.","Neither of their breaths was particularly long and drawn-out; one was even somewhat ragged.","However, the intervals between their steps were identical. They were clearly people who practiced Martial Arts.","Listening to the approaching footsteps, Chen Yi tightened his grip on the Immortal Drunk.","’Coming here just to watch the show was a bit reckless, after all.’","’If these newcomers are as powerful as Xie Tingyun, I might be in trouble this time.’","\"Young Master, I didn’t expect Xie Tingyun from the Celestial Sect to be here as well.\"","\"It seems you won’t need to intervene. Hundred Herbs Hall will be safe.\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. ’That voice sounds familiar.’","’Chun Ying?’","’And \"Young Master\" would be...’","Sure enough, he then heard Chen Yunfan say in a displeased tone, \"They’re all just third-rate Jianghu nobodies. I am very disappointed.\"","As he spoke, he glanced at the figure slumped over the windowsill and proceeded to sit down, pour himself some tea, and drink it.","\"Ordering a whole pot of spring tea from Jiangnan Prefecture for one person. This guy really knows how to live.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi made a mental note to put it on his tab. He’d make him pay it back later, with interest.","But listening to their conversation, he felt a flicker of doubt.","’Did Chen Yunfan come all this way specifically to save Hundred Herbs Hall?’","’But why?’"]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111 - 112: My Brother’s Secrets Run Deep","paragraphs":["Chun Ying glanced at the figure by the window, then looked outside Hundred Herbs Hall.","Xiao Xuanshuo was fighting three against one, tying down the three strongest Swordmen.","The remaining Personal Guard Armored Warriors, working in groups of two or three, were more than enough to suppress the other Wandering Martial Artists.","\"Young Master, the people from the Xiao Family Punishment Hall have yet to appear.\"","Chen Yunfan poured another cup of tea. \"The Xiao Family Punishment Hall is in the hands of the Xiao Family’s second branch. It’s a disaster waiting to happen.\"","\"Things are still manageable while the Old Marquis is alive and well, but once he passes, won’t Xiao Wang try to walk all over the first branch?\"","Chun Ying nodded, then shook her head, but did not speak.","Chen Yunfan shot her a look and pursed his lips. \"If you have something to say, just say it. There’s no one else here.\"","Chun Ying hesitated. \"I was just thinking about General Jinghong. Her mind is currently preoccupied with the provisions for the Dingyuan Army.\"","\"If she can successfully establish the Mutual Market with the Mountain Race, she’ll be able to free herself up to deal with the people in the Xiao Family.\"","\"Her?\"","Chen Yunfan thought for a moment, a slight smile appearing on his face. \"She does have some ability. Her Martial Arts and Military Strategy are both quite strong.\"","\"And it’s no small feat for a woman to hold up the Xiao Family’s banner. But because the family is holding her back, her progress in Martial Arts has slowed considerably.\"","Chun Ying deeply agreed. \"Yes, Xiao Fengchun died too soon.\"","\"Not necessarily. Rumor has it that Xiao Fengchun was a blindly loyal fool. He might not have been as good as Xiao Jinghong.\"","\"Of course, if he were alive, he probably could have protected the Xiao Family, and they wouldn’t have ended up being bullied at their own doorstep by the Sixth Young Master of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yunfan’s gaze fell upon the battle outside the window, and he sneered.","\"Right now, that bastard Liu Jing is probably still daydreaming. He has no idea his days are numbered.\"","\"He’s being used as a pawn and doesn’t even realize it. What an idiot.\"","Chun Ying chuckled. \"Young Master, you shouldn’t say such things in the Governor’s Office. Be careful it doesn’t reach Left Envoy Liu’s ears.\"","Chen Yunfan shot her an impatient glare. \"We’re just making idle chat in private. Must you keep nagging me about this and that?\"","\"If you really push me, believe it or not, I’ll send a message to the White Clothes Manor tomorrow and have them send someone new.\"","Chun Ying quickly put on an apologetic smile. \"This servant was wrong.\"","\"Hmph. So now you know you were wrong?\"","\"Young Master...\"","Chen Yi overheard their entire flirtatious banter, which they carried on as if no one else was around.","But his mind was no longer on such things.","’Looks like this brother of mine is hiding his abilities quite deeply.’","’He not only knew that people from the Jing State Liu Family were coming, but he even knew which young master it was—that Liu Jing whose days are numbered.’","’Moreover, Chen Yunfan was clearly aware of the Xiao Family’s situation and knew about the members of the first and second branches.’","’Adding that to his earlier warning outside Luoyi Lane, everything pointed to the fact that Chen Yunfan was not as simple as he appeared on the surface.’","’But...’","Chen Yi still couldn’t guess Chen Yunfan’s intentions.","Even his previous deductions—that Chen Yunfan wanted to deal with the Xiao Family, or that he wanted to replace Yang Ye as the Right Minister of the Shu State Governor’s Office—now had to be questioned.","At that moment, Chen Yunfan and Chun Ying’s conversation stopped, and they both came to the window to look outside.","\"So Elder Demon Jia really did come to Shu State. Heh.\"","\"Young Master, Fairy Tingyun was lured away. The remaining people are surely no match for him. Are you going to intervene?\"","\"No rush. Let’s just watch.\"","During their conversation, Chen Yi also saw the so-called Elder Demon Jia.","He was dressed in a black robe, his figure and face hidden, with only the long xiao flute in his hand being particularly conspicuous.","He appeared from nowhere. Upon seeing Xiao Xuanshuo and the others, he brought the long xiao to his lips.","The sound of a xiao flute drifted out.","The tune was bizarre, identical to that of the four Evil Demons from the Illusory Sound Sect from before.","Then, the few people who had been fighting, including Xiao Xuanshuo, suddenly froze in place.","Their bodies and minds alike turned rigid, as if their very souls had been seized.","Seeing such a strange scene, even though Chen Yi was prepared, he couldn’t help but break out in a cold sweat for the Xiao Family members.","’Have to admit, these Evil Demons from the Illusory Sound Sect really have some skill.’","A moment later, the xiao’s music ceased.","Just as the black-robed man was about to enter Hundred Herbs Hall, he suddenly whipped his head toward the clothing store on the other side.","A cold glint of light shot through the air.","Elder Demon Jia sidestepped to dodge it.","Then, Shen Huatang drifted out from the clothing store and asked in a cold voice, \"Elder Demon Jia, was it you who attacked outside the posthouse earlier?\"","Elder Demon Jia didn’t answer. The eyes hidden beneath his black robe stared at her coldly.","\"The Sword Madman spared you once. You should know to cherish your life.\"","Shen Huatang’s expression grew even colder. With her Long Sword pointed diagonally, she instantly drifted forward, her figure crossing several dozen feet like the wind.","Sword Qi rained down on Elder Demon Jia like snowflakes.","\"If Fairy Tingyun were here, I might be a little wary. But just you? Heh heh...\"","With a cold laugh, Elder Demon Jia stopped playing his xiao. Instead, he used it as a weapon, spinning it twice to block the Sword Intent.","The next moment, his figure shot out like a phantom, thrusting the long xiao forward.","The sound of the xiao flute unexpectedly rang out.","Shen Huatang faltered mid-charge, as if her mind had been captured by the sound, and she was slow to raise her Long Sword.","Just then, something came whistling through the air and, with a CLANG, knocked Elder Demon Jia’s long xiao aside, forcing him to dodge back.","Immediately, he looked toward the tavern where Chen Yi was, his voice hoarse and cold. \"Who’s there?\"","Then came Chen Yunfan’s laughing voice: \"Just an insignificant passerby who can’t bear to see a beautiful woman perish.\"","\"For any offense caused, I hope Elder Demon Jia can be magnanimous.\"","Chen Yi: \"...\"","’Damn, his Martial Arts are that good?’","Apparently, Elder Demon Jia outside didn’t think so. His eyes darkened as he said, \"Come out and die!\"","Chen Yunfan just chuckled again. \"You should worry about yourself first. Fairy Tingyun is here.\"","Before his words had faded, a figure could be seen flying in from the distance, and a sharp cry rang out:","\"Jia Gui’er, you dare bully a little sister from my Celestial Sect?\"","\"Today, my Celestial Firefly Sword is thirsty, and I’m sending you son of a bitch to meet your maker!\"","Elder Demon Jia looked back, fell silent for a moment, then turned and fled in another direction without a word.","Clearly, he knew today’s endeavor was a lost cause and wanted to escape.","\"Running? Jia Gui’er, you get your ass back here!\"","Then, Xie Tingyun drifted down, took one look around, and shot off in pursuit of Elder Demon Jia once more.","Shen Huatang came to her senses. Watching the two fly off into the distance, she cupped her fist in a salute to the surroundings. \"This junior, Shen Huatang of the Celestial Sect, thanks Senior for their life-saving intervention.\"","\"Not at all, not at all! HAHA...\"","The voice boomed, making it impossible for her to tell which direction it came from.","Chen Yi noticed this and inwardly pursed his lips. ’This brother of mine is a real expert at playing the mysterious hero.’","But he also breathed a sigh of relief.","If Chen Yunfan hadn’t acted just now, Shen Huatang would likely be dead at Elder Demon Jia’s hands.","Before long, the Shu State City Guard Army and people from the Imprisonment Department rushed over.","Seeing the state of the area, several orders were shouted:","\"Arrest these Wandering Martial Artists who dare to cause trouble in Shu State!\"","\"Go check for casualties!\"","\"...\"","Chun Ying scanned the area and said, \"Someone must have notified the Imprisonment Department and the City Guard Army in advance.\"","Chen Yunfan grunted in agreement. \"The Shu State Liu Family doesn’t dare to have a complete falling out with the first branch in Jing State yet. They have to show the proper attitude.\"","\"Young Master, now that the show is over, shall we go?\"","\"Indeed, it’s time to go.\"","Chen Yunfan stretched as if bored. \"If I’d known Xie Tingyun was here, why would I have bothered wading into these muddy waters?\"","With that, he turned and left.","Chun Ying followed behind, covering her mouth with her hand as she laughed. \"But Young Master, didn’t you say...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yunfan cut her off. \"Don’t say irrelevant things. Be careful or I’ll have you severely punished.\"","\"This servant will obey the Young Master’s command and shut her mouth.\"","\"Good girl...\"","[Witnessed the ordeal at Hundred Herbs Hall, the appearance of various parties, the Xiao Family learning of the Shu State Liu Family’s existence, the Illusory Sound Sect’s movements being exposed, and their pursuit by a top disciple of the Celestial Sect. Reward: Four Symbols Skill grade increased to Earth Tier, Opportunity +50.]","[Evaluation: You arrived at the scene, heard the key sounds, and witnessed the events. Your actions were limited, but your advance planning was effective. Performance: Satisfactory.]","Seeing the words float before his eyes, Chen Yi finally stood up, stretched his limbs, and prepared to leave.","’The outcome wasn’t bad. At least Hundred Herbs Hall was saved.’","’As for what happens next, we’ll have to see how the Xiao Family deals with the Liu Family.’","Just as he was thinking this, a voice came from behind him. \"My friend, did you have a nice nap?\""]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112 - 113: Charging You Some Interest, That’s Not Excessive, Is It?","paragraphs":["Chen Yi froze at the sound of the voice.","’Chen Yunfan? He didn’t leave?’","’No, that’s not right.’","’He must have left earlier, or the intelligence reward wouldn’t have appeared.’","’So he must have sensed something was wrong and came back.’","’My brother really is sharp-nosed and cautious enough.’","Just as Chen Yi was thinking this, he heard Chen Yunfan’s footsteps behind him.","\"Come on, turn around slowly.\"","\"Let me have a look. Who’s so bold as to hide right under my nose?\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips and said nothing.","As his mind raced, he flung the porcelain vial in his hand backward.","Without waiting to see what would happen, he vaulted out of the restaurant’s window.","Chen Yunfan looked at the vial in his hand and snorted. \"The same trick won’t work on me twice.\"","He clearly hadn’t forgotten being knocked out by a vial of sedative from Pei Guanli.","With that thought, Chen Yunfan zipped after him in pursuit.","But just as he reached the window, he heard the porcelain vial shatter, and a strange pink glimmer drifted before his eyes.","Confident that his True Essence was protecting him, Chen Yunfan wasn’t afraid of any poison, so he paid it little mind.","He kept his eyes on the distant figure and vaulted out as well.","Who would have known that the moment he landed, just as he was about to use a Body Technique, his legs would give way?","He staggered two steps.","His eyes immediately glazed over, and then he fell backward as if drunk.","THUMP.","\"You... what... what the hell is this stuff...?\"","In his daze, Chen Yunfan’s mind was still reeling with confusion.","’Dammit, what kind of sedative is this powerful? Even a shield of True Essence can’t block it?’","’Now Chun Ying is going to laugh me to death...’","Hearing the commotion, Chun Ying cried out in alarm and rushed over to check on him.","She breathed a sigh of relief only after confirming he had just passed out.","\"Ning Yu, Niu Mountain, come help me, quick!\"","A tall man and a short man answered the call, running over to carry Chen Yunfan away on their backs.","Naturally, the commotion on their side attracted the attention of the Imprisonment Department, the City Guard Army, and the Xiao Family’s group.","\"Who’s over there?!\"","\"Stop!\"","Obviously, neither Chen Yi nor Chen Yunfan’s group had any intention of obediently stopping.","\"After them!\"","Immediately, the men from the Imprisonment Department and the City Guard Army outside Hundred Herbs Hall gave chase, along with several members of the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard.","Shen Huatang had intended to follow, but fearing it was a ploy to lure the tiger from the mountain, she had no choice but to remain inside Hundred Herbs Hall.","During the pursuit, the tall, thin man carrying Chen Yunfan asked, \"Did the young master get hit with a sedative again?\"","\"It seems so.\"","Chun Ying was still puzzled.","’I clearly saw the young master hadn’t retracted his True Essence, so how could he still be taken down by a sedative?’","As she ran, Chun Ying looked at the porcelain vial she had just taken from Chen Yunfan’s hand, thinking she would find someone to study it later.","A sedative that could even take down a Third-Grade Martial Arts Powerhouse was a rare sight in the entire Great Wei Dynasty.","Then, Chun Ying thought of the vial’s owner, which gave her a bit of a headache.","’That person must have overheard my conversation with Chen Yunfan.’","At this, Chun Ying immediately gave an order, \"Brother Ning, you go track that Wandering Martial Artist who ran from the restaurant. You must find him.\"","\"Alright.\"","Ning Yu nodded, handed Chen Yunfan over to the short, stocky man, and his figure instantly transformed into a shadow, vanishing in the direction Chen Yi had fled.","Chun Ying watched him disappear into the distance and sighed for some unknown reason.","’I hope that person has no connection to the Liu Family.’","’If he’s from the Shu State’s Liu Family, I’m afraid the young master will face some trouble during his time in Shu State.’","Meanwhile, Ning Yu didn’t think that far ahead.","He charged straight toward the men from the Imprisonment Department, the City Guard Army, and the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard.","\"How audacious!\"","Seeing this, Wang Lixing roared as he thrust his long spear straight at him.","Ning Yu had no intention of getting entangled in a fight. He slapped the long spear aside with his palm and bypassed the group to continue toward Chen Yi’s position.","\"Don’t run!\"","An Imprisonment Officer gave chase on horseback, slashing with his long blade.","Ning Yu ducked to avoid it, and catching sight of his attacker, he stomped his foot and launched himself onto the horse.","He immediately sent the Imprisonment Officer flying with a palm strike and galloped away on the horse.","Wang Lixing watched in frustration as the men from the Imprisonment Department and City Guard Army chased after the horseman. After a moment’s thought, he continued pursuing Chun Ying’s group of three with his personal guards.","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi was also fleeing with great speed.","However, he didn’t dare run toward Wudong Street.","The Shu State Governor’s Office, the Prefect’s residence, and the Imprisonment Department were all located there.","If he ran in that direction, he would only encounter more powerful experts.","Therefore, after running past Hundred Herbs Hall, he turned north and ducked into a network of small alleys.","Along the way, he made sure to find a piece of cloth to cover his face, lest his disguise fall off as he ran.","At this point, the men from the Imprisonment Department and the City Guard Army were unable to follow on horseback through the narrow alleys, leaving only Liu Si’er and his men in hot pursuit.","But as they gave chase, they discovered that the man ahead of them was far faster, his Body Technique far superior to their own.","\"Brother Si, we’re going to lose him if this keeps up.\"","Liu Si’er didn’t respond, instead flinging the long spear from his hand.","SWOOSH!","Chen Yi sidestepped to dodge, and a long spear streaked past his eyes, embedding itself in the wall at the end of the alley.","The corner of his mouth twitched. ’That was a ruthless move, Liu Si’er.’","It was clear now that he had run into a dead end.","Without a second thought, Chen Yi pivoted, his hand gripping the spear’s shaft, and pulled it free with a slight tug.","Instantly, a strange sense of familiarity flooded his body.","\"Huuu...\"","Chen Yi let out a soft breath, half-turned, and faced the pursuing members of the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard and the distant figures from the Imprisonment Department, holding the spear in one hand.","’They’re easier to deal with than Chen Yunfan, at least.’","Seeing this, Liu Si’er raised a hand, signaling the others to be on alert, his eyes fixed on the black-clad man before them.","\"I suggest you surrender peacefully. Otherwise, your fate will be even worse.\"","Chen Yi’s voice was hoarse. \"Try me.\"","As his voice fell, the night sky, which had been somewhat bright, seemed to be affected. Dark clouds gathered rapidly.","Then, a light drizzle began to fall, carried on a gust of wind that swirled through the alley.","Amidst the WHOOSHING of the wind, Chen Yi’s long robes whipped about.","The next moment, he moved.","He took a step, and an immense power surged through it, instantly shattering the stone paving beneath his foot.","The long spear became like a great dragon, crossing ten feet in an instant, its cold tip aimed straight for Liu Si’er’s face.","\"You have some nerve!\"","Liu Si’er had fought for many years with the Dingyuan Army. Facing this spear thrust, not only did he feel no fear, but his blood began to boil with excitement.","As True Essence circulated through his body, he took a long spear from the personal guard beside him.","He brought his spear up horizontally to block.","CLANG.","After the sharp sound, Liu Si’er’s long spear was pierced straight through by the single thrust.","Moreover, an enormous force traveled up the shaft, sending him flying backward uncontrollably.","A look of horror crossed Liu Si’er’s face. He slammed his feet into the stone ground, coming to a screeching halt.","\"You...\"","Before he could say more, Chen Yi’s long spear was already in motion. With a flick of his wrist, he executed several flourishes, sending the other three Armored Warriors flying.","Even without using True Essence, his current Power was still enough to knock the Ninth Grade Realm Armored Warriors unconscious.","Seeing this, Liu Si’er gritted his teeth and charged again, thrusting with his broken spear and roaring, \"Kill!\"","The few Imprisonment Officers and City Guard Army soldiers behind him had also caught up and charged forward without hesitation.","In response, Chen Yi’s eyes remained calm. He lowered his stance slightly, gripping the end of the long spear with both hands.","After gathering his strength for a moment, he pushed off the tips of his toes, launching himself forward like a shot arrow.","This time, however, he didn’t restrain his True Essence with the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique. Instead, he unleashed it without reservation.","In an instant, the True Essence from his two Seas of Qi flooded his entire body.","—Dragon-Falling Spear: Zhaoqing Mountain!","Where the spear passed, the wind rose.","The surrounding raindrops strangely hung suspended in mid-air.","Only the deceptively fast long spear passed gently through the curtain of rain, as crisp and refreshing as a soft breeze blowing over a green mountain.","In the blink of an eye, Chen Yi’s figure appeared behind them.","Liu Si’er and the others suddenly halted their forward charge.","In the shadows, their eyes all widened in disbelief.","\"Spear... Spear Dao... How can an Eighth Grade...\"","Before he could finish, Liu Si’er’s left hand, which was holding the broken spear, snapped unnaturally, as if it had just been struck by a colossal force.","He then collapsed to the ground, unconscious.","Most of the other City Guard Army soldiers and Imprisonment Department men suffered the same fate.","Their conditions were slightly better than Liu Si’er’s; at least there was no audible crack of breaking bones.","Chen Yi glanced back, his eyes shimmering brightly.","After assessing the situation, he calmed the True Essence in his body and wiped his fingerprints from the long spear with the corner of his sleeve.","\"You’ve been tailing me for so long. It’s only fair I collect some interest, right?\"","He then tossed the long spear aside, leaped over a few rooftops, and sped toward Spring Lotus Garden.","「A short while later.」","The rain grew heavier, drumming down on Liu Si’er and the others.","Liu Si’er’s eyes shot open. The moment he sat up, he coughed up a mouthful of blood, his body slumping weakly.","He felt as if every inch of his body was in pain.","Especially his left hand.","Enduring the severe pain, Liu Si’er clutched his broken left arm and struggled to his feet, scanning his surroundings.","Once he confirmed that the man was gone and that none of his companions were in mortal danger, he slid down against the wall to sit.","His eyes were filled with viciousness.","\"Who was it?\"","\"Someone from the Liu family? The Xiao family? Or one of the other Noble Families and Clans?\"","Names floated through his mind, only to be dismissed one by one.","’It wasn’t one of the Liu family. If it were their people, they would have made a move on Hundred Herbs Hall earlier instead of hiding and watching the show.’","’It wasn’t one of the Xiao family either.’","’The Xiao Family has very few Martial Artists with that level of Spear Technique, and I know who they all are.’","After much thought, Liu Si’er guessed the man was probably a scout sent to Hundred Herbs Hall by one of the other Noble Families and Clans in Shu State.","\"Good. Very good!\"","\"You’d better hide in a ditch and never show your face again!\"","\"Otherwise, my White Tiger Guard will hunt you down!\"","As Liu Si’er was thinking this, he saw a figure run into the alley entrance. His tense spirit finally relaxed, and he fell unconscious once more.","「Not long after.」","Ning Yu arrived.","His expression was grim as he looked at the Imprisonment Officers and others lying on the ground. His gaze fell upon the long spear.","\"Spear Dao...\""]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113 - 114: A Lot to Look Forward To","paragraphs":["The general term \"Martial Arts\" did not involve Dao Intent.","Or, to be more precise, a Mental Realm.","Only Martial Arts Techniques could enter the Dao—Fist, Blade, Sword, Spear, and even the physical body itself.","This could manifest a Mental Realm, similar to the splendor of the Calligraphy Dao, to enhance the power of a Martial Cultivator’s techniques.","But getting a technique to enter the Dao was no easy feat.","This was especially true for Martial Artists in the Lower Three Grades Realm. Their bodies, True Essence, and techniques were all still in the foundational stages, making it utterly impossible to touch upon a realm where ’technique approaches the Dao.’","Even prodigies of the highest caliber often only had a chance for their techniques to enter the Dao after their cultivation reached the Middle Three Grades, when they could leverage their connection to the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi.","Yet at this moment, as Ning Yu surveyed the scene before him, his mind was reeling from a tremendous shock.","His gaze fell on Liu Si’er. It wasn’t hard to see that his injuries had been caused by being grazed by Spear Intent.","’It’s very faint, but it’s definitely ’Spear Intent.’ That means the man’s Spear Technique has already entered the Dao. But his cultivation...’","An experienced Martial Artist could use their True Essence to probe the fluctuations of the surrounding Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi, and from that, deduce the cultivation of the person who had fought here.","It wasn’t precise, providing only a rough range, but it was enough for Ning Yu to reach a conclusion.","’His cultivation is only in the Lower Three Grades!’","Having reached this conclusion, Ning Yu leaped onto a nearby roof. He paid no mind to the terrified commoners inside the house, instead gazing into the distance.","’To the north...’","After a moment’s thought, he decided against giving chase. He turned, took the Long Spear Chen Yi had used, and headed back the way he came.","A Martial Artist in the Lower Three Grades Realm with such peerless talent in both Martial Arts and the Spear Dao was not someone he could handle.","Besides, he needed to inform the Young Master of this matter as soon as possible.","Before long, several more people arrived.","Upon seeing Liu Si’er and the others lying unconscious on the ground, a shout echoed through the alley:","\"They’re here!\"","\"Someone, quickly! Take them to a Medicine Hall for treatment!\"","...","「About half an hour later.」","Chen Yi returned safely to the Spring Lotus Garden.","Only after seating himself at the eight-immortals table in his room did he finally let out a long breath.","’That was truly dangerous. I almost didn’t get away.’","If Chen Yunfan had been just a little more cautious, even the Immortal Drunk wouldn’t have helped.","In that case, his identity, Martial Arts Cultivation realm, and everything else would have surely been exposed.","Furthermore, if the Imprisonment Department, City Guard Army, and Xiao Mansion Armored Warriors outside Hundred Herbs Hall had been any stronger, the result would have been the same.","His safe return was owed, in no small part, to luck.","Chen Yi recalled the night’s events, a doubt creeping into his heart.","’When did Chen Yunfan start practicing Martial Arts? How did he get so strong?’","He searched his mind for a moment but found no relevant memories.","That being the case, either Chen Yunfan had started practicing Martial Arts in the last five years, while the original owner of this body was imprisoned, or Chen Yunfan had been cultivating in secret since childhood to have possibly reached his current realm.","However, regardless of which was true, he could easily deduce one thing—the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family was far more mysterious than he had previously understood.","Whether it was seeing the whole from a small part or just glimpsing a piece of the puzzle, the heir to a Noble Family with a legacy spanning several hundred years practicing Martial Arts could only be at the behest of the family itself.","’The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, the Qinghe Cui Family...’","Mumbling this a few times, Chen Yi suddenly recalled the conversation he had overheard at the restaurant.","It wasn’t just Chen Yunfan who was secretive; the maid, Chun Ying, who followed him also seemed to be more than she appeared.","’White Clothes Manor... people from the Jianghu?’","Chen Yi looked out at the wind and rain, shaking his head to himself.","He knew too little right now. For the time being, he could only suppress these questions and hope to find more clues in the future.","With this thought, Chen Yi’s mind calmed. He stood up, shed the black robe soaked by the rain, cleaned off his disguise, and went to fetch water to wash up.","Fortunately, his gains tonight were decent.","The Four Symbols Skill had been upgraded to the Earth Tier, enough to support his cultivation all the way to the Upper Three Grades Realm.","He had another hundred Opportunity Points, which meant he could raise another Dao to Great Success.","And there was also the information on the whereabouts of the Liu Family of Jing and Shu States, and Evil Demons like the Illusory Sound Sect. That was also a gain.","As long as the Xiao Family seized this opportunity, they could use the clues he’d uncovered tonight to resolve the crisis with their medicine halls.","As for whether the Old Master would make a move...","...he had no way of knowing.","After washing up, Chen Yi changed into a set of clean clothes and went to the window to look outside.","With a simple contraction and release of the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, the situation within the Spring Lotus Garden became clear in his mind.","There were no anomalies.","Chen Yi relaxed and sat on his bed to begin cultivating the Four Symbols Skill.","After the fight with Liu Si’er and his men, he had a clear understanding of his own strength.","He should be comparable to a Seventh Grade Realm Martial Artist whose techniques had not yet entered the Dao.","To have made such progress in his cultivation in just over two months was undeniably fast.","But compared to the likes of Xie Tingyun and Elder Demon Jia whom he had witnessed tonight, his Martial Arts were still far too weak.","’Cultivate, cultivate... I must cultivate!’","Right now, he was only one step away from the Seventh Grade Realm: opening his Ren and Du Meridians.","He estimated that a few more days would be enough.","By then, if he also raised his Spear and Fist to the Great Success Realm, he should be able to hold his own against a Sixth Grade Realm Martial Artist using techniques like the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique and the Mountain Shattering Fist.","It had to be said, he had a lot to look forward to.","...","「Just past midnight, a fine, dense rain was still falling.」","The Xiao Mansion, however, was once again brightly lit.","The incident outside Hundred Herbs Hall had not only alerted the Shu State Prefecture, the Imprisonment Department, and the City Guard Army, but had also alarmed the Xiao Family.","Xiao Xuanshuo hurried back, heading straight for the Qingjing Residence.","Second Master Xiao Wang and Third Master Xiao Shen arrived one after the other, seemingly intending to discuss the matter overnight.","During this time, representatives from the Xiao Mansion Armored Warriors, the Shu State City Guard Army, and the Imprisonment Department all came to the Xiao Family to pay their respects to the Old Master.","Even Xiao Wan’er, who had just fallen asleep, was startled awake by Shen Huatang’s rushed return.","Without a second thought, Xiao Wan’er dressed properly and asked, \"Did you catch the people from the Illusory Sound Sect?\"","Shen Huatang nodded, then shook her head. \"Five people from the Illusory Sound Sect came tonight. Senior Sister killed four of them, and one other...\"","She paused, then corrected herself. \"No, actually, six people escaped.\"","Among the six who fled, one was Elder Demon Jia of the Illusory Sound Sect.","However, Xie Tingyun hadn’t returned yet, so she was likely still tracking him.","The second was the man in black who had injured Liu Si’er and the others.","The remaining four were a few Wandering Martial Artists with stronger Martial Arts.","Shen Huatang felt a pang of regret for not having followed; otherwise, she might have been able to catch one or two of them.","After finishing her report, Shen Huatang continued, \"The Second Master captured several Wandering Martial Artists. They’re currently being interrogated in the Punishment Hall’s dungeons.\"","Xiao Wan’er knew she was talking about Xiao Xuanshuo and asked, \"Have they found out who’s behind them?\"","Shen Huatang shook her head. \"We’ll have to wait for the results of the interrogation.\"","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment, then nodded lightly. \"As long as Hundred Herbs Hall is safe, that’s what matters.\"","The Xiao Family’s few medicine halls had just started to show improvement, which meant she no longer had to worry about the mansion’s monthly allowance.","The last thing she wanted was for something to happen to Hundred Herbs Hall.","As long as they could maintain the current situation, and with the silver coins sent by Wang Ji, not only could the Xiao Family make it to the end of the year, but she might even have extra money to send to her younger sister to fund the \"Mutual Market.\"","Xiao Wan’er pulled her cloak tighter around herself. \"You’ve had a long day. Go get some rest.\"","\"Anything else can wait until tomorrow.\"","Shen Huatang acknowledged with a \"Yes,\" then bowed and exited the room.","Xiao Wan’er watched her go to the next room, then turned her gaze thoughtfully to the rain falling outside the window.","Although the Old Master had been vague, she knew that some of Shu State’s Noble Families were involved in the robbery of the medicinal herbs.","Now that the Illusory Sound Sect had shown itself, the people from the Punishment Hall should be able to find clues leading to whoever was behind this.","Thinking of this, a smile appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face. \"This matter is finally coming to a resolution.\"","Tomorrow, she would write a letter and share the good news with her younger sister.","She wondered if her younger sister had received the letter she and her brother-in-law had sent earlier.","Calculating the days, a reply should have arrived by now.","Xiao Wan’er’s gaze shifted slightly from the window toward the Spring Lotus Garden, and the smile on her face slowly faded.","’Tomorrow, I’ll have my brother-in-law write a letter to send along as well...’"]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114 - 115: This Blade Is the Price for Your Insubordination","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, a thousand li south of Shu State Prefecture City, deep within a dense forest.","A clearing a hundred zhang wide had been carved out of the woods. Some trees were cut down to stumps, others were uprooted completely, and the ground had been leveled.","The area was illuminated by surrounding bonfires.","Within the clearing, dozens of temporary wooden huts stood in neat rows.","Hanging on the outer wooden fence were the red banners of the Xiao Family and wolf-head carvings of the Wumeng Mountain Race.","Several of the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard, clad in black armor, were patrolling the perimeter.","It was late at night, but Xiao Jinghong was not resting.","She was at her desk handling official business, her eyes beneath the half-armor mask as calm as still water. The wolf hair brush in her hand would either circle a passage or jot down a few words.","She worked quickly.","Lately, she had been overseeing the survey and design plans for the Mutual Market, which meant she could only handle the Dingyuan Army’s affairs late at night.","Fortunately, Su Zhenyue was there to help, organizing the documents by urgency ahead of time so that Xiao Jinghong could manage everything.","Otherwise, delaying these matters for even a few days would be detrimental to both the Mutual Market and the Dingyuan Army.","After an hour of work, Xiao Jinghong finished all the official documents. She checked them one last time to ensure nothing was missed before finally standing up and calling out,","\"Zhenyue.\"","Outside, Su Zhenyue, who had also been writing at a desk, heard the call and hurried in.","Xiao Jinghong pointed to four stacks of booklets on her desk and gave her instructions.","\"These four are about the summer harvest. Take them to Yan Hong and have him deliver them to the Capital Commandery tonight, without fail.\"","\"As for the training of the New Army in the Profound Armor, Iron Wall, and Cang Lang Three Towns, a carrier pigeon will suffice. Tell them not to slack off, and that I will inspect them personally once I’m finished here...\"","Su Zhenyue noted everything down, then gathered the booklets from the desk and hurried out.","After she left, Xiao Jinghong sat back down at her desk. She picked up a cold, hard pastry and ate it in small bites, washing it down with tea.","Though her expression was calm, her mind was still swirling with various matters.","Most of her thoughts were on building the Mutual Market with the Mountain Race, a smaller portion on the Dingyuan Army, and the rest on the Xiao Family.","The site for the Mutual Market had been chosen, and the contract with the Mountain Race was settled. Once the blueprints were drawn up, construction could begin in earnest.","With the combined strength of the Dingyuan Army and the Mountain Race, it would take less than half a year to attract merchants from all over Shu State, and even from the prosperous Jiangnan and Capital Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty.","By then, the Dingyuan Army would no longer need to worry about funds and provisions.","As for the Xiao Family...","Xiao Jinghong put the last piece of pastry in her mouth. After chewing it slowly, she took two letters from her robes.","One was signed \"Chen Yi,\" the other \"Chen Qingzhou.\"","She spread the two letters out on her desk. The one on the left was the first letter Chen Yi had sent her, which contained a poem titled \"Thoughts of a Summer Night.\"","The one on the right, she had received just a few days ago.","It also contained a poem, this one titled \"Two Thoughts on a Summer Night.\"","\"Last night, the stars; last night, the wind. West of the Painted Tower, east of the Cassia Hall. We have no rainbow-phoenix wings to fly as one, yet our hearts are linked in perfect understanding.\"","Xiao Jinghong gazed at the elegant, glowing script of \"Two Thoughts on a Summer Night,\" and the weariness that had settled in her mind over the past days began to ease.","Still, she found Chen Yi’s casual approach to naming his poems somewhat amusing.","’Since this one is \"Two Thoughts,\" why wasn’t the previous one \"One Thought\"?’","’My husband was probably just being lazy.’","Xiao Jinghong had guessed correctly. When Chen Yi named the poem, he had indeed been too lazy to think of a new title.","But even so, she didn’t mind.","’In any case, the feeling of this poem is beautiful.’","’Our hearts are linked in perfect understanding...’","Xiao Jinghong sighed softly. Right now, her mind was completely focused on the Dingyuan Army, so when it came to Chen Yi...","Just then, her thoughts were interrupted. Her eyes turned cold as she looked outside the hut.","\"You have come three times. What is your business?\"","Her voice was soft, not disturbing the rest of the camp, yet it carried ten li to the ears of a Wandering Martial Artist with a long blade hanging at his waist.","It was none other than the \"Sword Madman,\" Liu Lang.","At that moment, he gazed at the fire-lit camp in the distance, his expression no longer casual as it had been in Shu State Prefecture City, but solemn.","\"Forgive me, General Jinghong.\"","Liu Lang spoke in a serious tone. \"Although I have come three times, I had not made up my mind until just a moment ago.\"","In fact, he had found Xiao Jinghong five days ago.","He had intended to challenge her directly.","But the first time he saw her, the mere sight of her eyes—as tranquil as an old well—made him lose his nerve.","At that moment, a voice echoed in his mind— ’Don’t attack her. You’ll die!’","’You will definitely die!’","Liu Lang believed it without a doubt.","He trusted his intuition; it was the secret to how he had run rampant across the Northern Desert for so long.","So, that first time, he had retreated without saying a word.","But after two days of deep thought, Liu Lang couldn’t accept leaving without making a single move.","So he came a second time.","Again, he only took one look.","Again, his body trembled uncontrollably.","Having no other choice, Liu Lang retreated once more.","Until this very moment.","When Xiao Jinghong finally spoke to him, Liu Lang still couldn’t suppress the fear in his heart.","He couldn’t help but find himself ridiculous.","He was called the \"Sword Madman,\" yet when faced with an opponent he truly could not defeat, even his blade grew fearful.","As he thought this, he gritted his teeth and continued, \"General Jinghong, will... will you accept my...\"","...challenge!","But no matter how hard he tried, that final word felt like a great mountain pressing down on him, impossible to speak.","Just then, Xiao Jinghong’s voice echoed around him. \"You wish to challenge me?\"","Liu Lang felt his tension ease, and he prepared to nod and say yes.","But the result left him dejected—his own body refused to let him nod, refused to let him speak.","A long silence followed.","Liu Lang gave up. Just as he was about to retreat, a figure appeared before him.","It was Xiao Jinghong, dressed in snow-white robes and wearing her mask!","Liu Lang froze. \"You... you...\"","Xiao Jinghong stood atop a tree branch, holding neither a sword nor a long spear, and simply watched him calmly.","After looking him up and down, she said lightly, \"I’ll give you one chance. Draw your blade.\"","Liu Lang opened his mouth. \"I... I...\"","His hand moved toward the long blade at his waist, as slow as that of a withered old man.","But veins bulged on the back of his hand, and the True Essence within him circulated madly as he tried to gather his strength.","Without even realizing it, his goal had shifted from challenging Xiao Jinghong to simply drawing his blade.","’Just one strike! That would be enough!’","Steeling his resolve, Liu Lang’s face twisted into a crazed snarl as he roared.","\"AHH!!\"","His hand finally closed around the hilt, and he drew the blade with a fierce tug.","A single strike, one that condensed his life’s work and contained all his strength, was finally unleashed—","A flash of blade light, like a bolt of white silk, shot out a hundred zhang.","Its Sword Intent shone like moonlight, illuminating the entire area.","The wrinkled bark of the trees and their tender green leaves became clearly visible.","Anything in the path of the blade’s edge was cleaved in two.","But in the next moment—","\"CRACK!\"","A crisp sound echoed.","Xiao Jinghong had caught the long blade between two fingers, easily snapping it and holding the broken piece steady.","\"Is that all?\"","\"I...\"","Before Liu Lang could finish, Xiao Jinghong flicked her finger. The shard of the broken blade arced like a crescent moon, grazing his chest before sinking into the earth below.","In an instant, the storm in the forest seemed to cease.","No wind, no rain, no sound.","Xiao Jinghong glanced at him and said calmly, \"This cut is the price for your insubordination.\"","\"Get lost.\"","With that, Xiao Jinghong turned and headed back to her camp.","She was a General of Great Wei, not one of the Jianghu People.","If Liu Lang hadn’t spoiled her mood, she wouldn’t have even bothered to strike back.","\"Wait, wait...\"","Just then, Liu Lang seemed to snap back to his senses. He looked at the broken blade on the ground, then at the blood seeping from his chest, and said,","\"You... you’re not going to kill me?\"","\"I... I robbed your Xiao Family, their medicinal herbs...\"","Xiao Jinghong paused.","After a moment of silence, she said without turning back, \"Next time you see your master, send him my regards.\"","\"Ma-master?\"","Liu Lang’s eyes widened as if he had realized something. \"You... you...\"","Xiao Jinghong ignored him, her figure flickering away into the night.","Liu Lang opened his mouth but said nothing more. He simply stared blankly at the treetop where she had stood, letting the blood flow freely from his chest.","Rain began to patter down through the forest, and gusts of mountain wind howled.","He stood there, stunned, for a long time.","Liu Lang’s gaze fell upon the distant camp, and he suddenly shouted.","\"General Jinghong, Liu Lang will one day repay the mercy you’ve shown me with this strike!\"","\"And another thing! The ones who sent me to steal the medicinal herbs were the Liu Family of Jing State!\"","\"They’re planning to move against the Xiao Family Medicine Hall soon!\"","A single word drifted back from the distance: \"Understood...\""]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115 - 116: I’m Scared...","paragraphs":["Xiao Jinghong watched Liu Lang stagger away, then returned inside and sat down.","What Liu Lang said weighed on her mind.","Although she had previously guessed that a Shu State Gate Valve was responsible for seizing the medicinal supplies, she had never considered the Liu Family as the main culprit.","Even her grandfather hadn’t explicitly mentioned it in his letter.","She pondered for a moment.","Realizing her grandfather’s intentions, Xiao Jinghong let out a long sigh.","’Grandfather must be waiting for news from my end.’","With that thought, she glanced at the two letters on the table before picking up another pastry and popping it into her mouth.","Her thoughts jumped back to an earlier moment.","’Now, where was I?’","’Oh, right.’","’Because of the matter with the Dingyuan Army, her feelings for Chen Yi had...’","\"My Lady.\"","Just then, Su Zhenyue came running over in a hurry.","A flicker of resignation crossed Xiao Jinghong’s eyes as she waved a hand, tucking the two letters and poems into her robes.","\"Has everything been arranged?\"","\"It’s all taken care of. Yan Hong has already set out. He should arrive at the Capital Commandery by noon the day after tomorrow.\"","As she spoke, Su Zhenyue noticed the damp patches on Xiao Jinghong’s clothes and couldn’t help but ask with some confusion,","\"My Lady, were you just outside?\"","Xiao Jinghong hummed in affirmation. \"Senior Sword Ghost’s closed-door disciple was just here. He’s gone now.\"","Su Zhenyue paused, slightly taken aback. \"Sword Ghost? Is his disciple that ’Sword Madman,’ Liu Lang?\"","\"The very same.\"","\"He didn’t come to challenge you, did he?\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded, her tone flat. \"Unfortunately, his Dao doesn’t lie solely with the blade. He’s also distracted by the Spear Dao, which makes him somewhat uninteresting.\"","Su Zhenyue chuckled, covering her mouth. \"Perhaps he wishes to emulate you, My Lady, but his talent is too limited for him to achieve much.\"","\"Still, the fact that he came to challenge you means Senior Sword Ghost didn’t reveal your identity to him.\"","\"Whether he revealed it or not is all in the past now.\"","Xiao Jinghong didn’t dwell on it, instead instructing, \"Go bring some more food.\"","Su Zhenyue took her leave.","Xiao Jinghong watched her go, then once again took the two letters from her robes.","She didn’t open them, however. Her thoughts merely continued from before: ’I truly have wronged my husband.’","She fell silent for a moment.","Xiao Jinghong recalled what Liu Lang had said just moments ago. ’The Jing State Liu Family will be sending people to make a move against the Xiao Family Medicine Hall soon.’","’I remember Elder Sister’s letter mentioned that business at our Medicine Halls has just started to improve.’","’And my husband is doing an excellent job as the Shopkeeper of Jishi Medicine Hall. He must be putting his heart into it.’","’If the Jing State and Shu State branches of the Liu Family join forces... they’ll surely cause trouble for the Medicine Halls, won’t they?’","Xiao Jinghong stared at the letters in her hand, lost in thought.","She only snapped out of it when Su Zhenyue placed a plate of steaming pastries on the table.","\"My Lady, are you still keeping the Young Master’s letters?\"","Xiao Jinghong noticed the teasing glint in her eyes and calmly put the two letters away.","\"I need to go out for something. I’ll be back tomorrow after nightfall.\"","Su Zhenyue blinked. \"Huh? Now? Where are you going?\"","\"My Lady, we have a geological survey tomorrow. Without you here, the people from the Mountain Race won’t be able to keep those oddballs from the engineering division in line.\"","Xiao Jinghong tossed a pastry into her mouth. \"Have Pei Guanli handle it... hmm...\"","She paused, then changed tack. \"Have her older brother handle it. Pei Guanli is coming with me.\"","Hearing this, Su Zhenyue hesitated for a moment before asking again, \"My Lady, may I ask where you are going so late?\"","Xiao Jinghong didn’t answer, merely instructing her to go wake Pei Guanli.","\"Then I’ll go prepare the horses.\"","\"No need. We won’t be gone long.\"","Seeing that her mind was made up, Su Zhenyue nodded and left the wooden cabin.","Xiao Jinghong watched her walk away, thinking to herself, ’It’s probably best if I go back and check on things.’","’I can also drop Pei Guanli off at the Xiao Mansion for a while. That’ll keep her from causing trouble here.’","Ultimately, she couldn’t set aside her worries about the Liu Family.","’And my husband...’","Not long after, Pei Guanli came running over, shouting at the top of her lungs.","Xiao Jinghong promptly grabbed her by the scruff of the neck and leaped into the night sky, turning her boisterous shouts into panicked shrieks.","\"Sister Jinghong, slow down! I’m... scared... of... heights... AHHH...\"","...","「The next morning, as dawn broke.」","The drizzle that had fallen all night had grown heavier, and raindrops the size of rice grains pattered against the roof tiles and the surface of the pond.","The Spring Lotus Garden was filled with the sound of PIT-PAT, PIT-PAT.","At first, the sound was crisp and pleasant.","Chen Yi awoke from his cultivation. He got up, opened the window, and stretched his limbs while gazing out at the rainy Spring Lotus Garden.","The cultivation effects of his Four Symbols Skill, now at the Earth Tier, were indeed much faster.","However, the amount of True Essence in his two Seas of Qi wasn’t the key to opening the final Ren and Du Meridians.","He could only proceed bit by bit to avoid any mistakes that might damage these two most vital meridians.","Just then, Xiaodie, apparently having heard him moving about, knocked and entered with a basin of warm water and a towel.","\"Good morning, Young Master.\"","\"Morning.\"","After their greeting, Xiaodie soaked the towel and used it to wipe his face.","After he changed into a fresh robe, she helped straighten it for him before she began to tidy up the room.","When she saw the soaking wet black robe, Xiaodie picked it up suspiciously. \"Young Master, did you go out last night?\"","Chen Yi just laughed and gave a vague excuse about practicing his Martial Arts in the garden.","Xiaodie didn’t suspect a thing and put the robe in a basin to be washed.","The two of them left the room, one after the other.","Xiaodie seemed to recall something. \"Young Master, it seems something happened in the mansion today.\"","Chen Yi’s interest was piqued. \"Oh? What’s that?\"","Xiaodie gestured with her chin toward the outer part of the garden. \"A lot of people came to the central courtyard. Some from the Imprisonment Department, others from the Prefectural Yamen and the City Guard Army.\"","\"No one’s clear on the specifics, but I heard that Brother Liu Si was injured by some ruffian last night.\"","\"I’m guessing the people from the Government Office are here because of that.\"","’Ruffian?’","Chen Yi smiled and glanced at her. \"Xiaodie, I want to have hot pot for lunch. Go let the kitchen know.\"","’You little brat, daring to call your young master a ruffian. As punishment, you can be the one to cook my meat slices.’","Xiaodie blinked in surprise, but she didn’t refuse.","But then she thought about the last time they had hot pot, and a pained expression crossed her face. \"Young Master, could we maybe prepare two pots...?\"","Last time, with the Eldest Young Miss here, she, Juan’er, and Cui’er couldn’t even sit at the table.","’Ugh, having to just stand there and watch, unable to eat... it was torture.’","Chen Yi saw her expression and let out a heartless laugh.","This made Xiaodie lower her head in embarrassment. \"Young Master, I want to try some too, you know.\"","\"Alright, alright. Tell the kitchen to prepare plenty of extra food.\"","\"You got it!\"","After breakfast, Chen Yi, knowing the situation with the Xiao Family Medicine Hall and Hundred Herbs Hall was likely still unresolved, settled down to play chess with Xiao Wuge in the pavilion.","He had to admit, Xiao Wuge was very bright. He picked up the rules, piece formations, and game records with incredible speed.","In just a day or two, his playing already looked quite polished.","They played until it was nearly noon. Not long after Xiaodie ran off to arrange the hot pot, Xiao Wan’er, Shen Huatang, and Xie Tingyun arrived together at the Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi saw them and asked with a smile, \"What a coincidence. I just sent Xiaodie to prepare hot pot.\"","Clearly, they hadn’t been drawn by the aroma.","But it also didn’t seem like they were here for anything too urgent.","At least, judging from the expression on her face, Xiao Wan’er seemed to be in a good mood.","And sure enough, Xiao Wan’er said with a smile, \"Hot pot sounds great! It’s a perfect chance to liven things up.\"","Shen Huatang, standing beside her, didn’t show much reaction, but Xie Tingyun was already acting familiar, winking and giving Chen Yi suggestive looks.","Her expression seemed to say, ’You really know how to live it up, pal.’","Chen Yi found this amusing and didn’t forget to invite them to sit. \"I heard there was some trouble in the mansion. An Armored Warrior was injured last night? Is it related to Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","He was, of course, feigning ignorance.","Xiao Wan’er nodded. \"Liu Si’er was injured, but thankfully, it wasn’t serious. We sent him to a Medicine Hall for treatment last night.\"","\"Also, the crisis at Hundred Herbs Hall has been resolved for the time being. Wang Ji and Yan Hai are both safe and sound.\"","\"It was a close call, though...\"","As he listened to Xiao Wan’er recount the events of the previous night, Chen Yi fought back a strange feeling, thinking only that she was quite an eloquent storyteller.","She recounted every detail with such clarity, it was as if she had been there herself.","\"It’s good that Boss Wang is alright.\"","Chen Yi paused, then asked, \"Did you find out who was behind the Illusory Sound Sect?\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated. \"I believe we already know, but Grandfather and Second Grand-uncle haven’t announced it publicly.\"","Chen Yi understood. He figured his grandfather-in-law and the others still needed to wrangle with the Liu Family.","After all, the Liu Family still had the Left Envoy of the Shu State Governor’s Office on their side.","It was unlikely that his grandfather-in-law and the others would push things to the point of no return.","The final outcome would probably be just as Chen Yunfan had guessed last night: the Liu Family would offer up their Sixth Young Master to appease the Xiao Family’s wrath.","Of course, none of this was Chen Yi’s concern anymore.","In his current situation, helping the Xiao Family earn some silver coins and ensuring the safety of Hundred Herbs Hall was the most he could do.","As for taking on a behemoth like the Liu Family himself... he’d rather not for the time being.","Before long, servants from the kitchen arrived.","Two hot pot sets were placed in the Spring Lotus Garden.","At one table sat Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the others. At the other sat Xiaodie, Juan’er, and Cui’er.","Despite their different statuses, everyone at both tables was now eating heartily, their mouths glistening.","Just then, Xiao Wan’er said, \"Brother-in-law, I’m writing a letter to Jinghong today.\"","\"You should write one too, and we can send them together.\"","Chen Yi paused, slightly surprised. ’Another one?’","’If I write another one, it’ll become *Three Thoughts on a Summer Night*.’","’Three thoughts... Re-thinking it...’","’On second thought, I should probably come up with a more fitting title.’"]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116 - 117: Xiao Jinghong: Blabbermouth","paragraphs":["By midday, news of what had happened at Hundred Herbs Hall the previous night had spread throughout Shu State City.","For a time, rumors flew.","Some said Hundred Herbs Hall was hiding a valuable treasure that could enhance a Martial Artist’s Cultivation.","They claimed that this, along with the Illusory Sound Sect’s previous theft of the Xiao Family’s medicinal ingredients, was all part of a search for that single Treasure Medicine.","Some said the Illusory Sound Sect was jealous of Hundred Herbs Hall’s tea business and sought to steal their recipes.","Still others claimed that after Hundred Herbs Hall’s business took off, it had cut into the profits of many other medicine halls in Shu State, which is why it invited disaster.","Whatever the case, it definitely couldn’t have been the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","After all, if the Xiao Family hadn’t stepped in to help last night, Hundred Herbs Hall would have likely been completely slaughtered by the Evil Demonic Dao of the Illusory Sound Sect.","But beyond the gossip, many people felt a lingering fear about the Hundred Herbs Hall incident.","This hadn’t happened in some remote backwater, but was a major event in the Shu State Prefecture City.","If those of the Evil Demonic Dao dared to rob and slaughter Hundred Herbs Hall today, couldn’t they go after jewelry stores or other shops tomorrow?","Furthermore, the fact that many people in the West Market had been knocked unconscious during the incident only heightened the worries of Shu State’s citizens.","This directly caused the pressure on the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office, the Imprisonment Department, and the City Guard Army to multiply.","Even the Governor’s Office and the Inspectorate Office, upon hearing of the matter, sent down orders for the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and the Imprisonment Department to capture the criminals as soon as possible.","Thus, before noon had even passed, officials from the Imprisonment Department, the Prefectural Yamen, and soldiers from the City Guard Army were seen all over Shu State Prefecture City.","The City Guard Army set up checkpoints at the city gates to inspect people coming and going.","The government officials went through the streets and alleys, questioning people door-to-door about any suspicious individuals.","The men from the Imprisonment Department, meanwhile, focused their investigation on the inside and outside of Hundred Herbs Hall, the shops in the West Market, and the locations where fighting had occurred the previous night.","Even many of the Xiao Family Armored Warriors were following along.","However, besides the Evil Demons of the Illusory Sound Sect, the Xiao Family’s other major focus of investigation was the place where Liu Si’er had been injured.","For this reason, Ge the Third even went to the Medicine Hall, first to ask about what happened, and second to take him back to the Xiao Mansion to recuperate.","By now, Liu Si’er had regained consciousness. His body was wrapped in bandages, his left arm was fixed in a splint, and his face was sallow.","A single glance was enough to tell his injuries were severe.","Ge the Third didn’t rush to ask about last night’s events. He first spoke with the Physician, and only after confirming that Liu Si’er’s life wasn’t in danger did he help him leave the Medicine Hall.","The two of them boarded a horse-drawn carriage.","Ge the Third’s expression was normal. He cursed under his breath as he asked, \"Brother Si, was that guy last night really that strong?\"","Liu Si’er didn’t want to bother with him, but the thought of the black-clothed man skilled in Spear Technique inevitably filled him with anger.","\"His Spear Technique is strong, but his Cultivation isn’t actually that high. He probably hasn’t reached the Middle Three Grades Realm yet.\"","\"His voice sounded a bit old, but from the look in his eyes, he couldn’t have been very old—probably around twenty.\"","After hearing this, Ge the Third recalled the speculation from the Imprisonment Department’s Imprisonment Officer and asked doubtfully,","\"But didn’t Magistrate Zhao say after inspecting the scene that the attacker’s Spear Technique has entered the Dao?\"","Liu Si’er froze. His suspicion was confirmed, and his expression instantly soured.","A Martial Artist who had not yet reached the Middle Three Grades Realm but could cultivate their Spear Technique to the point of entering the Dao could truly be called a \"Martial Arts genius.\"","Such individuals usually come from prestigious backgrounds.","They are either members of Noble Families and Clans, or disciples of renowned Jianghu Sects or famous masters.","Either way, it meant the man in black was no simple character.","Thinking of this, Liu Si’er asked, \"Ge the Third, have the masters in the mansion made any progress?\"","Ge the Third let out a sigh. \"Of the people who went to Hundred Herbs Hall last night, the dead are dead and the injured are injured. There’s no useful information for the time being.\"","\"However, a few Wandering Martial Artists were captured by the men from the Punishment Hall. They’re being interrogated in the mansion right now, so we should be able to get something out of them.\"","\"Brother Si, are you sure you don’t know who it was that injured you last night?\"","Liu Si’er replied curtly, \"If I knew who he was, I’d be leading a team over there right now.\"","Ge the Third cursed, \"Damn it. He dared to make a move against our Xiao Family. I think he’s tired of living.\"","The carriage made its way to the gates of the Xiao Mansion.","Ge the Third was just about to speak when he caught sight of two figures approaching through the rain out of the corner of his eye, and his curses died in his throat.","He couldn’t help but feel shocked and suspicious. ’Why is Xiao Jinghong back at a time like this? Is it because of what happened at Hundred Herbs Hall last night? Has the Old Master decided to make a final move against the Liu Family?’","These thoughts flashed through Ge the Third’s mind, but on the surface, he remained respectful as he bowed and said:","\"This subordinate greets General Jinghong.\"","Inside the carriage, Liu Si’er was startled. He quickly lifted the curtain and stepped out, enduring the sharp pain in his arm as he bowed.","\"Greetings, General.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked at the two of them, her gaze falling on Liu Si’er’s arm. \"Who did this?\" she asked.","Liu Si’er shook his head. \"This subordinate was tracking a criminal last night and was careless enough to be injured by him.\"","Xiao Jinghong paused slightly, her gaze shifting toward the Xiao Mansion. She listened intently for a moment before asking, \"Because of the Hundred Herbs Hall incident? Tell me everything.\"","Hearing this, both Ge the Third and Liu Si’er’s hearts went cold.","’She knows? She really does know.’","\"Reporting to the General, last night, this subordinate was with the Second Master, standing guard outside Hundred Herbs Hall... The man’s Spear Technique was incredible. He has entered the Dao despite only having a Lower Three Grades Cultivation. This subordinate speculates he must come from a prestigious background.\"","After speaking, Liu Si’er looked ashamed. \"Forgive me, General. It was a moment of carelessness that allowed him to knock me down with a single spear strike.\"","Just as Xiao Jinghong was about to speak, she heard a gasp from beside her.","She turned her head to look at Pei Guanli and saw her eyes were wide and round. \"Do you know who that person is?\" she asked.","Pei Guanli covered her mouth. \"I-I dunno.\"","Behind her mask, Xiao Jinghong’s eyes were calm. She pressed, \"You really don’t know?\"","Pei Guanli shook her head repeatedly. \"Dunno, dunno...\"","She truly didn’t know the identity of the man in black; she just felt that the spear strike Liu Si’er had just described was very similar to a Spear Technique Chen Yi had used before.","Seeing this, Xiao Jinghong thought for a moment and decided not to press the matter with her.","She then offered a few words of encouragement to Liu Si’er and Ge the Third before leading Pei Guanli into the Xiao Mansion.","Liu Si’er watched them walk away before letting out a soft sigh of relief.","Unexpectedly, Ge the Third next to him did the same.","The two sounds merged, just loud enough for each to hear the other.","Ge the Third and Liu Si’er glanced at each other, a strange look on their faces, and let out a few dry laughs.","\"Brother Si, the General’s return is perfectly timed. I doubt those petty criminals will dare to show their faces now.\"","\"You’re right...\"","「Meanwhile.」","Although Xiao Jinghong heard their conversation, she didn’t take it to heart.","She knew herself well enough.","She was used to being serious, and whether it was the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard or the soldiers of the Dingyuan Army, most of them feared her.","’It’s only human nature, I suppose.’","Just then, Pei Guanli calmed down. Looking at the familiar scenery around her, she giggled.","\"Sister Jinghong, you should have told me earlier that we were coming back to Shu State.\"","\"You had my heart pounding in my chest while we were flying just now.\"","Seeing Xiao Jinghong ignore her, she asked herself aloud, \"Sister Jinghong didn’t bring me here specially, did she?\"","\"Can I stay here for a while?\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded slightly. \"Indeed, I brought you here to stay for a while.\"","Pei Guanli was overjoyed. A smile bloomed on her round face, and she began to hop and skip, her fair, tender feet splashing in the puddles. The movement caused the bell on her chest to jingle incessantly.","JINGLE JINGLE. She hugged Xiao Jinghong’s arm, acting cutesy. \"I knew you were the best to me, Sister!\"","Xiao Jinghong moved her fingers slightly to push her away. \"I was just afraid you’d cause trouble if you stayed at the camp,\" she said.","Instead of being annoyed, Pei Guanli was delighted. She nodded. \"That’s right, that’s right! I would only cause trouble over there. It’s better to stay here.\"","\"I’ve been gone for so long. I wonder if brother-in-law missed me.\"","Xiao Jinghong glanced at her, her full, vermilion lips moving slightly, but no words came out.","’If my husband had been thinking of her,’ she thought, ’then \"Thoughts of a Summer Night\" and \"Two Thoughts on a Summer Night\" were sent to the wrong person.’","「Not long after.」","The two arrived in the rear courtyard.","From a distance, Xiao Jinghong could hear the cheerful laughter coming from the Spring Lotus Garden, and the trace of worry in her heart vanished.","’My husband... and Big Sister are so relaxed. The incident at Hundred Herbs Hall must not have affected them.’","While she was thinking this, Pei Guanli beside her had no such complex thoughts.","Upon hearing Chen Yi’s laughter, she let out a cheer and immediately quickened her pace, running into the Spring Lotus Garden.","As soon as she saw the group of people eating hotpot in the pavilion, a brilliant smile spread across Pei Guanli’s face.","Ignoring the rain splattering on her face and her soaked clothes, she ran toward Chen Yi with her arms wide open.","\"Brother-in-law, I’m back!\"","When Chen Yi saw her, his smile faltered for a moment.","Then he saw Xiao Jinghong behind her, and his smile returned.","He stood up and waved.","Seeing this, Pei Guanli ran even more gleefully.","But just as she was about to leap into Chen Yi’s arms, he planted a hand on her forehead, stopping her short.","Pei Guanli reached forward but couldn’t even touch the hem of his clothes. \"Brother-in-law, you...\"","Chen Yi glanced at her. \"Don’t mess around.\"","With that, Chen Yi steered Pei Guanli to the side and looked at Xiao Jinghong, who was walking over at a leisurely pace. He smiled and asked:","\"My lady, what brings you back today? Didn’t you say before that your return date was uncertain?\"","Xiao Wan’er, standing nearby, had the same question.","However, seeing Xiao Jinghong walking in the rain without an umbrella, she just said in a gentle voice, \"Hurry and come in out of the rain.\"","Xiao Jinghong’s gaze swept across the group, lingering for an extra moment on Xie Tingyun, before she looked at Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er and nodded.","\"I had some business and was just passing through.\"","But her words had barely faded when Pei Guanli, who was sulking off to the side, let out a sound of surprise.","\"Sister Jinghong, didn’t you say earlier that you came back specifically to bring me here?\"","Everyone froze.","Xiao Jinghong looked at her calmly. \"...\"","’Such a loudmouth.’"]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117 - 118: My Lady, You Need an Umbrella on a Rainy Day","paragraphs":["Amid the DRIP, DRAP of the falling rain.","Xiao Jinghong explained calmly.","\"Bringing you back was just on the way.\"","\"I’m going to the Ministry of Engineering later, then I have to rush back.\"","Pei Guanli simply said, \"Oh,\" not suspecting anything.","Then she saw the hotpot on the table and, without much ceremony, sat right down beside it. \"Can I have some?\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled gently. \"Of course you can.\"","While instructing Cui’er to fetch two sets of bowls and chopsticks, she went over and pulled Xiao Jinghong to a seat.","\"Second Sister, you came back in the rain. Don’t be in such a hurry to leave. Eat something to warm yourself up first. Brother-in-law had this hotpot specially prepared.\"","Xiao Jinghong didn’t refuse, her eyes fixed on the hotpot, unwilling to look away.","Evidently, Pei Guanli’s earlier words had made her somewhat uncomfortable.","Especially after seeing the half-smile on Chen Yi’s face, the ripple in her heart began to spread.","’It seems the decision to bring Pei Guanli back was a bit rash.’","Chen Yi sat down as well, the smile still on his face. \"Go on, try it. It’s not bad.\"","As he spoke, he took his own chopsticks, rinsed them in a bowl of water, and picked up some food for Xiao Jinghong.","Xiao Jinghong took it without any hesitation and began eating with his bowl and chopsticks.","After rushing about all night without a single drop to drink, she was indeed hungry.","Xiao Wan’er took this in, a complex emotion flashing across her pale, delicate face.","After a moment of silence.","Her expression returned to normal as she began to recount the events of the past few days.","She recounted everything, down to the last detail.","\"I was planning to send you a letter today to explain everything. Since you’re back, you might as well go ask Grandfather about it.\"","After eating some meat and vegetables, Xiao Jinghong felt a warmth in her stomach. \"Good. I’ll tell Grandfather about the Mutual Market at the same time.\"","Afterward, the group continued to make small talk in the pavilion.","It was mostly Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong who did the talking.","Xiao Wuge, of course, didn’t miss his chance, eagerly placing food on Xiao Jinghong’s plate.","Chen Yi, however, barely spoke, nor did he make any other significant moves.","He just sat to the side listening, occasionally chiming in with a word or two.","But he couldn’t help but guess at the reason for Xiao Jinghong’s return to the mansion.","For a moment, his thoughts were exactly the same as Liu Si’er’s and Ge the Third’s.","’The old master is going to make a move on the Liu Family, so he summoned Xiao Jinghong back.’","’But thinking about it carefully, it doesn’t seem like the time is right yet.’","’Besides, if Xiao Jinghong or the Xiao Family were going to strike at the Liu Family, they wouldn’t bring Pei Guanli along.’","After thinking it over and over.","Chen Yi decided to assume for now that Xiao Jinghong had simply made a special trip to bring Pei Guanli back for a temporary stay.","’She couldn’t possibly have come back for me, her husband.’","During this time, Xiao Wan’er naturally introduced Xie Tingyun of the Celestial Sect.","She explained that it was thanks to her that Hundred Herbs Hall had remained safe last night.","Xiao Jinghong nodded. \"Thank you for your assistance, Fairy Tingyun.\"","But Xie Tingyun waved his hands repeatedly. \"No, no, not at all. Ol—... I was here for Elder Demon Jia, but unfortunately, he escaped.\"","These few polite and proper words made Shen Huatang give him a sidelong glance.","She’d never expected her always-casual, unconventional senior sister to have such a reserved moment.","But what she didn’t know was that at this moment, Xie Tingyun’s heart was reeling.","’Holy hell.’","’In all my years running around the martial world, this is the first damn time I’ve been so scared my legs have gone weak.’","’Xiao Jinghong... she’s only in the Fourth Grade Realm?’","’Bullshit!’","’She must have entered the Upper Three Grades!’","Although everyone had different thoughts, on the surface, they all seemed happy and harmonious.","Xiao Jinghong had filled her stomach, seen that the Xiao Mansion was safe, and that Chen Yi’s Medicine Hall was unaffected. She could finally relax.","After a bit more small talk.","Xiao Jinghong said, \"It’s getting late. I’ll go see Grandfather, and then I’ll head straight back to the Mutual Market.\"","Xiao Wan’er said in surprise, \"In such a hurry?\"","\"Once the surveying is done, the blueprints are finalized, and construction on the Mutual Market has begun, I’ll come back.\"","\"If that’s the case, then I won’t keep you...\"","Hearing their conversation, Chen Yi glanced at the rain outside the pavilion, then stood up and went back inside without a word.","Xiao Jinghong watched him walk away. Although she was puzzled, she still stood up as planned to say goodbye to Xiao Wan’er and the others.","Just as she was about to leave, she saw Chen Yi walk out holding an Oil Paper Umbrella.","\"It’s chilly on a rainy day,\" he said. \"You should take an umbrella.\"","Xiao Jinghong paused, a flicker of warmth in her eyes. She took the Oil Paper Umbrella, a faint smile on her lips. \"Thank you... husband.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"You’re being too formal.\"","Seeing that smiling face, the two poems she had received earlier came to mind, and her expression became slightly unnatural.","Thankfully, her silver mask concealed it, so no one could see.","’With that thought,’ Xiao Jinghong opened the Oil Paper Umbrella, held it over her head, and turned to leave.","She had only taken a few steps when she remembered something and turned back.","\"Husband, about Mr. Yue Ming’s invitation for you to become an Instructor at Guiyun Academy, what are your thoughts?\"","Seeing her bring up the old topic again, Chen Yi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. \"Wife, my learning is... not that advanced.\"","\"I probably shouldn’t go to Guiyun Academy and lead the students astray, right?\"","’If I didn’t know I couldn’t beat her in a fight, I’d snatch that umbrella back no matter what.’","Xiao Jinghong looked him straight in the eye. Seeing his earnestness, she nodded and said:","\"Then I won’t try to persuade you anymore.\"","\"After I’m done with the Mutual Market, I’ll come back and find a position for you that you’ll be more satisfied with.\"","Huh?","Another position?","Chen Yi’s smile froze. \"Um...\"","Before he could say anything more to argue his case, Xiao Jinghong had already turned and walked away under the Oil Paper Umbrella.","’My husband... I believe he is a man of great learning.’","’I can’t bear to see him waste his time away in the Xiao Family like this.’","With these thoughts, her tall figure disappeared from the Spring Lotus Garden, vanishing into the curtain of rain.","Like an immortal descending to the mortal world, her steps had an unconcealable, nimble lightness to them.","It’s just that...","Chen Yi was in no mood to appreciate the sight.","’All I want is to be a lazy, live-in husband in the mansion!’","Xiao Wan’er looked at the expression on his face and knew he didn’t want to go.","Although she should have offered a few words of comfort or tried to mediate, the scene she’d witnessed earlier left her feeling a bit complicated.","’Second Sister and Brother-in-law really are a match made in heaven.’","Xiao Wan’er sighed inwardly and didn’t linger in the Spring Lotus Garden any longer, bidding Shen Huatang and the others to return to Jiaxing Garden with her.","After everyone had left.","Only Chen Yi, Xiao Wuge, Pei Guanli, and Xiaodie remained in the Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiaodie naturally got busy again, calling for the kitchen staff to clear the leftovers from the pavilion and clean everything up.","Then she took Xiao Wuge back to his room for an afternoon nap.","Chen Yi also wanted to go back and consider his next move.","Seeing how serious Xiao Jinghong was today, he figured that when she returned after dealing with the Mutual Market, she would definitely find some other position for him.","’The barracks? The Commandant’s Office? Or somewhere else?’","’They were all possibilities.’","But to be honest, comparing the options, Chen Yi was starting to think Guiyun Academy wasn’t such a bad place after all.","’It’s true what they say. Everything is relative.’","Pei Guanli, however, didn’t go anywhere. She stayed by his side, looking this way and that.","Her big, bright eyes were full of inquiry.","\"Brother-in-law, that person last night, was that...\"","Before she could get the word \"you\" out, Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat. He immediately clamped a hand over her mouth and made a \"zip it\" gesture.","’Good grief, girl, you really have no idea how formidable a Martial Arts Powerhouse is.’","’Xiao Jinghong is still in the mansion!’","’If she finds out from Pei Guanli that I was the man in black from last night, I’m done for.’","’I probably wouldn’t even have to wait for Xiao Jinghong to return from the Mutual Market. I’d be dispatched from Jishi Medicine Hall to the army barracks by tomorrow.’","Seeing his serious expression, Pei Guanli understood.","\"It’s the man who was injured last night.\"","\"Just now, when Sister Jinghong and I were returning to the mansion, we ran into him.\"","\"I remember his name is Liu Si’er, right?\"","Chen Yi let out a sigh of relief. \"It was him. You’ve seen him before.\"","\"But what happened last night has nothing to do with you, so stop asking questions.\"","’I’ve gotta say, this girl is seriously reckless.’","...","Xiao Jinghong left the Spring Lotus Garden and, holding the umbrella, made her way to the Qingjing Residence.","Just as she entered the residence, she heard the voice of Second Master Xiao Wang, his tone furious:","\"Marquis, how much longer are you going to wait?\"","\"If you’re worried about provoking retaliation from the Liu Family, this old man will just take the men from the Punishment Hall and go myself!\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong’s expression turned grim, and she immediately walked inside.","\"Second Grand-uncle...\""]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118 - 119: Husband, Still So Shameless","paragraphs":["\"Second Grand-uncle, I cannot agree with what you’ve said!\"","Xiao Jinghong’s sudden appearance silenced everyone in Qingjing Residence.","The expressions of everyone present immediately shifted.","Third Master Xiao Shen paused for a moment before settling back into his chair, looking perfectly composed.","The solemn look on Xiao Xuanshuo’s face eased.","And Xiao Wang, who had just been speaking in a grave tone, fell silent, merely frowning at the figure in the doorway.","Old Marquis Xiao, however, remained calm, seemingly unaffected. He beckoned to her.","\"Jinghong, you’ve come at just the right time.\"","\"A major incident occurred in Shu State last night. I was just discussing with them how to handle it.\"","Xiao Jinghong walked straight over, greeting each person in turn. \"I learned of this matter from my eldest sister earlier.\"","As she spoke, she took a seat beside Old Marquis Xiao. \"If we’ve confirmed the Liu Family is responsible, there’s no need to act rashly.\"","Old Marquis Xiao glanced at Xiao Wang, who had fallen silent, and nodded with a smile. \"Tell me your thoughts.\"","Xiao Jinghong stated bluntly, \"A conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families will benefit neither Shu State nor our Xiao Family.\"","She knew this very well.","Whether it was the Xiao Family or the Dingyuan Army, both needed time to rest and recuperate.","Clashing with the Liu Family now would undoubtedly throw Shu State into chaos.","The Xiao Family itself would know no peace.","This would affect the Mutual Market and create new setbacks for the newly re-established Dingyuan Army.","Hearing her words, Xiao Wang frowned deeply.","\"Jinghong, you are a member of the Xiao Family. You should know how difficult it has been for our family to survive to this day.\"","\"Putting aside ancient history, just in the last ten years, we have fought back the Barbarian Race’s grand army and launched an expedition to Poshisu. It is through blood and tears that our Xiao Family stands where it does today.\"","\"But how does the Liu Family treat us?\"","\"They instructed the Illusory Sound Sect to seize our medicinal herbs and even established Linglan Pavilion in Shu State, all to crush our Xiao Family Medicine Hall.\"","\"Wan’er overcame countless hardships and finally managed to partner with Hundred Herbs Hall to revive our Medicine Hall. Then that whelp from the Liu Family sent people to Hundred Herbs Hall, trying to drive our Xiao Family into the ground once again.\"","\"If we don’t fight back, what will outsiders think?\"","His words were reasonable and well-argued. Every sentence was from the Xiao Family’s perspective, and he certainly had a point.","Even Xiao Xuanshuo was somewhat swayed after hearing it.","In the past decade, several members of the Xiao Family had died on the battlefield, all to protect Shu State and defend the borders of Great Wei.","Yet, certain people were not only ungrateful but had the audacity to come bullying them.","Anyone would be furious in such a situation, to say nothing of the Xiao Family, with its two-hundred-year legacy.","However, after hearing Xiao Wang speak, Old Marquis Xiao and Xiao Jinghong merely exchanged a glance. In their hearts, they both knew what was most important right now.","No matter what, Shu State must not fall into chaos!","Old Marquis Xiao waved his hand. \"Now is not the time.\"","Xiao Wang struck the ground with his cane. \"Then when will it be time? When they’ve crushed the Xiao Family?\"","His face wasn’t old, but the deep lines framing his mouth gave his gaunt features an intimidating air even when he wasn’t angry.","Xiao Jinghong glanced at him and said coolly, \"If Second Grand-uncle truly feels that way, you are free to go directly to Jing State.\"","Xiao Wang froze, his slightly clouded eyes turning to her. \"Do you think I don’t dare?\"","\"If Second Grand-uncle agrees, I will send you there myself, today!\"","\"You...\"","\"Enough. Both of you, be silent.\"","Before either could say more, Old Marquis Xiao raised a hand to cut them off, his gaze landing on Xiao Wang.","\"I understand you’re thinking of the Xiao Family’s best interests, but we cannot act on impulse in this matter.\"","\"Give me three days. If Left Envoy Liu doesn’t provide an explanation, then you may handle this matter as you see fit.\"","Xiao Wang withdrew his glare from Xiao Jinghong and snorted. \"Three days it is. If the Liu Family doesn’t show up by then, I will personally lead the men of the Punishment Hall to demand an explanation.\"","As his voice fell, he got up and walked outside.","Just then, Xiao Jinghong spoke again, her voice cool. \"Second Grand-uncle, there is something I must say.\"","Xiao Wang’s steps paused.","\"The Punishment Hall belongs to the Xiao Family. It is not your private army, nor anyone else’s.\"","Xiao Jinghong looked at him calmly. \"Grandfather is still hale and hearty. He is the one who has the final say in this family.\"","Xiao Wang glanced back at her, his expression flickering with anger.","\"General Jinghong, if you are dissatisfied with my actions, you are welcome to call a clan meeting and have me dismissed from my position as Chief Steward of the Punishment Hall!\"","Without waiting for Xiao Jinghong to reply, Xiao Wang turned and stormed out.","With that, the matter was more or less settled.","Third Master Xiao Shen rose as well, saying with a chuckle, \"Eldest Brother, I’ll follow your lead on this.\"","\"But don’t be angry with Second Brother. He’s just letting his temper get the best of him. Even I can’t stomach what the Liu Family has been doing lately.\"","Old Marquis Xiao shot him a look. \"If you know he’s in a temper, why aren’t you going to calm him down?\"","\"Ah, I’ll go right now.\"","Xiao Shen smiled and nodded toward Xiao Jinghong, then also left Qingjing Residence.","Xiao Xuanshuo silently bowed and also did not linger.","In less than a quarter of an hour, only Old Marquis Xiao and Xiao Jinghong remained in Qingjing Residence.","Silence fell for a moment.","Old Marquis Xiao smiled and asked, \"How is progress with the Mutual Market?\"","Xiao Jinghong calmly replied, \"Everything is well.\"","\"In the contract with the Mountain Race, they are responsible for handling people from the Jianghu, while we handle pressure from the Imperial Court, the neighboring Zhou Mansion, and the noble merchant families.\"","\"The profits are split seventy-thirty. They take the thirty percent.\"","The smile on Old Marquis Xiao’s face widened. \"Excellent.\"","\"Once the Mutual Market is established, people will come from Shu State, Jing State, Guangyue Prefecture, the Western State, and You State.\"","\"When the time comes, you will receive them on my behalf. Do your best to reserve a stall for each of them in the Mutual Market.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded.","This was something she and the Old Marquis had discussed long ago, so no more needed to be said.","But thinking of the Liu Family, she couldn’t help but ask, \"People from the Jing State Liu Family came. Why didn’t you tell me?\"","Old Marquis Xiao paused and sighed. \"I thought that as long as I was still hale and hearty, those people would show some restraint.\"","\"I never imagined they would be so impatient.\"","\"My birthday banquet was only a month ago, yet they’ve already sent people to test the waters. They are indeed a bit too eager.\"","Xiao Jinghong pondered for a moment before asking seriously, \"Is it necessary for me to intervene?\"","Old Marquis Xiao chuckled and shook his head, waving a hand. \"The situation is far from reaching that point.\"","He paused for a moment, then decided to elaborate.","\"A series of great battles caused our Xiao Family to suffer heavy losses, letting those people see a certain possibility.\"","\"It’s not that they don’t understand the saying ’a starved camel is still bigger than a horse.’ It’s that they’ve smelled blood in the water, and it has stirred their greed.\"","\"But they have forgotten that the Xiao Family has been able to stand for two hundred years not because of the Dingyuan Army.\"","Old Marquis Xiao’s gaze drifted to the gloomy rain outside the hall, his smile unwavering as he said:","\"You don’t need to concern yourself with this matter. Focus on the Mutual Market for now.\"","Xiao Jinghong nodded silently. \"I understand.\"","Old Marquis Xiao withdrew his gaze and looked at her with relief. \"With you supporting the Xiao Family, I can rest much easier.\"","\"It is what I should do as your granddaughter.\"","\"I know well enough what you should and shouldn’t do. In this vast Xiao Family, the only ones I can truly trust are you, Wan’er, and just a few others.\"","\"Wuge is still young, so I must trouble you to bear more of the burden.\"","As Old Marquis Xiao spoke, a smile returned to his face. He changed the subject, \"Have you seen Chen Yi since you returned?\"","Xiao Jinghong was slightly stunned. \"I’ve seen him.\"","\"And? Did you notice any difference in him from before?\"","\"What is Grandfather referring to?\"","\"His hidden talents, of course. Haven’t you noticed how much he’s changed these past few months?\"","Meeting Old Marquis Xiao’s gaze, Xiao Jinghong shook her head, a hint of awkwardness on her face.","Other than his ability to compose poetry, his fine handwriting, and his grasp of certain principles, she really hadn’t noticed anything else.","Seeing this, Old Marquis Xiao didn’t press further, merely instructing, \"When the matters of the Mutual Market are settled, you should return to the manor to stay for a while.\"","\"After all, you two are husband and wife now. You should spend more time together. Perhaps next year...\"","He didn’t finish, but Xiao Jinghong already understood his meaning.","Her face instantly turned crimson, even the skin around her eyes flushing red.","\"Grandfather, I still have things to attend to at the Mutual Market. I’ll be leaving now.\"","With that, Xiao Jinghong walked out of Qingjing Residence without looking back.","Her hurried retreat made Old Marquis Xiao chuckle with satisfaction.","This only made Xiao Jinghong even more flustered, and her steps quickened as she held her Oil Paper Umbrella.","But as she reached the front courtyard, she couldn’t help but glance back in the direction of the Spring Lotus Garden.","She faintly overheard a conversation between Chen Yi and Pei Guanli.","\"Brother-in-law, did you write a letter to Sister Jinghong?\"","\"Yup.\"","\"Was it a poem?\"","\"You saw it?\"","\"No, I heard Sister Jinghong reciting it. Something about ’long-lasting,’ and ’morning and evening’?\"","\"Silly, you didn’t even hear it right. The line is, ’If love between two hearts can last for an age, why does it matter if they are together day and night?’\"","\"Wow, what a beautiful poem! Brother-in-law, you should write one for me too...\"","Hearing this, Xiao Jinghong couldn’t bear to listen any longer.","With a single step, she leaped into the air, flying over half the city.","’That husband of mine... he’s still so shameless.’"]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119 - 120: An Invitation...","paragraphs":["After Xiao Jinghong left, the Xiao Mansion grew much quieter.","The maids and household servants in the mansion kept their mouths shut about the Hundred Herbs Hall incident, as if someone had specifically instructed them to do so.","However, Chen Yi knew that while the mansion seemed calm on the surface, strange undercurrents were stirring beneath.","For one, the Personal Guards were still rushing about outside.","With Liu Si’er injured, the duty of patrolling the various medicine halls fell entirely to Wang Lixing, and several extra Personal Guards were assigned to him.","Several other Personal Guards went to the Imprisonment Department to help investigate the people who had appeared outside Hundred Herbs Hall that night.","This included Elder Demon Jia of the Illusory Sound Sect, the quartet who had fled, and the man in black who had injured Liu Si’er.","With these arrangements, and counting the Personal Guards who had left with Xiao Jinghong, the number of Armored Warriors within the Xiao Mansion was noticeably lower.","It was only natural that the Xiao Family estate was quieter.","Another point of interest was the Xiao Family Punishment Hall.","After two nights of interrogation, one of the Wandering Martial Artists they had previously captured finally broke and implicated Linglan Pavilion as their backer.","In less than half a day, Linglan Pavilion, which had been open for less than a month, was shut down by the Imprisonment Department, its doors sealed shut.","According to Liu Quan, the accountant from Jishi Medicine Hall, a host of government officials had descended on Linglan Pavilion in the East Market, arresting Qian Kuan and his men and hauling them all off to the Government Office.","He also said that by that very afternoon, Qian Kuan had cracked, confessing that he and several other Linglan Pavilion shopkeepers had conspired against the Xiao Family Medicine Halls.","Furthermore, they had been the ones who directed the practitioners of the Illusory Sound Sect’s Evil Demonic Dao.","First, they’d plundered the Xiao Family’s medicinal ingredients, then they’d moved to slaughter everyone at Hundred Herbs Hall to seize the recipes for those few tea infusions.","Upon extracting this confession, Prefect Liu ordered his men to find the Xiao Family’s stolen medicinal ingredients and return them.","Then, he sentenced Qian Kuan and the others to immediate execution.","Before the night was over, more than a dozen heads had rolled outside the public execution grounds of the East and West Markets.","As Liu Quan finished his story with a smile, Chen Yi smiled along with him.","He knew full well that the man from the Jing State Liu Family behind Linglan Pavilion was still safe and sound.","Qian Kuan and his men were merely scapegoats the Liu Family had thrown to the wolves.","’It happened just as Chen Yunfan predicted. Once the Liu Family was exposed, they sacrificed their pawns to save their king, pushing Linglan Pavilion forward to take the blame.’","’I wonder what fate has befallen the Jing State Liu Family’s Sixth Young Master, Liu Jing.’","’Presumably, the Shu State Liu and the Jing State Liu have had to give the Old Master an explanation for this matter.’","With these thoughts, Chen Yi stopped paying attention to Linglan Pavilion and the Liu Family.","In any case, the Xiao Family Medicine Halls were safe.","Not only had they recovered the stolen ingredients, but with Hundred Herbs Hall’s support, they shouldn’t be short on silver coins for a while.","This was evident from Xiao Wan’er’s mood over the past two days.","Her mood could be summed up in a single phrase: blooming with smiles.","Chen Yi saw this and was naturally in a good mood as well. At least he wouldn’t have to watch Xiao Wan’er take her own jewelry to the pawnshop for silver.","Three days passed like this, and his life seemed to return to its previous leisurely pace.","Playing chess, practicing calligraphy, drinking tea, and fishing.","But only Chen Yi knew that he was spending far more time on his Cultivation than before.","Although with Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang staying in the mansion he couldn’t go to the bamboo forest to practice his Punch, spear, and Step Techniques, he could focus solely on cultivating his Four Symbols Skill.","His Cultivation progress was gratifying, and a breakthrough was not far off.","Pei Guanli could also attest to this.","However, the Tiger Girl’s attention was no longer on Cultivation.","Ever since she found out that Chen Yi was the one who had injured Liu Si’er, she had been constantly vexed that she had missed out on so much fun.","In her free time after cultivating each day, she would relentlessly pester Chen Yi, asking if anything even more fun was going to happen.","To this, Chen Yi’s reply was, \"Of course there is.\"","’He hadn’t forgotten that there was still a more important and troublesome matter to deal with.’","Pei Guanli immediately grew excited, her big eyes filled with anticipation. \"What is it? What is it?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"I can’t tell you just yet, but... starting tomorrow, you need to go wander around Shu State City.\"","Pei Guanli’s expression turned to one of confusion. \"Brother-in-law, I don’t need to wander around the city.\"","\"No, you do.\"","’Not only did she need to go for a stroll, but Ge the Third had to go too.’","’Chen Yi hadn’t yet figured out how to deal with Xiao Dongchen, so for now, he could only find something to keep this Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer, Ge the Third, busy.’","’Keep him occupied from morning till night, to delay his plotting against the Dingyuan Army’s grain storehouses.’","Though her mind was filled with questions, Pei Guanli agreed after he promised it was all in preparation for something even more fun.","\"Brother-in-law, you can’t let me down, okay?\"","\"Or else... or else I won’t play with you anymore.\"","Chen Yi let out a helpless chuckle, nodded, and didn’t explain further.","’He was well aware of the principle that secrecy is the key to success.’","’Especially with a gung-ho girl like Pei Guanli, it was better for her to know as little as possible.’","「The next morning.」","Just as he had instructed, Pei Guanli feigned a \"plea\" to go wander around Shu State City.","Chen Yi naturally agreed.","However, he didn’t go himself, only sending Xiaodie along with her.","Unexpectedly, when Xiao Wan’er next door heard about it, she had Shen Huatang take Xie Tingyun along as well.","She said that since Xie Tingyun had been at the mansion for some time, she ought to see the splendor of the Prefecture City.","To that end, she even had Shen Huatang take some extra silver coins.","Looking at the four young women before him, Chen Yi couldn’t help but break into a cold sweat on Ge the Third’s behalf.","’If it were just Xiaodie and Pei Guanli, he would probably be able to find some free time to attend to his own business.’","’But with Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang present, he probably wouldn’t be able to make a single unusual move.’","After everyone had left, Chen Yi sat for a while in Jiaxing Garden, making small talk with Xiao Wan’er about the medicine halls.","\"Liu Quan came over the day before yesterday. Everything at Jishi Medicine Hall is fine, and the daily income in silver coins has increased quite a bit.\"","Xiao Wan’er knew he had been staying in the mansion these past few days and said with a smile, \"I’m just glad you still know to ask about the medicine halls.\"","Chen Yi said without batting an eye, \"With Liu Quan there, plus the renowned doctors from Hundred Herbs Hall holding down the fort, it makes no difference whether I go to the medicine hall or not.\"","\"If everyone thought like you, I’m afraid our Xiao Family Medicine Halls wouldn’t be far from closing down.\"","This was said in jest and not to be taken seriously.","But then Xiao Wan’er recalled a rumor she had heard, and her brilliant eyes turned to him.","\"I hear a rumor is spreading through Shu State City that a certain Shopkeeper said he needs ten days of rest every month.\"","\"Brother-in-law, tell me, is that right?\"","Chen Yi was quite thick-skinned. He laughed without hesitation and said, \"It just goes to show that under Eldest Sister’s leadership, everyone at our Xiao Family Medicine Halls is united in heart and purpose.\"","\"The fact that the medicine halls’ business is booming right now is clear proof.\"","Flattery will get you everywhere.","Xiao Wan’er, upon hearing this, found it quite pleasing.","However, the etiquette and rules she had studied since childhood were not enough to make her accept Chen Yi’s twisted logic.","Of course, she had no intention of blaming Chen Yi, so she let the matter drop after a few more jokes.","Still, thinking of the medicine halls’ earlier struggles, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but sigh.","\"It’s all thanks to Wang Ji and Hundred Herbs Hall for their support. Otherwise, the mansion wouldn’t have even been able to scrape together next month’s allowance money.\"","\"The clouds have parted to reveal the bright moon. Eldest Sister, you just need to look forward.\"","\"That’s easy to say... Did you know that when Wang Ji came asking for help before, he also brought a sum of silver coins?\"","Chen Yi feigned ignorance, shaking his head. \"I don’t recall you mentioning it.\"","Xiao Wan’er understood perfectly well. She lowered her head slightly and asked for his opinion:","\"Since Hundred Herbs Hall helped us so much, do you think we should give Wang Ji some silver coins as compensation, or something else?\"","Seeing her serious expression, Chen Yi mused, \"It’s fine as long as Eldest Sister decides. It doesn’t really matter whether we compensate him or not.\"","’Eldest Sister is too kind-hearted. What proper merchant would ever consider whether others live or die?’","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment. \"Let’s give him some silver coins. The mansion has a considerable daily income now, and my conscience would bother me if we took too much.\"","Just as Chen Yi was about to agree, Xiao Wan’er continued, \"I heard Hundred Herbs Hall also has a mysterious primary owner.\"","\"Wang Ji mentioned it briefly before. He said that owner has very strict rules. I wonder if the mansion giving silver coins to Wang Ji might arouse his displeasure.\"","Chen Yi said vaguely, \"Probably... not.\"","Hearing him say this, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but chide him. \"What I mean is, I want you to go to Hundred Herbs Hall and arrange a meeting with that owner on my behalf.\"","\"Is that really necessary...?\"","\"How is it not necessary? Hundred Herbs Hall did us such a huge favor. We should give him a gift to express our gratitude.\"","\"Well...\"","\"Shopkeeper Chen, will you please listen to me?\"","Facing Xiao Wan’er’s delicate and stunningly beautiful face, Chen Yi found he could no longer voice his refusal.","\"Alright, I’ll go find Wang Ji.\"","’A meeting it is, then.’","’But I’ll have to find a way to hide my identity.’"]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120 - 121: Breakthrough","paragraphs":["At Eldest Miss Xiao’s request, Chen Yi, who had intended to stay at the mansion, had to leave for the West Market Hundred Herbs Hall.","At this moment, there weren’t many Armored Warriors or carriages at the mansion; they were all busy outside.","Thus, Chen Yi didn’t have anyone accompany him, and he walked out of the Xiao Mansion under the blazing sun.","The three-day rain had stopped for three days, and the Shu State region once again returned to the sweltering heat of high summer.","Before seven in the morning, the sun was already strong enough to make one’s clothes scorching hot.","Among the pedestrians, the young ladies from wealthy families mostly carried parasols, while the young masters put on airs of elegance with their paper fans.","Even the Jianghu People who hurried past had their heads wrapped in turbans.","Compared to them, Chen Yi, who carried nothing, seemed like an oddity as he ambled slowly down the street.","Beads of sweat were faintly visible on his forehead.","With his Martial Arts, even while using the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to feign being an ordinary person, he could stay warm in winter and cool in summer, keeping his mind calm and his breathing steady.","However, to make his act more convincing, he had to break a little sweat.","About an hour later, Chen Yi arrived outside Hundred Herbs Hall.","A smile couldn’t help but appear on his face as he looked at the long line at the entrance.","It seemed that after the previous disaster, business at Hundred Herbs Hall hadn’t just been unaffected—it was even more prosperous.","Besides the people queuing to buy medicinal herbs and teas, Chen Yi also noticed several Guards stationed at the entrance.","Each wore a black long robe with the words \"Hundred Herbs Hall\" on it, and had blades and swords hanging from their waists. They were likely the Jianghu People that Wang Ji had hired before.","He sized them up for a moment before paying them no more mind.","’They’re just a few Lower Three Grades Martial Artists. They’re fine for guarding the establishment, but if a real crisis occurred, like an attack from the Evil Demonic Dao of the Illusory Sound Sect, they would be useless.’","He followed the line into Hundred Herbs Hall.","Chen Yi was inwardly amused to see Yan Hai busy and sweating profusely behind the counter.","’Good thing I don’t have to do all this myself, or I wouldn’t have a moment’s rest right now either.’","After a brief greeting, he walked straight toward the back.","From a good distance away, he could hear the sound of an abacus coming from the accountant’s office behind the main hall.","The crisp sounds were like falling hail, a ceaseless CLACK-CLACK-CLACK that filled the air.","Chen Yi walked in, scanned the room, and saw Wang Ji sitting in the accountant’s office, looking through the ledgers. He decided not to disturb him.","After waiting for about the time it takes an incense stick to burn, Wang Ji finally noticed him and hurried over in a fluster.","\"My Lo—... Shopkeeper Chen, my apologies. I was so busy just now, I didn’t notice you’d arrived.\"","Chen Yi gestured for them to talk upstairs, so Wang Ji led him to a special tearoom in the back.","The doors and windows were shut tight, and the soundproofing was excellent.","Even when Chen Yi retracted his Breath Concealment Technique, he could only hear the faint voices of the customers below.","’Wang Ji must have spent a lot to set up this room.’","Wang Ji was about to apologize again when Chen Yi waved his hand. \"It’s a good thing that Hundred Herbs Hall is so busy. Don’t look like you’ve done something wrong. Sit down and let’s talk.\"","Wang Ji cupped his hands, sat down carefully opposite him, and dared not show the slightest hint of disrespect or overstep his bounds.","After the incident with the Illusory Sound Sect, his reverence for this lord, Chen Yi, had grown even deeper.","’If not for Chen Yi’s earlier reminder and guidance, he wouldn’t just have been punished by the Xiao Family for embezzling silver coins from Jishi Medicine Hall; he would have died a miserable death at the hands of the Illusory Sound Sect’s Evil Demons.’","’How could he possibly have become the Shopkeeper of the most prosperous Hundred Herbs Hall in Shu State?’","’It is important to know one’s place, but even more so to be grateful.’","Wang Ji not only thought this way but acted on it, hoping only to stay close to Chen Yi and serve him with unwavering loyalty.","\"My Lord, are you here today to give me instructions for what’s next?\"","\"Yes and no.\"","As Chen Yi told him to brew some tea, he said casually, \"The Eldest Miss wants to see me, so she had me come to Hundred Herbs Hall to pass on the message.\"","Huh?","Thankfully, Wang Ji’s mind worked quickly, otherwise he wouldn’t have understood such a convoluted sentence.","As he brewed the tea, he asked cautiously, \"The Eldest Miss wants to see the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall... you?\"","\"So, do you intend to see her, or not?\"","Chen Yi took the cup, took a sip, and said, \"I’ll meet with her.\"","’He had already thought it through on the way here.’","’A meeting is necessary, but the when, where, and how are all up for discussion.’","’In any case, I need to find a way to change my appearance without any flaws.’","\"Go find some Jianghu People who are skilled in the Disguise Skill. It’s best if they can be hired. It doesn’t matter if it costs a lot of silver coins.\"","Hearing this, Wang Ji understood and agreed. \"The Guards I hired before are all old Jianghu veterans. They should know some people.\"","Chen Yi nodded, finished the tea in his hand, and gestured for him to pour more.","\"Tell me about the Illusory Sound Sect’s attack.\"","He had only watched the show from afar at a restaurant before and didn’t know the details of what had happened inside Hundred Herbs Hall.","After refilling the tea, Wang Ji recounted the events of that night in full detail.","He naturally threw in a few comments about how terrifying it was, but his description of the process was quite detailed.","Aside from the general events that Chen Yi already knew, his attention was focused on the investigation that followed—","an Imprisonment Officer had arrived, and after asking about what happened, wanted to take away the Wandering Martial Artists who had been captured by the Xiao Family Punishment Hall.","Xiao Xuanshuo and his men naturally refused, and the two sides almost came to blows over it.","It was only when Prefect Liu personally arrived and agreed to let the Xiao Family take the people for interrogation that the conflict was resolved.","After listening, Chen Yi asked thoughtfully, \"So you’re saying the Imprisonment Department was ordered by someone to destroy the evidence?\"","Wang Ji recalled, \"I think so too. The Imprisonment Officer who came that day was extremely hostile, and his attitude was very strange.\"","\"If Second Master Xiao and Miss Shen hadn’t been there, I’m afraid I would have been taken away by the Imprisonment Department for questioning as well.\"","Chen Yi nodded and said with a smile, \"Surviving a great disaster is a sign of good fortune to come.\"","\"I hope your auspicious words come true, My Lord.\"","\"I was just saying. You actually took it seriously? You’d be better off burning incense and praying to Buddha in a temple than believing me.\"","\"I will go tomorrow.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi shook his head with a smile. \"I think it would be safer for you to spend a hefty sum to hire two powerful Wandering Martial Artists.\"","Wang Ji readily agreed. \"After this incident, I’ve already had someone ask at the brokerage. I estimate we’ll have a lead soon.\"","\"That would be best. Business at Hundred Herbs Hall is booming now, and I’m counting on you to open branches all over the Great Wei Dynasty.\"","\"Uh...\"","Chen Yi asked with a half-smile, \"Lacking confidence, or lacking ability?\"","Upon hearing this, sweat instantly broke out on Wang Ji’s back. He quickly stood up, bowed, and said:","\"I will go through hell and high water to carry out My Lord’s orders, without hesitation!\"","Although he was apprehensive and indeed lacked confidence, admitting to himself that he was also short on ability, he was somewhat unwilling to give up such an opportunity.","He had squandered half his life, and now that an opportunity he had waited so long for had finally arrived, there was no way he would miss it.","Seeing him so nervous, Chen Yi offered a few words of comfort with a smile, only telling him to focus on running this Hundred Herbs Hall well first.","As for future expansion, that would take time, and they would need to wait for the right opportunity.","After chatting idly for a bit longer, Chen Yi told Wang Ji to go back downstairs and attend to his work. He, on the other hand, remained alone in the quiet room, planning to return later.","’This way, he could avoid being assigned another task by the Xiao Family.’","’This was one of the essential skills for a workhorse—stealing a moment of leisure amidst the hustle and bustle.’","With nothing else to do, Chen Yi sat cross-legged before the tea table and began to cultivate the Four Symbols Skill.","He had sent Xiaodie and the others out today with the intention of cultivating in Spring Lotus Garden, hoping for a breakthrough.","The location had changed to Hundred Herbs Hall, but that was fine too.","Soon, Chen Yi’s mind grew calm.","The True Essence within the two Seas of Qi in his body began to carefully probe the Ren and Du Meridians, attempting to clear the meridians.","According to the Profound Mysteries of the Martial Arts Body, once the Ren and Du Meridians were opened, his Cultivation would break through the Eighth Grade Realm.","At that point, the Four Symbols Skill could also perform a Minor Circulation, which would increase the speed of his cultivation.","As the Cultivation Technique circulated, the final blocked section of the Ren and Du Meridians slowly opened, until only the last membrane remained.","Chen Yi sensed this. With a flicker of his will, he mobilized all the True Essence from his two Seas of Qi and charged through in one go.","BOOM!","A sound like an explosion instantly reverberated in his mind, plunging his consciousness into chaos.","But a moment later, he came to his senses, and a line of text floated before his eyes.","[You have successfully cultivated the Four Symbols Skill. Your Cultivation has broken through to the Lower Seventh Grade.]","Chen Yi felt a sense of relief and continued to circulate the Four Symbols Skill, guiding his True Essence along its new path.","Before long, he slowly withdrew his power, stood up, and stretched a bit.","The sound of his bones cracking and popping instantly rang out. He felt light in body and mind, and the flow of his True Essence was much smoother and more effortless.","Chen Yi clenched his fist, a smile spreading across his face. \"Congratulations, you’ve reached the Seventh Grade achievement in Martial Arts.\"","He glanced out the window and saw that the sky had already darkened, only then realizing that most of the day had passed.","He didn’t stay any longer. Chen Yi called for Wang Ji, preparing to return to the Xiao Family.","Just then, Wang Ji said with a smile, \"My Lord, what a coincidence. You asked me at noon to find some Martial Arts experts, and someone came this afternoon.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Would it be convenient for you to meet them?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment and nodded. \"Might as well take a look.\"","Who would have known that the moment he followed Wang Ji downstairs to the accountant’s office and saw the figure sitting in the chair, he would freeze in astonishment.","’The Sword Madman, Liu Lang?’"]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121 - 122: Shopkeeper Chen, If You Please","paragraphs":["Chen Yi sized up the figure, even using his Qi Observation Skill.","He was sure.","It was Liu Lang.","He now sported a small mustache, and his complexion was pale, no longer ruddy as before. His clothes, appearance, and even the weapon at his waist were different.","But this was, without a doubt, the \"Sword Madman\" Liu Lang—the man who had plundered the Xiao Family’s medicinal herbs.","However, the Liu Lang of this moment was severely injured.","The gash on his chest had not only caused him to lose a great deal of blood, but it had also severely damaged his internal organs and the Sea of Qi at his Chest Acupoint.","Seeing Chen Yi’s silence, Wang Ji glanced at the seemingly oblivious Liu Lang and asked in a low voice:","\"Is something wrong?\"","Since they weren’t in a private room, he didn’t dare address him as \"sir.\"","Chen Yi shook his head slightly and said with a smile, \"Boss Wang, your business has certainly grown. It’s indeed time to hire a few skilled hands from the Jianghu.\"","Hearing the voice, Liu Lang turned his head. His gaze swept past Wang Ji and fell on Chen Yi, and he froze for a moment.","He recognized Chen Yi’s identity—the husband of Xiao Jinghong, the woman who had defeated him in a single move.","But it was precisely because he recognized Chen Yi that he couldn’t help but feel a pang of regret.","’For a remarkable woman like Xiao Jinghong to choose a man who is so clearly beneath her as a husband, all for the sake of the Xiao Family’s interests...’","’How pathetic. How lamentable. What a pity.’","With this in mind, Liu Lang rose and cupped his fist. \"Shopkeeper, do you have any instructions for me?\"","Wang Ji shook his head, then introduced him to Chen Yi. \"This is Brother Liu Yun. His Saber Technique is very formidable.\"","\"During the tryouts this afternoon, he defeated several of the men at the entrance with a single slash. He claims he isn’t afraid of the Evil Demons from the Illusory Sound Sect who came that night.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and greeted Liu Lang—or rather, Liu Yun:","\"Chen Yi from Jishi Medicine Hall, courtesy name Qingzhou. I’ve long been an admirer of Brother Liu’s great name.\"","The corner of Liu Lang’s mouth twitched. ’This man is quite the hypocrite,’ he thought.","’I’m just a nameless nobody in the Jianghu right now. What’s there to admire?’","\"I know you. General Jinghong’s husband, right?\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"My wife is a bit more famous than I am, so it’s not strange that Brother Liu would know of me.\"","Liu Lang nodded. Seeing that they had no further business with him, he sat back down in his chair.","He might have been defeated by Xiao Jinghong, but he was still a Fifth Grade Realm Swordman who had earned the title \"Sword Madman.\" A certain amount of pride was inevitable.","A frail-looking scholar was hardly worth his notice.","’So what if he’s the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law, Xiao Jinghong’s husband?’","Though Chen Yi didn’t know his exact thoughts, he could guess the gist of them. He said no more and started walking toward the exit.","Wang Ji followed, an embarrassed look on his face. \"He’s new and doesn’t quite understand the rules yet. Please... don’t take offense.\"","Chen Yi raised a hand, tracing a few words on Wang Ji’s back as he spoke:","\"No need to see me out, Boss Wang. It’s getting late, so I won’t impose any further.\"","Sensing the message, Wang Ji resisted the urge to look back and nodded in understanding. \"Take care. I won’t see you out.\"","He hadn’t expected the Wandering Martial Artist found by the brokerage to actually attract his lord’s attention, even earning instructions to be taken care of and watched closely.","’On second thought, this must be a good thing. It means I found the right man for the job.’","If Chen Yi knew what Wang Ji was thinking, he probably would have laughed until his sides ached.","He only wanted to find out why Liu Lang was disguised and hiding in Hundred Herbs Hall, and who was responsible for his injuries.","After all, the loss of the Xiao Family’s medicinal herbs that night was, in some way, connected to Liu Lang.","’But he’s probably not in league with the Liu Family. Otherwise, Shen Huatang would never have made it back that night.’","As Chen Yi pondered this, he glanced up at the completely dark sky and quickened his pace toward the Xiao estate.","He had spent more time at Hundred Herbs Hall than he’d realized. He wondered if Xiaodie and the others were back yet.","But just as he passed a tavern, a voice called out from a dark alley nearby.","\"Shopkeeper Chen?\"","Chen Yi’s steps faltered. He glanced to the side.","A middle-aged man in black was staring at him with a vicious grin, a gleaming dagger in his hand.","Instantly, the hair on the back of Chen Yi’s neck stood up. His Black Tortoise Concealment Technique faltered, and he was immediately on high alert.","\"And you are?\"","\"Shopkeeper Chen, come with us. Someone wants to see you.\"","’Us?’","Chen Yi heard footsteps approaching from both the front and back. Realizing he was surrounded, he calmly asked:","\"I wonder who it is that wants to see me? Putting on such a grand display... you’ve frightened me a little.\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, someone from behind gave him a hard shove. Chen Yi went with the force, stumbling into the alley.","\"Just go where you’re told and cut the chatter.\"","Chen Yi feigned a few stumbles before straightening up and sweeping his gaze around. He instantly had a measure of the situation.","’Three at the Ninth Grade Realm, two at the Eighth Grade Realm... I can handle this.’","However, he was in a bustling part of the city, and he only had two choices.","Either he could reveal his Martial Arts Cultivation, or he could go with them and see what this was all about.","Chen Yi quickly made his decision. He felt for the Immortal Drunk in his sleeve and said, \"Lead the way.\"","’Might as well go and see.’","’I’ll see who’s so bold as to send people to ambush me right on the street.’","’Are they so sure I won’t be able to resist?’","The burly Wandering Martial Artists exchanged a glance and sheathed their weapons.","The middle-aged man in the lead nodded, his smile not reaching his eyes. \"A wise choice.\"","\"Shopkeeper Chen, after you.\"","Though he said \"after you,\" the five Wandering Martial Artists immediately formed a circle around Chen Yi, blocking him from the view of any passersby.","But their efforts were clearly unnecessary.","Even in the relatively prosperous Shu State Prefecture City, the alleys were poorly lit after nightfall.","Only when passing the occasional wealthy household would the lanterns hanging by the door cast enough light to illuminate a few feet of ground.","Walking calmly in their midst, shrouded in shadow, Chen Yi memorized the route and kept track of their direction.","They walked for about an hour.","They traveled from the west side of the city to North City, to a location that was, surprisingly, not more than two miles from the Xiao estate.","Chen Yi looked at the large, high-gated courtyard before him. There was no plaque identifying the residence. He raised an eyebrow.","’This person certainly is bold.’","’To be this close to the Xiao estate... aren’t they afraid of being discovered?’","’The darkest place is under the lamp, I suppose.’","Just then, the burly middle-aged man knocked on the gate. It opened, and he stepped aside. \"Please, Shopkeeper Chen.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, deactivated his Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, and stepped into the courtyard, his True Essence beginning to circulate slowly within him.","Inside was a two-courtyard compound.","The front courtyard was rather plain, but the rear courtyard was brightly lit, where he could faintly make out a four-story wooden building with flying eaves.","’Looks like they have a powerful backer.’","’Who could it be?’","Chen Yi thought for a moment, and three possibilities came to mind.","The first was the group that had previously forced him to flee his own wedding.","However, that was unlikely.","Given the strange Cultivation Techniques they used, they were unlikely to send a few common Wandering Martial Artists.","The second was the Hidden Guard.","This was also unlikely.","The Hidden Guard always operated in secret. Exposing their movements and faces as they had today was clearly inconsistent with their identity and methods.","That left only one last possibility...","Just then, Chen Yi’s ears picked up the sounds of breathing and conversation from the tall wooden building.","’One, two... five. Five people inside, too.’","Chen Yi glanced back and saw that his escorts were still behind him. He smiled and asked:","\"Is your master inside?\"","Seeing that Chen Yi could still smile, a vicious look appeared on the burly man’s face. \"To be so calm when you’re about to die... you’re really something.\"","’Die?’","Chen Yi pointed to himself. \"You’re going to kill me?\"","\"Whether you live or die isn’t for us to decide. Get in!\"","Shoved again, Chen Yi shot the man a look, dusted off his clothes, and walked into the wooden building.","Inside the hall were five people.","At the head of the hall sat a young man in brocade robes. He had refined, handsome features, but his expression was somewhat sinister.","Among the other four,","two were seated on either side. They were both older and were scrutinizing him.","The remaining two were clearly guards, standing behind the young man.","SLAM.","The door closed behind him.","Chen Yi knew the guards who had brought him were now standing watch outside. He turned to the people in the hall and performed a formal bow.","\"Chen Yi, courtesy name Qingzhou. My greetings to you all.\"","The young man scoffed, his laughter growing louder. \"Did you all see that? He’s still so prim and proper, even now.\"","\"He really doesn’t know the meaning of fear, haha...\"","An old man beside him stroked his beard. \"Young Master, although he is the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law, he was born and raised in the Chen Family of Jiangnan Prefecture.\"","\"His scholarship is not lacking, nor is his grasp of etiquette.\"","Hearing this, the young man stopped laughing. He looked Chen Yi up and down and nodded as if in agreement.","\"A man of letters should indeed conduct himself this way.\"","With that, he rose to his feet and returned the formal bow. \"Liu Jing of Jing State, courtesy name Liu Huanzhi. My greetings, Brother Chen.\"","A glint flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes. \"I’ve long admired Brother Liu’s great name.\"","’So, it really is the Liu Family of Jing State.’","’Looks like my chances today are indeed slim.’"]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122 - 123: Suppress and Kill","paragraphs":["As the two exchanged scholarly courtesies, an inexplicable breeze rustled through the main hall, its doors and windows sealed shut.","Inside the gauze-covered lamps by the wall, the candle flames flickered gently.","The swaying, dim yellow candlelight stretched everyone’s shadows long.","Chen Yi watched the Liu Family’s Sixth Young Master, who was still laughing uncontrollably. His own expression slowly returned to a state of calm as he asked,","\"I wonder if Brother Liu could tell me why you’ve sought me out tonight?\"","Though he could deduce the general reason, he still wanted to hear Liu Jing’s own explanation.","The Jing State Liu Family’s scheme involving Linglan Pavilion had clearly failed, and the shopkeepers, including Qian Kuan, had already been executed.","Even Liu Hong, the Left Envoy of the Shu State Governor’s Office, had shown no intention of intervening on the Liu Family’s behalf, instead moving swiftly to give the Xiao Family a resolution, as if cutting a tangled knot with one clean strike.","’Why isn’t this Liu Jing thinking about returning to Jing State? Why take this unnecessary step of tracking me down?’","’Could it really be just to kill me and vent his frustration?’","’If that’s really the case, then this Sixth Young Master from the Jing State Liu Family is more witless than I thought.’","Liu Jing’s laughter died down. He looked Chen Yi up and down, a vicious glint slowly appearing in his eyes.","And yet, his face still held the trace of a smile. \"Naturally, I’ve come to invite Brother Chen to join me... to ascend to a high place and gaze into the distance!\"","Chen Yi paused, looked up, and then glanced in the direction of the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","He understood.","’The \"ascend\" part meant climbing to the top of this wooden building.’","’And \"gaze into the distance\" didn’t just mean looking at the horizon. It also meant looking over at the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.’","’Such a malicious method of revenge... truly not something an ordinary person would conceive.’","\"Brother Liu, your particular brand of ingenuity... truly leaves me somewhat... impressed.\"","Liu Jing replied with a humorless smile, \"And you as well, Brother Chen. Your scholarly backbone is quite admirable, I must say.\"","\"It’s just that what I hate most in my life are scholars. They think a little talent and learning gives them the right to look down on others. It’s just absurd.\"","\"I have status, I have wealth, I have men under my command. Why should I compete in scholarly talent with those bookworms who know nothing of the world?\"","\"Don’t you agree, Brother Chen?\"","Chen Yi looked at him, thought seriously for a moment, then nodded and shook his head.","\"What you’ve said, Brother Liu, is correct, but also incorrect.\"","Liu Jing uttered a soft \"Oh?\", the smile completely vanishing from his face.","\"Explain. In what way am I incorrect?\"","\"A scholar’s integrity may seem worthless, but that’s only because there is no scale to weigh it.\"","\"If it could be weighed, everything you just mentioned, Brother Liu, would probably be lighter than a feather in its presence.\"","After hearing Chen Yi’s words, Liu Jing was silent for a long while before gesturing toward the stairs.","\"Why don’t we continue this on the roof, Brother Chen? We can ascend to a high place and gaze into the distance. The view is much better from up there.\"","After giving him a long, searching look, Chen Yi readily complied and followed him upstairs.","The four other men in the main hall followed suit.","The top floor housed an exquisitely furnished study.","It was far more luxurious than Chen Yi’s own study, with signs of meticulous care visible everywhere.","The large, flat-topped desk was made of golden sandalwood, and the brush, ink, paper, and inkstone were all rare works from famous masters.","On the eastern and western walls hung a zither and a sword, symbolizing a mastery of both the scholarly and the martial.","In the main room hung a landscape painting by a famous master. It depicted a scene of Wumeng Mountain and the Chishui River, evoking a profound atmosphere.","A green gauze screen served as a partition, creating a separate tea room. Beside it was an opening leading to an octagonal veranda.","Chen Yi scanned the room and praised it generously, \"The decor here is truly inspired.\"","\"Was this your own design, Brother Liu?\"","Liu Jing shook his head repeatedly. \"You flatter me, Brother Chen. This is merely a temporary residence for me. I had no hand in its decoration.\"","\"What a pity.\"","Chen Yi crossed the gallery and stood behind the railing, looking out at the distant, partially lit Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","The night obscured most of the view.","He could still vaguely make out the wooden buildings of Spring Lotus Garden and Jiaxing Garden.","’It was certainly a view worthy of the phrase \"ascend to a high place and gaze into the distance.\"’","Liu Jing came to his side, stood with his hands clasped behind his back, and also looked at the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion as he asked with a smile, \"What do you think of the view, Brother Chen?\"","Chen Yi nodded, his tone even. \"It’s passable. You’ve gone to some trouble, Brother Liu.\"","He paused briefly before continuing, \"But inviting me here just to ’ascend and gaze’ seems like a bit of a waste.\"","\"You should be well aware, Brother Liu. I’m just a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family. My life or death won’t affect the Xiao Family in the slightest.\"","Upon hearing this, Liu Jing began to laugh again.","\"You’re not wrong, Brother Chen. You’re just an insignificant and disposable figure in the Xiao Family. Killing you wouldn’t be enough to shake them to their core.\"","\"But that is precisely why I’ve resorted to this... cruder strategy of targeting you.\"","Liu Jing paused, then asked with a smile, \"Do you know why I came here this time, Brother Chen? Do you know how much I staked on this?\"","Chen Yi turned his head to look at him. \"I’m listening.\"","\"I volunteered for this assignment in Shu State, to lay the groundwork with Linglan Pavilion. And while crushing the Xiao Family Medicine Hall was part of it, that was only incidental.\"","\"The fundamental reason was for my own sake.\"","\"If everything had gone smoothly, I would have had the chance to change all the signs of Linglan Pavilion to ’Xinglin Hall’.\"","A look of venomous resentment crossed Liu Jing’s face. \"Do you have any idea what that would have meant for me?\"","After a moment’s thought, Chen Yi understood. \"It would have allowed you to gain a firm foothold in the Jing State Liu Family and secure certain inheritance rights.\"","\"Exactly!\"","\"There are six of us—legitimate sons from the main branch.\"","\"If I don’t fight for it, I’ll never have a day in the sun.\"","\"I didn’t just make a military pledge to my father for this opportunity; I bet everything on it.\"","At this point, Liu Jing was practically seething, his words ground out through clenched teeth. \"And now it’s all ruined!\"","\"The Xiao Family could have just given in and closed their Medicine Halls! They didn’t have to fight back! Why did they insist on working against me?\"","\"And Hundred Herbs Hall! Those filthy, lowlife bastards! If they hadn’t stepped in to help, the Xiao Family Medicine Hall would’ve been finished ages ago!\""]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: Suppression Kill","paragraphs":["\"Brother Chen, tell me. In a situation like this, shouldn’t I feel hatred?!\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Yi just looked at him quietly.","After a moment of silence, he finally spoke. \"Indeed, you should.\"","The ferocious look on Liu Jing’s face faded slightly, his expression easing. \"You think so too, right?\"","Chen Yi nodded, his gaze falling upon the darkness outside as he spoke calmly,","\"Hate all you want, but it was foolish of you to come find me.\"","\"Foolish?\"","Liu Jing faltered, his face instantly darkening. \"Brother Chen, I was only indulging you with a few extra words because you seemed to know your place, letting you live a moment longer.\"","\"But your words... they chill my heart. I feel like my earnest goodwill has been thrown to the dogs.\"","Chen Yi let out an incredulous laugh. \"’Earnest goodwill?’ Coming from you, Brother Liu, that’s truly hilarious.\"","\"You?!\"","Just then, an old man behind him spoke up, advising, \"Young Master, there is no need to get angry with a man who is about to die.\"","\"To avoid any unexpected trouble, let’s deal with him quickly. Then we can head to You State to lay low for a while.\"","Liu Jing paused, the anger in his glare at Chen Yi receding. \"You’re right. I shouldn’t waste my breath on him. It’s just a waste of my time.\"","\"Brother Chen, it’s getting late. We’ll send you to the underworld now.\"","\"And when I return from You State, I will make the Xiao Family pay for today’s offense!\"","With that, he leaned in close and whispered with a smirk,","\"I hear that Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong are a pair of exquisite beauties, truly heavenly. I am so looking forward to what I’ll do with the two of them...\"","CRACK!","Before Liu Jing could finish, Chen Yi’s hand, which had been resting behind his back, was already clamped around his throat.","With the slightest pressure, his fingers crushed Liu Jing’s larynx.","Chen Yi then retracted his hand and looked at him, his expression cold.","\"Brother Liu, it would be impolite to say any more.\"","It all happened in an instant.","Chen Yi had moved so fast that even the two old men standing nearby hadn’t noticed a thing.","The two guards posted at the doorway, their backs to the room, also saw nothing.","Liu Jing stared in a daze, only then did a searing pain flare in his throat.","He clutched his throat, trying to scream, but no words would come out.","Only a gurgling whimper, like air escaping a puncture, came out.","He pointed frantically at his throat, pleading with the old men for help. \"Guh... urk...\"","Only then did the two men finally realize something was wrong.","\"Young Master?\"","The two guards, hearing the strange noise, turned around. Just as they were about to see what was happening, their vision blurred.","Chen Yi was already beside them, True Essence erupting from within his body.","He crouched slightly, pulling his arms in close. Mountain Shattering Force coiled around them as True Essence gathered in his hands.","Giving the two Martial Artists no chance to react, Chen Yi drove both palms upward and outward.","—Mountain Shattering·Heaven-Supporting Style!","Instantly, two faintly shimmering, palm-shaped projections of True Essence appeared over his hands.","\"You!?\"","\"How dare you!\"","The two guards’ cultivation was not weak; both were at the Seventh Grade Realm.","Though caught off guard, their reactions were swift, and they both tried to raise their hands to defend themselves.","But they had only just begun to raise their hands when an inexplicable, crushing force bore down on them.","It left them powerless, able only to watch as the palms struck them squarely on the neck.","CRACK! CRACK!","Amidst the crisp, clear sounds.","The necks of the two Seventh Grade Realm Martial Artists snapped backward, the backs of their heads touching their spines.","\"Ugh... urk... Punch...\"","\"Punch... Intent...\"","Before they could finish, they froze, standing completely still.","But Chen Yi didn’t stop there.","He executed the Meteor Butterfly Step, spinning around to strike down the two old men before they could cry for help.","Then, under Liu Jing’s astonished and horrified gaze, he vaulted over the railing of the wooden building. He landed directly behind a group of five men, led by a burly middle-aged man, who had heard the commotion and were about to head upstairs.","The five men heard the landing, paused, and turned to see Chen Yi. One of them roared in anger,","\"What did you do?!\"","Chen Yi looked at the five men in the hall, ignoring their question. He calmly stepped inside and casually closed the door behind him.","He looked at the leader, his gaze sweeping over the others.","\"You were wrong about something a moment ago.\"","\"Whether I live or die is not for your young master to decide.\"","Before the words had even faded, Chen Yi charged.","His body blurred into a streak like a shooting star, leaving a trail of afterimages in his wake.","The burly, middle-aged leader drew his long blade. \"You’re courting death!\"","\"Kill him!\"","The five men surrounded him, their long blades slashing down in unison.","Chen Yi’s footwork faltered for only a fraction of a second, but it was just to sidestep their attack. His eyes remained fixed on the burly, middle-aged man.","His figure flickered. His hands, shaped into palms, slipped past the long blade at an impossible angle and struck the man’s chest.","The man’s chest caved in. His eyes turned bloodshot as he stared down in disbelief.","Holding nothing back, Chen Yi used the Flower-Piercing Step from his Hundred Flowers Palm to weave around to the side of another Eighth Grade Realm Martial Artist.","He raised his hand, forming a blade shape, and jabbed his fingertips through the back of the man’s skull.","Instantly, the Martial Artist lost consciousness, his brain having been turned to mush.","\"Boss?!\"","\"Second Bro—\"","Before the remaining three could cry out in terror, Chen Yi’s form moved like a blossoming flower, its petals brushing past each of them.","THUD. THUD. THUD.","Three muffled thuds echoed in quick succession. Other than Chen Yi, no one else in the hall was left standing.","Chen Yi glanced around the room. Using his Qi Observation Skill to confirm they were all dead, he then strolled upstairs.","By now, Liu Jing was scared out of his wits.","He wanted to jump from the building, but with no knowledge of Martial Arts, he feared the fall would kill him.","He scrambled back into the room, trying to hide under the desk or behind a screen.","But all he did was make a mess of the tidy study; he couldn’t find a single place that felt safe.","\"Ugh, ghh...\"","Hearing the footsteps grow clearer and closer, the fear and panic in Liu Jing’s eyes reached a crescendo.","He threw himself to his knees at the top of the stairs and began kowtowing, smashing his forehead against the floor.","THUD, THUD, THUD...","Amidst the continuous thuds of his head hitting the floor, Chen Yi’s figure appeared at the bend in the staircase.","He looked up at Liu Jing, a gentle smile gracing his lips.","\"Brother Liu, what is the meaning of this?\"","\"Such a posture... you’re tarnishing the name of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi walked to his side and helped him to his feet.","\"To be honest, I much preferred your defiant and unruly demeanor from before.\"","\"It was, at least, fitting for a young master of a Noble Family.\"","\"It prevents me from feeling like my first kill is a worthless coward, which would be a waste of getting my hands dirty.\"","Chen Yi patted his shoulder. \"Here, pull yourself together.\"","Liu Jing stared at him in terror. After a dazed moment, he managed to force a hideous, savage grin. \"Heh... heh...\"","\"Not quite right, but... oh well.\"","Chen Yi looked at the smile, which was uglier than a crying face, and suddenly found the whole thing dull. He raised his hand and snapped his neck.","Liu Jing’s eyes bulged. His head lolled to the side, but that ugly smile remained frozen on his face as he stared at Chen Yi.","Fear, shock, and a smile.","Chen Yi looked at him for a moment, then reached out and brushed a hand over his eyes, closing them to give his face a more peaceful look. Then he dropped the body to the floor.","He scanned the wooden building one last time, confirming there was no other movement.","Then, Chen Yi began to erase all traces of his presence.","This primarily meant the marks left by his Fist Technique, Palm Technique, and Step Technique.","He had heard from Wang Ji at noon about the Imprisonment Department’s investigative methods, so he took some precautions.","After about fifteen minutes.","Once Chen Yi was certain he hadn’t missed anything, he walked out of the residence and headed toward the distant Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","Just as when he had arrived, his steps were so light that they left no footprints.","It was only when he was outside the Marquis’s Mansion that he activated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to mask the True Essence within his body.","Instantly, his scholarly aura returned in full.","Chen Yi looked at the distant lanterns bearing the character \"Xiao.\" He let out a soft breath and walked over at a calm, unhurried pace.","Old Li was right.","Kill a man every ten steps, leaving no trace over a thousand miles.","’I suppose that’s the true meaning of the line. Not just to travel, but to leave no trace of one’s form.’","As he drew closer, Chen Yi saw several figures waiting by the gate.","There was Xiaodie, her face etched with anxiety; Pei Guanli, looking utterly bored; and even Xiao Wan’er, who rarely set foot outside Jiaxing Garden, was standing outside, peering down the street.","Wang Lixing and Ge the Third stood guard beside them.","Hearing his approach, Pei Guanli was the first to spot him and waved eagerly. \"Brother-in-law, you’re finally back!\"","Hearing her voice, the others quickly looked over. They all breathed a sigh of relief when they saw it was Chen Yi.","Xiao Wan’er glanced in the direction he’d come from. Though she was smiling, her tone was tinged with reproach.","\"Brother-in-law, why did you come back that way? Why didn’t you take the main road?\"","Chen Yi chuckled and scratched his head. \"I was at the Hundred Herbs Hall for a while and thought I’d take a shortcut home, but I got a little lost...\"","Xiaodie trotted over, her eyes already welling with tears. \"Young Master, next time you go out, you must take someone with you! You made us... you made us so worried.\"","Chen Yi said a few words to comfort her, then led her inside the gates before turning to Xiao Wan’er apologetically.","\"My apologies, Eldest Sister. I’ve made you worry.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze for a moment, then turned her head and started walking into the mansion.","\"Who... who was worried about you?\"","\"Hurry up and get inside. The food’s gotten cold from waiting for you.\"","Chen Yi chuckled and called out, \"Coming...\"","After everyone had gone inside.","Ge the Third, however, remained at the gate, staring suspiciously at his retreating back.","’The scent on the Fledgling seems... a little strange...’"]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: Heaven’s Will is on My Side","paragraphs":["Chen Yi’s unexpected late return this time had likely truly worried the people of the Xiao Mansion.","So much so that when he came out after washing up and changing his clothes, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but say a few words.","She started by explaining, \"When Guanli and Huatang returned tonight, they waited and waited but saw no sign of you, so they came to find me.\"","Then, she distanced herself from the decision: \"I figured you’d be fine, but Wuge was a little worried, so I was the one who sent Huatang and the others to look for you.\"","Xiao Wuge: ???","Xiao Wan’er ignored his look and continued with a reminder:","\"Next time, remember to stick to the main roads. After all, you haven’t been out of the mansion many times, and you’ve always had the mansion’s Personal Guards with you. It’s easy to get lost wandering the streets and alleys at night.\"","As she reached the end, her tone was tinged with a bit of lingering fear.","\"If something had happened to you, how could I have explained it to Second Sister? After all, I was the one who sent you to Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Chen Yi agreed to it all, acting obedient and docile.","At a time like this, saying anything else would only displease those who were concerned about him.","The best thing to do was to remain silent and smile.","Before long, Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang returned. Upon seeing him, they both breathed a sigh of relief.","But upon learning that he had gotten lost in unfamiliar streets and alleys, Xie Tingyun, with her straightforward and carefree personality, said bluntly:","\"Young Master-in-law, you’re not familiar with the roads in the Prefecture City. It’s best if you go out less.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, but his eyes looked toward Xiao Wan’er.","’See? I told you I should just stay in the mansion.’","Xiao Wan’er naturally understood the meaning in his eyes. She gave a rare roll of her eyes and turned her head away, refusing to look at him.","\"It’s so late. Let’s eat first.\"","Chen Yi grinned and immediately picked up his chopsticks, digging into a bowl of rice.","He had been too active tonight and was so hungry his stomach felt like it was stuck to his spine.","Even Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, Xiaodie, and the others ate more than usual, perhaps due to the emotional rollercoaster they had been on.","Only Pei Guanli, who had long known about Chen Yi’s Martial Arts Cultivation, was completely unfazed.","Earlier, while waiting for Chen Yi to return, she had been the least worried of them all.","After dinner.","The group dispersed.","Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge returned to their rooms to rest.","Chen Yi, meanwhile, took a teapot to the pavilion to enjoy the summer night’s breeze.","Perhaps because it had been a long time since he’d come here this late, the Golden Carp seemed to remember him. They leaped and splashed, their tails flinging water all over him.","\"Holding a grudge, are we?\"","\"Just you wait...\"","Chen Yi chuckled and cursed under his breath, his mood finally relaxing completely.","Martial Arts were, in the end, the art of killing.","He had understood this from the moment he began his Cultivation and had long since prepared himself mentally.","Besides, the person he had killed tonight was someone like Liu Jing. He could just consider it ridding the world of a pest.","However, Liu Jing dying in Shu State at this time would likely change the course of some events.","Even if the people from the Imprisonment Department or the Liu Family didn’t trace it back to him, they would still suspect the Xiao Family.","There was no doubt about this.","After all, the Xiao and Liu Families had just had a minor clash.","Although it was merely an initial probe by the Liu Family, and apart from the deaths of Qian Kuan and his men, neither side had suffered significant losses.","But at a time like this, for the Sixth Young Master of the Jing State Liu Family to die in Shu State...","...the development of events would surely exceed the expectations of those in the know.","’The Xiao Family and the Liu Family should have tacitly downplayed this matter...’","Chen Yi watched the Golden Carp in the pond while slurping his tea.","His face was calm, but his mind was already a storm of crashing waves.","On an invisible game board, he picked up and put down white stones from the box, one by one.","The positions of the Heizi shifted unpredictably as he deduced several possibilities.","’The worst-case scenario is that this becomes the fuse that ignites a war between the Xiao and Liu Families.’","’The next worst is that the Xiao Family bows its head slightly, joins forces with the Imprisonment Department, and finds the person who killed Liu Jing—which is me.’","’After that, the Liu Family could accept their loss and proactively retreat, temporarily burying this grudge and waiting for an opportunity to make a comeback.’","’And the best outcome would be for the Xiao and Liu Families to shake hands and make peace...’","However, Chen Yi knew in his heart.","If the Jing State Liu Family wanted to use this as a pretext, then Liu Hong, the Left Envoy of the Shu State Governor’s Office, was the sharpest Blade in their hands.","Although the Jing State Liu Family had previously been dissatisfied with how Liu Hong handled the Linglan Pavilion incident, they were all still Lius at the end of the day.","Whether it was the Lius of Shu State or the Lius of Jing State, if they wanted to deal with the Xiao Family, they had to support each other.","’So, if the Xiao and Liu Families really do go to war in the future, the key will be Liu Hong.’","While labeling Liu Hong with the identity of a \"Heizi,\" Chen Yi recalled what he had recently learned about the political situation in Shu State.","The Shu State Governor’s Office, the Inspectorate Office, and the Capital Commandery each had two envoys.","Nominally, the Left Envoy was the head and the Right Envoy was the subordinate, but their official ranks were the same.","The Governors were both Junior Second Grade, in charge of a prefecture’s civil administration and taxation, with the Revenue Department and the Household Registration Bureau under them.","This system was designed to allow the Left and Right Envoys to counterbalance each other.","However, in the current Shu State Governor’s Office, the Right Envoy, Yang Ye, was old and about to retire to his hometown, giving him the air of someone who no longer cared for political affairs.","Therefore, Liu Hong, who was in his prime, effectively reigned supreme in the Governor’s Office.","’I must put some pressure on Liu Hong.’","’Otherwise, with no one in Shu State to check his power, he poses too great a threat to the Xiao Family.’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi placed the most crucial white stone on the board.","It was—the Right Envoy of the Shu State Governor’s Office, Yang Ye!","An old man on the brink of retirement, originally completely unrelated to this affair, was about to become the key piece that would determine the outcome of the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families.","With a rough plan in mind.","Chen Yi put down the teapot, let out a long breath, and stood up to look at the night sky.","He saw a thick bank of dark clouds appear beneath the once-bright full moon.","Immediately after, raindrops began to fall—PATTER, PATTER—on the pavilion roof.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. ’It seems heaven is on my side.’","Under the cover of the rain, the aura in that courtyard, along with any tracks he left after coming from Hundred Herbs Hall, would all be washed away.","If this wasn’t the will of heaven, what was?","After standing silently for a moment.","Chen Yi put away the teacup and returned to the wooden building to rest, a few thoughts surfacing in his mind:","’Getting Yang Ye to side with the Xiao Family will be difficult, but not impossible.’","’I’m afraid I’ll have to spend some time getting closer to Li Huai’gu.’","There was no other way. To move Yang Ye, this chess piece, going through Li Huai’gu was the most direct method.","After all, his wife was Yang Ye’s adopted daughter.","However, the fastest way to influence Li Huai’gu was through his teacher—Mr. Yue Ming of Guiyun Academy.","At this thought, Chen Yi couldn’t help but grimace as if he had a toothache.","After going around in circles, he seemed to have returned to the one question he had been avoiding for the past two days—","whether or not to accept the Instructor position at Guiyun Academy.","’It seems I don’t have a choice in the matter anymore.’","...","Just after 3 a.m.","The sky above Shu State Prefecture City boomed with continuous thunder, and flashes of lightning illuminated the night, one after another.","But in the torrential downpour, a pedestrian’s vision was still blurred and obscured by the curtain of rain.","In a residence about five li from the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","A group of more than a dozen Imprisonment Officers, wearing Raincoats, long Blades hanging from their waists, and rain boots on their feet, were busy working in the downpour.","\"Damn it all! This rain could’ve come earlier or later, but it just had to pour nonstop at a time like this.\"","A slender Imprisonment Officer walked through the courtyard, reminding his colleagues to carefully avoid the central area.","\"Everyone, pay attention! Don’t mess up the footprints.\"","\"It’s already a mess. If you all keep trampling all over the place, how the hell am I supposed to investigate this case?\"","The surrounding men cursed back good-naturedly and didn’t cause any more trouble.","Instead, they hurried into the main hall and cupped their hands in a salute to a woman inside who had taken off her Raincoat and was dressed in red brocade.","\"Lord Hundred Households, your subordinate has already questioned the surrounding residents. None of them saw any suspicious individuals pass by last night.\"","\"Only one person heard a disturbance from this direction, but because they were too far away, they thought it was just someone arguing.\"","The woman in red grunted in acknowledgment. Her gaze remained on the five corpses in the hall as she circulated her True Essence to probe the surrounding fluctuations in Spiritual Qi.","But too much time had passed, and she found nothing.","However, the corpses themselves offered some clues.","\"The killer was decisive, and every blow was fatal. His Cultivation and Technique are clearly far superior to these people’s.\"","\"Middle Three Grades, or... at least Upper Seventh Grade.\"","\"Additionally, he is skilled in Palm Technique and Body Technique, and possesses great Power.\"","\"He should be a tall, sturdy person with powerful muscles and bones. The Pile Skill he practices must be of a high grade.\"","The woman in red had someone record her findings, then she went up to the top-floor study.","She glanced past the two sickly old men and looked at Liu Jing lying on the floor, letting out a soft \"Huh?\"","She squatted down to observe him closely for a moment, then felt Liu Jing’s neck, her brow furrowing slightly.","\"The killer had a grudge against this man.\"","Hearing this, a nearby Imprisonment Officer asked in confusion, \"Lord Hundred Households Fang, how did you determine that he had a grudge against these people?\"","The woman in red stood up, her eyes scanning the surroundings as she spoke:","\"The killer crushed his throat first before killing the others. He clearly wanted him to live for a few moments longer.\"","She paused, then looked at the Imprisonment Officer and said grimly, \"And being alive at that moment would only have been more painful.\"","The Imprisonment Officer’s face lit with understanding, and he immediately began to flatter her, \"As expected of Hundred Households Fang, renowned throughout the Shu State Imprisonment Department.\"","\"Just tell us what to do.\"","The woman in red pondered for a moment. \"First, investigate the identities of these people.\"","\"Judging from their clothing and the decor here, they must have some background.\""]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: Such Great Power","paragraphs":["By now, the number of pedestrians on the street had gradually increased.","Most were merchants trying to make a living, servants and female family members from various households out for supplies, and government officials who needed to report for duty.","Even in such a downpour, they still had to go out.","And so, as they passed by South Street, the people coming and going all noticed the Imprisonment Officers outside the residence facing the street.","Unable to restrain their curiosity, most would go up and ask the crowd that was gathering in the rain.","\"Brother, what’s goin’ on in there? Somethin’ feels real off.\"","\"A huge case, I tell ya! Heard the bodies are piled up in there, their necks bent all the way back to their spines.\"","\"Just look at the Imprisonment Officer’s face. She’s worried sick.\"","\"There were hardly any clues to begin with, and on top of that, this damn storm hit. The killer’s footprints have been washed away to nothin’.\"","The Shu State dialect rose and fell, but passersby could still hear it clearly.","Looks of fear appeared on one face after another.","In times of peace, how much blood could the common folk have seen?","They might see a bit of gore during the New Year’s pig slaughter, or when a vicious criminal was sentenced to beheading by the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and executed outside the East and West Markets.","They might be scared at the time, but once it was over, it was over.","But a major case involving human life was different.","Until the murderer was caught, it would always leave the people nearby feeling terrified at night.","Just then, a figure walked out from the stately courtyard.","It was Fang Hongxiu, the Hundred Households from the Shu State Imprisonment Department in charge of investigating this case.","She was quite beautiful, with fair skin, red lips, and the ends of her eyebrows tilted slightly upward, framing a pair of peach-blossom eyes.","Her tall, full figure, set off by her bright red Imprisonment Officer’s robe, gave her a heroic air and a distinctly sharp, dashing aura.","Fang Hongxiu stood under the eaves, her eyes sweeping over the surrounding crowd.","She checked them one by one but found no suspicious individuals who might have returned to the scene. A sliver of disappointment couldn’t help but surface in her heart.","In her years of experience as an investigator, she knew that a small number of perpetrators would return to watch from the scene of the crime.","Some wanted to know the progress of the Imprisonment Department’s investigation; others were gloating over what they had done.","This was especially true for a case like the one behind her.","The victim’s death was horrific, he was clearly from a prominent family, and the scene was so clean it looked as if it had been swept.","It was enough for her to determine that the killer was a meticulous, calm, and seasoned individual.","’People like that often leave flaws in inconspicuous places.’","Fang Hongxiu thought about this, then composed her expression, clasped her hands toward the surrounding crowd, and said loudly:","\"This is a major case. If any of you have any leads, please report to the Imprisonment Department at any time.\"","\"If a lead proves helpful to this case, the Imprisonment Department will offer a reward of silver coins.\"","The words had barely left her mouth when, before the crowd could start murmuring, several Imprisonment Officers came running from outside.","The leader, a tall young man, had a grim expression—or perhaps it was a bit panicked.","He rushed over without bothering to salute. \"Lord, something’s happened! We’ve identified the person inside...\"","Fang Hongxiu raised a hand to cut him off, led them directly into the courtyard, and then gestured for them to continue.","\"The deceased is the Jing State Liu Family’s Sixth Young Master, Liu Jing. He’s the owner of the Linglan Pavilion from the other day.\"","\"Are you certain?\"","\"Lord Hundred Households, on a matter like this, this subordinate would not dare to speak recklessly.\"","\"Liu Jing...\"","A solemn expression immediately appeared on Fang Hongxiu’s face as her gaze shifted toward the nearby Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","\"The Xiao Family did this?\"","’But the Liu Family had already taken a step back, and there were rumors that the Xiao Family had agreed to let the matter drop.’","Fang Hongxiu could not figure out why the Xiao Family would make a move.","But she knew in her heart that this case was about to stir up a whole new mess.","...","With such a major case happening so close to the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, the Xiao Family naturally got wind of it quickly.","Even if the details weren’t clear yet, a few of the servants returning from their errands would have a thing or two to say.","Soon, people were gossiping in the front, middle, and rear courtyards.","Ge the Third had woken up at the crack of dawn, oblivious as he fed the horses and fitted their reins.","Though his hands were busy, his mind was preoccupied with other matters.","The expression on his face shifted from time to time, a clear sign he wasn’t in the best of moods.","He was supposed to be out inspecting the Medicine Halls with Wang Lixing these past few days, taking care of some private business on the side.","But unexpectedly, those young mistresses from the rear courtyard insisted he take them out for a drive, saying the young master-in-law had praised his steady driving and easygoing nature.","Hearing this, Ge the Third’s feelings were complicated, to say the least.","’He never would have thought that his usual laughing and joking in front of the Fledgling, a deliberate attempt to get closer, would have this kind of side effect.’","’While this reaction from the Fledgling was something he was happy to see, he had important things to do soon.’","’How could he spend all his time chauffeuring those young ladies around?’","’But he had no choice.’","Before returning to the mansion last night, Granny Shan’s granddaughter had specifically instructed him that they were going out again today, telling him to have the carriage ready first thing in the morning.","’Damn it.’","’This little patch of land called Shu State... what’s there to even see?’","Ge the Third cursed under his breath, but his movements didn’t slow. After preparing the carriage, he left the stables and headed to the front courtyard.","There, he heard several Household Servants and Armored Warriors talking:","\"I heard the Liu Family’s Sixth Young Master was found dead in his courtyard this morning. They say it was a horrifying sight.\"","Ge the Third’s heart skipped a beat, but he walked over with the same smile he always wore.","\"What are you all talking about? Sounds like someone died?\"","\"Old Third, take a guess.\"","\"Guess my ass. Just spit it out.\"","The Armored Warrior then lowered his voice and said, \"Last night, that Young Master Liu from Jing State died.\"","Hearing this, Ge the Third’s expression flickered slightly.","’He knew more about Liu Jing’s background and purpose than most people in the mansion.’ He couldn’t help but ask:"]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126 - 125: Surprisingly Potent","paragraphs":["\"How’d he die?\"","\"He was murdered, of course.\"","\"I heard it wasn’t just him. His Guards, Staff Officers, everyone who came with him... every last one of them was...\"","Seeing the Armored Warrior make a chopping motion across his neck, Ge the Third began to wonder.","’This couldn’t have been the work of the Punishment Hall, could it?’","’If this was ordered by the Second Master, there’s going to be chaos within the Xiao Family.’","Ge the Third was well aware of Xiao Wang’s and Xiao Dongchen’s ambitions.","They were ruthless enough to come up with a vicious plot like burning the granaries of the Three Towns; secretly slaughtering a direct descendant of the Jing State Liu Family wouldn’t be beyond them.","Just as he was pondering this, he heard someone else say, \"And the place where that Young Master Liu died isn’t far from here. It’s just to the west.\"","’West?’","Something stirred in Ge the Third’s mind, and he couldn’t help but ask a few more questions. \"West of South Street?\"","\"Yeah, about five li from here.\"","Ge the Third looked in the direction the man was pointing. Five li away, to the west, died last night...","For some reason, a figure surfaced in his mind.","Fledgling!","Ge the Third recalled the strange smell on Chen Yi last night, and the more he thought about it, the more plausible it seemed.","But after a moment’s thought, he instinctively wavered.","After all, he knew Chen Yi had only recently begun his journey in Martial Arts. He didn’t practice his Cultivation diligently and was at most a Lower Ninth Grade Martial Artist.","Given Liu Jing’s status, his Guards had to be at least at the Seventh Grade Realm.","’Could Fledgling really have killed them all on his own?’","As Ge the Third mulled this over, his gaze drifted toward the rear courtyard. After some hesitation, he made a decision.","’Regardless of whether Fledgling was behind this, I have to test him.’","’I can’t let him get into any unexpected trouble, one way or another.’","Just then, Ge the Third spotted three figures passing through the veranda.","One of them was skipping along, the JINGLE JINGLE of bells growing louder as they approached.","It was none other than Pei Guanli, Shen Huatang, and Xie Tingyun.","From a distance, Pei Guanli waved cheerfully. \"Ge the Third, Ge the Third! Hurry, get the horses ready! We’re leaving.\"","\"We’re going for a trip outside the city today. I heard the Chishui River tide is intense after the heavy rain. It must be a spectacular sight.\"","\"Right, Sister Tingyun, Sister Huatang?\"","Xie Tingyun, holding an umbrella, nodded nonchalantly.","\"Please wait a moment, you two. I’ll be right back.\"","Ge the Third put on a smile, but couldn’t help cursing inwardly.","’With these little madams around, it’s impossible for me to get anything done.’","...","「In Spring Lotus Garden.」","Chen Yi had a rare full night’s sleep. He didn’t get up to wash and dress until after Pei Guanli had left.","As Xiaodie straightened his collar, she asked, \"Young Master, are you going to the Medicine Hall today?\"","Recalling his plans from the previous night, Chen Yi said he wasn’t going. He then asked, \"Have Pei Guanli and the others gone out?\"","A smile spread across Xiaodie’s face. \"They left right after breakfast. Sister Huatang and Sister Tingyun went with them.\"","\"Why didn’t you go?\"","\"Young Master...\"","Xiaodie’s smile froze. She pouted and said, \"You nearly got lost last night. I don’t dare let you go out alone again.\"","But then, a look of lingering fear appeared on her face as she said mysteriously:","\"Young Master, something else happened this morning.\"","\"This morning, I heard from one of the older maids in the front courtyard who does the purchasing...\"","\"Young Master, isn’t that terrifying? That’s why you can’t take those small alleys anymore next time. What if...\"","Chen Yi wasn’t particularly surprised to hear that Liu Jing and his men had been discovered. He smiled and tapped her on the forehead.","\"Don’t say such unlucky things.\"","Xiaodie clutched her head. \"I’m just worried about your safety, Young Master.\"","Chen Yi understood her good intentions, of course. He offered a few comforting words with a smile, then went downstairs to have breakfast with Xiao Wuge.","During the meal, he naturally asked about how Xiaodie and the others’ outing had gone yesterday.","When he learned that Pei Guanli had made Ge the Third carry her things while she shopped in the West Market, he couldn’t help but give her a silent thumbs-up.","’Keep Ge the Third busy for now, so he doesn’t have a chance to go running around outside.’","He knew that compared to the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families, burning the grain of the Three Towns was a far more earth-shattering event.","Even though the Three Towns were heavily guarded, the secretive Hidden Guard should have a way to pull it off.","But the matter was difficult. Even if Chen Yi were to do it himself, it would require careful planning.","Besides finding the right person and the right time to act, the most crucial thing was to ensure he couldn’t be implicated.","Every single detail would require a great deal of time and energy to plan.","’In any case, I just can’t let Ge the Third have any free time to go out.’","After the meal, Chen Yi had no other plans.","He decided to continue teaching Xiao Wuge how to play chess and, at the same time, have Xiaodie ask if Mr. Sun the Elder was free.","Since he had decided to take a position as an Instructor at Guiyun Academy, he needed to find a plausible reason.","After thinking it over, the only suitable person was Elder Sun, with whom he had a tacit understanding.","’As for the others...’","’Xiao Wan’er would cooperate, but she’d probably nag a bit.’","’She’d probably say something like, \"Brother-in-law should have decided this long ago! Someone else can be the Shopkeeper of Jishi Medicine Hall, don’t you worry!\"’","’The Old Master’s mind was preoccupied with the Xiao Family, the Liu Family, the Dingyuan Army, and the Mutual Market.’","’He’d most likely just humor me and wouldn’t offer any real advice.’","’And then there’s the Old Master’s relationship with Mr. Yue Ming... Better not to step on that landmine.’","’Wouldn’t want the Old Master to start reminiscing about the late Old Mistress again.’","However, before Chen Yi could send Xiaodie out, an Armored Warrior came to report:","\"Young Master, you have a visitor.\"","Chen Yi was a bit surprised. He couldn’t think of who would be looking for him.","’Liu Quan was just here two days ago, so everything at Jishi Medicine Hall should be fine.’","’I was just at Hundred Herbs Hall yesterday, so Wang Jiying wouldn’t be coming either.’","\"Who is it?\"","\"Lord Li Huai’gu, Advisor to the Governor’s Office.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. After a moment’s thought, he ordered the warrior to show the man in.","He had just been thinking last night about getting closer to Li Huai’gu.","And now the man had shown up on his own initiative.","’Could it be that Mr. Yue Ming got impatient and sent him as a persuader?’","It had to be said, Li Huai’gu’s timing was perfect.","He was clearly a more suitable candidate than Mr. Sun the Elder.","Before long, Li Huai’gu, dressed in plain clothes and holding an umbrella, walked in. He seemed to breathe a sigh of relief upon seeing Chen Yi sitting in the pavilion with a game board in front of him.","\"Brother Qingzhou, my apologies for the intrusion. I hope you’ll forgive me.\"","\"Brother Fang Gui, you’re too kind. Please, sit.\"","Li Huai’gu sat down opposite him but didn’t mention Guiyun Academy. Instead, he asked:","\"I hear Brother Qingzhou has been in charge of Jishi Medicine Hall recently. Do you happen to know any renowned doctors in Shu State?\"","Chen Yi looked at him with some surprise. \"If I remember correctly, isn’t Brother Fang Gui’s family also a Noble Family of physicians?\"","\"Brother Qingzhou jests. My father’s Medical Skill is only good for treating common colds. We could hardly be called a Noble Family.\"","\"Then why come to me asking about renowned doctors... Is someone sick?\"","Li Huai’gu nodded and said with a wry smile, \"I’m afraid you may not know yet, Brother Qingzhou. Your older brother, Chen Yunfan... he...\"","\"He’s been on sick leave for four or five days.\"","\"At first, I thought he was faking it, but when I paid him a visit yesterday, I realized he’s truly bedridden.\"","A strange expression came over Chen Yi’s face, and he couldn’t help but ask, \"Bedridden how, exactly?\"","Li Huai’gu gave another wry smile. \"He just sleeps and sleeps, like he’s drunk.\"","\"We’ve had Physicians look at him during this time, but none of them can find anything wrong.\"","\"The summer harvest in Shu State is already over, and the Governor’s Office urgently needs to inspect the granaries in each county and collect taxes. But right at this critical moment...\"","\"As a last resort, I had no choice but to come and ask for your help, Brother Qingzhou, to see if you can find a Divine Doctor.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi already understood the cause of Chen Yunfan’s illness.","What he hadn’t expected was just how potent the Immortal Drunk was."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127 - 126: This Miss Cui...","paragraphs":["The news that Chen Yunfan still hadn’t woken up struck Chen Yi as both amusing and a little alarming. The Immortal Drunk was far too potent.","He had, of course, intended to amplify its effects when he was developing the formula.","But knocking out a Middle Third-Grade Martial Artist for several days straight was bound to attract unwanted attention.","Not to mention, once Chen Yunfan himself woke up, he would likely want a bottle of Immortal Drunk for his own protection.","’Hmm... It seems I do have a bottle on hand.’","With this in mind, Chen Yi did not refuse the request.","\"I’ll go ask Doctor Ma at the Medicine Hall later.\"","\"To be honest with you, Brother Fang Gui, this Doctor Ma of my Jishi Medicine Hall practiced in the Wumeng Mountain region for many years. His Medical Skill is quite remarkable.\"","Chen Yi, of course, knew perfectly well whether the doctor was actually capable or not.","Fortunately, with him pulling the strings behind the scenes, \"treating\" Chen Yunfan wouldn’t be difficult.","Li Huai’gu’s face lit up. He quickly cupped his hands and said, \"Thank you for your help, Brother Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi gestured for him to drop the formalities. \"Brother Fang Gui, you seem to have forgotten,\" he said with a smile. \"He is my brother, after all.\"","Of course, Chen Yunfan being his brother was only one of his reasons for getting involved.","More importantly, Chen Yunfan was the current Imperial Top Scholar, the Assistant Governor of the Shu State Governor’s Office, and probably had a mission from the emperor himself.","If he remained in this deep slumber, it would likely cause unnecessary complications.","Li Huai’gu smiled and nodded. \"That’s a relief.\"","In fact, over the past two days, Chen Yunfan’s servants had visited every renowned Medicine Hall in Shu State to no avail. They were so frantic they were considering sending him all the way back to Jiangnan Prefecture.","When he went over yesterday and saw the situation, he immediately reported it to Yang Ye.","The two conferred and decided to help find some renowned doctors to see if Chen Yunfan could be woken.","His visit to Chen Yi was a desperate, last-ditch effort.","The two then made small talk for a while.","Chen Yi deliberately steered the conversation toward Guiyun Academy, asking if Mr. Yue Ming was still pestering him about it.","Li Huai’gu’s expression flickered. \"To be honest, ever since I got married, every time I see our teacher, he urges me to come to the Marquis’s Mansion and try to persuade you.\"","\"If I hadn’t been so busy with official duties at the Governor’s Office lately, I would have paid you a visit much sooner.\"","Li Huai’gu paused before continuing his persuasion.","\"Brother Qingzhou, our teacher’s invitation for you to become an Instructor at Guiyun Academy... while he may have his own motives, he truly has your best interests at heart.\"","\"Forgive my bluntness, but now that you’ve married into the Xiao Family, seeking a post in the government or the military would inevitably arouse suspicion from certain quarters.\"","\"At Guiyun Academy, however, you wouldn’t have to worry about any of that.\"","\"You could not only devote yourself to your studies and showcase your talents but also build a fine reputation for yourself.\"","It was heartfelt, earnest advice.","Normally, given Li Huai’gu’s personality, his relationship with Chen Yi would have been a distant, formal one—the friendship of gentlemen, as bland as water.","But between Mr. Yue Ming’s request and Chen Yi’s own helpfulness toward him, he felt he could speak from the heart.","Upon hearing this, Chen Yi’s expression relaxed.","Li Huai’gu’s words gave him the perfect pretext to accept Mr. Yue Ming’s invitation.","Still, thinking of what his life would become, he couldn’t help but feel a little wistful.","If it weren’t for the Hidden Guard, if it weren’t for what happened last night, he could have found a way to weasel out of it, even if Xiao Jinghong herself tried to force him.","But reality had a way of foiling the best-laid plans.","Seeing it was getting late, Chen Yi suggested they go visit Chen Yunfan.","Li Huai’gu readily agreed.","The sooner Chen Yunfan woke up, the sooner the matters at the Governor’s Office could be properly handled.","A moment later, after Chen Yi wrote out a prescription in his study—imitating Ma Liangcai’s handwriting—and put it away, he instructed Xiaodie to take Xiao Wuge to Jiaxing Garden.","Once they were gone, he opened an umbrella and left Spring Lotus Garden with Li Huai’gu.","The moment he stepped out of the rear courtyard, Chen Yi noticed something was off about the expressions of the Armored Warriors in the mansion. They looked as though they were facing a formidable enemy.","He had a suspicion that news of Liu Jing’s death had arrived, putting the entire mansion on high alert.","Even Li Huai’gu, walking beside him, seemed to notice something was amiss.","However, since they were in the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion with so many eyes and ears around, it wasn’t convenient for him to speak openly.","Just then, they came face to face with Second Master Xiao Wang, who was leading several men dressed in Crimson Brocade Clothing.","Xiao Wang, dressed in a long black robe, had an air of natural authority. He glanced at Chen Yi and Li Huai’gu before hurrying past without a second look.","Chen Yi stopped and looked back, a fluorescent glint flashing deep in his eyes.","Under his Qi Observation Skill, the auras of the men in Crimson Brocade Clothing were fully revealed.","’Two at the Seventh Grade, two at the Eighth...’","’Are they from the Punishment Hall?’","Chen Yi turned back, his expression thoughtful.","’It seems the old master and Xiao Wang are preparing to make a move.’","’But according to my calculations, even if the Liu Family wants to use this as a pretext to cause trouble, they won’t act so quickly.’","’For one, the Jing State Liu Family will have to consult Liu Hong. For another, the Xiao Family’s response is also critical.’","’After all, the Xiao and Liu Families are both major wealthy families. If they truly decide to take action, the conflict will drag in far more than just the two of them.’","Seeing his odd expression, Li Huai’gu asked tactfully, \"Did I come at an inopportune time?\"","Chen Yi understood his meaning and shook his head. \"Everything is business as usual at the Medicine Hall. Let’s go pick up Doctor Ma first.\"","Li Huai’gu nodded and didn’t press the matter.","Chen Yi then followed him into a carriage, which headed for the East Market.","The sky was still blanketed by dark, oppressive clouds.","Lightning flashed, thunder rumbled, and a torrential downpour began.","Through the blurry rain-streaked view, Chen Yi noticed a significant increase in the number of government officials and Imprisonment Officers on the streets.","Most of them held portraits, questioning every person who passed by.","Chen Yi glanced at one of the portraits. Seeing it was of the five burly men who had abducted him last night, he lost interest.","’This world has many methods of investigation, but none are particularly efficient.’","’Especially after I deliberately cleaned up the scene last night, there’s little chance the Imprisonment Department will trace it back to me.’","’The torrential rain will have washed away what few footprints those thugs left behind.’","’The number of usable clues is minuscule.’","’In a situation like this, short of a lucky break, I can’t imagine what the Imprisonment Department could possibly do.’","’Then again, a lack of clues can sometimes fuel even more speculation.’","’Take the members of the Jing State Liu Family and the Shu State Liu Family, for example.’","’The longer the Imprisonment Department fails to find the killer, the more certain they’ll become that the Xiao Family was behind it.’","’All in all, the flap of this butterfly’s wings has certainly kicked up a tornado.’","Soon, the carriage stopped outside Jishi Medicine Hall.","Chen Yi went in alone to find Ma Liangcai. After a few quiet words of instruction, he brought the physician along and headed straight for Chen Yunfan’s residence.","The crippled physicians Wang Ji had found didn’t have much in the way of Medical Skill, but their talent for acting and setting a scene was second to none.","They were not only shrewd but also cunning.","Fortunately, Chen Yi had never revealed himself, always giving Ma Liangcai orders in Wang Ji’s name. So far, the deception had held.","「About an hour later.」","The carriage stopped in an alley in the western part of the city, and the three of them got out.","\"This is my brother’s residence?\"","Chen Yi looked at the character for \"Chen\" on the gate and glanced around. \"It’s quite secluded.\"","But as soon as he was led inside by Chun Ying, who had rushed out to greet them, he immediately retracted that thought.","The sound of falling rain, string and bamboo instruments, and wind chimes mingled in a continuous stream of noise. It was anything but secluded.","As he thought this, Chen Yi noticed several carriages parked in the front courtyard.","Besides one carriage bearing the Chen Family crest, the other three were also adorned with silk canopies. Atop each was the insignia of a \"Long River Sunset Painting.\"","From the look of them, they belonged to a young lady from a prominent family.","Chun Ying seemed to notice his gaze. As she led the way, she whispered:","\"Lord Councilor, Young Master Yi, you’ve come at an inconvenient time. Someone has just arrived to treat the Young Master.\"","Li Huai’gu smiled. \"No matter. We can wait a moment.\"","\"If their Medical Skill is great enough to wake Brother Yunfan, it would be a good thing.\"","Chen Yi nodded, but he was more interested in who the visitors were.","\"Who is it? They don’t look like they’re from around Shu State.\"","Chun Ying glanced back at him and said hesitantly, \"To be honest, Young Master Yi, it is someone from the Qinghe Cui Family.\"","Realization dawned on Chen Yi, followed by a strange expression. \"It couldn’t be... *her*, could it?\"","Chun Ying nodded. Saying no more, she hurriedly led them to a side hall in the rear courtyard before heading off toward a wing on the other side.","Chen Yi watched her go, his gaze following her toward the wing.","The Qinghe Cui Family was the maiden family of the Chen Family’s matriarch, Cui Yu. It was also the family of the young woman engaged to Chen Yunfan.","Moreover, like the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, the Cui Family was a Noble Family with a five-hundred-year lineage.","In terms of official positions, connections, and wealth, they were in no way inferior to the Chen Family.","In comparison, the Xiao Family, with its mere two-hundred-year heritage, was little more than \"new money\" in the eyes of the Chen and Cui Families.","Just as Chen Yi was mulling this over, three women and an old man, clearly a physician, emerged from the distant wing.","The woman in the lead was every bit as beautiful as Xiao Jinghong or Xiao Wan’er.","She had an oval face and captivating eyes, and was dressed in a long pink gown. She was leading her small party toward them.","Chun Ying hurried after her, offering words of reassurance.","\"My young master is in perfect health. Several physicians have confirmed it. I hope you can rest easy, Miss Cui.\"","The young lady in the lead nodded. \"Go back and take good care of Yunfan. I’ve already sent people to find a renowned doctor; they will arrive in two days.\"","Chun Ying breathed a sigh of relief. Spotting Chen Yi and his companions nearby, she quickly said:","\"Another physician has visited today, brought by Lord Councilor Li Huai’gu of the Governor’s Office and Young Master Yi. Perhaps you...\"","Before she could finish, Miss Cui stopped in her tracks. She glanced toward the side hall and frowned.","\"Nonsense. What renowned doctors could possibly be found in a place like Shu State?\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi let out a stifled laugh. ’So this must be Chen Yunfan’s fiancée.’","Just hearing that one sentence, though, made him understand why Chen Yunfan had never wanted to talk about his engagement."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128 - 127: Take Your Medicine","paragraphs":["Thinking about this, Chen Yi decided not to go out and start an argument with Miss Cui.","The sole purpose of his visit was to wake Chen Yunfan. He had no intention of getting involved in other affairs.","Li Huai’gu, however, was clearly displeased. \"Brother Qingzhou, her words...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi raised a hand to cut him off. \"The young lady of the Qinghe Cui Family has every right to her arrogance.\"","\"Never mind simply looking down on the Physicians of Shu State.\"","\"I reckon she looks down on the two of us just the same.\"","Li Huai’gu paused at his words, then cupped his hands with a bitter smile. \"Brother Qingzhou, my apologies. You’ve been put in an awkward position because of me.\"","He had, of course, heard of the Qinghe Cui Family and knew their current Patriarch, Cui Mao, was one of the Nine Ministers.","Their power and prestige were among the greatest in the Great Wei Dynasty, so it was only natural for the family’s younger generation to be a bit arrogant.","However, it was his invitation, after all, that had brought Chen Yi and the Physician from the Medicine Hall here.","They hadn’t even begun to diagnose Chen Yunfan, yet they were already being disparaged for no reason. That’s why he looked so displeased.","Chen Yi smiled and offered a few words of comfort before turning his gaze outside, saying no more.","A faint gleam flickered in his eyes.","Upon getting a clear look at the qi emanating from Miss Cui and her companions, his expression shifted slightly.","The auras of the three women were like clouds and mist, wreathed in a radiant glow.","The leading Miss Cui was even more impressive.","Seeing this, Chen Yi dispelled his Qi Observation Skill and thought silently, ’The Middle Three Grades Realm.’","’None of these people from the long-established Noble Families are to be trifled with.’","’Compared to them, disciples from the Lower Class are so much weaker in both scholarship and Martial Arts.’","Just then, Miss Cui, who seemed to have overheard their conversation, glanced toward the side hall and said placidly,","\"Chun Ying, your master is now the top scholar and the youngest Assistant Governor in the Governor’s Office. It’s inevitable that he will attract people with ulterior motives.\"","\"After I leave, you must look after your master well. Don’t be careless.\"","Chun Ying understood the implication of her words and looked troubled. \"Well...\"","\"I’ll let it slide this time. But if it happens again, I won’t let you off so easily, even if you are one of Yunfan’s people.\"","Without waiting for Chun Ying’s response, Miss Cui turned and led her people away.","Chun Ying hesitated for a moment before following them out to see them off.","Inside the side hall, Chen Yi and Li Huai’gu had, of course, heard everything clearly.","\"Brother Qingzhou, that woman...\"","Chen Yi raised his hand to interrupt him again. \"Brother Fang Gui, let’s just wait.\"","They hadn’t gone far.","With their level of Martial Arts Cultivation, they would certainly be able to hear their conversation.","If Li Huai’gu were to say something improper behind her back and that obviously difficult Miss Cui overheard him, it would inevitably lead to trouble.","Only after Chun Ying returned did Chen Yi, Li Huai’gu, and Ma Liangcai step out of the side hall.","\"Young Master Yi, please forgive her. That’s just Miss Cui’s temperament. She’s, um... not a bad person.\"","Chun Ying apologized in a low voice as she led Ma Liangcai toward the chamber.","Chen Yi smiled. \"It’s no matter.\"","When they arrived at the chamber, they saw Chen Yunfan lying peacefully on the bed, dressed in a light inner robe.","His complexion was ruddy, his breathing deep and even. He looked as though he were simply in a deep, peaceful sleep.","Chen Yi observed him for a moment and couldn’t help but feel amused.","’No matter how well my dear brother concealed his Martial Arts, he still ended up in a pinch at my hands.’","’I wonder what his expression will be when he wakes up.’","’It should be quite a sight.’","Just then, Chun Ying looked at the three men, stepped aside, and bowed. \"I’m entrusting him to you.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"There’s no need for such formalities.\"","He then motioned for Ma Liangcai to diagnose Chen Yunfan.","Ma Liangcai, truly living up to his reputation as a \"Divine Doctor\" who had been a charlatan for years, put on a show. He stepped forward to take a pulse, checked under the eyelids, and went through a whole routine.","After about a quarter of an hour, he let out a long breath, stood up smiling, and cupped his hands toward Chen Yi and the other two.","\"Lord Assistant Governor’s pulse is stable and his body is healthy. There is nothing seriously wrong.\"","\"His current inability to wake from this deep sleep is likely due to a peculiar poison.\"","\"Poison?\"","Chun Ying’s expression faltered. When she recovered, she quickly asked, \"Do you know what kind of poison my master has been afflicted with?\"","She knew exactly why Chen Yunfan was still unconscious—he had been drugged that night.","Hearing Ma Liangcai’s words, her heart naturally leaped with excitement.","Li Huai’gu, however, wore a solemn expression.","If word got out that a person of Chen Yunfan’s status had been poisoned, it would likely send shockwaves through Shu State.","With this in mind, he also asked, \"What kind of poison is it? Will it endanger Brother Yunfan’s life?\"","Ma Liangcai smiled and shook his head. \"Forgive me, I wasn’t clear. This poison isn’t fatal. It merely causes one to fall into a deep, drunken-like sleep from which they cannot wake.\"","\"So, it’s treatable.\"","At these words, both Li Huai’gu and Chun Ying breathed a sigh of relief and proceeded to ask him about the treatment.","Ma Liangcai glanced at Chen Yi out of the corner of his eye, then, following the instructions he’d been given, found a brush and paper and wrote out a prescription.","It consisted of several common medicinal herbs.","Chun Ying took it and gave it a quick glance before immediately leaving the chamber to prepare and decoct the herbs.","But just as she stepped out of the rear courtyard, she saw the members of the Cui Family standing not far off, holding umbrellas.","Apparently, they had gone only to return.","The leader of the group, Miss Cui—Cui Qingwu—glanced at her. Without a word, she simply held out her hand.","Chun Ying hesitated for a moment before handing over the prescription, saying,","\"Miss Cui, Advisor Li and Young Master Yi are not villains. Please, rest assured.\"","Others might not have known, but as a White-robed Minister, Chun Ying was well aware of Li Huai’gu’s and Chen Yi’s backgrounds and characters.","The two of them had neither reason nor inclination to harm Chen Yunfan.","Cui Qingwu took the prescription, glanced at it, and handed it to the old man behind her. Her tone was flat as she said,","\"After Elder Chang has a look, it will be crystal clear whether they are villains or not.\"","Chun Ying pursed her lips and said no more, her gaze shifting to the old man."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129 - 127: Dalang, Time for Your Medicine (Part 2)","paragraphs":["After waiting a moment.","The old man hesitated before speaking. \"Young Lady, forgive my unrefined Medical Skill. I... I cannot discern the medical principles behind this prescription.\"","Cui Qingwu’s brow furrowed slightly. \"Is there a problem?\"","The old man shook his head. \"There are no issues with the medicinal ingredients themselves. In fact, several of them are highly beneficial to the body.\"","\"I simply cannot comprehend the medicinal effects of combining these ingredients, but...\"","\"But what?\"","\"But I can confirm that this prescription should not harm Young Master Chen’s body.\"","Cui Qingwu hummed in acknowledgment and mused, \"Then let’s try this prescription.\"","Hearing this, Chun Ying’s anxious heart finally settled. She bowed, took the prescription, and went out to gather the medicine.","After a moment of silence.","Cui Qingwu turned her head to the old man and asked, \"If I recall correctly, your Medical Skill ranks in the top five at Xinglin Hall?\"","The old man looked ashamed. \"Although I am in the top five, my Medical Skill is far inferior to the few ranked above me.\"","\"Then what would you consider your level in the Medical Dao to be?\"","\"After practicing medicine for forty years, I have only just passed the entry-level Realm.\"","Pausing for a moment, the old man continued to explain, \"The ingredients in that prescription may seem common, but the medical principles behind their use are exceptionally unique.\"","\"It involves not only the principles of medicinal compatibility but likely also the harmony of yin and yang and the Five Qi and Six Cycles. It is beyond my comprehension.\"","To put it simply, the person who wrote this prescription had already surpassed the Minor Success Realm in the Medical Dao.","Even with the prescription right in front of him, he couldn’t grasp the principles behind its formulation. He could only make a simple judgment based on the properties of the ingredients themselves—it wouldn’t kill someone.","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu nodded. Her gaze drifted toward the rear courtyard as she gave a thoughtful command:","\"Huan’er, I want you to investigate the background of that Divine Doctor later.\"","\"Yes, Young Lady.\"","...","Before long.","Chun Ying hurried back carrying the medicinal ingredients. Seeing that Cui Qingwu and the others were still there, she greeted them with a bow before rushing off to the rear kitchen to brew the medicine.","After a moment’s thought, Cui Qingwu led her people into the rear courtyard again, heading straight for the room where Chen Yunfan was staying.","Chen Yi heard the commotion and glanced over from the corner of his eye, frowning to himself.","’They still haven’t left?’","Before he could dwell on it, the group pushed the door open and entered.","Cui Qingwu, at the head of the group, paid them no mind. She directly had someone bring a chair and sat down by the bed.","\"...\"","Watching their behavior, Chen Yi knew exactly what they were planning.","They were probably waiting to see Chen Yunfan wake up after drinking the medicine.","Beside him, Li Huai’gu glanced at his expression. Seeing that he remained calm, Li Huai’gu also kept silent.","Just when it seemed they would all remain silent, the old man approached Ma Liangcai and cupped his hands in a salute.","\"I am Chang Chengbi of Xinglin Hall. Might I ask where the Divine Doctor studied and where you currently practice?\"","Ma Liangcai instinctively glanced at Chen Yi. After receiving a subtle nod, he cleared his throat and said solemnly:","\"I am Ma Liangcai. I studied under the Wumeng Mountain Medicine Elder and am currently just the head Physician at the Xiao Family’s Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","\"The Wumeng Mountain Medicine Elder?\"","Chang Chengbi looked blank, clearly having no recollection of this person.","However, he did know of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.","And because of the relationship between Xinglin Hall and Linglan Pavilion, he was also aware of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s recent situation.","\"Is the tea beverage from Hundred Herbs Hall by any chance related to Elder Yao?\"","Ma Liangcai was taken aback for a moment, then nodded with an air of mystique. \"It is indeed the work of my master.\"","This was part of the script he had received earlier, so it wasn’t difficult for him to handle the question.","Chang Chengbi nodded in understanding and said no more, silently retreating to Cui Qingwu’s side to wait.","Their conversation was heard clearly by everyone present.","But they were all preoccupied with their own thoughts and did not speak.","Ma Liangcai was forcing himself to appear calm.","Li Huai’gu had already heard rumors, and he simply felt that he had found the right person in Chen Yi this time.","As for Chen Yi, he glanced, intentionally or not, toward Elder Chang, his thoughts inevitably turning to the background of Xinglin Hall.","He knew that Xinglin Hall was an enterprise of the Jing State Liu Family.","Now, this person from the Qinghe Cui Family had brought someone from Xinglin Hall with her, which couldn’t help but make him read more into the situation.","’Has the Jing State Liu Family allied themselves with Qinghe Cui?’","If the Liu Family truly became entangled with the Cui Family, then any future conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families would not bode well for the Xiao Family.","As Chen Yi considered these things, he calculated in his mind, ’It seems I’ll have to investigate this matter thoroughly later on.’","Not long after.","Chun Ying carefully carried the medicinal soup into the room. She saw the situation inside but came to the bedside without hesitation.","Just as she was about to feed it to Chen Yunfan, a slender, pale arm reached out from the side.","\"I’ll do it.\"","Cui Qingwu took the medicine bowl directly from her hand, went forward, propped up Chen Yunfan, and fed him the medicinal soup.","Watching from the side, the corner of Chen Yi’s mouth twitched.","Her movements were direct, neither gentle nor careful. It gave him a sense of déjà vu, reminding him of the famous scene, \"Da Lang, it’s time for your medicine.\"","Just as these random thoughts were running through his head,","Chen Yunfan took a few mouthfuls of the soup, and his eyes suddenly shot open. He shoved the bowl away from his mouth and leaned over the side of the bed.","He coughed and dry-heaved, spluttering:","\"Chun Ying, what is this stuff you’re feeding me? It’s sour and bitter, like horse piss!\"","After a round of cursing, Chen Yunfan finally noticed the unusual atmosphere in the room.","He lifted his head and looked around.","His eyes immediately landed on Cui Qingwu, who was holding the medicine bowl. A strange expression appeared on his scrunched-up face.","\"What are you doing here?\"","Then, his gaze swept to Chen Yi and Li Huai’gu not far away, and he was stunned again.","\"What are you guys doing here too?\"","Li Huai’gu was about to speak, but Chen Yi tapped his foot, and the words died in his throat.","Chen Yunfan saw the exchange and the mischievous glint in Chen Yi’s eyes. After a moment’s thought, he understood.","He was left speechless.","’Brother Yi is just going to watch me burn. And to think I was so worried about your affairs, too.’","With that thought, Chen Yunfan sat up straight and forced a smile at Cui Qingwu."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130 - 127: Big Brother Took His Medicine","paragraphs":["\"When did you arrive in Shu State?\"","Cui Qingwu set down the medicine bowl and had the maid beside her wipe the medicinal soup from her hands. When she looked at Chen Yunfan again, her face was wreathed in smiles.","\"I just arrived this morning.\"","\"However, I received news that you were unconscious while passing through Jing State, so I brought a Physician over from there.\"","\"Unfortunately, his medical skills were lacking, and he couldn’t wake Yunfan up.\"","Chen Yunfan froze, pointing at himself. \"I was unconscious?\"","Only then did Chun Ying manage to chime in and explain.","Even though Chun Ying omitted the events of that night, how could Chen Yunfan not understand that he had been taken down by that bottle of sedative?","His expression flickered between pale and grim, and he gritted his teeth, wishing he could just dig a hole and crawl into it.","Chen Yi took in his entire expression. While he kept a smile on his face, he was secretly ecstatic.","’It wasn’t a waste stopping Li Huai’gu from speaking earlier. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have been able to see such a spectacular show.’","After listening, Chen Yunfan forced a smile. \"Thank you for saving me, Brother Yi. I am truly ashamed.\"","That night, he had planned to rescue Hundred Herbs Hall so that Chen Yi would owe him a favor.","But in the end, not only did he do nothing and get knocked out by a sedative, he had to be rescued and woken up by Chen Yi and his men instead.","’Damn it, just you wait!’","Chen Yunfan cursed silently, vowing that he would find the person responsible.","Although Chen Yi didn’t know his exact thoughts, he could guess the gist of them.","’I bet when Chen Yunfan finds out in the future that I not only knocked him out but also saved him, the look on his face will be even more priceless than today’s.’","Suppressing these wicked thoughts, Chen Yi said with a smile:","\"Brother, you are now the esteemed Imperial Top Scholar and the youngest Assistant Governor in the Shu State Governor’s Office. It’s inevitable that you’ll attract some people with ulterior motives.\"","\"You were lucky this time; the poison wasn’t fatal. But if something like this happens again...\"","He paused, glancing at Miss Cui out of the corner of his eye, then continued, \"You might not be so lucky.\"","The smile on Cui Qingwu’s face froze. Those words sounded somewhat familiar.","The two maids behind her had already reacted, glaring daggers at Chen Yi.","If not for the others present, they probably would have already started scolding him.","Chen Yunfan, however, was oblivious to all this. \"You’re right, Brother Yi. I was indeed careless this time.\"","Chen Yi took in everyone’s expressions, chuckled softly, and turned to gesture at Ma Liangcai.","\"Later, have Liu Quan draw up the bill for the consultation fee and send it to my brother.\"","\"Yes, Shopkeeper.\"","Chen Yi gave a slight bow and took his leave directly.","After a moment’s daze, Li Huai’gu reminded Chen Yunfan about his duties at the Government Office and also followed him out.","After they had left, Chen Yunfan noticed the strange expressions on Cui Qingwu and her maids’ faces and raised an eyebrow.","\"Qingwu, you look terrible. Don’t tell me you also ate something you shouldn’t have?\"","Cui Qingwu snapped back to reality, a smile returning to her face. \"It’s nothing. I was just reminiscing about the past.\"","\"That man just now must be the Chen Yi who used to bully you all the time, right?\"","Chen Yunfan said, displeased, \"Bully me? As if he’d dare. I was clearly the one bullying him.\"","He had to maintain a strong front. He would never admit to being bullied by Chen Yi as a child.","Especially not in front of outsiders.","Cui Qingwu smiled and nodded. \"I remember seeing him at the Chen Mansion before. He looked like such a bookworm back then.\"","\"Seeing him again today, I find he’s changed quite a bit.\"","Chen Yunfan nodded. \"Brother Yi has indeed changed a lot. His abilities have grown considerably as well.\"","\"But now that he’s married into the Xiao Family, it’s a good thing that he has some skills.\"","Hearing this, Cui Qingwu asked with a half-smile, \"Yunfan, you seem quite concerned about him?\"","\"We are brothers, after all, and we’re both here in this backwater of Shu State. If I don’t look out for him, who will?\"","\"Is that so? Then I suppose it would be the same if I came to you for help with something.\"","\"What...\"","Watching the two of them talking and laughing, Chun Ying couldn’t help but break into a cold sweat for Chen Yunfan.","’It seems Young Master Yi has dug a trap for my master.’","...","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi and the others were in a carriage, heading straight for Jishi Medicine Hall.","Li Huai’gu thought of their earlier conversation and couldn’t help but laugh. \"Brother Qingzhou, after what you said back there, aren’t you afraid Miss Cui will come looking for trouble?\"","Chen Yi watched the rain fall outside the carriage and shook his head with a smile. \"With my brother there, he won’t let Miss Cui do anything reckless.\"","It wasn’t that he had intentionally set a trap for Chen Yunfan.","Rather, it was a spur-of-the-moment decision he made after learning that people from Xinglin Hall had arrived.","’Is there a connection between the Jing State Liu Family and the Qinghe Cui Family? There’s only one way to find out!’","「An hour later.」","Chen Yi returned to the Xiao Family residence, heading straight for the rear courtyard under an oil paper umbrella.","The armored warriors and maids he passed along the way were all hurrying about. This was, needless to say, due to the impact of Liu Jing’s death the previous night.","However, when he arrived outside Spring Lotus Garden, he saw Xiao Wan’er looking out from the entrance.","\"My lady, are you... waiting for me?\""]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131 - 128: Eldest Sister, Are You Okay?","paragraphs":["Seeing him return safely, Xiao Wan’er didn’t avoid him as she usually did. She nodded slightly and said,","\"I was indeed waiting for you.\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. ’It must be about Liu Jing’s death last night,’ he guessed, then said with a smile,","\"Let’s talk inside. The rain’s coming down pretty hard. You’ll catch a chill.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded and followed him into the wooden cabin, taking a seat in the main room.","Chen Yi didn’t press her for answers, instead going to fill a kettle and place it on a small stove to boil.","As the stove’s fire burned, Xiao Wan’er pulled her cloak tighter, her expression relaxing considerably.","\"How is your brother?\"","She had heard from Xiao Wuge why Li Huai’gu had come to their door, and now that her mind was at ease, she couldn’t help but ask.","Chen Yi pushed the stove a little closer to her. \"He’s woken up.\"","\"Ma Liangcai truly lives up to his name. He whipped up a prescription in no time, and my brother woke up right after drinking it.\"","\"That’s good.\"","\"If you accept Mr. Yue Ming’s invitation to Guiyun Academy, it shouldn’t affect the Medicine Hall’s business.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Did you hear that from Wuge?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement. \"What Advisor Li said was right. With your talent and learning, being a Shopkeeper at a Medicine Hall is truly a waste.\"","Seeing her earnest expression, Chen Yi thought for a moment and said, \"I was still hesitating, but since you say so too, I’ll make a trip to Guiyun Academy tomorrow.\"","Hearing this, a smile appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s pale face. \"Then why didn’t you agree right away when Second Sister came back?\"","’That was then, this is now.’ Chen Yi gave a vague reply before looking at her and asking, \"You were waiting for me outside earlier. Is something wrong?\"","Xiao Wan’er met his eyes, then instinctively turned her head to look at the falling rain outside the window. She said in a low voice,","\"I heard about something major this morning, so I thought I’d wait for you to get back and give you a heads-up.\"","\"What is it?\"","Xiao Wan’er lowered her head slightly, her expression unnatural as she replied,","\"Actually, there’s something I didn’t tell you before. The Linglan Pavilion was backed by the Jing State Liu Family.\"","Chen Yi feigned surprise. \"Is that so?\"","\"Yes, I heard it from my grandfather.\"","\"The Liu Family set up Linglan Pavilion with the goal of crushing the Xiao Family Medicine Hall.\"","\"With Linglan Pavilion closing down, the matter should have been over.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, then said, \"But unexpectedly, that man from the Jing State Liu Family... he died at home last night.\"","\"Grandfather summoned me this morning and specifically instructed me... that until the matter is investigated, I... we all need to be careful.\"","\"From now on, it’s best to have a Personal Guard with you if you leave the residence. And you absolutely must not ’get lost’ again like you did last night.\"","After listening, Chen Yi understood. ’She came all this way just because she was worried about me?’","At that thought, the smile on his face faded, and he nodded with a serious expression. \"I’ll keep that in mind.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at him from the corner of her eye. Seeing that he didn’t seem to be reading too much into it, she relaxed and pointed, saying,","\"The water, the water’s boiling.\"","Chen Yi gave her a deep look before closing the stove’s air vent and steeping two cups of tea.","One cup of green tea, and one of black tea.","Normally, one would drink cooling green tea in the summer, but due to her condition, Xiao Wan’er could only drink warm beverages.","Neither of them spoke again during the pause while the tea steeped.","The only sound was the PITTER-PATTER of rain from outside, striking the pond, the pavilion, and the roof tiles.","It wasn’t noisy, however. Instead, the atmosphere was quiet and warm.","A moment later, Chen Yi let out a light breath, raised his teacup, and took a sip.","The SLURP brought Xiao Wan’er back to her senses, and she too cupped her tea in both hands, taking small sips.","Due to her physical condition, she had never been sensitive to heat, even as a child.","Even freshly boiled water would cool rapidly upon contact with her skin, as if it had touched a block of ice.","Thus, she finished the cup of hot tea quickly.","Chen Yi picked up the kettle, refilled her cup, and said with a smile, \"Later, I’ll have Ma Liangcai come over to take a look at you and write a prescription.\"","He had wanted to do this for some time, but what with the Hidden Guard and the Hundred Herbs Hall, it had been delayed for a few days.","But upon hearing this, Xiao Wan’er shook her head. \"It’s useless.\"","\"My grandfather and father have found many renowned doctors to see me before, but none of them had any effect.\"","Chen Yi acted as if he hadn’t heard her. \"This afternoon. I’ll have him come over.\"","While he couldn’t completely cure Xiao Wan’er’s Extreme Cold Body, he did have methods to alleviate it. At the very least, he could make her more comfortable.","Xiao Wan’er gave him a reproachful look but didn’t refuse his kind offer again.","The two then chatted idly for a while.","It was mostly Xiao Wan’er talking and Chen Yi listening.","The topic revolved mainly around the Medicine Hall’s business, including recent arrangements and the future selection of a new shopkeeper for Jishi Medicine Hall.","Chen Yi just told her not to worry about it for now.","Even if he went to Guiyun Academy to be an Instructor, he wouldn’t have to go every day, so temporarily continuing as the Medicine Hall’s Shopkeeper wouldn’t be an issue.","Besides, the news that Ma Liangcai had cured Chen Yunfan today was bound to spread.","With Ma Liangcai’s subpar Medical Skill, his cover would be blown sooner or later if Chen Yi wasn’t around.","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment and nodded in agreement. The fact that Chen Yi seemed to care so much about the Medicine Hall appeared to lift her spirits.","It wasn’t until nearly noon that the two of them went to Jiaxing Garden for lunch.","「In the afternoon.」","After preparing the prescription for Xiao Wan’er, Chen Yi had one of the Armored Warriors in the residence bring Ma Liangcai over.","He also wrote a formal letter of introduction and had someone deliver it to Mr. Yue Ming at Guiyun Academy.","After all, Mr. Yue Ming was a great scholar renowned not just in Shu State but throughout Great Wei; certain proprieties had to be observed.","Soon, Ma Liangcai arrived, following the Armored Warrior.","Chen Yi, still using the same pretext involving Wang Ji, handed him a prescription.","Ma Liangcai looked at the prescription in his hand and trembled. \"Shopkeeper, is... is this to treat a cold-related illness?\"","Chen Yi shook his head and said flatly, \"It only alleviates the symptoms.\"","Even so, Ma Liangcai was still shocked.","His Medical Skill might be lacking, but he wasn’t entirely ignorant.","The Extreme Cold Body was a legendary incurable condition. Forget a cure; even prescriptions that could alleviate it were rare.","And yet, he was holding one in his hand...","At that thought, Ma Liangcai couldn’t help but ask, \"Shopkeeper, does Boss Wang really know some ’Elder Yao’?\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly. \"If there’s no Elder Yao, then where did your Medical Skill come from?\"","\"My apologies, Shopkeeper. I... I was just too surprised.\"","\"Next time, remember to talk less and do more. If anyone asks, just attribute it all to Elder Yao.\"","\"Understood, I understand.\"","Once Ma Liangcai had calmed down, Chen Yi took him to Jiaxing Garden.","This time was even simpler; he didn’t even have to take her pulse.","Ma Liangcai simply looked at Xiao Wan’er, then directly presented the prescription, saying with an air of nonchalant confidence,","\"My master, Elder Yao, once passed down to me a prescription left from a previous dynasty. While it cannot cure the Eldest Miss’s condition, it is enough to alleviate it somewhat.\"","Watching this charlatan-like performance, Chen Yi silently gave him a thumbs-up.","Xiao Wan’er, however, was skeptical.","But after some gentle persuasion from Chen Yi, she agreed to give it a try and had Cui’er and Juan’er go brew the medicinal herbs.","Before long, Xiao Wan’er looked at the bowl in her hands, which contained a medicinal soup as vibrant as a flame, and hesitantly took a sip.","Instantly, a warm current spread through her chest and abdomen. The long-forgotten sensation of warmth left her slightly stunned.","She sat there, completely motionless.","Her reaction nearly scared Ma Liangcai to death; he thought there was something wrong with the medicinal soup.","Only Chen Yi kept smiling.","Using his Qi Observation Skill, he could see the black, cold qi on Xiao Wan’er’s body slowly dissipating.","Seeing this, Xiao Wuge couldn’t help but wave a hand in front of her eyes. \"Sister, are you okay?\"","Xiao Wan’er snapped out of it, her voice filled with joy. \"It’s working. It’s really working.\"","With that, she drank the rest of the soup in one go. A hint of color even appeared on her pale face.","Seeing this, Ma Liangcai breathed a sigh of relief and quickly stood up to offer his congratulations.","Overjoyed, Xiao Wan’er was not stingy with her reward, telling Cui’er to lead him to the accountant to receive it.","After Ma Liangcai left, Xiao Wan’er’s face was not just flushed, but also faintly covered in a fine layer of sweat.","For her, this was a first-in-a-lifetime occurrence.","She touched her slightly feverish cheeks, a brilliant smile on her face. \"Doctor Ma is truly a Divine Doctor.\"","Chen Yi said with a smile, \"He did study under Elder Yao of Wumeng Mountain, after all.\"","\"It’s not just you. My brother saw so many renowned doctors to no effect, but today, Old Ma went over, and he woke up after just one dose of medicine.\"","Beside them, Xiao Wuge, Juan’er, and the others were all naturally happy for her.","Perhaps she felt hot.","Despite the stormy weather, Xiao Wan’er actually undid her cloak.","Beneath it was a snow-white dress, yet its color still couldn’t compare to the crystalline fairness of her skin.","Just as Xiao Wan’er was about to speak, she noticed Chen Yi’s gaze and, forgetting what she was going to say, quickly pulled her cloak shut again.","Her face flushed as red as if it were on fire. \"Um, it’s still a little cold.\"","Chen Yi suppressed a laugh. \"Indeed. It’s better to keep it on.\"","\"Ri-right...\"","After joking around for a bit, Chen Yi reminded her to take her medicine on time, then left with Xiao Wuge for Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wan’er watched them walk away, the heat on her face still refusing to subside.","She didn’t know if it was because of the medicine, or something else.","...","In this world, where there is joy for some, there is worry for others.","Li Huai’gu, who had just been feeling pleased about Chen Yunfan’s recovery, had been back at the Governor’s Office for only a moment before the smile vanished from his face.","Li Huai’gu looked at Right Governor Yang Ye, who was seated at his desk, and asked hesitantly,","\"Sir, do I really have to go to the Three Towns to collect the grain tax from the Dingyuan Army?\"","\"Wasn’t Assistant Governor Chen supposed to go?\"","A hint of helplessness appeared on Yang Ye’s aged face. \"Left Envoy Liu came by at noon specifically to stress the importance of this matter.\"","\"If Yunfan had woken up sooner, I might have been able to get you out of it, but now it’s difficult.\"","Li Huai’gu was still confused. \"But why the rush? A one-month deadline?\"","\"And a twenty percent tax rate? Is... is that collecting at the maximum possible rate?\"","Yang Ye was silent for a moment, then looked left and right before saying in a low voice, \"Last night, the Sixth Young Master of the Jing State Liu Family died here in Shu State.\"","\"I suspect that Left Envoy Liu’s current instructions are related to this.\"","Li Huai’gu’s expression changed slightly. \"Are you saying he’s going to move against the Xiao...\"","\"Silence!\"","Before he could finish, Yang Ye cut him off with a stern rebuke. \"Fang Gui, some things are best kept to yourself. Be careful, walls have ears!\"","Li Huai’gu quickly apologized. \"My apologies, Sir.\"","Despite his words, he was inwardly shocked.","’So Left Envoy Liu is dead-set on making a move against the Xiao Family.’","’Over two million shi of grain, taxed at twenty percent... that’s roughly five hundred thousand shi of grain...’","’Regardless of how heavy a burden it is, it’s bound to displease both the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army.’","After a moment of silence, Yang Ye gave his instructions in a low voice, \"In short, the implications of this matter are enormous. You must act with extreme caution.\"","\"If it proves impossible, write back to me, and I will try to mediate.\"","Li Huai’gu stood, bowed, and expressed his thanks. \"Thank you for your guidance, Sir.\"","Then, he said with some hesitation, \"I would like to ask my teacher for his opinion. Would that be permissible?\"","\"Yue Ming? Yes, that’s a good idea.\""]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132 - 129: Feeling Warm","paragraphs":["On an afternoon of torrential rain, a slight chill hung in the air, even for July in Linxia.","Thick, dark clouds obscured the sun. As lightning flashed and thunder rumbled, gusts of wind blew in from all directions.","They scattered fallen leaves across the grounds of the Spring Lotus Garden.","There were bamboo leaves, willow leaves, and even petals from freshly bloomed flowers torn from their bushes.","In weather like this, Chen Yi certainly wasn’t about to stay in the drafty, open-sided pavilion drinking tea.","Instead, he was in his study, having set up a Go board with Xiao Wuge.","One was teaching, the other learning.","The black and white stones were laid out on the board and then gathered up again; not a single game was played to completion.","Xiao Wuge was still a beginner. Though he was a quick study, he had mastered too few standard openings and patterns to sustain a full game.","Chen Yi, however, was in no hurry.","Since learning Go, the time he spent on the Chess Dao had already surpassed his calligraphy practice, second only to his time spent on Martial Arts and the Medical Dao.","This was partly due to his Martial Arts Body and his Great Success in the Medical Dao, but the fundamental reason lay in the utility of the Chess Dao itself.","Originally, Chen Yi hadn’t believed in the old adages about \"playing with all living beings as your pieces,\" \"using heaven and earth as your board,\" or \"judging a person’s character through their game.\"","But judging from the Profound Mysteries of the Chess Dao he had obtained, and from his own numerous strategies and deductions, he now knew that the Realms described in those phrases were indeed attainable.","It all depended on the player’s position and the objective they sought to achieve.","’For instance, at this very moment, the board in my mind is the land of Shu State itself, upon which I’m deducing the Xiao Family’s current predicament and its future course.’","’As I place the stones, my thoughts can be distilled into three words: \"Break the stalemate.\"’","’Should the Xiao Family’s situation improve in the future, the game would change along with it, evolving into an entirely new match.’","As Chen Yi pondered these things, he wore a gentle smile, occasionally offering a few words of guidance.","After listening, Xiao Wuge would usually pause to think for a moment.","Then, he would place a few more stones, combining the method he was taught with his own understanding.","Some of his interpretations were skewed, but others showed he could extrapolate from a single point, demonstrating a thorough grasp of the concept.","But regardless of whether his understanding was off the mark or correct, Chen Yi would offer a few words of praise before pointing out the problem or the cleverness of the move.","’He knew very well that the most precious quality in a child is the ability to think independently.’","’Any outside interference, no matter how small, only serves to stifle that invaluable trait.’","’So, I just need to be a good guide, an embodiment of the saying, \"The master opens the door, but the student must walk the path alone.\"’","Just then, having learned a new standard sequence, Xiao Wuge’s initial delight gave way to another question.","\"Brother-in-law, do you think my sister’s illness can be cured?\"","Chen Yi calmly gathered the stones into their bowls and replied, \"Perhaps.\"","He didn’t give a definite answer.","’My Medical Dao has already reached the Great Success Realm. In terms of theory, Medical Skill, and even my understanding of medicinal properties, I surpass ninety percent of the Physicians in Great Wei.’","’Even so, I still have no way to cure the ailment of extreme cold that afflicts Xiao Wan’er.’","’I can only wait for my own Realm to advance further before attempting it again.’","Xiao Wuge let out an \"oh,\" his heart sinking with a little disappointment.","\"That was the first time I’d ever seen my sister so excited. If only that Divine Doctor Ma’s Medical Skill was a little better.\"","Chen Yi smiled. \"It will be.\"","\"It’s like playing Go. As long as you immerse yourself in it, body and soul, your skill will gradually improve.\"","\"But everyone has different talents. The speed of improvement varies, and the upper limits of one’s potential will also be different.\"","Xiao Wuge thought for a moment, then nodded. \"You’re right, Brother-in-law.\"","Then he asked, \"So, how is my talent for the Chess Dao?\"","Seeing the earnest look on the boy’s face, Chen Yi decided to knock him down a peg. \"It’s so-so.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"What ’huh’? Set up the Pine Snow Chess Position for me.\"","\"Oh...\"","’Kids... they achieve some small success and immediately want recognition.’","’In these moments, you have to read the situation. You can’t just shower them with praise. A little humbling now and then helps them build a more stable foundation.’","While the two played Go, Xiaodie would always sit quietly to one side.","’To her, Go was something for scholars, an elegant pursuit that didn’t belong in her world.’","So, as she watched the black and white stones slowly fill the board, her eyes would close without her noticing.","Her head would nod, and nod again, until after a few bobs, it would fall still, leaving only the sound of her steady breathing.","And so, the afternoon passed in peace.","It wasn’t until just before nightfall that the sound of jingling bells echoed from outside the Spring Lotus Garden.","Chen Yi knew Pei Guanli and the others had returned. He gently tapped Xiaodie, signaling for her to go get dinner ready.","Xiaodie lifted her head, looked at him blankly, then glanced at the darkening sky outside before jumping to her feet and rushing out the door.","\"Forgive me, Young Master! Xiaodie didn’t mean to fall asleep.\"","Chen Yi shook his head and smiled. ’Whether she meant to or not, at least she got a peaceful nap.’","He then helped Xiao Wuge put away the Go board.","A moment later, Pei Guanli’s head popped into view at the study doorway, a smile on her cheerful, round face.","\"Brother-in-law, I’m back!\"","\"I heard your bells a while ago. Come in and have a seat.\"","Pei Guanli then padded in, her smooth, bare feet still wet and leaving a trail of small footprints.","\"Look! I bought so many things today.\"","Pei Guanli sat down to the side and held up the small bags in her hand, giving them a little shake.","\"There’s a present for you in here, Brother-in-law!\"","\"Can you guess which one it is?\"","Chen Yi glanced over and pointed casually at one of the bags. \"This one.\"","’I don’t have x-ray vision; how am I supposed to know which one is my gift?’","But he saw Pei Guanli’s smile falter. She pulled that very bag out separately and pouted.","\"Brother-in-law, you don’t have some kind of all-seeing eye, do you? You actually guessed it! And here I was, thinking I’d hidden it so well.\"","\"Just lucky.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, taking the bag from her. He opened it and took a look, and his expression immediately darkened."]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133 - 129: Feeling Warm (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Pei Guanli, is this the gift you prepared for me?\"","\"A dudou??\"","\"Ah? No, no, that’s mine, Brother-in-law! I grabbed the wrong one.\"","Pei Guanli snatched the bag back in a flurry, her face flushing red as she rummaged through it before finally finding a box and handing it to Chen Yi.","\"This is your gift, Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi shot her a look, then opened the box. Seeing it was a fan, he nodded. \"Not bad.\"","Pei Guanli stuck her tongue out. Then, as if remembering something, she pointed at him and said:","\"Brother-in-law, that means your guess was wrong.\"","\"...\"","’This Tiger Girl’s train of thought is certainly different from most people’s.’","After some lighthearted banter, the group finished dinner.","Chen Yi had Xiaodie take Xiao Wuge to rest. After asking Pei Guanli about her day, he sent her off to bed as well.","Xiao Jinghong was currently away, but Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang were still at the estate.","He still couldn’t go to the bamboo forest with Pei Guanli like before, so he could only stay in his wing and practice the Four Symbols Skill.","Soon, six hours had passed.","Chen Yi slowly withdrew his practice, waiting for the True Essence circulating in his body to return to his two Seas of Qi. Once his mind and body had settled, he stood up to stretch his limbs.","The Martial Arts Seventh Grade, unlike the Ninth and Eighth Grades, didn’t require tempering one’s Power or clearing meridians. It was simply a Realm for accumulating True Essence.","He just needed to cultivate diligently, gradually filling the True Essence within his two Seas of Qi.","Once his True Essence condensed from liquid into a mercury-like state, he could begin to break through to the next Realm.","As Chen Yi considered these things, his gaze shifted to the rain falling outside the window.","The rain had lessened, but the wind still blew strong.","The flowers, plants, and trees in the garden swayed, leaning in every direction.","But because the doors and windows were shut tight, the only sound that reached his ears amidst this scene was the PITTER-PATTER of the rain.","Unconsciously, Chen Yi’s thoughts drifted to the events of the past few days.","The first sentence that surfaced in his mind was what Xiao Wan’er had said: \"I was, in fact, waiting for you.\"","Starting with that fairly straightforward sentence, and combining it with what he had heard and discovered during the day, he could easily deduce the Xiao Family’s response to Liu Jing’s death.","’The Old Master and the Xiao Family must have prepared for the worst,’","’otherwise, he wouldn’t have specifically instructed Xiao Wan’er not to leave the estate these days.’","Of course, this was also the most prudent course of action for now.","After all, the incident had just occurred. More information was needed to formulate a more precise response.","However, if Chen Yi were in the Old Master’s position, the first thing he would do is conduct an internal investigation to see if the Xiao Family Punishment Hall or some other affiliated party had killed Liu Jing.","Only after confirming that it wasn’t the Xiao Family’s doing would he proceed to the next step.","There were two possible approaches here.","One was to cooperate openly with the Liu Family or the Imprisonment Department to catch the killer, allowing tensions between the two sides to ease.","The second was to take a more aggressive stance and force the Liu Family to back down.","The general idea was something like, ’Never mind that the Xiao Family didn’t do it—even if we did, you’d still have to bow your head.’","Evidently, given the Old Master’s current cautiousness, he would likely choose the first approach.","’Catch the killer, huh? I have no intention of rotting in a cell.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, thinking, ’I still need to see how the Liu Family reacts.’","If the Liu Family exercised restraint, there would still be room for maneuver.","Otherwise, it would be impossible for the Old Master to smooth things over, even if he wanted to.","Just then, the hour of Zi arrived—","[Daily Intel | Profound-rank Lower Grade: After the midpoint of the hour of You, Hidden Guards will be discussing important matters inside Fengchun Building. A small Opportunity may be obtained.]","’Tomorrow night at Fengchun Building, the Hidden Guards are meeting?’","Chen Yi frowned slightly as he looked at the content on the glowing screen.","’Xiao Dongchen, Ge the Third, Liu Si’er, Uncle Gui... these are the four Hidden Guards known to be in Shu State right now.’","First, Liu Si’er could be ruled out.","His injuries hadn’t healed, and he was still bedridden.","Next was Uncle Gui. As a servant of the Xiao Family, he would be too conspicuous at Fengchun Building.","Ge the Third...","His identity didn’t seem quite right either, but it wasn’t impossible for a member of the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard to visit Fengchun Building occasionally.","The most likely candidate was Xiao Dongchen.","At this thought, Chen Yi glanced in the direction of the Four Directions Hall, his expression shifting slightly.","’At a time like this, if it really is him... that’s not a good thing.’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi turned, returned to his bed, and sat cross-legged to resume his cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","Regardless of whether Xiao Dongchen was at Fengchun Building, he had to make the trip.","...","The night passed without incident.","Before dawn the next day, Chen Yi rose early and, with Xiaodie’s help, washed up and dressed neatly.","Because he was going to Guiyun Academy to visit Mr. Yue Ming, he had deliberately changed into a more formal long robe.","He checked his reflection in the mirror and, once satisfied, went downstairs.","Pei Guanli was already sitting at the dining table in the living room. When she saw him, her eyes lit up.","\"Brother-in-law, are you going out today, too?\"","Chen Yi grunted in affirmation. \"I’m making a trip to Guiyun Academy.\"","Hearing this, Pei Guanli couldn’t help but think of what she had done at Guiyun Academy before, and a mischievous grin spread across her face.","Chen Yi saw her expression and raised an eyebrow. \"I almost forgot. You’ve been to Guiyun Academy before and even attended a poetry gathering.\"","\"How was it?\"","Pei Guanli quickly lowered her head, covering her mouth to keep from laughing out loud. \"It was fine. There were a lot of people.\"","’She didn’t dare mention that she had drugged and knocked out Chen Yunfan. Otherwise, her brother-in-law would surely rap her on the head a few times.’","Chen Yi knew she was dodging the question, so he didn’t press further.","After breakfast, Pei Guanli ran off to Jiaxing Garden as usual to drag Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang out for a stroll around the city.","According to her, they had visited the west and north sides of the city the past two days, and today they were going to wander around the East Market.","Chen Yi paid her no mind. In any case, he needed her to keep Ge the Third occupied.","After taking Xiao Wuge to Jiaxing Garden, he told Xiao Wan’er he was going to Guiyun Academy.","Xiao Wan’er didn’t forget to remind him, \"Remember to take a Personal Guard with you, so you don’t get lost in the alleyways.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"I’ll see who’s free later.\"","Inwardly, however, he was unconcerned.","The Xiao Family’s Personal Guards were all in the Lower Three Grades Realm. Even if one followed him, they would be useless if he encountered any real danger.","Seeing his attitude, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but nag him some more, telling him not to be careless and so on.","Chen Yi smiled as he watched her, the words going in one ear and out the other, but he did notice a change in her appearance.","\"You’re not wearing your heavy cloak today. Don’t you feel cold?\"","Xiao Wan’er was currently dressed in a pale yellow long skirt with a short jacket, looking like a young lady from a wealthy family at the start of winter.","Compared to her usual attire of a heavy cloak, her figure was no longer so bulky.","Her elegant, gentle, and quiet temperament now further accentuated her stunning beauty.","Xiao Wan’er smiled and shook her head at his words, a hint of color returning to her normally pale face. \"I drank some medicinal soup this morning, so I feel warm.\"","This was the first time she had felt this way, so she was naturally in a good mood.","But because of this, not wearing her heavy cloak felt a little strange.","It was like... like...","like going out in winter wearing only undergarments; it felt like something was missing.","Especially under Chen Yi’s gaze, Xiao Wan’er felt a bit uncomfortable and quickly gestured that it was getting late, urging him to go and return soon.","Chen Yi knew she was thin-skinned, so he smiled, bid her farewell, and left Jiaxing Garden.","When he reached the front courtyard, he happened to run into Ge the Third and his men, who were preparing to leave.","He vaguely overheard an Armored Warrior call out:","\"Third Brother, Master Dongchen just said he’s hosting a banquet at Fengchun Building tonight. He wants you to go straight there and wait for him outside when you get back.\"","\"Got it.\"","As he watched the carriage drive away, Chen Yi glanced around, didn’t ask any of the other Armored Warriors to follow, and walked toward Guiyun Academy alone under his umbrella.","’So it really is Xiao Dongchen and Ge the Third?’","’It seems my having Pei Guanli keep Ge the Third occupied for several days has made Xiao Dongchen anxious.’","’Otherwise, given the Hidden Guard’s usual methods, he never would have resorted to such a poor tactic to arrange a meeting with Ge the Third.’","But what concerned Chen Yi was that if these two were meeting at a time like this, they were probably discussing more than just the \"Dingyuan Army grain\" matter.","It was highly likely the situation between the Xiao and Liu Families would be part of the conversation.","’Is Xiao Dongchen planning to stir up trouble and play the spoiler?’","’If the Hidden Guard gets involved, I’m afraid...’","As Chen Yi thought about this, a cold, harsh glint appeared in his eyes.","’I truly despise those who betray their own.’","Instantly, a piece on the chessboard in his mind moved—it was the black stone representing Xiao Dongchen.","’Looks like Xiao Dongchen will have to be grouped together with Liu Hong.’","\"Brother Qingzhou?\"","Just then, a voice called out from behind him. Chen Yi turned to look, a little surprised.","\"Brother Fang Gui, what a coincidence.\""]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134 - 130: Not Even Bothering to Pretend Anymore","paragraphs":["Upon learning that Li Huai’gu was also visiting Mr. Yue Ming, Chen Yi folded his Oil Paper Umbrella and boarded the carriage to go to Guiyun Academy with him.","Li Huai’gu sized him up and asked with a smile, \"Brother Qingzhou, have you already made a decision?\"","Chen Yi nodded, feigning helplessness. \"It’s better than waiting for my teacher to send a letter scolding me into going.\"","’He still remembered how Mr. Yue Ming had written to Mr. Ju Yi, who was all the way in Jinling, to persuade him to go to Guiyun Academy. It was the perfect excuse to use now.’","\"And of course, Brother Fang Gui’s words of persuasion yesterday left me quite ashamed.\"","Hearing the teasing tone in his voice, Li Huai’gu couldn’t help but shake his head. \"Brother Qingzhou, your way of thinking is truly different from others.\"","’In his opinion, any other Confucian scholar who received an invitation from a teacher would find it impossible to refuse. They would most likely accept on the spot. Chen Yi, on the other hand, not only didn’t accept the invitation but repeatedly declined it, his thoughts and considerations completely unlike those of an ordinary person. He couldn’t understand it and could only guess it was just his personality.’","Chen Yi glanced at him and changed the subject, asking:","\"Brother Fang Gui, what made you decide to visit Mr. Yue Ming? You said yesterday that things were busy at the Governor’s Office.\"","Li Huai’gu gave a wry smile at his words. \"There’s been a mishap at the office...\"","Then, as if he’d thought of something, he asked, \"Brother Qingzhou, have you heard any rumors lately?\"","’News of this matter would surely reach the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion today. It would be useless for him to try to hide it, so he might as well ask for Chen Yi’s opinion.’","Chen Yi was a little surprised. \"You’re referring to?\"","Li Huai’gu didn’t answer immediately. Instead, he lifted the curtain to look around before leaning in and lowering his voice:","\"The matter of the visitor from the Jing State Liu Family.\"","’Chen Yi immediately guessed that the mishap at the Governor’s Office he mentioned was likely related to the Liu Family.’","As his thoughts raced, he spoke bluntly, \"I’ve heard a little. That Young Master Liu unfortunately passed away the night before last.\"","After speaking, Chen Yi pointed behind the carriage—in the direction of the Government Office. \"Brother Fang Gui, since you bring this up, has the Governor’s Office made arrangements?\"","Li Huai’gu nodded. \"After I returned to the Government Office from Brother Yunfan’s residence yesterday, Lord Yang specifically summoned me.\"","\"He ordered me to travel through the Three Towns of Iron Wall, Cang Lang, and Profound Armor within one month to collect this year’s summer grain tax. And...\"","He paused, then said in a low voice, \"And it’s a tax of two-tenths.\"","Chen Yi frowned inwardly, but his face remained calm. \"An order from Left Envoy Liu?\"","Li Huai’gu hummed softly in affirmation, then sighed. \"That’s why I wanted to find our teacher and ask for his advice.\"","’The Liu Family has made its move.’","The thought popped into Chen Yi’s mind subconsciously.","But immediately after, he dismissed the idea.","’Not the Jing State Liu Family, but the Shu State Liu Family. Or rather, the doing of Left Governor Liu Hong from the Shu State Governor’s Office.’","’It was obvious. The incident happened the night before last, but Liu Jing’s body wasn’t discovered until yesterday morning. The earliest Liu Hong could have learned of it was early yesterday morning. And less than six hours had passed between that and Li Huai’gu receiving his mission to collect the grain tax from the Three Towns. In such a short time, not even an express courier or a carrier pigeon could have gotten the news to the Jing State Liu Family. From this, it wasn’t difficult to deduce—sending Li Huai’gu to the Three Towns was Liu Hong’s own decision.’","Thinking of this, Chen Yi breathed a small sigh of relief.","’If the Jing State Liu Family hadn’t made a move, there was still room to maneuver. Presumably, Liu Hong’s arrangement, giving Li Huai’gu only one month, was not only to declare his stance with the Liu Family faction but also to set a final deadline for the contest between the Xiao and Liu Families. Otherwise, he could have just sent a direct notice to the Three Towns and thoroughly enraged the Xiao Family.’","Just then, Li Huai’gu, seeing his silence, couldn’t help but ask, \"If you were in my position, Brother Qingzhou, what would you do?\"","Chen Yi snapped out of his thoughts. \"Brother Fang Gui, I wouldn’t dare to speak carelessly.\"","’It seemed this matter was deeply troubling Li Huai’gu. But then again, it made sense. Li Huai’gu had been assigned directly to the Shu State Governor’s Office without any experience in the Hanlin Academy, so he had to figure many things out on his own. And since the matter involved the Xiao and Liu Families, it was normal for him to be unable to see the path forward clearly.’","Li Huai’gu gave another wry smile and cupped his hands. \"I barely slept a wink last night.\"","Even with Yang Ye to back him up, he still didn’t dare to be careless, always worried about being drawn into some political vortex.","Seeing his serious expression, Chen Yi also thought seriously for a moment before speaking:","\"Brother Fang Gui, you’re too close to the situation to see clearly.\"","Li Huai’gu looked confused. \"Please, Brother Qingzhou, do not hesitate to enlighten me.\"","\"I wouldn’t dare presume to enlighten you.\"","\"In truth, this matter has nothing to do with you, Brother Fang Gui. You can simply follow the office’s orders and make the trip to the Three Towns.\"","\"But, I...\"","Before Li Huai’gu could speak, Chen Yi raised a hand to interrupt him. \"The Three Towns are thousands of miles apart. It’s a long journey, and one month might not be enough time.\"","Li Huai’gu was taken aback. He lowered his head in thought for a moment, then said with sincere admiration, \"Thank you, Brother Qingzhou.\"","’He now understood that Chen Yi was telling him not to rush, but to wait and see how things developed. As for whether he could actually collect the grain tax from the Dingyuan Army... the key didn’t lie with him at all. In the end, it would be decided by the Xiao and Liu Families.’","\"No wonder Left Envoy Liu both set a time limit and demanded the maximum tax rate. He probably never thought I could complete the task.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"It certainly seems that way at present.\"","Li Huai’gu paused, then asked, \"And if a letter from the office comes while I’m on the road...\"","\"Just accept it.\"","\"Aren’t you worried about the Xiao Family, Brother Qingzhou?\"","Chen Yi replied in a casual tone, \"What’s there for a live-in son-in-law like me to worry about?\"","\"When the sky falls, the tall ones hold it up.\"","Li Huai’gu glanced at him, a trace of disbelief in his heart. ’Originally, he had only been grateful to Chen Yi because of the matter with Yun Xiang and Chen Yunfan. But after their recent conversation, he understood that Chen Yi was not as simple as he appeared on the surface. Whether it was their discussion about the recent imperial examinations at the Fengchun Building when they first met, or the subsequent rumors of his Poetry and Calligraphy... everything pointed to this fact.’","With this in mind, Li Huai’gu remarked with a sigh, \"Brother Qingzhou, for you to marry into the Xiao Family is truly... a waste of your talents.\"","Chen Yi pulled aside a window curtain, watching the falling rain and the pedestrians outside.","\"I think my current life is quite good. I’m very satisfied.\"","Li Huai’gu was struck speechless for a moment, then chuckled and didn’t pursue the topic.","In any case, he now had a clear path forward in his mind, and his mood had improved considerably.","\"For what you’ve told me just now, Brother Qingzhou, I will certainly repay you generously in the future.\"","Chen Yi pulled his gaze away from the window to look at him, asking with a smile, \"Can that be converted into silver?\"","\"They all say, ’Three years as an honest prefect yields a hundred thousand taels of silver.’ My demands aren’t high. Just give me ten thousand taels.\"","\"...Brother Qingzhou, you’re joking.\"","Of course, Li Huai’gu couldn’t possibly take his words seriously. ’But the admiration and sentiment he had felt just moments ago all dissipated with that one joke. The friendship between gentlemen is as transparent as water. Brother Qingzhou must see it that way,’ he thought.","Not long after, the two of them arrived at Guiyun Academy.","With Li Huai’gu leading the way, they saved a lot of trouble, and their passage was unimpeded.","Upon entering the academy, Chen Yi was greeted by the sight of a garden landscape.","A winding stone path, flanked by lush flowers and trees, led to a secluded, tranquil place.","Archways connected the green-tiled roofs and white walls, offering faint glimpses of several wooden buildings with flying eaves.","It was just the Hour of the Rabbit, and many Confucian scholars dressed in the Guiyun Academy uniform were coming and going.","Whenever they saw the two, they would stop and offer a respectful bow.","Li Huai’gu returned each bow, and Chen Yi naturally did the same.","As they walked, Li Huai’gu began to explain:","\"Guiyun Academy was built at the beginning of the Wei Dynasty, not long after the Barbarian Race had been driven out, when everything was waiting to be rebuilt.\"","\"The Governor of Shu State at the time, Lord Gao Li, established a school on this site and even specially invited Mr. Honghai of Qinghe Academy to serve as its headmaster...\"","Listening to his explanation, Chen Yi followed him deep into the academy to a courtyard, where he saw Mr. Yue Ming waiting for them outside the gate from a distance.","\"Greetings, Teacher.\"","Mr. Yue Ming smiled and nodded, exchanged a few pleasantries, and then led them into his study.","\"Qingzhou, if you hadn’t sent someone with a calling card yesterday, I would have gone to the Xiao Mansion to find you today.\"","As he spoke, he handed over a letter. \"A reply from your teacher.\"","’Chen Yi winced inwardly. He hadn’t expected his words to become a self-fulfilling prophecy. Mr. Yue Ming had actually written to Mr. Ju Yi.’","With that thought, he stepped forward, took the letter, and glanced over it. He saw that Mr. Ju Yi approved of him teaching at Guiyun Academy.","The letter also contained a few words of praise, saying he was quite knowledgeable.","After reading it, Chen Yi said with a look of resignation, \"Since my teacher has given his approval, I can only obey.\"","Mr. Yue Ming laughed heartily. \"You should have done so long ago.\"","Seeing this, Li Huai’gu, who was standing to the side, offered his congratulations to Chen Yi.","Afterward, Mr. Yue Ming told Chen Yi a bit about Guiyun Academy and the arrangements for his position.","Older people inevitably tend to be a bit long-winded.","Chen Yi didn’t pay much attention to the rest, only remembering one thing: \"You only need to teach for four intensive days a month; the students will practice on their own the rest of the time.\"","Besides teaching, he would also need to take a day or two to grade and comment on the students’ Calligraphy practice books.","’All told, it was less than a week’s work, which was quite relaxed.’","When Mr. Yue Ming saw this was all he cared about, he couldn’t help but laugh and scold, \"You truly are a lazy one.\"","\"I am only teaching Calligraphy. Too many lessons would be counterproductive.\"","\"I suppose you have a point...\"","The three of them continued to chat for a while.","Li Huai’gu, remembering his purpose for coming, brought up the arrangement from the Governor’s Office and asked for Mr. Yue Ming’s opinion.","Mr. Yue Ming thought for a moment, then frowned. \"Liu Hong’s arrangement, on one hand, is likely meant to put pressure on the Xiao Family.\"","\"On the other hand, it also serves to show his stance to the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"In either case, it’s not aimed at you.\"","\"However, this matter has far-reaching implications. Fang Gui, you must remember not to act rashly. Perhaps in a few days, there will be a turn of events.\"","Hearing him say the same thing, Li Huai’gu’s eyes widened slightly, and he was about to speak.","Seeing this, Chen Yi discreetly stepped on his foot, signaling for him to speak carefully.","Li Huai’gu understood. The smile on his face froze for a second. \"I will remember my teacher’s instructions. I’ll go back and pack my bags now.\"","With that, he looked at Chen Yi. \"Brother Qingzhou, would you like to go together?\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"You go on ahead. I plan to stay at Guiyun Academy today.\"","’If he returned to the Xiao Mansion now, it would be difficult to find a good reason to come out again later, so he might as well just stay at the academy.’","Mr. Yue Ming was naturally delighted that Chen Yi could stay and immediately pulled him toward a side study:","\"Come, come! On this joyous occasion, Qingzhou, why don’t you leave behind a piece of your calligraphy?\"","Chen Yi: \"...\"","’He wasn’t even going to pretend anymore, was he? The contract for hiring the Instructor hadn’t even been signed yet.’"]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135 - 131: Lazy Fellow","paragraphs":["After Li Huai’gu left, Chen Yi was \"forced\" to write two calligraphy pieces.","One in Wei Qing’s Style, and one in Cursive Script.","Every character bloomed with elegance, wreathed in a radiant glow that brightened the study, which had been left dim by the overcast sky.","This made Mr. Yue Ming so delighted he couldn’t stop smiling, repeatedly praising the work.","However, after only a moment of admiration, he hastily rolled up the calligraphy, placed it in a box like a precious treasure, and deliberately hid it on the bottom shelf of his desk.","Seeing Chen Yi’s slightly odd look, Mr. Yue Ming explained in a low voice, \"The other instructors at the academy are all shameless old coots.\"","\"If they see these, they’ll inevitably come and trouble you for some. I’m doing this for your own good.\"","Chen Yi privately pursed his lips. ’He’s just hogging them for himself, but as for his excuse... it’s actually pretty good.’","Chen Yi didn’t like trouble to begin with.","Besides, with so many things on his plate recently, the less trouble, the better.","Afterward, Mr. Yue Ming, in his capacity as the head of the academy, gave him a tour of the grounds.","They visited the library, the study halls, the zither room for practicing the Six Arts of a gentleman, the archery range, the riding grounds, and so on. It took half a day to see everything.","Chen Yi gained a general understanding of Guiyun Academy’s situation.","If nothing else, based on the scale of its book collection and the layout of its academic buildings alone, Guiyun Academy could probably rank in the top twenty in the Wei Dynasty.","The only academies with larger grounds, more impressive buildings, and more extensive book collections were those with long, storied histories.","Such as Jinling Academy, Donglin Academy, and Yu Mountain Academy in Jiangnan Prefecture, as well as Yuelu, Bailu Academy, and Great Liang Academy in the heart of the Central Plains.","Most of these were places where great Confucian scholars and famous masters gave lectures, and they had always been revered by countless students who considered it an honor to be admitted.","However, Chen Yi only had a vague impression of these places and had never seen them himself, so he just considered them to be more famous than Guiyun Academy.","「At noon.」","Mr. Yue Ming took Chen Yi to the academy’s dining hall to sample the vegetarian meal.","The food wasn’t particularly good, but it was enough to fill one’s stomach.","But it had one obvious advantage—it was free.","\"Our Guiyun Academy currently has eight hundred students. The youngest is eleven, while the oldest is thirty-one.\"","\"Although most of them come from the scholarly families of Shu State, there are also one or two hundred from poor backgrounds. The annual tuition is already a burden for them, so it would be wrong to let them be distracted from their studies by hunger.\"","Seeing Mr. Yue Ming speak so earnestly, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"That’s wonderful. You’ve been very thoughtful, sir. I’m impressed.\"","Mr. Yue Ming looked pleased. Just as he was about to speak, he saw several other instructors walking over and waved them over to introduce them to Chen Yi.","\"This is Zhuo Ying. He’s in charge of teaching the classics and histories. His knowledge is no less than my own.\"","\"I am Chen Yi, courtesy name Qingzhou. It is a pleasure to meet you, Mr. Zhuo Ying.\"","\"No need for such formalities. When Yue Ming first proposed inviting you to be an instructor at the academy, I was also in favor of it.\"","A short, stout, and kind-faced old man nearby interjected, \"Qingzhou, don’t listen to him. At the time, he was going on about how young you were.\"","\"...I haven’t had a game with you in a while. Tomorrow, I’m going to crush you on the Go board until not a single piece is left standing!\"","\"Why wait for tomorrow? I’ll be waiting for you later.\"","From this point on, the originally elegant and scholarly atmosphere took a sudden turn.","The other instructors chimed in, some supporting Mr. Zhuo Ying, others backing the kind-faced old man.","In an instant, Chen Yi, the new instructor, seemed to have become invisible.","Even Mr. Yue Ming, the head of the academy, was ignored, a strained smile on his face.","\"Qingzhou, you’ve just arrived at the academy. Some things aren’t quite as they appear on the surface... ahem.\"","Chen Yi watched the instructors bicker and nodded with a smile. \"Actually, I quite like this kind of academic atmosphere.\"","Perhaps because Shu State was far from the heart of the Central Plains, the instructors here weren’t all stuffy old pedants.","Starting with Mr. Yue Ming, besides their scholarly pursuits, the instructors also played chess, practiced calligraphy, and played the zither in their leisure time.","Based on this alone, Chen Yi felt he could fit in quite well.","’If the academy built a pond and stocked it with some fish, adding fishing as a recreational activity, I believe I could stay here for quite a while longer.’","Of course, for now, this was just a thought.","After all, he had only been at the academy for a day. It wouldn’t be too late to bring it up after he got to know everyone better.","「After noon.」","Chen Yi followed Mr. Yue Ming to several study halls where students were present, officially announcing that he had become an instructor.","The younger students were fine, mostly just curious.","But the gazes from a few of the older students were another matter.","Most looked at him with surprise and suspicion, while a small minority regarded him with outright disgust.","Taking a closer look, Chen Yi laughed to himself.","Those students who detested him were none other than the so-called scholars who had appeared at Li Huai’gu’s wedding banquet.","Among them were the two students who, because of him, had been punished by Mr. Yue Ming to copy the academy’s regulations a thousand times.","’If I were in their shoes, I’d probably detest me too.’","Chen Yi saw this but simply smiled and dismissed it.","He had come to Guiyun Academy not only because of Mr. Yue Ming’s earnest invitation and the encouragement of his wife Xiao Jinghong, Xiao Wan’er, and others, but more importantly, he hoped to use his position here to build a good relationship with Li Huai’gu.","Everyone and everything else was irrelevant to him.","After Mr. Yue Ming finished the announcements, he had Chen Yi draft an employment contract with him.","After it was signed and thumb-printed, it was sealed and stored away.","Mr. Yue Ming said hesitantly, \"The academy isn’t wealthy. The monthly salary is only one tael of silver. I hope you won’t find it too little, Qingzhou.\"","Chen Yi smiled and said, \"You’re too kind, sir.\"","\"Wealth is a worldly possession; I don’t place much importance on it.\"","Not to mention the monthly allowance he received from the Marquis’s Mansion and his pay from the Shopkeeper of Jishi Medicine Hall, the monthly income from Hundred Herbs Hall alone was enough for him to lie back and count his money.","He wasn’t short on money at all.","However, Mr. Yue Ming didn’t know this and simply took him for a man of noble character, praising him generously.","Once all this was settled, it was nearing dusk. Chen Yi asked Mr. Yue Ming for a cup of tea, they chatted for a bit, and then he rose to take his leave.","Before he left, Mr. Yue Ming reminded him, \"Qingzhou, your first class is scheduled for three days from now. Remember to prepare for it.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"Rest assured, sir. I have it under control.\"","It was only teaching calligraphy; for him, it wasn’t a difficult task.","Besides, the Great Wei placed great importance on the imperial examinations, which meant focusing on policy essays, classics, and histories. Most academies didn’t attach much importance to peripheral subjects like calligraphy.","In fact, most academies didn’t even have a dedicated calligraphy instructor.","From this point, it wasn’t hard to see how highly Mr. Yue Ming regarded him—or rather, how much he \"adored\" his calligraphy.","After bidding farewell to Mr. Yue Ming, Chen Yi left directly.","Along the way, he naturally encountered some students who had heard the news and bowed to him.","\"Greetings, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"No need for formalities.\"","\"Student...\"","He had to admit, the feeling of having people bow respectfully to him wherever he went was quite enjoyable.","However, once he stepped out of Guiyun Academy, the sight of Kangning Street in the rain brought him back down to earth.","The passersby hurried along; forget bowing to him, most didn’t even spare him a glance.","Chen Yi held his oil-paper umbrella, glanced at the sky where only a light drizzle remained, and gave a self-deprecating smile.","\"One wall separates two different worlds.\"","\"Time to face reality.\"","The \"reality\" in Chen Yi’s eyes was none other than the Xiao Family’s current situation.","Thus, after a brief pause, he started walking toward Fengchun Building.","Evening was still an hour away, so he had plenty of time.","Chen Yi ambled along, stopping now and then. When he saw a trinket that caught his eye, he would pause to examine it closely.","He even bought some study supplies to take back and use as decorations.","With his casual and leisurely air, anyone who saw him would have just taken him for a scholar out for a stroll.","Just like all the other talented scholars and beautiful ladies on Kangning Street.","Before long, Chen Yi arrived outside Fengchun Building and immediately spotted a carriage at the entrance bearing the red flag of the Xiao Family.","Then he saw Ge the Third, sitting at the front of the carriage, dangling one leg and looking around.","Chen Yi glanced at the sky, puzzled.","It was now less than ten minutes before evening. Why was Ge the Third so unhurried?","Puzzled, Chen Yi walked over and clapped him on the shoulder. \"Ge the Third.\"","Ge the Third turned, and upon seeing him, seemed to let out a sigh of relief. \"Young Master, you’re not at the mansion at this hour. What are you doing strolling around here?\"","Chen Yi could feel Ge the Third tense up for a moment, but he just smiled and explained:","\"I went to visit Mr. Yue Ming during the day and ended up staying at the academy a little long.\"","\"But it was for a good reason. Your Young Master is now an instructor at Guiyun Academy.\"","Ge the Third was stunned for a moment, then forced a smile. \"Congratulations, Young Master. With your knowledge, becoming an instructor at Guiyun Academy is a simple matter.\"","Chen Yi nodded and asked, \"Are you waiting for someone? If it’s convenient, could you give me a ride back to the mansion later?\"","Ge the Third hesitated for a moment. \"Master Dongchen asked me to pick him up here this morning. I’m afraid it might not be convenient.\"","\"Uncle Dongchen? Don’t worry, I’ll go speak with him...\"","He never finished his sentence.","Chen Yi saw a screen of light materialize before his eyes—","[Opportunity +10.]","[Evaluation: The person has arrived, yet their voice is unheard and the scene is unseen. When an opportunity falls from the heavens, you do not take it. This is the mark of an inherently lazy person.]","After reading it, Chen Yi calmly changed the subject. \"On second thought, it really isn’t appropriate.\"","With that, he patted Ge the Third’s shoulder and walked toward Fengchun Building.","\"I hear the iced sticky rice cakes here are quite good. I’m going to get some to go for Wuge to try.\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136 - 132: Brother Yi, You’ve Grown So Distant","paragraphs":["Ge the Third watched him enter Fengchun Building. He breathed a sigh of relief, but couldn’t help feeling a little puzzled.","Just a moment ago, the Fledgling’s words had clearly implied he wanted to return to the residence with them. Why the sudden change of heart?","Although this suited his and Xiao Dongchen’s wishes, he still felt the Fledgling had been acting strangely lately.","Coupled with the scent of blood he’d caught on the Fledgling the night before last, that sense of strangeness grew even stronger.","’I’ll have to find a chance to test him.’","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi, who had already entered Fengchun Building, was unaware of Ge the Third’s thoughts.","Of course, even if he had known, his attention was currently focused on the people around him. He had no time to worry about Ge the Third.","Since it wasn’t the two Hidden Guards, Ge the Third and Xiao Dongchen, discussing important matters in Fengchun Building, that meant a third Hidden Guard had to be here.","Furthermore, the meeting had lasted less than half a quarter-hour—perhaps even shorter—making it easy to deduce that Xiao Dongchen’s \"discussion\" with the other Hidden Guard hadn’t been lengthy.","Or rather, ’exchanging intelligence’ was a more fitting description.","Chen Yi considered this, his expression remaining calm.","He scanned his surroundings and saw that the main hall was mostly filled with wealthy merchants and Wandering Martial Artists, so he summoned a waiter.","\"Sir, how many in your party?\"","\"I’m not dining in. I’d like two orders of iced sticky rice cakes to go.\"","\"Of course. Please have a seat for a moment. They’ll be ready shortly.\"","The waiter led Chen Yi to a table, then shouted the order for two iced sticky rice cakes toward the kitchen.","Chen Yi sat at the table, his eyes scanning his surroundings from the corners of his vision while he focused all his attention on listening.","He released the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","One breath, two breaths, three...","Chen Yi’s expression suddenly flickered. He immediately reapplied the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to hide his presence.","The moment had been brief, but he had already identified a few familiar voices from the private room upstairs, as well as many more unfamiliar presences and voices.","Among them were Xiao Dongchen’s laughter, Chen Yunfan’s lazy and casual speech, and a hushed whisper:","\"Miss, I’ve investigated and confirmed that Ma Liangcai was originally a renowned doctor from the Wumeng Mountain area. He was later found by Hundred Herbs Hall and signed a contract with them.\"","\"Later, because of his connection to the Xiao Family, he started practicing at Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","\"Oh? So he really is skilled?\"","\"He should be... Huh? A strange Martial Artist has just entered Fengchun Building!\"","That was all he heard.","But it was enough for Chen Yi to confirm their identities—it was the very same Miss Cui and her maid from yesterday.","Putting aside her reasons for investigating Ma Liangcai...","Xiao Dongchen was clearly hosting Chen Yunfan today. Their conversation was filled with congratulations and flattery, and seemed otherwise unremarkable.","’Could it not be him?’","’Are there other Hidden Guards in Fengchun Building discussing important matters?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing and couldn’t help but frown. ’If that’s the case, my previous line of speculation was completely wrong.’","Just then, the sound of light footsteps reached his ears.","Chen Yi instantly calmed his mind and remained still, pretending to be an ordinary customer waiting for his iced sticky rice cakes.","Not long after, he caught sight of a petite woman in the corner of his eye, descending from upstairs into the main hall. She seemed to be surveying the surroundings.","It was none other than one of the maids he had seen following Miss Cui yesterday.","The maid also noticed Chen Yi. She paused, a look of disgust flashing across her face, before immediately turning and heading back upstairs.","Faintly, Chen Yi could just make out a muffled voice with his own hearing.","\"Miss, perhaps I was mistaken. The Martial Artist from before isn’t in the building. However...\"","\"However what?\"","\"I saw the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law downstairs.\"","Before Miss Cui could speak, Chen Yi heard another clear voice ask in surprise:","\"The Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law? Is Brother Yi downstairs?\"","\"...Yes.\"","Then, Chen Yi heard the sound of a table and chairs shifting, clear evidence that Chen Yunfan was heading downstairs.","Chen Yi pursed his lips. ’My dear brother seems awfully concerned about me.’","At that moment, the waiter returned carrying the pastries. \"Sir, your Iced Eight-Treasure Sticky Rice Cakes.\"","Chen Yi stood up to take them, pulling out some silver from his robes to hand to the waiter.","Before the waiter could take it, Chen Yunfan approached with a smile. \"Hold on, Brother Yi. No need to pay. I’ll take care of it with my bill.\"","Chen Yi paused and turned his head to look at him, feigning surprise. \"Brother, what are you doing here?\"","Chen Yunfan came over, smiling as he pushed Chen Yi’s hand away and motioned for the waiter to add it to the tab for the private room upstairs. Only then did he speak:","\"Now you’re just playing dumb.\"","\"I was unconscious for days. After my first day back on duty at the Government Office, of course I have to celebrate with my colleagues in the evening.\"","\"Oh, right, Xiao Dongchen is here too. Want to go say hello?\"","Chen Yi shook his head and gestured to the pastries in his hand. \"No need. There are people at the residence waiting for me.\"","Chen Yunfan chuckled. \"Your wife isn’t in Shu State. You only have maids to keep you company when you go back. Who’s waiting for you?\"","Chen Yi shot him a look, not bothering to waste any more words. He gave a slight bow and said:","\"Brother, you should get back to your colleagues. As a commoner, I wouldn’t dare impose.\"","Plenty of people were waiting for him to eat back at the residence: Xiaodie, Pei Guanli, Xiao Wuge, and Xiao Wan’er.","But obviously, he didn’t need to explain any of that to Chen Yunfan.","With that said, Chen Yi turned and walked out.","Seeing this, Chen Yunfan didn’t press him further. \"Brother Yi, thank you for stepping in to save me yesterday. As for the consultation fee, I’ve already had someone send it to Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand and walked straight out of Fengchun Building.","When he saw Ge the Third still waiting outside, he didn’t mention taking the carriage back to the residence with him.","’Looks like I won’t be able to find out what the Hidden Guards were discussing this time.’","’And I still don’t know who the other Hidden Guard in Fengchun Building was, besides Xiao Dongchen and Ge the Third.’","Lost in thought, Chen Yi greeted Ge the Third, then opened his umbrella and started walking toward the Xiao Family estate alone.","’I might have to use some... methods to pry open Ge the Third’s or Xiao Dongchen’s mouths.’","Once Chen Yi was a good distance away, Ge the Third glanced inside Fengchun Building. His gaze fell on Chen Yunfan, who had already returned upstairs, and he frowned slightly.","’This Imperial Top Scholar seems a little too enthusiastic about the Fledgling.’","’But on second thought, this could be a good thing.’","’Perhaps when one door closes, another opens.’","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yunfan returned to the private room. He was about to speak when he noticed Xiao Dongchen was gone and casually asked, \"Has Advisor Xiao left?\"","Cui Qingwu shook her head. \"He said he ran into an acquaintance and went to ask for a cup of wine.\"","Chen Yunfan grunted. \"He certainly has a lot of acquaintances. He’s already stepped out a few times. I’m not sure if he’s hosting me or someone else.\"","Saying this, he paid Xiao Dongchen no more mind, sat down, and picked up his chopsticks to eat by himself.","As he ate, he muttered, \"Brother Yi is still so distant with me. I invite him for a meal, and he makes all sorts of excuses.\"","\"Doesn’t he realize his own brother would never harm him?\"","\"Advisor Xiao happened to be here today. I wanted him to come over and get acquainted, so his life in the Xiao Family might be a little easier in the future.\"","Cui Qingwu looked at him with her slightly narrow eyes. \"Yunfan, you still care for Chen Yi with such deep brotherly affection.\"","\"Of course. Blood is thicker than water.\"","\"Besides, it’s thanks to him that I woke up. He brought a Physician to save me yesterday. I almost missed something important.\"","Chen Yunfan continued rambling, \"I only found out today when I got to the Government Office that Left Envoy Liu of the Governor’s Office already made arrangements yesterday.\"","\"Everyone has to go to the various counties and towns to collect grain taxes, and I was assigned a post as well.\"","\"Luckily, I’m only in charge of the towns and villages around the Prefecture City. At least I don’t have to go to the military garrisons like that unlucky Li Huai’gu.\"","A faint smile appeared on Cui Qingwu’s face. \"I’m not familiar with the official duties of the Governor’s Office, so it’s not my place to comment.\"","\"My only concern is the powder that made you unconscious, and finding the person behind it.\"","Chen Yunfan glanced at her sideways and scoffed, \"You’re meddling in things that don’t concern you. I’ll find them myself.\"","\"You’re the Assistant Governor of the Governor’s Office now, busy with official duties. You can leave such minor matters to me.\"","\"You? You should just go back to wherever you came from.\"","\"I don’t know if you’re just bored or what. Does the Qinghe Cui Family not feed you or something? Running all the way to Shu State by yourself.\"","Cui Qingwu pressed her lips together, then broke into a smile. \"There’s nothing at home that requires my attention. I had nothing better to do, so I thought it would be nice to come here and keep Yunfan company.\"","\"...I think you’re just bored.\"","Cui Qingwu knew she couldn’t afford to be idle.","Either way, she wouldn’t be leaving Shu State just like that.","After Xiao Dongchen returned and they exchanged a few pleasantries, Chen Yunfan rose to take his leave.","「A short while later.」","A carriage bearing the insignia of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family traveled in front, followed by another bearing the insignia of the Qinghe Cui Family.","\"Miss, since Young Master Yunfan is so ungrateful, why must you...\"","\"Slap yourself!\"","SLAP, SLAP!"]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137 - 133: Great Success in Fist Dao","paragraphs":["In the overcast Shu State City, nightfall came a little earlier than usual.","The sky had already grown dim, though it wasn’t yet seven o’clock.","Along both sides of Kangning Street, shops began to light up lanterns, one by one, casting a warm, pearly-white glow.","Some lanterns were plain and white, while others bore characters like \"Medicine,\" \"Books,\" or \"Cloth.\"","In any case, they lit the way for the passing pedestrians.","Chen Yi held an Oil Paper Umbrella, walking unhurriedly along the side of the bluestone road to avoid blocking any passing carriages.","A fine, continuous drizzle tapped against the surface of the umbrella, making a series of faint, pattering sounds.","It mixed with the chirping of cicadas, the rumble of passing carriage wheels, and the sounds of laughter and arguments from the pedestrians all around.","It was noisy, but it was the lively clamor of the mortal world.","But none of it registered in Chen Yi’s ears. Even his eyes seemed to have become semi-automatic, mechanical things.","They only alerted him to turn left or right to bypass obstacles in his path.","His entire mind was still back inside the Fengchun Building.","He replayed the sounds from that brief moment—lasting only three breaths’ time—over and over.","There were the voices of Xiao Dongchen, Chen Yunfan, Miss Cui, and others, as well as sounds from the main hall and the private rooms upstairs.","Most were just half-sentences or meaningless filler words.","Things like \"...like Lord Liu, he...\" and \"...a tigress of a wife, not at all like Brother Fang’s concubine, who is so...\"","So... what?","Chen Yi subconsciously filled in a few adjectives: peerlessly beautiful, gentle, or charming.","Fragmented and pieced together.","Of the remaining meaningful words, most were not as valuable as Miss Cui’s focus on Ma Liangcai.","Chen Yi noted down the few pieces of useful information and who had said them, and a deduction formed in his mind.","’The Hidden Guards were discussing important matters. One of them could only be Xiao Dongchen.’","’He must have used an excuse to slip away from Chen Yunfan and the others to exchange intelligence with another Hidden Guard.’","The time was very short, and they couldn’t make any noise, or Chen Yunfan and the people from the Cui Family would have surely noticed.","’So he might have written down the intelligence beforehand, or simply written with water, discussing the matter silently with someone.’","Chen Yi reasoned thus. He then put himself in Xiao Dongchen’s shoes, wondering what could be considered \"important matters\" at a time like this.","’Sabotaging the Mutual Market between the Mountain Race and the Dingyuan Army?’","’No.’","’Burning the granaries of the Three Towns?’","’There’s a chance.’","But based on the information he’d overheard earlier, Xiao Dongchen should be conspiring with Ge the Third on that matter.","That left the arrangements of the Governor’s Office and the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families.","At this thought, Chen Yi came back to his senses, stopped, and rubbed the bridge of his nose.","He thought it over and over.","He still held to his previous deduction—Xiao Dongchen intended to profit from the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families.","Just like how he wanted to burn the granaries of the Three Towns to sabotage the construction of the Mutual Market.","This time, he would probably pull the same trick. His goal should be to incite conflict between the Xiao and Liu families and throw the Xiao Family into complete chaos.","’Only this would align with the goal of him and the second branch he represents: to seize control of the entire Xiao Family.’","Working backward from the goal and the likely outcome, it wasn’t hard to reach this conclusion.","The difficult part was,","what did Xiao Dongchen and the second branch plan to do, or what arrangements had he made for those Hidden Guards?","Just as Chen Yi was pondering this, he heard the sound of hooves and wheels from behind, followed by a familiar voice by his ear:","\"Young Master, why are you just standing at the gate instead of going in?\"","Chen Yi glanced back and saw Ge the Third returning with the carriage. Looking forward again, he finally noticed he was already standing outside the Xiao Mansion gate.","He smiled and said, \"I got tired from walking, just resting for a moment.\"","Ge the Third was about to say more when Xiao Dongchen, inside the carriage behind him, lifted the curtain and said:","\"Qingzhou, the city has been unsettled lately. If it’s not important, don’t go out. It’s better to stay in the mansion.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and nodded with a smile. \"Thank you for the reminder, Uncle Dongchen. I’ll keep it in mind.\"","Xiao Dongchen gave a noncommittal grunt, lowered the curtain, and gestured for Ge the Third to return to the mansion.","The carriage entered the Xiao Family grounds first.","Chen Yi watched them disappear behind the spirit screen, paused for a moment, and then followed them into the residence.","Faintly, he could still hear snippets of conversation.","\"He’s at Guiyun Academy now. He must have his own plans.\"","\"That’s your business, it has nothing to do with me. Don’t forget what you promised me.\"","\"Once I’m free... those people still want to wander around tomorrow...\"","The voices were barely audible.","If Chen Yi hadn’t been focusing his attention on the front courtyard, he probably wouldn’t have heard anything.","It was a good thing it was him. Anyone else, even if they had heard it, probably wouldn’t have thought much of it.","’Those two are a Hidden Guard and a Silver Banner Officer, and they’re not even trying to be discreet while discussing secret matters?’","He had his thoughts, but Chen Yi was also well aware that they didn’t give a second glance to a \"frail scholar\" like him.","’I’m sure the looks on their faces will be priceless when they find out my Martial Arts are not to be trifled with someday.’","Chen Yi snorted to himself and headed straight back to Spring Lotus Garden.","The three of them—Xiaodie, Pei Guanli, and Xiao Wuge—were in the pavilion and hurried over to greet him when they saw him.","\"Young Master, you’re back late again today.\"","\"Brother-in-law, I’ve been waiting for you for so long the food’s gotten cold.\"","Xiaodie’s tone was plaintive, but it was easy to hear the worry in her voice.","Pei Guanli, on the other hand, rubbed her stomach with genuine grievance. She had clearly been hungry for a long time.","Xiao Wuge was his usual cheerful self, asking with a grin, \"Brother-in-law, did everything go smoothly at Guiyun Academy?\"","Chen Yi entered the pavilion, closed his Oil Paper Umbrella, and said with a smile, \"It went well enough. In a few days, I’ll be going to the academy to teach calligraphy.\"","He then placed the iced sticky rice cakes on the stone table. \"I knew you’d be waiting for me, so I got two servings of iced sticky rice cakes to-go from the Fengchun Building.\"","Hearing there was something good to eat, Xiaodie’s face instantly lit up with a smile. She eagerly unwrapped the package, and then...","She first placed a rice cake in Xiao Wuge’s bowl, followed by Chen Yi’s and Pei Guanli’s.","When it was her turn, her big eyes looked toward Chen Yi.","As if asking, ’Can I have some, too?’","How could Chen Yi not know what she was thinking? He picked up a piece with his chopsticks and placed it in her bowl. \"Go on, try it.\"","\"Thank you, Young Master.\"","With food and drink, chatter and laughter, the atmosphere grew warm and cozy again.","Nearby, Xiao Wan’er heard their voices and breathed a sigh of relief, though she couldn’t help but mutter to herself that Chen Yi had let her warnings go in one ear and out the other.","’But since he came back so late, things at Guiyun Academy must have gone smoothly, right?’","...","After dinner, Chen Yi returned to his room. After a short rest, he summoned the luminous screen and took a look.","[Opportunity: 135]","’I can still raise one more Dao to Great Success...’","Currently, his Calligraphy Dao, Medical Dao, Martial Arts Body, and Step were at the Great Success Realm. His Martial Arts Fist, Martial Arts Spear, and Chess Dao were at the Minor Success Realm.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi used his Opportunity to raise his Martial Arts Fist to the Great Success Realm. Profound Mysteries immediately flooded his mind.","He currently lacked a weapon that was easy to carry. To be safe, upgrading his Fist Dao was the least likely to be discovered.","It wouldn’t be too late to upgrade his Spear Dao once he had enough Opportunity.","’My Chess Dao is sufficient for now. Later, I’ll need to find time to master the Zither and Painting to avoid anyone discovering my weaknesses.’","With that in mind, Chen Yi wasn’t in a hurry to comprehend the Profound Mysteries of the Fist Dao. He sat cross-legged on his bed and continued his Cultivation of the >.","Not until the hour of Zi, when a bright light appeared before his eyes, did he slowly cease his cultivation.","When he saw the contents of the luminous screen clearly, he couldn’t help but let out a soft \"Huh?\"","[Daily Intel · Profound-rank Middle Grade: At the hour of Xu, the Shu State Imprisonment Department will discover a trace of Liu Jing’s killer outside the Hui Xian Building in the West Market and will apprehend the culprit. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","Chen Yi frowned as he read the message. ’...Outside the Hui Xian Building, huh? Is the Imprisonment Department really that competent?’","That day, he had been \"invited\" away by Liu Jing’s men from an alley entrance right outside the Hui Xian Building.","He thought his work had been flawless, and with two consecutive days of rain, he never expected the Imprisonment Department to trace him there.","But then, Chen Yi realized something was wrong.","’Apprehend the culprit outside the Hui Xian Building?’","’Under normal circumstances, I should be at home tomorrow evening during the hour of Xu. How could I possibly end up there?’","After a moment of contemplation.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but curse inwardly. ’Damn it, don’t tell me someone is going to pose as the killer?’","Connecting this to the important matters Xiao Dongchen and the other Hidden Guards were discussing, he instantly had a bold guess.","He feared that \"culprit\" was going to be framed as someone acting under the Xiao Family’s orders.","Or perhaps, he was a member of the Xiao Family himself.","’If that’s the case... I have to go take a look, no matter what.’"]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138 - 134: A Big Mouth and a Smart Mouth","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, the rain that had fallen for two days finally stopped.","As the sun rose, the clouds in the east were painted in a riot of color.","However, this beautiful scene lasted for less than fifteen minutes before the sky cleared completely, filled with pristine white clouds that drifted and changed with the wind.","Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge rose early as usual, and even Pei Guanli was up, washed, and dressed before five in the morning.","Her fair, bare feet skipped along the bluestone path as she ran over, the bell on her chest swaying.","JINGLE, JINGLE, it rang without stopping.","When Xiaodie heard the noise, she quickly put a finger to her lips and pointed upstairs.","Pei Guanli took the hint, clutching her bell to silence it. She sat down quietly at the table. \"Brother-in-law isn’t up yet?\"","Xiaodie nodded softly. \"Perhaps he’s tired from all the walking at Guiyun Academy yesterday. I checked on him this morning, and he was still fast asleep.\"","Pei Guanli murmured an \"oh.\" After greeting Xiao Wuge, she picked up her breakfast from the table and began to eat.","She was a true native of Shu State and loved spicy food.","Back when she lived on Wumeng Mountain, her breakfast would be chili peppers and steamed cornbread, and she could eat several of them.","Sometimes, when the clan ran out of fine and coarse flour, they would make wild vegetable soup, and she would still cover her entire bowl with chilis.","Whenever she finished eating, her fair, round face would be flushed bright red, which was why the people of the Mountain Race called her \"Hong Mei’er.\"","Xiao Wuge, who was in the middle of eating his porridge, saw this and couldn’t help but ask, \"Sister Guanli, is plain porridge with chilis any good?\"","\"It’s delicious.\"","As she spoke, Pei Guanli scooped a spoonful of chilis into his bowl. \"Try it.\"","Xiao Wuge hesitated for a moment, then stirred his bowl a couple of times with his spoon and took a sip.","An intense spiciness immediately flooded his mouth.","\"Spicy! So spicy! Water, water, water! HSSS... HAH... HSSS...\"","Xiao Wuge’s little face visibly reddened, and he grimaced, motioning for Xiaodie to get him a glass of water.","At a time like this, Xiaodie knew better than to give him plain water. After a quick look around, she opened a bottle of Wangji Tea and handed it to him.","Xiao Wuge took it and gulped down a couple of mouthfuls, and only then did his mouth begin to feel better.","Seeing his reaction, Pei Guanli burst into carefree laughter, winking as she did so.","\"Your face is red now, too. From now on, I’ll call you Brother Hong.\"","That way, the Mountain Race would have its \"Hong Mei’er,\" and the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion would have its \"Brother Hong.\"","Xiao Wuge didn’t mind the nickname. His face was still scrunched up. \"It’s so spicy, Sister Guanli. Doesn’t it bother you?\"","\"Of course not. I’ve been eating like this since I was a kid.\"","As Pei Guanli spoke, her eyes landed on the Wangji Tea in his hand. She thought for a moment before saying:","\"This drink seems to be all the rage in the city lately. I’ve seen lots of people carrying it around the past few days.\"","Xiao Wuge subconsciously took another sip before replying, \"The Medicine Hall that Brother-in-law manages sells it. It’s made by Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","He gave a whole grown-up-sounding explanation, but Pei Guanli barely registered it. The only two words that stuck were \"tastes good.\"","\"Let me try some too.\"","\"I’ll go get some.\"","Xiaodie ran to the storeroom and returned carrying two porcelain bottles. \"One is Wangji Tea, same as what Young Master Wuge has, and the other is Mushroom Tea.\"","\"Which one do you want?\"","After asking, she added, \"The master said the Mushroom Tea is more suitable for women.\"","\"The mushroom one.\"","Pei Guanli took it, eagerly opened it, and took a sip. Her eyes immediately lit up.","\"It’s sweet and sour! This is delicious!\"","\"Back with my clan, I especially loved eating the wild peaches from the mountains. This tastes pretty similar.\"","Before long, she had finished the entire bottle.","She wanted to ask for another bottle, but seeing it was getting late, she had no choice but to wipe her mouth clean and run toward Jiaxing Garden.","\"I’ll buy a few more bottles to drink next time I’m out on the streets.\"","Watching her dash off in a flurry, Xiao Wuge put on an adult-like expression and remarked:","\"Sister Guanli is so valiant.\"","Xiaodie couldn’t help but laugh. \"’Valiant’ is a word used to describe men or soldiers.\"","\"If she were to join the army, I imagine she would still be... a bit lacking compared to Second Sister.\"","After they finished breakfast, seeing that Chen Yi still hadn’t gotten up, Xiao Wuge had Xiaodie take him to Jiaxing Garden.","After spending so much time with him, they all knew Chen Yi’s habits.","Occasionally, when he had nothing important to do, he would sleep until the sun was high in the sky.","Once Spring Lotus Garden had fallen completely silent,","Chen Yi, inside his room, let out a long breath. He slowly concluded his cultivation, rose to his feet, and looked out the window.","The sunlight was perfect. Spring Lotus Garden was awash in verdant green, and as the pond’s surface rippled, a few Golden Carp would occasionally leap from the water.","Some of the resulting splashes landed back on the surface, creating new ripples. Others struck a few birds drinking at the pond’s edge, causing them to fly off with a flurry of chirps.","Moreover, someone had swept the garden clean of fallen leaves and petals, making it look all the more fresh and natural.","Chen Yi’s spirits lifted as he took in the scene.","’Clear skies after the rain. That’s a good omen.’","However, this tranquil and comfortable state of mind vanished the moment he finished dressing and arrived at the Purple Bamboo Forest.","Chen Yi calmed his mind, planted his feet firmly, and began to practice the Big Spear Pile Skill.","Although the Power he gained from the Pile Skill was now minuscule, it was still an excellent way to activate his body.","His muscles, bones, skin, and flesh—his entire physical form, down to every strand of hair—could be controlled using the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique.","「About half an hour later.」","Chen Yi concluded his Pile Skill practice and, taking advantage of the surging Blood Qi and Power, switched to practicing the Mountain Shattering Fist and the Hundred Flowers Palm.","One was fierce and powerful, the other nimble and fluid.","Though they were two completely different styles of Fist Technique and Palm Technique, complete with their own Step Techniques, he executed them with a seamless, natural grace.","They possessed a far greater depth and rhythm than before.","This newfound rhythm was nothing other than the enhancement from his Mental Realm, a benefit of achieving the Great Success stage in his Martial Arts Fist."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139 - 134: Loose-tongued and a Smart Mouth","paragraphs":["Every move he made circulated his True Essence, drawing in the Spiritual Qi of Heaven and Earth and causing the ground to tremble in a wide radius around him.","With every fluid transition between fist and palm, a blurry, spectral image would appear behind him.","It greatly amplified the power of his punches and palm strikes.","The surrounding bamboo stalks would sometimes bend low as if struck by a gale, and at other times sway as though caressed by a gentle breeze, shaking loose a cascade of leaves.","Chen Yi was oblivious to all this, focused only on absorbing the profound mysteries of the Martial Arts Fist and improving his Mountain Shattering Fist and Hundred Flowers Palm as much as he could.","One hour, two hours, three...","It wasn’t until nearly noon that Xiaodie’s figure emerged from Jiaxing Garden.","Only then did Chen Yi stop. He calmed the surging True Essence and Power within him while using his True Essence to vaporize the sweat from his skin.","In just three breaths, he was back to his usual cool and composed self.","Before Xiaodie could find him, Chen Yi stepped out of the bamboo forest.","Xiaodie paused, startled to see him, but she didn’t ask any questions. She simply smiled and said,","\"Young Master, you’re awake! Are you hungry? The young mistress asked me to fetch you for lunch.\"","Chen Yi nodded and casually instructed, \"There are still some fallen leaves in the bamboo forest that haven’t been swept up. I’ll have to trouble you to take care of them.\"","Xiaodie let out a small \"Ah!\" and muttered that she had just swept that morning, but she still scrambled to get a broom and dustpan.","Chen Yi grinned. \"There’s no rush. It can wait until after lunch.\"","Xiaodie hesitated for a moment, then shook her head. \"Young Master, I’m not hungry. You should go eat, so the young mistress doesn’t have to wait.\"","Seeing her insistence, Chen Yi had no choice but to head toward Jiaxing Garden.","Xiaodie watched him walk away, a determined expression settling on her face. With a broom in one hand and a dustpan in the other, she charged into the Purple Bamboo Forest.","It was as if she were going to do battle with those \"disobedient bamboos.\"","Chen Yi heard the sounds behind him and thought, ’Sorry about that.’ He continued straight on into Jiaxing Garden.","Compared to the lush scenery of Spring Lotus Garden, Jiaxing Garden was much more serene and secluded.","Flowers and grasses grew in abundance, but there were few trees, making it resemble the landscape gardens typical of Jiangnan Prefecture.","Beyond the covered walkway was a small path paved with crushed stone. Taller flowering plants lined both sides, obscuring the view of what lay within.","After rounding the path, Chen Yi saw Xiao Wan’er waiting in front of the wooden house.","She was dressed differently today, wearing a simple white-padded jacket over a long, tangerine-colored skirt. Standing under the shade of a tree in front of the house, she was speckled with spots of dappled sunlight.","It made her seem all the more radiant.","Especially when she saw Chen Yi, the faint smile that touched her lips made her look even more graceful and captivating.","It seemed that as warmth returned to her body, she was no longer burdened by the worries and sorrows that once plagued her.","Seeing her from a distance, Chen Yi raised his hand in greeting. \"Morning.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s expression turned to one of playful reproach. \"It’s already noon. Still ’morning’?\"","Chen Yi walked over with a smile and explained casually,","\"Mr. Yue Ming showed me around Guiyun Academy yesterday, so I got back late and slept in a little this morning.\"","Xiao Wan’er knew as much, so she didn’t dwell on his greeting and simply asked, \"Did everything go smoothly?\"","Chen Yi was about to answer when he caught sight of Xiao Wuge rubbing his stomach. Realizing the boy was hungry, he just said, \"It went smoothly,\" and gestured for them to continue inside.","Taking his cue, Xiao Wan’er led him to a seat and called for Cui’er and Juan’er to bring out the food.","\"I thought as much. Since Mr. Yue Ming was the one who invited you to be an instructor at the academy, he wouldn’t go back on his word unless something unexpected happened.\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips. \"It would’ve been better if he had.\"","\"When I got there yesterday, a letter from my teacher had just arrived. That’s when I found out Mr. Yue Ming had actually written to him.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er’s eyes crinkled with a smile. \"I imagine Mr. Ju Yi also persuaded you to go to Guiyun Academy, didn’t he?\"","\"Yes, and he put in quite a few good words for me.\"","\"That’s good, then.\"","The food was served, and they chatted as they ate.","Xiao Wan’er asked, \"Now that you’re going to the academy, will you still be managing Jishi Medicine Hall?\"","Chen Yi hesitated for a moment before nodding. \"I’ll manage both. An extra shopkeeper’s monthly wage is always nice.\"","\"Don’t be ridiculous. If the academy takes up too much of your time, I’ll arrange for someone else to take over as shopkeeper at Jishi Medicine Hall.\"","\"That won’t be necessary for now. I only have to teach at the academy four days a month. I should be able to manage the Medicine Hall as well.\"","Before Xiao Wan’er could respond, Xiao Wuge piped up with a mischievous grin, \"Brother-in-law hasn’t been to the Medicine Hall in days.\"","\"...You and your big mouth.\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s disgruntled expression, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but beam. \"Well, if that’s the case, you certainly can continue as the Medicine Hall’s shopkeeper.\"","This sent Xiao Wuge, Juan’er, and Cui’er into peals of laughter.","At this, Chen Yi feigned a sigh. \"Ah, you all have no idea how hard I work.\"","\"Yes, yes, of course... Brother-in-law works the hardest.\"","The others simply took his words as a joke.","But only Chen Yi himself knew the truth. ’I must have been born to a life of toil.’","He had hoped to live as a leisurely son-in-law in the Marquis’s Mansion, but one matter after another, both present and future, forced him to stay busy.","After lunch, Chen Yi didn’t linger in Jiaxing Garden. He told Xiao Wan’er he had to make a trip to Hundred Herbs Hall.","Xiao Wan’er walked him to the door, reminding him, \"Things are unsettled in the mansion right now. Be careful when you go out.\"","\"Don’t be like yesterday, going out by yourself without even taking a Personal Guard.\"","At this, she paused, then added hesitantly, \"If this is about my earlier request to meet the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall, it can be postponed.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi smiled, gave a slight bow to show he understood, and told her to go back inside Jiaxing Garden.","\"Even though your health has improved, you still need to stay warm. For instance, what you’re wearing now...\"","He pointed to her tangerine skirt. \"You could easily catch a chill.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced down, her face instantly flushing red. She looked up, about to scold him, only to see that Chen Yi was already jogging away with a smile.","She could only swallow her words. As she turned, a single word escaped her lips:","\"Nosy...\"","And a smart mouth, at that.","...","He made his way out of the Xiao Mansion.","As usual, Chen Yi did not allow any Armored Warriors to accompany him.","Not that he could have, even if he wanted to. He reckoned the mansion couldn’t spare the manpower right now.","From what he could observe, the atmosphere in the mansion was even more tense today than it had been yesterday.","Not only were the Armored Warriors standing guard with grim expressions at various residences and strategic points, but even the maids and household servants were all rushing about their tasks.","Clearly, the atmosphere in the Xiao Mansion would remain like this until there were some leads in the matter of Liu Jing’s death.","Chen Yi was well aware of this, but for the moment, he had no good solution.","’It’s not like I can go to the Government Office and turn myself in, can I?’","However, while he couldn’t offer any major help, there were smaller things he could do.","Or, to be more precise, he could try to resolve this crisis himself.","Ever since seeing that message last night and forming that bold conjecture about Xiao Dongchen’s involvement, an idea had taken root in Chen Yi’s mind.","’If the Hidden Guard can find a scapegoat ’murderer,’ then so can I.’","Unfortunately, he didn’t have much time. His current plan was to go and check out the situation tonight before deciding on his next move.","If a \"murderer\" with ties to the Xiao Family really did appear, he would have no choice but to take some risks.","No matter what, he couldn’t allow that \"murderer\" to be linked to the Xiao Family.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi arrived outside the West Market. He scanned the area around the Hui Xian Building but didn’t see anyone from the Imprisonment Department.","After a moment’s thought, he decided not to rush to Hundred Herbs Hall. Instead, he circled the area a few times.","He explored the small alleyways and potential hiding spots, familiarizing himself with the lay of the land.","Once he was satisfied he’d seen enough, Chen Yi finally entered Hundred Herbs Hall.","Wang Ji, who was in the main hall attending to customers, spotted him at once and came over with a smile. \"Shopkeeper Chen, a rare guest indeed.\"","Chen Yi smiled and exchanged a few pleasantries before following him inside. He caught sight of the \"Sword Madman,\" Liu Lang, out of the corner of his eye, but followed Wang Ji upstairs without breaking stride.","’His injuries don’t seem to be getting any better. Are they really that severe?’","Through his Qi Observation Skill, Chen Yi could see that the wound on Liu Lang’s chest showed very limited signs of healing.","Even his internal injuries showed no improvement. It was as if wisps of some strange True Essence or other power were actively hindering his recovery.","Chen Yi mulled this over as he followed Wang Ji upstairs.","’All things considered,’ he thought, ’Liu Lang being in a state where he can only use his True Essence to keep his injuries from worsening is actually a good thing.’","’At least he can’t use his Martial Arts at will.’","They arrived at a private room.","Wang Ji closed the door and windows, then said in a tone eager for praise, \"Sir, there’s been a development on that matter you instructed me about last time.\""]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140 - 135: See if He’ll Take the Bait","paragraphs":["After listening, Chen Yi showed no sign of pleasure. Instead, he waved his hand dismissively and said with a smile,","\"I don’t dare accept such a title from you, Boss Wang.\"","\"After all, the business between Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall was arranged between you and the Young Miss. I’m just running an errand on her behalf.\"","Even though Liu Lang was injured and his True Essence was likely not flowing freely, his hearing alone was sharp enough to pick up the voices from upstairs.","Even with all the soundproofing in this quiet room, it was no use.","In fact, it wasn’t just Liu Lang.","Chen Yi himself could also hear some of the sounds from outside at that moment, but they were too faint for him to make them out clearly.","Wang Ji paused at his words, but when he saw Chen Yi raise a hand and point downstairs, he understood.","\"You jest, sir. Outside, I can call you Shopkeeper, but I’m afraid it’s improper in private.\"","\"If the Young Miss found out, she’d surely have me flogged.\"","Chen Yi made a gesture to maintain the status quo, then continued, \"As long as the person is capable enough, spending a bit more on silver coins doesn’t matter.\"","\"Rest assured.\"","Wang Ji took the opportunity to mention Liu Lang, saying, \"Just like Liu Yuan, this person’s abilities will certainly not disappoint you.\"","Chen Yi said with a smile, \"After what happened with the Illusory Sound Sect, it’s good that you’re being cautious, Boss Wang.\"","\"Indeed...\"","The two chatted idly upstairs, their voices carrying clearly to Liu Lang’s ears.","Listening to the Xiao Family’s son-in-law and the Hundred Herbs Hall Shopkeeper trade pleasantries, he couldn’t help but purse his lips.","’If you told people he was a scholar, I doubt anyone would believe you. What kind of scholar is so mercenary?’","Liu Lang felt more and more that Chen Yi was unworthy of Xiao Jinghong.","It wasn’t just a matter of education—in every conceivable way, he was unworthy of General Jinghong.","’I’d always heard the saying \"a beautiful flower stuck in a pile of cow dung,\" and I used to think it was just an expression. Now I’ve seen it with my own eyes.’","’This is an even more extreme case.’","Liu Lang continued listening to the conversation from upstairs, feeling indignant on Xiao Jinghong’s behalf.","As he mulled it over, his thoughts took another turn.","’Then again, for someone like General Jinghong, there aren’t many people in this world who would be worthy of her.’","His thoughts then drifted to this topic, and he began to list, one by one, the men who might be worthy of Xiao Jinghong in terms of family background, status, appearance, and power.","’The Young Master of the Broken Sword Manor is one. At only twenty years old, his Cultivation has already reached the Upper Three Grades, and he’s said to be strikingly handsome.’","’However, the Broken Sword Manor is a far cry from the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, so he’d have to be at the bottom of the list.’","’The second son of the Luo Family in Jiangnan Prefecture is another candidate. His family background is impressive, and his appearance, status, and Cultivation are likely all top-notch.’","’Then there’s \"Flying Flower Sword\" Gao Xun...’","Fortunately, Chen Yi didn’t know what Liu Lang was thinking. Otherwise, he would have, at the very least, tossed a bottle of Immortal Drunk his way before sharpening his blades.","After confirming the details about the Jianghu person skilled in the Disguise Skill that Wang Ji had mentioned, Chen Yi told him to get the man settled in first.","Wang Ji nodded with a smile. \"Sir, he’s in the back courtyard right now.\"","\"Speaking of which, he’s quite capable. Besides that particular skill, he also used to brew wine.\"","\"His technique is so-so, though. Just a little better than the rice wine an ordinary person might brew.\"","\"A well-rounded talent, I see.\"","As he said this, Chen Yi mused, \"But it’s not quite appropriate for him to be in the back courtyard. Find another place for him.\"","Wang Ji paused for a moment, then readily agreed. \"I’ll find another place for him tomorrow.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, asked about the current situation at Hundred Herbs Hall, and once he had a general idea of Wang Ji’s plans, he rose to leave.","As he walked downstairs, he added a word of caution,","\"Ma Liangcai and the other Divine Doctors are consulting at the Xiao Family Medicine Hall now, and they’re attracting a lot of attention.\"","\"In a bit, I’ll have to trouble you to look after a few things for them, Boss Wang.\"","Wang Ji’s expression shifted slightly. \"You mean...\"","\"For example, his family or neighbors... we should make a gesture of some kind.\"","Chen Yi was being subtle, merely reminding him that someone had their eyes on Ma Liangcai and that he needed to tie up any loose ends.","Wang Ji nodded in understanding. \"I’ll make the arrangements shortly. We certainly won’t treat them poorly.\"","\"Good.\"","Arriving downstairs, Chen Yi glanced at Liu Lang and saw him maintaining his usual lazy posture.","After a moment’s thought, he walked over, clasped his hands in a polite gesture, and said with a smile, \"I was just listening to Boss Wang praise Brother Liu’s incredible skills.\"","\"And looking at you now, Brother Liu certainly has an extraordinary air about him.\"","Liu Lang shot him a sideways glance and said flatly, \"You’re too kind.\"","\"I don’t know much about the affairs of the Jianghu. I was wondering, where would Brother Liu’s skills rank among its members?\"","\"Not as good as the best, but better than the rest.\"","Chen Yi asked with a smile, \"The Upper Three Grades?\"","Liu Lang’s eyes flew wide, and a curse almost escaped his lips.","’Do you think the Upper Three Grades are a dime a dozen?’","\"Shopkeeper Chen, you jest. I am merely in the humble Middle Three Grades Realm.\"","Chen Yi paused, then said with a smile, \"That’s already incredibly impressive. You’re a great deal stronger than the Personal Guards in the Xiao Mansion.\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang looked displeased. \"Shopkeeper Chen, you really don’t understand the ways of the Jianghu. Most men in the army only begin their Cultivation as adults, so it’s perfectly normal for their Martial Arts Cultivation to be low.\"","\"Is that so...\"","Seeing that Chen Yi wasn’t in a hurry to leave, Wang Ji didn’t rush him, simply chiming in with a few agreeable remarks from the side.","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi’s expression turned serious, and he asked, \"Brother Liu, your complexion doesn’t look good. Is there something wrong with...\"","Before he could finish, a subtle change came over Liu Lang’s eyes. \"You’re mistaken, Shopkeeper Chen. I am in perfect health.\"","At his words, Chen Yi said no more. With a brief apology for his presumption, he turned and walked toward the exit.","Wang Ji followed behind him and asked in a low voice, \"Sir, is he ill?\"","Chen Yi shook his head with a smile. \"I’ve only learned the barest basics from Divine Doctor Ma. I must have been mistaken.\"","With that, he patted Wang Ji on the shoulder, told him to keep an eye on things as usual, and headed out of the West Market.","’To be so heavily injured, yet not be the least bit anxious...’","’Could it be that Liu Lang didn’t come to Hundred Herbs Hall for healing?’","’Or does he already know his injuries are beyond what an ordinary Physician can treat?’","’How strange.’","As Chen Yi thought this, a slight smile appeared on his face. ’First, I’ll set out some bait and see if he bites.’","Once Chen Yi was a good distance away, Liu Lang pondered for a moment, his hand unconsciously pressing against his chest.","’Did that Xiao Family son-in-law really see my injuries, or was he just making a casual remark?’","After a moment of contemplation, he saw Wang Ji return from outside and hesitantly asked,","\"Shopkeeper, that man just now... does he know anything about Medical Skill?\"","Wang Ji froze for a second, looked him up and down, and countered, \"What do you think?\"","Without waiting for Liu Lang to reply, he walked straight upstairs.","’Others might not know whether Chen Yi knew Medical Skill, but how could he not?’","’He’d managed to coach those limping, \"renowned doctors\" like Ma Liangcai into looking the part. How could Chen Yi possibly be ignorant of Medical Skill?’","Liu Lang frowned slightly. Recalling the conversation he’d overheard, he made a decision.","’Ma Liangcai at Jishi Medicine Hall... I’ll have to go take a look when I have a moment. Maybe...’","...","「That entire afternoon.」","Chen Yi remained in Spring Lotus Garden.","Or to be more precise, in his study.","He would practice his Cursive Script and Wei Qing’s Style for a while, then his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill, before playing a few games of chess with Xiao Wuge.","After dinner, he told the others to go rest as usual.","Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge readily agreed. Only Pei Guanli seemed to have run out of patience, asking how much longer she had to keep \"wandering around.\"","Pestered until he had no other choice, Chen Yi could only hint that it would be another three to five days.","\"That’s good.\"","\"Ge the Third seemed suspicious today. He kept staring at me.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"What did you say?\"","Pei Guanli thought for a moment. \"I don’t remember.\"","\"Today, I went to South City Yanhua Lane with Sister Tingyun and the others...\"","Before she could continue, Chen Yi cut her off. \"If I were him, I’d stare at you too.\"","’What proper young lady goes for a stroll in Yanhua Lane?’","Pei Guanli looked bewildered. \"But why?\"","\"Because you’re pretty.\"","\"Hehe... Brother-in-law, you’re not the first person to say that, but I’m still very happy to hear it.\"","Chen Yi gave her a light flick on the forehead and said irritably, \"Enough chit-chat. Go back to your room, do your Cultivation, and go to sleep.\"","\"Oh.\"","Pei Guanli pouted and shuffled reluctantly out of the wooden building.","But a moment later, she poked her head back through the doorway, her round face once again wreathed in smiles.","\"Brother-in-law, am I really pretty?\"","\"As genuine as pure gold.\"","\"Hehe...\"","Pei Guanli seemed even happier now, and the TINKLE TINKLE of bells on her person faded into the distance as she skipped away.","Chen Yi shook his head with a smile, then returned to his room and, without delay, began preparing for the night’s activities.","Black martial arts attire, a face covering, and a vial of Immortal Drunk, among other things.","Over it all, he wore a black long-robe as a disguise.","Early in the evening, before Xiao Wuge, Xiaodie, and the others had fallen sound asleep, he quietly slipped out of Spring Lotus Garden.","Fortunately, his Cultivation had improved significantly, and his Martial Arts Step had reached the Great Success stage. So even without using the Meteor Butterfly Step, he could silently slip past Pei Guanli and cross through the Purple Bamboo Forest.","It was also a good thing it was Pei Guanli who was there.","If it had been Xie Tingyun or Shen Huatang, they likely would have discovered his movements long ago.","The journey was tense, but without incident.","Chen Yi bypassed the sentries and reached South Street. From there, he began to wind his way through the alleys, starting from in front of Liu Jing’s residence and heading toward the Hui Xian Building.","However, before he could reach the hiding spot he had picked out during the day, he heard several voices approaching from a distance.","\"Lord Hundred Households, my subordinates found someone over there who saw the Liu Family Guards.\"","\"He recalls that on that night, the Liu Family Guards were gathered near the Hui Xian Building, as if they were waiting for someone.\"","\"Where is he?\"","\"Oh, he lives not far behind the Hui Xian Building.\"","\"Take me to him!\""]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141 - 136: Making a Move","paragraphs":["Hearing their conversation, Chen Yi frowned slightly but continued to follow without missing a step.","As he walked, he took off his long robe and stuffed it into his clothes.","’There are only a few residences behind the Hui Xian Building. If someone was nearby that night, they definitely could have heard something, or seen those people... and me.’","If it were just an ordinary citizen, there would be nothing to fear.","The real fear was that this was someone with ulterior motives who had been bribed or was an imposter, all to draw the Imprisonment Department’s attention.","Chen Yi changed into combat attire and covered his face with a black cloth.","He silently concealed his figure in the shadows, following the Imprisonment Officers from a distance.","As he watched them move through the dim alley, a faint, fluorescent light flickered in his eyes.","One, two, three... six.","Among the six Imprisonment Officers.","The leader, a woman dressed in a crimson Official Robe, was a Seventh-Grade Martial Artist.","Another tall, thin Imprisonment Officer’s Cultivation had just barely reached the Eighth Grade Realm, while the Martial Arts Cultivation of the others was all in the Ninth Grade Realm.","After observing them, Chen Yi dismissed his Qi Observation Skill and thought to himself:","’The Martial Arts Cultivation of these Imprisonment Officers is secondary. What they rely on is the authority they possess to arrest and investigate cases.’","’But the key right now isn’t them. I need to see this so-called \"murderer\" who comes next.’","Before long, the Imprisonment Officers arrived in an alley beside the Hui Xian Building, where three people were already waiting.","By the light of the lanterns in their hands, Chen Yi could easily see that the three were not all Imprisonment Officers.","One of them was a simple-looking, middle-aged man wearing a short shirt made of coarse linen.","’He must be the one who provided the clue.’","After a quick look, Chen Yi scanned his surroundings, found a corner to hide himself in, and watched from a distance.","He heard the woman in red ask, \"Is that him?\"","A younger Imprisonment Officer beside her bowed and replied, \"Hundred Households Fang, that’s him. He lives around here. His name is Sun Erhu.\"","Sun Erhu smiled obsequiously, bowing his head. \"Greetings, my lady.\"","The woman in red looked at him calmly. \"I am Fang Hongxiu of the Shu State Imprisonment Department. I need you to answer a few questions.\"","\"Of course, of course. I’ll tell you everything I know.\"","\"Tell me in detail everything you saw or heard that night.\"","\"That night... it should have been before nightfall. I was coming back after buying some groceries from the West Market.\"","\"Passing by here, I saw a burly man leaning against the wall, staring at me.\"","Fang Hongxiu raised her hand to interrupt him and motioned for an Imprisonment Officer at her side to take out a portrait. \"Was it this person?\"","Sun Erhu glanced at it. \"Yes, yes, that’s him! With that brutish face, you can tell he’s no good.\"","\"And then?\"","\"After that, I didn’t dare to look any longer and hurried back to my home.\"","\"But the more I thought about it, the stranger it felt. After I got home, I kept an eye out, paying attention to the situation over here.\"","Sun Erhu gave a simple laugh. \"My lady, to tell you the truth, I’m a coward. I was afraid those people would sneak into my house after dark.\"","Fang Hongxiu frowned slightly. Before she could speak, the young Imprisonment Officer beside her snapped, \"Less nonsense!\"","\"Yes, yes...\"","Sun Erhu paused, then hurriedly continued, \"Later, not until it was completely dark, there was some commotion outside.\"","\"I only heard that man say something about the Xiao Family. I didn’t hear clearly; I could only confirm I heard the words ’Xiao Family’.\"","\"Continue. What else did you hear?\"","\"After that, an elderly-sounding voice said, ’Who are you people? What business do you have with this old man?’\"","\"Then the burly man said, ’My young master invites you...’\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi knew he didn’t need to listen any further.","It was obvious. Aside from the fact that Liu Jing’s men had indeed appeared near the Hui Xian Building, the rest of his story was a complete fabrication.","Still, using such a method to lead the Imprisonment Department’s investigation toward the Xiao Family was truly a crude tactic.","’But the Hidden Guards aren’t the only ones who would use such a method.’","’The Liu Family, or anyone who wants to stir up conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families, are all suspects.’","Chen Yi couldn’t help but broaden his list of suspects.","After all, considering the methods of the Hidden Guards, this clumsy approach was too straightforward.","Not only was it unrefined, but it also wouldn’t hold up to scrutiny.","Just as he was pondering this, the evening wore on, and the sky became completely dark.","A gust of wind blew from an unknown direction.","Then, Fang Hongxiu was heard shouting, \"Be careful!\"","Before her voice had faded, a throwing dart shot past the Imprisonment Officers, pierced straight through Sun Erhu’s brow, and embedded itself in the wall beside him.","Fang Hongxiu’s expression changed drastically. She looked out of the alley. \"Wang Han, you stay here and watch him! Everyone else, follow me!\"","\"...\"","Watching the Imprisonment Officers run off after the woman in red, Chen Yi couldn’t help but reveal a self-deprecating smile.","’My bad premonitions are always the ones that come true. Now this looks like the work of the Hidden Guards.’","’You have to hand it to them, the mastermind behind this is truly vicious.’","’Using a dead man as bait to both implicate the Xiao Family and eliminate the witness—truly killing two birds with one stone.’","This way, even if the Imprisonment Department didn’t believe it, they would have no choice but to pay the Xiao Family a visit.","’If the mastermind were just a bit more ruthless...’","At this thought, the look in Chen Yi’s eyes changed, and he immediately chased after Fang Hongxiu and her group.","The Imprisonment Officer left behind saw his figure and froze for a moment.","When he came to his senses, he drew the long blade from his waist and was about to shout.","But in that single instant, Chen Yi was already at his side, his hand chopping down like a blade onto the man’s neck.","THUD.","After the Imprisonment Officer collapsed unconscious, Chen Yi glanced at Sun Erhu beside him.","Confirming he was dead, Chen Yi transformed into a black shadow and headed toward the West Market.","Fortunately, because of the commotion caused by the Imprisonment Department earlier, most of the pedestrians on the West Market’s streets were distracted, and few noticed him.","But nothing is ever certain.","At that moment, in a private room in the Hui Xian Building, two figures stood by the window, looking toward the West Market.","Naturally, they spotted Chen Yi in the crowd.","One of them said in surprise, \"Miss, is that a member of the Xiao family?\"","The other figure stared at Chen Yi, their eyes flickering slightly. After a long moment, they nodded.","\"It should be.\"","But just as she finished speaking, another person in black appeared from a distance, moving far faster than the previous few.","After a moment’s pause.","\"Miss, then this one is...\"","\"One of them should be from the Xiao Family. The other is perhaps from the Liu Family.\"","As she spoke, the figure at the window turned and walked out of the private room.","\"Miss?\"","\"Let’s follow them and have a look.\"","\"Since I’ve already agreed to help Gray Wolf, I need to see this through to the end.\"","「Inside Hundred Herbs Hall.」","Liu Lang, who had already closed up for the night, naturally heard the sounds from outside as well.","The Imprisonment Officers, in particular, who were shouting as they gave chase, prompted him to get up and watch the show from his window.","When he saw two figures in black run past, closely followed by the Imprisonment Officers, he couldn’t help but grin.","\"Shu State City is quite chaotic tonight.\"","Of course, none of this had anything to do with him.","He was no longer the \"Sword Madman\" of the past, just an unknown, heavily injured Swordman.","...","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi had already chased them into the West Market. By now, most of the shops on the street were closed, and there were far fewer pedestrians.","In the cold silence, he heard footsteps behind him.","Without a second thought, he changed direction and headed off another way.","Finding a slightly higher eave, Chen Yi quickly suppressed the True Essence in his body and held his breath.","Soon, he saw a figure in black flash past with a swift Step Technique, heading straight for the Imprisonment Officers.","He frowned slightly. ’Who is this now?’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi couldn’t guess the newcomer’s identity, so he had no choice but to follow again.","This time, however, he was even more cautious.","Before long, Chen Yi heard the sounds of fighting in the distance, interspersed with rising and falling shouts.","\"The Imprisonment Department is apprehending a wanted criminal! All citizens, shut your doors and windows! Do not spectate!\"","\"Audacious villain, surrender now!\"","\"This old man advises you to let me go, lest you bring disaster upon yourselves!\"","\"In your dreams!\"","Chen Yi paused. Spotting the trail of the black-clad figure who had passed earlier, he carefully hid on the eaves of a shop on the other side and watched from a distance.","He saw that the man in black who had killed Sun Erhu with a dart was being surrounded and attacked by several members of the Imprisonment Department.","Clearly, the old-sounding man in black was not exceptionally strong; his skill was only about on par with Fang Hongxiu’s.","His defeat was only a matter of time.","’Fortunately, the voice isn’t familiar. He’s probably not from the Marquis’s Mansion.’","’Then again, that’s not absolute. He could be someone connected to the Marquis’s Mansion.’","Just then, the battle over there reached its conclusion.","The long blade in Fang Hongxiu’s hand flicked the black-clad man’s weapon away, and she kicked him straight to the ground.","\"I’d like to see just who is so bold as to kill someone right under the nose of my Imprisonment Department!\"","\"You...\"","Just as the old man was about to speak, the other figure in black, who had been hiding on the other side, charged forward.","A Long Spear had appeared in his hands at some point.","The moment he leaped out, the spear’s tip thrust forward, aimed directly at the man in black surrounded by Fang Hongxiu and her team.","\"How dare you!\"","Instantly alert, Fang Hongxiu swung her blade to block him.","CLANG!","The blade and spear clashed.","The long blade was nearly knocked from Fang Hongxiu’s grasp, and she stumbled back several steps.","Seeing this, the surrounding Imprisonment Officers immediately raised their blades and swarmed him.","For a moment, no one paid any attention to the old man on the ground.","Watching the chaotic scene, Chen Yi began to understand.","’The enemy of my enemy is my friend.’","’His goal must be to kill that old man to prevent disaster from befalling the Xiao Family.’","Having made this judgment, Chen Yi stopped watching the fight and fixed his gaze on the man on the ground.","When he got a clear look at the old man’s exposed eyes, he thought, ’Just as I expected.’","The old man was staring blankly at the fight nearby, showing no intention of getting up to flee.","’He was probably planning to be captured by the Imprisonment Department all along, so he could frame the Xiao Family.’","’In that case, I can’t let him live.’","At this thought, Chen Yi glanced at the fighting group and, without hesitation, shot out from his hiding place.","The man in black who was being surrounded was the first to spot him. He swung his Long Spear in a wide arc to push back Fang Hongxiu and the others, about to strike first.","But in the next moment, he saw the black shadow dance like a butterfly, heading straight for the old man who was lingering on the ground.","\"You...\"","Before the old man could even get up to resist, the black shadow’s fist smashed into his head.","BANG.","With a muffled explosion, the man’s head instantly burst apart.","Even in the dim night, bits of red and white could be seen splattering everywhere.","\"Huh?\"","Seeing this, a trace of confusion flashed in the spear-wielding man’s eyes.","\"The hell are you ’huh’-ing at? Run!\"","Chen Yi heard his exclamation, cursed in a raspy voice, and ran toward the north side of the West Market.","The man in black came to his senses, retracted his spear, and fled in the opposite direction.","\"Bastard!\"","Fang Hongxiu, seeing this, was instantly enraged.","Without thinking, she immediately gave chase in the direction Chen Yi had fled.","\"Let’s see if you can escape from my Imprisonment Department!\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi couldn’t help but sneer. ’These Imprisonment Officers really know how to pick on the weak.’","’Then again, it makes sense. I wasn’t as fast as the other man in black.’","Glancing left and right, he saw a small alley ahead and immediately ducked into it.","Behind him, Fang Hongxiu’s icy eyes were locked onto him as she followed him in.","But before she could get a clear look at the situation in the alley, her vision went dark.","A large hand was chopping down toward her neck.","It was as if she had run into it herself; she couldn’t react at all. She felt a sharp pain in her neck, and her consciousness instantly faded.","Looking at Fang Hongxiu’s resentful expression, Chen Yi sneered slightly.","Immediately after, using the same method, he knocked out the rest of the pursuing Imprisonment Officers one by one.","Once everything was quiet, Chen Yi dusted off his hands and let out a long sigh.","’You have to admit, tonight was incredibly eventful.’","’While I’m not sure if that old man was arranged by Xiao Dongchen, I am certain that the man with the big spear who came later is definitely from the Xiao Family.’","’From this, it seems the old master and the others aren’t completely unprepared.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself and looked down at his clothes.","After confirming he hadn’t been spattered with any blood, he walked out of the alley, preparing to return to the Xiao Family.","But just as he entered another deep alley,","He stopped. After scanning his surroundings, he suddenly spoke:","\"Is someone still following me?\"","\"Come on out.\""]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142 - 137: The Person Behind the Scenes","paragraphs":["Chen Yi’s words were not without basis.","It was because, even now that the dust had settled, the reward that should have appeared had not, which put him on guard.","He waited for another moment.","Seeing that no one had yet appeared, Chen Yi spoke again, his voice hoarse.","\"I just helped you take care of that man in black. You should be grateful. Why not come out for a chat?\"","\"I’d think the Xiao family wouldn’t repay kindness with enmity, would they?\"","As he spoke, he glanced back and forth.","The narrow alley remained empty and deathly silent.","He could only hear the sound of his own breathing.","’Not the Xiao family?’","Chen Yi thought, his heart sinking slightly.","’The Liu family?’","He continued to probe, \"It seems we have a guest from the Shu State’s Liu Family.\"","\"What?\"","\"You don’t really think the one who killed Liu Jing was from the Xiao Family, do you?\"","\"Don’t fall for someone’s plot to sow discord.\"","After a long moment, when there was still no sound from his surroundings, Chen Yi couldn’t help but grimace.","This was the outcome he had wanted to see the least.","The person behind the scenes!","\"Not the Liu Family, not the Xiao Family, yet you’re paying so much attention to me. You’re really putting me in a difficult spot.\"","\"Aren’t you?\"","\"Hidden Guard!\"","The moment the words left his mouth, the True Essence in Chen Yi’s body erupted. He fully unleashed the Meteor Butterfly Step, leaping onto a nearby wall in a single bound and disappearing as a black shadow in the direction of the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office.","Almost a split second after he moved, a cold, clear voice sounded by his ear:","\"Who are you? How did you know it was my Hidden Guard acting tonight?\"","A woman.","Chen Yi located the source of the voice and turned his head to see two women on a three-story wooden building not far away. They were clad in black cloaks with veiled faces, their figures and appearances obscured.","\"Heh, you’ve finally shown yourselves.\"","But this was even worse than them not appearing.","Under his Qi Observation Skill, the aura of one of the two women far surpassed his own. She was clearly a Martial Artist of the Middle Three Grades Realm.","To be precise, she should be Sixth Grade.","The other’s Cultivation wasn’t weak either; she was likely not far from the Middle Three Grades.","Seeing this, and after pinpointing their location, Chen Yi instantly changed direction and ran down the alley toward the main road.","As he ran, he shouted, \"Don’t bother chasing me! If I yell a few times here, your identities and your target will all be exposed!\"","Who would have thought that the Sixth Grade Realm Martial Artist, upon hearing this, would come straight after him?","\"You’re courting death!\"","Hearing the voice from behind, Chen Yi glanced over his shoulder.","\"You’re really not afraid?\"","\"If you have the guts, then say it!\"","\"The Xiao Family—\"","Upon hearing just those two words, the woman’s expression immediately changed, and she flung out three darts.","SWISH, SWISH, SWISH!","The faint whooshing sounds made Chen Yi quickly turn to evade, only to see three darts embedded in the wall beside him.","With a single glance, he recognized them as the same type of darts that had killed Sun Erhu.","\"So it was you who killed him before!\"","The woman didn’t respond at all, simply flinging out several more darts.","Three of them flew in a triangular formation straight for Chen Yi, while two others were aimed in front of him.","Seeing this, Chen Yi stopped short, ducked to avoid them, and was about to continue his escape.","But at that moment, the woman used some unknown Cultivation Technique, and her Body Technique speed suddenly tripled.","In the time it took Chen Yi to dodge the darts, the woman had closed the distance, drawn the Soft Sword from her waist, and thrust it straight at him.","The blade’s edge pulsed with a faint, dazzling light.","Chen Yi’s eyes scanned it from the corner, and he switched his footwork, using the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix Body Technique to evade the strike like a phantom.","Who could have known that the blade would suddenly bend? The edge of the sword, like a snake’s tongue, slashed across his waist in a bizarre arc.","In a flash of pain, Chen Yi’s eyes turned cold as he met her gaze directly.","His body tensed, and with a powerful stomp that shattered the bluestone slab beneath his feet, he advanced instead of retreating.","Then, he threw a punch.","As the True Essence in his body circulated and erupted, it also stirred the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi.","In an instant, the wild and domineering Mountain Shattering Fist Intent enveloped an area of ten feet.","—Mountain Shattering·Earth Split!","The woman was initially dismissive, but just as she raised her sword to thrust forward, she felt as if an immense weight was pressing down on her, causing her to stagger.","\"Great Success Fist Intent, like a mountain?!\"","The woman’s eyes filled with astonishment, but she quickly erupted with True Essence and raised her arm to block.","BOOM!","A mountain-like force slammed into her True Essence-protected arm, not only sending the woman flying backward but also causing Chen Yi’s own True Essence to be jolted, instantly damaging one of his meridians.","Chen Yi didn’t try to forcibly suppress the backlash. Instead, he took two steps back to dissipate the force, preventing himself from suffering a secondary injury.","\"Ugh.\"","Chen Yi looked at the woman who had steadied herself against a wall not far away. A trickle of blood seeped from the corner of his mouth, staining his black mask.","The woman watched him with suspicion and doubt. When the corner of her eye caught her left hand, which was swelling and turning red at a visible rate, a flash of anger appeared.","\"To have a mere Lower Three Grades Cultivation yet possess Great Success Fist Intent... your status in the Xiao Family must be quite high, right?\"","Chen Yi calmed the chaotic True Essence in his body slightly and said in a hoarse voice:","\"If I were one of the Xiao family, you and your colleagues hiding within the Xiao Family would have been dead long ago.\"","\"I’ll ask you one last time. Are you willing to let me leave?\"","\"Hmph!\"","\"Impossible!\"","The woman snorted coldly and leaped toward him, executing several sword flourishes that sent slashes of light at him.","Clearly, having learned her lesson from before, she no longer dared to fight Chen Yi in close combat.","Chen Yi was also aware of this. He dodged while using his True Essence to repair his damaged meridians.","At the same time, he didn’t forget to mock her, \"A grand Martial Arts Powerhouse of the Middle Three Grades, yet you haven’t even developed Sword Intent. You’re utterly useless.\"","\"If I were you, I wouldn’t have the face to live in this world.\"","\"You might as well go find a block of tofu to smash your head against.\"","The woman’s tone was icy. \"Once I’ve exhausted your True Essence, we’ll see if you can still be so sharp-tongued!\"","\"I can. Why couldn’t I?\"","\"If a grand Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer like you has the nerve to live like this, why can’t I live on in dishonor?\"","Hearing what Chen Yi said, the woman’s eyes grew even colder. She thrust out dozens of streams of Sword Qi as she asked:","\"How exactly did you find out our identities?\"","Chen Yi dodged each one. \"Not only do I know your identity, I also know that you were discussing important matters with someone at the Fengchun Building yesterday.\"","\"Xiao Dongchen, am I right?\"","\"As for you... your voice sounds a bit familiar. Let me guess...\"","However, before he could finish, the woman, clearly infuriated by his words, charged at him again.","Not only that, but she also called for the other woman in black to join her.","\"Attack together!\"","\"He knows too much! We absolutely cannot let him escape!\"","Instead of being angry, Chen Yi was pleased by this. His eyes ignored the Soft Sword right in front of him and focused intently on her shoulder and wrist.","When he saw the woman flick her wrist to create several sword flourishes,","Chen Yi’s footwork changed, and using the Meteor Butterfly Step, he charged straight toward her.","SHINK—","Risking having his left hand pierced by a ray of sword light, he threw a porcelain vial from his right hand, hitting the Soft Sword.","Without waiting to see the result, Chen Yi shifted his feet, using the Wandering Dragon and Phoenix to dodge the other sword lights, and abruptly retreated into the distance.","\"You...\"","The woman was about to give chase when her vision was suddenly filled with a pink, fluorescent light. She immediately knew something was wrong.","\"Huan’er—\"","She only had time to get out one word before her eyes rolled back and she collapsed to the ground.","With a CLANG, the Soft Sword flew several feet away.","\"Miss!\"","Hearing the shout, Chen Yi stopped a short distance away. A flicker of realization crossed his eyes. ’So it was them!’","Miss Cui, Cui Qingwu, and her Maid!","No wonder.","No wonder Xiao Dongchen was able to secretly exchange information with someone.","He and the Cui Family were in the same private room yesterday.","But how could Cui Qingwu, the young lady of the Qinghe Cui Family with its long-standing heritage, be a Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer?","Before he could think further, the other woman was already standing in front of Cui Qingwu, glaring at Chen Yi and berating him:","\"How dare you!\"","\"If anything happens to her, you and whoever is behind you will surely face retaliation!\"","Those words...","Chen Yi believed them.","Setting aside the power of the Hidden Guard, the Qinghe Cui Family alone was enough to turn Shu State upside down.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi clutched his injured left hand, trying to calm the True Essence that was surging again from the fight, and nodded with a smile.","\"Of course, of course. I wouldn’t dare provoke retaliation from a certain family of Qinghe.\"","\"You...\"","Before the Maid named Huan’er could say more, Chen Yi had already turned and dashed away.","\"When she wakes up, remember to tell her she owes me her life.\"","A flash of anger crossed the Maid’s eyes, but she didn’t dare give chase.","Only after Chen Yi had unhurriedly walked into the distance did she realize, stomping her foot fiercely.","’He’s seriously injured, yet he...’","’How dare he trick me like that? The audacity!’","But by now, the person was long gone, and no amount of anger from Huan’er would help.","Worried about Cui Qingwu’s safety, she had no choice but to carry Cui Qingwu on her back and run off in another direction.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi, clutching his bleeding left hand, slipped silently into the Hundred Herbs Hall.","’That was truly dangerous.’","’If Cui Qingwu’s Sword Dao had been just a little stronger, I would have died back there.’","As he thought, he fumbled in the dark, searching the cabinets for Silver Needles and various herbs.","After lighting an oil lamp and sterilizing a Silver Needle in the flame, Chen Yi pierced his left arm and his waist with it.","At the same time, he ground the herbs he found into a powder, mixed them, and applied the paste to his wounds.","The bleeding from the wound that pierced his arm coagulated. The gash on his waist was just a scratch, a superficial injury.","Seeing this, Chen Yi breathed a small sigh of relief.","Without pausing, he took out three more Silver Needles and inserted them one by one around the damaged meridians.","Then, he used a minuscule amount of True Essence to control the Silver Needles.","He turned them left and right, using them to clear and unclog the damaged meridians.","Just as Chen Yi was concentrating on healing himself, a voice came from nearby:","\"You’re not shy, are you? Barging in to take medicine and using needles to treat yourself. You think you own the place?\"","Chen Yi looked up to see Liu Lang leaning against the entryway outside the accountant’s office, watching him with a half-smile.","\"Just borrowing them. I’ll pay.\"","\"I’d think the great ’Sword Madman’ wouldn’t be so stingy, would he?\"","\"Er...\"","Liu Lang, who had been about to speak, was stunned by his words.","After it registered, the smile on his face slowly faded. Combined with the aged face from his disguise, his expression couldn’t help but turn serious.","\"Who are you?\"","\"I am hiding here. No one should know.\"","Chen Yi’s hands didn’t stop. He continued treating his wounds as he said casually, his voice still hoarse:","\"Brother Liu, don’t even think about making a move. Your injuries are even more severe than mine.\"","\"It’s not worth making your own situation worse over a nobody like me.\"","Liu Lang was stunned again. He looked Chen Yi up and down, his serious expression turning to one of inquiry.","\"Controlling Needle with Qi?\"","\"Forgive me for failing to recognize a great master. May I ask... Senior, which Medical Saint Hand of the Jianghu might you be?\""]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143 - 138: My Wife Is So Formidable, It Makes Me Seem...","paragraphs":["’Medical Saint Hand?’","Chen Yi chuckled to himself. The skill of Controlling Needle with Qi was indeed a rare Medical Skill.","It wasn’t that few Physicians knew of it, but rather that not many could actually perform it.","This was partly due to the high barrier to entry for learning it.","Not only did it require the user to have Mastery in the Acupuncture Skill, allowing them to accurately identify acupoints and diagnose the pulse, but it also demanded a certain level of Martial Arts Cultivation.","Only a Physician at the Eighth Grade Realm or higher, who possessed True Essence, could learn and use \"Controlling Needle with Qi.\"","It could not only clear the meridians but also use True Essence to repair damaged internal organs and the eight extraordinary meridians, turning the decaying into the miraculous.","That was why a Martial Arts Powerhouse like Liu Lang, whose meridians were damaged, would show such respect to a Physician with Mastery in \"Controlling Needle with Qi.\"","As he thought this, Chen Yi continued treating himself and said, \"I wouldn’t dare call myself a Saint Hand. It’s just a minor trick.\"","’A minor trick...’","Liu Lang opened his mouth but was momentarily speechless.","This man was exactly like the great masters of the Medical Dao spoken of in Jianghu legends.","His arrogance was astonishing.","’If \"Controlling Needle with Qi\" were so easy, why would I have to hide in Hundred Herbs Hall and try my luck?’","After a moment of silence, Liu Lang asked hesitantly,","\"Um, Senior, since you can see my injuries, I wonder if you could help treat me?\"","Although Liu Lang was puzzled as to how the man knew his identity, the most important thing right now was to treat his injuries.","Otherwise, just as the man in black had said earlier, most of his True Essence was being used to suppress his injuries, leaving him unable to fight at all.","Chen Yi glanced at him and chuckled. \"Treating you is simple. But can you afford my fee?\"","Hearing this, a bitter smile appeared on Liu Lang’s face.","\"Senior, since you know my identity, you should also be aware that I have always been alone since I started roaming the Jianghu.\"","\"Other than a Broken Blade and a Long Spear, I have nothing else. I don’t even have much silver or gold.\"","During his many years in the Northern Desert, he had indeed made some silver from jobs similar to robbing the Xiao Family of their medicinal herbs.","But he had always been a spendthrift, and most of that money was spent on wine and women.","Otherwise, he wouldn’t have skipped out on paying at the Spring Rain Building when he first arrived in Shu State.","Chen Yi looked him up and down, raising an eyebrow. \"Besides the Saber Dao, you also practice a Spear Technique?\"","Of course, that wasn’t his main point of interest. ’The important thing is, where is his spear?’","A smug look appeared on Liu Lang’s face. \"My Spear Technique is in no way weaker than my Saber Technique. It’s just that I’ve rarely met an opponent worthy of me using it.\"","While he boasted outwardly, he added inwardly:","’Xiao Jinghong doesn’t count as an opponent—she’s just too strong.’","’It’s not that I didn’t have the chance; even if I did, I’d still be killed in a single move.’","Chen Yi nodded slightly. \"Then where is your spear?\"","Liu Lang hesitated for a moment before rolling up his left sleeve, revealing the Long Spear bound to his forearm in the candlelight of the main hall.","\"I had this Long Spear custom-made. For convenience, the shaft is connected by refined iron links, allowing it to be assembled into a full spear when needed.\"","Chen Yi looked at the several sections of the spear’s shaft and blade wrapped around the man’s arm, a flicker of interest in his eyes.","\"How about we use it as part of your treatment fee?\"","Liu Lang was taken aback for a second, then immediately unfastened the Five-section Spear and placed it on the counter.","\"If you want it, Senior, please take it.\"","Seeing this, Chen Yi actually felt a little embarrassed.","A gentleman does not take what another holds dear.","A weapon carried at all times was something precious to any Martial Artist.","\"You don’t mind parting with it?\"","Unexpectedly, Liu Lang shook his head without hesitation. \"Actually, after being severely injured this time, I’ve decided to focus solely on my Saber Technique from now on.\"","\"Oh? And why is that?\"","\"You may not know this, Senior, but my master is the ’Sword Ghost.’ I should have progressed further on the Saber Dao.\"","\"If not for my own arrogance in wasting energy practicing the Spear Technique, which hindered my progress in the Saber Dao, my strength would likely be a level higher by now.\"","After hearing Liu Lang’s explanation, Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"Focusing on one path is a good thing.\"","\"In that case, I will accept this Long Spear.\"","Chen Yi paused, then smiled. \"But this isn’t enough. As I said just now, this Long Spear is only part of the fee.\"","Liu Lang had heard him clearly. He took a deep breath and said earnestly, \"Please speak freely, Senior. As long as you ask, I will find a way to do it.\"","Physicians who had mastered Controlling Needle with Qi were mostly elusive figures.","Ordinary people couldn’t even meet them, let alone know their whereabouts.","Furthermore, Liu Lang had also heard some rumors about Medical Saint Hands.","Like the \"Evil Doctor\" who demanded a limb for every life saved, or the \"Medical Demon\" who demanded Cultivation Technique manuals as payment.","Even with such strange demands, many heavily injured Jianghu People still sought them out.","For no other reason than that compared to one’s own life, limbs and Cultivation Techniques were trivial, external possessions.","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"In that case, you can do three things for me.\"","Seeing Liu Lang about to agree immediately, he raised a hand to add, \"You should think this through.\"","\"My tasks will be somewhat dangerous. Don’t blame me if you die and I didn’t warn you.\"","After the events of the past two days, he was well aware that his own strength was still somewhat lacking.","Take tonight for example. Whether it was the man in black with the Long Spear, or Cui Qingwu and her Maid, their Cultivation and Techniques were all a cut above his.","If he hadn’t been fully prepared, he would have had difficulty escaping.","Therefore, his proposal for Liu Lang to do three tasks was also for his own future benefit, saving him the trouble of putting himself in harm’s way.","Liu Lang smiled and nodded. \"Never mind three tasks. Even if it were thirty, I would do them all without fail.\"","\"Since I set foot in the Jianghu, I’ve long since put life and death aside. My only desire is to stay alive and meet the powerhouses of the Jianghu.\"","Chen Yi was quite satisfied to hear this.","\"Alright then. Three tasks is indeed a bit too few for you. Let’s make it thirty.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang’s smile froze. Then, he said, at a loss for whether to laugh or cry, \"Senior, I was just... I was just joking.\"","Chen Yi paid him no mind. \"A man of his word never goes back on it. Thirty it is.\"","After saying that, he didn’t forget to offer some comfort. \"Don’t worry.\"","\"If you get injured because of this, as long as you’re still breathing, I guarantee I can make you healthy again.\"","’If you die, then there’s nothing I can do.’","’I don’t possess any heaven-defying means to bring people back from the dead.’","Seeing the situation, Liu Lang could only cup his fists in a salute. \"In that case, I thank you for your help, Senior.\"","’Thirty it is, then.’","’Fortunately, I’ll be staying in the Shu State region for a while longer, so taking on a few extra jobs won’t be a problem.’","’Besides, if I can get on good terms with this Medical Saint Hand, it’s like gaining a protective talisman for the future.’","’It’s not a bad deal at all.’","During their idle chat,","the meridians inside Chen Yi’s body had already been fully repaired. Even the wounds on his arm and waist had healed considerably. A few days of quiet rest would see them fully recovered.","Liu Lang witnessed all of this, and his admiration for Chen Yi’s Medical Skill grew even deeper.","’A great master of the Medical Dao like him must have Medical Skills on par with the Evil Doctor and the Medical Demon.’","\"Senior, when would be convenient for you?\"","Chen Yi glanced at the sky outside. \"Tomorrow night.\"","Liu Lang’s heart leaped with joy. \"Then where should I go to find you?\"","\"Right here, of course. Have Wang Ji prepare a quiet room. I’ll be here around nine p.m.\"","’Wang Ji?’","Liu Lang was momentarily stunned. After a moment’s thought, he realized and said in astonishment, \"You... you’re the mysterious owner of Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then rose and picked up the folded Long Spear from the counter. He smiled and said,","\"So when I said I was coming home to Hundred Herbs Hall, I meant it.\"","Liu Lang’s face flushed with embarrassment. \"I see. I’m ashamed of myself.\"","\"You must have seen through my identity the moment I arrived at Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod. He weighed the Long Spear in his hand, then strapped it to his arm.","He had been looking for a suitable weapon, but he never expected to \"snatch\" one from someone else.","With that thought, he looked at Liu Lang and asked, \"Tell me about what you’ve been up to recently.\"","\"I heard you weren’t injured when you robbed the Xiao Family of their medicinal herbs. How did you end up in this state?\"","When Liu Lang heard this question, his heart stirred, and he couldn’t help but speculate about the man’s identity.","During his time at Hundred Herbs Hall, he had long been aware that the relationship between Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family was not a shallow one.","Never mind that the Shopkeeper of Hundred Herbs Hall, Wang Ji, had come from the Xiao Family himself.","The matter of that incredibly profitable tea beverage alone was enough to prove it.","Without the approval of this mysterious owner, Wang Ji would never have supplied the tea to the Xiao Family Medicine Hall on his own initiative.","’So...’","As this thought crossed Liu Lang’s mind, his expression grew more serious. \"I won’t hide it from you, Senior.\"","\"I robbed the Xiao Family of their medicinal herbs because I was hired to do so.\"","\"The Jing State Liu Family? I know about that. Tell me something I don’t know.\"","\"Er... since you already know about that, Senior, I won’t say more. After that incident, I left Shu State.\"","Chen Yi asked with great interest, \"To evade the Xiao Family’s pursuit?\"","Unexpectedly, Liu Lang shook his head. \"I left the Prefecture City to challenge General Jinghong.\"","Chen Yi was struck speechless, then laughed. \"So you were injured by her... hmm, by General Jinghong?\"","’Serves you right. She did a good job.’","Liu Lang smiled bitterly. \"General Jinghong’s Martial Arts Cultivation far surpasses my own. She defeated me with a single move.\"","He paused, then corrected himself with more precision. \"Or rather, she only used two fingers.","\"Not only did she catch my full-powered strike, but she also broke the long blade in my hand.\"","Chen Yi froze for a moment. He held two fingers of his right hand together and made a few gestures. \"Like this?\"","Liu Lang nodded, his tone tinged with melancholy. \"In fact, if General Jinghong hadn’t allowed it, I wouldn’t have even been able to launch that strike.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi couldn’t help but ask, \"Your strength shouldn’t be weak. Are you in the Middle Three Grades?\"","\"Upper Fifth Grade, with Great Success in the Saber Dao.\"","\"Then Xiao Jinghong is...?\"","Liu Lang pondered for a moment. \"She must have reached the Upper Three Grades Realm long ago. As for the specifics... I don’t know.\"","Even now, the memory of being unable to even raise his hand against Xiao Jinghong sent a shiver down his spine.","He had only ever felt that kind of helpless, insignificant feeling from his master, the \"Sword Ghost.\"","’I suppose that even among those in the Upper Three Grades Realm, Xiao Jinghong is no ordinary person.’","\"I see.\"","Chen Yi nodded thoughtfully, offering a perfunctory reply. \"Then your loss wasn’t unjust.\"","Connecting this to the Xiao Family’s current situation, he began to understand.","’It seems Xiao Jinghong has been hiding her true strength. Otherwise, Wang Lixing and the others wouldn’t have said she was at the Fourth Grade Realm.’","’As expected, the Xiao Family isn’t as simple as I first thought.’","’This is good news, in a way.’","’It’s just that...’","’With my wife being so powerful, it makes me look like a total weakling, doesn’t it?’","\"It’s getting late. I’ll be going now.\"","Liu Lang quickly understood and cupped his fists. \"Take care, Senior.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand and left without lingering, heading straight out of Hundred Herbs Hall and back to the Xiao Family estate.","Along the way, he saw many members of the Imprisonment Department and the City Guard Army rushing past with hurried expressions.","’It seems the events of tonight have alarmed quite a few people.’","The journey back was tense but uneventful. He finally returned to the Spring Lotus Garden just before midnight.","However, just as he walked out of the Purple Bamboo Forest, he saw Xiaodie run out from the wooden building, her face pale with panic.","\"N-No, this is bad! The Young Master is missing!\"","\"Young Master! Young Master, you... you haven’t run away again, have you?\"","\"...\""]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144 - 139: The Young Master Will Laugh Xiaodie to Death, Won’t He?","paragraphs":["Without a second thought, before Xiaodie could alert Xiao Wan’er, Xie Tingyun, and the others in Jiaxing Garden, Chen Yi quickly circled around to the back of the wooden building and headed straight for his room.","Just then, Xiaodie, who was by the door, didn’t run directly to Jiaxing Garden. Instead, she went to find Pei Guanli.","Presumably, she wanted to wake her up so they could search together.","While Chen Yi found it slightly amusing, a warmth also spread through his heart.","This must be what it feels like to have someone care for you and worry about you.","It was a warm, comforting feeling.","With that thought, Chen Yi pushed open the window, pretending to have just woken up. \"Xiaodie, what’s with all the noise?\"","Xiaodie, her hair a mess, stopped in her tracks when she heard his voice and looked back.","\"Young Master?\"","She looked left and right but couldn’t see Chen Yi, who was hidden in the shadows behind a lantern. The anxious look returned to her face, and her eyes began to well up with tears.","\"Young Master, where are you? Please don’t scare me like this.\"","Chen Yi sighed and tapped the windowsill. \"Here, I’m over here.\"","Hearing his voice, Xiaodie looked up. Only after she could make out Chen Yi’s blurry figure did she finally smile.","But as she smiled, her lips began to tremble, and the tears that had been welling in her eyes streamed down her face.","\"Young Master, where were you?\"","\"I thought... I thought you...\"","\"Thought I’d run away again, right?\"","Chen Yi finished her sentence for her, saying irritably, \"It’s pitch-black out. Where would I even go?\"","But seeing her wiping away her tears, he could only console her with a smile.","\"Don’t just stand there.\"","\"If anyone saw you like this—with your hair all messy, your clothes in disarray, and crying your eyes out—they’d think I did something to you.\"","With teary eyes, Xiaodie looked up, then glanced down at herself.","Though she was wearing a long-sleeved top, two of the buttons had come undone, revealing a small patch of skin.","One glance was all it took. Forgetting to cry, Xiaodie lowered her head, clutched at her chest, and ran back into the wooden building.","As she ran, she stammered, \"Young Master... I... I didn’t mean to.\"","Her voice, mixed with muffled sobs, was barely audible.","If not for the recent improvement in his Martial Arts Cultivation, Chen Yi likely wouldn’t have heard her at all.","\"It’s late. Go back to your room and get some sleep.\"","Chen Yi offered a few more words of advice, shook his head, and was about to turn away to clean the traces off his body.","Just then, he caught a movement out of the corner of his eye. Looking toward Jiaxing Garden, he saw Xie Tingyun from the Celestial Sect standing on the wall between Jiaxing Garden and Spring Lotus Garden, sizing up the situation over here.","He paused for a moment, then calmly closed the window.","’Sure enough, having a Martial Arts expert next door is a real pain.’","’The slightest disturbance, and she comes over to investigate.’","’Luckily, I got back in time tonight. Otherwise, my cover would have been blown.’","While Chen Yi was quietly changing his clothes in his room, Xie Tingyun muttered to herself and headed back to Jiaxing Garden.","Shen Huatang, who had also been awakened by the noise, glanced toward Spring Lotus Garden and asked,","\"Senior Sister, what happened over at the Young Master’s place?\"","\"Nothin’s wrong. Dunno what’s gotten into that master and servant. Playin’ hide-and-seek in the house in the middle of the night.\"","\"What’d you say?\"","Shen Huatang was so stunned that she lapsed into the Shu State dialect herself.","Xie Tingyun ignored her, yawning as she headed for their building. \"You’ve got the second half of the night. I’m going to bed.\"","...","Shen Huatang watched her go, her mind reeling with confusion.","’The Young Master and Xiaodie... playing hide-and-seek?’","’It’s pitch-black. How could they even find each other?’","It was a good thing Chen Yi didn’t hear the conversation between the two martial sisters; otherwise, he would have insisted they try it for themselves.","He took off his black clothes, used the water in a basin to clean his wound, and after drying himself, changed into a long robe.","He glanced at the blood-stained clothes and put them away with the Five-section Spear for the time being, planning to bury them in the bamboo forest the next morning.","’I’ll have to prepare a few more sets of Night Clothes.’","Chen Yi muttered to himself, then opened the light screen to check his latest gains.","The Opportunity had already arrived earlier, after he’d left Cui Qingwu and her companion. But his injuries had been severe, so he had gone straight to Hundred Herbs Hall without taking a closer look.","[Witnessed the Shu State Imprisonment Department searching for the \"murderer\" outside the Hui Xian Building in the West Market. Reward: Brocade Spring Saber Technique (Profound Tier), Opportunity +38.]","[Evaluation: Arrived on scene, witnessed events. Slaying the \"murderer\" disrupted the Hidden Guard’s plot, causing the Imprisonment Department to return empty-handed. Performance: Satisfactory.]","’Satisfactory?’","Chen Yi curled his lip. ’He was finally starting to understand the logic behind these evaluations.’","’It’s not enough to just be a spectator, an audience member, or an eavesdropper. The system wants me to participate in some way.’","’I could interfere, make a name for myself, or even push events forward, whether directly or indirectly.’","’The bottom line is, I can’t just stand by and do nothing.’","’Otherwise, not only would the rewards be smaller, but I’d also get a \"lazy\" or \"slothful\" evaluation.’","’Conversely, depending on my actions, I could earn extra Opportunity rewards.’","’Take this time, for example. Compared to the previous Profound-rank Middle Grade event—the marriage of Li Huai’gu and Yun Xiang—the amount of Opportunity Points awarded was completely different.’","As he thought about this, Chen Yi considered the *Brocade Spring Saber Technique* in his mind but decided to set it aside for now.","His Martial Arts already encompassed four aspects: Body, Step, Punch, and Spear. Learning a Saber Technique on top of that was possible, but it wouldn’t provide a major boost to his power.","It would be better to focus all his efforts on raising his Cultivation first.","If he had been in the Sixth Grade Realm tonight, Cui Qingwu would have been no match for him, even without using Immortal Drunk.","But the thought of Cui Qingwu sparked his curiosity again.","’I really can’t think of any reason why she would become a Hidden Guard.’","’Could it be that, like Xiao Dongchen, she also wants to take control of the Cui Family?’","’I wonder if Chen Yunfan knows about this. Then again... he’s probably still in the dark.’","Chen Yi shook his head, pushing the thoughts aside.","He then sat cross-legged on his bed, preparing to practice the Four Symbols Skill.","Just then, shortly after midnight—","[Daily Intel - Yellow-level Lower Grade: At the hour of Chou (1-3 AM), a Cultured Courtesan will fall into the water outside Spring Rain Building in Yanhua Lane.]","He gave it a passing glance.","Chen Yi immediately began circulating his True Essence, cultivating with the Four Symbols Skill.","A Yellow-level Lower Grade event wasn’t worth running out in the middle of the night to spectate.","Especially not one in South City’s Yanhua Lane.","Besides, Xiaodie was still downstairs, agonizing over her earlier state of undress.","He could faintly hear her tossing and turning under her covers.","\"What do I do? The Young Master is going to laugh his head off at me, isn’t he?\"","\"He will, he totally will...\"","...","「Xiao Family Estate, Central Courtyard. Qingjing Residence.」","Inside the tranquil residence, lanterns cast a lonely red glow, illuminating the main hall.","The Old Master of the Xiao Family sat impeccably dressed in a Grandmaster’s Chair.","Both hands rested on a yellow pearwood cane, and his slightly clouded eyes stared calmly at the moonlight outside.","Faintly visible in the shadows, a figure dressed in black leaned against a nearby pillar.","After a long silence,","the Old Master spoke. \"Tonight’s events were likely not the work of the Liu Family.\"","The figure in the shadows sounded surprised. \"Marquis, if not the Liu Family, then who could it be?\"","\"Another of the Noble Families and Clans in Shu State? Most of those with that kind of power are waiting to see how the Liu Family reacts.\"","\"Even the Tang Family... because of that incident three years ago, Tang Zixing now just keeps to his Inspectorate Office and stays out of any other conflicts.\"","\"Or the Xie Family?\"","\"But Xie Ying is in the same boat as our Xiao Family. Whether or not he can hold on to his position as Commander-in-Chief depends entirely on...\"","Before he could finish, the Old Master tapped his cane on the floor.","The voice cut off instantly.","The Old Master glanced at him. \"Regardless of who it is, their goal is to provoke a dispute between the Xiao and Liu Families.\"","The man in black hesitated. \"Then what about Liu Jing’s death? Was that part of it?\"","The Old Master paused. \"Whether it was or not is no longer important.\"","\"Liu Hong has already dispatched an Advisor from the Governor’s Office to the Three Towns to collect the summer grain tax. That is his way of declaring his position.\"","The Old Master coughed, then continued, \"His actions are understandable, all things considered.\"","\"As a member of a branch of the Liu Family, he has to show some consideration for the main family’s stance.\"","The man in black understood this. After a moment’s thought, he asked cautiously, \"Marquis, how do you intend to respond? Shall I...\"","The Old Master knew what he was implying and raised a hand to cut him off. \"It hasn’t come to that.\"","The man in black sullenly fell silent.","After a moment of thought,","the Old Master used his cane to push himself to his feet and gave an order. \"We must give the Liu Family a way to back down gracefully.\"","\"Find someone unimportant, someone with no connection to the Xiao Family, to take the fall for now.\"","The man in black seemed to let out a sigh of relief and nodded. \"Yes, sir.\"","\"Also, have your men keep an eye on the person from the Cui Family.\"","\"For Cui Qingwu to appear in Shu State at such a critical juncture... it can’t possibly be just for that boy from the Chen Family.\"","\"Cui Mao is now the ’Minister of Heaven,’ head of the Nine Ministers. He controls the Ministry of Personnel and has followers across the realm. He is not a man to be underestimated.\"","\"There are often hidden depths to his thoughts and intentions. We cannot afford a single misstep.\"","The man in black nodded. \"I’ll arrange for the Hidden Guard to watch her closely.\"","He was about to leave when he paused and asked, \"Marquis, what about the person who helped me tonight? Should I investigate them?\"","The Old Master turned and walked toward a side room, waving his hand wearily. \"Yes, an investigation would be good.\"","\"The Xiao Family is in a precarious position. For someone in Shu State to risk helping us... that’s not something to be taken lightly.\"","\"Once you find them, just take note of who it is. After this all blows over, the Xiao Family will be sure to reward them handsomely.\"","\"Yes, Marquis!\""]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145 - 140: Something’s Wrong, the Young Miss, She...","paragraphs":["「The next day, just as the sky began to lighten.」","Inside Tingyu Pavilion, about three miles from the Xiao Family’s estate.","A gentle breeze blew, causing the wind chimes hanging under the eaves to sway, creating a crisp, tinkling sound.","The courtyard was much quieter now than when it rained.","But Chen Yunfan, it seemed, was spared from the torment of these gentle sounds.","Ever since the members of the Cui Family arrived, they had taken up residence in Tingyu Pavilion’s rear courtyard.","He had no choice but to move to the middle courtyard with Chun Ying and the others.","Though Chen Yunfan was less than thrilled, he remembered his lessons in etiquette and decided to fulfill his duties as a host.","He didn’t want his mother, Cui Yu, to find out and think he was bullying Cui Qingwu.","But even so, he still couldn’t sleep in.","Just then, Chun Ying saw the pale light of dawn spreading in the east. She hesitated for a moment before entering the room and gently shaking the soundly sleeping Chen Yunfan.","\"Young Master, Young Master, wake up.\"","\"Huh?\"","Chen Yunfan groggily opened his eyes. When he saw it was Chun Ying, he rolled over to go back to sleep and muttered,","\"I ran all over the place collecting the summer harvest tax yesterday. My legs are about to break.\"","\"Be a dear and let me get some proper sleep.\"","\"Young Master, something’s happened.\"","Seeing Chun Ying’s serious tone, Chen Yunfan reluctantly sat up.","He scratched his messy hair, yawned, and asked, \"Alright, spit it out. What happened?\"","\"Ning Yu just reported that last night, he saw Miss Cui being carried back by her maid. It looked like she was injured.\"","Chen Yunfan stopped mid-yawn and stared at her blankly. \"Really?\"","Chun Ying nodded. \"It’s absolutely true.\"","To her surprise, Chen Yunfan burst out laughing. \"That’s great!\"","\"She laughed at my expense just the day before yesterday, and I was still fuming about it. This is the perfect chance for me to return the favor.\"","Chun Ying: \"...\"","Even though she’d been with Chen Yunfan for years, she still couldn’t quite grasp his temperament.","It was true for how he treated Young Master Yi, and it was true for how he treated Miss Cui, the woman he was engaged to.","While she was lost in thought, Chen Yunfan had already thrown on a long robe. He didn’t even bother to put his shoes on properly, instead just stepping into them like slippers as he walked out the door.","\"Don’t just stand there gawking. Hurry up and come with me to have a look.\"","\"If you make me late for the show, watch out. I’ll have you punished.\"","\"Yes, right away...\"","Chen Yunfan excitedly led Chun Ying straight to the rear courtyard.","As he walked, he rubbed the corners of his eyes, muttering about how sleepy he was.","Chun Ying sighed and said in a low voice, \"Young Master, your Martial Arts...\"","Chen Yunfan stopped in his tracks and huffed. \"I’ve been faking it for so long, I almost forgot I even have a cultivation.\"","As he spoke, he circulated his True Essence once through his body and was instantly refreshed and invigorated.","His spirits soared.","Then he quickened his pace, heading straight for the rear courtyard.","However, just as they reached the veranda, before they could even go in, they were stopped by the maids guarding the entrance.","\"Young Master Yunfan, our Miss has not yet finished her morning preparations. It is inconvenient for you to enter.\"","Chen Yunfan looked left and right and couldn’t help but chuckle.","He pointed at the ground beneath his feet. \"Look closely. This is Tingyu Pavilion. This is *my* house.\"","The two maids glanced at each other, then sidestepped again to block his path, bowing as they spoke:","\"Our apologies, Young Master. Our Miss is not available to receive guests at the moment.\"","The corner of Chen Yunfan’s mouth twitched. He cut to the chase. \"I heard your miss was injured. I came to have a look.\"","\"Injured?\"","\"Young Master Yunfan, who did you hear that from? My miss just woke up. She isn’t injured at all.\"","\"She’s not?\"","Chen Yunfan looked suspiciously at Chun Ying. When he saw her shake her head slightly, he understood.","’So Cui Qingwu is worried I’ll laugh at her and has decided to pretend she’s fine, huh?’","\"In that case, go and announce me. Just say that I... hmm... am inviting her to have breakfast with me.\"","Hearing this, the two maids hesitated for a moment before one of them agreed and trotted off toward the room.","Not long after, she returned, bowed, and said, \"Young Master Yunfan, our Miss invites you in.\"","Chen Yunfan raised an eyebrow. ’So Cui Qingwu isn’t injured?’","But on second thought, Chun Ying had been with him for years and had never lied to him. She wouldn’t start now.","Thinking this, Chen Yunfan clasped his hands behind his back. \"Lead the way.\"","Chun Ying, however, did not follow them in. Watching the group walk away, she couldn’t help but feel puzzled.","After a moment’s thought, she summoned Ning Yu.","\"Last night, was Miss Cui really carried back?\"","\"Absolutely.\"","Ning Yu paused, then added, \"I also saw bloodstains on her.\"","Chun Ying didn’t doubt him and muttered, \"Then why would she let the Young Master in now? Isn’t she afraid of being exposed?\"","While the two of them were puzzled, Chen Yunfan had already entered the room—which was originally his—and immediately spotted Cui Qingwu sitting at her dressing table.","Chen Yunfan paused, looking her up and down.","At the moment, Cui Qingwu’s long, glossy black hair was slightly disheveled, and her face looked a bit wan and pale, as if from a poor night’s sleep.","But she certainly didn’t look injured.","Glancing around, Chen Yunfan noticed an empty bowl on the table. His nose twitched slightly, and a smile crept onto his lips.","Just then, Huan’er finished combing Cui Qingwu’s long hair and securing it with a phoenix hairpin. Cui Qingwu stood up, looked at him, and asked with a smile,","\"Yunfan, you’re up so early today?\"","Chen Yunfan smiled and nodded. \"I heard you were injured, so I came to see for myself.\"","\"Feeling better?\"","Cui Qingwu’s smile froze. Her eyes flickered to the empty bowl on the table, and she understood.","Before she could speak, Huan’er, who was beside her, quickly went over to clear the bowl away and hurried out of the room.","Chen Yunfan watched her go, then casually sat down at the table. \"So, tell me, who injured you?\"","Seeing that she hadn’t managed to fool him, Cui Qingwu couldn’t help but feel a flicker of annoyance.","It was directed at the person who had injured her last night, but also at Huan’er.","A moment of silence.","Cui Qingwu let out a breath and met his mocking gaze. \"It was probably the same person who knocked you unconscious before.\""]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146 - 140: Oh No, the Young Miss, She...","paragraphs":["Hearing this, Chen Yunfan’s smile vanished.","\"You got hit too?\"","Cui Qingwu nodded. \"Elder Chang came by this morning. He confirmed my condition was the same as yours from the day before yesterday and brewed a medicinal soup using that same prescription.\"","Chen Yunfan turned away, speechless.","Any inclination he had to tease her evaporated at the thought of that bastard from the other night.","\"So, do you know who he is?\"","\"I don’t.\"","Cui Qingwu paused, then continued, \"But he should have some connection to the Xiao Family.\"","Chen Yunfan looked at her again. \"The Xiao Family?\"","Cui Qingwu adjusted her sleeve to cover her injured arm as she spoke.","\"I believe so.\"","She then gave him a carefully selected account of what had happened the previous night.","Naturally, she omitted her and Huan’er’s true identities and purpose.","After listening, Chen Yunfan stroked his chin thoughtfully. \"Someone wanted to frame the Xiao Family for Liu Jing’s death, and he killed them?\"","After a moment’s thought, he clapped his hands together. \"That’s it. He’s definitely connected to the Xiao Family.\"","\"Good, very good. That bastard drugged me, then he drugged you. He clearly doesn’t take us seriously at all.\"","Seeing this, a strange light flickered in Cui Qingwu’s eyes. She asked, \"Where exactly were you drugged by him, Yunfan?\"","\"The West Market... hmm?\"","Their eyes met. \"We have to find him!\"","\"I’d like to see what kind of nerve he has to offend both the Chen and Cui Families!\"","After speaking, Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu shared a knowing smile.","\"It’s been so many years, Qingwu. You seem to have changed a bit.\"","\"In what way?\"","\"I can’t quite put my finger on it. But you’re not as stiff and old-fashioned as when we were kids.\"","’Stiff and old-fashioned...’","The smile on Cui Qingwu’s face vanished. A little vexed, she turned away from him.","\"If that’s the case, Yunfan, why don’t you go find a girl who isn’t ’stiff and old-fashioned’ to have breakfast with.\"","\"Er...\"","Chen Yunfan stared at her, dumbfounded. ’There shouldn’t have been anything wrong with what I just said,’ he thought.","’That was a compliment, wasn’t it?’","...","Chen Yi was also up bright and early.","A night spent in Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill left him feeling invigorated.","Even though the wounds on his arm and waist hadn’t fully healed, it didn’t hinder the progress of his Cultivation.","’Five days to advance from the Lower Stage of the Seventh Grade to the Middle Stage... the progress isn’t slow.’","Of course, he was only comparing himself to himself.","If an outsider found out someone had broken through a minor Realm within the Seventh Grade in just five days, they would probably try to hack him to death.","’I’ll aim to break through to the Middle Three Grades by the end of the month.’","With that thought, Chen Yi washed up and got dressed.","He then quietly buried the torn, bloodstained black clothes in the Purple Bamboo Forest before casually strolling back.","After Xiaodie helped Xiao Wuge and Pei Guanli get ready, the group ate breakfast together.","Though he had sustained some injuries last night, it didn’t affect Chen Yi’s appetite in the slightest.","As usual, he had four large steamed buns, two bowls of hot congee, and two portions of glutinous rice cakes, which left him about fifty percent full.","Xiao Wuge’s appetite was also quite good, but he seemed to have developed some sort of trauma, refusing to even glance in Pei Guanli’s direction.","Apparently, the Tiger Girl had already covered her congee with a thick layer of chili peppers.","In contrast to them, Xiaodie, who was usually a foodie, kept her head down the entire time, stirring her bowl of congee into a mush with her chopsticks.","Chen Yi saw this and chuckled inwardly.","’The little maid is still agonizing over what happened last night.’","After a moment, he looked out the window and said, \"Xiaodie.\"","Xiaodie jumped. \"Here!\"","Chen Yi said leisurely, \"I was just thinking about what we should have for lunch.\"","\"How about hot pot?\"","Xiaodie immediately looked up at him, her eyes already picturing a divided pot of spicy and numbing broth.","But before she could speak, Chen Yi shook his head. \"No, no. It’s too hot today. It’s not a good day for something so spicy.\"","\"Braised fish head? No, that doesn’t seem right either. A bit too bland.\"","\"Or maybe beef and potato stew?\"","\"I heard yesterday that a tenant farmer on the fief accidentally worked an ox to death. How about we eat that?\"","After hearing him list the dishes, Xiaodie’s attention was completely captured. She forgot all about last night’s embarrassing incident and nodded repeatedly.","\"Young Master, that sounds great! Beef! We don’t get to eat beef very often.\"","When she met Chen Yi’s smiling gaze, her face flushed slightly, and she immediately lowered her head again.","\"Y-Young Master, are you making fun of me?\"","\"Why would I make fun of you? It’s settled. Go tell the kitchen staff later that we’ll be having beef for lunch.\"","\"Okay...\"","Upon hearing this, Pei Guanli was about to raise her hand in agreement when she suddenly remembered she had to go out today, and her head drooped.","\"Brother-in-law, I don’t want to go out anymore.\"","Chen Yi shook his head very seriously. \"No, you do.\"","\"...\"","At his words, Pei Guanli could only muster a tragic expression and nod firmly. \"I already promised Sister Tingyun and the others that we’d go to North City today.\"","\"The Mid-Autumn Festival is in a little over half a month. We’re going to buy some things for the holiday.\"","\"Sister Huatang and the others need to send things back to the Celestial Sect, and I need to send some things home too.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"You’re not going back to the Mountain Race for the Mid-Autumn Festival?\"","Pei Guanli said nonchalantly, \"It’s just Ah Ma at home. My brother went into the mountains to pay respects to Granny Shan. It would be lonely and boring if I went back.\"","Since she put it that way, Chen Yi didn’t try to persuade her further.","\"There’s still some time. If you change your mind, you can still make it back.\"","\"I know, Brother-in-law. Sometimes I feel like you’re just like my older brother.\"","\"What?\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s stern face, Pei Guanli stuck out her tongue and quickly scurried out of the room.","Not until she was near Jiaxing Garden did she shout from a distance, \"Just like a little old man!\"","After shouting, before Chen Yi could say anything, Pei Guanli was already laughing.","She skipped and hopped away.","Listening to the fading sound of her bell, Chen Yi couldn’t help but shake his head and smile.","’Having this Tiger Girl around Spring Lotus Garden is quite lively.’","After breakfast.","Chen Yi couldn’t think of anything else to do for the moment, so he took Xiao Wuge to go fishing in the pavilion.","He hadn’t fished in a while and his hands were itching to try.","Even knowing he would likely catch nothing, he eagerly baited his hook and cast his line.","Xiao Wuge sat next to him on the pavilion railing and copied him, casting out his own line.","The once-calm pond instantly became lively.","To be precise, it was still quiet on Chen Yi’s side; the liveliness was all on Xiao Wuge’s.","He didn’t even have bait on his hook, yet the Golden Carp swarmed around it as if they were mad.","This delighted Xiao Wuge, who couldn’t stop grinning.","Chen Yi was used to this. He silently turned halfway, not even giving Xiao Wuge a sideways glance.","People’s joys and sorrows are not interconnected.","It was just like this moment: one person gets skunked, while another has a bountiful harvest.","Xiaodie brewed tea nearby as usual, watching the backs of the man and the boy while looking forward to the beef and potato stew for lunch.","But as she thought about it, her mind drifted back to last night’s events.","Her little face immediately felt like it was on fire, and her heart began to pound.","It was, for the most part, the shyness of a traditional and conservative girl in the presence of an outstanding man.","After a long moment, she finally calmed down and handed the teacups to Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge.","\"Have some tea.\"","Chen Yi took a slurp, his eyes still fixed on the ripple-less surface of the pond, and muttered:","\"Today, these fish... erm... this tea, is utterly tasteless.\"","Just as the three of them were comfortably enjoying the summer sun, a flurry of hurried footsteps sounded from behind them.","Xiaodie turned around and exclaimed, \"Sister Cui’er, what’s wrong? Why are you in such a hurry?\"","Cui’er arrived outside the pavilion. Looking at Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge, who had turned at the sound, she said breathlessly:","\"Y-Young Master, it’s terrible.\"","\"The Young Mistress, she... she’s sick.\"","Chen Yi frowned slightly, put down his fishing rod, picked up a nearby towel to wipe his hands clean, and asked:","\"Did she catch a cold? Does she have a fever?\"","\"I think... I think so. Her forehead is very hot, and she’s coughing.\"","\"Alright, I’ll go have a look.\"","Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie wanted to go too, but Chen Yi stopped them.","\"Be careful not to catch it. You two stay here.\"","With that, Chen Yi followed Cui’er to Jiaxing Garden.","He had just reminded Xiao Wan’er yesterday to stay warm, and today she had a cold.","’It’s always the bad predictions that come true...’"]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147 - 141: That... That’s Too Embarrassing","paragraphs":["’What a jinx.’","Chen Yi thought, pausing his steps to let Cui’er go on ahead.","\"I’m going to grab something. You and Juan’er go boil some water and have it ready.\"","\"Yes, Young Master.\"","After giving the order, Chen Yi turned back to his room in the wooden building, retrieved his acupuncture kit, and tucked it into his robes.","Xiao Wuge saw him come out and couldn’t help but ask, \"Brother-in-law, should we notify that Divine Doctor Ma?\"","Chen Yi replied that it wasn’t necessary for now, then headed toward Jiaxing Garden.","For an ordinary person, a minor cold would be no big deal.","But Xiao Wan’er’s constitution was special.","With her profoundly cold body, which was already riddled with drafts, a single cold was considered a severe illness.","Fortunately, he had previously prescribed a Yang Storage Formula for Xiao Wan’er through Ma Liangcai; otherwise, her condition would be even worse.","「A short while later.」","Chen Yi arrived at Jiaxing Garden and saw Cui’er and Juan’er in a frantic flurry.","One was boiling water while the other was using a towel to wipe the sweat from Xiao Wan’er.","Meanwhile, Xiao Wan’er was lying listlessly on the bed, sweat beading uncontrollably on her forehead and two unnatural crimson flushes on her cheeks.","Not only that, but her eyelids twitched from time to time, and her lips parted and closed, a clear sign that she was losing consciousness.","When Cui’er saw him appear at the door, she was on the verge of tears.","\"Young Master, I... should I go notify the Old Master?\"","\"Miss... she was still awake just now. She said she wanted to rest, but by the time I went to get you, she... she...\"","Chen Yi waved his hand and offered a reassuring lie. \"There’s no need for now.\"","\"The formula Divine Doctor Ma prescribed for Big Sister before was quite effective. It shouldn’t be anything serious. Let me take a look first.\"","As he spoke, he walked straight into the room, a faint glow flickering in his eyes.","He used his Qi Observation Skill.","He saw that the yang energy Xiao Wan’er had accumulated from several days of medicine was already gone, and her entire aura was as black and glossy as ink.","Seeing this, Chen Yi didn’t hesitate. He stepped forward, disregarding the propriety between men and women, and placed his hand on her wrist.","\"This...\"","Cui’er and Juan’er, who had been anxious just a moment ago, were both stunned by the sight.","After exchanging a look, they both tacitly fell silent.","’A doctor’s heart is like a parent’s... A doctor’s heart is like a parent’s... The Young Master, he...’","’We should just wait for Miss to wake up and decide.’","A moment later, after confirming Xiao Wan’er’s condition, Chen Yi’s slightly furrowed brow relaxed.","\"It’s nothing serious, just a common cold.\"","Hearing this, Cui’er and Juan’er both breathed a sigh of relief. \"That’s good.\"","\"That puts our minds at ease.\"","’At ease?’","’At ease my ass.’","What Chen Yi had just said was merely an excuse to calm them down.","In truth, Xiao Wan’er was already showing symptoms of \"qi collapse.\"","If not for his sufficient skill in the Medical Dao and the fact that he happened to be in the residence, Xiao Wan’er would have passed on within two hours.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi gave his orders, \"Cui’er, go get a brush and paper, write down a prescription, and then go to the Medicine Hall to fetch the herbs.\"","\"Okay.\"","Once Cui’er had written it down and confirmed it was correct, she hurried out of Jiaxing Garden.","Chen Yi then instructed Juan’er to open the windows for ventilation and move the stove outside to boil water.","「After sending them both away.」","Chen Yi looked at Xiao Wan’er on the bed, hesitated for a moment, and then whispered a few words.","They were mostly phrases like \"desperate times call for desperate measures\" and \"forgive my offense.\"","In any case, there was no response.","Seeing this, Chen Yi lifted the pink blanket, revealing Xiao Wan’er’s body, clad only in a thin undergarment.","She was already drenched in sweat, so much so that even the simple silk undergarment was soaked through, clinging tightly to her delicate and shapely figure.","\"Ahem.\"","Chen Yi rubbed his nose and muttered, \"...so fragrant.\"","Just then, feeling the chill on her body, Xiao Wan’er seemed to sense something and groggily opened her eyes to look at him.","Their eyes met.","Taken aback, Chen Yi raised a hand and waved it in front of her eyes. \"Big Sister, can you see me?\"","A hazy veil seemed to cover Xiao Wan’er’s clear, bright eyes, which moved slightly to follow his hand.","After a good while, she parted her crimson lips. \"Brother... Brother-in-law?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"What... what’s happening to me?\"","\"You caught a chill.\"","\"Oh... I’m a little cold...\"","\"It’ll be over soon. Get some sleep.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in agreement and obediently closed her eyes, though she continued to mumble something incoherently.","Her voice was intermittent and barely audible.","\"Brother... Brother-in-law, can you tell me... that poem... was it written about... me?\"","\"I... I hope it wasn’t, but I also hope...\"","\"I hope...\"","Xiao Wan’er never finished saying what she hoped for before she fell unconscious again.","Chen Yi looked at her haggard yet lovely and pitiable face, remained silent for a moment, and then sighed.","\"That poem... it was indeed written for you.\"","With that, Chen Yi steadied his mind, took the Silver Needles from his robes, and began performing acupuncture on her.","Thirteen needles in a row, each one sealing a point where her qi was dissipating.","Immediately after, he used his True Essence to meticulously regulate the acupoints and meridians in Xiao Wan’er’s body.","He only stopped when his Qi Observation Skill showed that some of the cold qi in Xiao Wan’er’s body had dissipated, yang energy was beginning to form, and her aura had gradually stabilized.","Chen Yi put away his Silver Needles and wiped the sweat from his forehead.","Just as he was about to cover Xiao Wan’er with the blanket, he heard Juan’er’s trembling voice from behind him:","\"Y-Young Master, you... you, you, you...\"","Chen Yi glanced back, calmly rising to his feet. \"I just took Big Sister’s pulse again.\"","\"Only then did I understand why her condition wasn’t improving.\"","He paused briefly, his tone turning serious. \"Look at her. Her clothes are soaked through. How is she supposed to get better like this?\"","Hearing this, Juan’er looked at him suspiciously, then at Xiao Wan’er, whose breathing was now steady and whose complexion had improved greatly. She quickly bowed.","\"Forgive me, Young Master. Juan’er didn’t realize... Juan’er...\""]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148 - 141: Th-That’s Too Embarrassing","paragraphs":["Chen Yi hmphed, walking past her to give an order. \"Stop with the nonsense. Hurry up and change the Eldest Miss into some dry clothes.\"","\"Yes, yes. I’ll change the Eldest Miss right away.\"","When he heard the door close behind him, the stone-faced Chen Yi couldn’t help but let out a long sigh of relief.","’Thank goodness... Thank goodness I’m a quick thinker.’","’Otherwise, if things had gone wrong, I’d probably be accused of defiling my sister-in-law.’","’If I’d actually done it, I would have accepted the accusation.’","’But the thing is, I didn’t do a single thing!’","With that thought, Chen Yi glanced back before sitting down in a nearby pavilion to wait for Cui’er to return with the medicine.","All that mattered was that Xiao Wan’er was safe.","As for the future...","Who can say what the future holds?","...","After noon, the scorching summer sun beat down, and the sound of cicadas in Jiaxing Garden was endless.","That was the one downside to a courtyard shaded by lush trees.","They chirped day and night. If you didn’t close the windows, the noise was sometimes loud enough to wake a person from a deep sleep.","And it was this chirping of cicadas that woke Xiao Wan’er.","She groggily opened her eyes, her mind dimly aware that she was in her room.","She turned over, propping herself up with her left hand, then switching to her right to support her weight on the bed as she surveyed her surroundings.","Her slightly dehydrated body made her lick her lips subconsciously. \"What... what’s wrong with me?\"","It had been a long time since Xiao Wan’er had been sick.","Or rather, aside from the chronic chill that afflicted her body, she had almost never suffered any other illness.","So much so that she had to think for a good while before she remembered that she’d caught a cold.","’Am I better already?’","Xiao Wan’er touched her face, feeling a faint warmth. She then looked down at herself, and upon confirming that she was all right, couldn’t help but sigh in relief.","She remembered that when she was a child, the old woman at the Wumeng Mountain Dojo had told her she must never get sick.","Given her constitution, even a minor illness could be fatal.","’Thank goodness...’","Xiao Wan’er patted her chest in lingering fear, a small gesture to reassure herself.","She had known about her body’s condition for a long time and had grown accustomed to it.","As a result, she had a detached view of life and death, hoping only to live each day to the fullest.","She wanted to do what she could without being a burden to others.","Fortunately, she had done a good job of that so far.","At this thought, a small smile graced Xiao Wan’er’s lips. \"Thank goodness.\"","Then, she got out of bed to get dressed.","She didn’t call for Cui’er or Juan’er, instead dressing herself in a long skirt, fleece-lined trousers, and a short jacket.","After a moment’s thought, Xiao Wan’er opened her wardrobe. She looked at the several clean, neatly folded cloaks inside, then took one out and draped it over her shoulders.","Once fully dressed, she looked at herself in the Copper Mirror. ’This looks much more like me.’","Framed by the fur-trimmed collar of her cloak, her pale face, with its faint rosy tint, still looked undeniably delicate.","But while she had a delicate air about her, her features were truly beautiful, with eyes as captivating as autumn ripples.","Xiao Wan’er looked at her reflection in the Copper Mirror, but she wasn’t admiring her own beauty. Instead, she was recalling what Chen Yi had said the day before yesterday—to be careful not to catch a cold.","The corners of her mouth lifted into a smile. \"Jinx.\"","Her tone was not quite a complaint, nor was it one of pure delight.","All in all, she was in a rather good mood.","Just as Xiao Wan’er was about to leave her room to take a look outside, she heard a surprised cry from the corridor.","\"Really?\"","\"The Young Master really lifted the Eldest Miss’s blanket?\"","’The Young Master? Blanket?’","Xiao Wan’er blinked and couldn’t help but move closer to the door, just in time to hear Juan’er explain:","\"Don’t get the wrong idea.\"","\"At first, I also thought the Young Master was doing something improper to the Eldest Miss.\"","\"But when I was changing the Eldest Miss’s clothes, I realized the Young Master was right.\"","\"You and I covered the Eldest Miss with such a thick quilt that she ended up soaked in sweat, which was keeping her from getting better.\"","\"If the Young Master hadn’t lifted the blanket, the Miss wouldn’t have recovered.\"","\"Oh, I see. Then I misunderstood the Young Master.\"","\"Still, it wouldn’t be good if word of this got out. Let’s just keep it between us.\"","\"Don’t worry, my lips are sealed...\"","After hearing this, Xiao Wan’er felt her chest tighten. Her hands instinctively flew to her chest, as if to keep her wildly pounding heart from leaping out.","Her face flushed pink, and it wasn’t just from embarrassment.","There was also a hint of vexation, and perhaps something else entirely.","Amidst a whirlwind of emotions, a single phrase echoed in her mind: ’My brother-in-law... he lifted my blanket, he lifted my blanket...’","’Doesn’t that mean... I was just in my chemise, and he... he... saw...’","’He saw everything?’","Having been in charge of the Medicine Hall for so long, Xiao Wan’er knew a little about Medical Skill herself.","She had never heard of treating a cold by uncovering someone to dissipate heat. It was always about bundling up tightly to sweat out the fever for a faster recovery.","’My brother-in-law, he... he wouldn’t do something like that.’","Just as she was grappling with her shame and vexation, fragments of memory surfaced in her mind.","It was like a hazy dream where she was lying on the bed and Chen Yi was sitting beside her.","They were talking about something, off and on.","’What did they say?’","’It seemed to be about that poem.’","Vaguely, she seemed to hear her brother-in-law’s gentle voice say, \"It was indeed written for you.\"","\"...\"","Xiao Wan’er’s mind instantly went blank. The vexation on her face vanished.","Or rather, the vexation was gone, leaving only a deep blush in its place.","’That... that was a dream, right?’","’It had to be a dream, right?’","’Otherwise... otherwise, it would be too mortifying.’","Just then, Cui’er and Juan’er pushed the door open. Seeing her state, they were startled, thinking she hadn’t recovered yet.","\"Miss, are... are you all right?\"","\"Should we summon Doctor Ma?\"","Hearing their voices, Xiao Wan’er forced herself back to her senses. She lightly bit her lip and shook her head. \"I... I’m fine.\"","\"There’s no need to find a Physician. Just... just get me a cup of water.\"","Cui’er quickly went out to the main hall to pour some water.","Juan’er helped her back to the bed to sit down. \"Miss, you scared me to death. You must rest well and not catch a cold again.\"","Xiao Wan’er composed herself, looked at the maid, and said quietly, \"Indeed. I must rest and not catch another cold.\"","Juan’er said happily, \"It’s a good thing the Young Master knows some Medical Skill. Otherwise, Cui’er and I wouldn’t have known what to do.\"","’He knows Medical Skill?’","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment before asking, \"Tell me what happened after I fell unconscious.\"","Not suspecting a thing, Juan’er quickly recounted the earlier events.","Just as she and Cui’er had agreed, she didn’t mention Chen Yi lifting the blanket.","After listening, Xiao Wan’er took a sip of water. \"Is that all?\"","Juan’er and Cui’er glanced at each other and nodded guiltily.","\"Yes, yes. After that, you got better, Miss. And now you’re awake.\"","Xiao Wan’er gave them a complicated look but didn’t press further.","\"My brother-in-law... where is he?\"","\"He went back. We heard someone from Guiyun Academy came to discuss his teaching post that starts tomorrow.\"","\"Oh. Well, then... go prepare some food. I’m hungry.\"","After everyone had left, Xiao Wan’er sat in a daze for a moment. Her expression shifted rapidly—from pale to pink to a deep, feverish blush—mirroring the turmoil in her heart.","After a long while, she finally rose and walked to the window. The bright sunlight illuminated her face, making her skin seem as white and translucent as crystal.","She gazed in the direction of the Spring Lotus Garden, only a single thought remaining in her mind:","’My brother-in-law... he had better truly know Medical Skill.’","’Otherwise... otherwise...’"]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149 - 142: Playing Dirty","paragraphs":["At that moment, Chen Yi was still unaware of Xiao Wan’er’s complex feelings.","In fact, after watching Cui’er and Juan’er give Xiao Wan’er her medicinal soup, he had completely relaxed.","He had even been planning to go back to the Spring Lotus Garden and continue fishing.","Who would have thought that Mr. Yue Ming from Guiyun Academy would arrange for someone to deliver something so unexpected.","—Nearly fifty calligraphy practice workbooks.","The official reason was to let him get a feel for the students’ calligraphy skills before classes started the next day.","Chen Yi looked at the two stacks of calligraphy workbooks piled on the stone table. Each stack was about two feet high, and he asked with a growing headache:","\"Mr. Yue Ming... he doesn’t actually expect me to grade all of these today, does he?\"","The visitor’s name was Ma Guan, with the style name Heming. He was a slender young man with regular, honest features.","His dark blue long robe was slightly faded, and fine black threads could be faintly seen at the corners and cuffs, revealing patches sewn on the inside.","Clearly, he wasn’t wealthy.","But Ma Guan didn’t seem to mind, and his bearing was poised and proper.","In response to Chen Yi’s question, he offered a respectful bow, then met his gaze directly, not flinching away.","\"To answer your question, sir, the Dean said that whether you grade them or not is entirely up to you.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and looked him up and down. \"Is there a separate register?\"","\"Yes, I’ll find it for you, sir.\"","As he spoke, Ma Guan rummaged through the two stacks of workbooks for a moment before pulling out a palm-sized booklet, which he presented with both hands in a bow.","Chen Yi took the booklet, flipped it open, and his gaze froze.","After checking it several times, he pointed at the first few names on the register and laughed in disbelief.","\"Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying... their names are on here. Don’t tell me they plan to practice calligraphy with me too?\"","Ma Guan met his gaze, his relatively calm expression twisting slightly as he tried to suppress a smile. He replied:","\"The Dean says, ’In learning, there is no seniority; mastery is what matters.’\"","\"With your level of skill in calligraphy, sir, you are more than qualified to instruct him and Mr. Zhuo Ying.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"That may be so, but I’m afraid they haven’t considered the implications of this.\"","With that, he had Xiaodie fetch him a brush and ink from the study, then picked up the brush and struck out their names.","’If not for the status of Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying, I would have just called this utter nonsense.’","Ma Guan was stunned by his action. \"Sir, this... this... I’m afraid it will be difficult for this student to explain when I return...\"","Before he came, Mr. Yue Ming had specifically instructed him in person, emphasizing that he must get Chen Yi to agree to the \"students\" on this register.","How could he have known that Chen Yi wouldn’t even give him a chance, striking out the instructors’ names with a single stroke of the brush.","Chen Yi wrote a few words on it before handing the booklet back to him with a smile. \"Take this back to Mr. Yue Ming. He won’t give you any trouble.\"","Ma Guan took the booklet and bowed hesitantly. \"Yes, sir.\"","Chen Yi glanced at the workbooks on the table. \"And as for the rest of these... forget it, I’ll finish looking through them all today.\"","\"But when you go back, remember to inform Mr. Yue Ming that my comments might be a bit harsh, so he should be prepared.\"","Ma Guan paused, a blank look on his face. \"Prepared for what?\"","\"To comfort these students, of course. Lest they burst into tears after seeing my comments.\"","\"Er...\"","Seeing that he had taken it seriously, Chen Yi chuckled. \"It was just a joke. Just report back to Mr. Yue Ming exactly what happened.\"","’This Ma Guan seems like someone who’s been ’poisoned by his studies’ of Confucianism.’","’Balanced, proper, neither servile nor overbearing, but also a bit rigid.’","’If he’s like this as a student, he’ll likely face some hardships if he becomes an official at court.’","’He’ll either have to quickly change his ways and go with the flow, or stick to his rigid principles and get beaten down by reality until he’s black and blue.’","’Compared to him, Li Huai’gu, the Third Place Scholar who also studies at Guiyun Academy, is clearly much more flexible in his thinking.’","After Ma Guan left, Chen Yi sighed, picked up the topmost workbook, and began to flip through it.","On the first page were two large words: \"Yue Ming.\"","Chen Yi paused. He instinctively straightened his posture, sitting upright at the stone table and looking seriously at the calligraphy workbook in his hands.","Setting aside whether it was appropriate for Mr. Yue Ming to bend the rules and pull strings for himself, his earnestness was clear just from the two words, \"Yue Ming.\"","Since that was the case, Chen Yi couldn’t be too casual about it either.","’It’s as they say, \"If a gentleman treats me with sincerity, I must treat him with sincerity in return.\"’","He turned the pages one by one, seeing it was a copy of the *Pine Wave Record*, a widely circulated piece in the Wei Dynasty. The full text was exactly five hundred characters long.","It took him about a quarter of an hour to finish reading it.","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then picked up his brush and, beneath the two words \"Yue Ming,\" wrote two lines of small text in Wei Qing’s Style:","\"Your form is proper, but it lacks grandeur. It is misaligned with your intent.\"","Calligraphy Dao, the Dao of Calligraphy... only when it aligns with one’s own Dao can it truly be expressed.","A great Confucian scholar like Mr. Yue Ming, so well-read and yet willing to take on \"educating others\" as his life’s mission, ought to possess an ambition that encompasses the world.","Yet every character in this calligraphy workbook strictly adhered to Wei Qing’s Style, with perfectly horizontal and vertical strokes, which inevitably conflicted with his own inner spirit.","Deviating from the \"Calligraphy Dao\" is like walking down the \"wrong\" path; naturally, one will never find the proper entrance.","Next, Chen Yi looked at the calligraphy workbooks of the other few instructors. Most had problems similar to Mr. Yue Ming’s.","It was just that each person had a different state of mind and level of calligraphic skill, so the Calligraphy Dao that suited them was naturally different as well.","He graded them one by one, treating it as a gift to Mr. Yue Ming and the others.","Whether they acknowledged it, whether they listened, was all up to them to decide.","As for the other workbooks, Chen Yi’s examination was not nearly as detailed.","With a quick glance, he could tell the state of the students’ calligraphy and whether they had been serious or not. His comments were mostly fair and to the point.","Some read, \"Poor. Needs more diligent practice,\" while others said, \"Terrible. Poor attitude. Advise starting over from basic strokes.\"","In less than the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, Chen Yi finished looking through all the workbooks, put down his Wolf Hair Brush, and remarked:","\"As expected. In an imperial examination system centered on ’testing,’ these people focus their minds mostly on the classics and histories. Their only standard for calligraphy is ’neatness’.\"","\"Not a single one is even passable. The best among them might get a ’Below Average’ grade.\"","Xiaodie, who had been watching him write his comments the whole time, couldn’t help but laugh. \"Young Master, aren’t you afraid they’ll go complain to the Dean tomorrow after seeing your grading?\"","Chen Yi pursed his lips. \"I wish them the best of luck.\"","If he didn’t have his own plans, he never would have agreed to be an Instructor at the academy.","But he knew, of course. In the current environment where Confucianism reigned supreme, respecting one’s teachers was paramount. Even if you gave those students a healthy dose of courage, they wouldn’t dare to gossip or complain.","And they certainly wouldn’t dare to formally accuse him of grading too harshly.","If the students actually did go complain, he’d actually think more highly of them.","Once Xiaodie had tidied up, Chen Yi glanced at the sky. Remembering he had one more thing to do today, he decided to leave the mansion for a bit.","\"Young Master, it’s about to get dark. Are you still planning to go out?\"","\"Yes, I’m going to Hundred Herbs Hall to postpone what the Eldest Miss asked me to do for a few days. She just fell ill and needs to rest for a while.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wuge, who was playing chess nearby, turned and asked, \"Brother-in-law, is my sister feeling better?\"","Chen Yi paused and glanced toward Jiaxing Garden. \"She should be fine now. Why don’t you go over and see for yourself?\"","\"Okay.\"","But before Xiao Wuge could put away the chessboard, Cui’er came over from Jiaxing Garden, smiling and bowing.","\"Young Master, the Eldest Miss invites you over. She says the household has prepared some wild game, and she wants you to join her for dinner.\"","Xiao Wuge’s eyes lit up, and he was about to go with her.","Suddenly, he saw Chen Yi standing beside him and asked, \"What about my brother-in-law? Didn’t my sister invite him too?\"","Cui’er shook her head, her smile a little strange as she replied, \"The Miss said the Young Master doesn’t like wild game.\"","\"...\"","How could Chen Yi not understand Xiao Wan’er’s intention? He didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","’She must have found out about what I did when I was treating her this morning.’","’But that wasn’t my fault.’","’How was I supposed to treat her without lifting the blanket?’","Xiao Wuge, unaware of all this, just blinked in confusion and looked at him. \"Brother-in-law?\"","Chen Yi could only smile and nod. \"Your sister is right, I really don’t care for it.\"","With that, he told Xiaodie to go along with them.","Xiaodie nodded in agreement, not forgetting to add, \"Young Master, please remember to come back early.\"","\"I know.\"","Chen Yi watched them walk away, tidied himself up, and strapped on his folding spear in case of trouble, before leisurely leaving Spring Lotus Garden.","The sun was setting in the west, and the late afternoon light was no longer so harsh.","The once-white clouds were now tinged with a layer of gold, and the temperature was pleasant, not so hot anymore.","With the flowers, trees, pavilions, and towers of the Marquis’s Mansion all around, and the occasional cool breeze on his face, Chen Yi was in a reasonably good mood.","But as he walked from the rear courtyard to the front, the expressions of the Armored Warriors and servants along the way were not nearly as relaxed.","And compared to two days ago, their stern looks now held an extra trace of gravity.","Faintly, he could hear whispers from all around.","\"I heard the Second Master was furious at noon. Someone from the government office sent a message saying Liu Jing’s killer might be from the Xiao Mansion.\"","\"The Imprisonment Department almost caught the killer last night, but someone took advantage of the chaos and killed them.\"","\"The killer’s dead?\"","\"Seems so. That’s what the people from the government office said.\"","\"Since the person is dead and there’s no evidence, aren’t the government office people afraid the Old Master will go knocking on their door?\"","\"Sigh, that’s true...\"","After listening, Chen Yi couldn’t help but reflect.","’Although the Hidden Guard’s plan to frame them last night failed, they still managed to draw the attention of the Imprisonment Department and the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office to the Xiao Family.’","’But I’m not as nervous as I was before.’","’Originally, because I was the one who killed Liu Jing, I felt somewhat guilty and wanted to secretly help the Xiao Family deal with the Liu Family.’","’But after I saw that man in black wielding a great spear last night and guessed he might be one of the Xiao Family’s people, I realized the Old Lord has his own plans.’","’Since that’s the case, I’m not in a hurry to make a move.’","’Or rather, I want to see how the Xiao Family responds, deduce the Old Lord’s plans from that, and then decide what to do.’","’Thinking about it carefully, a place as vast as the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion couldn’t possibly be so simple.’","Just as he was pondering these matters, he saw Liu Si’er, wrapped in bandages, walking toward him.","\"Greetings, Young Master.\"","Chen Yi snapped out of his thoughts. \"Oh, Brother Si, how are your injuries?\"","Liu Si’er raised his hand. \"Still a bit inconvenient, but it’s no longer a serious issue.\"","Chen Yi nodded. Noticing that he was returning from outside the mansion, he asked with a smile, \"An injured man like you is still out and about?\"","Liu Si’er gave a wry smile. \"To be honest, Young Master, I was in South City, helping Ge the Third out of a jam.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Didn’t Ge the Third go to South City yesterday with Miss Tingyun, Miss Guanli, and the others? Who knew that dog would somehow get himself hooked up with some girl.\"","\"Last night, the girl was threatening to kill herself. We barely managed to save her. When we asked what was wrong, we found out Ge the Third had promised to go over last night and buy her freedom.\"","Chen Yi’s heart stirred. \"Buy her freedom? And he didn’t go?\"","Liu Si’er sighed. \"He’s a spendthrift. Where would he get that kind of money? Of course he didn’t go.\"","\"The dog didn’t expect the girl to take his casual joke seriously.\"","\"But when he gets back, he’s definitely in for a beating.\"","After listening, Chen Yi smiled along, exchanged a few more pleasantries with Liu Si’er, and then left the Marquis’s Mansion directly.","He was a good distance away before the meaning finally dawned on him.","’So that’s what they meant last night when they said a girl from Yanhua Lane tried to jump into the river.’","’No wonder.’","’No wonder Tiger Girl said yesterday that Ge the Third was acting strange, staring at her the whole time.’","’There must be Hidden Guard agents in South City. He was secretly passing intelligence to them.’","Chen Yi understood. ’The Three Towns granaries...’","’Ge the Third caused such a commotion not for any other reason, but for the matter he and Xiao Dongchen were planning.’","’It seems Xiao Dongchen put a lot of pressure on him the day before yesterday.’","With these thoughts, Chen Yi glanced back at the towering green-brick outer walls of the Marquis’s Mansion, then walked calmly toward the West Market.","Xiao Dongchen, Ge the Third, Cui Qingwu.","’Three Silver Banner Officers. Different identities, different strengths, and their missions should be different as well.’","’But for them to work together to cause trouble for the Xiao Family... it’s a bit unsportsmanlike, to say the least.’"]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150 - 143: Are You Crazy?","paragraphs":["Several hours later, the daylight began to fade.","In a residence about five li west of Hundred Herbs Hall.","By the faint light, Chen Yi carefully studied his reflection in a copper mirror.","His formerly refined and scholarly appearance had transformed into one of striking handsomeness.","—Fair skin, sharp brows, star-like eyes, and a high-bridged nose.","Aside from his bright, clear eyes, his facial structure, mouth, and nose had all been subtly altered.","Whether at a glance or under close scrutiny, no one would recognize him as the live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family.","Seeing no flaws, Chen Yi nodded. \"Not bad.\"","Hearing this, Wang Ji beamed and quickly bowed.","\"As long as you’re satisfied, my lord.\"","\"It’s just that it’s a bit too handsome. It’ll attract unwanted attention.\"","\"You jest, my lord. You drew attention before, too.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, ignoring the flattery. He looked toward the figure outside the door and ordered,","\"From now on, have him follow you.\"","\"It’s a waste of talent for someone so young to be idling away in this residence.\"","Wang Ji quickly assented and gestured to the short, slender youth outside. \"What are you waiting for? Come thank my lord.\"","This young man, Zhang Dabao, was the Jianghu expert in the Disguise Skill whom Wang Ji had found for Chen Yi.","It was both true and untrue to call him one of the Jianghu People.","To be precise, Zhang Dabao had just completed his apprenticeship and was about to step into the Jianghu when he was recruited by Wang Ji.","But the fact that his Disguise Skill came with recommendations meant he was certainly skilled.","His master, after all, was a famous master thief in Shu State, nicknamed \"One Finger.\"","Legend had it he once stole his way from South City to North City using only a single finger, his hand never missing its mark. Since then, his name had become legendary in the thieving circles of Shu State.","Besides his ultimate thieving technique, \"One Finger\" was also a master of the Disguise Skill, which he often used to evade capture by the Government Office.","Zhang Dabao had learned everything he knew from \"One Finger.\"","When Wang Ji found him, he was planning to follow in his master’s footsteps and make a name for himself by accomplishing the grand feat of stealing his way from the east side of Shu State City to the west.","If Wang Ji hadn’t made such a high offer, the lands of Shu State might already be abuzz with tales of a master thief named \"Two Fingers.\"","Seeing Chen Yi’s satisfaction, the young Zhang Dabao couldn’t help but grin. \"My deepest thanks, my lord.\"","Even though time was short, he had relied on his superb skills to craft a \"human skin mask\" for him, just as Chen Yi had requested.","Of course, it wasn’t real human skin, but a \"mask\" made of a special material.","It not only had realistic skin texture and fine hairs but could also be padded to simulate different bone and muscle structures, completely altering a person’s appearance.","And the disguise he had made for Chen Yi did just that.","From any angle, Chen Yi bore no resemblance to his former self.","Except for his build and a certain indescribable air about him.","So, after his praise, Zhang Dabao added a reminder, \"My lord, appearance is only one part of it. If you want to completely become someone else, you’ll also have to change your...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi understood. Without moving his feet, he gave a slight shrug and clasped his left hand behind his back.","Combined with the calm expression on his face, his entire demeanor instantly became far more aloof.","\"How about this?\"","Zhang Dabao stared blankly, rubbed his eyes, then broke into a wide grin. \"A lord is a lord, after all. I can’t see a single flaw.\"","Though blunt, Zhang Dabao’s words were far more pleasing to Chen Yi’s ears than Wang Ji’s earlier flattery.","He grunted in acknowledgement and instructed Wang Ji, \"Only four people know about this. Make sure no one else finds out.\"","Wang Ji naturally gave his assurance. \"Rest assured, my lord.\"","\"Besides me, Yan Sea, and Zhang Dabao, absolutely no one else will know.\"","Chen Yi nodded and walked toward the door. \"Remember, my public name at Hundred Herbs Hall is Chen Yu.\"","Afterward, the three of them arrived at Hundred Herbs Hall.","Yan Sea glanced over curiously, and just as he was about to speak, he saw Wang Ji clap his hands and announce with a smile to the surrounding Guards, Physicians, and apprentices:","\"This is the boss of our Hundred Herbs Hall, Chen Yu.\"","\"He’s made a special trip to see how things are going.\"","Everyone from Hundred Herbs Hall turned to look at Chen Yi, as did the customers buying herbal teas and medicines.","Hundred Herbs Hall had been open for some time and had recently caused quite a stir in Shu State City, so it naturally attracted attention.","Besides Wang Ji, the Shopkeeper, many people were more interested in the mysterious boss behind Hundred Herbs Hall.","There had been some rumors in the past.","Some said Hundred Herbs Hall was a Xiao Family business that hadn’t been publicly claimed for some reason.","Some said it was the work of some Divine Doctor from the Jianghu.","Others guessed it was some great Noble Family from outside Shu State, who had come specifically to support the Xiao Family.","The theories were many and varied, but no one could say for sure.","Now that the boss of Hundred Herbs Hall had appeared, it was a decent piece of gossip for these people.","\"He’s the boss of Hundred Herbs Hall? He certainly has a dignified bearing. He looks like he comes from a great family.\"","\"Why do I get the feeling he’s one of the Jianghu People? He has a bit of a cold air about him.\"","Never mind the discussions in the hall; Yan Sea and the others were too preoccupied with bowing respectfully.","\"Greetings, Proprietor.\"","Even Liu Lang did the same.","But as he bowed, he breathed a small sigh of relief.","The sky was already dark, and the person who had promised last night to heal his injuries still hadn’t appeared. He’d been starting to think he’d been tricked.","Fortunately, he had finally arrived.","It was just that the person before him was somewhat different from what he had imagined.","Strikingly handsome and cold, unlike the easygoing person he’d spoken with the night before.","Chen Yi paid no mind to the thoughts of those around him, simply saying in a level voice, \"Everyone, back to your work.\"","\"Yes, Proprietor.\"","After Yan Sea and the others continued to attend to the customers, Chen Yi signaled for Wang Ji to take Liu Lang to a quiet room and to bring the box of Silver Needles along.","Wang Ji brought Liu Lang over, looking perplexed. When Chen Yi waved a dismissive hand, he left without another question, despite his confusion.","Liu Lang looked at Chen Yi, who was sitting at the table preparing tea, and asked with a half-smile: \"Senior?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him and asked faintly, \"Don’t I look the part?\"","Liu Lang shook his head and sat down across from him. \"You were gentler last night.\"","A smile touched Chen Yi’s handsome face, a hint of his nonchalance returning. His tone grew more casual.","\"One has to wear a disguise when away from home.\"","Seeing him act this way, Liu Lang looked him up and down before bursting into laughter.","\"Boss Chen, this must be your real face, right?\"","’It’s not,’","Chen Yi thought. He cut to the chase. \"I’ll ask you one last time: are you sure you’ll agree to my terms?\"","Liu Lang was momentarily stunned, then replied, \"I have roamed the Jianghu for years, and I have never once broken my word. You can rest assured on that.\"","\"In that case, sit still.\"","\"Sit still? I...\"","Before Liu Lang could react, Chen Yi waved his hand and lightly tapped the box by his side, and his True Essence began to flow.","Instantly, a needle pierced his left shoulder, followed by another at his Chest Acupoint, and a third below his right pectoral muscle.","The three Silver Needles formed a straight line, each one landing perfectly on his wounds.","Liu Lang froze, staring at Chen Yi in shock. He was utterly dumbfounded.","He had long heard legends of \"Divine Doctors\" in the Jianghu, but seeing it for himself, he realized the rumors had been far too conservative.","How could \"miraculous\" even begin to describe this?","It was... it was simply divine.","Chen Yi had no time to care about Liu Lang’s thoughts, focusing only on using his True Essence to repair his damaged meridians.","In less than a quarter of an hour, he waved his hand and instantly retracted the three Silver Needles.","Liu Lang paused, looking at him blankly. \"It’s done?\"","\"It’s done just like that?\"","\"So fast?\"","As Chen Yi put the Silver Needles back into the box, he instructed, \"I’ll leave a prescription with Wang Ji later. Drink it for three days, and you’ll be fully recovered.\"","\"Remember not to fight with anyone during this time, lest your newly repaired meridians rupture.\"","Liu Lang remained stunned for a moment. When he finally came to his senses, he stood and clasped his fist in admiration.","\"Please forgive me for my ignorance. I hope you will pardon my earlier impudence.\"","’He was utterly convinced. An injury that had tormented him for days had been healed in less than an hour. Anyone would be in awe.’","Chen Yi glanced at him. \"You must not get out much.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang gave a dry laugh, then sat up straight again and said seriously,","\"Since you have healed my injuries, I will be sure to fulfill every part of our agreement.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgement, thought for a moment, and said, \"As it happens, I have something I need you to do.\"","\"I am at your command.\"","\"You know about the Three Towns of Shu State, right?\"","Liu Lang smiled and nodded. \"Who doesn’t? Those garrisons are the foundation of the Xiao Family’s power in Shu State.\"","\"I need you to find people to burn the summer grain that was just put into storage in the Three Towns.\"","\"Uh...\"","Liu Lang’s smile froze, the shock even greater than before. \"Y-y-y-you... are you insane?\"","’Burn the summer grain of the Three Towns? If I really do this, even ten heads won’t be enough to pay the price.’","’Damn it, this is one \"command\" I’d like to \"refuse\"!’"]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151 - 144: Common \"Enemy","paragraphs":["Had he gone mad?","Chen Yi had not, of course, gone mad.","But that didn’t stop him from pretending for a moment.","\"So, the great ’Sword Madman’ plans to go back on his word?\"","Liu Lang opened his mouth, but only after a long moment could he force a bitter smile. \"Boss, you’ve truly given me a difficult task.\"","\"Burning the Three Towns—no, even just burning one town’s summer grain—is a task with no chance of survival.\"","\"The Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion’s fury would be a given, but even the Holy Emperor and the entire Imperial Court would be shaken. When that time comes, the worst I face is death, but you, my lord...\"","Liu Lang looked at Chen Yi’s calm expression and hesitated. \"You would have no way to escape involvement either.\"","\"Scared?\"","\"This—it’s not a matter of being scared or not...\"","\"Mm, it’s not a bad thing to admit you’re a coward.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang finally understood. The young Medical Saint Hand before him was dead set on burning the Three Towns’ summer grain.","He decided to throw caution to the wind, gritting his teeth. \"Since you’ve already made your decision, I won’t try to persuade you further.\"","\"Just tell me. When do you need me to go? Which garrison town should I burn first?\"","Seeing Liu Lang utter such righteous words with such an aggrieved expression, Chen Yi could no longer maintain his calm facade. He broke into a smile and said:","\"As expected of the ’Sword Madman.’ You even dare to undertake such a treasonous act. I’m impressed, truly impressed.\"","When Liu Lang saw him laughing so heartily, he knew he had been played. He couldn’t help but fume.","\"To toy with me like this is truly going too far, my lord.\"","Chen Yi shook his head, still smiling. \"It’s not exactly toying with you. The matter of burning the summer grain is real.\"","\"Uh.\"","Liu Lang was utterly confused by this back-and-forth. \"So are you going to burn it or not?\"","But Chen Yi just shook his head. \"We’re not burning it.\"","He then explained, \"I’m not actually asking you to do the burning. I just want you to find some people and spread the word that there’s a plot to burn the Three Towns’ summer grain.\"","\"Of course, to make it look authentic, we can’t skimp on the necessary preparations.\"","\"For example, the reward for completing the job, which notorious Evil Demons have accepted the mission, and a rough timeline. Try to make as big a scene as possible.\"","After listening, Liu Lang was still only half-clear on the details, unable to grasp the full intent behind the plan.","But at least he now understood he didn’t have to actually go and burn the Three Towns’ summer grain.","\"But by doing this, aren’t you afraid of getting burned yourself?\"","\"Even if it’s not real, once word gets out, the Xiao Family is bound to investigate it to the very end.\"","\"If something goes wrong and they trace it back to us, we’ll lose our heads all the same.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then smiled and nodded. \"You could say that’s one of my goals. What I want is to put the Xiao Family on alert.\"","Since Xiao Dongchen and Ge the Third were plotting to burn the Three Towns, and in such a clandestine manner, he naturally had to give the Xiao Family a heads-up.","After thinking it over, he concluded that making it public was the best way to get the Xiao Family to raise its guard.","He refused to believe that under these circumstances, those two Hidden Guards would still dare to defy the world and burn the Three Towns’ summer grain right under the Xiao Family’s watch.","Liu Lang was beginning to understand. \"You mean someone else is *actually* plotting to burn the Three Towns?\" he asked, astonished.","\"Damn it, who’s that bold? Do they have a death wish?\"","Considering what he already knew about the close relationship between Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family, he realized Chen Yi was doing this for the Xiao Family’s benefit.","Therefore, it wasn’t hard to deduce that someone was planning to make a move against the Three Towns’ summer grain.","It was just as he’d said: for an ordinary person, it was an act they wouldn’t even dare to imagine, let alone carry out.","He guessed that only followers of the Evil Demonic Dao, like the Illusory Sound Sect who would slaughter entire families on a whim, could devise such a vicious plot.","But the result would be the same. Once word got out, it would surely invite thunderous wrath.","Even a Martial Arts Grandmaster would perish under the iron heel of the Imperial Court and the Xiao Family.","The consequences, to say the least, would be severe.","Chen Yi smiled. \"They’re just people who thrive on chaos.\"","He didn’t elaborate, instead changing the subject to a warning. \"But this is no small matter. You must be careful and not expose yourself.\"","Liu Lang nodded. \"Rest assured.\"","\"Before I came to Shu State, I associated with people from all walks of life, some from less-than-reputable circles.\"","\"Their Martial Arts may be mediocre, but when it comes to plots and schemes, few can match them.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment. With the main business concluded, he poured two cups of tea and went over the finer details of the plan with Liu Lang, making some small talk as well.","He had only told Liu Lang one of his objectives.","In fact, his other objective was to muddy the waters in Shu State even further.","The murkier the situation, the more hesitant those with malicious intent would be to make a move, which would, in turn, buy more time.","Even if the Hidden Guards ultimately took a desperate risk, the forewarned Xiao Family would not let them succeed easily.","Seeing it was getting late, Chen Yi urged Liu Lang to be careful before leaving Hundred Herbs Hall and heading toward a residence to the west.","Wang Ji watched him go, then turned to look at everyone inside the hall. After a moment of thought, he said with a smile:","\"The boss just gave an order. Everyone has worked hard this month, so at the end of the month, you’ll all receive a big bonus as a reward.\"","The physicians and apprentices were overjoyed. \"Our thanks to the boss! And thank you, Shopkeeper!\" they chimed.","Hearing this, Liu Lang shot Wang Ji a peculiar look, a sense of admiration blooming in his heart.","’No wonder Boss Chen Yu is so confident leaving Hundred Herbs Hall in his hands,’ he thought. ’The man really is capable.’","Filled with respect, Liu Lang also began to ponder the matter of burning the Three Towns.","’It has to seem authentic, enough for the Xiao Family to take precautions when they get the news, but not so much that they doubt its veracity.’","’It’s difficult, but at the same time, not so difficult.’","’The key is finding the right people for the job.’","Suddenly, Liu Lang thought of someone: Black Tooth, the man who had brought him from the Northern Desert to Shu State in the first place.","’With his money-grubbing nature, he’d never refuse such a ’lucrative’ opportunity.’","...","As expected.","After Chen Yi left Hundred Herbs Hall, several unidentified individuals began to tail him.","He had to waste some time using the lingering crowds in the West Market to shake them.","By the time he had changed his clothes at the safe house and removed his disguise, the sky had grown completely dark.","’Looks like I’ll have to ask Wang Ji to find another house,’ Chen Yi thought.","With that thought, Chen Yi returned to the streets of the West Market, blending into the somewhat crowded throng and heading for the exit.","It was just past five in the evening. The streets of the West Market were still lined with vendors, mostly selling cheap rouge, powder, and jewelry.","They attracted the attention of maids and plainly dressed women, who stopped to browse.","The occasional food stall was also surrounded by people.","There were sizzling, greasy fried rice cakes and roasted game that, while not elegantly presented, filled the air with a mouth-watering aroma.","It was enough to make the stomach of Chen Yi, who had yet to eat dinner, rumble in protest.","Helpless, he stopped an old man selling candied hawthorns on a stick and bought one to whet his appetite.","It would serve as a pre-dinner snack.","Just as Chen Yi started eating on his way back to the Xiao Family residence, he suddenly spotted two people not far off, and a peculiar expression crossed his face.","The two were none other than Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu.","Faintly, he could overhear their conversation.","\"Yunfan, I heard the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall made an appearance today. His name is Chen Yu.\"","\"Chen... Heh. To think he shares a surname with me.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Do you think it’s him, Qingwu?\"","\"Doesn’t seem like it.\"","\"I don’t think so either. Ning Yu saw him before and said he was just an ordinary person with no training in Martial Arts.\"","\"Oh, but he didn’t look ordinary. His clothes and bearing clearly marked him as someone from a prominent family.\"","\"I suppose...\"","Listening to their back-and-forth, Chen Yi’s mouth twitched. How could he not know they were talking about him?","What he couldn’t figure out was why they were together now. Chen Yunfan had clearly been unhappy with their engagement, and he and Cui Qingwu had seemed to be a couple in name only.","So why were they now together, united against a common enemy—him, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall?","After a moment’s thought, realization dawned on Chen Yi. ’Immortal Drunk.’","Cui Qingwu had been afflicted with Immortal Drunk last night, yet here she was in the West Market today. She had clearly used the antidote he had given to Chen Yunfan.","And just like that, the two of them had a common \"enemy.\"","Thinking this, Chen Yi ducked his head, pretended not to see them, and took a detour to leave the West Market from another direction.","What he didn’t know was that his every move had been spotted by Ning Yu and Huan’er, who were following a few steps behind Chen Yunfan.","Huan’er snorted in displeasure. \"Why is he everywhere? That live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family.\"","\"We ran into him at Fengchun Building before, and now we see him again in the West Market.\"","Ning Yu glanced at her, then watched Chen Yi walk away before saying flatly:","\"Your young mistress was able to wake up so quickly thanks to one of Young Master Yi’s physicians.\"","\"You...\"","Huan’er’s face stiffened, and she turned her head away.","Clearly, she was still holding a grudge over Chen Yi’s veiled insults the other day.","Ning Yu paid her no mind. After a moment’s thought, she leaned in and whispered a few words to Chen Yunfan.","\"Hm?\"","\"Brother Yi was just in the West Market, and he saw me?\"","Chen Yunfan stopped in his tracks and looked back into the distance.","Amid the bustling crowd, he naturally spotted Chen Yi’s figure.","It wasn’t that his eyesight was particularly sharp; rather, Chen Yi’s unhurried gait and ramrod-straight posture were too distinctive.","Even in the dim light of night and surrounded by a dense crowd, he still exuded a hint of an extraordinary aura.","After a moment of silence.","Chen Yunfan gave a wry smile. He didn’t chase after him, instead turning to continue deeper into the West Market.","Cui Qingwu had also seen Chen Yi. She caught up to Chen Yunfan and mused aloud:","\"Compared to you and me, Chen Yi has changed more over the years.\"","A smile played on Chen Yunfan’s lips. \"Qingzhou has indeed changed a lot.\"","\"It seems marrying into the Xiao Family has made him give up any ambition for fame and fortune. He’s much more low-key now.\"","Cui Qingwu nodded thoughtfully, her mind drifting back to their encounter at Tingyu Pavilion and, naturally, to Chen Yi’s veiled insults.","\"One thing that hasn’t changed is his silver tongue.\"","\"You mean ’sharp-tongued,’ don’t you?\"","\"Yes, but you didn’t have to be so blunt about it, Yunfan.\"","\"Haha! It’s because I agree his tongue is unforgiving. Even I...\"","Chen Yunfan immediately launched into a rambling account of his various encounters with Chen Yi in Shu State.","To say they were like diamond cutting diamond would be no exaggeration.","Seeing how animated he was, Cui Qingwu listened attentively.","But as he spoke, she realized that Chen Yunfan wasn’t truly annoyed with Chen Yi. On the contrary, it was just like when they were children.","\"Yunfan, do you remember when I visited the Chen Mansion when we were ten?\"","\"How could I forget? You brought a whole entourage, including that younger brother of yours. He was dreadfully dull.\"","\"I’m not talking about him. I’m talking about how you and your brothers got punished because of Chen Yi.\"","Cui Qingwu paused, looking at the grinning Chen Yunfan.","\"If I remember correctly, while everyone else was blaming Chen Yi, you not only spoke up for him but also taught your cousins a lesson for it.\"","\"That... Well, we’re brothers, after all. And Qingzhou, he...\"","\"Ah, what’s the point of bringing that up? It’s all ancient history.\"","Chen Yunfan brushed the topic aside, pointing to a nearby shop with renewed interest.","\"Come on, let’s go buy some rouge.\"","\"Chun Ying is still at the mansion helping me with my work. I should get her a little reward.\"","Cui Qingwu paused, a hint of fond exasperation in her eyes as she watched his retreating back.","’He never knows how to act seriously.’"]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152 - 145: The Headmaster is So Generous?","paragraphs":["An hour had passed by the time Chen Yi returned to the Xiao Family.","From a distance, he saw Xiaodie standing at the entrance, peering in another direction.","Pei Guanli was squatting beside her, digging the big toe of one pearly-white foot into a bluestone slab as if trying to exfoliate the sole.","She was muttering, \"Brother-in-law will be fine, really. Just trust me this once.\"","Without turning her head, Xiaodie said, \"I don’t.\"","She clearly remembered the time Pei Guanli went to the poetry gathering at Guiyun Academy, promised to be back soon, and then disappeared for hours.","\"Hey, why don’t you trust me? Brother-in-law, he...\"","Pei Guanli looked up and saw Chen Yi approaching. A smile instantly brightened her round face. \"Brother-in-law, you’re finally back.\"","Hearing her voice, Xiaodie kept looking the other way. \"This is the third time you’ve tried to trick me. I’m not falling for it.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but chuckle. He lightly tapped Pei Guanli on the head and said with a smile, \"Don’t bully Xiaodie.\"","Pei Guanli stuck out her tongue and giggled, saying she understood. Then she hugged Xiaodie, who had turned around. \"See? I wasn’t lying this time.\"","Unable to break free, Xiaodie let herself be held and looked at Chen Yi. \"Young Master, you’re back late again today.\"","\"Yes, I was wandering around the West Market.\"","As Chen Yi spoke, he held up a half-eaten stick of candied hawthorns as proof. \"I haven’t even finished...\"","Before he could finish, Pei Guanli had already snatched the skewer, which had only two hawthorn berries left, and ate them in two quick bites.","\"Delicious, Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi shook his head helplessly and entered the Xiao Mansion first. \"Let’s go. We’ll talk more once we’re back at the Spring Lotus Garden.\"","Xiaodie quickly pulled Pei Guanli along, following closely behind him.","\"Young Master, have you eaten?\"","\"Not yet. Go to the kitchen later and see what’s left to eat.\"","\"No need. The Young Mistress had me save some food for you tonight. It’ll be ready as soon as I heat it up.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi turned his head to look at her and asked with a raised eyebrow, \"The wild game?\"","Xiaodie nodded, a look of fond remembrance on her face. \"It was delicious. Young Master Wuge ate two whole bowls.\"","\"I... I got a bowl too, and so did Cui’er and Juan’er.\"","Pei Guanli muttered from the side, \"Tingyun, Huatang, and I got back too late, so we didn’t get to eat any.\"","Chen Yi let out a soft \"oh\" and turned to look at the corridor at the end of the central courtyard, almost picturing Xiao Wan’er’s face as she pretended to be calm while ordering them to save some food for him.","’She must have been conflicted about it.’","At the thought, a smile touched Chen Yi’s lips. \"Then you’re out of luck.\"","\"Brother-in-law, shouldn’t you share some with me?\"","\"Wan’er is biased. She left a huge bowl just for you.\"","\"Is that so? I’m still not sharing with you.\"","\"Hmph.\"","When Chen Yi finally saw the \"huge bowl,\" he froze for a moment before telling Xiaodie to heat the food. Then he invited Pei Guanli to eat with him.","’Who serves food in a bowl this big and heaps it up so high?’","’Even if I use my True Essence to speed up digestion, I’d still struggle to finish this much food.’","Pei Guanli wasn’t thinking that far ahead. She pulled Xiaodie over to join them as well.","She called it \"good sisters must know how to share.\"","Chen Yi certainly wasn’t going to refuse. While chewing on some meat, he asked about what she’d accomplished during her outing that day.","\"I bought lots of things.\"","\"Two carts of flour, two carts of coarse grains, and some cured meat. I had it all sent to the Mountain Race.\"","After speaking, Pei Guanli didn’t forget to add with praise, \"Wan’er is so nice. She didn’t even make me pay.\"","Chen Yi was taken aback. \"That’s all you bought?\"","Pei Guanli nodded. \"My people live off the mountain, and we have to trade for grain at the market. So I thought I’d buy some to send over.\"","\"...And you hired an Escort Agency to transport it?\"","\"Of course. I was afraid it would get stolen on the way.\"","Chen Yi’s mouth twitched. He decided against saying the three words \"not cost-effective\" and changed the subject to ask about the others.","Pei Guanli seemed to remember something and asked mysteriously, \"Brother-in-law, I heard something fun. Want to know what it is?\"","Chen Yi didn’t indulge her, serving her a flick on the forehead instead. \"Cut the chatter.\"","Pei Guanli didn’t even feel the pain. She rubbed her smooth forehead and giggled.","\"When we were coming back today, Ge the Third was taken away by men from the Punishment Hall. They said he was going to get ten strikes of the paddle.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Tell me the details.\"","\"I heard that the day before yesterday, while we were out, he got involved with some young woman and caused her to threaten suicide.\"","\"After the mansion sent someone to investigate and get the full story, he was punished.\"","\"I heard from Cui’er and the others that the Punishment Hall ordered Ge the Third to handle it properly tomorrow—either buy the woman’s freedom or resolve the matter.\"","At this, Pei Guanli’s eyes widened. \"Huh? Brother-in-law, that means he won’t be around tomorrow.\"","\"Does that mean I don’t have to go out?\"","Chen Yi hummed thoughtfully, and a slight smile appeared on his face.","’Ge the Third is certainly willing to go to great lengths.’","’To get away as soon as possible, he even resorted to a self-injury ploy.’","’I just hope he can remain this \"resourceful\" after he learns that someone wants to burn down the Three Towns.’","After they finished eating, they each went back to their rooms to rest.","Chen Yi changed into his nightclothes and stretched his limbs while gazing at the bright moon outside, running a few matters through his mind.","’The Liu Family affair isn’t over yet. The Xiao Family should be making some moves soon.’","’They can’t just let the Governor’s Office lead them by the nose.’","’As for burning the Three Towns, even if Ge the Third finds someone for the job, my interference has drastically increased the difficulty.’","’Then there are Xiao Dongchen and Cui Qingwu.’","’Xiao Dongchen’s goal is already clear. He just wants to use the power of the Hidden Guard to supplant the main branch of the Xiao Family.’","’What about Cui Qingwu?’","’Did she also come to Shu State to deal with the Xiao Family?’","’Last night, at least, she definitely made a move to frame the Xiao Family.’","’Besides them, there should be other Hidden Guards in Shu State.’","’A Silver Banner Officer... their superior?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing.","’I should probably muddy the waters in Shu State first and see what sort of monsters are hiding beneath the surface.’","He then sat cross-legged on his bed and began his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","Not until the Zi Hour, when a flash of light appeared before his eyes, did he momentarily rouse from his state.","[Daily Intelligence · Yellow-level Middle Grade: At the Si Hour, the Prefect of Shu State will visit the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion with several people from the Imprisonment Department to request an audience with Xiao Yuan. A miniscule Opportunity can be obtained.]","After reading it, Chen Yi muttered a few words to himself and resumed his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","’The Si Hour is before noon. I’ll probably still be at Guiyun Academy and won’t be back yet.’","’I’m afraid I won’t make it back in time to see Prefect Liu and the Imprisonment Department visit the Old Master.’","’There’s probably not much to see anyway.’","’Liu Si and the people from the Imprisonment Department are visiting to report to the Old Master about Liu Jing’s death.’","’Given the Old Master’s status, they wouldn’t dare cause trouble in the Marquis’s Mansion even if they were ten times bolder.’","’Still, the Hidden Guard’s frame-up that night did lead the Imprisonment Department to focus its investigation on the Xiao Family.’","’This is a good chance for me to see how the Old Master will handle it.’","...","「The next day, just after the Yin Hour」","The starlight was gradually fading, but a bright moon still hung stubbornly in the night sky.","Street vendors had already claimed all the best spots.","This was especially true for the breakfast stalls.","A flatbed cart, a wok, two tables, and eight stools were all it took to provide a meal for passersby.","Ma Guan was one of them. \"Two steamed buns.\"","\"Here you go, sir.\"","After paying, Ma Guan headed toward Guiyun Academy.","Today, as usual, he had gotten up to dress and wash just after the Chou Hour.","He then spent an hour reading, reviewing the classics and histories he had studied the day before and preparing for today’s lessons.","It was a habit he had developed after passing the County Examination and enrolling in Guiyun Academy.","Ma Guan had always believed that diligence could make up for a lack of natural talent. As long as he worked harder than his classmates, he was certain he could pass the Provincial Examination and qualify for the Metropolitan Examination.","Even though he had failed the Provincial Examination twice, wasting six years of his life, he remained undiscouraged, firmly believing he would pass on his next attempt.","Then, like Li Huai’gu, he would return home in silken robes, bringing glory to his ancestors.","About fifteen minutes later, Ma Guan arrived at the academy and went straight to the study hall.","The students who had arrived early were greeting each other.","\"Brother Heming, you’re as early as ever today.\"","\"I heard the Headmaster sent you to the Marquis’s Mansion yesterday?\"","\"Yes. The Headmaster had me deliver a Calligraphy practice booklet to Mr. Qingzhou.\"","Hearing this, two classmates beside him couldn’t help but sneer.","\"Brother Heming, what kind of ’master’ just teaches Calligraphy? Even if his writing is a work of art, he can’t become an official.\"","\"That’s right. Chen Qingzhou may have a reputation for his talent, write beautifully, and compose excellent poetry, but in the end, he’s only a mere Scholar.\"","\"He’s nothing compared to Brother Xin Nian and Brother Gui Yun, who are both Provincial Scholars.\"","\"On top of that, he’s now the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law. Hah. Even if he has some talent, I’d be ashamed to be associated with him.\"","Ma Guan pursed his lips at their words but didn’t argue, simply quickening his pace.","Seeing this, the two long-robed students were slightly taken aback.","Only after Ma Guan was some distance away did they recover, letting out another sneer.","\"The master was right: birds of a feather flock together.\"","\"That poor sod Ma Heming. We don’t look down on him, yet he’s the one who scorns our company.\"","\"Pah! Who cares?\"","Ma Guan vaguely heard the conversation behind him and quickened his steps again.","It wasn’t that he held any particular admiration for Chen Yi.","He simply kept his teacher’s lesson in mind: \"When sitting quietly, reflect on your own faults; in idle talk, do not discuss the failings of others. This is the mark of a gentleman.\"","Even if Chen Yi truly lacked knowledge or had done something against moral principles, Ma Guan would not discuss it with others.","All in all, he was a gentleman who was strict with himself.","When he arrived at the study hall, a few students were already inside.","Glancing around, Ma Guan saw they weren’t reciting their texts and asked with surprise, \"What are you all doing today?\"","One of them pointed to the front of the study hall. \"Brother Heming, didn’t you notice something different?\"","Ma Guan followed their gaze and immediately sensed that something was off.","Where the sand tray should have been, there was now a white rack.","Looking closely, he saw that the white part in the middle of the rack was nothing other than stacks of paper.","And it wasn’t ordinary Xuan paper, but the thicker Yunsong Paper.","Ma Guan was astonished. \"Did the academy bring all its Yunsong Paper to the study hall?\"","\"Looks like it.\"","\"But I don’t understand what this is for. They can’t possibly be letting us use such expensive paper to practice our writing, can they?\"","One of them seemed to have thought of something and said hesitantly, \"I heard... that Mr. Qingzhou is coming to teach us Calligraphy today.\"","Hearing this, Ma Guan understood. \"I get it.\"","\"The Headmaster plans to replace the sand tray with Yunsong Paper for Mr. Qingzhou to use when he teaches us Calligraphy.\"","\"Huh? That’s very likely. No wonder they’re using Yunsong Paper.\"","\"Only this kind of paper is thick enough that you don’t have to worry about the ink bleeding through.\"","\"Uh, the Headmaster is that generous?\"","\"Maybe he wants to preserve Mr. Qingzhou’s calligraphic works...\""]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153 - 146: What Heaven Ordains Is Called Nature","paragraphs":["Chen Yi was also up bright and early, washing up and getting dressed.","Because he was going to Guiyun Academy, Xiaodie had rummaged through chests and cabinets to find him a dark cyan long-robe.","It was made of silk and had a rather slim, tailored fit.","A matching sash was tied at his waist, from which hung a Double Fish Jade Pendant. On his feet, he wore a pair of black boots.","He didn’t look overly extravagant, nor so plain that people would think he was being mistreated in the Xiao Family.","At a glance, Chen Yi looked every bit the part of a handsome and refined scholar.","Xiaodie smoothed out the wrinkles on his robe, nodded in satisfaction, and said with a smile,","\"Young Master, when you go to the academy looking like this today, you’re sure to make them all envious.\"","Chen Yi didn’t know about that, but he was well aware that most scholars didn’t judge a book by its cover.","Even if he were decked out in gold and silver, he would still be looked down upon if he had no real knowledge.","Among scholars, competitions were ultimately decided by knowledge and talent.","But of course, Chen Yi wouldn’t say any of this to Xiaodie, lest he trouble her simple little mind with such worries.","\"Go get the carriage from the mansion and have them load those practice workbooks on first.\"","Xiaodie nodded in agreement and ran downstairs ahead of him.","Chen Yi, however, unhurriedly made his way to the living room to have breakfast with Xiao Wuge and Pei Guanli.","The three of them chatted idly back and forth.","It was mostly Pei Guanli, the Tiger Girl, who did all the chattering.","She didn’t have to go out and wander around today, so early in the morning, she had run over to Jiaxing Garden to discuss having a friendly spar with Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun.","Chen Yi raised his eyebrows. \"You’re going to fight them?\"","Pei Guanli let out a hum of affirmation and blinked. \"Brother-in-law, my cultivation has broken through! I’m in the Eighth Grade Realm now.\"","In fact, her cultivation had already broken through back when she returned to the Mountain Race with Xiao Jinghong.","It was said that when Granny Shan learned of this, she was very pleased and praised her for quite a while.","Subsequently, when Xiao Jinghong was establishing a pact with the Mountain Race, Granny Shan even took the initiative to make a concession, calling it a thank-you gift for the Tiger Girl’s cultivation breakthrough.","Pei Guanli was naturally delighted, but she never revealed the reason for her breakthrough.","That was a secret between her and Chen Yi.","\"But I can’t beat Sister Tingyun and Sister Huatang.\"","\"Sister Tingyun has now reached the Fourth Grade Realm, and her Sword Dao is at the Great Success stage. She’s considered a first-rate expert in the Jianghu.\"","\"Sister Huatang’s cultivation and Sword Dao are a bit weaker than hers, but she’s still at the Middle Stage of the Fifth Grade Realm.\"","\"So when I say a fight, it’s really just me asking them for some pointers.\"","After finishing his congee, Chen Yi chuckled. \"If you work that hard, I’m sure you’ll have another breakthrough soon.\"","The Tiger Girl’s previous breakthroughs had just been a bit slow, and she was a bit lazy, but her progress in technique was passable.","If she could just be a little more diligent, breaking through to the next realm would be no problem at all.","Pei Guanli’s eyes crinkled with a smile. \"I think so too.\"","After a pause, she glanced at Xiao Wuge, who was still focused on his congee, and made a couple of mysterious hand gestures.","The general meaning was to ask Chen Yi about his current Martial Arts Cultivation progress.","Chen Yi hadn’t wanted to crush her spirits, but seeing her with her head held high and chest puffed out proudly, he gestured the number \"seven.\"","Pei Guanli recognized the gesture and froze. \"Seven?\"","Seeing Chen Yi nod, the smile instantly vanished from her face. Her mind reeled as if struck by lightning; she was clearly in immense shock.","The Seventh Grade Realm!","’Brother-in-law... he... he’s not human! How can anyone cultivate so fast?’","’Mountain Goddess, you have to come see this! There’s a monster here!’","Perhaps hearing her say the number aloud, Xiao Wuge looked at her suspiciously. \"Sister Guanli, what’s ’seven’?\"","\"N-nothing. I... I was just thinking of the dog we have at home named Xiao Qi...\"","\"Really? In that case, Sister Guanli, can you bring Xiao Qi to the mansion? I really like puppies.\"","\"No need. He’s already in the mansion.\"","\"What? Where?\"","Seeing the Tiger Girl spouting nonsense, Chen Yi shot her a glare and stood up.","\"You two behave and stay in the mansion. I’m leaving for the academy.\"","Just then, Xiaodie arrived with an Armored Warrior. Chen Yi instructed them to carry the thick stacks of calligraphy practice workbooks from his study and load them onto the carriage.","Just as he was about to get in, a gentle voice called out from behind him. \"Wait a moment.\"","Chen Yi turned to see Xiao Wan’er approaching with Cui’er.","She wore a vibrant red cloak, and as she hurried forward, a pure white dress could be glimpsed underneath.","Her stunningly beautiful face was tinged with a slight blush, unlike its previous paleness. She must have just drunk her medicinal soup.","With a quick glance, a crystalline light flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes as he used his Qi Observation Skill to check Xiao Wan’er’s condition.","After confirming there were no issues, he finally spoke. \"Eldest Sister, your body has just recovered. It would be best for you to get more rest.\"","Who knew that his words would have the opposite effect? The moment he mentioned it, the shyness Xiao Wan’er had been struggling to suppress surged up once more.","Originally, after learning about those embarrassing matters yesterday, she had planned to avoid seeing Chen Yi for a while.","She wanted to be a little willful, like a girl from an ordinary family—to not let him eat the wild game, to not care whether he was going to Guiyun Academy or not.","But when the time came, Xiao Wan’er still rushed over.","Just like last night, when she had ultimately saved him dinner.","Deep down, she knew that Chen Yi hadn’t truly defiled her.","’He... he only glanced a few times...’","Xiao Wan’er suppressed her shyness, turning her head to avoid looking at Chen Yi. Instead, she gestured for Cui’er to place the items she had prepared onto the carriage.","\"Brother-in-law, since you’re going to the academy today, remember to take these to Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying.\"","Chen Yi saw they were writing supplies and went along with her arrangements, cupping his hands in a respectful gesture. \"Thank you, Eldest Sister.\"","Xiao Wan’er glanced at him from the corner of her eye, an unnatural blush on her face.","\"If anyone should be thanking anyone, it should be... hmm...\"","She didn’t finish her sentence, realizing it was inappropriate, and changed the subject to a reminder.","\"Mr. Yue Ming invited you to the academy because he holds you in high regard. You must be mindful of your etiquette.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding and bowed as well.","\"I’m heading to the academy now. I estimate I’ll be back after noon.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in acknowledgment. Only when he turned and boarded the carriage did she dare to look at him directly.","But when Chen Yi lifted the carriage curtain, she quickly averted her gaze again, saying,","\"And remember not to wander off. The city hasn’t been safe lately. I heard someone died over in the West Market the night before last.\"","Chen Yi replied with a smile that he understood and said no more, signaling for the Personal Guard at the front to drive the carriage down the side path and out of the rear courtyard.","With a RUMBLE RUMBLE, the carriage gradually receded into the distance.","Xiao Wan’er watched him leave until he disappeared from sight, the blush on her cheeks still not having faded.","Beside her, Cui’er noticed her expression and spoke cautiously.","\"Miss, the Young Master was right. Your body has just recovered, you need to get more rest.\"","\"The wind is a bit strong out here, and you’re looking a little pale.\"","Before she could finish, Xiao Wan’er had already turned and started walking toward Jiaxing Garden.","As she walked, she touched her slightly feverish cheeks, her mind inevitably drifting back to yesterday’s events.","’She was lying on the bed, drenched in sweat.’","’He sat beside her, watching... watching...’","’How embarrassing.’","As Xiao Wan’er thought about it, her pace quickened, and she began issuing orders.","\"See if Wuge has finished his breakfast and have him come over to study.\"","\"Summon the Shopkeepers of the Medicine Halls. From Jishi Medicine Hall, have Liu Quan come.\"","\"Also, after the summer harvest, the tenants on the fief’s lands need to pay their grain taxes. Send someone to notify the village chief to come to the mansion tomorrow.\"","\"Furthermore, organize the account books for the other properties in Shu State and calculate next month’s allowances...\"","As she rattled off one order after another, the redness in Xiao Wan’er’s face began to subside.","But a trace of shyness inevitably remained in her heart, along with a few indescribable emotions.","In the end, she needed to keep busy to calm herself down.","...","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea what was on Xiao Wan’er’s mind.","As the carriage left the Xiao Mansion and headed for Kangning Street, he sat inside, taking in the scenery outside the window while thinking about his trip to Guiyun Academy today.","Although he had accepted Mr. Yue Ming’s invitation for his own purposes, now that he was an Instructor at Guiyun Academy, he couldn’t just go through the motions.","It was just like yesterday when he had received the calligraphy practice workbooks from Ma Guan. Though he had spoken casually, when it came to actually marking them, he had been completely serious.","He couldn’t help it; it was just his nature.","’That’s what makes a workhorse a workhorse—too much of a sense of responsibility, always trying to be conscientious and thorough.’","Just like now, sitting in the carriage, Chen Yi’s mind was already contemplating how to teach the students the Calligraphy Dao.","That’s right.","He wasn’t thinking of just teaching Calligraphy, but rather trying to guide those students onto the path of the \"Calligraphy Dao.\"","’He had no intention of jealously guarding his knowledge, nor did he worry about the old saying that teaching an apprentice all you know will leave the master to starve.’","He simply operated on the principle of doing everything well, teaching the students as much as he possibly could.","The results didn’t matter.","’What Heaven confers is called Nature. Following this nature is called the Dao. Cultivating this Dao is called Instruction.’","’After all, everyone’s comprehension, temperament, and habits are different. Even if they learn the exact same content, what they gain from it will vary.’","Chen Yi mused to himself, naturally aware that this was far more difficult than simply teaching Calligraphy.","Nevertheless, he had made his decision.","’All great Daos lead to the same end; they all require dedication. If the students have the heart to practice the Calligraphy Dao, sooner or later, they will gain something from it.’","Before long, the carriage stopped outside Guiyun Academy. Chen Yi didn’t have the driver accompany him, simply carrying the practice workbooks into the academy by himself.","From a distance, he saw the student from yesterday, Ma Guan, running toward him.","\"Mr. Qingzhou, my apologies. The headmaster just notified me, so I’m a little late.\"","\"You can just give those workbooks to me. I’ll take you to the study hall.\"","Chen Yi didn’t refuse. He handed the two stacks of workbooks to him, said a smiling \"thank you,\" and walked on ahead.","Ma Guan struggled to carry the workbooks with both arms, barely managing to keep up behind him and give directions.","But after just a few steps, he was already starting to sweat and couldn’t help but wonder to himself.","’He had clearly seen Chen Yi carrying the workbooks so easily just now. Why was it so difficult for him?’","Chen Yi saw his struggle and, knowing the reason, took one of the stacks from him with a smile.","\"Although I’m an Instructor at the academy, I’m probably not as old as you. I’m at the peak of my energy.\"","Ma Guan felt a wave of relief, but also a bit of embarrassment. \"My apologies, sir... I... I...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi asked, \"Besides teaching the Six Arts, does the academy teach Martial Arts?\"","Ma Guan paused, then shook his head. \"None of the other masters are skilled in Martial Arts. Only Mr. Qi Chen, who teaches archery and charioteering, has a Martial Arts background.\"","He knew why Chen Yi was asking and felt a little bitter.","Many of the students at the academy who came from prominent families practiced Martial Arts Cultivation.","Their cultivation might not be high, but they were still much stronger than a mere mortal like him.","At least they wouldn’t struggle to carry fifty calligraphy practice workbooks.","Chen Yi let out a soft \"oh.\" As he glanced at the student, his Qi Observation Skill allowed him to see the state of his aura.","He wasn’t exactly feeble, but his qi and blood seemed somewhat deficient. He probably didn’t eat well most of the time.","Chen Yi understood and didn’t ask any more questions.","Soon, they arrived at the study hall. Ma Guan went in first to place the workbooks on the desk, then quickly took the remaining stack from Chen Yi and set it beside the first before bowing and returning to his seat.","Chen Yi scanned the room. Seeing that Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and the other masters weren’t present, he knew the message he had Ma Guan deliver yesterday had been effective.","Just as he was about to speak, all forty-five students in the study hall bowed in unison.","\"We students greet Mr. Qingzhou. We respectfully invite you to begin your lecture.\"","Their voices were loud and clear, echoing through the relatively spacious study hall.","Chen Yi glanced around, noting that most of them looked serious and respectful, though a few had strange expressions. Taking it all in, he gave a slight bow in return.","\"Please be seated.\"","Once everyone had taken their seats, Chen Yi sat down at the lecturer’s desk. He turned his head, noticed a rack to the side, and let out a curious \"hmm?\"","\"You don’t use sand trays to teach Calligraphy anymore? You’ve switched to Yunsong Paper?\"","’But all the students in front of him clearly had sand trays at their desks.’"]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154 - 147: A Student Succeeded","paragraphs":["Once Chen Yi understood the full story, he didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.","Mr. Yue Ming had certainly gone to great lengths just to get a sample of his Calligraphy.","But using Yunsong Paper—a fine material usually reserved for great clans—to teach Calligraphy was indeed extravagant.","Chen Yi looked at the students sitting primly before their sand trays in the study hall and realized they must be thinking the same thing.","He figured most of them would add the word \"wasteful\" right after \"extravagant.\"","They were, by and large, unconvinced by him, their new Instructor.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi didn’t launch into a long, classical lecture like the other masters he had seen the day before. Instead, he calmly poured water and began grinding the ink.","As he ground the pine-soot ink stick on the inkstone, he began to speak.","\"Before we begin, I want you to consider a few questions.\"","\"What is a ’character’?\"","\"What do you take ’writing,’ one of the Six Arts, to be? And what is the ’method’ within the art of Calligraphy?\"","\"Finally, what is the ’Dao’ in ’Calligraphy Dao’?\"","Hearing this, the students were all taken aback. They glanced at each other, though they weren’t entirely surprised.","It was only natural for a new master to test them.","What they hadn’t expected was for Chen Yi to ask such simple, straightforward questions.","Soon, one student stood up, bowed, and said, \"I believe characters are the foundation of the classics and the arts. Without characters, the many histories and texts of the ancient sages could not have been passed down to this day.\"","\"’Writing’ is the act of recording characters, chronicling all things under heaven and on earth.\"","\"The ’method’ in Calligraphy refers to the ’principles of writing,’ the six ways characters are formed: as pictographs, abstract symbols, combined ideas, sound-and-meaning compounds, transferred meanings, and phonetic loans.\"","\"As for the ’Calligraphy Dao’...\"","The mature-looking student paused, then shook his head. \"I do not know. I ask for the master’s guidance.\"","Chen Yi nodded slightly and looked at the others, asking with a smile, \"Are there any other perspectives?\"","Immediately, another person stood to offer his own view.","One after another.","Some echoed the first student, some differed, and a few were even rather unconventional.","In any case, no one was just going through the motions; they all seemed to have their own understanding.","Even the youngest among them could articulate a reasoned opinion.","’Then again, it’s to be expected.’","’To be admitted to Guiyun Academy, they must have at least passed the County Examination to become Scholars. They’ve read many books and have a certain breadth of vision.’","When everyone had spoken, Chen Yi looked at their eager, questioning faces and said with a smile:","\"You are all correct. It’s simply that your individual understandings differ.\"","With that, Chen Yi picked up a Wolf Hair Brush, dipped it in ink, and rose to stand before the easel.","He had no intention of forcing a single viewpoint on the students. It was both unnecessary and pointless.","After all, he wasn’t some old pedant who taught straight from a textbook, nor did he plan to follow convention.","’The Great Dao has a thousand paths, but they all lead to the same destination. In the end, my purpose is to teach the Calligraphy Dao.’","Chen Yi centered himself, then lifted his brush and, with a flourish, wrote three characters.","The first was a pictogram, the second was in Wei Qing’s Style, and the third was in Cursive Script.","The strokes were different, but they all formed the same character: the one for \"writing.\"","But as he wrote these three characters, Chen Yi used his True Essence to channel the power of heaven and earth.","The moment his brush stopped, a brilliant fluorescent light appeared on the Yunsong Paper.","Not only that, but he had also intentionally imbued it with a trace of Dao Intent, giving the characters an air of cool detachment and freedom.","After finishing, Chen Yi stepped aside. He was about to speak when he saw that Ma Guan and the others were completely captivated by the Calligraphy.","The originally silent study hall was filled with faint murmurs.","\"A manifestation of brilliance... that’s a sign of Accomplishment in the Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"No, it’s more than that. There’s the master’s Mental Realm in it. The brushstrokes form a Painting... Great Success?\"","\"This must be Great Success in the Calligraphy Dao!\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, glancing at a tall, slender student at the back of the study hall. ’This one has some insight,’ he thought.","A faint manifestation of brilliance is the mark of Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao. A Mental Realm indicates Great Success.","Seeing their reactions, however, he was in no hurry to speak.","Only after the murmurs died down did Chen Yi, under the students’ gazes of admiration, reverence, and confusion, say with a smile:","\"So, what do you think? Not too bad, right?\"","\"Uh...\"","The expressions on Ma Guan and the others froze.","Academy Masters of this era were typically learned men who conducted themselves as gentlemen, prizing humility and solemnity above all.","Even if the three characters on the Yunsong Paper were truly magnificent, anyone else would have humbly said something like, \"I must continue to practice diligently.\"","Who would be like Chen Yi, brazenly praising himself with a \"not too bad\"?","But Chen Yi’s next words left them even more stunned:","\"You can do it too. It’s not actually that hard.\"","Though his voice was soft, it struck them like a clap of thunder. Most of them were too stunned to think of anything else, the words \"do it\" echoing in their minds.","’Not hard?’","’I can do it too?’","’If it’s not hard, then why, among all the famous Calligraphy masters in the Great Wei Dynasty, are there so few who can make their characters manifest brilliance?’","After a moment of muttering, Ma Guan was the first to recover. He stood up solemnly and performed a deep bow.","\"Please, Master, teach me the Calligraphy Dao!\"","Connecting this to the earlier questions, he finally understood Mr. Qingzhou’s intention.","’He doesn’t just want to teach us writing and its methods—he wants to pass on the Calligraphy Dao itself!’","Seeing this, the other students also realized what was happening. One by one, they rose and bowed.","\"Please, Master, teach us—the Calligraphy Dao!\"","Hearing their pleas, Chen Yi just nodded and gestured for them to sit down first. He said with a smile:","\"The reason I asked those questions is because they are the foundation of the art of ’writing’.\"","\"They also represent what I want to teach you, which naturally includes the Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"Of course, I can only guarantee that each of you will gain something. Whether you can truly enter the gate of the Calligraphy Dao depends on both talent and hard work—neither can be lacking.\"","As he spoke, he scanned the room.","Seeing that the earlier disdain had vanished from their faces, he knew he had successfully navigated the trap Mr. Yue Ming had set for him.","\"Now then, for the first lesson...\"","For the remainder of the session, Chen Yi didn’t write another character, nor did he have the students practice on their sand trays.","He simply expounded on the questions he had posed earlier.","The Profound Mysteries he had gained from the Calligraphy Dao allowed him to clearly express the nature of characters, Calligraphy, and the Calligraphy Dao.","Soon, a bell rang outside the study hall. The students belatedly realized that an hour had passed so quickly.","Chen Yi knew this signaled a break, so he called Ma Guan over and had him distribute the Calligraphy practice workbooks.","The students, however, immediately noticed the evaluations written inside.","\"Mr. Qingzhou gave me a ’Poor’ evaluation. ’Scattered form.’\"","\"You’re lucky. I got ’Extremely Poor’...\"","Hearing the dejected murmurs, Ma Guan looked at the two words \"Fair Minus\" on his own workbook, a mix of emotions swirling within him.","He didn’t know whether to laugh or feel as dejected as the others.","Chen Yi took in all their reactions but had no intention of offering any words of comfort.","Instead, he tapped the Yunsong Paper and said with a smile, \"Compared to this, aren’t my evaluations quite fair?\"","\"...\"","At this, even the most optimistic student couldn’t help but lower his head, muttering complaints under his breath.","Before long, the break was over.","This time, Chen Yi didn’t give another long lecture. Instead, he went through the workbooks, critiquing each student’s Calligraphy one by one.","Not only did he point out their problems and offer suggestions for improvement, but he also used it as an opportunity to get to know each student.","At the very least, he could now match names to faces.","\"Master, my name is Fang Huan, courtesy name Youda.\"","\"Youda, your fundamentals are a bit weak. Your character forms and strokes lack balance and centering. Practice a hundred characters diligently every day.\"","\"Ma Guan, your writing is the best in this study hall...\"","Chen Yi spent half an hour giving pointers. For the remaining half-hour, he had them copy his example and write the character for \"writing\" in their sand trays.","\"Remember, strokes and form are secondary. The root of the Calligraphy Dao lies within yourselves.\"","\"When your brush can convey your intent, without a single sloppy or failed stroke, you will have crossed the threshold...\"","...","「In a residence not far from the study hall.」","Mr. Yue Ming was sitting with Mr. Zhuo Ying and a few other masters, chatting idly and playing chess in a very congenial atmosphere.","Every so often, a Guiyun Academy Guard in a long black robe would run up and present them with a notebook.","One of the notebooks read:","Writing is writing, the Dao is the Dao.","Writing is like a Martial Arts Technique; it is a skill, a method.","The Dao is hidden within heaven and earth. If one’s thoughts, ideas, and actions are all in harmony with the Dao, one can attain the Dao.","The content was brief, but simple and easy to understand.","Mr. Yue Ming looked at the contents of the notebook, stroked his graying beard, and sighed in admiration.","\"I knew teaching Calligraphy wouldn’t be a challenge for Qingzhou, but I never imagined he would actually teach the ’Calligraphy Dao’.\"","Beside him, the clean-shaven Mr. Zhuo Ying sat ramrod straight at the table, nodding with a smile.","\"That magnanimity alone is beyond that of an ordinary person.\"","\"But practicing the Calligraphy Dao is easier said than done.\"","\"Just look at us. We’ve been writing for decades, and have our characters ever manifested brilliance?\"","Mr. Yue Ming grunted in agreement. He looked thoughtfully at the notebook in his hand and said:","\"Qingzhou’s perspective on the Calligraphy Dao is truly original.\"","\"I’ll give it a try later. Perhaps I’ll make some progress.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying nodded. \"I’ll try later as well. I’ve always been constrained by rules and the axioms of the sages; I’ve never tried to just express my heart directly.\"","\"Thinking about it, what Qingzhou says makes some sense.\"","The two old men playing chess beside them also nodded.","\"It’s quite impressive. He isn’t selfishly hoarding his knowledge. That truly exceeded my expectations.\"","\"Much better than certain calculating individuals.\"","Mr. Yue Ming saw the man’s glance and knew instantly he was the target of the jab. He lifted his head proudly and said:","\"Rather than have Qingzhou waste his characters on a sand tray, I would rather spend some silver to keep them at the academy.\"","\"If you’re unhappy about it, I’ll just keep the calligraphy sample for myself.\"","The other old man cursed good-naturedly, \"Don’t even think about it! We agreed that we’d each get to keep the Calligraphy from one of his lessons.\"","\"It’s just your bad luck today that Qingzhou only wrote three characters. You can’t blame anyone else for that.\"","\"True enough...\"","Just as the masters were joking around, another set of footsteps sounded from outside.","From a distance, they heard the stocky, black-robed Guard shout:","\"Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, it happened! It happened!\"","\"It happened!\"","Mr. Yue Ming frowned, looking at the overjoyed Guard at the door. \"What happened?\"","\"A student... a student succeeded!\"","Seeing his excitement, Mr. Yue Ming exchanged a glance with the others, a single possibility springing to their minds.","\"Are you saying a student has achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao?\"","The black-robed Guard: \"Yes, yes! I heard... no, that’s not right, I saw it! There was a faint brilliance on the character written by Ma Guan—Ma Heming!\"","\"Truly?\"","\"It’s the absolute truth!\"","Mr. Yue Ming didn’t bother asking any more questions. He immediately stood and walked outside, a look of excitement also spreading across his face.","Seeing this, the others quickly followed.","\"That Ma Heming kid’s Calligraphy is usually just by the book.\"","\"But what if it’s true?\"","\"What’s there to even say? Our Guiyun Academy has struck gold!\"","This treasure, of course, was not Ma Guan.","It was the man who could teach the Calligraphy Dao—Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou!"]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155 - 148: Success from Deliberation, Ruin from Carelessness","paragraphs":["Ma Guan had achieved Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao.","Not only was Mr. Yue Ming shocked and thrilled, but even Chen Yi himself hadn’t expected it.","He was confident in the Calligraphy Dao he taught and believed that talented students could embark upon the path with enough effort.","But he had never imagined that someone would take this step in the very first lesson.","It was simply unbelievable.","Chen Yi could hardly imagine the sensation it would cause once word got out.","Never mind the future—right at this moment, after Ma Guan wrote the character for \"Book,\" which now faintly glowed with splendor, the study hall fell completely silent.","The students sat upright in their seats, their eyes fixed on the sand tray before Ma Guan, staring with utter disbelief at the glow on the character for \"Book.\"","Even Ma Guan himself stared blankly at the sand tray, as if he couldn’t believe he had written it.","He murmured, \"Did... did I write this?\"","Chen Yi glanced around, then rose and came to his side. He smiled and said, \"You did indeed.\"","\"But if you don’t want this to be a one-time fluke, recall the state of mind you just had and write a few more characters.\"","Ma Guan paused. Instead of immediately following the instruction, he suddenly stood up and performed a deep bow.","\"Thank you, Teacher!\"","Chen Yi smiled. ’The young man really is as straightforward as I thought.’","’But I suppose I’ve earned this bow.’","\"Alright, you’ve given your thanks. Sit down and write a few more characters.\"","\"Yes, Teacher.\"","With a solemn reply, Ma Guan sat back down before the sand tray, wiped away the character for \"Book,\" and smoothed the sand.","He recalled his previous state of mind.","’A gentleman must be centered and serene, resilient and unyielding, grand and magnanimous.’","He paused for a moment.","Ma Guan once again picked up the tree branch at his side and wrote the word \"Gentleman\" in the sand tray.","The strokes were level and straight, possessing an upright and grand air.","The moment the tip of the branch paused, a crystalline luster faintly appeared on the sand tray.","Though not as brilliant as the character for \"Book\" that Chen Yi had written, it was, without a doubt, a character \"revealing its splendor.\"","Ma Guan’s mind relaxed, and he looked up at Chen Yi. \"Teacher?\"","Chen Yi clapped him on the shoulder and praised with a smile, \"Not bad at all.\"","’Not bad at all? It was far better than that.’","’You can judge a man by his calligraphy.’","’Just by looking at this one word, \"Gentleman,\" I can discern Ma Guan’s character and state of mind.’","’He truly has the air of a gentleman.’","Only then did the surrounding students, who had been holding their breath, finally cup their hands and congratulate Ma Guan.","\"Brother Heming, congratulations.\"","\"Brother Heming, with time, you will surely become a master of Calligraphy in our Great Wei Dynasty.\"","\"Why wait for the future?\"","\"Even now, in our Guiyun Academy, besides Mr. Qingzhou, there’s no one who can compare to Brother Heming in the Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"That’s right. Even our Dean and Mr. Zhuo Ying are slightly inferior.\"","What the student who spoke didn’t know was that Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying, having heard the news and rushed over, were standing right outside the study hall and had heard every word.","The joyful expressions on their faces instantly stiffened.","Their expressions made the other old men who hadn’t been named roar with laughter and start teasing them.","\"Mr. Yue Ming, it seems you still have work to do on your Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"Zhuo Ying, is your Calligraphy still presentable these days?\"","Hearing the voices from behind, the students finally noticed their arrival and quickly sat up straight.","Only the student who had just spoken had a wry smile, lightly slapping his own mouth a few times.","Mr. Yue Ming shot the two old men a glare, then walked into the study hall first. He offered a quick apology to Chen Yi for the interruption before heading to Ma Guan’s side.","After seeing the word \"Gentleman\" on the sand tray, a gratified smile couldn’t help but appear on his face.","However, Mr. Yue Ming didn’t praise Ma Guan first. Instead, he bowed deeply to Chen Yi.","\"Qingzhou, this old man thanks you on behalf of Heming and Guiyun Academy for imparting the Calligraphy Dao.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying and the others behind him did the same.","Seeing this, Chen Yi said helplessly, \"Sirs, are you trying to shorten my lifespan with such a gesture?\"","’For someone to achieve Minor Success in Calligraphy Dao during the first class was already beyond my expectations, and now Mr. Yue Ming and the others are thanking me so formally. Aren’t they afraid of blowing this out of proportion?’","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming straightened up and glared at him. \"What nonsense is that?\"","\"You’ve taught an academy student to the level of Minor Success in Calligraphy Dao, a prodigy with the potential for Great Success in Calligraphy Dao, a future master of Calligraphy for our Great Wei Dynasty! Is it wrong for this old man to thank you?\"","Chen Yi watched him earnestly pile all sorts of titles onto Ma Guan and shook his head with a wry smile.","\"You’re the Dean. Whatever you say, goes.\"","\"Now that’s more like it.\"","Mr. Yue Ming’s expression softened slightly. He turned and praised Ma Guan, \"Heming, well done.\"","\"From now on, learn well from Qingzhou. Strive to achieve Great Success in Calligraphy Dao as soon as possible, so our Guiyun Academy can become famous throughout the Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures.\"","At this point, Mr. Yue Ming paused and shot a sidelong glance at Chen Yi. \"Of course, Mr. Qingzhou’s name will likewise spread far and wide.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi privately pursed his lips.","Things had come to this; he could only let it be.","’But who could I blame? It was just my luck that this class produced a student like Ma Guan, with more than enough talent and skill in Calligraphy.’","However, with Mr. Yue Ming’s arrival, the lesson clearly couldn’t continue as normal.","The minds of the students in the study hall were all on Ma Guan, their feelings a complex mixture.","They all knew that regardless of whether Ma Guan could pass the provincial and metropolitan examinations in the future, he could become famous far and wide on the strength of this Calligraphy skill alone.","Meanwhile, outside the study hall, many other students had rushed over after hearing the news.","Some were envious, some were jealous, but most were filled with regret.","\"When Mr. Yue Ming told us to sign up to study with Mr. Qingzhou, what possessed me to refuse?\"","\"Me too. Ma Heming really lucked out.\"","\"Who could have possibly thought that what Mr. Qingzhou was teaching wasn’t simple Calligraphy, but the Calligraphy Dao?\""]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156 - 148: Accomplishment Through Thought, Ruin Through Whim (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"Alas, what are we to do now...\"","Several quick-witted people exchanged a glance. They immediately turned, pushed their way out of the crowd, and ran from the academy.","Missing the first registration didn’t matter. At worst, they would just have to spend a little extra to take the place of another student in the study hall.","Or they could find a way to use their connections to get to Mr. Yue Ming and try to become Chen Yi’s student.","For students from prominent families, this was not a difficult task.","Even if Mr. Yue Ming disagreed, they could find a way to petition the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","They absolutely could not miss this opportunity.","One must understand that proficiency in Calligraphy also brought certain advantages in the imperial examinations.","Although no past imperial examination had ever explicitly tested Calligraphy, observant people had noticed that students accomplished in Calligraphy would receive some preferential treatment, even if their essays were slightly lacking.","They might be favored by the chief examiner or praised by certain great scholars. In any case, there were always some benefits.","But aside from the students inside and outside the study hall, the busiest person right now was Ma Guan himself.","Ordered by Mr. Yue Ming and the others, he continued to write, character by character, on the sand tray.","Streaks of radiance manifested, only to vanish as the sand tray was smoothed over.","By the end, Ma Guan’s face, which had originally held some color, was now pale and drenched in sweat.","Seeing this, Chen Yi had to interrupt. \"Characters written at the level of Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao are extremely mentally taxing. Let’s stop here for today.\"","Mr. Yue Ming and the others, though not yet fully satisfied, finally nodded. \"Heming should indeed get some rest.\"","Hearing this, Ma Guan let out a long breath, weakly got up, and bowed. \"I will continue to work hard in the future and strive to achieve Great Success in the Calligraphy Dao as soon as possible.\"","Chen Yi shook his head. \"Just do your best. Don’t try to run before you’ve learned to walk.\"","Ma Guan was slightly taken aback, then bowed solemnly again. \"This student will remember your teachings, teacher.\"","Just as Chen Yi was about to announce that class was over for the day, Mr. Yue Ming came to his side and said in a low voice:","\"Qingzhou, this is your first class, after all. It wouldn’t be right to only write three characters.\"","Chen Yi glanced at him. How could he not understand his intentions?","He asked with a half-smile, \"What instructions does the Headmaster have for me?\"","\"How about you write a piece of calligraphy to hang in the study hall, to encourage the students of our Guiyun Academy?\"","\"No.\"","\"Ahem... On behalf of the students, I thank...\"","Seeing Mr. Yue Ming about to give another deep bow, Chen Yi quickly took a step to the side. \"Stop.\"","Mr. Yue Ming immediately stopped, looking at him with a pained expression on his old face.","Seeing this, Chen Yi shook his head helplessly. \"Headmaster, I’m only letting this slide because you’re my elder.\"","\"If there’s a next time, don’t blame me for switching the Yunsong Paper back to the sand tray.\"","\"I guarantee it won’t happen again.\"","Beside them, Mr. Zhuo Ying and the others silently chuckled and cursed the shameless old man, but they didn’t speak up to ruin Mr. Yue Ming’s good fortune.","After all, their scheme of using Yunsong Paper to trick Chen Yi into creating a calligraphy piece couldn’t be exposed.","Otherwise, if Chen Yi got angry, none of them would benefit.","Fortunately, Chen Yi didn’t know about this.","After agreeing to Mr. Yue Ming’s request, he picked up his brush and spread the ink, writing a line of characters on a wide sheet of Yunsong Paper:","\"Excellence is born of diligence and destroyed by frivolity; success is born of contemplation and ruined by caprice.\"","Although this sentence couldn’t compare to the Four Sentences of Hengqu, it was a reflection of the \"gentlemanly conduct\" Chen Yi saw in Ma Guan.","At the same time, it served as his message to the students.","Whether in practicing writing, studying, or conducting oneself, only with both diligence and virtue could one become accomplished.","When Mr. Yue Ming and the others saw the content on the paper, along with the free and easy spirit between the lines, their earlier thoughts of scheming against Chen Yi inevitably made them feel a little ashamed.","\"On behalf of...\"","Before they could finish, Chen Yi dropped the Wolf Hair Brush and turned to walk out of the study hall.","’Again?’","’Do they really think my lifespan is endless?’","Mr. Yue Ming and the others exchanged a glance, smiles appearing on their faces.","\"Headmaster, you are truly a disgrace to the scholarly arts.\"","\"Heh heh.\"","\"The scum of the literati!\"","\"Heh heh.\"","Seeing this, Mr. Zhuo Ying and the others knew that Mr. Yue Ming had thrown all face to the wind, so they immediately chased after Chen Yi.","Mr. Yue Ming, of course, paid them no mind, a smile on his face as he carefully put away the two sheets of Yunsong Paper.","As he turned his head, he saw the students inside and outside the study hall. His old face couldn’t help but flush, and he feigned a cough before saying:","\"I will go mount this calligraphy piece first, to prevent it from getting damaged...\"","「...」","While Chen Yi was being led away by the teachers of Guiyun Academy, laughing and talking, the Qingjing Residence within the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion was not so quiet.","The Prefect of Shu State, Liu Si, had arrived with three people from the Imprisonment Department.","At first, the atmosphere was relatively relaxed.","But when Hundred Households Fang Hongxiu of the Imprisonment Department mentioned the discovery in the West Market from the night before last, the atmosphere instantly grew tense.","\"The Xiao Family?\"","\"Hundred Households Fang, are you implying that the person who murdered Liu Jing was one of the Xiao family?\"","The Elder Master was calm, but a trace of anger had already appeared on Xiao Wang’s face beside him.","Fang Hongxiu paused, then rose and bowed. \"My apologies, Second Master Xiao. I was merely stating the facts of the matter. I am not certain that the ’Xiao Family’ Sun Erhu mentioned is the Marquis’s Mansion.\"","Xiao Wang stared at her and snorted coldly. \"Coming to the Xiao Family to mention this matter doesn’t seem as simple as you claim.\"","Just as Fang Hongxiu was about to explain further, she saw Liu Si beside her wave his hand.","\"Hundred Households Fang, what the Second Master says is not without reason.\"","\"Since the Imprisonment Department is uncertain of the killer’s identity, it was inappropriate for you to mention the ’Xiao Family’ in front of the Marquis.\"","Fang Hongxiu pressed her lips together slightly, bowed, and retreated to her seat.","But the middle-aged man beside her was not about to give up. He stood up, bowed, and said:","\"Reporting to the Marquis, although the Imprisonment Department is not certain if the killer is from the Xiao family,\"","\"all the clues we currently have do indeed point to the Xiao Family.\"","He was about forty years old, with a gaunt figure, prominent cheekbones, and unremarkable features.","As he spoke these solemn words, his long, narrow face looked somewhat sharp-featured and cunning.","At his words, the great hall fell silent.","Liu Si frowned slightly and said no more, only looking at Old Marquis Xiao.","Fang Hongxiu was slightly surprised.","But Xiao Wang was already furious. He slammed his hand on the table. \"Huang Zhuo, do you know what you are saying?!\"","Just then, Elder Master Xiao raised his hand slightly, his tone calm as he interrupted, \"Second Son, let Thousand Households Huang finish.\"","Xiao Wang glanced at his father, then shot a fierce glare at the middle-aged man.","Huang Zhuo, however, did not look at him, keeping his gaze fixed on Elder Master Xiao as he said respectfully:","\"Marquis, I am merely discussing the facts of the case. I hope you will forgive me.\"","The Elder Master was noncommittal, saying faintly, \"Thousand Households Huang, why don’t you elaborate on what clues point to my Xiao Family.\"","Huang Zhuo nodded, then took a booklet from his robes and began to read:","\"There are three clues.\"","\"First, Liu Jing, the sixth son of the Jing State Liu Family, came to Shu State this time to establish Linglan Pavilion. His purpose was connected to the Xiao Family Medicine Hall...\"","Before he could continue reading, Elder Master Xiao spoke up. \"Are you saying that the Jing State Liu Family is deliberately targeting my Xiao Family?\"","Huang Zhuo faltered, a difficult expression on his face. \"That is not what I meant. I was just, just...\"","\"Just what?\"","Huang Zhuo quickly changed his tune. \"My apologies, Marquis. I must have misread. Please wait a moment.\"","Although the Liu Family’s purpose in coming to Shu State was indeed to deal with the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, saying so openly was tantamount to slapping the Xiao Family in the face.","Furthermore, if word of this got back to the Jing State Liu Family, he, a mere Thousand Households of the Imprisonment Department, would likely be implicated.","As he spoke, Huang Zhuo turned his head to glare at Fang Hongxiu before continuing to read.","Only now he no longer dared to read verbatim from his script. Instead, he glossed over the more serious points, mentioning only the minor clues that were unfavorable to the Xiao Family.","After listening, the Elder Master looked at him. \"Is that all?\"","By now, beads of sweat had formed on Huang Zhuo’s forehead. \"My apologies, Marquis. This is all the Imprisonment Department has found so far.\"","Hearing this, a smile appeared on the Elder Master’s face. \"With just these ambiguous clues, you dare to come to my Xiao Family and press charges...\"","\"Who gave you the nerve?!\""]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157 - 149: Brother-in-law, These Ladies Are...","paragraphs":["Seeing Elder Master Xiao erupt in anger, not only did Huang Zhuo’s face turn ashen, but Liu Si’s and Fang Hongxiu’s expressions also changed slightly.","Even Xiao Wang, who was sitting calmly to the side, was a little surprised.","He had thought Elder Master Xiao would let the matter pass nonchalantly, as he had before.","He never expected Elder Master Xiao to have such a strong reaction.","Huang Zhuo wiped the sweat from his forehead and said with a trembling voice, \"Marquis, please calm your anger. I... I failed to investigate this matter clearly. It is my dereliction of duty. I beg your forgiveness.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao continued to stare at him and asked, \"I ask you, who exactly gave you the nerve?\"","\"Did the Jing State Liu Family send you?\"","\"Or was it the Shu State Governor’s Office?\"","Huang Zhuo hurriedly knelt, his expression changing drastically.","\"Marquis, please forgive me! No one ordered me to do this. It was all my dereliction of duty. I implore the Marquis to see the truth.\"","\"You think you can settle this with a simple ’dereliction of duty’? Do you really think I’ve gotten old? That I can no longer lift my blade?\"","\"No...\"","At this sight, Xiao Wang frowned as he looked down at the hall. The corner of his eye glanced at Elder Master Xiao; he clearly hadn’t expected this scene.","’What is my elder brother trying to do?’","’Is he really going to have this Thousand Households of the Imprisonment Department put to death?’","Seeing Huang Zhuo single-mindedly kowtowing and admitting his fault, Liu Si, who was at the side, thought for a moment and tried to speak:","\"Marquis, please calm your anger. It was indeed wrong of Thousand Households Huang to jump to conclusions without a thorough investigation...\"","Elder Master Xiao shot him a glance and interrupted in a cold tone, \"Did Prefect Liu not know about the progress of the Imprisonment Department’s investigation before this?\"","Sweat immediately beaded on Liu Si’s face. In his heart, he was already cursing Huang Zhuo to high heaven.","Elder Master Xiao’s question seemed simple, but in reality, there was no right way for him to answer.","He was the Prefect of Shu State, responsible for public order and various affairs, so the Imprisonment Department naturally fell under his jurisdiction.","If he said he didn’t know, it would make him, the Prefect, seem incompetent and suspect for dereliction of duty.","But if he said he did know...","Choosing the lesser of two evils, Liu Si could only brace himself and say:","\"My apologies, Marquis. Thousand Households Huang did not, in fact, inform me beforehand.\"","\"You didn’t know?\"","\"The Lord Prefect manages countless affairs every day. It’s only right that he wouldn’t know.\"","Hearing this, Liu Si quickly knelt beside Huang Zhuo, bowing his head to admit his fault. \"Marquis, please forgive me.\"","Seeing her two superiors kneeling, Fang Hongxiu also knelt behind them.","Seeing this, Elder Master Xiao snorted. \"A Prefect and a Thousand Households of the Imprisonment Department, and you can’t even figure out such a small matter. If word of this got out, it’d be a laughingstock.\"","\"Fortunately for you, you’re not soldiers of the Dingyuan Army. Otherwise, this old man would have beheaded you today.\"","Hearing this, not only did Liu Si and Huang Zhuo not feel relieved, they grew even more terrified.","Or rather, Liu Si was the one who was terrified.","Not being soldiers of the Dingyuan Army meant they were not considered one of the Old Marquis’s own people.","\"Marquis, you speak too gravely. I am based in Shu State and will certainly not forget my roots!\"","Huang Zhuo’s face was ashen. He pressed his forehead to the floor, not daring to utter a single word.","’I must have been a complete idiot, believing someone else’s words and daring to run my mouth in front of the Old Marquis.’","Fang Hongxiu, however, seemed oblivious, clearly not catching the underlying meaning.","At this moment, Xiao Wang glanced around and suddenly spoke up, \"Elder Brother, in my opinion, why don’t we let the Prefect go back and investigate this clearly first?\"","Elder Master Xiao shot him a look. \"What? Did you really think this old man was going to punish them?\"","\"I...\"","Before he could speak again, Elder Master Xiao had already turned to Liu Si and the others, waving his hand.","\"Get out of here and come back when you’ve investigated this properly.\"","\"If it truly was one of my Xiao Family who did this, even if it were my own brother, I would strike him down myself!\"","Xiao Wang froze for a moment, then his expression darkened, and he said no more.","He naturally understood the thinly veiled jab.","But more than that, he was concerned about Elder Master Xiao’s words and actions today.","’Something feels off.’","As for Liu Si and the other two, they hastily bowed and took their leave without a moment’s delay.","After everyone had left, Xiao Wang also rose, preparing to depart.","Just then, Elder Master Xiao spoke up and asked:","\"Second Brother, tell me, if this old man were to kick the bucket one day, who could support this great Xiao Family?\"","Xiao Wang’s steps faltered. He turned his head to look at him, and seeing his direct gaze, a chill ran through his heart.","\"Who do you think, Elder Brother?\"","\"You.\"","\"Me...\"","But just as he was about to speak, he saw Elder Master Xiao shake his head. \"You can’t do it.\"","\"Second Brother, don’t blame me for being harsh.\"","\"Although your Martial Arts are so-so, leading an army is not a one-man fight. Commanding thousands of troops is not comparable to leading the men of the Punishment Hall in their little affairs.\"","Xiao Wang’s expression immediately darkened. \"I have no such intentions.\"","\"The Xiao Family has one and only one heir, and that is Wuge!\"","After saying this, he strode directly out of Qingjing Residence.","Elder Master Xiao watched him walk away, a desolate look on his face, and he let out a deep sigh.","’If I say you can’t, you really can’t.’","’Even if I tied Dongchen and Qiuyun to you, you still couldn’t hold up the sky for the Xiao Family.’","\"If not for Wuge’s youth, why would this old man...\"","...","「Outside the Marquis’s Mansion.」","Liu Si’s expression was extremely ugly as he looked at Huang Zhuo and said in a low voice:","\"If I didn’t know you were always a blockhead, I might have thought you were acting on someone’s orders today.\"","Huang Zhuo’s lips moved, but he said nothing. He gripped the hilt of his blade, looking like he was furious but didn’t dare to speak.","\"My apologies, Lord Prefect. I will definitely uncover the truth shortly and give you an explanation!\"","\"To me? You’d better think about how to appease the Marquis’s anger.\"","Just as he was about to say more, a carriage flying the red flag of the Xiao Family pulled up beside them, and the group quickly made way.","After the carriage entered the Xiao Mansion, Liu Si gave Huang Zhuo a few more instructions, then boarded his own carriage to leave.","Just then, an Imprisonment Officer ran over with an excited expression:","\"Lord Prefect, Lord Thousand Households, Lord Hundred Households, we’ve found the murderer!\"","The three of them froze. \"What murderer?\"","\"The murderer who killed Liu Jing has been found.\"","Huang Zhuo was overjoyed. \"Quick, tell us! Who was so bold?\"","\"It was a guard from Huilin Hall. He was acting suspiciously outside Hui Xian Building today. When we questioned him, he tried to flee. Luckily, there were many of us, and we joined forces to capture him.\"","\"Under questioning, we learned that he was the one responsible for what happened that night.\"","After hearing his report, Liu Si asked thoughtfully:","\"That Huilin Hall is one of the Wan Family’s businesses, right?\"","Huang Zhuo nodded and said with a smile, \"It is indeed the Wan Family. I never thought...\"","Before he could finish, the smile on his face vanished.","If the Wan Family did it, then the things he had just said in the Marquis’s Mansion were truly utter nonsense.","Liu Si nodded, got into his carriage, and commanded in an inscrutable tone, \"Interrogate him thoroughly. We’ll hold court tomorrow.\"","Huang Zhuo bowed in acknowledgement, then hurriedly boarded his carriage and left.","After the carriages had departed, Fang Hongxiu, who had been standing to the side, felt that there was something strange about this matter.","\"How does the Wan Family’s strength compare to the Xiao and Liu Families?\"","The Imprisonment Officer who brought the news thought for a moment and said, \"They’re not even in the same league.\"","\"Then is it possible he did this to frame the Xiao Family?\"","\"Lord Hundred Households, we’re...\"","Seeing the Imprisonment Officer point to the Xiao Mansion’s plaque not far away, Fang Hongxiu nodded. \"We’ll talk back at the office.\"","’There must be a hidden story behind all this, anyway.’","Once it was quiet outside the gates, Chen Yi, who had been lingering inside the Marquis’s Mansion for a good while, finally stepped out of his carriage.","He glanced at the spirit screen outside the gate, his expression unchanging, and turned to walk toward the rear courtyard.","’The murderer was found? Someone from the Wan family?’","’Another one of Shu State’s Noble Families?’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi’s gaze shifted toward Qingjing Residence, and he began to understand.","This was Elder Master Xiao’s handiwork—he was eighty to ninety percent sure.","[Opportunity +2]","[Arrived, but missed the scene. Xiao Yuan was furious; the Imprisonment Department captures the true culprit.]","Chen Yi glanced at the contents of the light screen and became even more certain that this was Elder Master Xiao’s arrangement.","’The Hidden Guard’s attempt to frame someone failed, but Elder Master Xiao managed to pull it off.’","’What do you call this? A counter-frame?’","’A shame. I hurried as fast as I could, but still didn’t make it in time. I wonder how exactly Elder Master Xiao showed his fury.’","Chen Yi muttered a few things to himself, but he understood Elder Master Xiao’s intentions.","He was likely giving the Xiao and Liu Families a way to gracefully back down.","Of course, it could also be considered the Xiao Mansion taking the first step back.","’A concession?’","’It seems Elder Master Xiao still hopes to turn a big issue into a small one, and a small one into nothing.’","’If the Liu Family can accept this outcome, both sides taking a step back would be a happy ending for everyone.’","As Chen Yi thought about this, he felt much more relaxed.","Elder Master Xiao’s mind was as clear as a mirror; he probably didn’t need his live-in son-in-law to \"add to the chaos.\"","’This counts as one of the few pieces of good news recently.’","Before long, Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden.","He saw Xiao Wan’er sitting in a pavilion, laughing and talking with several older women.","Only Xiaodie and Cui’er were in attendance, serving them like it was a tea party—pouring tea and bringing out snacks.","Seeing him return, Xiao Wan’er smiled, stood up, gave him a subtle wink, and said, \"Brother-in-law, these ladies came to visit the mansion at noon. They said they wanted to meet the academy instructor who is so accomplished in the Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"This must be Mr. Qingzhou, right?\"","\"He’s certainly a fine, talented man! No wonder my boy came home at noon telling everyone he met that a Mr. Qingzhou had arrived at the academy, and that his skill in the Calligraphy Dao is incredible.\"","Chen Yi: \"...\"","’Damn it, word travels that fast?’"]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158 - 150: A Gentleman Is Forbidden to Court","paragraphs":["Three women make a drama.","But the number of women in the Spring Lotus Garden at this moment was more than you could count on one hand.","Yet there was only one and a half men.","One was Chen Yi. The other half... was Xiao Wuge.","Not many men could handle such a scene with ease.","You’d either have to be a monk who had purged all worldly desires, an ignorant child, or a man who had grown up surrounded by women.","Chen Yi, of course, belonged to none of those categories. His ability to deal with these ladies and young misses of extraordinary birth was entirely thanks to Xiao Wan’er being by his side.","Just think about it.","When a woman of such transcendent, otherworldly beauty is present, would you even notice any other woman?","It was, in essence, a practical application of the \"darkness under the lamp\" effect.","With Xiao Wan’er sitting in the pavilion like a brilliant, radiant lamp, even when she said nothing and only smiled gently, all the other women lost their luster.","At least in Chen Yi’s eyes, the only woman who could sit beside Xiao Wan’er and shine just as brightly was his wife, Xiao Jinghong.","Fortunately, Xiaodie didn’t know what he was thinking. Otherwise...","Otherwise, she wouldn’t have thought much of it either.","On the contrary, she probably would have said, as if it were a matter of course, \"The Young Master has good taste. Xiaodie is naturally no match for the two Young Misses.\"","Perhaps she would even have a shy smile on her face, feeling happy that Chen Yi had even considered her in the same league as Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Jinghong.","In any case, over the course of about four hours that afternoon...","Chen Yi simply adhered to the basic principles of hospitality, sitting properly beside Xiao Wan’er and making small talk with these ladies and young misses of supposedly extraordinary backgrounds.","There was Madam Zhang of the Zhang Clan, wife of Tang Zixing, the Inspector General of the Shu State Inspectorate Office.","There was Madam Sun of the Sun Clan, wife of Bai Yelin, the Grain and Grass Supervisor of the Shu State Capital Commandery.","And there was Wan Rourou, the eldest young miss of the Wan Family, a great local clan with a hundred-year heritage in Shu State.","The first two ladies were older, around forty or so.","The latter was not young either, at twenty-five or twenty-six. She had a graceful and dignified appearance, yet she remained unmarried.","Perhaps due to their similar circumstances, Xiao Wan’er and Wan Rourou were clearly a bit closer.","Of course, in the current situation, Xiao Wan’er would not show it so obviously.","Most of the time, she deferred to Madams Zhang and Sun, treating them with the respect due to elders.","This was especially true for Madam Zhang.","Her husband, Tang Zixing, as the Inspector General of Shu State, was specifically in charge of monitoring all officials, which was equivalent to wielding an imperial sword.","However, according to Madam Zhang, Tang Zixing had been arriving at and leaving his post on time lately, as if there were no urgent matters to attend to.","But her own status and the Tang Family’s standing were undeniable.","Whether they had a guilty conscience or not, others would more or less show her and the Tang Family some deference.","However, Madam Zhang clearly knew her place. She wasn’t arrogant about her position, and her conversation was always proper, never causing any dislike.","\"Ever since my boy passed the County Examination the year before last and entered Guiyun Academy, he’s shut himself off from the world and focused solely on his studies.\"","\"Unfortunately, he’s not very gifted. He failed the provincial examination last year and is preparing to try again in two years. At least he can be considered diligent.\"","As Madam Zhang spoke these two sentences, although her eyes were on Xiao Wan’er, her words were inevitably aimed at Chen Yi, the academy Instructor, hoping he would pick up the conversation.","’Tang?’","Chen Yi recalled a student in his study hall, Tang Ye.","’He’s only fourteen. I don’t know how learned he is, but his calligraphy is at least decent.’","’His evaluation in the calligraphy practice book, if I remember correctly, was \"Passable Plus.\" It’s definitely decent.’","’For his age, he must have put in a lot of hard work on his calligraphy.’","Seeing Chen Yi remain silent with just a smile on his face, Xiao Wan’er said naturally:","\"My brother-in-law only just arrived at the academy today, so perhaps he hasn’t gotten to know everyone yet. But that’s alright, there’s plenty of time ahead.\"","Seeing Madam Zhang’s strained smile, Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Tang Ye is the youngest student in my study hall. His handwriting is quite good.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Hearing this, Madam Zhang’s face immediately broke into a smile.","She was happy both because of Chen Yi’s praise and because he remembered her son.","After a few humble remarks, the subtext of her words was a clear hope that Chen Yi would teach Tang Ye with great care, essentially wishing for Tang Ye to achieve success in the Calligraphy Dao.","\"Where there’s a will, there’s a way. Since your son has the heart for it, he will surely become a great talent.\"","It was a good thing Chen Yi added the word \"great,\" otherwise the statement might have sounded a bit arrogant.","Madam Zhang’s smile became even more dignified. \"Ye’er doesn’t need to achieve something as extraordinary as Mr. Qingzhou. A little talent would be enough.\"","This, of course, was another humble remark.","After all, in a great clan like the Tang Family, a little talent could only ensure the family’s status wouldn’t decline for a time.","Only a person of great talent could take the family to the next level.","Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er were both well aware of this, so they exchanged a few pleasantries and let the topic pass lightly.","During this time, the other two ladies also spoke up.","Madam Sun came from a humbler background; at least, compared to the Xiao Family and the Tang Family, her Bai Family was only a minor clan.","However, her husband’s position as the Grain and Grass Supervisor for the Dingyuan Army was an extremely important office.","Even the Old Master and Xiao Jinghong would see the value in winning him over.","Therefore, Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er naturally had no intention of slighting her.","At the very least, Xiao Wan’er, having been immersed in her family’s affairs, would not slight Madam Sun.","As for Madam Sun’s request, it was also very simple.","She just hoped that her son, Bai Yutang, could enter that study hall and learn the Calligraphy Dao from Chen Yi.","Although she put it tactfully, Chen Yi knew in his heart that her son had likely looked down on him before.","’To put it nicely, it was a case of \"scholars scorn each other,\" or \"there is no first place in literature.\" To put it bluntly, it was more like, ’What can a live-in son-in-law possibly teach anyone?’’","Therefore, Chen Yi did not agree, instead deferring the matter to Mr. Yue Ming and others at the academy, thus tactfully refusing her."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159 - 150: A Gentleman Is Not Allowed to Woo (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Madam Sun was also well aware of her own child’s situation, so although she was somewhat disappointed, she didn’t press the matter.","It seemed she planned to find other connections. In any case, she was determined to get her child into the academy.","The reason was simple.","The emergence of a student who had achieved Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao at Guiyun Academy today was simply too shocking.","The more discerning scholars were, the more clearly they understood the difficulty of mastering the Calligraphy Dao.","Natural talent, hard work, Opportunity, and the guidance of a master teacher—not a single one could be missing.","Clearly, in the eyes of the Noble Families who had pieced together the situation in such a short time, Chen Yi was the very embodiment of that \"Opportunity\" and \"master teacher.\"","No one wanted to miss an opportunity like this.","Even if the chance was only one in a hundred, or even one in ten thousand.","As for the final guest, the young lady of the Wan Family, Miss Wan Rourou.","She, on the other hand, seemed to have come just for a casual visit, merely echoing Xiao Wan’er’s words the entire time.","When Chen Yi’s name came up, she never mentioned whether any of her own family members were studying at Guiyun Academy.","She only offered a few words of praise for Mr. Qingzhou’s great talent, remarking that while there had been many teachers of Calligraphy throughout history, teachers of the Calligraphy Dao were exceedingly rare.","It was almost as if she had come specifically to play the supporting role for the Xiao Family.","However, Chen Yi knew Wan Rourou must have had a purpose for visiting the Xiao Family this time.","He suspected it had something to do with the \"murderer\" responsible for Liu Jing’s death, whom the Imprisonment Department had just found.","After all, the culprit was a Guard from the Wan Family’s Nianlin Hall.","With this in mind, Chen Yi couldn’t help but glance at Wan Rourou a few more times, waiting to see when she would reveal her purpose.","But he didn’t get a chance to hear from Wan Rourou. Instead, he received a reproachful glare from Xiao Wan’er, who had noticed his unusual gaze.","Chen Yi knew she had misunderstood and reined himself in.","’You’re the patient. Whatever you say goes.’","Thus, the host and guests were all pleased.","As evening approached, Madam Zhang and Madam Sun left one after the other. Both had gained something from the visit, so they were naturally in high spirits.","And surprisingly, Wan Rourou also took her leave.","From start to finish, she never uttered a single word about Nianlin Hall or Guiyun Academy.","This left Chen Yi’s suspicions unfounded.","After seeing all the guests off, Xiao Wan’er didn’t return to Jiaxing Garden, but came back to Spring Lotus Garden instead.","While instructing Xiaodie and Cui’er to prepare dinner, she fixed her bright, beautiful eyes on Chen Yi.","Once Xiaodie and the others were gone.","Chen Yi met Xiao Wan’er’s gaze, glanced down at his clothes, and asked with a smile,","\"Is something wrong?\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er didn’t answer. She simply sat at the stone table in the pavilion, sizing him up as if meeting him for the very first time.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. He had a few suspicions, so he smiled and sat down beside her.","\"What happened at the academy was just an accident.\"","\"It’s true that I taught them the Calligraphy Dao, but the first class was just a general overview, meant only to introduce them to the entry-level path.\"","\"I was just as surprised as anyone when a student suddenly achieved Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao. It’s also a bit of a headache. We’ll be having a lot more visitors like the ones today.\"","\"And over at the academy, Mr. Yue Ming, the others, the students... I doubt they’ll let me have a moment’s peace either.\"","When he was done, however, Xiao Wan’er didn’t follow up on that topic. Instead, she asked,","\"Why were you staring at Miss Wan?\"","\"Er...\"","Chen Yi paused, then it dawned on him. \"So that’s why you were staring at me? You were mulling that over?\"","Xiao Wan’er’s pretty face flushed, but she forced herself to keep a stern expression. \"Who was staring at you?\"","\"We had guests earlier. It’s not proper for you to be staring at Rourou like that.\"","\"If word gets out, people might think... they might think that you and my sister aren’t getting along.\"","Chen Yi broke into a laugh. He said nothing, simply staring at her.","One second, two seconds, three seconds passed...","Xiao Wan’er shot him a glare, her face flushing an even deeper red as she turned away. She stubbornly kept muttering about how improper it was.","Then, she began to explain with painstaking earnestness:","\"Miss Wan is a bit older than me. The reason she’s still unmarried isn’t because she was never betrothed.\"","\"It’s because her fiancé, the Young Master of the Wang Family, passed away from an illness ten years ago. That’s why she...\"","At this, Xiao Wan’er caught Chen Yi’s teasing smile out of the corner of her eye and couldn’t help but chide, \"Are you even listening to me?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"Of course I’m listening. It’s just...\"","He paused, a mischievous glint in his eye, and changed the subject. \"It’s just... ’A fair maiden is a gentleman’s desire,’ and I...\"","Before he could finish, Xiao Wan’er whipped her head around to stare right at him, her voice urgent.","\"How can you say something like that out loud?\"","\"What ’fair maiden’? What ’gentleman’s desire’? I forbid it!\"","When she saw the clear mischief in Chen Yi’s eyes, Xiao Wan’er realized she’d been had, and her face turned an even brighter shade of crimson.","Even her eyes were slightly bloodshot.","’It’s either from embarrassment or anger,’ he guessed.","Chen Yi couldn’t be sure which, so he dropped the teasing mood, his smile fading as he began to explain.","\"I happened to run into some men from the Imprisonment Department outside the estate gates earlier.\"","\"They said the Imprisonment Department has already found the man who murdered Liu Jing. His identity? A Guard from Nianlin Hall.\"","\"I also heard them say Nianlin Hall is a Wan Family business. That’s why when I saw Miss Wan Rourou, I couldn’t help but stare a little.\"","After listening to his explanation, Xiao Wan’er finally understood.","But the conversation they’d just had was still echoing in her mind.","And it wasn’t just Chen Yi’s teasing; it was her own overreaction that stood out more.","It was mostly shyness, embarrassment, humiliation...","Humiliation, which eventually curdled into a bit of anger.","Not at Chen Yi, but at herself for her momentary lapse in composure.","Xiao Wan’er stopped thinking about it. After a moment of silence, she turned away, rose from her seat, and walked out of the pavilion, calling back over her shoulder without turning around,"]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160 - 150: Gentlemen Are Not Allowed to Woo (Part 3)","paragraphs":["\"Alright.\"","\"You’ve had a busy day. Get some rest. I’m heading back.\"","Chen Yi watched her walk away, surprised. \"Wan’er, didn’t you just tell Xiaodie and Cui’er to get dinner ready here?\"","But when she heard him, Xiao Wan’er only faltered for a second before her pace quickened abruptly.","If not for her somewhat frail constitution, she probably would have broken into a run all the way back to Jiaxing Garden.","’This man... I’m ignoring him.’","’Let him go play \"fair lady, worthy suitor\" all by himself.’","It would have been fine if she hadn’t thought of that line, but as soon as she did, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but think of that poem.","The thought made her burn with embarrassment all over again...","It was enough to make her forget her frail health and break into a light run back to Jiaxing Garden.","She’d taken it to heart after all.","As Xiao Wan’er’s figure vanished at the end of the long corridor, Chen Yi smiled and looked away. He shrugged and muttered to himself.","The gist of it was that Wan’er couldn’t take a joke.","Of course, those were words he could only say to himself.","If he actually said it to Xiao Wan’er’s face, he’d get an earful of complaints and a lecture at the very least.","However, from what Chen Yi knew of Xiao Wan’er, he was sure she wouldn’t get truly angry.","At most, she’d give him the silent treatment. She wasn’t even the type to hide a soft heart behind a sharp tongue.","At dinnertime, Xiao Wan’er, as expected, did not show up.","Furthermore, when she instructed Cui’er to serve dinner in Jiaxing Garden, she specifically had Pei Guanli and Xiao Wuge stay and eat with her.","As a result, only Chen Yi and Xiaodie, master and servant, were left in Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiaodie, of course, didn’t think much of it. Instead, she felt that eating with the Young Master was like returning to the days when he was under house arrest.","Back then, just like tonight, the two of them would eat while discussing which dishes were delicious and which weren’t cooked quite right.","As they talked and laughed, the sky grew dark.","Pei Guanli came skipping over, the bell on her neck swaying and ringing, JINGLE JINGLE JINGLE. She was clearly in a good mood.","\"Brother-in-law, did you make Wan’er angry again?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Why do you say that? Did your sister say something tonight?\"","Pei Guanli chuckled. \"Sister Wan’er didn’t mention you, Brother-in-law, but she kept going on about Wuge, telling him not to learn any bad habits from a certain Academy Master.\"","\"’Learning Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting is fine,’ she said, ’but he absolutely cannot learn Poetry.’ She even said she wants to hire a tutor to teach Wuge proper etiquette.\"","...","’Xiao Wan’er must be really annoyed this time,’ Chen Yi thought.","’Looks like I’ll have to add a few days to my ’silent treatment’ prediction.’","Last time, when he saw a few things he shouldn’t have while treating her, Xiao Wan’er had ignored him for the better part of a day.","’This time, will it be a full day?’","’Maybe two days. Or even three.’","As Chen Yi was thinking this, he changed the subject. \"Weren’t you supposed to have a duel with Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun today? How did it go?\"","The smile on Pei Guanli’s face vanished instantly. She puffed out her cheeks and glared at him.","\"Brother-in-law, now I know why Sister Wan’er didn’t let you come over for dinner.\"","\"You really know how to touch a sore spot.\"","Chen Yi flicked her on the forehead. \"So you lost. It’s nothing to be ashamed of.\"","He couldn’t do anything about Xiao Wan’er.","But he could still handle this Tiger Girl.","Pei Guanli rubbed her forehead, saying sullenly, \"I did lose. Even without using True Essence and only comparing Techniques, I still lost.\"","Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh out loud at the thought of it.","\"Your Cultivation is still lacking. It’s normal that your Cultivation and Technique can’t compare to that pair of martial sisters.\"","Pei Guanli’s eyes glistened with unshed tears as she stared at him intently. \"Brother-in-law, helpmehelpmehelpme...\"","She must have said \"help\" twenty times in a single breath.","Chen Yi shot her a look and said irritably, \"Help with what? I’m just a frail scholar. What am I going to do, write a letter of challenge for you?\"","Pei Guanli pouted. Knowing he didn’t want to expose his abilities, her whole posture seemed to slump.","Seeing this, Chen Yi shook his head helplessly. He raised a hand, dipped his finger in some water, and wrote a few words on the table.","\"Cultivate first. We’ll talk when an opportunity arises.\"","After Pei Guanli read it, the sadness on her face was instantly swept away. She grinned and said, \"I knew you were the best, Brother-in-law! You dote on me the most!\"","\"...Honestly.\"","...","「In the blink of an eye, a few days passed.」","August was approaching, and the weather in Shu State was as scorching as a furnace.","Even a Martial Artist like Chen Yi, whose Cultivation was by no means weak, could feel the oppressive heat—let alone anyone else.","Xiao Wuge was the first to succumb. He moved to Jiaxing Garden overnight, claiming it was cooler being closer to Xiao Wan’er.","This earned him a couple of playful swats from Xiao Wan’er, but in the end, she had to let him have his way.","Because of this, however, with Xiao Wuge no longer acting as a messenger between them, the two residences of Jiaxing Garden and Spring Lotus Garden, separated only by a wall, seemed to have lost all contact.","For several days, there was no news from either side.","To be precise, Chen Yi could occasionally overhear Xiao Wan’er’s words thanks to his sharp hearing.","Whether Xiao Wan’er could hear what he said, however, was unknown.","In any case, because of the matter with Miss Wan Rourou, Xiao Wan’er still remembered that line: \"fair lady, worthy suitor.\"","On another note, there had also been plenty of good news in the estate these past few days.","First, on the day after Liu Si of the Imprisonment Department came to visit, the tense atmosphere within the Xiao Family eased.","Though nothing was said outright, it seemed the conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families would unfold toward a stable resolution.","Chen Yi was well aware of why.","As long as the Jing State Liu Family accepted that the \"murderer\" was not one of the Xiao family, there would be no major conflict between the Xiao and Liu Families.","Even if they didn’t accept it, Liu Hong, the Governor of Shu State, could no longer press the Old Master any further.","This much was clear from a recent letter from Li Huai’gu:","\"The department reports that the summer grain tax for the Three Towns will be calculated at the lowest rate of one-twentieth.\"","That’s roughly one hundred thousand shi of grain.","All told, that’s a five-fold difference.","Presumably, even if the Xiao Family and the Three Towns were reluctant, they would still pay this grain tax."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161 - 150: A Gentleman Is Forbidden to Court","paragraphs":["The second piece of good news came during the final days of July: the profit share from Hundred Herbs Hall for the Xiao Family Medicine Hall had arrived.","A total of 33,000 silver’s worth of tea drinks were sold. After deducting costs and applying the fifty-percent profit share, the Xiao Family earned a profit of 14,000 silver.","Wang Ji said that when Xiao Wan’er saw the silver notes, she was stunned for a moment and asked with a strange expression if the calculations were wrong.","Apparently, she wasn’t surprised by the amount of money, but by how incredibly low the cost of the tea drinks was.","Chen Yi, however, thought nothing of it.","If not for his fear of scaring Xiao Wan’er and the Xiao Family, that cost could have been slashed by another four thousand-some silver coins.","That’s right. For over thirty thousand silver’s worth of tea drinks sold, the production cost was less than one thousand silver.","Five hundred and thirty-two silver, to be exact.","The rest was the cost of hiring workers, building a warehouse, and transportation, which hardly cost anything at all.","Forget Xiao Wan’er—even Wang Ji found it hard to believe after calculating Hundred Herbs Hall’s profit for the month.","The profit was exactly thirty thousand silver.","And this was just the revenue from one Hundred Herbs Hall and the five Xiao Family Medicine Halls, all within the single prefecture of Shu State.","If he were to follow Chen Yi’s previous plan and open branches of Hundred Herbs Hall all over Shu State, or even throughout the Nine States and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty, the daily profit would be...","The moment Wang Ji considered that possibility, his eyes turned red.","Without needing any orders from Chen Yi, he decided to expand Hundred Herbs Hall into the neighboring prefectures and counties next month.","Chen Yi didn’t try to stop him, only reminding him to be mindful of his own safety.","He wasn’t worried about the recipe, however.","Even if someone managed to decipher it, they would still be a step behind Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, which had the first-mover advantage.","At worst, he could just develop a few more tea drink recipes, enhance their medicinal effects, and improve the flavor.","He could also continue using a distribution system, winning over the local Noble Families and gentry to grow Hundred Herbs Hall.","In short, he had plenty of ways to handle commercial competition.","The last piece of good news was that Xiao Jinghong had sent a letter back, saying that the surveying for the Mutual Market was finished and construction was about to begin.","The tentative start date was the first day of the eighth month.","Once the foundation for the Mutual Market was firmly laid, Xiao Jinghong would head back, aiming to return before the Mid-Autumn Festival.","It was also thanks to this occasion that Chen Yi saw Xiao Wan’er for the first time in four days.","It was a moderately good piece of news, all things considered.","At least the two of them were finally speaking to each other, weren’t they?","Besides all this, it wasn’t as if Chen Yi had been a complete shut-in these past few days.","While he had to avoid the endless stream of wives, young ladies, and high-status scholars who came to call on him, he also found time to follow up on some juicy bits of gossip and gain a few Opportunities.","Though they were all Yellow Level intelligence, the Opportunities were minor, and the rewards were low-grade Fist Techniques and Palm Techniques, but it was better than nothing.","Most crucially, that night, Chen Yi’s Cultivation broke through again, reaching the Upper Seventh Grade.","’Now that I’ve reached the Middle Three Grades, I’m considered a second-rate expert in the Jianghu.’","’If one of my Martial Arts reaches the Great Success stage, it’s like having one foot among the ranks of first-rate experts.’","Just like \"Sword Madman\" Liu Lang.","His Cultivation is only at the Fifth Grade Realm, but his Saber Dao has reached Great Success, making him a notable figure in the Jianghu.","If he broke through to the Upper Three Grades Realm, he would be considered a top-tier existence even among first-rate experts.","If his Saber Dao were to break through again, he could be called a \"regional hegemon,\" a name that would command great renown.","「Nearing the Zi hour.」","Chen Yi rose and walked to the window, gazing at the dimly lit Spring Lotus Garden as the night wind picked up. \"Ah, it’s going to rain.\"","Gazing at the scene, his expression remained calm, but thoughts began to stir within him.","’The Hidden Guard’s plot to sow discord between the Xiao and Liu Families failed.’","’Xiao Dongchen definitely won’t let this go. And Ge the Third... hmm... After he went to Yanhua Lane that day to buy that girl’s freedom, he moved out of the Xiao Mansion.’","’He must be busy plotting that business these days.’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi made a decision—he would take the opportunity of going to the academy to teach tomorrow to also make a trip to Hundred Herbs Hall.","’Liu Lang’s injuries have healed. It’s time to ask him about his progress.’","’And then there’s...’","Before he could finish the thought, a light appeared before his eyes—","[Daily Intelligence · Earth-level Lower Grade: At 10:15 PM, in a tailor shop in the West Market, Hidden Guards are plotting an important matter. A great Opportunity may be obtained.]"]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162 - 151: Paying Respect to the Mountain, the Gods and Buddhas, and the Evil Ghosts","paragraphs":["Earth-level Lower Grade.","Aside from not having seen intelligence of this grade for many days, Chen Yi was more concerned with its content.","At a time like this, the only major event the Hidden Guard could be plotting was likely the burning of the Three Towns.","’Ge the Third is helping Xiao Dongchen, distancing himself from the Xiao Mansion to the point of disregarding his own reputation.’","’He’s really gone to great lengths.’","’But I can’t shake the feeling that Ge the Third’s recent methods are a bit strange compared to before.’","Chen Yi clearly remembered that Ge the Third’s mission was supposed to be him, the \"Fledgling.\"","But recently, Ge the Third hadn’t appeared at the Marquis’s Mansion, and he had rarely even shown his face to Chen Yi.","As he thought about it, an idea sparked in his mind.","’Could my appointment as an Instructor at Guiyun Academy also be part of the Hidden Guard’s plan for me?’","’But according to my previous deductions, this \"Fledgling\" was supposed to make a name for himself within the Xiao Family and gradually build up power.’","’And to do that, I’d need a corresponding status, strength, and reputation or prestige...’","’Prestige?’","Chen Yi finally understood. A strange expression appeared on his face as he grinned.","’It’s actually quite possible.’","If he had just kept a low profile at Guiyun Academy, being an ordinary Instructor teaching Calligraphy, he naturally wouldn’t have gained any fame or prestige.","At most, he might have earned a reputation for being \"diligent and responsible.\"","But more likely, those with ulterior motives or people who disliked him would have labeled him as \"muddling through\" or \"lacking ambition.\"","There would have been no way to get a good reputation.","But the current situation was different—in just one lesson, he had taught a student to achieve success in the Calligraphy Dao.","He not only earned the approval of Mr. Yue Ming and others at the academy but also attracted visits from numerous Noble Families in Shu State.","For example, Madam Zhang of the Tang Family, Madam Sun of the Bai Family, and others.","Then there were the other great Noble Families who had sought out the Xiao Family these past few days.","In order to have their family’s children learn the Calligraphy Dao from him, they had truly stopped at nothing.","They hadn’t just approached Xiao Wan’er; people had even gone to the Old Master, Second Master Xiao Wang, and Third Master Xiao Shen.","With all this, even if Chen Yi were to now deny that Ma Guan’s Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao was his doing, it would probably be useless.","’A single miscalculation on my part actually gave the Hidden Guard the false impression that I intended to use Guiyun Academy to make a name for myself.’","After figuring it out, Chen Yi couldn’t help but give a wry, helpless smile.","His original intention was merely to teach something genuine, to allow those students a glimpse into the gateway of the Calligraphy Dao.","He had never expected things to unfold like this.","He pondered for a moment.","Chen Yi shook his head to himself. ’Still, this is good too.’","’If this can make the Hidden Guard shift their attention away from me for a while, it’s not a bad thing.’","’At least it’s better than the Hidden Guard coming to cause trouble time and again.’","Most importantly, he could take advantage of the misunderstanding to do other things in secret.","At this thought, Chen Yi confirmed the time for tomorrow night—the hour of Hai—and then resumed his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","’I have to go take a look to be at ease.’","...","「Half an hour later.」","Under a sky shrouded in dark clouds, just as Chen Yi had predicted, a heavy rain began to fall after a bout of thunder and lightning.","It brought a welcome cooldown to a Shu State that had been scorched by the sun for days.","Amidst the RUMBLING, the rain PATTERED and SPLASHED against the eaves and flagstones, creating a noisy din.","But when Liu Lang came to the window and saw the downpour outside Hundred Herbs Hall, he grinned in admiration. \"What great weather.\"","A torrential downpour like this was something he wouldn’t have dared to even imagine back when he was still in the Northern Desert.","Most of the time, the Northern Desert was under a blazing sun, and a hot wind would kick up endless yellow sand.","Forget rain; you were lucky if the heavens showed mercy and didn’t whip up a sandstorm.","But it was in that harsh environment that Liu Lang had managed to break through with his Saber Dao to the Great Success Realm.","As Liu Lang thought about the past, he suddenly sighed.","’In the end, I was just a frog in a well.’","’I deserved to be defeated in a single move.’","That night, Xiao Jinghong had been ruthless. He not only defeated him in one move but also completely shattered his arrogance.","Liu Lang recalled the fleeting brilliance of that blade strike. He felt a mix of awe and dejection, muttering to himself that it was useless to dwell on it.","One had to look forward.","Just as his master, \"Sword Ghost,\" had said, while you’re young, you should measure the world with your footsteps—travel far and see much.","If everything went smoothly along the way, then he should try to walk the path of invincibility.","If he encountered setbacks, it wasn’t a bad thing. As long as he was still alive, overcoming that hurdle would lead to a smooth road ahead.","’Master, you old man, you should have cut me down a notch back then. Then I wouldn’t have become so arrogant and conceited.’","When Liu Lang remembered what he had said to Black Tooth before, even his face, as thick as a city wall, couldn’t help but burn with shame.","\"The winner lives, the loser dies. This is called ’proving the Dao’.\"","’What kind of Dao was I proving?’","It was clearly just him having it easy for too long, underestimating the heroes of the world, and deluding himself into thinking he could walk the path of invincibility.","’I bet when Black Tooth sees me again, he won’t be able to resist mocking me.’","Liu Lang muttered to himself, grimacing as if he had a toothache. He then threw on a raincoat, put on a bamboo hat, and walked out of Hundred Herbs Hall.","He had now returned to his original appearance, but the cynical, arrogant smile was gone from his face.","In its place was only the composure of a man who had suffered a blow.","Even as he strolled through the downpour, he no longer swayed from side to side as he used to. Instead, he walked with steady steps, gradually disappearing into the night.","「About half an hour later.」","Liu Lang bypassed the West Market and arrived at a deep, dark alley in the west of the city, near Yanhua Lane.","This was a place where filth and corruption hid within Shu State Prefecture City.","It housed horse bandits from Poshisu Country, peddlers and porters who traveled year-round between the Barbarian Race and the Wei Dynasty, and also notorious villains wanted by the Jianghu.","In comparison, the people in the east of the city who had come to Shu State from elsewhere to make a living could be considered law-abiding citizens.","The reason these villains could hide here without being rounded up by the Government Office was, naturally, because they were protected by people who made a living from this sort of thing.","As the saying goes, money makes the world go round.","As long as enough silver was spent, forget just finding a hiding place for some villains—there were plenty of people willing to do even more vicious deeds.","Black Tooth was one of them.","He was not only the Chief Steward of this den of iniquity but also a member of the famous Jianghu organization, Bright Moon Building.","And he wasn’t just an ordinary member; he was the Elder in charge of all intelligence for Shu State.","Furthermore, because Black Tooth had a reputation for keeping his word, many Jianghu people who knew of him would come to \"pay their respects\" upon arriving in Shu State.","Even some Noble Families and people with official positions had close ties with him.","Just as Liu Jing of the Jing State Liu Family had relied on him to find Liu Lang and the people from the Illusory Sound Sect.","Similarly, Liu Lang had come here to find this very Black Tooth, a man with connections in both the light and the dark.","In the pouring rain, Liu Lang glanced around and then reached out to knock three times on a nearby wall.","Two long, one short—a request to see Black Tooth.","A moment later, an indifferent voice echoed in the alley. \"What is your mountain gate?\"","\"Northern Desert, Liu Lang.\"","\"Are you here to bow to the mountain gate, to the gods and buddhas, or to the evil ghosts?\"","Liu Lang paused, then clasped his hands. \"The evil ghosts.\"","To bow to the mountain gate meant seeking protection. To bow to the gods and buddhas meant the matter involved officialdom or the great families.","And to bow to the evil ghosts meant it was a matter of life and death.","Murder, arson, pillaging, and the like.","These were the rules of the Bright Moon Building, and they were also Black Tooth’s rules.","After hearing Liu Lang’s reply, the surroundings fell silent once more, leaving only the SPLASHING sound of the rain.","「About half an hour later.」","A person finally appeared. Without speaking, he simply beckoned to Liu Lang.","Liu Lang silently followed him, weaving through streets and alleys.","They left the area of dilapidated, low-slung houses and came to the brightly lit Yanhua Lane.","Liu Lang scanned his surroundings, a hint of emotion showing on his calm face. ’Black Tooth is Black Tooth, all right. He even has businesses here.’","’It made sense upon reflection.’","’For these people hiding in the darkness, establishments like the Qin Building and gambling dens were not only their money-makers but also their hiding places and their public fronts.’","When the black-clothed man led him to the Spring Rain Building, Liu Lang couldn’t help but smile even more brightly.","’Son of a bitch, good thing I got a freebie last time, or I would’ve been at a loss.’","「Not long after.」","Liu Lang went through the back door of the Spring Rain Building and made his way to a hidden room on the top floor.","Along the way, he didn’t see a single girl, not even a shadow of another person.","’It really is well-hidden.’","Liu Lang sized up his surroundings and said with a laugh, \"Black Tooth, making me wait in the rain for half an hour is hardly your way of treating a guest.\"","The words had barely left his mouth when a smooth section of the wall in the quiet room slowly opened, and a slender figure dressed in black brocade walked out.","But his face was covered by an opera mask, revealing only a pair of eyes.","The wall slid shut, becoming seamless again.","Only then did the man speak. \"What kind of guest are you?\"","\"I told you back then not to go looking for Xiao Jinghong. You didn’t listen, causing the Liu Family’s plan to fail and costing me a hefty sum of silver.\"","Liu Lang took off his bamboo hat, set it aside, and said with a smile:","\"With Xie Tingyun of the Celestial Sect helping the Xiao Family, the Liu Family’s affair would have failed even if I had been here.\"","He said this, but inwardly he was thinking of the mysterious owner of Hundred Herbs Hall.","’With that person’s Medical Dao, who’s to say he couldn’t find an even more powerful Wandering Martial Artist?’","Black Tooth snorted, looking him up and down. \"Your injuries have healed?\"","\"I haven’t heard of any ’Divine Doctor’ passing through Shu State recently. Who treated you?\"","\"Take a guess.\"","\"Hah. Looks to me like Xiao Jinghong knocked your brains loose, too.\"","Liu Lang shook his head noncommittally. \"It’s not convenient for me to tell you that person’s identity.\"","He paused, then continued, \"I didn’t come here today for idle chat. Let’s talk business.\"","\"Fine. You’re the employer, you call the shots. So, who do you want to kill?\"","\"I’m not here to kill anyone.\"","Black Tooth’s eyes instantly turned cold. He stared at him and said icily, \"The evil ghosts have been summoned. If you’re not here to kill someone, then I’ll kill you.\"","Liu Lang smiled, unhurriedly taking a silver note from his robes and slapping it on the table.","\"Isn’t there another part to that? ’Money can make even a ghost push a millstone’?\"","Black Tooth didn’t speak, nor did he look at the silver note on the table. His gaze only grew colder.","Seeing this, Liu Lang stopped beating around the bush and said directly, \"I want to burn the summer grain in the Three Towns. Name your price.\"","Black Tooth was slightly stunned, asking in surprise, \"The Three Towns of Shu State?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"I’m not taking the job.\"","\"Why not? With your money-grubbing nature, how could you refuse?\"","\"Because someone has already offered more money to do the same thing—burn the summer grain in the Three Towns.\"","Liu Lang’s brow furrowed slightly. \"Is that true?\"","Black Tooth nodded. His gaze fell on the silver note on the table, and he reached out to pick it up, waving it slightly as he spoke:","\"Now it’s my turn to ask you.\"","\"Are you willing to take a piece of this business?\""]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163 - 152: A Woman’s Heart is a Needle at the Bottom of the Sea","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, lightning flashed and thunder roared.","The downpour had lasted for six hours, and far from letting up, it was only growing stronger.","BOOMING thunder echoed intermittently, cracking across the overcast sky and startling the people of Shu State from their sleep.","Xiao Wuge was one of them.","It wasn’t that he was afraid, but weather like this always brought back unpleasant memories.","He sat up and looked around. The candle in the dim room had long since gone out, and only the occasional flash of lightning offered a brief moment of illumination.","It was enough to remind him that he was in Jiaxing Garden, not Spring Lotus Garden.","He sat there for a moment, dazed.","Xiao Wuge climbed out of bed, struggled into a long robe, and headed outside.","The loose robe, without its sash tied, hung sloppily on his frame.","\"Young Master, you’re awake?\"","Cui’er, who was on duty outside the door, heard the noise. Turning to see him, she hurried over to straighten his clothes and tie his sash before using a warm, damp towel to help him wash his face.","Sensing that Xiao Wuge wanted to go out, Cui’er quickened her pace and asked with a smile,","\"Is the Young Master going to find the Eldest Miss?\"","Xiao Wuge looked at the raging storm outside the window and shook his head. \"It’s not hot anymore. I’m going to Spring Lotus Garden to find my brother-in-law.\"","Cui’er smiled and nodded reassuringly. \"Then let me finish getting you dressed, and I’ll take you to Spring Lotus Garden to find Master Chen.\"","\"Master Chen is going to Guiyun Academy today, so he should be awake and having breakfast by now.\"","\"Oh, I’ll go eat there too.\"","Once his clothes were in order, the two of them went downstairs.","Xiao Wan’er was sitting in the main hall, looking out the door. When she saw them, she said with a gentle smile,","\"Wuge, you must be hungry. I’ve already told Juan’er to bring breakfast from the kitchen. It will be here in a moment.\"","Xiao Wuge shook his head again. \"Big Sister, I’m going to Spring Lotus Garden to eat with Brother-in-law.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s smile faltered. \"The rain is so heavy right now, it would be very inconvenient. It’s not too late to go after you finish breakfast.\"","\"But if I’m too late, Brother-in-law will have already left the mansion for Guiyun Academy.\"","Seeing how earnest he was, Xiao Wan’er hesitated for a moment before standing up as well.","\"In that case, I’ll take you there, so you don’t slip and fall on the wet paths.\"","Although Xiao Wuge felt it was a little inappropriate to be treated like a child, he was still happy to be returning to Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wan’er had Cui’er fetch a raincoat and help Xiao Wuge put it on. Then, holding an oil-paper umbrella, she led him out of the wooden building toward Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wan’er carefully avoided the puddles while sheltering Xiao Wuge, saying with a laugh,","\"When the weather was hot, you ran over to Jiaxing Garden. Now that it’s cooled down a bit, you’re running right back to Spring Lotus Garden.\"","\"You really treat your big sister like a fan, only useful in the summer.\"","Xiao Wuge knew she wasn’t actually angry, so he just chuckled sheepishly.","\"Go on, laugh.\"","Xiao Wan’er poked him on the head, but she could only indulge him and continue on their way.","However, as they neared Spring Lotus Garden, Xiao Wan’er began to hesitate.","Over the past few days, aside from meeting yesterday because of a letter from Xiao Jinghong, she and Chen Yi had had no contact whatsoever.","Most of the time, she only heard about what Chen Yi was doing from Xiao Wuge.","Playing chess, practicing calligraphy, drinking tea, fishing.","Occasionally, he would go out for a stroll.","For instance, he’d gone to the West Market to watch a couple from out of town argue, or to North City to see two scholars compete in a couplet duel.","Another time, in the East Market, he saw a Barbarian Race laborer who had tried to escape get caught and whipped.","All in all, his life was far more leisurely than that of the Eldest Miss of the Marquis’s Mansion, as if he didn’t have a single care in the world.","When Xiao Wan’er heard these things, she couldn’t help the strange thoughts that arose in her mind.","Every time she recalled the events of that day, she wondered if she had overreacted, if she had read too much into things.","Other than his comment—\"A fair maiden is a gentleman’s desire\"—her brother-in-law hadn’t done anything else out of line.","Even his lingering glances at Miss Wan Rourou were because the Imprisonment Department had just caught Liu Jing’s murderer.","This point had been confirmed by the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office in the last two days.","The Old Master had even lifted the lockdown on the mansion because of it.","Thinking about all this, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but be reflective.","The more she thought about it, the more it seemed she really had overreacted.","And yet, when she had seen Chen Yi yesterday, the words of explanation on the tip of her tongue were swallowed back down.","Then, for some inexplicable reason, she had said a few things that sounded like a lecture.","Things about paying attention to propriety, a gentleman’s conduct, and so on.","Xiao Wan’er didn’t even know why she had said such things, and she couldn’t help but feel they were inappropriate in hindsight.","It had gotten to her so much that she hadn’t slept well last night.","When the thunder began to boom in the middle of the night, it became even harder for her to fall asleep.","Absorbed in these thoughts, Xiao Wan’er looked down at Xiao Wuge and asked, \"Do I look unwell?\"","Xiao Wuge looked up at her and saw a face that was slightly pale, her eyes downcast.","\"Not at all. You look much better than you used to, Big Sister.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Xiao Wan’er breathed a sigh of relief, dispelling some of the clutter in her mind. A smile appeared on her face. \"Let’s go.\"","By the time the two of them arrived at Spring Lotus Garden, Chen Yi was just coming downstairs for breakfast.","He was a little surprised to see them, but his expression betrayed nothing.","He welcomed them inside while telling Xiaodie to add two more place settings.","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er swallowed the words she had been about to say—that she would return to Jiaxing Garden to eat—and sat down at the table with Xiao Wuge.","Looking around, she asked, \"Is Sister Guanli not up yet?\"","Chen Yi sat across from her, picking up a pastry from the table as he shook his head.","\"I just had Xiaodie check. She said she’s had a breakthrough in her Martial Arts and is focused on her cultivation.\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in acknowledgment. Noticing his eyes on her, she unconsciously lowered her head and focused on her congee.","She gave herself a silent pep talk.","’I should say something to smooth things over and just let this whole incident pass.’","But before she could figure out what to say, Chen Yi finished a pastry and asked with a smile,","\"Big Sister, you mentioned before that you wanted to meet the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall. Do you still want to?\"","His words broke her train of thought. She hesitated, then nodded.","\"Yes, I do.\"","\"After Wang Ji came over the day before yesterday and delivered such a large sum of silver coins, I feel I should thank him in person.\"","After she spoke, a flicker of doubt crossed Xiao Wan’er’s mind.","’It seems my brother-in-law hasn’t taken our previous disagreement to heart at all. His tone and attitude are exactly the same as before. It seems that \"fair maiden\" comment was truly just an offhand joke. So, I was just overthinking everything?’","At this thought, the corners of Xiao Wan’er’s mouth turned down in a pout.","A rare, seldom-seen expression of playful reproach—not quite resentment, but close—appeared on her face.","Just then, Chen Yi happened to look up and catch her expression, leaving him slightly baffled.","He looked down at his own clothes. ’Nothing wrong here.’","He was dressed in white robes, his hair was neatly combed—the very picture of a refined and easy-going scholar.","\"Big Sister, is there something else you need?\"","Caught by him, Xiao Wan’er composed herself, replied that it was nothing, and lowered her head to continue eating.","\"...\"","Chen Yi glanced at her, then at the oblivious Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie. Seeing nothing out of the ordinary with them, he couldn’t help but wonder,","’Did I just see that wrong?’","Just then, Xiao Wan’er put down her bowl and chopsticks and said in a calm tone,","\"Second Sister’s letter arrived yesterday. I plan on writing a reply to her today. Brother-in-law, once you return from the West Market, you can give me your letter as well. I’ll have someone deliver them together.\"","Chen Yi nodded. ’I must have imagined it,’ he thought. ’We just smoothed things over yesterday, and I haven’t said anything today that could possibly have displeased her.’","But the moment that thought crossed his mind, he heard Xiao Wan’er say,","\"Wuge, after you finish eating, remember to change into more formal clothes.\"","\"The etiquette tutor I hired for you is coming today. You mustn’t be impolite.\"","Xiao Wuge froze. Seeing her serious expression, which didn’t seem to be a joke, he could only nod. \"I know, Sis.\"","As he said this, he shot Chen Yi a look of utter despair.","It was the exact same expression Pei Guanli had worn yesterday when she’d repeated the word \"help\" twenty times in a single breath.","Chen Yi shrugged, helpless.","Clearly, he had just done *something* to upset Xiao Wan’er, so there was no way he could help Xiao Wuge now.","’But... I didn’t say anything, did I?’","After wracking his brain, Chen Yi still couldn’t figure it out, so he simply chalked it up to Xiao Wan’er still holding a grudge about their earlier disagreement.","’A woman’s heart is a needle in the ocean. The ancestors were right all along.’","Not long after, they finished breakfast. When Xiaodie offered to call for a carriage, Chen Yi waved her off. He grabbed an oil-paper umbrella, intending to go to the front courtyard himself and see if any were available.","After bidding farewell to Xiao Wan’er and the others, he left Spring Lotus Garden.","Xiao Wan’er watched him walk into the distance. The tense look on her face softened, and she let out a faint, melancholic sigh.","’It seems I’ve done something inexplicable again. I had it all planned out before I came. I was going to smooth things over with my brother-in-law, but instead...’","Xiao Wuge studied her face. Seeing her brow slightly furrowed, he couldn’t help but ask,","\"Big Sister, you don’t look so well. Are you feeling alright?\"","Xiao Wan’er snapped out of her thoughts and turned to him. \"I... I don’t look well?\"","\"A little. A bit worse than just now.\"","\"Is that so? It’s probably just because I’m worried about your lessons and your etiquette. When the tutor arrives, I’ll have Cui’er stay with you.\"","\"...\"","’Stay with me?’","’More like keep an eye on me.’","At this thought, a worried frown that didn’t quite suit his young age creased Xiao Wuge’s face.","’Why did I have to open my big mouth and ask?’","Xiao Wan’er glanced at him, her mood seeming to lift slightly. After giving a few instructions, she headed straight for Jiaxing Garden.","’Next time.’","’Next time, I will smooth things over with him. I’ll put all of this behind us.’","...","Chen Yi reached the front courtyard and saw that the mansion’s Armored Warriors were all present.","Even Ge the Third, whom he hadn’t seen in days, was there.","It seemed Ge the Third was being teased by Liu Si’er and the others about a recent event.","\"So, Third, how’s married life treating you?\"","\"Wonderful. Simply wonderful.\"","\"You son of a bitch, I can’t believe you actually went through with it. You’re lucky the Marquis didn’t have your head.\"","\"Heh heh...\"","Ge the Third was about to retort when he saw Chen Yi and quickly called out a greeting,","\"Master Chen, heading out?\"","\"Yes, to Guiyun Academy.\""]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164 - 153: The Jing State Liu Family","paragraphs":["Amidst Ge the Third’s joking complaints, Liu Si’er and the others didn’t argue with him about who would take Chen Yi to Guiyun Academy.","Chen Yi, naturally, didn’t specify who should be his driver, letting Ge the Third go to the stables to prepare.","While waiting, Chen Yi made some small talk with Liu Si’er and the others.","\"Oh? So the tense atmosphere in the mansion a few days ago was because that disciple from the Jing State Liu Family died in Shu State?\"","\"Someone from the Wan Family killed him? How could that be?\"","\"Young Master, you might not understand the situation in Shu State. The Wan Family is also a major clan here, and they’ve always been in the Medicine Hall business.\"","\"When our mansion opened its own Medicine Hall, the head of the Wan Family specifically came to request an audience with the Marquis. The seeds of disaster were likely sown back then.\"","Hearing Liu Si’er’s explanation, Chen Yi smiled and asked, \"Are you saying the Wan Family deliberately killed someone to sow discord between the Xiao and Liu Families?\"","\"It’s hard to say. But for now, the Prefectural Magistrate’s Office and the Imprisonment Department have already convicted the murderer. He’ll be executed as soon as someone from the Liu Family arrives. They probably don’t want any more complications.\"","An Armored Warrior nearby, listening to their conversation, couldn’t help but chime in, \"The way I see it, the Wan Family was behind it, but their plot was exposed.\"","\"I think so too.\"","\"If the Wan Family’s scheme had succeeded, even if we didn’t completely fall out with the Jing State Liu Family, it would have created a hidden danger.\"","\"I heard that even the Lord Governor initially thought our mansion was responsible.\"","\"Yeah, but luckily the misunderstanding has been cleared up.\"","Listening to their words, Chen Yi got a general idea of the Government Office’s investigation and felt a strange mix of emotions.","’Although he didn’t know the \"murderer’s\" situation or what arrangements the Old Master had made, this whole affair was ultimately because of him.’","’It was still a human life.’","’And it had dragged the Wan Family into it.’","Thinking about this, Chen Yi sighed inwardly. ’I might have to do something about this.’","’The Liu Family, the Liu Family, the Liu Family.’","Just as he was lost in thought, Ge the Third led the carriage over. \"Young Master, let’s get going.\"","\"This rain isn’t going to let up anytime soon. We should head out early to avoid any mishaps on the way.\"","Chen Yi came back to his senses, nodded a greeting to the surrounding Armored Warriors on guard, and then boarded the carriage, which made its way out of the Marquis’s Mansion.","He looked out the window. Under the onslaught of the downpour, most of the pedestrians on the road were hurrying past.","Occasionally, a few scholars or young ladies who enjoyed rainy days would be strolling among them, treating it as an elegant affair.","After watching for a moment, Chen Yi asked, \"Old Third, I heard from Brother Si and the others that the murderer who killed Liu Jing is going to be executed soon?\"","Ge the Third, who was carefully holding the reins and controlling the carriage’s speed, heard this and turned his head with a smile.","\"Young Master, for a vicious killer like that, the fact that the Lord Prefect isn’t having him drawn and quartered is already a sign of mercy.\"","\"If it weren’t for him this time, the Liu Family would have definitely clashed with us. The grain tax of the Three Towns is just one thing, and it’s just a small trick from the Governor of Shu State.\"","\"If the Jing State Liu Family refused to let it go, the consequences would have been severe.\"","Chen Yi made a sound of understanding. \"So, the Jing State Liu Family is quite powerful.\"","\"You can say that again.\"","\"Don’t be fooled by the fact that no one in the Liu Family’s main branch holds an official post. The second and third branches, as well as the side branches, all have capable people.\"","\"For example, the third branch’s Chief Steward, Liu Hong, is our Left Governor of Shu State, in charge of the state’s finances, taxes, and civil affairs. And speaking of which, the Lord Prefect Liu Si is also related to the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"Then there’s Liu Zhen from the second branch. He’s the Jing State Imprisonment Department Governor. That man is a baleful star—I heard he ransacked the homes of several great clans in Jing State.\"","\"And there’s another one: Consort Yi, Liu Xiangning, who currently holds the Holy Emperor’s favor. She’s another pillar of support for the Jing State Liu Family...\"","Listening to Ge the Third list them off as if counting his family treasures, Chen Yi gained a clear understanding of the Jing State Liu Family.","’Their power might not necessarily be greater than the Xiao Family’s, but their network is extremely wide, with many entanglements behind the scenes.’","’If they were to truly have it out with the Xiao Family, it’s hard to say if both sides would be devastated, but it would definitely alarm the Holy Emperor.’","’Given the Xiao Family’s current situation, the Holy Emperor probably wouldn’t even be able to treat them equally.’","’No wonder the Xiao Family was so tense when Liu Jing died.’","Thinking about this, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"Old Third, you seem to know a lot about these things. How do you know so much?\"","Ge the Third chuckled. \"It’s what’s been going around the mansion these past few days. I just picked up a little here and there.\"","\"Is that so? I thought since you just got married, you’d be lost in the land of love.\"","\"Young Master, please spare me! Don’t let a word of this reach the masters and misses.\"","\"Haha, of course not...\"","After a bit of idle chat, Ge the Third steered the conversation toward Chen Yi, praising him.","\"Young Master, your reputation has really exploded recently.\"","\"A while ago, I heard you were going to be an Instructor at the academy. I thought you were just going there to relax. I never would have imagined you’d produce a student who achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao after just one lesson.\"","\"You have no idea how much of a sensation it’s caused in the city these past few days. They say most of the Noble Families in all of Shu State have already heard about it.\"","Chen Yi asked noncommittally, \"Who, for instance?\"","’Ge the Third’s words just confirmed his suspicions. People really thought he was trying to make a name for himself through Guiyun Academy.’","\"Oh, plenty! I’ve heard of at least ten myself recently. And some famous Calligraphy masters who’ve been renowned for a long time are even planning to come to Shu State...\"","As Ge the Third continued, Chen Yi realized he had still underestimated the impact of Ma Guan achieving success in the Calligraphy Dao.","’After fermenting for a few days, the news has likely spread not just through the Prefecture City, but to all the scholars in Shu State.’","’Even the neighboring Jing State and You State have probably heard the news, thanks to those with a mind to spread it.’","’The direct impact, aside from the Noble Families who had been visiting the Marquis’s Mansion day after day, was that these people were now showing up at Guiyun Academy’s gates.’","’Mr. Yue Ming and the others must have talked themselves hoarse these past few days.’","’As for those so-called Calligraphy masters, most of them had fame that far outstripped their achievements in the Calligraphy Dao.’","’Just like Mr. Yue Ming. He’s a Calligraphy master, through and through.’","’But his Calligraphy Dao hasn’t even stabilized at the level of Minor Success.’","’It was predictable that for a long time to come, even more people would be drawn here by the reputation he’d gained.’","Before long, the carriage stopped outside Guiyun Academy.","Chen Yi told Ge the Third to head straight back to the mansion, then walked into the academy alone, holding an umbrella.","As soon as he approached, he saw the student guards at the gate bowing to him from a distance.","\"Student greets Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"Morning.\"","Chen Yi casually said the word \"morning,\" gave a nod by way of greeting, and walked straight into the academy.","Such behavior, which didn’t conform to etiquette and wasn’t befitting of a scholar, naturally surprised the students.","In the past, he would have likely been slapped with the label of \"disrespectful.\"","But now, what were the students saying?","\"Mr. Qingzhou is truly worthy of being a teacher who can produce a student successful in the Calligraphy Dao. So unconcerned with trivial formalities.\"","\"Exactly. You can see it in Mr. Qingzhou’s characters—so free and easy, so nonchalant. Every stroke exudes an air of transcendent detachment.\"","\"This must be what Mr. Qingzhou meant by ’the calligraphy and the person become one,’ right?\"","Chen Yi heard the discussion behind him but paid it no mind, walking straight toward the study hall.","Just then, Ma Guan came running toward him.","\"Student greets Teacher.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and kept walking forward without stopping.","But before he had taken two steps, he saw Ma Guan jog to a stop in front of him.","\"What’s this? Now that you’ve achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao, you’re starting to disregard me?\"","Who would have thought this one joking remark would scare Ma Guan so badly that sweat beaded on his forehead? He hurriedly bowed deeply in a grand salute.","\"Teacher, please forgive me! This student would never dare!\"","Chen Yi paused. Remembering Ma Guan’s upright and proper personality, he realized he had taken the joke too far.","\"Alright, stand up and talk. It was just a joke. Look how scared you are.\"","Hearing this, Ma Guan cautiously raised his head and glanced at his face. Seeing no trace of anger, he couldn’t help but breathe a sigh of relief.","\"Student thanks Teacher.\"","\"So, what is it?\"","\"Student wanted to inform Teacher that today’s Calligraphy class has been moved to another location. The Dean ordered me to lead you there.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Moved where?\"","Ma Guan wiped the sweat from his forehead and stammered, \"It’s better if you see for yourself, Teacher. This student doesn’t dare say more.\"","Seeing this, how could Chen Yi not know that something had happened at the academy? And he guessed it probably wasn’t anything good.","Chen Yi thought for a moment, shook his head inwardly, and said, \"Let’s go.\"","「A short while later.」","The two passed through a pavilion and arrived outside a study hall not far from Mr. Yue Ming’s residence.","Chen Yi froze for a second, looking at the largest study hall in Guiyun Academy. \"Here?\"","Ma Guan nodded with a bitter smile. \"Yes, Teacher. This is the place.\"","Chen Yi confirmed it, and his steps halted.","He cocked his ear to listen for a moment, then gritted his teeth and couldn’t help but curse.","\"Did the Dean take a bribe?\"","\"Why have the numbers increased so much?\"","Inside the study hall, there were neither more nor less than exactly one hundred faint breaths.","Ma Guan shrank back, not daring to speak. He didn’t dare say a single word.","’He figured that besides Chen Yi, there were few people in the entire academy who would dare to curse Mr. Yue Ming like that.’","Chen Yi didn’t care what he was thinking. He turned and started walking toward the academy exit.","\"Heming, go tell the Dean I need to take a leave of absence. Just say I suddenly remembered I haven’t brought the laundry in at home.\"","\"On a cloudy, rainy day like this, I can’t let them get ruined.\"","\"Huh?\""]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165 - 154: Sculpting a Gilded Body","paragraphs":["In the end, Chen Yi was stopped.","The one who stopped him was none other than Mr. Yue Ming, the headmaster of Guiyun Academy.","Moreover, Mr. Yue Ming hadn’t come from his own residence, but from the study hall right behind Chen Yi.","Seeing the \"explain yourself, or I’m going home\" look on Chen Yi’s face, Mr. Yue Ming gave a wry smile.","\"Qingzhou, I’m afraid I’ve let you down on this matter.\"","\"But ever since that day, people have been flocking to the academy, many of whom are old friends of mine.\"","\"Besides, these people are already students of the academy. It was truly difficult for me to refuse them.\"","Chen Yi smiled noncommittally. \"I thought the Headmaster was a man of great principle. I didn’t expect you to be swayed by worldly pressures.\"","He paused, then continued, \"After all, you’ve never been particularly courteous to the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.\"","Mr. Yue Ming froze, a touch of embarrassment on his face. \"I’m not targeting the Xiao Family. It’s just... I have a disagreement with Marquis Xiao...\"","\"So, you also understand that you treat friends and strangers differently?\"","\"This...\"","Seeing his troubled expression, looking as if he wished the ground would swallow him whole, Chen Yi shook his head and said:","\"Headmaster, don’t blame me for being blunt.\"","\"But when it comes to many things, if you make an exception once, you’ll make it twice.\"","\"Today, you opened the door for fifty students. Tomorrow, there will be a hundred waiting for you.\"","\"If people are allowed into that study hall every time, it’s not a good thing for me, for those students, or for Guiyun Academy.\"","That said, he also knew that letting this reach a stalemate would only embarrass Guiyun Academy and Mr. Yue Ming.","However, he didn’t plan to let it go so easily.","He was willing to offend some members of the Noble Families if he had to.","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming’s face flushed with shame. He cupped his hands in a bow and said:","\"I was in the wrong this time, and I broke the academy’s rules. I hope you can forgive me, Qingzhou.\"","\"But when I think about how the academy could rise to a new level because of this, and attract some truly talented young scholars, I just can’t give up on the opportunity.\"","’So it’s for student recruitment?’","’No wonder.’","If Guiyun Academy could produce a few more students who had achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao, it would cement the academy’s reputation as a place that could teach the Calligraphy Dao.","Then, in a very short time, it would gain immense prestige, possibly even surpassing higher-ranked institutions like Yuelu Academy and Jinling Academy.","Once word spread, it would attract students from all over the Great Wei Nine State and Three Prefectures.","Even some Confucian Scholars, members of great clans, and officials dedicated to the Calligraphy Dao would be drawn by the reputation.","Chen Yi understood Mr. Yue Ming’s intentions, but he still put on a troubled expression and said:","\"My energy is limited. I can’t teach that many people.\"","Mr. Yue Ming hesitated for a moment. \"Qingzhou, if you have any concerns or demands, please speak freely.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. \"To avoid affecting the students’ progress in the Calligraphy Dao, I must set three conditions with you, Headmaster.\"","\"If you agree to all of them, we can let today’s matter go. Otherwise, you should find someone more capable.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming nodded solemnly. \"I agree.\"","Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"Headmaster, you should hear my conditions first. It’s not too late to agree then.\"","\"Please, speak.\"","\"First, the limit is one hundred students. If the academy wants to let someone else in, someone must leave.\"","\"Fine.\"","\"Second, anyone who wishes to study the Calligraphy Dao with me in the future must have my approval.\"","\"That’s only natural. I was inconsiderate before. If anyone else comes to me, I will certainly have you review them first.\"","Seeing him agree to the first two conditions, Chen Yi nodded and calmly stated the last one:","\"Third, every student who achieves success in the Calligraphy Dao must do one thing to benefit Shu State.\"","Mr. Yue Ming was taken aback. \"This... Qingzhou, isn’t this condition a bit too harsh?\"","\"Many future students may not be from Shu State. If they pass the imperial examinations and earn an official post, they’ll be scattered throughout the Nine State and Three Prefectures. I’m afraid...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi shook his head. \"I’m not asking them to do anything major.\"","\"Even just repairing a few houses, donating some silver coins, or doing anything within their power would be considered benefiting Shu State.\"","Originally, he had wanted Mr. Yue Ming and the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion to reconcile, which would allow Guiyun Academy’s students to join the Dingyuan Army.","But upon further thought, he realized that if such a requirement became public, it would definitely cause trouble for him.","It could also very likely affect the Xiao Family, making their already difficult situation even worse.","Therefore, he proposed a compromise: to benefit Shu State.","Just as Mr. Yue Ming was about to speak, Ma Guan, who was standing beside them, bowed and said, \"I am willing.\"","\"Benefiting Shu State is the fundamental reason I chose to study. Even if you hadn’t mentioned it, sir, I would do it anyway.\"","Mr. Yue Ming thought for a moment and then agreed as well.","As far as he was concerned, none of Chen Yi’s three conditions were excessive.","Especially the third point. Not only would it earn Chen Yi a good reputation, but it would also elevate the prestige of Guiyun Academy, which was already established in Shu State.","Seeing this, Chen Yi smiled. \"In that case, let’s go to class.\"","The three of them then returned to the study hall.","The students, who had been feeling anxious, all felt relieved.","But before they could be happy for long, Mr. Yue Ming publicly announced the three conditions Chen Yi had just proposed.","To be precise, he announced the first and third conditions.","These two involved all the students in the study hall, so it was only right that they knew.","\"Benefiting Shu State is understandable. We study to benefit the people.\"","\"But with a limit of one hundred, and someone having to leave for a new person to join, doesn’t that mean any of us could be kicked out of this study hall?\"","\"I don’t think so. The Headmaster and Mr. Qingzhou must have some specific rules.\"","\"Like poor attitude, slow progress, or someone not performing well in certain areas.\"","\"This is like an assessment? I don’t agree.\"","\"What’s a newcomer like you got to complain about?\"","Chen Yi ignored the students’ discussions.","’Whether they agree or not, my rules are set.’","After a sweeping glance around the room, he began today’s lesson.","Chen Yi didn’t slow down for the new students. He simply reviewed the content of the first lesson and then continued.","\"Calligraphy, like Painting, is a way to directly express one’s heart...\"","Having learned his lesson from last time, to prevent anyone from achieving success in the Calligraphy Dao during class again, Chen Yi simply left no time for practicing characters in the sand trays.","He lectured eloquently for an hour, then sent them back to practice their writing.","But even though Chen Yi had planned for this, something unexpected still happened.","It wasn’t the students, but Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying, who had returned to their residences after auditing the class.","Both of them were already famous calligraphers.","They had previously failed to achieve Minor Success in the Calligraphy Dao simply because they were on the wrong path.","They were either limited by the upright and proper nature of Wei Qing’s Style, or they had weaknesses in their fundamentals.","In short, after listening to Chen Yi’s lecture, they understood the root of their problems. As soon as they returned to their residences, they began to practice their writing.","A floral brilliance emerged from every character.","This situation left Chen Yi, who had just finished his class and come over to say goodbye before leaving, not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","But seeing the excited expressions on Mr. Yue Ming’s and Mr. Zhuo Ying’s faces as they thanked him profusely, he could only reluctantly accept it.","However, Chen Yi had no intention of letting them off the hook.","\"Headmaster, Mr. Zhuo Ying, although you two aren’t students in the study hall, you have, after all, achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao.\"","\"Don’t forget to do one thing to benefit Shu State.\"","Mr. Yue Ming, still immersed in the joy of his achievement, nodded and said, \"Never mind one, I’d do a hundred.\"","Chen Yi loved nothing more than helping others fulfill their promises. \"Then you should do a hundred, Headmaster.\"","Mr. Yue Ming’s smile froze. He stared at him, speechless. \"I was actually just joking.\"","\"A gentleman’s word is his bond.\"","\"Fine, fine. A hundred it is. I’ll just consider it setting an example for the students.\"","Compared to him, Mr. Zhuo Ying was a bit more cautious and reserved. \"The Headmaster is a man of great principle. I... COUGH COUGH... I’ll just do two.\"","\"...\"","Whether he was a man of great principle or not, Chen Yi didn’t know.","But he did know that once word of Mr. Yue Ming’s and Mr. Zhuo Ying’s success in the Calligraphy Dao spread, Guiyun Academy and the Xiao Mansion would become even livelier.","Fortunately, he had already set the three conditions with Mr. Yue Ming.","’In the future, who stays in that study hall and who leaves will be a problem for the newcomers to figure out.’","’I definitely won’t get involved.’","’Not even if the old master of the Xiao Family himself gave the order.’","’Unless my wife and Eldest Sister both...’","Not long after, Guiyun Academy was once again in an uproar because Mr. Yue Ming and Mr. Zhuo Ying had achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao.","\"First Brother Heming, and now the two sirs have achieved success in the Calligraphy Dao. Mr. Qingzhou’s attainments in the Calligraphy Dao are truly frightening.\"","\"Indeed. Throughout history, there have been many masters who’ve achieved Great Success in the Calligraphy Dao, but very few who could teach multiple students to achieve success themselves.\"","\"Plus, besides Wei Qing’s Style, Mr. Qingzhou is also skilled in a new style. The two styles are different, yet his mastery of both is equivalent, which just shows how high his Realm in the Calligraphy Dao is.\"","\"I regret not signing up at the beginning. Ai, it’s going to be so difficult to get into that study hall now.\"","\"What’s so difficult about it?\"","\"If even Bai Yutang could get in, so can we.\"","\"Heh, Bai Yutang had his father vouch for him. Who do you have in your family?\"","\"Besides, after today, there will be even more people with the same idea. The competition will be fierce. How can we from the Lower Class compete with them?\"","\"In the end, it all came down to a moment of hesitation. We doubted Mr. Qingzhou’s abilities before. We have no one to blame but ourselves...\"","It wasn’t just the students who were filled with regret; even the other teachers were green with envy, beating their chests and stamping their feet, regretting that they hadn’t gone to audit the class.","After all, at their age, their knowledge was largely set, and it was difficult to make any further progress.","But the Calligraphy Dao was different.","Having a hand for good calligraphy was, at the end of the day, a fine skill worth showing off and talking about.","\"Speaking of the three conditions Qingzhou proposed, the first two are nothing special, but this last one... I feel there’s more to it than meets the eye.\"","\"Oh?\"","Hearing an old man speak, Mr. Yue Ming calmed the joy of his recent breakthrough and asked, \"Do tell.\"","\"Think about it. Qingzhou taught them the Calligraphy Dao. In the future, when those students benefit Shu State, who among the beneficiaries won’t remember Qingzhou’s good deed?\"","\"One or two wouldn’t be a big deal, but if there are many students who achieve success in the Calligraphy Dao... tsk tsk tsk.\"","Hearing this, Mr. Yue Ming sighed in admiration. \"It brings him many benefits, but it is also good for our Guiyun Academy.\"","Mr. Zhuo Ying nodded and said with a smile, \"It’s a pity that Qingzhou is currently just a live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family. Such a reputation will have a hard time helping him.\"","\"If he were an official...\"","His voice trailed off.","The teachers looked at each other, all understanding the hidden benefits.","It would not be an exaggeration to say that because of this, Chen Yi could build an untouchable reputation among the common people of Shu State.","...","Leaving aside the commotion at the academy.","After leaving Guiyun Academy, Chen Yi headed straight for the West Market Hundred Herbs Hall.","Fortunately, he had sent Ge the Third back to the Marquis’s Mansion earlier. Traveling to the Hundred Herbs Hall alone was a bit slower, but it was safe.","He didn’t linger. With just a look at Wang Ji, he had him take Zhang Erbao and head straight for a residence deep within the West Market.","After changing his appearance, Chen Yi sat in the main hall and ordered, \"My meeting with the Eldest Miss is set for five days from now.\"","\"By then, you need to have the account books ready, as well as the plans for expanding Hundred Herbs Hall into neighboring states and counties.\"","Wang Ji paused. \"My lord, are you preparing to join forces with the Xiao Family?\"","Chen Yi nodded, not hiding it from him. \"Hundred Herbs Hall is doing well right now, but there are some hidden dangers.\"","\"First, our foundation is weak. It’s just the two of us. We can manage in Shu State Prefecture City.\"","\"But if we go to other states and counties, even if we win over the local noble families and gentry by sharing profits, there’s still a huge risk.\"","\"Rather than being reactive later, it’s better to rely on the Xiao Family for support and grow Hundred Herbs Hall as quickly as possible.\"","Hearing this, Wang Ji nodded. \"I will follow all of your orders, my lord.\"","Compared to this, the account books and plans were minor matters.","After discussing business, Chen Yi sent Wang Ji and the others away, telling them to leave a message for Liu Lang when they returned to the Hundred Herbs Hall.","\"Tell him to come see me.\""]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166 - 155: Sudden Complications","paragraphs":["After writing another list for Liu Lang to bring back the medicinal herbs, Chen Yi sent Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao back.","Afterward, he deactivated his Black Tortoise Concealing Breath and listened intently to the sounds around him.","Once he confirmed there were only commoners nearby, he slowly began to practice a set of the Mountain Shattering Fist.","Not for Cultivation, but simply to stretch his muscles.","Outside, the sky was still blanketed by dark clouds.","However, the thunder and lightning had ceased, and the rain had lightened considerably.","A series of dripping sounds echoed through the modest residence.","Some were from the rain striking the roof tiles, others from water dripping off the eaves and onto the stone pavers below.","It added a touch of life to the surrounding quiet.","Chen Yi, however, paid them no mind. The sounds didn’t even register.","He simply practiced the Mountain Shattering Fist in the dimly lit room, his mind occupied with what was to come.","The Jing State Liu Family was quite powerful.","Although the Xiao Family was not afraid of them, they wouldn’t want to provoke a head-on conflict.","And vice versa.","The Liu Family wouldn’t dare to move against the Xiao Family openly.","It was just like before, when the Liu Family’s people didn’t dare operate under the banner of Xinglin Hall, opening Linglan Pavilion instead.","Their only goal was to test the waters.","They weren’t just testing the Xiao Family’s circumstances, but also Liu Hong in Shu State.","One was overt, the other covert, that was all.","If Liu Jing hadn’t shown up at their door, the closing of Linglan Pavilion would have signaled the end of the Jing State Liu Family’s probing, and nothing more would have come of it.","But the end of their probing didn’t mean there would be no follow-up.","That’s why Hundred Herbs Hall had to stay open and become a major asset to the Xiao Family.","Publicly, however, it was best for Hundred Herbs Hall to only maintain its cooperation with the Xiao Family in Shu State Prefecture City. In other prefectures and counties, the Xiao Family needed to remain in the shadows.","’Xiao Wan’er probably can’t make this decision on her own. I suspect the Old Master will have to get involved.’","Having deduced this much, Chen Yi knew that the Liu Family’s influence over the Xiao Family in Shu State was now limited to just one person: Left Governor Liu Hong.","After some thought, he decided to stick with his original plan for now: try to have Yang Ye act as a shield.","It would undoubtedly involve some complications.","’Then there are those Hidden Guards.’","As Chen Yi mulled these things over, his mind gradually relaxed, yet his Fist Technique grew ever sharper.","With his Martial Arts Fist having reached Great Success, both his Mountain Shattering Fist and Hundred Flowers Palm had also reached the level of Mastery, their power far surpassing what it once was.","This was especially true for the Mountain Shattering Fist.","Combined with the Mental Realm of Great Success in Fist Dao, every single move could overwhelm an opponent with sheer Fist Force.","Coupled with his solid foundation and his Power reaching the Realm of Symbols Power, any Martial Artist with lesser Cultivation wouldn’t even be able to withstand a single punch.","The Hundred Flowers Palm, on the other hand, leaned toward agility, its Fist Intent centered on nimble and unpredictable movements.","A single palm strike, a blur of feints and reality, made it impossible for an opponent to discern the true direction of the attack.","The combination of the two was enough for him to handle any Martial Artist in the Lower Three Grades Realm.","Even against the Middle Three Grades... or rather, against a Martial Artist at the Sixth Grade Realm, he could still put up a fight.","It was just like with Cui Qingwu that night.","When her Dao Realm was inferior to his, he was able to escape even though her Cultivation was an entire major Realm higher.","But if an opponent was at the Fifth Grade and had also achieved Great Success in their Dao Realm, he would be completely outmatched.","Just then, Chen Yi’s ears twitched. He heard undisguised footsteps approaching from outside the door.","He immediately ceased his practice, calmed his mind, and activated the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to hide his internal aura.","Soon, the footsteps drew near.","Liu Lang, dressed in a raincoat and bamboo hat, pushed the door open. A long blade hung at his waist, and he carried a dozen or so packets of herbs in his hands.","He glanced at Chen Yi, who was seated at the head of the room, placed the packets of herbs to the side, and bowed with cupped fists.","\"We meet again, Boss Chen.\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod and gestured for him to sit down and speak.","Liu Lang didn’t stand on ceremony, sitting down beside him with a smile.","\"If you hadn’t come today, I would’ve had Shopkeeper Wang contact you.\"","Chen Yi’s interest was piqued. \"Any leads on that matter?\" he asked.","\"Leads... You could say that, yes.\"","Liu Lang then recounted everything he had done the previous night for Chen Yi, holding nothing back.","He explained the local power dynamics in Shu State—the so-called ’gods, buddhas, and demons’ you have to appease at the wharf—and his meeting with Black Tooth of the Bright Moon Building.","From what he said, the Bright Moon Building was some kind of intelligence network. They weren’t considered a righteous faction in the Jianghu, but you couldn’t simply classify them as part of the Evil Demonic Dao either.","At this, Liu Lang paused, a strange look on his face.","\"Originally, I intended to put on a full performance, getting Black Tooth to find some men to head to the Three Towns. I never expected someone else to contact him, wanting to actually burn them down.\"","\"And they offered a very high price. Black Tooth didn’t say so outright, but I’m guessing it was at least ten thousand taels of gold.\"","Chen Yi frowned, mentally noting the names Black Tooth and Bright Moon Building. \"When was this?\" he asked.","\"The night before last, I believe.\"","’The night before last... The Hidden Guard?’","’But could the Hidden Guard come up with ten thousand taels of gold?’","Ten thousand taels of gold is equivalent to about a hundred thousand taels of silver. An ordinary person could never afford that.","’Even Xiao Dongchen and Ge the Third combined couldn’t possibly come up with that kind of money.’","’Not unless Cui Qingwu herself was involved.’","’But that doesn’t seem right either.’","The Hidden Guard belongs to the Imperial Court; they have their own procedures, subordinates, and resources.","For a clandestine operation like ’burning the summer grain in the Three Towns,’ it’s highly unlikely they would outsource the job.","This is Shu State, after all—the Shu State Prefecture City, the Xiao Family’s home turf.","Even if Black Tooth is discreet, in a place teeming with all sorts of characters, it would be impossible to keep it a secret from the Xiao Family.","The more he thought about it, the more Chen Yi felt certain the Hidden Guard would never use Black Tooth for something like this.","’Could it be someone else?’","’Who?’","’The great Noble Families of Shu State? Or the Jing State Liu Family?’","Unable to come to a conclusion, Chen Yi simply asked, \"What else?\"","Liu Lang grinned. \"Black Tooth invited me to join in on this deal.\"","\"Hm? You didn’t tell him you were supposed to be faking the arson?\"","\"It’s a good thing I didn’t. Otherwise, he never would have revealed so much.\"","\"He may be from the Evil Demonic Dao, but when it comes to business, he always keeps his word. Otherwise, the Liu Family wouldn’t have used him as a middleman to hire me and the people from the Illusory Sound Sect.\"","Chen Yi understood. After a moment of thought, he asked, \"So, did you agree?\"","Liu Lang shook his head. \"I wouldn’t dare get involved in this mess without your approval.\"","\"This deal is extremely dangerous. Succeed or fail, it’s bound to attract Xiao Jinghong’s attention. If she gets angry, she’ll find me even if I run to the ends of the earth.\"","A flicker of surprise went through Chen Yi. \"She can leave Shu State as she pleases?\"","\"An ordinary Military General couldn’t, of course. But she...\"","Liu Lang stopped, leaving the rest unsaid. \"Don’t ask me. I don’t dare say.\"","\"If you get the chance, you should ask her yourself.\"","Chen Yi shot him a sidelong glance. \"And what if I insist on knowing?\"","Liu Lang opened his mouth, a pained smile on his face. \"I really can’t.\"","\"Even if you were to use that favor, I can’t go gossiping about her behind her back.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. ’My wife has secrets even I don’t know about?’","After a moment’s thought, he stopped pressing Liu Lang and changed the subject.","\"In that case, agree to Black Tooth’s offer for now. Find out for me who’s behind this.\"","Liu Lang let out a small sigh of relief, as if the prospect of losing his head was less terrifying than facing Xiao Jinghong’s wrath.","\"Does this count as the second favor?\"","\"It does.\"","\"Also, I recall you mentioning you wanted to repay Xiao Jinghong for sparing your life, correct?\"","\"I did. Are you saying...\"","Seeing he had caught on, Chen Yi nodded. \"Find a way to secretly pass this information to the Xiao Family.\"","\"Consider that the third favor I’m asking of you.\"","But to his surprise, Liu Lang shook his head. \"Let’s not mix matters.\"","\"If I’m passing a message to the Xiao Family, that can’t count as a favor for you.\"","Chen Yi let out a surprised laugh. \"You’re quite the man of principle. Very trustworthy.\"","\"A man is nothing without his word. I may roam the Jianghu and have done my share of foolish things, but when I make a promise, I see it through.\"","\"In that case, let’s just say you’re doing two favors for me.\"","\"Deal.\"","Chen Yi then asked about a few other matters.","For instance, which of the Evil Demonic Dao figures hiding in Shu State would most likely get involved.","\"I’m new to Shu State, so I don’t know much about the local Jianghu. But I doubt many Evil Demons would dare linger here.\"","\"Not many?\"","\"Boss, you don’t know? The Mountain Race is here in Shu State.\"","Liu Lang scratched his head. \"Even though Granny Shan hasn’t left her mountain in a long time, very few from either the righteous or demonic paths would dare cause trouble right under her nose.\"","\"Even the Illusory Sound Sect, when they came to plunder the Xiao Family’s herbs, they came and left in a hurry, not daring to linger.\"","\"Only some low-life riffraff would dare hide out in Shu State. Those old monsters with profound Cultivation wouldn’t dare make a move even if they came here, for fear of breaking Granny Shan’s rules.\"","Chen Yi murmured her name, \"Granny Shan.\" This was the first time he truly understood the weight of her reputation.","’No wonder when Tiger Girl poisoned the Marquis’s Mansion’s Armored Warriors and acted so recklessly, my wife only gave her a light punishment.’","After some thought, Chen Yi gave a few more instructions before dismissing Liu Lang.","After he had gone, Chen Yi waited a moment longer before changing back into his own clothes, removing his facial disguise, and heading back to the Xiao Family under an oil-paper umbrella.","Along the way, the wind howled and the rain beat down.","The stalls in the West Market were long since deserted, and there were few pedestrians about. Only the shops lining the street still had people inside.","Places like tailor shops, taverns, and inns.","But Chen Yi didn’t linger. He only took a moment to survey the area around a certain tailor shop before disappearing into the downpour.","On the way back, his thoughts were still occupied with the Hidden Guard and the mastermind behind the plot to burn down the Three Towns.","’Who could it be?’","By the time Chen Yi returned to Spring Lotus Garden, he was still no closer to an answer.","He could only pin his hopes on Liu Lang, trusting he might get a lead from Black Tooth.","Just then, Xiaodie came running up to him. She took the herbs from his hand and said:","\"Young Master, you’re finally back! The Eldest Miss has already sent someone to ask about you three times.\"","\"Oh? What about?\"","\"It seems many people came to visit this afternoon. Not only the Eldest Miss, but the Master also sent people to ask where you were.\"","Chen Yi understood and curled his lip. \"Refuse all visitors. Just tell them I’m ill.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Just tell Eldest Sister that.\"","It was obviously about the academy. Some people were trying to get to him through the Xiao Family.","’But how could he possibly yield?’","’With so many students, just grading their Calligraphy workbooks would be enough to kill him.’","He had expected Xiaodie to return quickly so he could eat and prepare for the evening’s business.","But after waiting for quite some time, not only did Xiaodie return, but Xiao Wan’er came with her.","Behind her, Cui’er and Juan’er were even carrying some medicinal soup.","\"Brother-in-law, I heard you were ill?\"","\"...\"","’Xiaodie, what did you tell her?’"]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167 - 156: I’m Having a Hard Time","paragraphs":["When it came to Xiao Wan’er brewing the medicinal soup, Xiaodie was also a bit confused.","She remembered that when she rushed to Jiaxing Garden as Chen Yi had instructed, Xiao Wan’er was chatting and laughing with a stately and elegantly dressed lady.","Upon learning that Chen Yi had returned, the lady even suggested going to see him.","But when Xiaodie said, \"The Young Master is ill,\" before the lady could say anything, Xiao Wan’er stood up and asked a couple of questions.","\"What illness?\"","\"I think... a cold?\"","\"Cui’er, Juan’er, go brew some medicinal soup for the Young Master.\"","At the time, Xiaodie had intended to explain further, but seeing that Xiao Wan’er had already ordered Cui’er to brew the soup and that the lady was still present, she swallowed her words.","And that’s what led to the current situation—","Chen Yi sat in the living room, clutching his stomach, a \"pained\" look on his face.","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er quickly brought over the medicinal soup and said, \"This is freshly brewed ginger tea. It’s the best for driving out the cold. Drink it while it’s hot.\"","Chen Yi opened his mouth, wanting to explain that he was just hungry.","But faced with Xiao Wan’er’s earnest gaze and the trace of worry on her gentle, beautiful face, he could only pinch his nose and drink the soup down.","’Great.’","He hadn’t had a single bite of dinner, and his stomach was already half-full.","Before he could speak, Xiao Wan’er had Cui’er bring food and place it on the dining table. \"I had them make congee especially for you.\"","\"Since you’re sick, you should eat something light.\"","\"...\"","Again, meeting that concerned gaze, Chen Yi could only glare at Xiaodie before picking up his bowl with a smile.","I don’t know if you’ve ever been that hungry.","The kind of ravenous hunger where your mind is filled with nothing but pork, beef, lamb, or maybe roasted meat, stewed meat, and the like.","In any case, it certainly wouldn’t be plain congee and vegetables.","As he ate, Xiao Wan’er sat beside him, talking about the afternoon’s events in the mansion, peppering the conversation with soft-spoken reminders.","Things like, \"Eat slowly,\" \"Be careful of catching a cold in the rain,\" and \"Take care of your health.\"","Chen Yi gave a wry smile to himself and decided not to explain. He’d just treat it as a beautiful misunderstanding.","After a bit of chatter, just as Xiao Wan’er was about to get up and leave, she suddenly remembered something and asked:","\"Have you finished the letter for Second Sister?\"","\"Shu State has entered its rainy season recently. I wonder how Second Sister is doing over there.\"","Chen Yi paused and shook his head. \"Not yet. I’ll write it later.\"","An understanding expression appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face. \"You must not have had a free moment with so much going on at the academy during the day.\"","\"But there’s no rush. Just give it to me tomorrow morning.\"","Chen Yi nodded, stood up to see her out of the wooden building, and watched as she walked gracefully away under the umbrella held by Cui’er.","After Xiao Wan’er entered Jiaxing Garden, the smile on Chen Yi’s face faded. He turned to look at the timidly shrinking Xiaodie and said irritably:","\"Go get your Young Master some more food.\"","\"Huh?\"","Xiaodie snapped out of it, quickly answered \"Yes,\" and ran out of Spring Lotus Garden, heading straight for the rear kitchen.","’Thank goodness, thank goodness. The Young Master didn’t blame me.’","There was no way he could blame her.","After eating some more leftovers and rice, Chen Yi patted his seventy-percent-full stomach and let out a long breath.","\"Finally, some meat.\"","Seeing this, Xiaodie also breathed a sigh of relief and said sheepishly, \"Young Master, I know I was wrong.\"","Chen Yi glanced at her and shook his head. \"I wasn’t clear enough.\"","Whether it was a white lie or playing along with the act, it had ultimately achieved his goal: turning away all visitors.","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi told Xiaodie to clean up and get some rest, while he himself took the medicine packets to the study.","After a brief rest, he sat down at his desk and wrote a letter to Xiao Jinghong.","This time, it was certainly no *Three Thoughts on a Summer Night*.","It was a proper letter.","[Jinghong, may this letter find you well.","Your husband has accepted Mr. Yue Ming’s invitation to become an Instructor at Guiyun Academy. All is well...]","He wrote several hundred characters fluently.","In less than a quarter of an hour, he finished writing, sealed it in an envelope, and set it aside to give to Xiao Wan’er tomorrow.","Chen Yi looked out the window.","Seeing that the rain still hadn’t stopped, he estimated there were still four hours before the Hidden Guard’s important discussion at the tailor shop.","He didn’t linger, instead taking out a mortar, pestle, medicinal scale, and other tools, and began to meticulously grind the herbs.","The Immortal Drunk he’d made before was too potent. This time, he planned to reduce its strength while retaining its ability to penetrate True Essence defenses.","After concocting four new vials of Immortal Drunk, he moved on to creating another new medicine.","It was a powder that could make a person’s body go limp and weak.","Its potency was much less than Immortal Drunk, but its advantage was that it was colorless and odorless, making it more convenient to use.","He named it \"Qingfeng Drunk.\"","After busying himself for over an hour, Chen Yi finally finished his work.","After tidying up the study, he took a few vials of the powder back to his room, changed into black clothes, disguised himself, and secured his five-section Long Spear. Everything was ready.","Chen Yi let out a soft breath, stretched his limbs, and quietly left Spring Lotus Garden.","It was now deep into the night, and with the heavy rain and strong wind, there weren’t many people lingering on the streets.","The occasional carriage or pedestrian he encountered also hurried past.","To avoid attracting attention, Chen Yi didn’t take the main road this time. Instead, he took a familiar route through dark, deep alleys to the outskirts of the West Market.","However, just as he was about to emerge from the alley outside the Hui Xian Building, his eyes flickered, and with a quick turn, he slipped back into the alley, hiding in the shadows.","A moment later, a cold voice rang out, \"That night, Sun Erhu’s death was too strange. I don’t believe the person who killed Liu Jing was a Wan Family Guard.\"","\"Even if he was, it wasn’t the work of one person. He must have had at least two accomplices.\"","Then, another young man’s voice spoke, \"Hundred Households Fang, the department has already closed this case.\"","\"Even if you have your suspicions, it will be difficult to overturn the verdict. Why bother...\"","\"Hmph! Even if the Lord Prefect has already announced the verdict, I will find the culprit who injured us that night!\"","Just from their voices, Chen Yi knew it was Fang Hongxiu and her group of four from the Imprisonment Department.","He grimaced to himself.","’I can’t believe knocking out Fang Hongxiu that night would make her pursue this so relentlessly.’","Fortunately, the case of the Wan Family Guard killing Liu Jing was closed, which had eased the tensions between the Xiao and Liu Families.","Otherwise, if it had dragged on for a few more days, there was no guarantee the Imprisonment Department wouldn’t have discovered something.","Once he was sure Fang Hongxiu and her group had walked away, Chen Yi quickly cut through the curtain of rain and entered the somewhat deserted West Market.","Who would have thought that just as he rounded the corner past Hundred Herbs Hall, he would see a few familiar figures in a corner.","It was none other than the tall and short Jianghu People he had seen in the West Market that day.","But the last person was a surprise—the Maid named Huan’er who was always by Cui Qingwu’s side.","But now it was too late to avoid them. He could only pull his bamboo hat lower and walk hurriedly past a few taverns and inns, just like the other pedestrians passing by.","The tall, thin man and the short, stout man over there naturally saw him but clearly didn’t recognize him.","The stout man was heard saying, \"Brother Yu, it’s been so many days and there’s still no sign of that person. Could the Young Master’s guess be wrong?\"","The tall, thin man withdrew his gaze from Chen Yi and said flatly, \"The Young Master is never wrong.\"","Huan’er, standing nearby, glanced at the two men. \"This was a joint deduction by my Young Miss and your Young Master. It can’t possibly be wrong.\"","\"Oh.\"","\"But besides knowing his build, we don’t even know what he looks like. Are we sure we can find him by waiting here?\"","\"Just do as the Young Master instructed. Don’t ask so many questions.\"","As he spoke, the tall, thin man paused, stood up, and looked deeper into the West Market, a contemplative look on his face.","\"You’ve reminded me, though. The build matches.\"","\"What’s up?\"","\"Did you find something?\"","\"The man in black with the bamboo hat who just passed by has a build that’s extremely similar to his.\"","Hearing this, Huan’er scanned the area. \"Where?\"","Without waiting for an answer, the tall, thin Ning Yu had already stepped into the rain, chasing in the direction where Chen Yi had disappeared.","Seeing this, the two behind him quickly followed.","\"Once we find him, I’ll show him what’s what.\"","\"Miss Huan’er, you should still be careful. His Spear Dao has already reached Minor Success. His strength shouldn’t be underestimated.\"","\"Minor Success in Spear Dao? He’s clearly reached Great Success in Fist Dao, with his Fist Intent already manifested.\"","\"Huh?\"","Hiding not far from the tailor shop, Chen Yi saw the three of them hurry past and faintly overheard their conversation, causing him to frown.","’Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu are really relentless.’","’To find me, they actually had people wait here in the West Market, hoping I’d just show up.’","’Was all this really necessary?’","Chen Yi cursed to himself. As the trio moved farther away, he quickly relocated.","He moved to the spot he had scouted earlier in the day—the flying eaves of the residence to the side and rear of the tailor shop.","It was about five zhang away. While he couldn’t see inside the tailor shop from there, he could hear sounds from it.","Moreover, the height gave him a perfect bird’s-eye view of the tailor shop’s surroundings.","It was an excellent position.","After waiting quietly for a moment and seeing Ning Yu’s group hurry back to their previous spot, Chen Yi let out a small sigh of relief.","’No wonder this intelligence is rated Earth Level. A dangerous place like this, with people watching from all sides—of course the rank would have to be higher.’","The thought of the Imprisonment Department, as well as Chen Yunfan’s and Cui Qingwu’s people, all circling the West Market from now on gave Chen Yi a bit of a headache.","’This is too difficult.’","’I’ll have to come up with a more thorough plan for the future.’","Otherwise, if those people found him, it would inevitably lead to complications.","He waited like this for about another hour or so.","The number of pedestrians inside and outside the West Market dwindled, and most of the shops on the street had closed for the night.","Many of the lanterns hanging by the doorways had been extinguished, making the entire West Market much dimmer.","Even Ning Yu’s group, who had been waiting at the entrance to the West Market, had gone silent, having apparently left.","Seeing this, Chen Yi didn’t relax his guard. Instead, he became even more vigilant, his eyes fixed on the area around the tailor shop and his ears perked.","Circulating his True Essence, he simultaneously used the Four Symbols Skill and the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique, slightly enhancing his five senses.","But at this moment, aside from the faint sound of a drunkard’s laughing curses and the PITTER-PATTER of the rain, he heard no noise at all from the tailor shop.","It wasn’t until four more lanterns at a nearby shop were extinguished that the sound of footsteps approached from the distance.","Chen Yi’s heart skipped a beat. He carefully concealed himself, blending into the shadows beneath the flying eaves.","Soon, he saw two figures in black, one tall and one short, appear outside the tailor shop.","One of them was none other than Ge the Third, an Armored Warrior from the Xiao Mansion.","And the other person..."]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168 - 157: Lady Tiger, Conspiracy","paragraphs":["Who was the other person?","Judging by their figure, it was a woman, but she didn’t look like Cui Qingwu or Huan’er, the Hidden Guards identified earlier.","’Could it be the Hidden Guard who was hiding in Yanhua Lane before?’","The one who helped Ge the Third escape from the Marquis’s Mansion.","’It’s a distinct possibility.’","With this thought, Chen Yi lowered himself slightly and held his breath, trying to avoid detection.","The next moment, he saw Ge the Third step forward and knock on the door. He called out in a hoarse voice, \"Shopkeeper, I’m here to pick up some clothes.\"","\"We’re closed. Come back tomorrow.\"","\"I have something important tomorrow and urgently need that formal outfit. I hope you can...\"","The voice was secondary; as he spoke, there was a series of knocks.","KNOCK. KNOCK. KNOCK-KNOCK.","Two long, two short. The pattern repeated twice with a distinct rhythm.","On this night of pouring rain, the sound carried clearly for several dozen yards.","Chen Yi, of course, heard it clearly, but he was more concerned with the identity of the slightly slender person beside Ge the Third.","After a moment of conversation, the tailor shop’s door opened, and Ge the Third and his companion walked inside.","Along with a slightly displeased voice from within, the slender woman spoke.","\"Our apologies for the impertinent intrusion, shopkeeper.\"","Her voice was crisp and pleasant, with a slightly ethereal quality, like that of a lark.","It was quite beautiful.","Chen Yi was certain he had never heard this voice before; she had clearly never appeared in his presence.","Soon, the three of them exchanged a few pleasantries. The tailor shop owner said to wait a moment, then shut the door planks again.","The voices inside abruptly dropped to a murmur.","He could only hear an intermittent, mosquito-like buzzing.","\"This subordinate... Lord Lady Tiger...\"","’Lady Tiger?’","’It’s her.’","The \"Lady Tiger\" that Xiao Dongchen and Ge the Third had discussed previously.","Chen Yi’s brows furrowed slightly.","He had assumed \"Lady Tiger\" was Cui Qingwu, but now it seemed to be someone else entirely.","’But on second thought, my previous guess really doesn’t hold up to scrutiny.’","’It’s obvious.’","Ge the Third and Xiao Dongchen had been hiding in Shu State for many years, so it stood to reason that \"Lady Tiger\" had been as well.","Cui Qingwu and Huan’er, on the other hand, had only recently arrived in Shu State.","Furthermore, they had traveled openly under the banner of the Qinghe Cui Family, so their route must have been clear and traceable.","’Perhaps that day at the Fengchun Building, it wasn’t necessarily Xiao Dongchen who contacted Cui Qingwu.’","’It’s possible... it’s possible Cui Qingwu initiated the meeting with Xiao Dongchen.’","Musing on this, Chen Yi carefully shifted his position, moving a little closer to the tailor shop.","Faintly, he heard Ge the Third’s voice. \"I don’t understand. Why did you have to contact Gray Wolf?\"","\"That madman is actually planning to burn the summer grain from the Three Towns. The whole thing is giving me a headache.\"","\"Because Xiao Yuan and Xiao Jinghong have already noticed something is amiss in Shu State. Building the Mutual Market is their preventative measure.\"","Lady Tiger’s voice was much softer than Ge the Third’s.","But due to its unique timbre, it was actually clearer to Chen Yi’s ears.","\"On top of that, the Liu Family’s recent actions have made the Xiao Family even more guarded.\"","\"If we don’t throw the Xiao Family into chaos now, by the time the Mutual Market is built and the morale of the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army has stabilized, Shu State will inevitably become a pool of stagnant water again.\"","\"At that point, it will be nigh impossible for you and I to complete the Pavilion Master’s plan.\"","Ge the Third paused, then mumbled, \"But I still think Gray Wolf is too selfish.\"","Lady Tiger said, \"Having selfish motives isn’t necessarily a bad thing. As long as his goal is the same as ours, we can let him be.\"","\"So, you approve of the plan to burn the summer grain?\"","\"It’s not just us. Someone else has already approached Black Tooth and offered thirty thousand taels of gold to burn the Three Towns.\"","\"Black Tooth? Thirty thousand taels?\"","\"This, this... you’re relying on those from the Evil Demonic Dao to get things done?\"","Hearing this, not only was Ge the Third astonished, but a trace of surprise also flashed in Chen Yi’s eyes.","Liu Lang had said it was over ten thousand taels during the day; he never expected it to be thirty thousand.","That was enough money to support ten thousand common households for a year.","It could even sustain a private army of five thousand elite soldiers for a year.","’There can’t be many people in Shu State who can produce that much money, right?’","Just then, he heard Ge the Third ask, \"Who on earth is it? To be so reckless as to approach Black Tooth.\"","\"If word gets out from Black Tooth’s side, the Xiao Family will get the news in no time, and we can forget about succeeding.\"","Lady Tiger replied, \"I don’t know either. Even Black Tooth isn’t sure.\"","\"But I heard him say that the person is quite ruthless, and their strength is at least at the Middle Three Grades.\"","Ge the Third scoffed, \"Hah. Is there anyone in Shu State who dares to scheme against the Xiao Family who isn’t a ruthless person?\"","\"But this makes things difficult. Black Tooth may be reputable, but the people from the Evil Demonic Dao he hires are another story.\"","Lady Tiger hummed in agreement. \"You need to think carefully about whether you want to help Gray Wolf.\"","\"He came to you because he clearly has his eyes on your Iron Banner Officers hidden in the army.\"","\"If you decide to help him, your Iron Banner Officers will have to die, regardless of success or failure.\"","Hearing this, Ge the Third cursed and grumbled for a bit.","After a moment of silence, his voice was heard again. \"I’ll help!\"","\"But I’m very worried about a leak from Black Tooth’s side. Do you have a plan?\"","\"Simple. Have your people go to him and take the job. With thirty thousand taels of gold in hand, it will be more advantageous for our next moves.\"","\"...No wonder you took the initiative to contact me. It was for that ill-gotten fortune.\"","\"So, is it a deal or not?\"","\"It’s a deal! Since you’re the one asking, even if not for Gray Wolf, I’ll take this risk for you, Lady Tiger!\"","Listening to this, Chen Yi’s expression grew a little strange.","’Are the Hidden Guards short on silver?’","’What a ridiculous joke. Shouldn’t the Imperial Court be funding their operations?’","’Surely the Imperial Court doesn’t treat the Hidden Guards the same way it treats the Dingyuan Army.’","He pondered for a moment.","Chen Yi couldn’t help but become more curious about this Lady Tiger’s identity and mission.","Just then, he heard Lady Tiger ask, \"How are things on your end? I heard that Fledgling has been causing quite a stir these past few days.\"","Ge the Third paused, then said with a hint of self-satisfaction, \"Everything is under control.\"","\"Originally, he was unwilling to go to Guiyun Academy. I used a little trick, and he obediently fell in line.\"","\"Look at the commotion he’s causing at Guiyun Academy now. You can tell he’s still the same old Fledgling. He could never live a quiet life.\"","\"Is that so?\"","\"Of course...\"","Chen Yi secretly pursed his lips, gaining a new appreciation for Ge the Third’s shamelessness.","’The guy did absolutely nothing, yet he’s taking all the credit for himself.’","\"That’s good, then. Tomorrow, pass these matters on to the Lord Golden Banner Officer and the Pavilion Master. Once we receive their reply, you and I can act according to the plan.\"","\"Alright.\"","The voices paused for a moment.","Just as Chen Yi thought they were about to leave the tailor shop, he heard Ge the Third ask:","\"You must already know that the Simurgh Phoenix has come to Shu State, right?\"","\"Yes, I heard.\"","\"I originally thought she came on her own initiative, but I never expected her to have the Pavilion Master’s White Tiger Order.\"","\"When Gray Wolf saw the White Tiger Order in her hand earlier, his legs almost gave out, and he nearly knelt on the spot.\"","Lady Tiger asked, slightly surprised, \"She showed the White Tiger Order of her own accord?\"","Ge the Third lowered his voice. \"That’s what Gray Wolf said. To make him obey, the Simurgh Phoenix specifically promised him one thing.\"","\"To frame the Xiao Family for Liu Jing’s death.\"","Lady Tiger said, \"Oh? No wonder Shu State has been so restless lately. So there was this hidden story behind it all.\"","Ge the Third said, \"Unfortunately, she failed. Someone interfered, and he even seems to know about our identities as Hidden Guards.\"","\"When I first heard about it, I thought it might be that girl from the Mountain Race, but it turned out to be a man. From the looks of it, he doesn’t seem to be from the Xiao Family either. Do you think he could be a spy from the Poshisu Country or the Barbarian Race?\"","Lady Tiger paused for a moment before saying, \"No matter who it is, we cannot be careless. Report this matter back to the Pavilion tomorrow along with the rest.\"","\"Sounds good to me.\"","\"But I’m more curious about the Simurgh Phoenix’s purpose in coming to Shu State. Did the Pavilion Master have special instructions?\"","\"Ask fewer questions about things that don’t concern you. Knowing too much is not good for either of us.\"","\"Oh, then what about you...\"","\"Don’t ask what doesn’t concern you!\"","With that, the voices stopped, and silence fell within the tailor shop.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. ’From the sound of it, Lady Tiger’s mission seems even more important?’","’Even Ge the Third can’t ask about it freely?’","’And that Simurgh Phoenix they just mentioned.’","’If I’m not mistaken, that must be Cui Qingwu’s codename within the Hidden Guards.’","’The White Tiger Order...’","Chen Yi silently committed these details to memory, then quietly backed away a little, retracting his aura to wait for what came next.","Before long, he heard a few sounds from the tailor shop. The door opened, and Ge the Third and Lady Tiger emerged, wearing bamboo hats and raincoats.","After a brief pause, the two of them headed off in opposite directions.","[Witnessed a major Hidden Guard conspiracy. Reward: Zither Score \"Carefree Travel,\" Opportunity +35.]","[Evaluation: You arrived and listened, but you did not see the scene. Having taken no action, your ultimate achievement is limited.]","Chen Yi glanced at it, the corner of his eye twitching.","’A Zither Score?’","’Among Ge the Third, the tailor shop owner, and Lady Tiger, only Lady Tiger is likely skilled in that art.’","’Combining this with Liu Lang seeing Black Tooth at the Spring Rain Building last night, it’s not hard to deduce that Lady Tiger must be hiding in Yanhua Lane.’","This made him even more certain of his earlier guess—it was indeed Lady Tiger who helped Ge the Third move out of the Marquis’s Mansion.","Seeing that all was quiet around him, Chen Yi quietly leaped down from the eaves and headed for the Xiao Mansion from behind the tailor shop.","His gains tonight were substantial.","He had basically figured out the identities of all the Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officers hiding in Shu State.","’Gray Wolf, Xiao Dongchen.’","’Hawk, Ge the Third.’","’Lady Tiger, the woman with the beautiful voice.’","’Simurgh Phoenix, Cui Qingwu.’","’As for their missions, from the information gathered so far, they each seem to be different.’","’Or rather, their ultimate goal is likely the same, just with a different division of labor.’","’In the end, they just want to throw Shu State into chaos.’","\"Knowing too much really isn’t a good thing.\"","\"Because it just raises more questions.\"","For example, why were the Hidden Guards or the Imperial Court doing this? What benefit was there for the Great Wei Dynasty if Shu State fell into chaos?","Or was his previous speculation wrong, and the Hidden Guards weren’t actually people of the Imperial Court?","And who was the person who spent thirty thousand taels of gold to contact Black Tooth?","As Chen Yi pondered these things, he failed to notice several figures appear a short distance ahead.","The person in the lead was dressed in a bright red, short-cut outfit, a long blade hanging from their waist.","The moment they saw him, that person called out, \"It’s so late. Where are you going, out in the rain?\"","Huh?","’Fang Hongxiu?’","Chen Yi raised his head slightly, his gaze peering out from under the brim of his bamboo hat. Seeing the four Imprisonment Officers ahead, he was momentarily speechless.","It was nearly midnight, yet she was still out and about.","\"Lord Hundred Households, what do you think?\"","Fang Hongxiu froze, feeling that this hoarse, deep voice was very familiar. When she realized who it was, she immediately drew the long blade from her waist.","\"It’s you!?\""]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169 - 158: Bastard! Lecher!","paragraphs":["\"It wasn’t me.\"","Realizing she had recognized him, Chen Yi flatly denied it and turned to run.","\"After him!\"","There was no way Fang Hongxiu would let him get away. She immediately led several of her subordinates in pursuit.","As they chased, she reminded them, \"Be careful. Don’t let him use the terrain to his advantage like last time.\"","The three Imprisonment Officers beside her nodded repeatedly. \"Rest assured, Lord Hundred Households.\"","They clearly remembered the last time they’d chased him relentlessly, only to be successfully ambushed by Chen Yi around a corner.","Chen Yi, of course, remembered as well, so this time he repeated his old trick, ducking into a small alley.","Fang Hongxiu and her men were instantly on alert, their pursuit slowing for a moment.","Then, they all drew the long Blades from their waists. As they rounded the corner, they led with their weapons.","This way, even if they were ambushed, they could still fight back.","But when they entered the alley, they weren’t attacked. Instead, they saw the tall figure in the Raincoat and bamboo hat standing about fifty feet away.","Behind him was a high wall; he was at a dead end.","Fang Hongxiu’s heart stirred. She raised a hand to signal a halt, her brow furrowed as she stared at the figure.","\"You can’t escape. Surrender now.\"","Seeing them stop at the alley’s entrance, Chen Yi grinned. \"Are you so sure?\"","\"Believe it or not, if I count down from ten, you’ll obediently let me go.\"","He then extended one hand, palm open toward Fang Hongxiu, and began to count down.","\"Ten.\"","\"Nine...\"","Fang Hongxiu frowned. Her eyes were fixed on Chen Yi, but her peripheral vision scanned the surroundings.","After confirming that there was nothing out of the ordinary, she couldn’t help but grit her teeth and scoff, \"Stop with the theatrics!\"","An Imprisonment Officer beside her immediately berated him, \"Who in the world are you, daring to interfere with the Imprisonment Department’s business time and time again?\"","Another spoke up as well. \"You can stay silent for now. Once we capture you, we have plenty of ways to make you talk.\"","Chen Yi ignored them, continuing his count, one number after another.","\"...Three, two, one.\"","\"Fall.\"","Before Fang Hongxiu could voice her confusion, she felt her entire body go limp. She couldn’t even hold onto the long Blade in her hand.","\"You... you... you used poison?\"","\"You...\"","As she glared fiercely at Chen Yi, the three people behind her had already collapsed to the ground.","CLANG, CLANG, CLANG.","After the crisp sound of three long Blades hitting the ground, Fang Hongxiu couldn’t hold on any longer either. She propped herself up with her Blade and knelt on the ground.","No matter how much she struggled, she couldn’t muster an ounce of her Power under the effects of the Qingfeng Drunk.","Seeing this, Chen Yi smiled and walked over.","As he walked, he pulled the bamboo hat on his head lower. \"Why chase me so relentlessly?\"","\"I already told you, you’d obediently let me go.\"","With that, Chen Yi came to Fang Hongxiu’s side. Seeing her struggling desperately, unable to even turn her neck, he couldn’t resist giving her a hand.","He gave Fang Hongxiu’s shoulder a gentle push, causing her to topple to the other side.","THUD.","Her bamboo hat flew off.","Fang Hongxiu lay limply on the rain-soaked ground, her Imprisonment Officer uniform drenched.","But on her beautiful face, her eyes were still wide open, trying to get a clear look at Chen Yi’s features.","But in the dim, rainy night, all she could see under the bamboo hat was a section of a rounded, bearded chin.","\"You... you’d better... not let me catch you...\"","If she weren’t currently paralyzed, she would have definitely pressed her long Blade against this bastard’s neck.","It wasn’t just her.","The three Imprisonment Officers beside her were also glaring fiercely at Chen Yi. \"You won’t get away.\"","\"Bastard, don’t let us catch you!\"","Chen Yi stepped over them noncommittally, sighing in his hoarse voice, \"I’m just a nobody. Let me go.\"","Fang Hongxiu gritted her teeth. \"N-Never.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi paused, turned his head to look at her, and chuckled.","\"Including last time, I’ve spared your lives twice now.\"","\"The old saying goes, ’Once is a pass, twice is a warning, but there won’t be a third time.’ Tell me, if we meet again, do you think I’ll still let you go?\"","With that, he swaggered off, disappearing into the dim curtain of rain.","But Fang Hongxiu still didn’t look away, her beautiful eyes fixed on the direction he had gone.","Faintly, she could still hear that despicable man’s voice.","\"Oh, right. The poison’s effects will last for four hours.\"","\"You’ve been out in the rain for so long, be careful not to catch a cold. Remember to take a hot bath and make some ginger tea when you get back.\"","\"And Hundred Households Fang, you’re so pretty, with such a nice figure. I hope no roving degenerates happen to pass by while you’re like this.\"","\"Otherwise... tsk, tsk, tsk...\"","After hearing this, Fang Hongxiu couldn’t help but curse, \"Bastard! Pervert!\"","But the thought of what Chen Yi had just said sent a chill through her.","The three Imprisonment Officers beside her had also heard his taunts. They all flinched, not daring to speak.","\"After we get back, remember what to say and what not to say.\"","\"Don’t worry, Lord Hundred Households. We know what to do...\"","Hearing this, Fang Hongxiu gritted her teeth, her heart filled with extreme hatred for the villain who had taken them down twice now.","’No matter what, I will hunt you down, bring you to justice, and throw you in the great prison!’","This minor interlude, of course, did not affect Chen Yi much.","However, he was a bit more careful on the way back, no longer lost in thought about the matter of the Hidden Guard as he had been before.","It took him about an hour.","Only then did he manage to slip past the Xiao Family’s Personal Guard and return to Spring Lotus Garden.","After washing up and changing into a clean long robe, Chen Yi didn’t rest. Instead, he went to his study.","He lit an oil lamp and sat alone at his desk.","Then, he glanced out the window and listened intently for a moment.","Seeing that Xiaodie, Xiao Wuge, and Pei Guanli were all sound asleep, he poured water to grind the ink, spread out a sheet of Yunsong Paper, and took up his brush to write and draw on it.","By now, midnight had passed.","Amidst the rush of the downpour, Spring Lotus Garden was filled with a chorus of croaking frogs, intermingled with the DRIP, DROP, SPLAT of the rain, creating a rather noisy ambiance.","Outside the two wooden buildings, eight lanterns swayed, illuminating two circles of light where flying raindrops were visible.","Faintly, within the study lit by the dim yellow candlelight, the distinct silhouette of a figure bent over a desk was cast upon the window paper.","About two hours later.","Chen Yi put down his Wolf Hair Brush. He looked at the circles and dots on the paper, muttering thoughtfully to himself.","\"’To resist foreign aggression, one must first bring peace to the home front.’\"","Compared to Ge the Third, Cui Qingwu, and that Lady Tiger, at least, Xiao Dongchen—the Gray Wolf—was far too selfish.","Add to that Xiao Wang, who controlled the Punishment Hall; Xiao Qiuyun, who had married into Duke Qian’s Mansion; and Xiao Ziqi, who served in the Military Supervision Institute...","These members of the second branch, colluding with the Hidden Guard from both inside and out, posed too great a threat to the Xiao Family.","He pondered for a moment.","While crossing out \"Xiao Dongchen\" on the paper, Chen Yi added a white piece to the chessboard in his mind: Liu Lang.","’I’ll use the incident with the summer grain fire in the Three Towns to get rid of him, then.’","’It’s a shame I don’t have three hundred thousand silver coins right now, otherwise...’","Chen Yi muttered a few more things to himself, then held the Yunsong Paper over the oil lamp until it burned to ash.","Fortunately, although he didn’t have that much silver, someone else did.","It seemed he would have to make Liu Lang put in some extra effort.","...","「Two days passed in the blink of an eye.」","The rain over Shu State Prefecture City had eased somewhat.","The downpour had turned into a steady drizzle.","It made the sweltering summer much more bearable.","But for some people, the cool, rainy days also had major downsides.","This was especially true for the artisans and street vendors who relied on good weather for their livelihood.","Fewer people on the streets naturally affected their business.","Even the tea sales at Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall were somewhat affected.","In particular, Wangji Tea, which was made specifically to relieve summer heat, saw sluggish sales as the weather cooled.","Even though it only accounted for ten percent of the revenue, it still pained Wang Ji.","And so, first thing in the morning, he brought his account books to the Xiao Mansion.","Ostensibly, he was there to inform the Xiao Family’s young lady, Xiao Wan’er, of the meeting date with the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall.","In reality, after leaving Jiaxing Garden, he turned and headed straight for Spring Lotus Garden.","From a distance, he spotted Chen Yi drinking tea in the pavilion and couldn’t help but feel a little emotional.","’This lord truly pays no mind to the affairs of the world.’","Setting aside the matter of Hundred Herbs Hall’s declining profits, just the recent buzz in Shu State Prefecture City would have kept any ordinary person from being so leisurely.","And the \"buzz\" he was thinking of was none other than the news that Guiyun Academy had gained two new masters accomplished in the Calligraphy Dao.","Ever since the news spread that day, most of the scholars in Shu State City had been discussing it.","Some envied the students of Guiyun Academy, some were grateful to have passed the County Examination and would soon be joining the academy, and others praised Chen Yi, also known as Chen Qingzhou.","\"’A scholar accomplished in the Calligraphy Dao will do something for Shu State.’ Tsk, tsk.\"","\"With that statement, regardless of Chen Qingzhou’s scholarship or whether he holds an official position, his reputation in Shu State, at least, won’t be poor.\"","\"You’re right, my friend, but your view is a bit one-sided.\"","\"How could that Chen Qingzhou lack scholarship? His previous works, like the birthday and wedding poems, all show his extraordinary knowledge.\"","\"Besides, he’s now the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law. Even without an official post, he’ll be well-fed and clothed for life.\"","\"True enough...\"","Amid all the chatter, no one questioned the truth of the matter.","This was especially true for the members of the great Noble Families. Regardless of whether they had children studying at Guiyun Academy, they all hoped to get Chen Yi to teach them a thing or two.","But of course, that was an impossibility.","As far as Wang Ji knew, everyone who had approached the Xiao Family had been turned away by the Old Master and the Young Lady.","Dealing with those who went to Guiyun Academy was even simpler.","Mr. Yue Ming simply presented his \"three-point agreement\" with Chen Yi, dispelling the notions of many.","Thinking of all this, Wang Ji approached with a smile and a bow. \"Mr. Qingzhou, I hope you’ll forgive my intrusion.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly and gestured for him to sit. \"Shopkeeper Wang, when it comes to business, let’s keep it business. You should still call me Shopkeeper.\"","\"I wouldn’t dare.\"","\"If word got out, all the scholars in Shu State would curse my name.\""]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170 - 159: A Little Cold Plum","paragraphs":["Chen Yi knew Wang Ji wasn’t just being polite.","After his visit to Guiyun Academy the day before yesterday, the discussions among the scholars in Shu State City had already reached his ears.","If he hadn’t been feigning illness at home and refusing visitors, Spring Lotus Garden would have been overflowing with people long ago.","Even so, many members of Noble Families who felt they had some influence with the Xiao Family were still flocking to Qingjing Residence and Jiaxing Garden.","Chen Yi was aware of all this.","It wasn’t because his Cultivation had improved, sharpening his hearing.","It was because of Xiaodie, his personal \"ace reporter.\"","He didn’t know if she was just particularly popular, but in the few times she left Spring Lotus Garden each day, she always returned with some news.","Which master from what family, what his former official rank was, had gone to see the Old Master.","Which lady and her daughter had visited Jiaxing Garden, and so on.","On top of that, Xiao Wan’er had been coming over to talk with him these past two days.","When she came in the morning, she would bring a bowl of ginger tea and tell him to drink it while it was hot.","If she came in the evening, she would arrange for dinner in Spring Lotus Garden.","Then, during the meal, she would tell him about the people she’d met that day, what a few of them had said, and what their current relationship with the Xiao Family was like.","Most of the time, Chen Yi let it go in one ear and out the other, making no promises.","Of course, Xiao Wan’er wouldn’t make any promises either, nor would she force Chen Yi to agree to those people’s requests to \"pull some strings.\"","In a way, she was helping Chen Yi fend off a lot of trouble.","However, not everyone in the Marquis’s Mansion was as reasonable as the Old Master and Xiao Wan’er.","For example, Xiao Dongchen from the second branch had approached Xiao Wan’er, asking her to help put in a word for him.","And someone from the third branch’s Xiao Shen had also come knocking.","Chen Yi had naturally refused them all.","These days, just annotating the workbooks for the hundred students in the study hall already took him a full hour, which was enough of a headache.","He had no desire to take on more students and become a beast of burden for Guiyun Academy.","After a few pleasantries, Wang Ji used some tea to write two words on the stone table, sighing as he spoke,","\"The dog days of summer are almost over. I expect it will affect tea sales.\"","Chen Yi glanced at the two words on the table—\"Seeking Advice\"—and smiled, but he didn’t rush to answer. He picked up the teapot and poured him a cup of tea.","\"Boss Wang, you think three steps ahead. Not bad.\"","Wang Ji looked embarrassed and raised his teacup to hide it. \"Mr. Qingzhou, you flatter me.\"","\"I’m sure you’re aware of Jishi Medicine Hall’s recent situation. With the continuous rain, the wharf and the East and West Markets are full of idle folk. Wangji Tea sales are down by ten percent compared to before.\"","\"Although many people still come because of our reputation, there will come a time when they’ve had their fill of this tea.\"","Chen Yi took a sip of tea, understanding his meaning. He shook his head with a smile.","\"In business, not losing money is a win. Earning less is still earning. Small fluctuations are perfectly normal.\"","\"Instead of wasting energy on this, you should think more about how to open up new sources of revenue.\"","The current five tea drinks were sufficient. It wasn’t that he couldn’t create new ones, but that it was unnecessary.","He had previously thought Wang Ji understood that the next priority was to expand Hundred Herbs Hall to other states and counties. Now, it seemed Wang Ji’s vision was still not farsighted enough.","As long as they could open a few more Hundred Herbs Hall branches, he was confident he could be rolling in money even if he gave Wangji Tea away for free.","After hearing this, Wang Ji lowered his head in thought for a moment. Realizing the root of the issue, he couldn’t help but look enlightened and cupped his hands. \"Thank you for your guidance, Mr. Qingzhou.\"","\"You’re too kind, Boss Wang.\"","\"I’m just an armchair strategist. In the future, Jishi Medicine Hall will have to rely more on your Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Mr. Qingzhou, you’re being too serious...\"","After a bit more small talk, Wang Ji took a letter from his robes and placed it on the table.","\"This is a thank-you letter from Liu Yun. He asked me to pass it on to you. His injuries have healed.\"","\"Oh?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. He guessed there had been progress with Liu Lang’s matter, so he simply put the letter away.","Seeing this, Wang Ji stood up to take his leave.","Just as Chen Yi was about to return to his study to read Liu Lang’s news, Xiao Wan’er approached with several people, each carrying a few account books.","Chen Yi saw them from a distance and had no choice but to put the letter away again.","He stood up and instructed Xiaodie to move the tea set to the other side of the railing while greeting,","\"Elder Sister.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded. After gesturing for Cui’er and Juan’er to put down the account books, she looked him up and down and said with a smile,","\"Your complexion is much better. You must be fine now.\"","Chen Yi nodded. ’If it weren’t for avoiding all those unnecessary social obligations, why would I need to feign illness?’ he thought.","\"Did no one from the mansion visit Jiaxing Garden today?\"","Xiao Wan’er shook her head gently. \"I’ve already instructed Huatang to turn them away for now.\"","After speaking, she paused and then pointed to the account books on the table.","\"Wang Ji just told me that the boss of Hundred Herbs Hall will arrive in Shu State in two days. I want to calculate our profits and buy him a presentable gift.\"","\"Elder Sister, you can decide. I don’t understand these things.\"","\"You don’t understand, or you’re just trying to be lazy?\"","Chen Yi paused, a little stunned. Seeing the mock reproach on her face, he said frankly, \"I really don’t.\"","\"I’ll choose to believe you for now.\"","Despite her words, after calculating all of next month’s expenses, Xiao Wan’er saw that the storeroom would still have a surplus of eleven thousand taels in silver coins. Joy bloomed across her features.","\"Brother-in-law, what do you think we should get him?\"","Him?","’Me, I suppose.’","Seeing that she was really preparing to buy a gift for him, Chen Yi’s heart stirred.","\"I heard from Wang Ji that the boss of Hundred Herbs Hall loves fishing. How about we get him a fishing set?\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. \"Is that a good idea?\"","\"We’ve earned so much silver from Hundred Herbs Hall. How can we just give him a fishing set?\"","\"Elder Sister, you probably don’t have much experience with fishing. There’s a lot more to fishing gear than meets the eye.\"","\"It’s true that the ordinary fishing gear in the East Market only costs fifty copper coins, and the ones in the West Market are only one or two taels in silver coins.\"","Chen Yi said with a serious expression, \"But for true fishing enthusiasts, the gear in their hands is worth at least eight or ten thousand taels of silver.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s beautiful eyes widened in surprise. \"Just for a fishing rod? Worth ten thousand taels?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"The rod itself is made from a special Ice Bamboo found only in the East Sea. It’s perfectly round, smooth, and jade-white, with incredible resilience. A single rod is worth three thousand taels in silver coins, and it’s so rare you can’t buy one even if you have the money.\"","\"The fishing line is woven from the sinew of a deep-sea whale. It’s said that even an Upper Three Grades Martial Arts Powerhouse would have trouble snapping it.\"","\"The hook is forged from Cold Iron. The moment an ordinary fish bites the bait, it’s frozen solid.\"","At this point, Chen Yi couldn’t help but rub his hands together, smiling. \"So tell me, how could it not be worth ten thousand taels of silver?\"","He shouldn’t have brought it up. Just talking about it made his own hands itch with desire.","He had first heard about this fishing set from Duke Qian and Sun Fu. It had an elegant name: \"A Little Cold Plum.\"","This was because when the hook was cast into the river, the combined effect of the Ice Bamboo and the Cold Iron would cause an ice flower to bloom on the water’s surface.","Evidently, Xiao Wan’er had never heard of \"A Little Cold Plum.\"","Even if she had, she would never spend that much money to give the Shopkeeper of Hundred Herbs Hall a fishing rod.","\"Let’s wait until we’re earning more before we gift something like this.\"","Chen Yi nodded with a hint of regret. \"Alright.\"","Seeing his expression, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but tease,","\"I think my brother-in-law wants one for himself.\"","\"Of course! It’s the ultimate treasure for any fishing enthusiast.\"","Xiao Wan’er saw the trace of longing on his face. Her heart stirred, and she asked thoughtfully,","\"Where can one buy that... Ice Bamboo fishing rod?\"","\"It’s called A Little Cold Plum, not some Ice Bamboo fishing rod. As for where to buy it, I have no idea.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded and said no more, but she silently committed this to memory.","Right now, the mansion’s finances were tight, and they didn’t have much in the way of silver coins.","If the storerooms were full in the future, she wouldn’t mind gifting Chen Yi \"A Little Cold Plum.\"","Although Chen Yi was eager, he also felt that spending so much money on a fishing rod was a bit extravagant, so he changed the subject.","This would prevent him from impulsively spending the silver coins he had on him.","As noon approached, Xiao Wan’er got up to leave.","\"The day after tomorrow, remember to accompany me to meet the boss from Hundred Herbs Hall. I hear his surname is also Chen, and his name is Chen Yu. Perhaps you two are related in some way.\"","\"I probably won’t have time. I have to go to the academy that day.\"","\"That’s fine. You can just say a few words to him when you come back for dinner.\"","\"...\"","Watching Xiao Wan’er give her instructions as she stood to return to Jiaxing Garden, Chen Yi sighed to himself.","’I don’t have a Clone Skill or some other divine power. How can I appear under the same roof as myself?’","’Looks like I’ll have to find an excuse to stay outside the mansion that day.’","After lunch, Chen Yi returned to his room and opened Liu Lang’s letter.","The contents were very short, just three lines.","I’ve agreed to Heizi’s proposal. The time has not been set.","I hear others want to get involved. Heizi is very pleased and says the chances of success are high this time.","Heizi has arranged for me to meet that person tomorrow night. Do you have any instructions?","After reading, Chen Yi’s brow furrowed slightly.","\"Others? High chances of success?\"","The first thing he thought of was the Hidden Guard.","But the Hidden Guard had previously said they needed to send a message to some Pavilion Master in the Capital Prefecture.","’Two days isn’t enough time for letters to go back and forth, is it?’","’Or did the Hidden Guard contact Black Tooth in advance?’","After a moment’s thought, Chen Yi had two suspicions.","The first was the \"Lady Tiger\" from the Hidden Guard.","From what he’d overheard the night before last, she already had connections with Black Tooth. It was possible she would make her move before receiving news from the Capital Prefecture.","The second was the Financier who was paying for the job, or some other figure with immense power and connections.","If it was the first, it wouldn’t be so bad. The Hidden Guard was influential, but they didn’t have many Martial Arts Powerhouses. The \"Sword Madman’s\" strength would be enough to handle them.","If it was the latter... he was afraid he would have to come up with a plan.","\"Tsk, I knew things wouldn’t go this smoothly. Luckily, there’s still time.\"","’It seems a trip to Hundred Herbs Hall will be necessary tomorrow.’","’I wonder if the Old Master and the others have gotten wind of this,’ Chen Yi muttered to himself, glancing out the window in the direction of Qingjing Residence and shaking his head slightly.","’Whether they know or not doesn’t matter.’","’This time, I’m going to do something. I’m going to take care of some people.’","...","At dinnertime, Xiao Wan’er sent a messenger to say that she was hosting a banquet for the Tang Family’s first lady and her daughter, so she wouldn’t be coming over.","Chen Yi had already heard the sounds from Jiaxing Garden, so he told Xiaodie to bring their food from the back kitchen.","Speaking of which, it seemed the spread of his Calligraphy Dao had also brought some benefits to the Xiao Family.","Take the Tang Family, for example.","Although Tang Zixing hadn’t shown his face, his wife had been visiting the Xiao Family quite frequently these past few days.","Although she came for the sake of her son Tang Ye’s education, everyone in the Xiao Family was happy to see it happen.","Chen Yi was aware of this but didn’t try to take credit.","After all, every matter had its pros and cons.","In the eyes of the Old Master and others, this was a good thing.","But in the eyes of others with ulterior motives, it was an out-and-out bad thing.","In any case, he still needed to be careful for the time being.","Just as Xiaodie finished preparing dinner, Xiao Wuge and Pei Guanli arrived in the living room.","\"Brother-in-law, guess what my Cultivation level is now!\"","\"Mid-Eighth Grade.\"","\"Yep, yep! Aren’t I amazing?\"","He didn’t know if it was because of the duel between Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang or for some other reason, but she had been cultivating diligently for several days straight.","If not for the fact that the meals Xiaodie sent over were always scraped clean, he would have suspected the Tiger Girl was sick.","Fortunately, hearing that her Cultivation had broken through was good news.","\"What about you, Brother-in-law?\"","Seeing Pei Guanli’s blunt question, Chen Yi replied irritably, \"The Middle Three Grades.\"","\"Huh?\"","Chen Yi rapped her on the head. \"What ’huh’? I’m a Ninth-Grade Martial Artist. What’s there to ask about my Cultivation?\"","Seeing this, Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie laughed heartlessly at the side.","But the Tiger Girl wasn’t annoyed. ’I’m someone who knows Brother-in-law’s secret,’ she thought.","’Those who don’t know are not to blame. Ignorance is innocence.’","After some laughter and a short rest,","Seeing it was getting late, Chen Yi returned to his room, sat cross-legged on his bed, and began to practice the Four Symbols Skill.","In a way, what he’d told the Tiger Girl wasn’t exactly a lie.","Because his breakthrough to the Middle Three Grades was happening tonight!"]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171 - 160: Divine Position, Spiritual Essence","paragraphs":["\"The Four Symbols are the Cyan Dragon, Black Tortoise, Vermilion Bird, and White Tiger. They represent the Spiritual Qi of the Four Directions, which are Wood, Water, Fire, and Gold...\"","Chen Yi silently recited the Cultivation Technique Mantra for the Four Symbols Skill, guiding the True Essence in his body to circulate through the twelve Main Meridians and the Ren and Du Meridians in a grand cycle.","His cultivation had now reached the Perfection stage of the Seventh Grade Realm. The True Essence within him had liquified from its gaseous state, and both its quality and quantity far surpassed what they were before.","As a result, when the True Essence surged through his meridians, one could faintly hear a rumbling sound, like a great river rushing forth.","At this moment, as these sounds intertwined, the surrounding Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi seemed to reverse its flow like a river, pouring from his limbs and bones into his meridians and Sea of Qi.","After the Four Symbols Skill had completed four grand cycles, Chen Yi felt his consciousness drift upward from his Dantian and the Sea of Qi in his Chest, along the Ren and Du Meridians, until it finally came to rest at his Forehead Acupoint.","Instantly, he felt his consciousness settle upon a sea of clouds that had no substance.","In a daze, he saw phantom images emerge one after another from within the gray sea of clouds, taking up positions in the four cardinal directions.","He could vaguely make out the phantoms of the Four Divine Beasts—the Cyan Dragon, White Tiger, Vermilion Bird, and Black Tortoise.","’Guide the Four Directions Spiritual Qi to merge into the Sea of Qi, opening the Four Divine Positions...’","The mantra for the Four Symbols Skill suddenly surfaced in his mind.","Chen Yi had an epiphany—merging into the Sea of Qi meant not just the Dantian and the Sea of Qi in his Chest, but also the Sea of Qi in his forehead.","Only by opening the Sea of Qi in his forehead could he establish the Four Divine Positions.","As he came to this understanding, the four faint, rumbling cries he’d heard before grew clearer.","Listening closely, a tiger’s roar, a dragon’s cry, a tortoise’s bellow, and a phoenix’s call echoed one after another in his ears.","In the next moment, the circulation path of the Four Symbols Skill changed.","The True Essence that had originally returned to his Dantian and the Sea of Qi in his Chest now merged with the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi like a whale swallowing the sea, pouring straight into the Sea of Qi in his forehead.","With a single breath, the True Essence within the Sea of Qi in his forehead became full and abundant.","With the second breath, the True Essence within all three Seas of Qi—the Dantian, the chest, and the forehead—surged in unison.","And with the third breath, the True Essence transformed from liquid into something like mercury. He could vaguely feel four-colored streams of light entwining around it, as brilliant as a rainbow.","As Chen Yi noticed these changes, a line of large, golden characters floated before his eyes:","[Cultivation successful. Cultivation: Lower Sixth Grade.]","[Four Symbols Skill (Earth Tier) has been promoted to Mastery Level Perfection. Divine Positions opened. Blessed by the spiritual qi of Wood, Water, Fire, and Gold.]","[Black Tortoise Concealment Technique has been blessed by the Wood and Water Spirits, allowing it to Nourish the Body and cultivate essence.]","[Mountain Shattering Fist has been blessed by the Fire Spirit, gaining Violent Power.]","[Dragon-slaying Spear has been blessed by the Gold Spirit, gaining increased Sharp Power.]","[Hundred Flowers Palm has been blessed by the Water Spirit, gaining Flowing Power.]","[Meteor Butterfly Step has been blessed by the Wood Spirit, gaining Surging Power.]","[Wandering Dragon and Phoenix has been blessed by the Wood and Fire Spirits, gaining increased Vortex Power...]","Seeing all this, Chen Yi paused for a moment. \"It’s done.\"","’An Earth Tier Four Symbols Skill already grants such powerful blessings. How strong would it be if it reached the Celestial Tier?’","However, he had just reached the Middle Three Grades. The effects of his True Essence and the blessings of the four spirits weren’t obvious yet, and were far less tangible than his Dao Intent.","Only when his cultivation rose further would he be able to display the true power of this technique.","’The Upper Three Grades?’","He clicked his tongue. ’No wonder Liu Lang said he was defeated by Xiao Jinghong in a single move.’","’The gap in strength between an Upper Three Grades martial artist and one from the Middle Three Grades is absolutely massive.’","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi once again immersed his consciousness in the circulation of the Four Symbols Skill.","The surrounding Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi returned to calm, with only faint wisps of spiritual qi being drawn into and devoured by his body.","「In Jiaxing Garden.」","\"Hmm?\"","Xie Tingyun, who had been sitting in meditation with her eyes closed, seemed to sense the unusual disturbance in the surrounding world. She snapped her eyes open and walked out of the wooden building.","\"This feeling is...\"","She furrowed her brow, looking in all directions as she carefully sensed her surroundings.","A moment later, Xie Tingyun frowned slightly, a hint of suspicion on her face. \"Is it gone?\"","The Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi had indeed just fluctuated, however weakly.","She wouldn’t have sensed it incorrectly.","\"That felt like someone breaking through in their cultivation.\"","Xie Tingyun tilted her head, her beautiful eyes glancing left and right. None of the possibilities seemed likely.","’There’s only a frail scholar and a girl from the Mountain Race in Spring Lotus Garden. They couldn’t possibly have caused such a change in the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi.’","’In Four Directions Hall, there’s a frail old scholar, also with no cultivation to speak of.’","’The only possibility is the Armored Warriors in the central or front courtyards.’","Xie Tingyun thought for a moment, muttered a few words to herself, then shook her head and returned to the wooden building to sit cross-legged.","She had two tasks on this trip down the mountain: one was the old demon from the Illusory Sound Sect, and the other was protecting the Xiao Family’s eldest young miss.","And the second task was more important.","Therefore, she would have to wait until her business with the Xiao Family was concluded before she could free her hands to hunt down the Illusory Sound Sect.","’In any case, I can’t let that old demon from the Illusory Sound Sect have an easy time of it.’","...","Night had fallen, and most of the lights in the Qingjing Residence had already been extinguished.","In the courtyard, only two lanterns hung outside the pavilion and two outside the main hall.","As the wind of the rainy night blew, the lanterns swayed gently, their candlelight flickering and casting a hazy glow.","Faintly, a dark figure vaulted over the rear wall into the courtyard.","After a brief pause, he walked straight into the main hall through the open doors and, with light steps, lit the candles on the altar.","As the light flared up, the old patriarch sitting quietly in the Grandmaster’s Chair opened his eyes, glanced at him, and waved his hand in a gesture.","\"Sit and speak.\"","The newcomer was tall and dressed in black. After bowing in greeting, he first closed the hall doors before sitting down on a chair at the far end of the room.","He seemed to habitually keep his upper body in the shadows.","The man in black spoke in a low voice, \"Marquis, there’s been trouble.\"","Hearing this, the old patriarch’s expression remained unchanged as he asked, \"What is it?\"","For some time now, the great Xiao Family had been like a lump of coal, riddled with holes. He had long since grown accustomed to trouble and unexpected changes.","’Nothing surprises me anymore, I suppose.’","\"My Hidden Guards stationed in the Black Market were completely wiped out last night.\"","\"Overnight?\"","\"Yes.\"","The man in black wore a dark cloth over his face, and his large, dark eyes were filled with gravity as he said:","\"Although I haven’t yet identified who was behind it, the number of people in the entire Black Market with that kind of power can be counted on one hand.\"","\"The most likely suspect is Black Tooth of Bright Moon Building. He controls the entire Black Market, so finding our Hidden Guards wouldn’t be difficult for him.\"","\"The next possibility would be the practitioners of the Evil Demonic Dao kept by those other families.\"","The man in black paused, then looked at the old patriarch and said with a hint of suspicion, \"But I can’t figure out their motive for acting.\"","The old patriarch lowered his head in thought for a moment before saying in a grave voice, \"When things are this unusual, there must be something sinister afoot.\"","\"Go and investigate if Black Tooth is planning any major moves.\"","\"Understood. I’ll have someone contact Black Tooth shortly.\"","\"And don’t overlook those other families. They are opportunists who always follow the wind. If someone takes the lead, they won’t mind making the situation in Shu State even more chaotic.\"","The man in black nodded, already understanding the meaning behind the old patriarch’s words.","An act that so clearly targeted the Xiao Family would likely be followed by an even bigger move.","If they didn’t investigate thoroughly and prepare in advance, they would inevitably face a situation where \"everyone kicks a man when he’s down.\"","After a moment of silence, the old patriarch, certain he had no other instructions, asked, \"Anything else?\"","The man in black thought for a moment and said, \"Miss Cui has shown no unusual activity recently.\"","\"When Chen Yunfan is around, the two of them stroll about and amuse themselves together.\"","\"When Chen Yunfan is not here, Cui Qingwu stays inside Tingyu Pavilion and never goes out. It’s as if she came to Shu State specifically for him.\"","Hearing this, the old patriarch chuckled. \"This Great Young Master of the Chen Family is truly fortunate.\"","The man in black was puzzled. \"Fortunate?\"","\"The fortune of his birth.\"","\"He is the direct heir of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family, he’s betrothed to someone from the Qinghe Cui Family, and now he even has the Holy Emperor’s trust, holding the title of ’Imperial Top Scholar’.\"","\"It’s no exaggeration to say he was born with a silver spoon in his mouth.\"","As he said this, the old patriarch couldn’t help but sigh with some emotion. \"Others can have smooth sailing for twenty years. I hope our Wuge can, too.\"","The man in black smiled and agreed, \"The Young Master is blessed by heaven. He will naturally turn misfortune into fortune and grow up smoothly.\"","The old patriarch nodded, a serious expression returning to his aged face.","\"We can’t let our guard down. Continue.\"","The man in black said, \"Aside from Miss Cui, the person who helped my subordinate that night has not yet been found, but they should be near the West Market.\"","\"I have already ordered my men to pay close attention to the people near the West Market. We should be able to confirm their identity the next time they make a move.\"","After listening to the man in black, the old patriarch grunted in acknowledgment. \"Anyone who has helped our Xiao Family, every single one of them, will be richly rewarded in the future.\"","The man in black nodded. \"There is one last matter. The people from the Jing State Liu Family will soon arrive in the Prefecture City.\"","The old patriarch’s hand, which was gripping his cane, paused. A stern look appeared on his face. \"Who is coming?\"","\"Liu Yu from the second branch, as well as Second Young Master Liu Wen and Third Miss Liu Zhaoxue from the Liu Family’s main branch.\"","\"Liu Yu isn’t particularly famous. Although he can’t compare to his elder brother, Liu Zhen, the Governor of the Jing State Imprisonment Department, his status in the Liu Family is not low.\"","\"He is in charge of businesses like Xinglin Hall and Liu’s Cloth Shop.\"","The man in black paused for a moment. Seeing that the old patriarch was just listening quietly, he continued:","\"Second Young Master Liu is a scholar. He passed the provincial examinations last year, but for some unknown reason, he did not participate in this year’s metropolitan examinations.\"","\"As for Third Miss Liu Zhaoxue... our Hidden Guards don’t have much information on her, only that she is very beautiful and is known as the ’Number One Beauty of Jing State.’\"","After listening, the old patriarch merely gave a slight nod, then lowered his head to look at the light and shadows at his feet.","The hall fell silent.","Only the pitter-patter of rain outside the door and the soft rustling of willow branches in the slight breeze could be heard.","A moment later, the old patriarch looked up at him and ordered in a grave voice:","\"Have the Hidden Guards watch them closely.\"","\"I want to know where they go, who they see, and what they say every day after they arrive in Shu State. I want to be clear on every single detail, no matter how small.\"","\"Understood.\"","\"Also, the same goes for Liu Hong.\"","\"After that case was closed, he and the Governor’s Office have made no moves. They must be waiting for the people from Jing State to arrive as well.\"","As the old patriarch spoke, a hint of killing intent appeared on his face. \"If Liu Yu and the others don’t accept this outcome, there will be more trouble with the grain tax for the Three Towns.\"","\"We might just have to show the Liu Family the sharp end of a blade this time.\"","Hearing this, the man in black’s gaze also grew solemn. He stood up and bowed. \"I obey your command.\"","\"Alright, handle these matters together.\"","The man in black paused, then hesitated slightly before asking, \"Marquis, should we inform the Second Miss about these matters?\"","The old patriarch thought for a moment, then shook his head. \"Don’t distract her for now. The Mid-Autumn Festival is not far off. It won’t be too late to tell her when she returns.\"","\"I understand.\"","After the man left, the old patriarch sat quietly for a moment, then rose, blew out the candles on the table, and slowly paced to his side room.","Leaving behind only a low, inaudible sigh:","\"Ten more years... these old bones of mine have to hold on...\""]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172 - 161: Traveling with a Beauty","paragraphs":["A night passed, but the skies above Shu State remained thick with dark clouds.","The continuous drizzle paused for a moment before starting up again, this time a little heavier, as if the heavens couldn’t bear to see too many people walking about outside.","Unfortunately, in weather like this, few people appreciated the sentiment.","More often than not, people would mutter a few curses at the \"damned heavens,\" clearly displeased with the days of endless rain.","But there were also many people unaffected by the weather, their faces wreathed in smiles, looking overjoyed.","For example, some idlers could use it as an excuse to sleep in.","Or the shop owners selling Oil Paper Umbrellas and Raincoats.","All of them wore smiles on their faces.","Chen Yi was one of them.","However, he wasn’t happy because of the rainy weather, but because of a breakthrough in his Cultivation Realm.","In the morning, past the midpoint of the Yin hour, he finished his practice and felt the True Essence surging within his body.","Since then, the smile had not left his face.","If last night Chen Yi had only a vague inkling that his various Techniques would grow stronger after being enhanced by the Four Symbols Skill’s Divine Position Spiritual Essence...","...then at this moment, the direct sensation of holding a river of stars in his grasp now filled his body and mind.","Whether it was his Pile Skill, Fist Technique, Step Technique, or the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique, under the enhancement of True Essence, their power had increased by ten to twenty percent.","And that was without even factoring in the boost from his Martial Arts Realm.","If he used his full strength, forget about others; even Cui Qingwu, who had heavily injured him that night, would have a hard time if she ran into him now.","Chen Yi indulged in this fantasy for a moment before calming his mind and glancing at the light screen:","[Opportunity: 128]","[Daily Intelligence - Yellow Rank Top Grade: At a quarter past the Wu hour, in the East Market’s Jishi Medicine Hall, Ma Liangcai will receive a ’Divine Doctor’ plaque. A small amount of Opportunity can be obtained.]","After reading it, Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"Jishi Medicine Hall?\"","’Old Ma’s finally made something of himself.’","’He’s even getting a ’Divine Doctor’ plaque from someone.’","But upon further thought, the smile on Chen Yi’s face faded a little.","He knew very well what level Ma Liangcai’s Medical Dao was at.","Even with his guidance, he was only slightly better than Old Li and the others.","How could a Physician of that caliber possibly cure people with complicated or terminal illnesses?","After some thought, Chen Yi decided to go and check it out.","He just couldn’t shake the feeling that something was off.","After making his decision, Chen Yi glanced again at the Opportunity and Dao Intent on the light screen.","After a moment’s hesitation, he raised his Spear Dao to the Great Success Realm.","With this, of the eight paths he practiced—including Calligraphy Dao, Medical Dao, Chess Dao, Martial Arts Body, Punch, Step, and Spear—only his Chess Dao remained at the Minor Success Realm. All the others had reached the Great Success Realm.","As for his various Techniques, only the Dragon-Falling Spear Technique and the Thousand Hands Chess Manual were at the Skilled Level. The others could not be upgraded further, having reached the peak of the Mastery Level.","In addition, he still had the Brocade Spring Saber Technique and the \"Carefree Travel\" Zither Score left to practice when it was convenient.","’You can never have too many skills.’","’Perhaps by practicing more of them and letting them cross-reference each other, I might get another chance for an epiphany.’","That being said, epiphanies were indeed an Opportunity that relied heavily on luck.","So far, only his Calligraphy Dao had advanced to the Great Success Realm through an epiphany, which he’d had after writing a poem for Xiao Wan’er.","Despite practicing the others for so long, none had resulted in an epiphany.","With these thoughts, Chen Yi waited for the Profound Mysteries of the Great Success Realm Spear Dao to settle in his mind before calling for Xiaodie to help him wash up and get dressed.","\"Young Master, are you going out today?\"","\"Mhm, I’m heading to the Medicine Hall today. I haven’t been in a while, and I’m afraid the Eldest Miss will give me a talking-to.\"","Seeing him make up stories about the Eldest Miss with a straight face, Xiaodie couldn’t help but giggle.","\"You’re joking again, Young Master. The Eldest Miss would never blame you for that.\"","\"Not only will the Eldest Miss not blame you, but neither will the other masters in the mansion. Not now, not ever.\"","Chen Yi straightened his clothes, headed downstairs first, and casually replied, \"Is that so?\"","Xiaodie followed behind him, smiling. \"Yes,\" she said. \"You haven’t been out these past few days, Young Master, so you haven’t seen how everyone in the mansion has been praising you.\"","\"Praising me how?\"","\"They’re all saying that the masters of the various courtyards these past few days...\"","It all came down to the fact that he had taught several great masters of Calligraphy at Guiyun Academy.","There had been a constant stream of visitors to the mansion.","Under these circumstances, the masters of the mansion naturally wouldn’t speak ill of him in front of their guests.","Even Xiao Xuanshuo and Xiao Wang, who had never liked him, had to say a few good words.","\"Qingzhou? I saw long ago that his scholarship was profound. Otherwise, on the day of the Marquis’s birthday, the Holy Emperor wouldn’t have given him a personal verbal edict.\"","\"Qingzhou’s knowledge is impressive, and his handwriting is excellent, but it’s no use coming to me.\"","When words like these were overheard, they inevitably spread throughout the mansion.","Xiaodie, with her simple heart, loved hearing such praise for him, as if she shared in the glory.","Chen Yi, however, felt nothing.","’When people want something from you, words like that aren’t really praise, nor are they sincere. ’Flattery’ is a more fitting description.’","’It felt less genuine than Xiaodie saying, ’Young Master is a really good person,’ or Pei Guanli saying, ’Brother-in-law is a nice guy.’’","And as it happened, Pei Guanli and Xiaodie had said just that after breakfast.","Chen Yi quite enjoyed it and tactfully avoided mentioning his promise to bring them back some things when he returned.","Xiao Wuge wanted something too.","But before he could open his mouth, Xiao Wan’er arrived in the hall with Shen Huatang.","Compared to before, her complexion had improved a great deal. It was no longer a sickly pale, but had a healthy touch of color.","Her originally thin face had filled out a little, making her even more radiant.","Chen Yi habitually used his Qi Observation Skill to take a look and, confirming that her health was being well-maintained, beckoned for her to sit.","\"On a rainy day like this, you should stay indoors more, Wan’er. You don’t want to catch a chill.\"","It would have been fine if he hadn’t mentioned it, but the moment he brought up catching a chill, Xiao Wan’er was reminded of that one experience as if it had happened just a moment ago.","Her lovely face couldn’t help but flush red as she shot him a playful glare.","\"I’m dressed warmly, and I drink medicinal soup every day. My health has improved a lot.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, then followed up with a few compliments.","These words could also be categorized as flattery, but they brought a wide smile to Xiao Wan’er’s face.","He praised her so much that she even started to feel a little embarrassed.","She quickly changed the subject. \"Last night, I put together a list of gifts for Chen Yu. I’d like to go out shopping today. Are you coming?\"","\"Me?\"","Chen Yi hesitated slightly. He wanted to refuse, but seeing Xiao Wan’er’s earnest expression, he nodded.","\"As it happens, I need to make a trip to the Medicine Hall. Let’s go together.\"","The words had barely left his mouth when, before Xiao Wan’er’s smile could fully blossom, Xiao Wuge raised his hand.","\"I’m going too, I’m going too!\"","\"Eldest Sister, Brother-in-law, I haven’t been out in ages! Take me with you.\"","Seeing his pitiful look, Xiao Wan’er hesitated before nodding. \"Alright then, I’ll have someone inform your etiquette tutor to take the day off.\"","Xiao Wuge immediately broke into a grin, grabbing Xiaodie and running upstairs, saying he needed to change his clothes.","Seeing this, Chen Yi looked at the Tiger Girl. \"What about you? Staying home or coming out for a stroll?\"","But Pei Guanli’s expression changed, and she shook her head repeatedly.","With a jingle of ornaments, she said, \"Nope, not going! We went out shopping for days on end before. I’ve had more than enough.\"","As she spoke, Pei Guanli looked at Shen Huatang and asked, \"Sister Huatang must feel the same way, right?\"","\"Not at all.\"","In front of Xiao Wan’er, Shen Huatang naturally couldn’t say what she was really thinking.","Truth be told, the three of them had spent several days in a row shopping before, and they had truly explored every corner of Shu State Prefecture City.","After a short rest, Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun went to get the carriage.","Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Wuge, and Xiaodie sat in the carriage. It wasn’t too crowded.","Before long, the carriage left the Marquis’s Mansion and headed straight for Kangning Street in the North City.","By now, it was past the Mao hour.","Even with the light rain, there were quite a few pedestrians on the road.","This was especially true for a place like Kangning Street, which was popular among scholars and young ladies from prominent families.","From a distance, all one could see was a sea of people holding Oil Paper Umbrellas.","Xiao Wan’er looked out the window, took a piece of paper from her sleeve, and handed it to Chen Yi.","\"This is the list I put together. Take a look and tell me if it’s suitable.\"","Chen Yi took it and glanced over it. It was mostly calligraphy supplies, paintings, and antiques.","\"What do you think?\"","\"It should be fine, but it’s a bit much.\"","\"One can never be too courteous. After all, considering how much silver was involved, it makes sense to buy him a few more gifts.\"","Since she put it that way, Chen Yi nodded. \"You’re the one making the decisions.\"","Xiao Wan’er chided him playfully, \"See if there’s anything you want to add.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment. Other than a fishing rod, there didn’t seem to be anything he particularly wanted for himself.","After a moment’s thought, he came up with something. \"How about we get him an Ancient Zither or a long blade?\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback. \"Is... is that appropriate?\"","In this day and age, many scholars were proficient with melodies, and many also knew Saber Techniques.","However, unless one knew the recipient’s hobbies beforehand, very few people would specifically give such uncommon gifts.","\"I only mention it because I heard from Wang Ji that their boss has excellent Saber Technique and is also skilled at playing the Zither. If the price isn’t too high, it might be good to buy one just in case.\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t suspect a thing and nodded. \"Then let’s buy an Ancient Zither. The mansion has plenty of long blades, all masterpieces by famous craftsmen. When we get back, I’ll have Huatang pick one out from the armory.\"","Chen Yi, of course, did not refuse.","However, a different thought was forming in his mind.","He was imagining the awkward scene that would unfold in the future when Xiao Wan’er discovered the truth.","He reckoned Xiao Wan’er would either fly into a rage out of shame or become angry from embarrassment. In any case, she wouldn’t let him off easy.","The thought of such a scene brought an irrepressible smile to Chen Yi’s face.","Noticing his expression, Xiao Wan’er’s heart stirred.","\"Speaking of which, that Boss Chen’s hobbies are quite similar to yours.\"","Chen Yi’s smile froze. \"Er, I don’t think so?\"","Xiao Wan’er watched him with a faint, unreadable smile, her beautiful eyes reflecting the slight unease on his face as she said:","\"You are a master of Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, and you also love to fish. That Boss Chen happens to like fishing and is also skilled in the Zither Dao, isn’t that right?\"","Chen Yi grunted in agreement, his expression returning to normal. \"He’s probably a scholar. It’s normal for them to enjoy such things.\"","\"That’s true.\"","After a bit more small talk, the topic was finally dropped, and Chen Yi relaxed inwardly.","’They say a woman’s intuition is sharp. I have to admit, it’s true.’","Of course, Xiao Wan’er didn’t actually think Boss Chen was Chen Yi; she had merely connected their similar hobbies.","She then began to talk about Madam Tang’s visit the previous evening.","\"I heard that Guiyun Academy’s gates have been nearly trampled down these past few days. People have been coming from the Prefecture City and even from neighboring states and counties.\"","\"Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and that student named Ma Guan have to write several calligraphy pieces every day.\"","\"Along with the calligraphy pieces you left at the academy, they’re all put on display for visitors to see.\"","Chen Yi chuckled and said, \"I imagine the Headmaster must be very happy.\"","Xiao Wan’er smiled and nodded. \"Madam Tang said that it’s a good thing her son, Tang Ye, got into that study hall early. Otherwise, those who came later would probably have to resort to all sorts of tricks to snatch a spot.\"","\"Snatch?\"","\"Yes. After your three-point agreement with Mr. Yue Ming spread, the number of students was fixed at one hundred and couldn’t be changed. Naturally, the latecomers have to find a way in.\"","\"I heard someone already offered a thousand silver coins to trade for a spot, but no one would take it.\"","\"Later, someone even offered five hundred Gold, but Mr. Yue Ming sternly refused.\"","Chen Yi said, \"Five hundred... Gold?\"","’If they sold all one hundred spots, wouldn’t that be an easy fifty thousand Gold?’","’I hope the Headmaster can resist such a temptation.’","It took them the better part of the morning to finish shopping on Kangning Street.","They not only bought plenty of gifts for Chen Yu but also picked up a few useful things for Xiao Wuge.","Mostly books and the like.","When Chen Yi saw that the carriage was nearly full, he suggested they head to Jishi Medicine Hall first.","Xiao Wan’er naturally had no objections. \"Perfect. There’s a restaurant in the East Market that’s very good. I remember my father taking me and my second sister there when we were little.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"In that case, I’ll have to go and try it...\""]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173 - 162: A Meeting Gift for My Madam","paragraphs":["It had been raining incessantly for days, and the artisans in the East Market were long past restless.","Especially those with families to support.","They relied on their daily performances to earn an income.","When the weather was good,","if the crowd was generous, they could make over a hundred copper coins.","Even with fewer passersby, they could still make several dozen.","It wasn’t much, but at least it was enough to feed their families.","But on overcast, rainy days, forget setting up a stall to perform—it was hard enough just to find a dry place to take shelter.","Their situation was much like the saying, \"when the roof leaks, it pours all night.\"","Thus, as noon approached, quite a few of these people were taking shelter inside the Jishi Medicine Hall on the edge of the East Market.","Some were alone.","Like the fortune teller, who had spread his cloth banner beneath him and was half-reclining on it, muttering, \"Less complaining saves energy. Then you don’t feel hungry.\"","Others truly had families in tow—a group of three, a grandparent and grandchild, old and young, all dressed in ragged clothes.","Perhaps feeling self-conscious, they huddled in a corner just inside the entrance, trying their best not to interfere with the Medicine Hall’s business.","Still others tried to get something out of the Medicine Hall directly.","\"Accountant Liu, it’s raining so hard today, it must be a problem for you all to even get lunch. How about I run errands for you?\"","A young man in short clothes with dark skin said with a cheeky grin, \"Just a bite to eat in return would be fine.\"","Liu Quan shot him a sideways glance and waved his hand dismissively. \"Go cool off somewhere else. Don’t bother me.\"","If Chen Yi hadn’t said something along the lines of \"making things convenient for others makes things convenient for yourself,\" he would have chased these people out long ago.","Before, these people still had some spare cash and could buy a few bottles of tea.","But after so many days, they were all sallow-faced and gaunt. It was clear they could barely afford food, so how could they possibly spend two copper coins on Wangji Tea?","\"If you’re not going to let me, then just say so. Why be so fierce?\"","The dark-skinned young man grumbled, sitting down next to the fortune teller and squeezing onto his cloth banner, sighing dramatically.","\"When is this cursed weather going to end?\"","The fortune teller, with his head pillowed on his hands, glanced up at him and said with a smile,","\"How about I read your fortune?\"","The dark-skinned young man nodded. \"For free.\"","\"There’s no such thing as a free lunch. You’ve miscalculated if you think you can squeeze any silver coins out of me.\"","Before the young man could reply, a brawny man nearby sneered,","\"Old Ji, don’t you go swindling people.\"","\"With your knack for palm reading and matchmaking, you barely make a few coins a day. You think you can tell when the heavens will stop raining?\"","\"Hey, you looking down on me?\"","\"Today, I’ll have to show you what I’m made of, just to save face.\"","\"Let Old Ji do it! Let’s see what he comes up with...\"","Just as the crowd in Jishi Medicine Hall was getting rowdy, the sound of gongs, drums, and suonas erupted from outside.","It sounded festive, but not quite like the music for a wedding.","Before long, the procession of musicians drew closer and stopped at the entrance of Jishi Medicine Hall.","The piercing music, combined with the noise inside the hall, made the already-irritated Liu Quan’s brow furrow.","He immediately dropped his ledger and abacus, strode out of the Medicine Hall, and demanded rudely,","\"This is a Medicine Hall! How can you make such a racket here? If you disturb the patients, can you bear the responsibility?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, the music from the procession outside stopped.","A thin old man in brocade robes, standing before two men holding a long object wrapped in red cloth, smiled and clasped his hands.","\"We are here today to deliver a plaque to Ma Liangcai, Divine Doctor Ma. It was inconsiderate of us. I hope Accountant Liu will forgive us.\"","Liu Quan was taken aback. ’A plaque for Old Ma?’","When it sank in, his impatience vanished, replaced by a look of delight. He quickly called back into the hall,","\"Old Ma, come quick! They’re here to deliver a plaque for you!\"","\"This is wonderful news! Truly wonderful!\"","Hearing the commotion, Ma Liangcai walked out of the Medicine Hall with a puzzled expression, followed by a crowd of artisans craning their necks to see the spectacle.","From a distance, it looked as if heads were sprouting from his back.","Ma Liangcai paid no mind to his surroundings. He studied the thin old man and asked with a frown,","\"And you are, old sir?\"","He didn’t remember ever treating this man, nor did he recognize anyone in the procession behind him.","The thin old man, however, stepped forward with a smile and took his arm. \"Divine Doctor Ma, a great man like you is bound to be forgetful.\"","\"Have you forgotten? You once treated a child when you were practicing medicine at the foot of Wumeng Mountain.\"","’The foot of Wumeng Mountain?’","A chill went down Ma Liangcai’s spine. He realized this man had not come with good intentions.","Back when he was knocking around the Wumeng Mountain area, he had been a complete fraud, swindling people for food and drink.","He could handle minor illnesses and injuries, curing them with a bit of medicine.","But when faced with more complex cases, he would just send the patients to a more skilled Physician and pocket a referral fee.","After a moment of silence, Ma Liangcai forced a smile and clasped his hands. \"I don’t recall. I must ask you to leave, old sir.\"","Seeing this, the thin old man maintained his sincere expression. \"For Divine Doctor Ma to say so puts this old one in a difficult position.\"","\"After all, you saved my young master. Even if you’ve forgotten, you can still accept this plaque today.\"","He paused, then turned to Liu Quan beside him. \"Wouldn’t you agree?\"","Liu Quan didn’t know the full story, but he knew that a \"Divine Doctor\" plaque would be good for the Medicine Hall’s business.","So he pushed through the crowd, first whispering a word of encouragement to Ma Liangcai, then said with a laugh,","\"The old sir is right. Of course we can accept a plaque.\"","With that, he stepped forward to unveil the plaque by lifting the red cloth.","Seeing this, the old man smiled and took a step back.","Just then, a calm voice came from beyond the crowd of onlookers.","\"Wait a moment.\"","Liu Quan’s hand froze. He looked up and around.","He saw the circle of Oil Paper Umbrellas part, revealing Chen Yi at the opening.","Without hesitation, Liu Quan hurried over and bowed. \"Shopkeeper, what brings you here?\"","Chen Yi glanced at him, then walked into the crowd, holding his Oil Paper Umbrella.","He looked at the old man, whose smile had faded slightly, and then at Ma Liangcai’s uneasy expression, and said calmly,","\"Old sir, we appreciate the sentiment, but please take the plaque back.\"","The thin old man was momentarily stunned, then quickly forced a smile. \"Ah, you must be the Shopkeeper of Jishi Medicine Hall. Forgive my poor eyes, please forgive me.\"","\"It’s just that my young master specifically instructed that Divine Doctor Ma’s Medical Skill is superb, and the plaque must be delivered.\"","\"I hope the Shopkeeper will accept it and fulfill my young master’s wish.\"","\"A wish?\"","A smile touched Chen Yi’s calm face. He stepped forward, lifted a corner of the plaque to glance at the contents, and then let it fall back into place.","\"Please go back, old sir. Curing the sick and saving lives is the duty of my Jishi Medicine Hall. We do not do it for a ’Divine Doctor’ plaque.\"","\"This...\"","Before the thin old man could say more, Chen Yi gestured for Ma Liangcai and the others to return to the Medicine Hall, then instructed,","\"Liu Quan, see our guests out.\"","Liu Quan hesitated, but seeing that Chen Yi’s mind was made up, he dazedly asked the thin old man and his entourage to leave.","Although the procession seemed reluctant, seeing that both the Shopkeeper and the Physician had gone back inside, they had no choice but to turn back.","In moments, the crowd of onlookers, both inside and outside the door, had mostly dispersed.","[Witnessed Ma Liangcai receiving a Divine Doctor plaque. Reward: Massage Skill, Opportunity +10.]","[Evaluation: The man arrived, the noise was heard, the scene was witnessed. By causing Ma Liangcai to lose the Divine Doctor plaque, you allowed him to escape a disaster. Performance: Passable.]","Chen Yi glanced at the notification and understood. He gestured for Ma Liangcai to follow him to the inner hall to talk.","\"Write.\"","Ma Liangcai understood and wrote a short message: \"Shopkeeper, he said he was from Wumeng Mountain, but I don’t remember him.\"","Chen Yi read it, nodded, and wrote a short message back to him: \"Keep a low profile for a while. I’ll have someone investigate this thoroughly.\"","After Ma Liangcai finished reading, Chen Yi wiped the words from the table and said with a smile,","\"Someone delivering a plaque today might seem like a good thing, but in reality, it would put our Medicine Hall under immense pressure.\"","\"Doctor Ma, I hope you don’t mind me acting on my own authority?\"","Ma Liangcai understood and bowed deeply. \"I am part of Jishi Medicine Hall. Naturally, the Shopkeeper makes all the decisions.\"","Chen Yi clapped him on the shoulder. \"Keep up the good work. I’ll have Liu Quan give you some silver later as this month’s bonus.\"","\"Thank you, Shopkeeper.\"","After a bit more small talk, the two of them left the inner hall.","Chen Yi also offered some words of encouragement to the others, instructed Liu Quan to distribute some silver coins, and left amidst the cheerful clamor of the people in the hall.","\"It’s been a while! Shopkeeper Chen is as sharp as ever.\"","\"Still calling him Shopkeeper Chen? You should be calling him ’Mr. Qingzhou’ now.\"","\"Oh, right, right, Mr. Qingzhou! Heh, I almost forgot. He’s a teacher at Guiyun Academy now, quite famous.\"","\"If those scholars heard you say that, you’d get an earful...\"","Chen Yi overheard some of this chatter.","But as he left the Medicine Hall and headed straight for where Xiao Wan’er and the others were, he had no mind to pay attention to it.","In fact, when the musical procession had first arrived at the East Market, Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the others were already there.","However, their path was blocked by the people playing gongs and drums, so they had simply followed behind.","But after hearing what the old man said, Chen Yi had a bad feeling. That’s why he had asked Xiao Wan’er and the others to wait while he went to the Medicine Hall alone to handle it.","The outcome was just as he had expected.","Ma Liangcai was a Physician with a limp and no real Medical Skill. How could he possibly receive a \"Divine Doctor\" plaque for any reason other than a conspiracy?","But Chen Yi couldn’t immediately figure out who would plot against Ma Liangcai like this.","’Cui Qingwu and Chen Yunfan?’","’Unlikely.’","’The Hidden Guard?’","’Also impossible.’","’Such a tedious scheme. Besides causing some trouble for the Xiao Family, it wouldn’t really affect the Medicine Hall, nor could it harm the Xiao Family.’","’Thinking it over, it seemed more like the work of a rival.’","Mulling this over, Chen Yi returned to the carriage, gave a brief explanation, and then said with a smile that he was hungry.","Xiao Wan’er, suspecting nothing, led Xiao Wuge and the others out of the carriage and said gently,","\"That old restaurant is just in the alley nearby.\"","\"I wonder if you can smell it? The aroma is wonderful.\"","\"It is...\"","A few moments later, they walked into the alley and sat down in the restaurant.","But what they didn’t notice was another, ornately decorated carriage parked on the edge of the East Market.","The two people sitting inside were staring at their departing backs.","\"Second Brother, your plan failed.\"","\"It was just a small welcome gift for my ’madam.’ If it failed, it failed.\"","\"Come on, let’s go say hello.\""]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174 - 163: He... Touched My Hand...","paragraphs":["As the voice faded, two women who looked like maids, dressed in green skirts, disembarked from the magnificent canopied carriage, one after the other.","Oil paper umbrellas were opened.","Next, a tall man in black brocade robes lifted the carriage curtain and jumped down.","His face was pale, and with sword-like brows and star-like eyes, he could be considered handsome.","But a pair of long, narrow phoenix eyes gave him a sinister, effeminate air.","Especially under the overcast sky, his entire presence seemed somewhat gloomy.","He stood beside the maids and urged the person still in the carriage, \"Third Sister.\"","\"Coming.\"","Amidst a slightly chilly voice, a woman in a long dress, her face covered by a veil that revealed only a pair of peach-blossom eyes, stepped out of the carriage.","Her glossy black hair was adorned with a phoenix hairpin and pearls. Two neat strands of hair fell beside her ears, making her look even more stern and cold.","She glanced at the man and said coolly, \"Second Brother, the family sent you to Shu State, but not to secure a marriage alliance with the Xiao Family.\"","Hearing this, the handsome man’s lips curled into a smile. \"Don’t you think that eldest daughter of the Xiao Family is a perfect match for me?\"","\"I don’t.\"","Hearing the cold woman’s words, the effeminate man wasn’t annoyed. Instead, he smiled and nodded. \"You’re right, Third Sister. Xiao Wan’er is indeed not worthy of me.\"","\"Setting aside her sickly constitution, the now-weakened Xiao Family alone is no match for our Liu Family.\"","He finished speaking to himself, his smile tinged with a hint of wickedness. \"But I did just catch a glimpse of her. Her looks are quite pleasing, comparable to yours.\"","The cold woman shot him a look and started walking toward the alley outside the East Market.","Seeing this, the effeminate man followed, muttering to himself, \"Zhaoxue, do you think I should go to the Marquis’s Mansion tomorrow to propose, or should I wait a bit?\"","\"There’s no rush.\"","\"Right. We’ve just arrived in Shu State, so we should indeed pay our respects to Third Uncle first.\"","\"After we’ve seen Third Uncle, how about you accompany me to the Marquis’s Mansion to propose?\"","\"I’m not going...\"","Deep in the alley, inside the restaurant called the \"East Market Entrance Eatery,\" the place was buzzing with noise.","The small eatery was packed with people—locals from Shu State, travelers from afar, and even a few Jianghu People carrying sharp weapons.","The moment one stepped inside, the pungent aroma of chili peppers assaulted the senses.","Besides the din of chatter from all corners of the land, one could also hear the SIZZLE of hot oil meeting woks from the kitchen.","Since there were no private rooms, Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and the others had to sit in the main hall.","However, none of them looked disgusted; on the contrary, they found it novel.","After simply ordering six stir-fried dishes, two stews, and a few bottles of tea, the group waited quietly.","Xiao Wan’er was in a good mood, a smile never leaving her face.","Even though the strong smells made her a little uncomfortable, she still looked around with great interest.","She hadn’t been out like this in a very long time.","Even when she left the mansion, it was mostly to go to the Medicine Hall or to the tenant farmers on their fiefdom. She almost never came to a place like this.","If Chen Yi hadn’t mentioned the Jishi Medicine Hall today, she wouldn’t have even remembered this place existed.","\"This place is just like it was before. It hasn’t changed at all.\"","Chen Yi saw her happiness and asked with a smile, \"When was the last time you came here?\"","\"Eleven years ago. Back then, Father and Mother were both still here. They brought me and my second sister here to shop.\"","\"When we were about to return to the mansion, we happened to pass by. Father smelled the aromas from here, so he had the carriage stop and brought us in to eat.\"","\"I remember my second sister and I ate so much...\"","Xiao Wan’er spoke with a smile, her eyes filled with reminiscence, but it was inevitably tinged with a hint of sadness.","She was clearly thinking of her deceased parents.","Chen Yi saw this but said nothing, simply keeping a smile on his face for her.","Xiao Wuge listened with great interest, feeling no particular sadness.","Xiaodie’s attention was fixed on the fiery red stir-fry at the next table, and she was secretly swallowing her saliva.","Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang had clearly been to places like this many times; they were quite familiar with the setting.","However, since sitting down, both of them had worn strange expressions and kept glancing toward the entrance.","Chen Yi, sitting opposite them, noticed their gazes. He glanced at the entrance, and his ears naturally caught some sounds.","\"Second Brother, you plan to meet Xiao Wan’er here?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"Me, the second young master of the Jing State Liu Family, meeting the eldest daughter of the Xiao Family in a common marketplace eatery. Don’t you find that interesting, Third Sister?\"","\"I don’t.\"","\"But I have to remind you, this is Shu State. You’d best not go too far.\"","\"Listen to you. Do I look like an idiot like Liu Jing? Why would I come here just to offend people?\"","\"Especially when it’s my future wife I’d be offending.\"","\"Second Brother, the Xiao Family hasn’t agreed to your proposal yet. I advise you not to displease anyone in a moment.\"","\"I know, I know...\"","’The second young master of the Jing State Liu Family?’","’A marriage proposal?’","Chen Yi frowned to himself, looking at Xiao Wan’er, who was still smiling happily, completely unaware.","He had already guessed who was behind the words on the plaque given to Ma Liangcai earlier.","’But why now, of all times...’","’How irritating.’","But then again, many people and many things in life are rarely to one’s liking.","Before long, Chen Yi saw a handsome man in black brocade robes walk in.","Beside him was a woman wearing a veil, her bright eyes glinting with coldness.","After the two entered, the man looked toward Chen Yi, Xiao Wan’er, and their group.","Then they started walking over.","Xiao Wan’er naturally saw them too, but she only spared them a glance before continuing with a smile,","\"Brother-in-law and Wuge, you two should eat more later. Huatang and I don’t have large appetites.\"","The words had barely left her mouth.","Xiao Wuge had just said \"Okay,\" when the man walked straight up to them and interjected as if he knew them well.","\"Miss Wan’er, rest assured, my appetite is not small either. I can help you with that.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, the smile vanishing from her face. She asked with a hint of displeasure, \"Who are you?\"","The handsome man offered a smile and a bow.","\"Liu Wen of Jing State, also known as Liu Liming, greets Miss Wan’er.\"","\"I hope you’ll forgive my sudden intrusion.\"","With that, he paused slightly, and upon seeing Xiao Wuge beside her, bowed again. \"And I greet the Young Master as well.\"","The woman beside him also curtsied, her voice cold. \"Liu Zhaoxue greets you all.\"","Xiao Wan’er studied the two of them with a slight frown, clearly not understanding why people from the Jing State Liu Family had sought her out.","Just as she was about to speak, Shen Huatang leaned in and whispered a few words in her ear.","After hearing her out, Xiao Wan’er’s eyes widened slightly. She glanced at the calm and composed Chen Yi beside her and seemed to let out a sigh of relief.","Then, her expression turned cold as she said, \"Since you know you’re intruding, please leave.\"","Liu Wen seemed to have expected this and shook his head with a smile. \"They say that a chance encounter is better than a planned meeting.\"","\"For my third sister and I to meet Miss Wan’er the very day we arrived in Shu State is truly a matter of fate.\"","\"Why must Miss Wan’er push us away?\"","At this, Liu Wen paused, looking at them with a smirk.","\"Or could it be that Miss Wan’er is worried something might happen between me... I mean, *us*?\"","The moment he finished, Xiao Wan’er’s brows furrowed tightly, her face icing over.","\"Huatang, see them out.\"","Even Xiao Wuge sensed the visitor’s ill intentions and tensed his little face.","Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang rose as instructed, their hands resting on the hilts of their swords.","Their auras turned cold and grim as they stared intently at the newcomers.","Seeing this, Liu Wen’s smile remained. Just as he was about to say more, Liu Zhaoxue stepped in front of him. \"Please forgive us, Sister Wan’er. My brother meant no offense. We’ll leave now.\"","\"Third Sister, you...\"","Before Liu Wen could finish, Liu Zhaoxue turned and started pulling him away.","\"I’m not done talking.\"","\"Hey! Third Sister... no, I mean, Miss Wan’er, I will pay a formal visit in a few days!\"","Chen Yi, who had been silent all this time, watched their retreating backs, a sharp glint in his eyes.","Under his Qi Observation Skill, he could see the auras emanating from them.","’Liu Wen’s True Essence aura is coarse and heavy.’","’Liu Zhaoxue’s aura is weaker than Liu Wen’s. She should be at the Sixth Grade Realm.’","’In that case, Liu Wen’s cultivation should be at the Fifth Grade Realm, a bit weaker than Liu Lang.’","After his assessment, Chen Yi discreetly retracted his gaze.","The tense atmosphere in the restaurant finally broke. The surrounding patrons breathed a sigh of relief and began to whisper amongst themselves.","Most of them were talking about the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion, the Xiao Family, and the Jing State Liu Family.","Hearing these whispers, Xiao Wan’er was about to get up and leave.","But then she saw Chen Yi raise his voice and ask, \"Waiter, when will the food be ready? I’m starving.\"","\"Just a moment, sir! It’s coming right up.\"","Huh?","Xiao Wan’er stared blankly at Chen Yi, but when he looked over at her, she instinctively lowered her head.","The words she had just heard from Shen Huatang had completely ruined her earlier mood.","The others also looked at Chen Yi with various expressions, seemingly a little confused.","Chen Yi glanced around and said with a smile, \"Man is iron, food is steel. If you don’t eat, you’ll feel it.\"","\"It’s rare for us to come out. We should at least try the delicious food Eldest Sister mentioned before we go back.\"","As he spoke, he reached out and patted Xiao Wan’er’s hand, asking,","\"What do you think, Eldest Sister?\"","Xiao Wan’er froze. Her gaze was fixed on the hand that had just left her own. A wave of heat rushed through her, making her forget all her previous displeasure. Only a single thought remained in her mind:","’He... he... he... touched my hand...’","Seeing her silent, Xiao Wuge chimed in approvingly, \"Brother-in-law is right.\"","\"Sis, we can’t let some nobodies ruin our mood, right?\"","Xiao Wan’er was stunned for a good while before she snapped out of it. She lifted her head, revealing a slightly flushed face, and lightly slapped Xiao Wuge.","\"What do you mean, ’nobodies’? You can’t be so rude.\"","Xiao Wuge’s eyes darted around, and he grinned. \"Brother-in-law taught me.\"","\"He also said you shouldn’t let other people’s mistakes affect your own mood. People who do that are usually pretty stupid.\"","Chen Yi was struck speechless for a moment, then laughed. He clearly hadn’t expected Xiao Wuge to remember something he had said so casually.","\"I don’t recall ever saying that.\"","Xiao Wan’er’s face grew even redder. She shot him a reproachful look.","\"You should teach him some better things, you know.\"","Chen Yi spread his hands. \"Me? I’m really not that knowledgeable.\"","\"If you don’t believe me...\"","At this moment, whether she believed him or not was unimportant.","At least Xiao Wan’er was smiling, having temporarily forgotten the unpleasantness from before.","Seeing this, Xiaodie, Xie Tingyun, and Shen Huatang breathed a sigh of relief. It looked like they would get to eat their spicy lunch after all.","Chen Yi really hadn’t thought that far ahead. He just seized the rare opportunity to joke around and lighten the group’s mood.","\"Brother-in-law, save me some sliced meat!\"","\"That’s mine...\"","[Meanwhile]","Back in the carriage, Liu Wen’s face darkened when he heard the sounds of laughter and chatter from the restaurant.","He glared at Liu Zhaoxue and demanded, \"Don’t you think you should explain yourself?\"","Liu Zhaoxue stared out the window and said coolly, \"If you had continued, Second Brother, you would only have been asking for trouble.\"","\"From them?\"","\"Those two maids are Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang of the Celestial Sect. Could you have beaten them?\"","\"And Xiao Wan’er—you’ve already displeased her. You still want to go propose marriage?\"","Hearing Liu Zhaoxue’s words, Liu Wen froze. His anger vanished, and he smiled and nodded. \"You’re right to remind me, Third Sister. I almost forgot what’s important.\"","\"My mistake, my mistake.\"","Liu Zhaoxue gave a noncommittal nod but still didn’t look at him. Her gaze fell on the alley, her thoughts unreadable.","Liu Wen, however, seemed not to notice and said to himself, \"That man from just now must be the Xiao Family’s live-in son-in-law, Xiao Jinghong’s husband. Heh, he certainly does look frail.\"","\"Recently, I’ve heard rumors in Shu State that he can teach students to achieve success in the Calligraphy Dao. I don’t believe it. A mere live-in son-in-law...\"","Just then, Liu Zhaoxue interrupted him in a low, haunting voice:","\"Second Brother, that ’live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family’ you speak of was a concubine-born son of the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family before he came to Shu State.\"","\"Have you forgotten what Father taught you back then?\"","\"He told you to surpass Chen Qingzhou in talent and learning, and to overcome Cui Xiayang in Martial Arts.\"","Liu Wen paused, recalling the past. His face soured as he said, \"I’d forgotten. So I have this old score to settle with him. If I get the chance this time, I’ll compete with him.\"","Hearing this, Liu Zhaoxue secretly shook her head and said in a cold voice:","\"Let’s go. To Third Uncle’s house...\""]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175 - 164: I, I Don’t Agree...","paragraphs":["After lunch, the group was no longer in the mood to stroll around.","This was especially true for Xiao Wan’er.","Although she had gotten to eat the delicious meal she’d been craving thanks to Chen Yi, her mood had inevitably been affected.","Specifically, what Liu Wen had said about a \"marriage proposal\" made it difficult for her to calm down.","She was very worried that the Old Marquis would agree to a marriage alliance with the Jing State Liu Family.","It was just like how Xiao Jinghong and Chen Yi’s marriage had been single-handedly arranged by the Old Marquis.","Before that, no one else in the Xiao Family knew about it.","If Xiao Jinghong hadn’t accepted, perhaps the entire Great Wei Dynasty would be laughing at the expense of the Xiao and Chen Families right now.","Now that a similar situation was happening again, and to her of all people, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but feel nervous and uneasy.","So much so that on the way back, she sat silently on one side of the carriage.","Her face, which had just regained some color, turned pale once more. Her delicate eyes gazed out at the dreary rain.","She was like a vibrant flower on the verge of withering—exquisitely beautiful, yet tinged with sorrow.","Chen Yi saw it all but could only pretend he knew nothing about it.","He tried to crack a few jokes along the way, but Xiao Wan’er remained lost in her worries.","Instead, it was Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie who were amused by his antics.","Before long, the carriage entered the Marquis’s Mansion.","Without waiting for Xie Tingyun to return from the stables, Xiao Wan’er instructed Shen Huatang to take her to Qingjing Residence under an umbrella.","Chen Yi wanted to follow, but on second thought, he felt it wouldn’t be appropriate.","Whether the marriage alliance happened or not was an internal matter for the Xiao Family, and the decision would ultimately be made by the Old Marquis.","Never mind him, a mere husband married into the Xiao Family; even Xiao Wan’er’s own wishes were unlikely to sway the Old Marquis’s decision.","In this era, the saying \"a parent’s command, a matchmaker’s word\" was not just empty talk.","This was especially true for Noble Families like the Xiao Family.","The marriages of their children were mostly used to ensure the family’s continuation or to forge new paths for advancement.","Just like Chen Yunfan and Cui Qingwu.","Just like Xiao Jinghong and him.","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi patted Xiao Wuge on the shoulder, pointed at the departing Xiao Wan’er, and said in a low voice,","\"You haven’t gone to pay your respects to the Old Marquis in a long time.\"","Xiao Wuge froze for a second, then remembered the last time Chen Yi had told him to go to Qingjing Residence to eavesdrop. His eyes darted around as he said,","\"Brother-in-law, I want to learn to play chess with you at the mansion tomorrow.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, patting his head. \"I can’t make that decision. You’ll have to ask your Big Sister and see if she agrees.\"","\"Brother-in-law, if you’re the one who asks, Big Sister will definitely agree.\"","Seeing that Xiao Wan’er had already entered the central courtyard, Chen Yi agreed. \"I’ll try, but I can’t guarantee anything.\"","Xiao Wuge giggled. \"It’ll definitely work.\"","With that, he ran after Xiao Wan’er and Shen Huatang, completely ignoring the rain that was still falling.","Chen Yi shook his head and muttered, \"That kid’s getting smart,\" then told Xiaodie to follow them.","Xiaodie paused and hesitated. \"Sir, then how will you get back?\"","\"I’m not going back yet. I have some business to take care of in the West Market.\"","\"Then...\"","\"If you wait any longer, Wuge will be soaked to the bone.\"","Although Xiaodie didn’t quite grasp the expression, she understood he was worried about Young Master Wuge.","Without another word, she quickly opened her oil-paper umbrella and hurried after them.","Once they were some distance away, Chen Yi looked up at the sky.","The dreary rain was still falling, but it was much lighter than it had been at noon.","The wind from the north blew the rain into southward-slanting lines.","Chen Yi let the fine droplets hit his face, feeling their slight chill as his heart grew calm.","’The Jing State Liu Family...’","’It seems they’re dead set on taking a pound of flesh from the Xiao Family.’","With that thought, Chen Yi averted his gaze, calmly turned, and left the Marquis’s Mansion, heading for the West Market.","His figure, unprotected by an umbrella, walked with steady steps through the curtain of rain.","Fading into the distance.","...","Xiao Wan’er hurried to Qingjing Residence, followed by Xiao Wuge, who wore a mischievous smile.","As soon as she reached the residence, she heard faint voices coming from the main hall.","\"...My Liu Family’s junior came to Shu State for the first time and, not knowing the rules, caused some offense. I hope you can forgive us, Marquis.\"","\"I am not aware of any offense.\"","\"You are a man of great importance, Marquis. It’s only natural you wouldn’t concern yourself with the business of a mere Medicine Hall, hehe...\"","’Someone from the Liu Family?’","Xiao Wan’er froze, her hands clutching her chest as she stared at the main hall. She unconsciously bit her lip, her expression tinged with worry.","Xiao Wuge heard the voices from inside as well. He looked up at her, then took her hand and asked in a low voice,","\"Sister, can I go pay my respects to Grandfather?\"","Xiao Wan’er snapped back to her senses and shook her head gently. \"Let’s wait.\"","Even though she didn’t know who from the Liu Family had come, just hearing the words \"Liu Family\" threw her mind into turmoil, making her even more anxious than before.","She didn’t know how to describe it.","Resistance, hesitation, worry...","Amid the complex emotions, it all boiled down to three words: I am unwilling.","About the time it takes for an incense stick to burn, the person inside finally said his goodbyes.","Only then did Xiao Wan’er relax.","Fortunately, during that time, she hadn’t heard words like \"marriage alliance\" or \"proposal\" from inside.","Before long, the Old Marquis, leaning on his cane, escorted a slightly paunchy, middle-aged man in fine clothes out of the main hall.","\"When you go back, give my regards to Liu Xuan. We haven’t seen each other in many years, and I fear we won’t have the chance to meet again.\"","\"This junior will certainly pass on your words, Marquis.\"","The somewhat portly middle-aged man spoke and bowed respectfully. \"Marquis, please, don’t trouble yourself further. This junior will be on his way.\"","\"Very well.\"","When the middle-aged man turned and saw Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge at the entrance, he paused for a moment, then smiled and bowed as well.","\"You must be Miss Wan’er and the Young Master, I presume?\"","The Old Marquis made the introduction. \"Wan’er, Wuge, this is Liu Yu, of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","Xiao Wan’er hesitated before giving a slight curtsy. \"Wan’er greets Uncle Liu.\"","Xiao Wuge greeted him as well.","Liu Yu sized them up and praised, \"Miss Wan’er is indeed as gentle and graceful as the rumors say.\"","\"And the Young Master is a dragon among men. I’m sure he will one day carry on Brother Fengchun’s legacy and bring glory to the family name.\"","The Old Marquis glanced at him and said with a chuckle, \"Now those are words I like to hear.\"","After looking at Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge, Liu Yu suddenly turned his head and asked, \"I wonder, would my Liu Family be so fortunate as to marry into your esteemed family?\"","For a rare moment, the Old Marquis was stunned.","Beside him, Xiao Wan’er’s heart leaped into her throat. Her mind went blank, and she felt a strange wave of dizziness.","’It’s here.’","In the end, the Old Marquis was far more experienced. He feigned confusion and asked, \"My good nephew, what do you mean by that?\"","Liu Yu decided to lay it all out. \"To be honest with you, Marquis, before I came to Shu State, my elder brother gave me instructions.\"","\"If you agree, Marquis, my Liu Family hopes to join with the Xiao Family in marriage to strengthen the relationship between the Xiao and Liu Families.\"","\"What are your thoughts on this, Marquis?\"","The Old Marquis glanced at the stunned Xiao Wan’er, his expression unchanging as he spoke.","\"I recall that the eldest legitimate son of your Liu Family’s main branch is already engaged, is he not?\"","\"You are correct, Marquis. My eldest nephew, Liu Wu, is indeed engaged.\"","\"However, the second son of the main branch, Liu Wen, is not yet betrothed.\"","\"His scholarship, talent, and Martial Arts are all superb. He would be a fine match for Miss Wan’er.\"","Before the Old Marquis could speak, Xiao Wan’er, who had heard everything, said with a pale face,","\"I... I do not agree...\"","Liu Yu glanced at her, then looked back at the Old Marquis as if he hadn’t heard a word she said.","’A parent’s command, a matchmaker’s word—was that just for show?’","The Old Marquis looked at Xiao Wan’er, who was biting her lip, and said after a moment’s thought, \"Allow me to decline this matter for now.\"","\"I will make a final decision after I have corresponded by letter with the main branch of your Liu Family.\"","The smile on Liu Yu’s face froze, and a flash of displeasure crossed his eyes, but he said nothing more.","\"In that case, this junior will take his leave.\"","\"Marquis, please take care.\"","The Old Marquis nodded. He watched him walk out of Qingjing Residence, waited a moment, and only then turned to Xiao Wan’er with a smile, beckoning her over.","\"The wind is strong out here. Come inside to talk.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded numbly and followed him inside.","Xiao Wuge, however, rushed forward and spoke first. \"Grandfather, that Jing State Liu Family is so awful! I don’t agree to any proposal either.\"","The Old Marquis chuckled, patting his lap for the boy to sit. He asked with a smile,","\"You know the people of the Liu Family are awful?\"","Xiao Wuge nodded. \"I heard Big Sister say before that if the Liu Family hadn’t been causing trouble, our family’s Medicine Hall business wouldn’t have been affected.\"","\"Brother-in-law also said... um...\"","Seeing the boy clamp a hand over his mouth, the Old Marquis’s interest was piqued. \"What did your brother-in-law say?\"","\"Brother-in-law said something about how a tall tree attracts the wind, and that our family has become a target.\""]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176 - 165: In Short, He’s Awesome","paragraphs":["Coveting...","Elder Master Xiao’s smile didn’t falter, but inwardly, he somewhat agreed.","His Xiao Family had been in Shu State for many years, not only commanding a large army but also possessing extensive connections.","Furthermore, aside from those who joined the Dingyuan Army, many of the family’s children had become Civil Servants.","For instance, Xiao Dongchen of the Governor’s Office and Xiao Ziqi of the Military Supervision Institute.","Adding to that was the marriage alliance between the Xiao Family’s second branch and the Zhang Family of Duke Qian in Guangyue Prefecture. United, they gave the impression of dominating the entire southern region of the Wei Dynasty.","To outsiders, it was no exaggeration to describe such a behemoth, the Xiao Family, as the local emperors of Shu State.","If the Xiao Family had remained powerful, if Xiao Fengchun and the others hadn’t died, the Noble Families of Shu State, and even neighboring state capitals like Jing State, would never have dared to emerge.","But the reality was that the Xiao Family was now in decline. It was at its weakest, so it was understandable that a major family like the Jing State Liu Family would come sniffing around.","Elder Master Xiao was aware of all this, which was why he had taken every step with such caution these past few years.","As if walking on thin ice.","What Elder Master Xiao hadn’t expected was that Chen Yi would see through all this and say such things to Xiao Wuge.","After a moment of thought, he glanced at Xiao Wan’er and asked:","\"Wuge, why did your second brother-in-law tell you all this?\"","\"I asked him.\"","Xiao Wuge didn’t think twice and said directly:","\"The other day, I was fishing with Brother-in-law and mentioned that the family seemed to be short on silver lately. I also said that Eldest Sister had to pawn some of her jewelry.\"","\"Then I asked him why that Linglan Pavilion was stealing business from our Medicine Hall, and he just casually replied with that sentence.\"","\"Is that so...\"","The Elder Master nodded thoughtfully.","If he remembered correctly, Linglan Pavilion had only just opened at the time, and Liu Jing of the Liu Family hadn’t yet shown his face.","And Chen Yi...","It seemed Chen Yi hardly ever left the house back then, didn’t he?","’He saw the heart of the problem right away?’","’Did someone tell him, or did he deduce it himself?’","’If it’s the former, that’s one thing. But if it’s the latter...’","’...then it means Chen Yi isn’t as oblivious to the outside world as he appears.’","As the Elder Master mulled this over, he silently filed it away and turned to the quiet Xiao Wan’er beside him, asking with a smile:","\"Still thinking about what happened earlier?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded hesitantly, a wronged look on her face as she bit her lip and said:","\"Grandfather, we just saw Liu Wen at the East Market. He’s not as outstanding as Liu Yu... as Uncle described.\"","The Elder Master shook his head and said with a laugh, \"Whether he’s outstanding or not, our family and the Liu Family could never be joined by marriage.\"","Upon hearing this, Xiao Wan’er let out a sigh of relief, a hint of joy appearing on her face.","But before she could voice her thanks, she heard the Elder Master say:","\"However, Wan’er, you’re not getting any younger.\"","\"Before, because of your health, Grandfather never rushed you. But now that your health is visibly improving, shouldn’t you start considering marriage?\"","Xiao Wan’er’s smile froze, and she quickly shook her head.","\"No, no... Grandfather, I... my health is still very poor. It hasn’t improved at all.\"","\"Just the other day I came down with a serious illness, I caught a bad cold...\"","\"A cold?\" The Elder Master’s expression immediately grew serious as he interrupted, \"When did this happen?\"","Xiao Wan’er realized her slip and mumbled, \"It’s already better.\"","\"It got better that same afternoon. It was probably from being in the wind that afternoon.\"","Elder Master Xiao stared at Xiao Wan’er for a moment. After confirming she was fine, his expression finally softened.","Just as he was about to speak, Xiao Wuge piped up from the side, \"Grandfather, my sister really is better.\"","\"It’s all thanks to Brother-in-law. After he went to check on her that day, my sister’s illness went away.\"","A blush crept onto Xiao Wan’er’s face, clearly recalling the events of that day.","But Elder Master Xiao was surprised. \"Wuge, your brother-in-law knows how to treat illnesses?\"","He didn’t believe for a second that Chen Yi could treat Xiao Wan’er.","For so many years, only the Daoist Nun from Wumeng Mountain had a Method to suppress her Extreme Cold Body. Everyone else, even some so-called Divine Doctors, were helpless.","\"He does! Brother-in-law even knows Acupuncture. I saw him come back with an acupuncture kit that day.\"","\"Acu... Acupuncture?\"","It was no wonder the Elder Master was shocked. If someone said Chen Yi knew a bit of Medical Skill, he could grudgingly believe it.","But to say Chen Yi knew Acupuncture? He wouldn’t believe it if you beat him to death.","One must understand that Acupuncture wasn’t like other basic medical techniques. It could only be practiced after mastering the principles of the Medical Dao, as well as concepts like the celestial and terrestrial seasons, the human meridians and acupoints, and the Five Elements and Six Qi.","Otherwise, applying needles carelessly was just harming people.","Xiao Wan’er also showed a strange expression.","She wasn’t surprised that Chen Yi knew Acupuncture, but rather because certain images were popping into her head.","’Her, lying on the bed soaked to the bone, with Chen Yi holding Silver Needles to perform Acupuncture on her... wouldn’t that mean they would have some... physical contact...?’","Just imagining such a scene, let alone it actually happening, was enough to make her blush.","It was even more embarrassing than just being looked at.","Xiao Wuge, however, was oblivious to their thoughts and continued on his own:","\"Brother-in-law knows a lot of things.\"","\"Not just Acupuncture and treating people; he can play chess, compose poetry, has excellent handwriting, and understands so much...\"","\"Basically, Brother-in-law is amazing.\"","Hearing this, Elder Master Xiao dotingly stroked the back of his head and said:","\"It seems you hold your brother-in-law in high regard, Wuge.\"","\"Of course! I think Brother-in-law is the most amazing person. Even more than Second Sister, um... except he can’t out-argue her, and he can’t beat her in a fight.\"","The Elder Master laughed heartily. \"A harmonious couple follows each other’s lead. Your Second Sister would never lay a hand on him.\"","Although Xiao Wan’er was blushing, she couldn’t help but smile at their conversation.","After some lighthearted talk and laughter,","the Elder Master once again reassured her, \"Wan’er, you don’t need to worry too much about the Liu Family. I’m here for you.\"","\"Yes. Thank you, Grandfather.\"","\"We’re family. No need for such formalities.\"","After a pause, the Elder Master added proudly, \"Besides, that Liu Family has no sincerity. To think they wanted the second son of their main branch to marry you... they’re looking down on us.\"","\"Putting the Xiao Family aside, just for you alone, Wan’er, it would only be somewhat acceptable if the eldest son of the Liu Family came over himself.\"","Xiao Wan’er said shyly, \"Grandfather...\"","\"I am merely stating a fact.\"","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er quickly stood up with Xiao Wuge to take their leave.","Elder Master Xiao, looking as if he hadn’t had his fill of the conversation, nodded and watched them leave, the smile on his face slowly fading.","He was silent for a moment. He tapped the table beside him and ordered, \"Keep a close watch on the visitors from the Liu Family. See what they’re planning.\"","A faint voice answered from a corner, \"Yes, Marquis.\"","\"Also... never mind. That’s all. Get to it.\"","The Elder Master had originally intended to have a Hidden Guard follow Chen Yi, but on second thought, he decided it wasn’t necessary.","After all, Chen Yi’s recent behavior had been quite acceptable.","Not only had he shown no interest in taking the imperial exams to become an official, but he also hadn’t suggested joining the Dingyuan Army. More importantly, he hadn’t stirred up trouble within the Xiao Family, nor had he tried to cozy up to or side with the second or third branches.","He could be considered a decent and proper person.","It would be normal even if Chen Yi did know a few things.","After all, he came from the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family. Having been immersed in that environment since childhood, it wasn’t impossible for his perspective and grasp of the situation to be beyond that of an ordinary person.","As for his Medical Skill...","’Hah. Even if he were an accomplished physician, he couldn’t cure the ailments of the current Xiao Family.’","...","Chen Yi had no idea that Xiao Wuge’s few words had nearly exposed his secrets.","He had already changed his clothes and was now waiting in his residence for Liu Lang to arrive.","Amidst the pitter-patter of the rain,","Chen Yi walked to the window and gazed out at the modest courtyard. His face was calm, but his mind was a turbulent sea of thoughts.","Ideas rose and fell one after another, an endless cycle like the tides.","’The Jing State Liu Family will definitely team up with Liu Hong within Shu State’s territory. Only by borrowing the power of the Governor’s Office can they hope to suppress the Xiao Family.’","’Among the group that arrived is Liu Yu, the second master in charge of the Liu Family’s businesses. They must be planning to stir things up in Shu State as well.’","’Furthermore, the Divine Doctor plaque they gave to Ma Liangcai today supports this speculation.’","’So, the key players are Liu Hong and Liu Town. The siblings, Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue, are secondary.’","As Chen Yi considered these points, he naturally knew how to proceed.","If the Liu Family targeted his Medicine Hall’s business, it would be playing right into his hands.","As for everything else, he would have to adapt to the circumstances.","In any case, he would not let the Liu Family’s schemes succeed.","Just as Chen Yi was contemplating this, Liu Lang finally arrived. He cupped his fist and said:","\"Greetings, Boss.\"","\"No need for formalities. Tell me the details about Black Tooth.\"","Liu Lang nodded and said, \"Black Tooth has been making a lot of moves these past few days.\"","\"Besides mentioning that Financier to me, he’s also taking me to meet a few people tonight. They’re all participants in this mission.\"","\"There’s also a small, unremarkable detail. Last night, quite a few people died on the street where Black Tooth lives. It’s said they might have been members of the Xiao family.\"","Chen Yi paused. \"The Xiao family?\"","Liu Lang affirmed, \"Something like Personal Guards or subordinates.\"","Chen Yi said thoughtfully, \"They were probably trying to prevent any leaks, worried about being discovered by the Xiao Family.\"","\"You’re truly remarkable, sir. It took me a long time to figure that out.\"","\"...Continue.\"","\"That’s it. That’s all he said.\"","Liu Lang shook his head. \"However, I should be able to gather more detailed intelligence tonight.\"","\"I’m just not sure if you need me to do anything else.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, a slight smile gracing his lips.","\"Actually, there is one thing.\"","\"Please, tell me.\"","\"Tonight, take me with you!\""]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177 - 166: Black Tooth’s Rules","paragraphs":["Liu Lang froze for a moment, then said, stunned, \"You... You’re going in person?\"","It was no wonder he was so surprised.","Typically, a Medical Saint Hand was devoted to their Medical Skill and rarely meddled in worldly affairs.","Even if they did have some distracting thoughts, they would usually have some Jianghu People or close associates act on their behalf, rarely taking action themselves.","When they were forced to get involved, it was almost always related to the Medical Dao or medicinal herbs.","It was obvious that Black Tooth was summoning them tonight to discuss that business deal.","Putting aside whether Black Tooth would be displeased, just being surrounded by members of the Evil Demonic Dao presented unpredictable risks.","Thinking of this, Liu Lang couldn’t help but try to dissuade him. \"It’s too dangerous.\"","\"Boss Chen, if you really want to know what happens tonight as soon as possible, just wait here. After I meet with them, I’ll come back and report to you immediately. How about it?\"","Chen Yi shook his head and said with a smile, \"My mind is made up. You just need to tell me how Black Tooth and the others will react when they see me with you.\"","This wasn’t a spur-of-the-moment decision, but the result of careful consideration.","Black Tooth and his group had accepted the \"business\" from that mysterious Financier. To that end, they had not only eliminated the Xiao Family’s hidden agents but had also gathered a host of people from the Evil Demonic Dao, including Liu Lang.","This meant that, in their assessment, the chances of this \"business\" succeeding were extremely high.","They were confident they could pull it off, even if the Xiao Family got wind of it in advance.","Chen Yi was going in person precisely to figure these things out.","Black Tooth’s plans and schemes.","To confirm whether the \"Lady Tiger,\" \"Hawk,\" and others from the Hidden Guard were involved.","And finally, the most important point—what made these people think they could escape the retaliation of the Xiao Family and the Dingyuan Army after completing this job?","Liu Lang couldn’t possibly convey the answers to these three questions clearly to him.","The members of the Hidden Guard alone were impossible for an outsider to see through.","Ultimately, because of the Liu Family’s appearance today, Chen Yi didn’t have much time to get entangled with Black Tooth’s group. He wanted to deal with this matter swiftly and decisively.","Seeing how resolute he was, Liu Lang thought to himself,","’For a major deal like this, Black Tooth, as the organizer, has certain requirements for all participants and those in the know.’","’First is identity. There’s no doubt about that. He would never allow a new face to show up.’","’You need an Identity Token issued by the Bright Moon Building.’","’Second is strength or ability... Of course, with your Medical Dao, that goes without saying.’","At this point, Liu Lang paused, looking at Chen Yi seriously as he added a warning:","\"The most crucial thing is that you might face some unexpected situations.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. \"So I’m missing a Token?\"","’I have to say, the rules of this Bright Moon Building and Black Tooth are stricter than I imagined,’ he thought. ’They even have Tokens to prove one’s identity to participate in the \"business\".’","As for the danger, he had already anticipated it and was fairly confident he could handle it.","The rest could be handled by adapting to the situation as it unfolded.","Liu Lang nodded. \"Without an Identity Token, your presence at that meeting would likely cause Black Tooth to cancel it on the spot.\"","\"Not only would you get nothing, but you might also end up being hunted by Black Tooth and the other members of the Evil Demonic Dao.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then asked, \"How do I get an Identity Token? Is there still time?\"","\"...Of course not.\"","\"Is there no other way?\"","\"No... Well, there is one.\"","Liu Lang said hesitantly, \"Do you remember the reason I gave for seeking out Black Tooth before?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"To have Black Tooth issue a job to burn the summer grain of the Three Towns?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"If you go as a Financier, you won’t need an Identity Token.\"","This was the most viable method Liu Lang could think of.","After all, as an Elder of the Bright Moon Building, everything Black Tooth did was for the sake of earning silver.","Under such circumstances, he naturally wouldn’t make too many demands of a paying Financier.","\"But there’s still one problem with doing it this way...\"","Before Liu Lang could finish, Chen Yi had already guessed his words. \"I’ll need to give a reason for wanting to ’burn the summer grain of the Three Towns’.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"If your reason is convincing, not only will Black Tooth not make many demands of you, he might even let you participate.\"","At this, Liu Lang reminded him again, \"Even so, you might still encounter danger.\"","In truth, questions were popping up one after another in his mind.","His biggest question was what relationship this \"Medical Saint Hand\" before him had with the Xiao Family that would make him take such a huge risk.","He knew that Black Tooth and his cronies were not good people.","If anything went wrong, not only would Chen Yi be in danger, but he, the one who brought him, would also be risking his life.","Even with his reputation as the \"Sword Madman,\" he probably wouldn’t be able to escape.","After hearing Liu Lang out, Chen Yi didn’t speak again. He just sat quietly in the Grandmaster’s Chair, his right hand tapping rhythmically on the armrest.","TAP, TAP, TAP...","The crisp tapping sound seemed to echo the pitter-patter of the rain falling outside the window, creating a steady rhythm.","Seeing this, Liu Lang didn’t press him.","He had said all he needed to say and given all the necessary warnings.","The rest was up to \"Boss Chen\" to consider.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi’s tapping stopped. A smile appeared on his calm, handsome face as he said,","\"Get ready. I’ll wait for you here before Hai hour.\"","\"...\"","Seeing his smiling face, Liu Lang couldn’t help but ask, \"Aren’t you going to give me a heads-up so I know what to expect?\"","If Chen Yi hadn’t saved his life, he would have lost his patience long ago.","’Damn it.’","’What legitimate reason or identity could a fake Financier who wants to \"burn the summer grain of the Three Towns\" possibly have to convince Black Tooth he’s for real?’","’In any case, I can’t think of anything.’","Chen Yi shook his head and said with a smile, \"Don’t worry, I wouldn’t joke about my own life.\"","With that, he changed the subject. \"Is there anything else I should be aware of?\"","Seeing that he was unwilling to reveal his plan, Liu Lang felt helpless but had no choice but to trust him.","’Who told me to run my mouth and promise him \"thirty things\"?’ he thought ruefully.","\"Not for now. As for anything else... forget it. I’ll do my best to back you up when the time comes.\"","At this point, a hint of grievance crept onto Liu Lang’s face. \"Are you really not going to give me a preview?\"","\"If your reason doesn’t get past Black Tooth, there’s no way you’ll achieve your goal for going.\"","’If that’s the case, it would be better if I just went by myself,’ he thought.","However, to avoid seeming petty, Liu Lang kept that last thought to himself.","Chen Yi seemed to guess his thoughts and just shook his head with a smile. \"You’ll find out tonight.\"","With the serious business concluded, he relaxed and started making small talk with Liu Lang.","He mostly asked about Black Tooth, the Bright Moon Building, and other trivial matters of the Jianghu.","For instance, which members of the Evil Demonic Dao had recently appeared in Shu State.","Or who the strongest expert in Shu State’s Martial Arts was, and what their reputation in the Jianghu was like.","「About half an hour later.」","Liu Lang licked his somewhat dry lips and said, \"That’s about it.\"","\"Shu State is far from the Central Plains, after all, and you also have the Mountain Race masters who are skilled in poison and Witchcraft. You rarely see anyone from the Upper Three Grades walking around here.\"","\"Most of them are Middle Third-Grade Martial Artists, like Elder Demon Jia of the Illusory Sound Sect.\"","After listening, Chen Yi nodded with a smile. \"This is more than enough. Thank you.\"","Liu Lang gave a bitter smile and waved his hand. \"As long as you’re satisfied.\"","\"I just hope tonight’s trip goes smoothly. Otherwise, if Black Tooth gets angry, both of us might end up dead there.\"","Chen Yi let out a helpless laugh, stood up, and patted his shoulder. \"Alright, you’ll find out tonight.\"","With that, he had Liu Lang leave first.","After waiting a moment, once he confirmed there was no one around, Chen Yi dropped his disguise, changed back into his previous clothes, and walked out of the residence.","It was now close to dusk, and the dreary rain had let up, with only a few scattered raindrops drifting down.","In this weather, the number of pedestrians in the West Market had increased quite a bit.","Even though they all carried umbrellas, none were open. They walked in twos and threes, talking and laughing as they passed by the various stalls.","Chen Yi blended in perfectly, strolling about casually and looking around.","In the end, he only bought a few candied haws.","In less than half an hour, Chen Yi returned to the Xiao Family estate.","The moment he returned to the Spring Lotus Garden, he saw Xiao Wuge sitting in a nearby pavilion with a miserable expression.","Beside him sat old Mr. Sun Fu, whom he hadn’t seen in a few days, apparently giving Xiao Wuge a lesson.","When he saw Chen Yi, Xiao Wuge immediately shot up and frantically gestured with his eyes.","\"Brother-in-law, you’re finally back! Save me, save me...\""]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178 - 167: Characters Manifesting a Painting, Calligraphy Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["With Mr. Sun the Elder by his side, Xiao Wuge couldn’t possibly ask him for help for real.","But the aggrieved look in the eyes on his small face all but spelled out one word: \"pitiable.\"","Chen Yi saw his expression and couldn’t help but chuckle to himself, but he also gave him a meaningful look.","He then gave a slight bow, greeted Elder Sun, and sat down at the stone table.","Sun Fu naturally noticed the two of them exchanging glances.","How could he not know what Xiao Wuge was thinking at that moment? He had no choice but to temporarily stop his \"lecture\" and say with a smile:","\"Qingzhou, I have come today to bid you farewell.\"","Chen Yi wasn’t surprised.","A long time ago, Sun Fu had revealed to him his intention of traveling to Jinling.","He had thought Sun Fu would set out shortly after Duke Qian, Zhang Xuan, had left. He never imagined nearly a month would pass before Sun Fu was finally ready to depart.","\"You’ve made your final decision?\"","Sun Fu glanced at the oblivious Xiao Wuge, sighed, and nodded.","\"A few days ago, I sent a letter to my wife and son explaining the situation. They will pack their bags tomorrow.\"","\"After I return home, I will travel with them to Jinling.\"","\"Since you’ve made up your mind, I won’t try to dissuade you. But the road to Jinling is long; please take good care of yourself.\"","Chen Yi knew Sun Fu’s move to Jinling was something of a gamble.","After all, Xiao Wuge’s ability to attract the phenomenon of the thrashing Golden Carp had a touch of the metaphysical about it.","But on second thought, Sun Fu going to Jinling would only be beneficial for Xiao Wuge, with no downsides.","With this elder, who was on good terms with the Xiao Family, in Jinling, Xiao Wuge’s future days as a hostage there would be a little easier.","At the very least, they had a rapport.","Sun Fu nodded slightly and said with a smile, \"Just saying these pleasantries won’t be enough.\"","\"Don’t forget the two calligraphy scrolls you promised me.\"","Chen Yi chuckled, told Xiaodie to prepare dinner, and then led Sun Fu straight back to the study.","Watching the two of them walk away, Xiao Wuge couldn’t help but let out a sigh of relief. ’My brother-in-law really knows what he’s doing.’","Xiaodie saw his pensive expression and asked in a low voice, \"Young Master, are you that afraid of Mr. Sun the Elder?\"","\"It’s not fear... it’s just... a little strange.\"","Xiao Wuge wasn’t really bothered by Sun Fu’s earlier lecture; he just found the look in his eyes very odd.","Although it looked like the caring gaze of an elder, there was a fiery intensity within it that made him uncomfortable.","’Good thing he’s leaving tomorrow. Going to Jinling... Jinling?’","Xiao Wuge’s little face went blank as unpleasant images surfaced in his mind.","’Why is *he* going to Jinling?’","’Don’t tell me he’s planning to go to Jinling early to wait for me to arrive as a hostage?’","’Nooo.’","「Inside the study.」","Sun Fu had no idea that Xiao Wuge had figured out his little scheme. He was currently acting like an attendant, grinding ink for Chen Yi.","It had to be said.","As a Confucian Scholar who had studied for decades and served as an official for decades, even the simple act of grinding ink was performed with more poise and propriety than an ordinary person.","So as not to be impolite, Chen Yi also stood before the table.","He spread out a few slightly larger sheets of Yunsong Paper while making small talk with Sun Fu.","Most of it was asking about his plans after arriving in Jinling.","\"I have two distant relatives there. I’ve already asked them to find a place to live. It’s a small, private courtyard right by the Qinhuai River.\"","\"I have a few old friends in Jinling I can visit from time to time.\"","\"I’m not worried about finances, either. There are several private schools I can teach at. I could even get a position at the Jinling Academy.\"","\"My son is strong and hardworking, and my daughter-in-law is skilled at needlework. We’ll be able to make a living.\"","Listening to Elder Sun ramble on about these details, Chen Yi’s initial thought that this was a gamble began to fade.","For a man over sixty to find a worthy goal to strive for in the final stage of his life was truly a blessing.","\"To learn the Dao in the morning and die by evening is perfectly fine.\"","It was much like that.","When the ink was smooth and its glossy black surface reflected the dim yellow light of dusk from beyond the window, where the evening clouds had finally scattered.","Chen Yi calmed his mind slightly. Then, under Sun Fu’s watchful gaze, he brandished his brush and wrote down the title:","\"Farewell to Duke Changming in Shu State.\"","He paused for a moment.","The image of Sun Fu’s heroic, all-or-nothing gamble involuntarily surfaced in Chen Yi’s mind, and he switched the poem he had originally intended to write for a new one.","Then, his hand moved with his heart. With a slight pressure from the brush’s shaft, the two words \"Thousand Li\" leaped onto the paper.","Instantly, a heroic aura with the power to uproot mountains emerged.","This was followed by the two words \"Yellow Clouds,\" the brushwork light and deft, linking the new characters to the old and creating a seamless flow.","When the four words were complete.","Wisps of golden fluorescence appeared, as if outlining the characters, dyeing the black ink with a layer of gold.","Faintly, on that narrow sheet of paper, a scene of \"a thousand li of yellow clouds\" actually materialized.","It appeared with lifelike vividness, like a weather phenomenon of yellow sand swirling into the sky to form clouds.","It also reflected an expression of utter shock onto Sun Fu’s previously calm face.","\"The words... the words... The words are revealing a painted scroll! The Calligraphy Dao at Perfection...\"","But Chen Yi was completely unaware of this, still writing with single-minded focus.","Even as the glow washed over him in a golden sheen, he did not pause for an instant.","At this moment, Sun Fu’s slightly clouded eyes were wide with astonishment.","He swallowed subconsciously, glanced at the serene-faced Chen Yi, and then looked back at the Yunsong Paper on the table.","He softly recited the poem that was unfolding like a painted scroll.","\"A thousand li of yellow clouds... the white sun dims.\"","\"The north wind blows the wild geese through swirling snow.\"","\"Don’t worry about having no friends on the road ahead, for who in all the world does not know of you?\"","Without a single pause, Chen Yi brandished his brush and splashed ink, completing the poem \"Farewell to Duke Changming in Shu State.\"","Only after he had written his signature, \"Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou,\" affixed his seal, and set down the Wolf Hair Brush did he finally return to his senses."]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179 - 167: Words Manifesting a Painting Scroll, Calligraphy Dao Perfection","paragraphs":["He then watched as the magnificent scenes depicted on the Yunsong Paper shifted one after the other.","Endless yellow sand swirled toward the horizon, and through the haze, the silhouette of the sun emerged.","Amidst wind and snow, the north wind buffeted a neat formation of wild geese.","And in the final scene, a man stood high atop a city wall emblazoned with the word \"Jinling,\" gazing into the distance.","He wore a gray long robe, and his hair and beard were streaked with gray. His smile, however, was gentle yet tinged with a fiery passion, as if he were taking in the entire world with a single glance.","It was none other than Sun Fu—Sun Changming!","As he watched, Chen Yi was satisfied, yet also felt a wave of emotion.","He had originally planned to just write a couple of poems to fulfill the obligation, but at the last moment, he was moved by Sun Fu’s aspirations and chose this piece instead.","He looked up at Sun Fu, still lost in the calligraphy piece. Just as he was about to speak, a golden light flashed before his eyes:","[Text of Natural Perfection. Calligraphy: Cursive Script has broken through to Perfect Level. You have gained a glimpse into the meaning of the Perfection of the Calligraphy Dao.]","[Calligraphy Dao: Great Success. Progress +1000. Perfection Realm has been reached.]","Chen Yi froze, murmuring, \"Calligraphy Dao at Perfection... Perfection... Another epiphany.\"","Perhaps hearing his voice, Sun Fu snapped out of his trance and looked at Chen Yi, his expression ecstatic.","But his first words weren’t to praise Chen Yi’s latest breakthrough in the Calligraphy Dao. Instead, he asked:","\"Qing- Qingzhou, are you sure this calligraphy piece is for me?\"","’It must be. It has to be for me.’","’The figure in the scene is me, after all.’","Hearing this, Chen Yi didn’t know whether to laugh or cry. He simply nodded. \"Of course it’s for you.\"","He pointed to the beginning of the poem. \"’A Farewell Gift for Duke Changming.’ It’s written right here, clear as day.\"","The moment the words left his mouth, Sun Fu had already snatched the calligraphy piece into his hands.","Laughing, he said, \"I knew you wouldn’t go back on your word, Qingzhou,\" all while blowing the ink dry.","He looked like a man who had just acquired a priceless treasure and didn’t want anyone else to lay eyes on it.","Chen Yi knew the old man was ecstatic, so he retrieved a brocade box from the bookshelf behind him for storing the piece.","Once Sun Fu had admiringly closed the lid and was clutching the box to his chest, Chen Yi said teasingly,","\"It seems I won’t need to write that second poem. You look quite satisfied with this one.\"","Unexpectedly, Sun Fu actually nodded and laughed heartily. \"Indeed, you don’t. To have this one piece—with such fine words and finer calligraphy—is more than enough for me.\"","’Who in all the world would not know me?’","Even if he, Sun Fu, were to drop dead this very moment, his name would be recorded in the annals of history thanks to this poem.","How could he not be utterly content?","\"Qingzhou, your Calligraphy Dao has already captured its true essence. The heart moves before the brush, and the technique flows with the wrist. Only when the artist and their art have aged as one can the true face of heaven and earth be seen.\"","\"Given time, you will surely enter the Saint Realm and become a Calligraphy Saint of this era, as renowned as Zhao Tian and Wang Meng.\"","Chen Yi knew that Zhao Tian and Wang Meng were the only two \"Calligraphy Saints\" in the Great Wei Dynasty.","It was said that when they completed a piece, not only did the characters shimmer with a golden aura, but their Mental Realm could manifest an entire illusory world, as vivid as a painted scroll.","\"You flatter me, senior. I am still a long way from reaching that Realm.\"","\"I always speak the truth. This is no exaggeration. When they were your age, the Calligraphy Dao of those two was nowhere near yours.\"","Sun Fu was in high spirits from the happy occasion, and he seemed several years younger.","Beyond his delight over the poem itself, he felt even more resolute about his prior plans.","Never mind becoming Xiao Wuge’s teacher or guiding him to success. For the sake of not bringing shame upon this poem, he had to give it his all.","They chatted and laughed for a while longer.","Chen Yi tidied the desk, neatly arranging the brush, ink, paper, and inkstone, before sitting down with Sun Fu by the window to chat.","As they chatted, the conversation naturally turned to the Xiao Family’s current circumstances.","Having stayed with the Xiao Family these past few days, Sun Fu had a clear perspective on some matters. He had also spoken with the Old Marquis several times, so he was better informed.","Chen Yi, for his part, relied on intelligence from clandestine channels, so he too was well aware of the family’s situation.","However, there were many things he couldn’t elaborate on, lest Sun Fu assume he had some ulterior motive concerning the Xiao Family. It would only invite unnecessary trouble.","Sun Fu looked at the calm, composed, and inscrutable young man, knowing there was far more to him than met the eye. He couldn’t help but ask more bluntly:","\"What are your plans for the future?\"","\"In what respect, senior?\"","\"Your personal plans. You can’t possibly intend to remain an Instructor at Guiyun Academy forever, can you?\"","At that, Chen Yi met his gaze directly and replied with a frank smile:","\"And why not?\"","\"Because with your talent and ability, it’s highly unlikely you’ll remain confined to that academy. Even the Xiao Family would find it difficult to hold on to you.\"","Seeing how blunt he was, Chen Yi guessed what was on his mind. He thought for a moment before asking:","\"Are you worried I’ll act against the Xiao Family’s interests, or that I’ll abandon them?\"","Sun Fu didn’t mince words. He nodded. \"Both.\"","\"The Xiao Family is currently beset by troubles both internal and external. If you were to lend your aid, some of these problems would be solved with ease.\"","\"If you stand by and do nothing, it will be more difficult, but I believe Marquis Xiao and Jinghong can still resolve things.\"","\"But if you were to work against the Xiao Family, then...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi raised a hand to interrupt, his expression turning serious.","\"I am already tied to the Xiao Family. To say we will ’live and die together’ might be a stretch, but ’the husband follows where the wife leads’ is an apt description.\"","Sun Fu stared, taken aback. Then, unsure whether to laugh or cry, he pointed at Chen Yi. \"’The husband follows where the wife leads?’\"","\"Qingzhou, if you were to say such a thing in front of others, I imagine you’d be condemned by every scholar in the land.\"","But Chen Yi replied with self-assurance, \"I’m a live-in son-in-law. I follow my wife and rely on her for support. What’s wrong with that?\"","\"You... you...\"","Although Sun Fu found the phrase unorthodox, he understood Chen Yi’s meaning.","’Ultimately, it meant he was on the Xiao Family’s side.’","And that was enough.","Later, after they had all finished dinner.","Chen Yi found out what time Sun Fu was leaving the next day, then walked him out of Spring Lotus Garden, watching his brisk figure disappear into the lamplit night.","He couldn’t help but feel a little wistful.","’With such an elder to teach him by word and example, Xiao Wuge’s time in Jinling should be a little easier,’ he thought.","With that, Chen Yi called for Xiao Wuge to ask about the situation at Qingjing Residence.","\"Liu Yu of the Liu Family?\"","\"The Old Marquis refused him.\"","\"When Big Sis came back, she was smiling. She seemed really relieved.\"","After Xiao Wuge had recounted everything, his young face tensed.","\"Brother-in-law, the Liu family are such bad people! They bullied Big Sis! I’ll never forgive them!\"","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod. For matters like this, actions spoke louder than words.","He was somewhat relieved, but he couldn’t resist pinching Xiao Wuge’s cheek.","\"I, your brother-in-law, only have a few little ’secrets,’ and you’ve gone and blabbed them all.\"","Xiao Wuge didn’t dare move, grinning painfully. \"But I was just telling the truth!\"","\"You know Acupuncture, and you were the one who cured Big Sis.\"","Chen Yi let go of his cheek and said irritably, \"It looks like I’ll have to suggest to Big Sis tomorrow morning that she add a few more lessons to your schedule.\"","\"No, Brother-in-law...\"","No?","It didn’t matter if he wanted them or not.","’This little brother-in-law of mine is practically a spy the Xiao Family planted on me.’","Chen Yi let out a few sinister chuckles, scaring Xiao Wuge into promising he’d never do it again. Only then did he let the boy go wash up and head to bed.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi also washed up, changed into comfortable clothes, and sat quietly in his room, gazing out the window.","By now, the sky had grown completely dark.","At some point, dark clouds had gathered in the night sky, looking as if they were building toward another torrential downpour.","And so, the croaking of frogs within Spring Lotus Garden was incessant.","Loud, chaotic, and grating.","As Chen Yi listened and watched, his gaze drifted to the nearby Jiaxing Garden, his thoughts racing.","Figures and names surfaced in his mind, one after another.","The Jing State Liu Family.","The Hidden Guard.","Black Tooth, Bright Moon Building.","The Shu State Governor’s Office, Liu Hong, Yang Ye, Xiao Dongchen, and Chen Yunfan.","The Xiao Family, Xiao Jinghong, Xiao Wan’er, the Old Marquis...","It was as if a great net had been cast over them all, or a chessboard upon which they were merely pieces.","About an hour later, Chen Yi finally pulled back his gaze and let out a soft sigh.","\"Still just a chess piece, in the end...\"","He murmured softly.","Chen Yi rose and donned the black clothes he had prepared, strapping the five-section Long Spear to his left forearm.","Next came the Immortal Drunk and Qingfeng Drunk, as well as the case of Silver Needles.","Tonight, he was going with Liu Lang to meet Black Tooth and the others. Since he couldn’t reveal his Martial Arts, he would likely have to display more of his Medical Dao.","As for his identity...","Other than a representative from the Jing State Liu Family, there was no other choice!"]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180 - 168: Black Tooth, Lady Tiger","paragraphs":["Why the Jing State Liu Family?","There were many reasons.","First, someone from the Liu Family had just died in Shu State after a conflict with the Xiao Family.","Second, Liu Jing had worked with Black Tooth before—once when the Illusory Sound Sect and Liu Lang robbed the Xiao Family of its medicinal herbs, and another time when they targeted Hundred Herbs Hall.","Although both attempts ended in failure, Black Tooth had indeed earned quite a bit of silver from the Liu Family.","In fact, those prior failures made Chen Yi’s mission all the more favorable.","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi finished his preparations, grabbed the silver notes hidden in his room, and slipped silently out of the Spring Lotus Garden. He wound his way through the streets and alleys, heading for the house in the West Market.","It was now deep into the night.","The streets were mostly empty, the narrow alleys even more so.","The few people he did encounter were mostly drunks or gamblers.","But none of them noticed him pass by.","It was all thanks to his much-improved Body Technique.","Since his cultivation advanced to the Sixth Grade Realm, his control over his True Essence had become much more fluid, leading to significant improvements in all of his techniques.","Especially after a \"Divine Position\" was born in his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi, his Fist Technique, Body Technique, and Spear Technique were all enhanced by Spiritual Essence.","For example, the Meteor Butterfly Step, enhanced by the Wood Spirit, gained a Surging Power.","When he used this Body Technique, not only did it consume less True Essence, but it also allowed him to slightly restore the True Essence in his three Seas of Qi.","The Wandering Dragon and Phoenix, on the other hand, was enhanced by the Vortex Power from his Wood and Fire Dual Spirits. It was far more explosive and dramatically increased the speed of his Body Technique.","It allowed him to circle an opponent like a raging vortex.","His other techniques, such as the Mountain Shattering Fist, Hundred Flowers Palm, and Dragon-slaying Spear, had also received noticeable improvements.","The specifics would require further testing.","Just then, a steady drizzle began to fall, and the faint rumble of thunder rolled across the sky.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow and quickened his pace.","Such weather was even better for those who moved in the dark than a moonless, windy night.","But it also tended to frustrate those accustomed to the light, like Hundred Households Fang Hongxiu and her party from the Imprisonment Department, who were currently patrolling the area around the West Market.","She glanced at the sky and ordered her subordinates to put on their raincoats, lest they get soaked.","A younger-looking Imprisonment Officer beside her muttered under his breath while putting on his raincoat and bamboo hat:","\"Damn this weather. Raining again.\"","The mere mention of rain made Fang Hongxiu frown.","Ever since Chen Yi had taken her down with Qingfeng Drunk and verbally ’humiliated’ her, she thought of nothing but capturing him and throwing him in prison.","If not for the other cases at the Imprisonment Department, she likely would have dedicated all her time and energy to hunting down that scoundrel.","Even so, Fang Hongxiu brought her subordinates to patrol the West Market every night.","Her intuition told her the scoundrel’s lair was somewhere in the West Market.","If she could find just one clue, she was confident she could follow the trail straight to him.","\"Stay sharp, everyone. Weather like this is when shady characters are most active.\"","\"Especially that scoundrel who’s made us lose face twice now. If we find him again, we absolutely must not let him get away!\"","\"Yes, Lord Hundred Households!\"","The Imprisonment Officers exchanged glances, wry smiles on their faces.","They felt the same as Fang Hongxiu, eager to bring the man to justice, but if they did run into him again, how were they supposed to actually capture him?","They had failed twice in a row—ambushed the first time, poisoned the second.","’What about next time?’","They were all a little worried. If they were taken down a third time, their failure as Imprisonment Officers would likely become infamous throughout Shu State.","It would be an absolute, utter humiliation.","From a safe distance, Chen Yi saw Fang Hongxiu’s group and heard her voice. He couldn’t help but smirk.","’This Hundred Households from the Imprisonment Department seems to have become obsessed after I took her down twice.’","’Patrolling the West Market every single night...’","’Is she vowing not to rest until I’m brought to justice?’","Chen Yi was bemused by her dedication, but he had no intention of causing trouble and delaying his real objective.","Once he was sure Fang Hongxiu and her group were gone, he skirted around Hundred Herbs Hall and arrived at the house.","Zhang Dabao, who had already retired for the night, saw him arrive and quickly rose to his feet, bowing.","\"Sir.\"","Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment, setting his bamboo hat on the table and motioning for Zhang Dabao to begin the disguise.","Though Zhang Dabao didn’t understand why he had come so late, he did as instructed and got to work.","Thanks to their previous practice sessions, it took less than the time of half an incense stick for him to transform Chen Yi into \"Chen Yu.\"","Zhang Dabao was just about to pack up his tools when Chen Yi spoke. \"Apply another mask on top of this one.\"","After a slight hesitation, Zhang Dabao warned, \"Sir, wearing two human skin masks makes it easier for someone to spot the flaws.\"","\"It’s fine. Just do it.\"","\"Then, what do you have in mind?\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then said a single word: \"Sinister.\"","He had met Liu Wen once before, and his strongest impression of the man was that he was both insidious and ruthless.","’His subordinates are probably the same type of people.’","Fortunately, Zhang Dabao’s craftsmanship was superb.","In the time it took for an incense stick to burn, he had prepared a half-mask and completed Chen Yi’s new disguise.","It was a half-mask, a deliberate choice to make the disguise less obvious at a glance.","It was a thoughtful precaution.","Chen Yi examined his reflection in a copper mirror by the light of an oil lamp.","The overall shape of his face hadn’t changed much; he was still handsome.","But his eyes were now slightly narrower, his lips thinner, giving him a sharp, cruel look.","\"Not bad.\"","Chen Yi nodded, and his expression immediately shifted.","It was as if he’d become another person entirely. The aura around him turned colder, more sinister.","Seeing his transformation, Zhang Dabao’s jaw dropped.","Although he was a master of the Disguise Skill, his work was mostly physical transformation; the finer details could often betray the ruse.","But with Chen Yi’s transformation, even he was starting to believe this was the man’s true appearance.","No, it was more like Chen Yi himself was inherently a sinister man.","Watching him, Zhang Dabao couldn’t help but give a thumbs-up. \"Sir, you’re incredible.\"","A smirk played on Chen Yi’s lips. He shot Zhang Dabao a sidelong glance and said disdainfully, \"A mere parlor trick.\"","His expression and tone now bore a striking resemblance to Liu Wen’s.","The two chatted for a moment longer.","Liu Lang arrived in a hurry, dressed in black Night Clothes.","When he saw Chen Yi, he stopped short, stunned. \"You... Boss?\"","Chen Yi gave a slight nod. \"As expected of the Sword Madman. A man who keeps his word.\"","Liu Lang looked him up and down, finding no flaw in the disguise. He couldn’t help but ask,","\"So, are you going to tell me who you’re going as?\"","Chen Yi shot him a look and instructed Zhang Dabao to secure the doors and windows. He then led the way out of the house.","\"The Jing State Liu Family.\"","Liu Lang pondered for a moment, then a look of understanding spread across his face as he hurried after him.","\"Someone from the Liu Family... that could actually work.\"","\"That Liu Jing fellow hired Black Tooth before to go after the Xiao Family. This time, with the fire...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi raised a hand, cutting him off. \"Quiet.\"","Liu Lang nodded in understanding and led the way.","The two then moved toward the southwest, keeping to the shadows.","Under the cover of the dark, rainy night, their journey was unobstructed.","Before long, Liu Lang led him into a narrow alley nestled between dilapidated houses.","A hoarse voice suddenly echoed from the shadows. \"Visiting the wharf, the heavens, or the hells?\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. ’A password?’","Before he could give it much thought, Liu Lang had already stepped forward and exchanged a few words with the figure in the darkness.","It was mostly underworld slang, incomprehensible to outsiders.","In any case, they had successfully passed the first checkpoint.","Next, a short man in black led Chen Yi and Liu Lang to Yanhua Lane in the South City.","Seeing the large sign for the Spring Rain Building, Chen Yi couldn’t help but have the same thought Liu Lang had expressed earlier.","’Just like Black Tooth. The best place to hide is in plain sight. To think he’s hidden right inside the Spring Rain Building.’","Suddenly, Chen Yi thought of the Hidden Guard, Lady Tiger.","In a way, Lady Tiger and Black Tooth were cut from the same cloth.","According to his earlier theory, Lady Tiger was probably also hiding somewhere in Yanhua Lane.","Soon, the man in black led them to a quiet room upstairs in the Spring Rain Building, closed the door behind them, and left.","The two of them took their seats.","Liu Lang pointed to the opposite wall, signaling that Black Tooth would emerge from there.","But before he could even lower his hand, a section of the side wall swung inward, and two figures—one tall, one short—stepped into the room.","\"...\"","Liu Lang lowered his hand, looking slightly embarrassed, and said irritably,","\"You’re as elusive as ever, Black Tooth.\"","As he spoke, however, his gaze landed on the smaller of the two figures.","Chen Yi did the same, sizing up the arrivals.","Both were wearing black masks, but he could surmise that the taller one must be Black Tooth.","As for the identity of the smaller one...","Before Chen Yi could even guess, the shorter figure covered her mouth with a delicate laugh. \"’The ’Sword Madman’ didn’t come alone, I see~\"","\"’Black Tooth, this seems to be against your rules, no?’\"","Her voice was ethereal, with a faint, wispy quality.","A chill went down Chen Yi’s spine as he instantly recognized her.","’The Hidden Guard... Lady Tiger?’","’She’s appearing here together with Black Tooth?’"]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181 - 169: I’ve Said My Piece, Now It’s Your Turn","paragraphs":["There were only two possibilities for Lady Tiger’s presence here.","First, Lady Tiger was one of Black Tooth’s people, or perhaps one of the Bright Moon Building’s.","Second, Lady Tiger had already been open with Black Tooth, striking a deal to complete that business transaction together.","Regardless of which it was, it was bad news for Chen Yi.","Unexpected developments often led to unnecessary trouble.","As his thoughts raced, Chen Yi spoke before Black Tooth could, his head tilted up slightly, his tone dismissive.","\"I came here only to settle a score with Black Tooth.\"","Then, he tilted his head slightly, glancing at Lady Tiger only from the corner of his eye, and continued,","\"Your presence here, however, displeases me.\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang glanced at him and obediently kept his mouth shut.","’No wonder Boss Chen was willing to take such a risk.’","’This level of composure alone was something no ordinary person could hope to match.’","The eyes beneath Black Tooth’s mask glinted strangely. He raised a hand to stop Lady Tiger, who was about to speak, and asked in a cold tone,","\"Forgive my ignorance, but may I ask who you are?\"","\"Liu... Wu. Of the Jing State Liu Family.\"","Chen Yi casually fabricated a name, his gaze meeting Black Tooth’s eyes.","\"So tell me, shouldn’t I be here to settle a score with you?\"","Black Tooth’s eyes twitched. \"The Jing State Liu Family?\"","\"And which member of the Liu Family might you be?\"","\"Who I am is not important. What’s important is that your previous failure led to the death of my family’s Sixth Young Master in Shu State.\"","At this, Chen Yi turned to face him and asked in a low voice,","\"Shouldn’t we settle this score?\"","Black Tooth was silent for a moment before gesturing for Lady Tiger to sit down with him, opposite Chen Yi and Liu Lang.","The dim, quiet room was lit only by the oil lamp on the table.","There was no breeze; the flame stood perfectly still, pointing straight up.","But as Black Tooth and Lady Tiger took their seats, the dim, yellow candlelight flickered. Lady Tiger sized up Chen Yi and asked,","\"Liu Wu... How can you prove your identity?\"","Chen Yi didn’t even look at her, keeping his eyes fixed on Black Tooth. The implication was clear.","Seeing this, a flash of coldness crossed Lady Tiger’s eyes, but her tone shifted, taking on a flirtatious, worldly air.","\"Such posturing... It seems you really might be from the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"Black Tooth, you never mentioned the Jing State Liu Family would be involved in this ’business.’ Otherwise, this little lady would have surely had to make a concession.\"","A tactical retreat to advance.","Chen Yi saw right through it, his expression remaining impassive.","Liu Lang glanced at him, then smiled and asked, \"Black Tooth, aren’t you going to introduce this young lady?\"","He had dealt with Black Tooth many times, so he could afford to speak with a familiar tone.","But in this situation, it was clear Black Tooth was carefully assessing everyone present.","He considered \"Sword Mad\" Liu Lang a semi-ally. That Lady Tiger could arrive with him also spoke to an unusual relationship.","Thus, the one who truly concerned Black Tooth was the stranger, Chen Yi.","\"How can you prove your identity?\"","\"The fifth child of the Liu Family’s main branch is their Second Young Miss. I’ve never heard of her becoming a man.\"","Chen Yi had anticipated this question. He answered evasively,","\"That’s not funny in the slightest.\"","\"My family’s Fifth Young Miss is far too precious. Why would she ever set foot in a den of filth like this?\"","Even someone as calm and astute as Black Tooth couldn’t help his tone turning cold after being provoked time and again.","\"I’ll ask one last time. How do you prove your identity?\"","At these words, Liu Lang’s heart tightened. Just as he was about to make a joke to defuse the tension, he saw Chen Yi let out a soft laugh and calmly pull a stack of silver notes from his robes, placing it on the table.","Black Tooth glanced at it. Recognizing them as notes for ten thousand taels of silver, he was about twenty percent convinced.","There were quite a few people in all of Shu State who could produce ten thousand taels in silver notes.","However, those who would do so before any agreement had been reached were few and far between.","Such a person was either a fool or possessed unshakable confidence.","Clearly, Black Tooth didn’t believe a fool would dare to act so presumptuously before him.","Not even if he truly was from the Jing State Liu Family.","Chen Yi didn’t need to guess his thoughts. After stacking the silver notes neatly, he said,","\"Today, I only intend to speak with you. I’m not accustomed to, nor do I appreciate, the presence of others.\"","Before Black Tooth could speak, Lady Tiger purred from the side, \"Brother Liu, you seem to hold quite a deep prejudice against this little lady, don’t you?\"","\"It’s not prejudice,\" Chen Yi said with a glance in her direction. \"I simply don’t believe a woman is capable of accomplishing great things.\"","Most members of the Noble Families were misogynistic, so his words fit his assumed identity.","\"You...\"","Even a saint would lose their temper, to say nothing of Lady Tiger, a Hidden Guard Silver Banner Officer.","At that moment, Black Tooth raised a hand. \"This woman beside me, Lou Yuxue, is one of my Bright Moon Building’s people,\" he said, his voice devoid of emotion.","Lou Yuxue. Lady Tiger.","Chen Yi silently committed the name to memory and dropped the issue, speaking directly.","\"Originally, I hadn’t planned to reveal myself. Or rather, my young master was unwilling to have his identity exposed.\"","\"Unfortunately, ’Sword Mad’ failed to complete his task, and someone from your Bright Moon Building interfered. I had no choice but to step in and resolve this, so that I can answer to my young master.\"","A strange expression flashed across Liu Lang’s face; he had no idea what task Chen Yi was talking about.","Black Tooth glanced at him, then turned back to Chen Yi. \"And which young master would that be?\"","\"The one who just arrived in Shu State.\"","\"Liu Wen?\"","With the Bright Moon Building’s extensive network, they would naturally know about the arrival from the Jing State Liu Family.","At this, Black Tooth was fifty percent convinced.","\"But I’m still a bit puzzled,\" he said. \"Is Second Young Master Liu planning to go against the Xiao Family to the bitter end?\"","Chen Yi’s brow furrowed. Feigning displeasure, he tapped the silver notes on the table.","\"Whether this matter succeeds or fails, it ends with me.\"","Black Tooth paused, then nodded in understanding. He knew that mentioning Liu Wen’s name was as far as Chen Yi could go.","Just as he was about to speak, Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue chimed in with a smile,","\"After all this talk, your identity is still rather vague.\"","\"How can you prove you work for Second Young Master Liu, and aren’t just using his name to run a scam?\"","Chen Yi froze, his gaze turning colder as he looked at her.","\"How would Miss Yuxue have me prove myself?\"","Lou Yuxue glanced at Black Tooth. Seeing no reaction, she understood his intent and said with a smile,","\"Brother Liu, don’t be angry. This is a serious matter. A little caution on our part is beneficial for you as well, isn’t it?\"","Chen Yi stared at her, his expression unmoved.","Lou Yuxue thought for a moment. \"Why don’t you tell us Second Young Master Liu’s purpose for coming to Shu State?\"","\"Or perhaps a secret that we can verify later?\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi replied without a change in expression, \"Miss Yuxue, you’re asking for the impossible.\"","Then he turned to Black Tooth. \"Is this what you think as well?\"","Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue exchanged a look before he nodded. \"She can speak for the Bright Moon Building.\"","Instantly, the quiet room plunged into a dead silence.","The candlelight flickered weakly, and the atmosphere grew palpably tense.","Seeing this, Liu Lang couldn’t help but break into a cold sweat for Chen Yi.","His hand, hidden beneath the table, rested on his thigh, ready to draw his blade at the first sign of trouble.","Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue paid him no mind, their gazes fixed solely on Chen Yi.","A long silence followed.","A sinister smile slowly spread across Chen Yi’s ice-cold face. \"As expected of the Bright Moon Building. Such strict rules. I like it very much.\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, his speech quickened. \"One of my young master’s purposes in coming to Shu State this time is a marriage alliance with the Xiao Family’s eldest daughter.\"","\"Oh?\" Lou Yuxue murmured, then asked in that same sweet voice, \"From what I know, relations between the Xiao and Liu Families are strained. Why would they arrange a marriage alliance?\"","This time, before Chen Yi could explain, Black Tooth cut in, \"We can verify the truth of this later.\"","Lou Yuxue gave an obedient murmur of assent and fell silent.","Black Tooth glanced at her, then his gaze swept over Chen Yi and Liu Lang before finally landing on the silver notes on the table. He mused,","\"I wonder, what is Brother Liu’s true purpose in coming here today? Surely it isn’t just to demand an explanation from me for Liu Jing’s death?\"","With the first test passed, Chen Yi relaxed slightly. He spoke based on what he already knew of the situation:","\"That ’business’ of yours has a new player. Naturally, I had to come and assess the situation.\"","\"Is that all?\"","\"If my assessment is unfavorable, then I’ll have no choice but to get involved myself.\"","Black Tooth seemed taken aback. He asked in a strange tone, \"You don’t mind conspiring with the other party?\"","The \"other party\" was the one who had previously offered a bid of thirty thousand taels of Gold.","Chen Yi gave a slight nod. \"I might as well be blunt. This ’business’ is my young master’s betrothal gift.\"","\"Therefore, failure is not an option.\"","At this, Black Tooth and Lady Tiger exchanged a look of mutual surprise.","Only Liu Lang, who knew the truth, bit down hard on his back teeth, afraid he would burst out laughing.","If he hadn’t known about Chen Yi’s relationship with the Xiao Family from the start, he might have actually believed the story.","’Betrothal gift, my foot.’","’If the Three Towns’ summer grain were actually burned, this Boss Chen would be the first to raise hell.’","After a moment’s thought, Black Tooth smiled. \"In that case, our goals are aligned.\"","\"With Brother Liu’s involvement, our chances of success in this ’business’ will certainly be much higher.\"","As he spoke, he collected the stack of silver notes.","Chen Yi raised a single eyebrow and turned his head, pointedly not watching the action.","’That was one of my few personal stashes of cash, besides my income from the Hundred Herbs Hall.’","’Gone, just like that... It stung a little.’","Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue noted his reaction, her heart still half-convinced and half-skeptical of his identity.","’She felt there was something very fishy about his appearance tonight.’","After a moment’s thought, Lou Yuxue turned to the silent Liu Lang and asked,","\"Speaking of which, Brother ’Sword Mad,’ how did you manage to get involved with the likes of the Liu Family?\"","Liu Lang sneered, crossed his arms, and refused to acknowledge her.","Chen Yi, however, glanced at her and said coolly, \"I healed his injuries.\"","Before Lou Yuxue could react, Black Tooth, who knew of Liu Lang’s condition, asked with keen interest,","\"Brother Liu is a ’Medical Saint Hand’?\"","Lou Yuxue was taken aback, her beautiful eyes fixed on Chen Yi in clear disbelief.","Chen Yi looked at the two of them. \"You people from the Bright Moon Building truly make a fuss over nothing.\"","The moment he finished speaking, he flicked out a Silver Needle, which embedded itself upright in the table.","Then, with a series of flicks from his fingers, threads of True Essence made the Silver Needle vibrate rapidly.","A piercing hum immediately echoed through the quiet room.","Black Tooth’s eyes narrowed, as did Lady Tiger’s.","They both stared, unblinking, at the Silver Needle on the table. \"Controlling Needle with Qi... a skill only a ’Medical Saint Hand’ can perform.\"","Hearing this, Chen Yi crooked a finger, retrieving the Silver Needle. \"I hope this is the last of your tests,\" he said coldly.","At that, Black Tooth clapped his hands in admiration. \"If Brother Liu had shown this skill earlier, I naturally wouldn’t have dared to question you further.\"","Lou Yuxue chimed in with a smile, \"I had heard there were two ’Medical Saint Hands’ in the Liu Family’s Xinglin Hall. It seems the rumors were mistaken.\"","\"At Brother Liu’s age, your future achievements in the Medical Dao will surely reach even greater heights.\"","After this, neither of them had any more doubts about Chen Yi’s identity.","Chen Yi gave a noncommittal nod, a coolly sinister smile appearing on his handsome face.","\"I’m finished with my business. Now, let’s talk about yours.\""]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182 - 170: Easily Amazed","paragraphs":["After Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue finished their probing, they moved on to discuss matters related to the current deal.","For the most part, however, Chen Yi had already learned of the situation from Liu Lang.","Or had gleaned it from eavesdropping on the Hidden Guard.","Among the new information, only two things concerned Chen Yi.","The first was news about the other financier.","Although Black Tooth was vague, the few scraps of information he let slip made it easy to deduce that the person was likely a local from Shu State.","Probably a member of one of the great Noble Families.","This aligned with Chen Yi’s earlier speculation. However, with so little information available, he couldn’t be certain which family the person was from.","After all, there were many families in Shu State on good terms with the Xiao Family, but even more who were their enemies.","Until that person’s identity was exposed, it would be difficult to deduce who they were from such fragmented clues.","The second piece of news concerned the members of the Evil Demonic Dao who were participating in this deal.","Besides Liu Lang, there were four other Middle Third-Grade Martial Artists.","There were also rumored to be two Upper Third-Grade Martial Arts Powerhouses.","However, Black Tooth didn’t elaborate, nor did he reveal their identities.","Another person worth mentioning was Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue.","During their conversation, Chen Yi had focused most of his attention on her.","Beyond her identity as a Hidden Guard, he was more focused on memorizing her features so he could determine her public-facing identity.","To be honest, of all the Hidden Guards he knew, Lady Tiger and Simurgh Phoenix were the two he knew the least about.","He didn’t even know what their mission was in Shu State.","He was, at the very least, curious.","After about the time it takes an incense stick to burn, Black Tooth and Lady Tiger rose to leave.","\"Wait here a moment,\" Black Tooth said. \"Once everyone else has arrived, I will summon you to discuss our next steps.\"","\"Brother Liu~\" Lady Tiger cooed. \"See you in a bit~\"","With that, they departed through an opening that appeared in the wall behind them, not the way they had originally entered.","Once the wall of the room sealed shut, Liu Lang grinned. \"That Black Tooth is damn cautious, building so many secret passages.\"","He paused, glanced at the opposite wall, and added, \"I’ll bet there’s one on that side, too.\"","Chen Yi glanced over and remarked nonchalantly, \"That’s the outer wall of the Spring Rain Building.\"","\"...\"","Liu Lang thought for a moment, then scratched his head and muttered a few words under his breath.","It was something along the lines of how he couldn’t stand people who liked to overthink things.","Chen Yi paid him no mind, simply sitting quietly in his chair and contemplating what was to come.","Based on the information he had gathered, the ones responsible for \"burning the summer grain of the Three Towns\" were likely Hidden Guard members stationed in the Three Towns.","Specifically, the Hidden Guards under the command of Ge the Third.","Lady Tiger was responsible for liaising with Black Tooth, acting as an intermediary.","Gray Wolf Xiao Dongchen, on the other hand, was pulling the strings from behind the scenes.","This division of labor made it clear that while all three were Silver Banner Officers, Xiao Dongchen carried more weight.","The fact that Simurgh Phoenix Cui Qingwu had acted on Xiao Dongchen’s behalf to frame Liu Jing and implicate the Xiao Family further supported this conclusion.","From this, he could confirm that while the Hidden Guard aimed to throw Shu State into chaos, they were more concerned with the Xiao Family, the great banner of the state.","In other words, as long as chaos erupted within the Xiao Family, Shu State was sure to follow.","Therefore, throwing the Xiao Family into disarray was a shortcut to achieving their mission’s objective.","Compared to that, his own importance as a \"fledgling\" took a backseat.","However, the Hidden Guard was only one party involved in the plot to \"burn the summer grain of the Three Towns,\" and it was the party he had the most information on.","At least for the moment, the three Hidden Guards could be moved to the back of his mind.","His top priority now was to figure out the identities of all the Evil Demons involved, as well as that of the \"financier.\"","As Chen Yi was pondering these things, Liu Lang’s gaze suddenly snapped to the right, the direction from which Black Tooth and Lady Tiger had come.","\"A real powerhouse just arrived.\"","\"Hm?\"","Seeing Chen Yi look over, Liu Lang grinned and said, \"It’s an Upper Third-Grade expert, but his aura is only average. His Technique Realm probably isn’t that high.\"","Of course, he was comparing the newcomer to the likes of Xiao Jinghong and his master, Sword Ghost.","He himself, of course, would stand no chance against an Upper Third-Grade expert.","The words had barely left his mouth when a sinister voice suddenly echoed through the private room:","\"I was wondering who was speaking with such bravado. Ah, it’s the ’Sword Madman,’ Liu Lang.\"","A surging aura descended upon the private room along with the voice.","But there was something strange about the aura; it seemed vast and boundless, yet it felt somewhat unfocused.","\"All show and no substance\" would not be an exaggeration.","Liu Lang sneered. \"Minor Achievement in Fist Intent? You’d best not embarrass yourself with that, old-timer.\"","As he spoke, a domineering and razor-sharp Sword Intent erupted from his body.","Its edge was utterly exposed.","The moment it manifested, it cleaved the surging pressure in the room in two.","Though Chen Yi said nothing, he withstood the pressure as well, slowly raising his hand to rap a knuckle on the table.","THUD.","A muffled sound.","It was as if a majestic mountain had descended, crushing the presence that had been split in two.","Faintly, it was as if a colossal RUMBLE echoed in the ears of all who were paying attention to the private room.","\"Hm?\"","\"This is...\"","\"A mountain... the Fist Dao... at Great Success!\"","Even Liu Lang was stunned, staring at Chen Yi in utter disbelief. \"You... Your Punch...\"","He had always thought Chen Yi specialized in the Medical Dao. Even if he had dabbled in the Martial Arts, he couldn’t have been that strong.","Who would have thought he’d achieved Great Success in the Fist Dao?","’Dammit, did this mysterious Boss Chen start his Cultivation in the womb?’","’The Medical Dao and the Fist Dao... Minor Success in one, Great Success in the other.’","’Two separate Daos, both requiring immense time and effort, had been mastered by a young man about his own age.’","The Medical Dao was universally acknowledged in the Jianghu as being incredibly difficult to master; its practitioners were far fewer in number than Martial Arts Powerhouses.","Otherwise, Black Tooth and Lady Tiger wouldn’t have been so accommodating earlier after learning that Chen Yi was a Medical Saint Hand.","Chen Yi naturally heard the surprised gasps from the surrounding rooms.","He simply lifted his head slightly, glanced out of the corner of his eye at the Upper Third-Grade expert who had just acted, and said coolly,","\"Such a fuss over nothing.\"","The very same words he had used when he revealed his Medical Dao.","\"You!?\"","The Upper Third-Grade powerhouse, who had just lost face, grew furious from the humiliation. But just as he was about to strike again, he heard Black Tooth say, his voice tinged with delight,","\"Elder Demon Fang, stay your hand.\"","\"Not only has Brother Liu achieved Great Success in the Fist Dao, but he is also a Medical Saint Hand. He is the guarantee for our entire deal.\"","\"If you make a move and anger him, don’t come crying to me when you get injured later. Don’t say I didn’t warn you.\"","Hearing this, not only was Elder Demon Fang, who had been about to attack, left stunned, but the others were even more shocked than before.","Even Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue couldn’t help but praise him. \"Brother Liu, you are truly terrifying.\"","\"To have achieved Minor Success in the Medical Dao is one thing, but you’ve also cultivated the Fist Dao to Great Success. This little lady is thoroughly impressed~\"","The other listeners were likely Middle Third-Grade Martial Artists, their strength not even a match for Liu Lang’s, let alone Chen Yi, who cultivated both the Medical and Martial Daos.","For a moment, all the surrounding private rooms fell silent.","After a moment of silence, Chen Yi frowned slightly and tapped the table, feigning impatience. \"Black Tooth, my time is short. Let’s begin.\"","Black Tooth certainly wasn’t going to refuse. His tone was even friendlier than before.","\"Just a moment, Brother Liu. I’m on it.\"","A series of rustling sounds followed, evidently from Black Tooth contacting the various parties.","Seeing this, Chen Yi said nothing more.","Beside him, however, Liu Lang gave him a thumbs-up. \"O—uh... Brother Liu, you’re amazing.\"","\"I thought you only focused on the Medical Dao and weren’t an expert in the Martial Arts. I never expected you to have such a powerful Fist Dao up your sleeve.\"","Chen Yi shot him a look and snorted, half in jest. \"If you weren’t so incompetent, would I have needed to step in?\"","Liu Lang’s smile froze, and the corner of his mouth twitched.","’If this weren’t the wrong time and place, he would have insisted on testing Chen Yi’s Martial Arts, no matter what.’","’But a thought was just a thought. He knew that the stronger Chen Yi was, the more advantageous it would be for what they had to do next.’","’In any case, he had already boarded Hundred Herbs Hall’s pirate ship. He had no choice but to see this through to the end.’","「Not long after.」","A short man dressed in black entered, bowed respectfully, placed two black iron masks on the table, and left.","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"Is this really necessary?\"","After all the posturing and talking, many of them had already revealed telling details. Putting on masks now felt a bit like burying their heads in the sand.","More importantly, of course, if everyone was wearing a mask, it would be harder for him to identify the members of the Evil Demonic Dao.","Liu Lang glanced at him, picked up the two masks, and handed one over as he put the other one on himself.","\"It’s a rule of the Bright Moon Building. Before a mission, only the organizer knows everyone’s identity.\"","\"As for guessing or recognizing anyone else, that’s all up to individual skill.\"","Chen Yi grunted, took the mask, and put it on. \"What about you?\" he asked casually.","Elder Demon Fang had already recognized him as the \"Sword Madman\" and announced it to everyone.","Obviously, Liu Lang couldn’t hide his identity anymore.","\"I am who I am and I’m not afraid to show it,\" Liu Lang said nonchalantly. \"What’s there to fear?\"","In truth, his reason for not hiding his identity was quite simple.","’In his view, with him and Boss Chen here to stir up trouble, this deal was bound to fail.’","’Besides, with Boss Chen around afterward, he wouldn’t have to worry about being hunted down by the Xiao Family.’","’Hiding his identity was completely unnecessary.’","’After all, if Black Tooth and the others found out that he and Boss Chen had secretly sabotaged the deal, he wouldn’t be able to escape the Bright Moon Building’s hunters even if he did hide.’","’He just hoped Boss Chen could be a bit more subtle about it.’","’Being hunted by the Bright Moon Building was no laughing matter.’","Chen Yi, of course, was unaware of Liu Lang’s devil-may-care reasoning, but he couldn’t help feeling a measure of admiration.","It was the kind of admiration one felt for a man of the Jianghu who kept his word and was open and honorable.","’Perhaps if an opportunity arose in the future, he would have to give Liu Lang some kind of reward.’","’He wouldn’t let Liu Lang’s help go unrewarded.’","「Not long after.」","After putting on their masks, Chen Yi and Liu Lang were led by a man in black into the depths of the Spring Rain Building.","Judging by his sense of direction, they were in a hidden space between the inner walls of the Spring Rain Building.","He had no idea what method Black Tooth and the others had used to construct such a spacious private room that was completely invisible from the outside.","When he arrived, several people wearing black iron masks were already seated inside.","They were of all shapes and sizes, both men and women.","Most of them were sizing up Chen Yi and Liu Lang, though their gazes ultimately lingered longer on Chen Yi.","After all, with the long blade hanging at his waist, Liu Lang was all too easy to recognize.","Chen Yi, of course, was sizing them up in return. He could make a reasonable guess as to which ones were Elder Demon Fang, Lady Tiger, and Black Tooth.","But after a sweeping glance, his expression remained unchanged, though inwardly he began to laugh.","’Well, well. An unexpected acquaintance.’"]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183 - 171: A Disorderly Mob","paragraphs":["That acquaintance was none other than Ge the Third, a Personal Guard from the Xiao Mansion.","He was currently sitting ramrod straight beside Lady Tiger Lou Yuxue, but his attire was far more concealing than anyone else’s.","He wore not only the black iron mask but also a hooded robe.","But under Chen Yi’s Qi Observation Skill, such a disguise was useless.","Never mind Ge the Third’s build, bearing, and the occasional small mannerisms he let slip.","The very signature of the Five Elements and Six Qi within his body was enough to confirm his identity.","Besides Ge the Third, Black Tooth, Lady Tiger, and Elder Demon Fang, there were fourteen other Jianghu People present. They were dressed in various styles, their auras ranging from strong to weak, but all were Middle Third-Grade Martial Artists.","One of them, a slender Evil Demon carrying a long zither on his back, must be Elder Demon Jia of the Illusory Sound Sect, with whom he’d had a brief encounter before.","Chen Yi silently committed their auras to memory, his gaze shifting to Black Tooth and Lady Tiger at the head of the room.","He was just about to ask when they would begin.","Just then, the midnight hour arrived—","[Daily Intelligence - Earth Rank Middle Grade: Fifteen minutes past midnight, Yanhua Lane. Many from the Evil Demonic Dao are gathered in the Bright Moon Building to discuss important matters. A small Opportunity can be obtained.]","’Oh?’","Chen Yi’s eyes brightened slightly after reading it, and he remained seated quietly at the table, his expression unchanging.","’At least this trip wasn’t a waste.’","After everyone had sized each other up,","Black Tooth knocked on the table before him, his voice a notch colder and more gravelly than usual.","\"Since you’re all here, you should all be clear on the objective of this deal. Since no one has backed out, I’ll assume you’ve all agreed to participate.\"","\"If anyone has second thoughts or lets word slip, the Bright Moon Building will deal with them according to our rules.\"","Black Tooth paused. When no one spoke, he narrowed his eyes and continued,","\"Let’s cut the crap. If you have any questions or demands about this deal, now’s the time to speak up.\"","At that moment, a tall man in the corner deliberately lowered his voice.","\"How is the pay being split?\"","Black Tooth nodded at him. \"The Bright Moon Building will take a thirty-percent cut. The rest will be divided into two portions.\"","\"One for the inside man, and the other to be split evenly among the rest of you.\"","The words had barely left his mouth when Elder Demon Fang snorted. \"Black Tooth, an even split doesn’t seem right, does it?\"","Seemingly unsurprised, Black Tooth glanced at him. \"And how do you think it should be split, Elder Fang?\"","\"Naturally, the strongest should get the biggest share.\"","Elder Demon Jia, sitting off to the side, chuckled.","\"Some people might look like they have profound cultivation, but they’re all flash and no substance. All bark and no bite. They really shouldn’t get that much.\"","The crowd burst into laughter, their gazes drifting, intentionally or not, toward Elder Demon Fang.","They all clearly remembered what Liu Lang had said earlier.","Elder Demon Fang’s eyes turned instantly glacial, his aura flaring. \"You want to spar, Jia Qing?\"","Elder Demon Jia sneered. \"I have no problem with that.\"","Seeing their auras begin to clash, Black Tooth tapped the table. An even colder, more tyrannical presence instantly enveloped the room.","Chen Yi felt the pressure descend upon him and his heart lurched.","’This Black Tooth is even stronger than Elder Demon Fang. I’d guess his cultivation is in the Upper Three Grades, and his Technique has reached the Great Success Realm.’","Once everyone had quieted down, Black Tooth snorted. \"A fight is unnecessary. It would only cause bad blood.\"","\"There’s a lot of money in this deal. On top of that, a valued client has added another ten thousand taels of silver. Even with an even split, you’ll all make a killing.\"","The group exchanged glances and broke into smiles.","\"Another ten thousand taels? Hah, fantastic news.\"","\"That means we’ll each get at least five thousand taels of silver. Not bad, not bad at all.\"","\"I agree to an even split.\"","\"Me too.\"","\"I got no objections. So much money, heh heh...\"","For a moment, the room descended into a chaotic cacophony, like a den of dancing demons.","Laughter, by turns shrill, loud, and deep, filled the air.","Chen Yi, however, frowned inwardly at the sight.","’Have all these gutter-dwelling Evil Demons gone blind with greed?’","’All they care about is silver coins. Not a single one is asking any relevant questions about the job itself?’","With that thought, Chen Yi tapped the table, his tone impatient.","\"Black Tooth, what’s your plan to pull this off?\"","\"Don’t tell me you’re planning to pull off this job with just this rabble.\"","Hearing this, the crowd of cackling Evil Demons all turned to face Chen Yi.","\"Rabble? You’ve got a lot of nerve!\"","\"How arrogant!\"","\"Even if you’ve got some skills, kid, you shouldn’t be so reckless!\"","\"You...\"","Seeing this, Liu Lang lightly tapped the scabbard of the long blade at his waist, then slid out a few inches of steel.","SHING.","The crisp sound was followed by a flash of light reflecting off the blade.","The crowd flinched. \"Sword Madman,\" one of them asked, his voice a mixture of anger and shame, \"what do you think you’re doing?\"","Nevertheless, their eyes held a clear note of apprehension.","The same was true for even Elder Demon Fang and Elder Demon Jia.","After all, a swordsman at the Fifth Grade Realm who had achieved Great Success in the Saber Dao was stronger than most people in the room.","Paired with Chen Yi, a Sixth Grade Realm practitioner with a Great Success Fist Dao, the two of them could inflict significant casualties even if they couldn’t win.","Liu Lang scanned the room, tilted his head back slightly, and scoffed. \"A bunch of brainless fools. Just shut up and listen.\"","\"It’s not like we get your share of the silver if the job succeeds, is it?\"","He wasn’t one for thinking things through, but he knew that with Chen Yi here, all he had to do was listen.","\"Well...\"","The dozen or so men exchanged glances, then all turned their gazes to Black Tooth.","Chen Yi paid them no mind, his gaze also fixed on Black Tooth as he continued,","\"Don’t blame me for being blunt, but frankly, with these people, I see no chance of success.\"","\"Elder Demon Fang? Are you expecting him to take on an army by himself?\"","No matter how low the cultivation of the Garrison Soldiers of the Three Towns, even an Upper Three Grades master would die if surrounded.","’Let alone the rest of these clowns.’","Hearing this, Black Tooth scanned the room and looked at Chen Yi. \"What Brother Liu says is precisely the key to this deal.\"","At this point, Lou Yuxue, who was sitting beside him, chimed in. \"Perhaps you’ll allow me to explain to our esteemed heroes?\"","Black Tooth’s eyes focused. After a moment’s silence, he gave a slight nod. \"Fine.\"","Lou Yuxue covered her mouth with her hand, letting out two delicate laughs. \"Since my dear brother from the Liu Family has asked, this little lady can’t very well keep things to herself.\"","\"Your task in this deal is simple—attract the Xiao Family’s attention. Create a diversion. Lure the tiger from the mountain, so to speak.\"","\"As for the specifics, Black Tooth and I have our own plans.\"","\"Everything else... will be handled by the Bright Moon Building’s informant inside the Three Towns.\"","After hearing her explanation, Chen Yi understood.","’I knew it,’ he thought. ’With their level of strength, these Evil Demons could never pose a real threat to the Garrison Soldiers of the Three Towns.’","’So they’re all just cannon fodder, meant to draw fire on the periphery.’","’The real work—burning the Three Towns’ summer grain—will be done by the Hidden Guard members under Ge the Third’s control.’","As he was mulling this over, Lou Yuxue looked at him. \"Does my dear brother from the Liu Family have any other questions?\"","Chen Yi met her gaze. \"What are the odds of success?\"","\"You wouldn’t believe me if I said it was a sure thing, my dear brother, but I’d say we have a sixty to seventy percent chance.\"","\"When do we move? The exact date?\"","\"Undecided.\"","\"And what is our part in this?\"","\"Undecided.\"","Chen Yi looked at Lou Yuxue, a faint smile playing in her eyes. Realizing he wouldn’t get any more details out of her, he fell silent.","Seeing this, Black Tooth scanned the room and was the first to rise.","\"If there are no more questions, that’s all for today. You may all go.\"","Soon, several men in black entered and led the group back to the waiting room they had arrived in.","Chen Yi glanced around and stopped Liu Lang, who was about to leave, signaling for him to wait.","Liu Lang nodded, took off his black iron mask, and leaned back in his chair with a stretch.","\"I can’t believe we’re just playing a supporting role. This is easy money.\"","\"Five thousand taels of silver, tsk tsk. That’s enough for me to live like a king in Yanhua Lane.\"","Chen Yi shot him a look. \"If you really want to live like a king, five thousand taels won’t be nearly enough,\" he said flatly.","\"You’d be better off using it to buy your favorite girl’s freedom. At least that might give you a taste of the warmth of a ’home’.\"","\"...I was just exaggerating.\"","They sat in silence for a moment.","Then, Chen Yi rose and walked outside.","Liu Lang followed, grumbling to himself.","’Leaving this late? Aren’t we just giving those petty old bastards a chance to ambush us?’","He’d been navigating the black market for years.","He prided himself on having a good read on these Evil Demon scumbags.","Their high-profile display in the meeting room was more than enough to attract the covetous attention of a few members of the Evil Demonic Dao.","Or, to be more precise, their killing intent.","Once they were long gone and the area around the room fell silent...","A side wall slid open, and Black Tooth and Lou Yuxue stepped in silently, observing the empty room.","They were silent for a moment.","\"The man from the Liu Family will be an asset to this operation.\"","\"Oh, you think so, Brother Black Tooth?\"","\"Don’t you?\"","\"But this little lady feels they’re more likely to cause trouble~\"","Black Tooth’s eyes twitched. \"You think they’ll ruin the plan?\"","Lou Yuxue gazed in the direction Chen Yi and Liu Lang had departed. \"A Medical Saint Hand with a limitless future,\" she said slowly.","\"If you were in charge, Brother Black Tooth, would you be willing to let someone like that risk his neck coming here?\"","Black Tooth considered this for a moment before speaking slowly. \"I would not.\"","\"I’ll send someone to confirm the Liu Family’s objective for this mission.\"","\"We certainly should. We can’t let ourselves be fooled and make the Bright Moon Building a laughingstock.\"","She paused, then added, \"Then again, judging by his bearing earlier, he certainly acts like he comes from a major family.\"","\"He’s completely different from mud-caked Jianghu riffraff like Elder Demon Fang and Elder Demon Jia.\"","Black Tooth grunted in agreement, his gaze growing sharp. \"He’d better not be here to ruin this deal. Otherwise... Hmph!\"","Lou Yuxue knew exactly what he meant and let out a delicate laugh, covering her mouth with her hand.","\"This little lady has no taste for fighting and killing. I only care about when we’re going to make our move, and when that silver will finally be in our hands.\"","Black Tooth glanced at her, meeting her faintly seductive eyes, then turned and left the room.","\"You decide when we strike. It’s best to do it before the Mid-Autumn Festival, lest we alert Xiao Jinghong.\"","\"As for the silver... within three days. If it’s not delivered, I’ll go collect it myself.\"","\"With that, this little lady knows just what to do~\"","Lou Yuxue watched him leave, a crystalline glint in her eyes that seemed to take the shape of a gold bank note.","Then she, too, followed after him, her steps light and breezy.","...","It was late at night, and a storm was raging.","The wind howled through the night, whipping the torrential rain into a frenzy as it SPLASHED down on Shu State City.","Chen Yi and Liu Lang, wearing bamboo hats, made their way back through the streets and alleys.","But what Liu Lang couldn’t figure out was why Chen Yi was walking at such an unhurried pace, as if he wanted to get soaked.","After they passed through another alley, he couldn’t hold back any longer. \"Hey, boss...\"","Before he could finish, Chen Yi stopped in his tracks and raised a hand to cut him off.","\"You’ve followed us all this way. Come out.\"","Liu Lang froze for a second, but his hand reacted instantly, landing on the hilt of his blade as he spun around.","Though he was puzzled, having noticed nothing himself, he saw Chen Yi’s certain expression and chose to trust him.","A moment later, sure enough, a tall, black-clad figure appeared silently at the far end of the alley.","The newcomer tilted up his bamboo hat slightly, his sinister eyes locking onto the two of them as he spoke in a cold, harsh voice.","\"I don’t give a damn about any deal. Anyone who offends me dies!\"","Liu Lang raised an eyebrow. \"Elder Demon Fang?\"","At that, Chen Yi glanced over his shoulder. \"Idiot.\""]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184 - 172: This Handwriting is Damn Ugly","paragraphs":["In fact, back at the Spring Rain Building, Chen Yi had planned to wait for his reward before leaving.","But when everyone else left and he still hadn’t received the Opportunity reward, he knew that either Black Tooth or the Lady Tiger was watching him and Liu Lang.","The same was true after they left the Spring Rain Building.","He appeared to walk at an unhurried pace, but in reality, he was constantly on guard against his surroundings.","At the same time, he had secretly been at work, sprinkling Immortal Drunk and Qingfeng Drunk along their path.","But when they reached Black Tooth’s territory without any sign of movement, how could he not have guessed his pursuers’ intentions?","After weighing his options, he decided to deal with the tail right here.","It was the only way to keep his and Liu Lang’s location from being exposed.","Elder Demon Fang was naturally unaware of his thoughts, but he heard his curses, and his eyes grew even colder.","\"You’ve humiliated me three times now. Do you really think you can defeat me with just your Great Success Saber Dao and Fist Dao?\"","As he spoke, he slowly closed in. \"I’ve roamed the Jianghu for decades, and I’ve never seen scum so eager to be reincarnated.\"","Seeing this, Liu Lang placed his hand on his blade’s hilt and drew it two inches, revealing a glint of cold light.","\"If victory were decided by Cultivation level alone, wouldn’t soldiers just surrender whenever they faced an enemy general?\"","\"To put it simply, Elder Demon Fang, even if your Cultivation is higher, your Technique is unrefined. You’re still a far cry from a true top-tier expert.\"","\"In a life-or-death battle, why would I fear your clumsy Fist and Foot skills?\"","As his voice fell, his Sword Intent took shape.","Like a silvery-white thread, it shot across twenty feet to land right in front of Elder Demon Fang.","Fierce, domineering, and utterly sharp.","Elder Demon Fang also felt that sharp Sword Intent, but he didn’t dodge. He simply protected his body with True Essence Gang Qi.","His robes instantly billowed and surged.","SHIING—","A sound like a blade striking an iron shield rang out. Through the veil of rain, sparks seemed to fly from Elder Demon Fang’s body.","Elder Demon Fang blocked the Sword Intent, but the impact forced him back a step.","Even so, he had blocked it.","Elder Demon Fang stared at the two, a savage sneer twitching at the corner of his eye. \"Sword Madman? Heh. Your blade isn’t mad enough, nor is it sharp enough!\"","The moment he finished speaking, he stomped forward, his True Essence Gang Qi solidifying into claws around his hands.","He then flicked his hands, sending two Eagle Claw strikes flying out.","A heavy pressure, infused with Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi and a hint of Fist Intent, repelled the driving rain from the claw-shaped Gang Qi.","In the blink of an eye, it pierced the curtain of rain and arrived before Liu Lang and Chen Yi.","Seeing Liu Lang about to draw his blade to meet the attack head-on, Chen Yi uttered a single word, \"Dodge.\"","The two dodged to the left and right.","Immediately, two deafening roars erupted behind them.","Chen Yi glanced to the side and saw that the house at the end of the alley had completely collapsed, while two millstone-sized claw marks were gouged into a nearby wall.","It was a clear testament to the power of Elder Demon Fang’s move.","Liu Lang also realized that even if they teamed up, they were no match for Elder Demon Fang. The gap in their Cultivation was just too large.","Even though Elder Demon Fang’s Fist Intent was unrefined, at only Minor Success, his Upper Three Grades Cultivation was enough. His protective Gang Qi alone could block their Great Success Dao Realms, putting him in an inherently invincible position.","Keeping his eyes on Elder Demon Fang, Liu Lang turned sideways, drew the long blade from his waist, and gestured to Chen Yi. \"Boss?\"","Chen Yi’s gaze swept over the long blade. Seeing that the blade’s body was only a palm’s length and utterly useless for fighting, he asked, half amused and half exasperated:","\"It’s been a few days. You never thought about getting a new blade?\"","\"Haven’t found one that feels right.\"","\"So, do we run or fight?\"","Chen Yi shook his head and told him there was no rush. Then, he looked at the charging Elder Demon Fang and called out:","\"Black Tooth, if you don’t come out now, you can come collect his corpse.\"","Liu Lang froze, a strange feeling rising in his heart.","’It’s good that the boss is confident, but how are the two of us supposed to kill Elder Demon Fang?’","Hearing this, Elder Demon Fang flew into a greater rage. \"Brat, you’re courting death!\"","He immediately pushed off the ground, spread his arms to the sides, and dove toward them like a falcon.","Just then, an icy voice rang out. \"Stop.\"","\"Black Tooth, this is a grudge between them and me! Even if you’re an Elder of the Bright Moon Building, this is none of your business!\"","Seeing that Elder Demon Fang had no intention of stopping, Black Tooth appeared before Chen Yi and Liu Lang like a phantom.","Then, he flicked a finger at Elder Demon Fang.","Instantly, with a rustle like a light breeze through willow branches, Elder Demon Fang’s forward momentum halted, and he was sent flying backward.","He didn’t manage to stop himself until he was back at the alley’s entrance, bracing himself on his hands and feet.","He raised his head and glared furiously at Black Tooth. \"You?!\"","Black Tooth, still wearing his mask, looked at him coldly. \"What?\"","Elder Demon Fang looked at him, then at Chen Yi and Liu Lang behind him, and gritted his teeth.","\"...Black Tooth, today, I’ll spare them out of respect for you.\"","\"But this doesn’t mean I’ll let them off in the future. This isn’t over!\"","With that, Elder Demon Fang turned to leave.","But before he could take three steps, his vision suddenly went black, and his limbs grew weak and numb, forcing him to lean against a wall for support.","\"What’s happening to me...\"","Elder Demon Fang shook his head, but he couldn’t stay conscious any longer and collapsed to the ground.","SPLASH.","\"Hm?\"","Black Tooth froze at the sight, then immediately understood. He turned his head to look at Chen Yi behind him, an inscrutable light flickering in his eyes.","\"Brother Liu, what a fine move.\"","Chen Yi met his gaze, glanced at Elder Demon Fang out of the corner of his eye, and said with feigned displeasure:","\"This is the man you found?\"","\"With a mind like that, forget about accomplishing anything great. I’d say he even lacks the ability to provide support from the outside.\"","\"If not for the respect I have for your Bright Moon Building, he would already be a corpse.\"","Black Tooth was silent.","After a moment, he finally sighed. \"My apologies, Brother Liu. I will be sure to give you a satisfactory explanation for this matter.\"","\"That would be best.\"","\"Otherwise, how can we conspire to achieve great things if some fool without eyes keeps jumping out?\"","\"Brother Liu is right.\"","After a few more pleasantries, Chen Yi chuckled as he watched Elder Demon Fang struggling to get up in the distance.","\"I’ll leave *them* to you.\"","With that, he and Liu Lang headed straight for the West Market.","Black Tooth watched them walk away and stood silently for a moment before turning to look at Elder Demon Fang.","\"’Them?’\"","’There are others?’","「Not long after.」","When Black Tooth reached Elder Demon Fang’s side and glanced at the scene in Yanhua Lane, he suddenly started laughing.","His laughter was a mixture of astonishment, pleasant surprise, and a trace of confusion.","From the Spring Rain Building to where he stood, a distance of just a few hundred feet, more than a dozen men in black lay scattered about.","Among them were his own men from the Bright Moon Building, as well as some Jianghu People who had come for the deal.","Even the petite Lou Yuxue seemed to have fallen for it. She was leaning against a corner wall, her head tilted up at the sky, using the cold rain to force herself to stay awake.","As he laughed, Black Tooth’s eyes swept over Elder Demon Fang, who had managed to get back on his feet, and a cold glint flashed in his eyes.","\"I can tolerate your lack of strength and your simple mind. I can even overlook your impulsiveness.\"","\"But you should never, ever have brought such disgrace upon the Bright Moon Building.\"","Hearing this, Elder Demon Fang looked at him dazedly. \"What?\"","Before he could figure it out, he saw a black shadow flash before his eyes, and the world began to spin.","THWACK.","RUMBLE RUMBLE.","Elder Demon Fang’s head flew through the air, hit the wall, then bounced to the ground and rolled a few times. His eyes suddenly widened, staring blankly at Black Tooth.","\"You, you...\"","\"Hmph!\"","As if too lazy to waste any more words on him, Black Tooth flicked out a finger.","BANG.","A spray of red and white exploded in the rain.","Black Tooth spared it a glance before heading toward the Spring Rain Building.","As he passed by Lou Yuxue, he spoke coldly, \"Clean this up.\"","Before his voice had even faded, his figure had already vanished into the curtain of rain.","「A good while later.」","Lou Yuxue shook her head. When she came to her senses and saw the figures lying all over the ground, a flash of anger crossed her eyes.","\"Liu Wu!\"","...","Chen Yi led Liu Lang on a long, deliberate detour. Soon, a screen of light appeared before his eyes—","[Witnessed the Bright Moon Building gathering a host of Evil Demons to discuss a major affair. Reward: Mountain Shattering Fist tier upgraded to Earth Tier, Opportunity +100.]","[Evaluation: You arrived, you heard, you saw the scene. As an infiltrator, you participated in the Bright Moon Building’s major affair, gaining the trust of the Bright Moon Building and the Hidden Guard. You engineered the murder of Fang Zhengtai. You intimidated a host of Evil Demons. Performance: Satisfactory.]","Only after the Profound Mysteries of the Earth Tier Mountain Shattering Fist Technique flooded his mind did Chen Yi let out a long breath and signal for Liu Lang to return to their lodging.","「Not long after.」","The two entered their courtyard and woke up Zhang Dabao to fetch them some towels.","Chen Yi wiped the rain from his body and handed the towel to Liu Lang.","Liu Lang took it and began to dry his long hair, asking in confusion:","\"Boss, when did you use the sedative? Even I didn’t notice a thing.\"","\"If even you could detect it, how would Elder Demon Fang, who is so much stronger than you, have fallen for it?\"","\"...Give me a good blade, and I’ll chop him to death!\"","At his words, a thought stirred in Chen Yi’s mind. He smiled and said, \"In a couple of days, I’ll find a good blade for you.\"","\"How good?\"","\"It’s a treasure from the Xiao Family’s vault. What do you think?\"","Hearing this, Liu Lang grinned. \"I knew you had a deep connection with the Xiao Family, Boss. The cat’s out of the bag now, huh?\"","’The cat’s out of the bag?’","Chen Yi shook his head inwardly.","He had simply been observing Liu Lang’s recent performance and had come to trust him a little.","Besides, he now understood the situation with Black Tooth and had a clearer idea of his subsequent plans.","So, there were some things he no longer intended to hide from Liu Lang.","They chatted for a bit.","After drying himself off, Liu Lang thought for a moment and asked, \"There’s one more thing I don’t understand.\"","\"Since we had the chance just now, why did you call Black Tooth over? Wouldn’t killing Elder Demon Fang ourselves have solved the problem once and for all?\"","Chen Yi leaned back in his chair, mulling over his next steps as he replied:","\"It was unnecessary, and it would have caused more trouble.\"","\"Our goal this time is just to participate in that deal, not to get into a pissing contest with those Evil Demons.\"","\"If we had killed Elder Demon Fang ourselves, it would have only made Black Tooth suspicious, which would have been bad for us.\"","After a pause, Chen Yi looked out the window, a smile playing on his lips. \"But I don’t think Elder Demon Fang will meet a good end anyway.\"","Liu Lang shook his head and sighed. \"I really don’t know how your brain works.\"","Once again, he felt that people who used their heads were too much trouble. A straightforward, life-or-death fight was much more satisfying.","Chen Yi just smiled, not bothering with his thoughts.","’If I were strong enough right now, I wouldn’t need to use my brain. I would’ve just gone to the Spring Rain Building and slaughtered them all.’","After a moment of thought, Chen Yi spoke up. \"Next, there are two things I need you to do.\"","Liu Lang raised an eyebrow. \"Is this in exchange for that good blade? Or does it count toward the thirty tasks I promised you?\"","\"Up to you.\"","Chen Yi said nonchalantly, continuing, \"First, tomorrow, I need you to find out where the people from the Jing State Liu Family are staying. You and I will need to meet with that Second Young Master Liu later.\"","\"Meet them? Why?\"","\"With a brain like yours, do you think it would do any good if I told you?\"","\"...You’re the boss. Whatever you say.\"","Chen Yi ignored the resentful look in his eyes and continued with his instructions. \"I remember you said before that you wanted to thank Xiao Jinghong for sparing your life?\"","\"Now’s your chance.\"","\"I need to write a letter to her in your name.\"","This time, Liu Lang understood and said cheerfully, \"You want to leak this matter to General Jinghong?\"","Chen Yi nodded and asked him to get a brush and paper and write a few characters.","Although Liu Lang was confused, remembering how he had just been mocked, he obediently took the brush and wrote a few characters.","The strokes were all there—horizontals, verticals, slants, and hooks—but they looked as if they were about to fall apart.","Seemingly sensing Chen Yi’s gaze, Liu Lang scratched his head and said with some embarrassment:","\"My master never let me study or write...\"","Chen Yi shook his head, chalking it up to the obsessive-compulsive tendencies that came with his Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao.","Then, suppressing the intense, visceral revulsion, he forced himself to start writing in Liu Lang’s handwriting.","[For General Jinghong’s eyes only:","Black Tooth of the Bright Moon Building has gathered a host of the Evil Demonic Dao. They intend to burn the summer grain supply of the Three Towns. I urge you to prepare in advance.","Additionally, the ones carrying out the act may be inside men from the Three Towns’ garrison.","—The Sword Madman.]","After finishing, Chen Yi read it over, an expression of disgust appearing on his face.","\"This handwriting is so f***ing ugly.\"","Liu Lang: \"...\""]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185 - 173: Brother-in-law, Just You Watch","paragraphs":["The letter was finished.","Chen Yi folded the letter. He made some small talk with Liu Lang, all the while contemplating what to do next.","’It’ll be impossible to get this letter to Xiao Jinghong through normal channels. Aside from myself, everyone else—Liu Lang, Lady Tiger, and the other Evil Demons—is definitely being watched by Black Tooth. And trying to send it from the Xiao Family carries the risk of premature exposure. I’d just be tipping them off.’","As he mulled it over, an image of a figure surfaced in his mind, and he could almost hear a faint, tinkling sound.","’Looks like having Tiger Girl return to her clan for a family visit is the most reliable plan.’","\"Black Tooth and their people will be on high alert these days,\" Chen Yi said. \"They’ll be watching you, me, and everyone else who knows what’s going on. Be careful.\"","Liu Lang glanced at the letter in Chen Yi’s hand. \"Don’t you need me to deliver it?\" he asked.","Chen Yi retorted, \"If I could send you, why would I have bothered writing this letter in the first place?\"","Liu Lang smiled sheepishly. \"I forgot.\"","\"I was just thinking that delivering the letter to General Jinghong would be a good chance to ask her for a few pointers.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi shook his head to himself. ’These Jianghu types are all the same—they don’t sweat the small stuff, always acting too direct and blunt. They don’t realize that details are what determine success or failure. Failing to handle one seemingly insignificant detail can lead to disaster.’","\"Anyway, when you’re looking for Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue tomorrow, make sure you aren’t spotted.\"","Liu Lang nodded, committing the warning to memory.","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi sent Liu Lang on his way.","He watched Liu Lang depart, then his gaze drifted to the gloomy rain outside. He sat in silence for a while.","Then, he called Zhang Dabao over to remove his disguise.","While Zhang Dabao worked, Chen Yi took the opportunity to calm his mind.","As he relaxed, he couldn’t help but ask a few things about the Disguise Skill.","Zhang Dabao held nothing back, explaining the basics of the Disguise Skill in detail.","\"My master said his Disguise Skill comes from the Thief Sect. It’s divided into three aspects: Face, Form, and Spirit.\"","\"The simplest is altering the face. You can do that easily with a skin mask and a few finely crafted bone fragments.\"","\"Next is Form. Legend says that a Thief Sect master from a past dynasty could shrink and expand his bones, changing his height, build, and even his gender.\"","\"The hardest is the Spirit. My master says that while you can fake the exterior, the inner essence is extremely difficult to change.\"","Zhang Dabao explained as he peeled off the mask.","Chen Yi listened intently. He smiled and asked, \"So to completely transform one person into another, you need all three—Face, Form, and Spirit—right?\"","Zhang Dabao froze for a second, giving him an odd look. \"My lord, are you thinking about finding a body double?\"","\"Just curious. I have no such intention.\"","’A body double would be like a shadow, making things more convenient for me,’ Chen Yi thought, ’but a double is still a person. And people have their own thoughts and selfish desires.’","Chen Yi had no desire to create that kind of trouble for himself.","He was only asking out of \"academic\" curiosity.","Zhang Dabao didn’t suspect a thing. He nodded and said, \"That’s what my master said. I’ve only scratched the surface.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"I keep hearing you mention your master. Where is he now?\"","\"He’s off living as a wandering hermit.\"","\"Before he left, he declared my apprenticeship complete and told me not to tarnish the Thief Sect’s name. A pity...\"","Seeing the look of regret on Zhang Dabao’s face, Chen Yi let out a soft laugh. \"A pity you ended up following Wang Ji, is that it?\"","\"A little... Forgive me, my lord.\"","\"It’s just that I’ve spent years honing my craft, but now I only use the Disguise Skill. I can’t help but feel my other abilities are going to waste.\"","Chen Yi nodded in understanding. ’He feels like his talents have no place to shine. Then again, it makes sense. Zhang Dabao might seem mature and steady, but he’s still a young man of seventeen or eighteen. It’s only natural for him to yearn for fame and fortune.’","\"For now, learn what you can from Wang Ji. You’ll get your chance to shine eventually. Then the name ’Two Fingers’ will be known throughout all of Shu State.\"","\"Heh heh, thank you, my lord.\"","A short while later, Chen Yi was back to his usual appearance and had changed his clothes.","After a moment’s thought, he gave an instruction:","\"Tomorrow, go to Wang Ji and have him acquire a residence in the East Market and another in North City. We can’t stay here for the time being.\"","Zhang Dabao smiled and agreed. He saw Chen Yi off, then turned and went back to his room to rest.","Young men like him rarely had complicated thoughts. The moment he hit the bed, he was asleep.","A smile played on his lips as he slept, and he mumbled something about \"Two Fingers.\"","All in all, he was having a good dream.","Adults like Chen Yi, however, had far more complicated minds.","Especially while walking through the quiet, dim, rainy night, he had to be constantly vigilant.","Even though he had sorted out his plans, his mind was inevitably pulled in several different directions, like threads of silk.","One thread was focused on his immediate surroundings, to avoid being detected by the Imprisonment Department, the Hidden Guard, or the Bright Moon Building.","Another was tangled with concern for those close to him.","He wondered what Xiao Jinghong and Xiao Wan’er would think if they ever found out what he was doing.","And a third thread was a jumble of his own miscellaneous thoughts.","Thoughts like the \"A Little Cold Plum\" lure he used for fishing; how he had yet to master the Zither and Painting to complete his skills in Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting; and how he needed to restock his supply of Sedatives and Poisons.","With so much on his mind, he had to walk slowly and carefully through the rainy night, lest he step in a puddle or get soaked to the bone.","Nearly an hour later, Chen Yi arrived back at Spring Lotus Garden.","He washed up, changed his clothes, and drank a cup of hot tea.","As warmth spread through his body and mind, he finally let out a long sigh and relaxed.","Though he hadn’t been with the Xiao Family for long, his recent experiences and the time spent with those close to him had given this place the feeling of \"home.\"","Chen Yi glanced at the sky outside. After a moment’s thought, he took the letter and slipped quietly over to the wooden building next door.","To avoid being noticed, he didn’t knock. Instead, he pried the door open, slipped inside the wooden building, and headed straight for Pei Guanli’s room."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186 - 173: Brother-in-law, Just You Watch","paragraphs":["Arriving outside her door, he pressed his ear against it and heard Tiger Girl’s steady breathing.","After a moment’s hesitation, Chen Yi knocked on the door.","THUMP. THUMP, THUMP.","Although the muffled sound was masked by the patter of the rain, it was enough to jolt a martial artist awake.","\"Who is it?\"","\"It’s me.\"","\"Brother-in-law?\"","Not suspecting a thing, Pei Guanli scrambled out of bed and opened the door.","Perhaps because she had been startled awake, her round face still looked dazed and sleepy.","She didn’t even notice she was only wearing her undergarments, and the heavy bell she wore swayed with a soft tinkle.","Chen Yi glanced at her, then averted his gaze and coughed. \"Get dressed. I’ll wait for you in the living room.\"","With that, he turned and went downstairs.","After he was gone, Pei Guanli muttered, ’We could have just talked here.’","But as she rubbed her eyes and became more alert, she noticed the chill on her skin and glanced down.","She let out a yelp, followed by a frantic JINGLE-JANGLE.","Chen Yi found it amusing. He knew Tiger Girl was wild by nature and didn’t pay much mind to the proprieties between men and women.","He didn’t think she’d done it on purpose.","A short while later, Pei Guanli came timidly downstairs, her face beet red. She sat beside him with her head lowered. \"Brother-in-law.\"","Chen Yi looked at her and couldn’t help but smile. \"You’re a grown woman now. It’s time you got married.\"","\"I am not!\"","\"Not a grown woman, or not time to get married?\"","Forgetting her shyness, Pei Guanli wrinkled her nose. \"I don’t want to get married so early! Even Ah Ma isn’t rushing me.\"","Chen Yi didn’t press the issue. He smoothed her messy hair and said with a smile,","\"I have something urgent I need your help with.\"","Pei Guanli touched the stray hairs at her forehead, her pretty, round face blushing slightly. She blinked her big eyes and stared intently at him.","\"Brother-in-law, what is it?\"","Chen Yi took out the letter and handed it to her. \"I need you to get this letter to the Madam as soon as possible,\" he instructed.","\"For Sister Jinghong?\"","Pei Guanli took the letter and began to read, sounding out the words: \"Fire in the Three Towns... Sword Madman...\"","Despite the messy, crooked handwriting, she managed to understand its meaning. A look of excitement instantly appeared on her face.","\"Brother-in-law, is something fun happening again?\"","’Fun?’","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"You could say that.\"","\"But when you go, you must act as if you found this letter by chance. Don’t let on that you knew about it beforehand.\"","\"So I need to keep your secret from Sister Jinghong again, right?\"","\"Yes. She can’t know for the time being, so you’ll need to find a good excuse to go back.\"","Pei Guanli nodded repeatedly, grinning. \"I get it, I get it! I’m going back to visit Ah Ma, right?\"","\"Exactly. The Madam will get suspicious if you’re too obvious about it.\"","Chen Yi wasn’t sure if Tiger Girl truly understood or was just pretending, but he had no better person for the job. He could only meticulously explain every last detail.","Pei Guanli took note of everything and began to rehearse her role convincingly.","\"First, I’ll do this, and then this... and then I’ll ’accidentally’ let the letter fall out for Sister Jinghong...\"","\"Right, I have to say I’m going back to the clan to visit Ah Ma and my brothers. The excuse... the Mid-Autumn Festival?\"","\"Brother-in-law, that’ll definitely work, right?\"","After running through it a couple of times, Pei Guanli had the whole process figured out.","\"Okay, I’ll set off now.\"","\"Don’t be in such a rush. Wait until dawn, then tell your eldest sister and have her prepare a horse for you before you leave.\"","\"Okay, okay! Don’t worry, Brother-in-law. A little thing like this is no problem for me.\"","Seeing how confident Pei Guanli was, Chen Yi didn’t hold back his praise.","\"It’s a good thing you never took up opera. You’d be the star of the show by now.\"","Pei Guanli giggled, her two canine teeth peeking out. She was clearly enjoying the praise.","\"I think so too...\"","After giving her a few more instructions, Chen Yi told her to hide the letter well, then got up and left.","Pei Guanli closed her door, looked left and right, then furtively pulled the letter from her robes like a thief, unable to suppress a mischievous chuckle.","’Just you watch, Brother-in-law.’","’I guarantee Sister Jinghong won’t suspect a thing.’","After muttering to herself for a moment, Pei Guanli tucked the letter under the string of bells she wore, patting it as if it were a treasure.","JINGLE, JINGLE...","In his study, Chen Yi heard the faint jingling from the next room and shook his head with a smile.","’Whether this succeeds or not is all up to you, Pei Guanli.’","...","「In the pre-dawn hours, the rain began to subside.」","Sun Fu, dressed neatly for travel, arrived at the Qingjing Residence holding a brocade box. Inside was the calligraphy scroll titled \"Farewell to Duke Changming in Shu State.\"","He was set to depart for Jinling today, and before leaving, he wanted to have a word with Marquis Xiao.","In fact, he had already informed Marquis Xiao of his plans a few days prior.","It was just that, back then, he hadn’t yet obtained the treasured scroll and lacked confidence in his upcoming trip to Jinling.","He certainly wasn’t as full of vigor as he was now.","Even Elder Master Xiao, who was in the middle of washing up and dressing, was surprised when he saw him.","He looked Sun Fu up and down.","The Elder Master blurted out, \"Did you spend the night in Yanhua Lane?\"","Sun Fu nearly choked, so furious his beard bristled and his eyes went wide.","\"You old coot! Can’t anything good ever come out of that mouth of yours?\"","\"This is what they call ’glowing from a happy occasion’!\"","\"A happy occasion? I seem to recall you looking all doom and gloom just a couple of days ago, the very picture of desolation.\"","\"What happened? Is your daughter-in-law expecting?\"","\"I wish...\"","The two old-timers bickered for a bit out of habit.","Sun Fu knew the man was just being difficult and didn’t continue the banter. He placed the brocade box he was carrying onto the table and said,","\"Take a look. *This* is the ’happy occasion’.\"","\"And it’s not just for me, but for you too.\"","Marquis Xiao looked at him, slightly curious. \"You’re sure it’s a happy occasion?\"","\"Just make sure it’s not a ’fright’ instead of a pleasant surprise. I’m telling you, my health might be a bit better these days, but I can’t handle any sudden shocks.\"","Sun Fu ignored him, opening the brocade box and taking out the roll of Yunsong Paper.","He paused, his expression serious. \"Watch closely. Don’t blink.\"","Marquis Xiao eyed the paper in his hands dubiously and urged, \"Stop dithering. Hurry up and open it.\"","\"I’d like to see just what treasure has you acting so secretive.\"","Then, Sun Fu unfurled the roll of Yunsong Paper.","The moment the first character came into view, a fluorescent glow filled the dimly candlelit hall.","Faintly, a voice could be heard chanting, \"A thousand li... of yellow clouds... the bright sun dims...\"","At the same time, an illusory scene manifested on the paper: yellow sand blotted out the sky, obscuring the sun’s halo, while a lone figure stood below, gazing up into the distance.","Marquis Xiao’s expression immediately turned serious after just one glance.","He then watched as the scene on the paper shifted again. Wild geese flew south amidst a heavy, drifting snow. Then, another figure appeared, walking and smiling, with a crowd of people following behind.","...until the figure stood atop the walls of Jinling City, gazing into the distance.","Marquis Xiao saw the figure’s face clearly—it was none other than Sun Fu, Sun Changming!","Marquis Xiao was visibly moved. \"This... This is?\"","Before Sun Fu could explain, the Marquis’s eyes swept to the bottom-left corner of the paper. His cloudy eyes instantly cleared, shining with the same brilliant light they had when he led his troops into Poshisu Country.","\"Chen Yi, Chen Qingzhou. Late summer, the twenty-first year of Anhe.\"","Sun Fu smiled and nodded, seemingly satisfied with the Marquis’s stunned expression.","\"I told you it was a happy occasion for you as well. I wasn’t wrong, was I?\"","Marquis Xiao stared intently at the calligraphy scroll and the illusion it projected, only speaking after a long moment.","\"Heh... Indeed... it is a happy occasion.\"","Sun Fu studied the Marquis’s face as he carefully rolled up the scroll and returned it to the box.","\"You certainly don’t look like you’re celebrating a happy occasion.\"","\"What’s wrong? Your grandson-in-law has achieved Perfection in the Calligraphy Dao. He’s just one step away from becoming a contemporary Calligraphy Saint, and you’re not happy?\"","Marquis Xiao’s gaze drifted toward the Spring Lotus Garden as he sighed softly. \"I am happy, of course. It’s just...\"","\"The more brilliant Qingzhou’s talent becomes, the more... worried I feel.\"","Sun Fu burst out laughing. \"You old coot, are you worried Qingzhou has designs on your Xiao Family?\"","Marquis Xiao nodded hesitantly, his expression a little strained.","\"Changming, you should be aware of the Xiao Family’s current situation. If Qingzhou were to develop... other ideas, I’m afraid Jinghong wouldn’t be able to control him.\"","\"You’re worrying over nothing. Qingzhou is a fine young man.\"","\"Fine, I won’t hide it from you...\"","Sun Fu then recounted his conversation with Chen Yi from the previous day, concluding with,","\"Feeling better now?\"","\"Qingzhou has never had any such ideas.\"","\"Instead of worrying about him, you’d be better off keeping an eye on your family’s Second and Third Branches, not to mention Duke Qian’s household.\"","Marquis Xiao’s expression grew grim. \"Are you serious?\"","Clutching the brocade box, Sun Fu snorted. \"When have I ever deceived you?\"","Seeing him speak with such conviction, the Marquis’s expression softened.","He was silent for a long time.","He couldn’t help but sigh again. \"We have wronged Qingzhou.\"","\"It’s good that you realize that.\"","\"In the future, if he really does become a Calligraphy Saint with a world-renowned name, your Xiao Family may well have to rely on his favor.\"","\"That’s... not entirely impossible...\""]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187 - 174: Let’s Fight","paragraphs":["Maybe it was just his imagination, but when Chen Yi came to the front courtyard early in the morning to see Sun Fu off, he felt that Elder Master Xiao was giving him a very strange look.","It was the kind of look one would give a priceless treasure that was just out of reach.","He couldn’t help but wonder, ’Did the Elder Master find out that my Calligraphy Dao has reached Perfection?’","But even if he knew, he shouldn’t be looking at me like this.","’After all, I’m practically one of the Xiao family.’","Little did Chen Yi know that in Elder Master Xiao’s heart, it was only at this moment that he truly considered his grandson-in-law a part of the Xiao Family.","Before this, the Elder Master had simply had a good impression of Chen Yi, feeling that he was a worthy match for his granddaughter, Xiao Jinghong.","He never expected Chen Yi to make any contributions to the Xiao Family.","Even now, after learning that Chen Yi’s Calligraphy Dao had reached Perfection and going on a complex emotional journey, he still couldn’t bring himself to order Chen Yi to do things for the Xiao Family.","It was probably a matter of conscience.","After all, given the Xiao Family’s current circumstances, dragging anyone in was tantamount to asking them to put their lives on the line.","If not for the fact that Xiao Wan’er, Xiao Jinghong, and Xiao Wuge were bound by blood, the Elder Master would have wished for them to stay out of it as well.","Alas, that was impossible now.","Sun Fu watched the old man and his grandson-in-law, able to guess what was on their minds. After placing the brocade box in the carriage, he said with a smile:","\"Qingzhou, if you have free time in the future, you should visit the Qingjing Residence more often. Otherwise, this old fellow will have no one to talk to, and his condition might worsen.\"","Chen Yi was moved and was just about to nod in agreement when he heard the Elder Master retort with a laugh:","\"Since when do I need you to worry about me?\"","\"You should worry about yourself! Don’t get to Jinling only to find you can’t make a living to support your family.\"","Sun Fu wasn’t annoyed by this. He simply gave Chen Yi a slight nod and a meaningful look before firing back at the Elder Master with something along the lines of how he’d rather be a beggar than ask him for help.","Listening to the two elders bicker, Chen Yi just smiled.","He understood the meaning in Sun Fu’s eyes and guessed that Sun Fu must have said something to the Elder Master to cause such a change in him.","However...","Chen Yi could only refuse silently in his heart.","’Having tea and playing chess with the Elder Master is fine, but actively going over to find things to do for them...’","’Impossible.’","For one, he had no interest in becoming an official or joining the army.","For another, while it might not cause problems in the short term, it would inevitably arouse suspicion in the long run.","’And with those people from the Hidden Guard fanning the flames, heaven knows what would happen if I actually became an official or joined the army through the Xiao Family’s connections.’","’There’s no guarantee Ge the Third wouldn’t arrange some \"meritorious deeds\" for me just to get me promoted.’","’None of this is what I want.’","Not long after, Sun Fu bid farewell to each person who had come to see him off, sharing a few laughs before elegantly climbing into his carriage and announcing, \"Let’s depart.\"","The carriage started moving at his word.","Amidst the RUMBLE of the wheels and the CLOP-CLOP of the hooves, the carriage gradually blurred in the curtain of rain.","Faintly, an aged yet vigorous voice drifted back:","\"Don’t worry about having no friends on the road ahead; is there anyone under heaven who doesn’t know you? Haha...\"","Hearing Sun Fu’s laughter, Elder Master Xiao’s face broke into a smile as he grumbled good-naturedly:","\"That old coot got a great deal and now he’s showing off.\"","Chen Yi smiled but said nothing.","Beside him, Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge both seemed to have thought of something as their eyes fell on him.","\"Brother-in-law, did you write those lines for Grandpa Sun?\"","Chen Yi met their gazes and didn’t hide it, nodding as he said:","\"Elder Sun came to see me yesterday. I couldn’t very well let him leave empty-handed.\"","Before Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge could respond, the Elder Master put on a stern face and said:","\"Qingzhou, if shameless old fools like him come knocking in the future, just refuse them. I’ll back you up.\"","\"Especially Sun Fu and Zhang Xuan. Those two have been in the army for too long. They’re the most thick-skinned of all—nothing but army ruffians.\"","At his words, not just Chen Yi, but also Xiao Wan’er and the others couldn’t help but chuckle.","Laughing and talking, the group returned to their respective residences.","After passing through the central courtyard, Xiao Wan’er didn’t forget to remind him, \"Brother-in-law, please come back early today.\"","\"Boss Chen Yu from Hundred Herbs Hall is visiting this afternoon, and I’d like to have him stay for dinner.\"","Chen Yi smiled, nodded, and readily agreed.","Of course, he couldn’t be in two places at once. If Chen Yu was there, he himself certainly couldn’t be.","’Fortunately, whether I’m Chen Yu or Chen Yi, I’ll be able to get a bite or two of that dinner.’","Xiao Wan’er, naturally unaware of his thoughts, began giving instructions to Cui’er and Juan’er while also saying:","\"Just now, Guanli came by and said she’s returning to her clan. I’ve already had someone prepare a generous gift to be sent to the Mountain Race along with her.\"","\"I was thinking of writing another letter to Second Sister. You should write one too, and we’ll have it delivered at the same time.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi wanted to say that Xiao Jinghong hadn’t even replied to his last letter, so there was nothing more to write.","But after a moment’s thought, he kept it to himself and went straight to his study. With a flourish of his brush, he composed a short poem of a few dozen characters, titled \"Thoughts of Summer.\"","’However, I estimate that once Xiao Jinghong sees the letter mentioning the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain,\" she won’t be in any mood to appreciate this \"Thoughts of Summer\" poem.’","’So, it should be fine if I just dash something off, right?’","After tidying up the study, Chen Yi gave the letter to Xiao Wan’er and also secretly gave Pei Guanli a few instructions to make sure she didn’t slip up.","Tiger Girl’s eyes were full of laughter as she nodded vigorously at him, then she hopped onto her carriage and rode off.","Once she was gone, Chen Yi saw that it was getting late, so he said goodbye to Xiao Wan’er and headed to the academy.","In an instant, the Spring Lotus Garden became completely empty.","Even Xiaodie was with Xiao Wuge in the Jiaxing Garden, studying.","After arranging everything, Xiao Wan’er took out the letter Chen Yi had written.","She hesitated for a moment, then put it away again.","’It’s not right to read other people’s letters without permission.’","With that thought, Xiao Wan’er gazed out at the gloomy, rainy weather, her mind drifting off to who knows where.","「...」","The morning’s Calligraphy class passed quickly.","As usual, Chen Yi gave the one hundred students in the study hall an assignment.","\"Write a piece of Calligraphy, but this time, do it in the way that best suits your heart.\"","\"It doesn’t have to be perfectly neat, and you don’t have to follow Wei Qing’s Style, but you must put your heart into it.\"","Drawing on his general impression of the students, Chen Yi pointed to a handsome-looking boy sitting in the front row as an example.","\"Take Tang Ye, for example.\"","\"You have a lively nature and are always full of wild and creative ideas. You can apply that same divergent thinking to the Calligraphy Dao.\"","As he spoke, Chen Yi wrote the character for \"eternity\" on a sheet of Yunsong Paper.","His brushstrokes followed his heart.","The horizontal stroke slanted slightly upward, the vertical one leaned to the lower left. It looked crooked, yet it gave off an extremely comfortable feeling.","Fourteen-year-old Tang Ye stared at the character, then imitated it on his sand tray.","Judging by its form alone, it was already thirty to forty percent similar to the one Chen Yi had written.","Tang Ye stared blankly at the sand tray and asked, seemingly half-understanding, \"Sir, is... is this considered a new style of calligraphy?\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded. \"As I’ve said, Calligraphy is like Painting. Whatever the world looks like in your eyes, that is how you should write.\"","\"A so-called ’new style’ is nothing more than following your heart to write characters that best reflect your true intentions.\"","\"The reason those who came before you failed is simply that they weren’t skilled enough, or their understanding of the Calligraphy Dao was one-sided.\"","\"After all, not everyone can break free from the shackles of established rules.\"","Chen Yi put down his Wolf Hair Brush and said, \"Class dismissed.\"","After the students bowed, he returned the bow and walked out of the study hall.","Mr. Yue Ming, Mr. Zhuo Ying, and others were already waiting at the door.","Chen Yi greeted them and followed Mr. Yue Ming to the rear residence, paying no mind to who in the study hall collected those sheets of Yunsong Paper.","Once they were seated in the study of the rear residence,","Mr. Yue Ming handed him a cup of tea that had already been prepared. \"How did the students perform today?\"","Chen Yi took a sip of tea. Noticing the headmaster’s embarrassed expression out of the corner of his eye, he asked with a smile, \"Did someone pull some strings, and you couldn’t refuse them, Elder Sir?\"","Mr. Yue Ming knew he couldn’t hide it from him and nodded with a bitter smile.","\"Five years ago, when the Barbarian Race attacked, there was a food shortage throughout Shu State, and even our academy was affected.\"","\"At that time, a great clan generously offered their help, and I promised them that I would repay them handsomely in the future, so...\"","As he spoke, Mr. Yue Ming stood up and bowed. \"I hope Qingzhou will grant permission.\"","Chen Yi quickly stepped aside and said, exasperated, \"Headmaster, please don’t bow at the drop of a hat. I can’t bear such a gesture.\"","Mr. Yue Ming straightened up and looked at him. \"I truly couldn’t refuse. I had no other choice.\"","Chen Yi thought for a moment, then nodded. \"If that’s the reason, then I have no objection.\"","\"However, since you’re the one adding a person, you’ll have to remove one student as well.\"","\"This... can’t you make an exception?\"","\"Without rules, there can be no order. I hope you’ll understand, Headmaster.\"","Mr. Yue Ming’s expression turned bitter, but he didn’t press him further. \"Since it has come to this, I will go discuss it with Heming.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow. \"You really know how to pick them, Elder Sir.\"","But on second thought, Ma Guan was indeed the most suitable choice.","After all, his Calligraphy Dao was already well-developed.","Even if he didn’t study under Chen Yi, as long as he continued on his current path, his future achievements in the Calligraphy Dao would not be insignificant.","\"A temporary measure...\"","After this incident, Mr. Yue Ming understood the difficulty of the situation and secretly decided that he could not make any more exceptions in the future.","A moment later, Chen Yi finished his cup of tea and was about to get up and leave.","Just then, Mr. Yue Ming stopped him, picked up an envelope from the desk, and handed it to him.","\"This is a letter from Fang Gui. He says he wants us to help him decide what to do.\"","\"Oh? A letter from Brother Huai’gu?\"","Chen Yi took it and glanced at it, his brow furrowing.","The letter’s content was none other than the matter of the grain tax for the Three Towns’ summer harvest.","Originally, after the Imprisonment Department captured the \"murderer\" of Liu Jing, the Governor’s Office had sent a message to Li Huai’gu, telling him to collect the grain tax at a rate of one-twentieth.","Who would have thought that just the day before yesterday, Li Huai’gu received another letter from the Governor’s Office.","Or rather, a seal and an order.","\"’Strictly investigate the amount of summer grain stored in the Three Towns and collect the grain tax at a rate of one-tenth?’\"","\"The Governor’s Office has certainly mastered the art of issuing orders in the morning and rescinding them by evening.\"","It wasn’t hard to guess that this was Liu Hong’s \"attitude\" on display for the people who had arrived from the Jing State Liu Family.","All in all, he had laid his cards on the table for the Xiao Family to see—he was still ready for a fight!","Hearing his words, Mr. Yue Ming shook his head. \"With the dispute between the Xiao and Liu Families flaring up, Fang Gui is the one who suffers.\"","Chen Yi grunted in agreement and thought for a moment. \"The way I see it, this matter will go back and forth a few more times.\"","\"Oh? Qingzhou, you think Governor Liu will change his mind again?\"","\"Probably.\"","Chen Yi didn’t elaborate, only telling Mr. Yue Ming to reply as they had previously discussed and have Li Huai’gu continue to slow his progress.","There were still over twenty days left before the one-month deadline.","Before then, the matter between the Xiao and Liu Families should be settled.","He refused to believe that the Liu Family would dare to be so shameless after being implicated in the \"burning of the Three Towns’ summer grain.\"","If they really were, it went without saying that Elder Master Xiao would not let them off the hook.","After a bit more small talk, Chen Yi took his leave and rushed to the West Market without stopping.","He even specifically hired a carriage for the trip, hurrying all the way to Hundred Herbs Hall.","There, he switched to Wang Ji’s carriage and headed for Xichuan Street, west of Kangning Street in North City.","It had to be said, Wang Ji was fast.","The task he had given Zhang Dabao last night—acquiring two residences in North City and East City—Wang Ji had completed in just four hours.","One of them was in an alley behind Xichuan Street.","It was about two li from Liu Jing’s former residence, not too far.","\"Sir, time was short, so we haven’t prepared everything. Please bear with us.\"","Chen Yi waved his hand. Seeing that time was tight, he had Zhang Dabao disguise him directly.","While this was happening, he gave his instructions, \"When you see Eldest Miss Xiao, you take the lead. Explain the plan to expand Hundred Herbs Hall to her clearly.\"","Wang Ji hesitated. \"Sir, that’s not appropriate.\"","He was just the shopkeeper of Hundred Herbs Hall. If he was too forward in that kind of setting, not only would people think he had no manners, but they would also think Chen Yi was too lax with his subordinates.","Chen Yi waved his hand. \"It’s fine for me to be a man of few words. Just do as I say.\"","He had already decided to say and do as little as possible, preferably becoming a complete wallflower.","Seeing this, Wang Ji had no choice but to nod.","Then Chen Yi gave a few more instructions. Once the disguise was complete and he had checked it for any flaws, he took the carriage to the Xiao family estate.","Who knew that while his plan was well-laid, he hadn’t expected Eldest Miss Xiao to not play by the rules.","\"Shopkeeper Wang, the young miss has given her orders. Boss Chen is to go in alone. You and the others are to wait outside.\"","\"This...\""]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188 - 175: He seems like... Chen Yi?","paragraphs":["Not only had Wang Ji not expected such a request, but Chen Yi hadn’t either.","However, the two men felt completely different about it at this moment.","Wang Ji was mostly relieved.","He hadn’t been confident he could present the future plans for Hundred Herbs Hall completely and clearly under the watchful eyes of both Chen Yi and Xiao Wan’er.","Like an employee facing their boss, he felt nervous and anxious, lacking in confidence.","Chen Yi, on the other hand, was the exact opposite.","According to their original plan, he wouldn’t have had to say much, which would have lowered his risk of being exposed.","He wouldn’t have felt nervous at all in that scenario and would have been full of confidence.","But now, he had no choice but to speak with Xiao Wan’er face-to-face.","It wouldn’t do to remain silent and act like a nobody.","Chen Yi thought this, but his expression remained calm. He tilted his head up slightly and commanded in a haughty manner:","\"In that case, you two will wait here.\"","That expression and tone, combined with his faintly arrogant and superior demeanor, did indeed give him the air of someone from a great clan.","Furthermore, he wasn’t currently using the Black Tortoise Concealment Technique to restrain his aura. With his Power and True Essence stirring slightly, he appeared much more imposing and powerful.","Compared to his usual gentle, humble, and frail scholar-like appearance, this persona had more impact and a hint of flamboyance.","However, when Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao saw these changes, they were impressed but also couldn’t help but break into a cold sweat for him.","After all, they were inside the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.","Not only did he have to face Xiao Wan’er, but Martial Arts experts like Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun were also watching from the side.","If he revealed even the slightest flaw, no amount of disguise would be of any use.","But Chen Yi had no time to worry about their thoughts right now.","After taking the Oil Paper Umbrella from Zhang Dabao and the *Baicao Hall Expansion Charter* from Wang Ji, he followed Shen Huatang into the wooden building.","Cui’er then led Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao to an adjacent guest room to wait.","After Cui’er left, the two men looked at each other and couldn’t help but share a helpless smile.","\"Shopkeeper...\"","\"Shh.\"","Before Zhang Dabao could speak, Wang Ji raised a finger to his lips, signaling that the walls had ears.","Zhang Dabao nodded in understanding and mouthed, \"Do you think the boss can handle it?\"","\"Probably. The boss has always been composed. He should be able to control the situation.\"","Despite saying so, Wang Ji wasn’t very certain either.","’I hope the boss doesn’t make any mistakes.’","Mistakes?","’Of course, there wouldn’t be any.’","Chen Yi’s previous arrangements had just been a precaution.","But when that \"one in a million\" chance actually occurred, he didn’t panic. He was merely a little surprised.","’Xiao Wan’er must have some small scheme in mind,’ he mused. ’Probably a little ploy to seize the initiative or show how much she values this.’","With these thoughts, Chen Yi followed Shen Huatang into the wooden building and took a seat in the living room.","He wore a magnificent black brocade robe embroidered with a landscape painting, a sachet hanging from his waist to mask any scent. He simply sat quietly in his chair.","His handsome face was expressionless, abnormally calm, one might even say cold.","And yet, his every action conformed to the rules of etiquette.","Whether walking, sitting, or responding to Shen Huatang’s guidance and welcome, the details of his conduct all displayed the refined upbringing of a great clan.","Naturally, Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun observed all of this and reported it to Xiao Wan’er.","\"Young Miss, this man has an extraordinary bearing and outstanding looks. Judging by his aura, his Martial Arts are not weak either. He must come from a significant background.\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded, her beautiful head lowered slightly in thought. \"Then let’s proceed with the original plan. Present the gift first, then we’ll discuss other matters.\"","At this moment, she was still wrapped in a large cloak, but the collar was pulled even tighter than usual, almost covering her mouth and nose.","Even so, her pale face, with its hint of fragility, was still stunningly beautiful. With bright eyes and pearly teeth, her every glance exuded grace and nobility.","After exchanging a few simple words, Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun, each holding a tray covered with a red cloth, followed Xiao Wan’er into the living room.","Chen Yi heard them approaching and even faintly caught snippets of their conversation. Seeing them walk in, he glanced at the three of them out of the corner of his eye before rising to bow.","\"Chen Yu of Hundred Herbs Hall, I greet you, Young Miss.\"","Chen Yi had long been prepared for this, so he naturally didn’t act out of character. Furthermore, every aspect of his demeanor was different from his usual self.","His posture was more upright, his tone colder and stiffer, and his every move carried a hint of dominance. Even the look in his eyes was not entirely the same.","But when Xiao Wan’er saw him, she was still momentarily stunned, an inexplicable sense of familiarity surfacing in her heart.","That posture, that expression, those looks, that voice, and the bearing in his every move...","They should all have been unfamiliar, but she felt as if she had seen him somewhere before.","At first glance, he was like... like... a very, very proper Chen Yi.","So much so that Xiao Wan’er was slow to return the bow.","A few breaths later, Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun exchanged a look, both feeling a little puzzled.","But seeing that Boss Chen was still bowing, and that to continue any longer would be a breach of etiquette, Shen Huatang had no choice but to give a light cough as a reminder.","The sound brought Xiao Wan’er back to her senses. An unnatural blush appeared on her face as she curtsied.","\"Young Master Chen, there’s no need for such formality. Please, be seated.\"","As she spoke, she took the seat of honor, unable to prevent some strange thoughts from arising in her mind.","They mostly consisted of her grumbling about Chen Yi.","That man not only wrote her poems, but he also frequently stared and spoke improperly, teasing and flirting with her, which had left her with deep-seated \"resentment.\"","Otherwise, why would she now mistake a stranger for him?","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea that in just these few moments, Xiao Wan’er had already started grumbling about him in her head.","After taking his seat, he merely glanced at Xiao Wan’er before turning his head slightly and sitting ramrod straight, wearing a stern and unsmiling expression.","Xiao Wan’er also remained silent. She glanced at his profile, and that feeling of familiarity washed over her once again."]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189 - 175: He Seems Like... Chen Yi?","paragraphs":["’That profile...’","’It really does look like... my brother-in-law.’","Fortunately, after her initial stupor, Xiao Wan’er didn’t let her composure slip.","When Chen Yi didn’t speak, she beckoned with her hand and instructed in her usual tone,","\"Boss Chen, since this is our first meeting, I hope you will accept these small gifts.\"","As Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun placed the trays on the table beside him, Chen Yi inclined his head in thanks. \"Thank you, Eldest Young Lady.\"","A glance from the corner of his eye was enough. Even without lifting the red cloth, he could tell from the shapes underneath that they were the zither and long blade he had mentioned before.","Xiao Wan’er smiled. \"Lately, I must thank your Hundred Herbs Hall for all the help you’ve given our Xiao Family Medicine Hall.\"","\"From the sale of the herbal teas alone, the Xiao Family has earned a share of fourteen thousand taels of silver this month. It is I who should be thanking you.\"","\"You’re too kind,\" Chen Yi said, lowering his head slightly. \"My Hundred Herbs Hall is still new and lacks influence. We must rely on the support of you, Eldest Young Lady, and the Xiao Family.\"","\"If Fairy Tingyun hadn’t intervened to help us before, my Hundred Herbs Hall would have surely suffered a devastating blow. For that, I am eternally grateful and will never forget it.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused at his words. She glanced at Xie Tingyun, then said hesitantly, \"Ultimately, this matter arose because of my Xiao Family.\"","She then explained the whole affair with Liu Jing and Linglan Pavilion.","\"Young Master Chen, you were not aware of the circumstances. In truth, it is the Xiao Family that has wronged you.\"","Chen Yi glanced at her. Seeing her earnest expression, he let a faint smile touch his lips.","\"As they say, adversity reveals true friendship. If not for this incident, Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall would not have our current, mutually beneficial partnership.\"","Seeing that smile, Xiao Wan’er’s expression grew a little strained again.","This time, she didn’t continue the topic of their two medicine halls. Instead, she changed the subject, asking, \"If I may ask, Young Master Chen, where is your home?\"","Chen Yi looked away, the smile fading from his face. He replied calmly,","\"I was orphaned at a young age. I simply followed my master, studying the Medical Dao in the mountains. You could say I have no fixed home.\"","Xiao Wan’er was taken aback for a moment. But his words also dispelled the stray thoughts in her mind, and she mentally chided herself for asking such an inappropriate question.","\"My apologies, Young Master Chen. It’s just that you resemble an old acquaintance of mine, so... please, forgive my impertinence.\"","’An old acquaintance?’","A chill went down Chen Yi’s spine. ’I’ve been so careful. Could she have seen through my disguise?’","’Impossible.’","’Bluffing is against the rules, Xiao Wan’er. Don’t try to scare me like that.’","\"There’s no need to be so formal, Eldest Young Lady. I am but a commoner, a man of the Jianghu, in a manner of speaking. I am not worthy of such polite treatment from you.\"","\"You’re too modest, Young Master Chen. I was worried my own etiquette was lacking.\"","\"Not at all...\"","Watching the two of them exchange stiff pleasantries, Xie Tingyun, who stood to the side, started curling her toes in embarrassment.","Even Shen Huatang was filled with doubt.","She had served Xiao Wan’er for many years.","She had seen many similar scenes.","But normally, Xiao Wan’er was always poised and magnanimous. While appearing polite, her words and expression actually kept people at arm’s length.","Never had she been so... restrained.","Shen Huatang looked at Xiao Wan’er’s slightly unnatural expression and felt that something was very strange.","And then there were those two words from before: \"old acquaintance.\"","She racked her brain but couldn’t think of anyone who bore even the slightest resemblance to this Boss Chen Yu.","All in all, the current situation felt bizarre.","Chen Yi, of course, also sensed that something was off.","After her repeated probing, how could he not realize that Xiao Wan’er had spotted some cracks in his facade?","Thus, after a few more pleasantries, Chen Yi decided to cut to the chase.","Taking advantage of a pause in the conversation, he respectfully presented the \"Baicao Hall Expansion Charter\" that he had at hand.","\"I have come today with another matter to discuss with you, Eldest Young Lady.\"","Xiao Wan’er motioned for Shen Huatang to accept it. When she saw the title, she recognized Wang Ji’s handwriting. Suppressing the strange feeling in her heart, she asked,","\"The ’Baicao Hall Expansion Charter’? Young Master Chen, have you brought the wrong document?\"","Chen Yi shook his head slightly. \"Why don’t you take a look first, Eldest Young Lady.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er hesitated for a moment, then opened the booklet and began to read.","At first, she assumed it was a document concerning Hundred Herbs Hall’s internal affairs and read it rather casually.","But after only a few lines, her expression grew serious.","It took her nearly the time it takes for half a stick of incense to burn to read it all carefully. When she was done, her face was an unconcealed mix of astonishment, excitement, and gratitude.","After flipping through it quickly one more time, she calmed the tempest in her heart and looked at Chen Yi, asking earnestly,","\"Young Master Chen, what’s written in here... is it all true?\"","\"Do you truly intend to partner with my Xiao Family to open branches of Hundred Herbs Hall all over Shu State, and even throughout the Nine State and Three Prefectures of the Great Wei Dynasty?\"","Chen Yi turned his head to look at her, his expression serious. \"What you say is correct, Eldest Young Lady, but with one small clarification.\"","\"Within the borders of Shu State, the Xiao Family’s reputation is quite high, which will be beneficial for opening trade routes in the various state capitals and counties. Naturally, you can provide patronage to Hundred Herbs Hall.\"","\"Therefore, within Shu State, the Xiao Family will be responsible for handling the state and county government offices, the local noble families, and the Jianghu powers. In exchange, Hundred Herbs Hall can share fifty percent of all its profits with the Xiao Family.\"","He paused, and seeing Xiao Wan’er listening with rapt attention, he continued,","\"Outside of Shu State, however, the rules will naturally have to change.\"","\"For instance, in the neighboring Western State, Jiao State, and Guangyue Prefecture, if the Xiao Family is confident it can provide patronage for Hundred Herbs Hall, you can also receive a fifty-percent share of the profits.\"","\"But the Wei Dynasty is vast. Some places are near, and others are far.\"","\"In places like Jiangnan Prefecture and the Capital Prefecture, which are teeming with merchants and noble families, as well as faraway places like the Northern State, Ji State, Meng State, and You State, we will need to cooperate with powerful local clans.\"","\"In any state capital where the Xiao Family’s influence cannot reach, the profits will need to be shared with the local noble families who can provide that patronage.\"","Chen Yi’s explanation was detailed, and Xiao Wan’er naturally understood his meaning."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190 - 175: He Seems Like... Chen Yi?","paragraphs":["It was just that she’d never imagined business could be done this way.","According to her previous understanding,","a medicine hall was a thankless and laborious business.","It required a storefront, Physicians with superb Medical Skill, a Shopkeeper and apprentices to coordinate, a steady supply of medicinal ingredients, and so on.","Every single step had to be followed methodically, with no room for the slightest carelessness.","But according to the *Baicao Hall Expansion Charter* that Chen Yi had provided,","this Hundred Herbs Hall could operate without Physicians, or at least they wouldn’t need to be exceptionally skilled; a basic understanding of medical principles would be sufficient.","They would primarily sell common prescriptions and medicinal ingredients.","Profits would mainly come from various medicinal teas and pills that promoted the health and well-being of the common folk.","All of this left Xiao Wan’er somewhat astonished.","Whether it was Hundred Herbs Hall’s business model or its method of using profit-sharing to win over the Noble Families across the Nine State and Three Prefectures, it was all unlike anything she had ever encountered.","After thinking for a moment,","Xiao Wan’er grasped the key points and spoke up. \"I have two questions, and I hope Young Master Chen will enlighten me.\"","\"First, is it not unbalanced to only sell pre-made formulas? After all, a thousand people require a thousand different remedies.\"","She was clear on the matter of selling medicinal teas and certainly didn’t see a problem there.","Her only concern was that the pills, unable to be prescribed for specific symptoms, would cause people to miss their opportunity for treatment.","Chen Yi listened but didn’t respond immediately, merely gesturing for her to continue.","Xiao Wan’er paused. \"My second question concerns the more remote regions. Cooperating with the Noble Families is not the issue.\"","\"But all sorts of problems will inevitably arise. How can Young Master Chen guarantee they won’t line their own pockets, or even set up their own competing businesses?\"","Chen Yi nodded to himself upon hearing this. The first question was one thing, but the second one hit the nail on the head.","’At the start of the partnership, those great families, unaware of the potential profits, might just let Hundred Herbs Hall develop on its own.’","’But after seeing the profits, it’s inevitable that some would be tempted to take desperate measures.’","With this in mind, Chen Yi grunted in acknowledgment and said, \"Eldest Miss, you can rest assured about the matter of the pills.\"","\"My Hundred Herbs Hall has been open in Shu State for over a month now, and there have been no issues with the pills sold.\"","\"Later, I will have Wang Ji deliver Hundred Herbs Hall’s detailed ledgers. You will understand as soon as you see them, Eldest Miss.\"","\"As for the second question...\"","After a brief thought, Chen Yi continued, \"Merchants chase profits, and the Noble Families are no exception.\"","\"It’s likely impossible to completely avoid the problem you mentioned, Eldest Miss, but it can be managed through exclusive formulas, profit incentives, and force.\"","He then explained the details of these three methods one by one, his expression turning serious as he said,","\"Everything has its pros and cons. My expansion charter for Hundred Herbs Hall is designed for one thing: to spread across the Great Wei’s Nine State and Three Prefectures as quickly as possible.\"","\"When that time comes and the momentum is on our side, a few petty villains won’t be able to block our path.\"","’To be precise, as long as the Imperial Court doesn’t intervene, the competition between the Noble Families and Hundred Herbs Hall will remain within the scope of \"commercial warfare.\"’","’Problems of that nature could, for the most part, be solved with force.’","—A combined effort from Jianghu Sects, Medical Saint Hands, and the private armies of the Noble Families.","Xiao Wan’er was silent for a long time after he finished. Once she understood everything he had said, she finally let out a soft breath and remarked with admiration,","\"Young Master Chen, your thoughts are so meticulous and far-reaching. Wan’er is truly impressed.\"","\"However, this matter is of great importance. I cannot make this decision alone. I need to consult my grandfather before I can give you an answer.\"","Chen Yi nodded. He had expected as much.","’After all, this wasn’t about expanding Hundred Herbs Hall throughout Shu State Prefecture City, but across the entire Shu State, and even the whole Wei Dynasty.’","’The many aspects involved were tangled and complex, and the number of connections and personal networks that would have to be mobilized was beyond counting.’","’With Xiao Wan’er’s current status and authority, it would be difficult for her to undertake such a task.’","However, by Chen Yi’s estimation, this venture, which relied on both Hundred Herbs Hall and the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, would ultimately fall on Xiao Wan’er’s shoulders.","’When that time comes, I’ll inevitably have to meet with Xiao Wan’er again as \"Chen Yu.\" ’","’Hmm... Looks like I’ll have to find a way to be a hands-off boss.’","\"There’s no rush on this matter. It won’t be too late to make a decision after you’ve consulted the Marquis, Eldest Miss.\"","After he spoke, Chen Yi thought for a moment and couldn’t help but add a reminder,","\"However, this plan is of the utmost importance. I hope you will be careful not to let it be stolen by anyone with ill intentions, Eldest Miss, to avoid unforeseen complications.\"","\"And who might these people with ill intentions be, Young Master Chen?\"","\"...The Liu Family, for example.\"","Chen Yi had wanted to mention the second and third households of the Xiao Family, but on second thought, he figured the old Marquis would already be on guard against them, so he only brought up the Liu Family.","Xiao Wan’er understood. She smiled and said, \"Rest assured, Young Master Chen. Wan’er understands the stakes.\"","Chen Yi nodded. \"That’s good.\"","Seeing that their official business was concluded,","Chen Yi pretended to glance at the sky outside, then cupped his fists. \"I have intruded enough for one day. I will take my leave now.\"","Xiao Wan’er froze for a second, surprised. \"Young Master Chen, I’ve already arranged a banquet in the garden for you today. You...\"","Before she could finish, Chen Yi had already risen and bowed. \"I must ask for your forgiveness, Eldest Miss.\"","\"I have matters to attend to this evening, so I cannot linger. Please forgive me.\"","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er knew she couldn’t insist he stay. She instructed Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun to carry the trays and escort him out of the wooden pavilion.","After a few more politeries,","Chen Yi, along with Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao, directly boarded the carriage and departed from the Xiao Family estate.","’Finally, I can breathe a sigh of relief.’","’If I stayed any longer, with no serious business to occupy Xiao Wan’er’s attention, there’s no guarantee she wouldn’t notice something was off.’","’It was better to leave early.’","Wang Ji glanced at his expression. \"Boss, was there no...\"","\"’No’ what? You seem to have a lot of free time lately. When we get back, I’ll find something for you to do.\"","\"Uh...\"","\"Hm?\"","\"This subordinate obeys.\"","\"Mm.\"","Such a nonsensical conversation naturally reached the ears of Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, who were behind them.","Although they didn’t understand why that Boss Chen was being so harsh with Wang Ji, they knew that Xiao Wan’er was being a bit strange.","It was because, at that moment, Xiao Wan’er was staring blankly at the departing carriage.","Her eyes still held a hint of doubt and inquiry, as she still felt a sense of familiarity about this person, Chen Yu.","「After a long while.」","Xiao Wan’er felt a chill and subconsciously pulled her cloak tighter around herself, turning to head back to Jiaxing Garden.","As she glanced toward Spring Lotus Garden, she couldn’t help but ask,","\"Huatang, Tingyun, don’t you two think that Young Master Chen is very similar to... my brother-in-law?\"","\"The young master?\"","Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun followed her gaze toward Spring Lotus Garden and shook their heads in unison.","\"Not at all, Miss.\"","\"The young master is frail and scholarly, and not skilled in the Martial Arts.\"","\"It’s true that the young master excels at Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting, but he is not well-versed in the ways of business. He could never have such deep foresight like Boss Chen Yu.\"","After listening, Xiao Wan’er nodded doubtfully, muttering to herself nonstop.","\"Not alike... they’re not alike...?\"","After thinking for a moment, Xiao Wan’er temporarily set aside the strange feeling in her heart and gave an order,","\"Huatang, when my brother-in-law gets back, please invite him to Jiaxing Garden for dinner.\"","\"We’ve prepared so much food; it would be a shame to let it go to waste...\""]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191 - 176: I Have Confidence in Him","paragraphs":["Xiao Wan’er took a short rest.","The strange notion in her mind, triggered by Chen Yu reminding her of Chen Yi, finally began to fade.","Just as Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun had said.","Chen Yi was not skilled in Martial Arts. He was merely a delicate scholar who excelled at Music, Chess, Calligraphy, and Painting—worlds apart from Chen Yu, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall.","As for why she felt they were similar, after much thought, she could only attribute it to coincidence.","’It couldn’t possibly be for some outlandish reason like Chen Yu being Chen Yi’s long-lost brother.’","Seeing that it was still early, Xiao Wan’er instructed Xiao Wuge to focus on his etiquette lessons, then took the \"Baicao Hall Expansion Charter\" with her to Qingjing Residence.","In truth, she was not a decisive and efficient woman by nature.","Perhaps it was due to her frail health.","It had made her gentle since childhood, always thinking of others and rarely considering herself first.","Take the matter of Hundred Herbs Hall, for example.","The reason she was in such a hurry to see the Old Master was simply because she recognized the value of this charter.","If Hundred Herbs Hall could expand as rapidly as the charter proposed, it would bring the Xiao Family all benefits and no drawbacks.","Not only could it bring the Xiao Family considerable wealth and solve financial issues for the estate, the Dingyuan Army, and most future matters involving silver coins,","It was also a charitable act.","Healing the sick and saving lives could be considered an accumulation of good karma.","It would also improve the Xiao Family’s reputation.","Xiao Wan’er knew very well that for Noble Families, the latter was often more important than the former.","Upon arriving at Qingjing Residence,","Xiao Wan’er had Shen Huatang and Xie Tingyun wait under the eaves, not forgetting to instruct them,","\"If anyone comes to visit, just say that Grandfather is unavailable at the moment.\"","She still remembered Boss Chen’s reminder to handle this matter with caution and discretion.","Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang nodded and stood guard at the entrance.","Although they didn’t quite believe that Hundred Herbs Hall could expand across the Great Wei Nine State and Three Prefectures, seeing how seriously their Young Miss was taking it, they naturally didn’t let their skepticism show.","Afterwards, Xiao Wan’er went alone, holding an Oil Paper Umbrella, to pay her respects to the Old Master.","Qingjing Residence was not exactly quiet at the moment.","The torrential downpour inevitably made it feel a bit noisy.","The rain pounded on the slate paths, fell upon the flowers and trees, and dripped from the roof tiles.","The various sounds merged, making it difficult for Xiao Wan’er to hear the voices from inside the house.","\"...The Young Miss is here.\"","It seemed someone had said that.","But when Xiao Wan’er walked into the main hall, she only saw the Old Master drinking tea alone in the living room.","She scanned the room, found nothing amiss, and smiled as she curtsied. \"Your granddaughter greets you, Grandfather.\"","The Old Master, seated in the Grandmaster’s Chair, nodded with a smile and gestured for her to sit.","\"The rain has been heavy and the wind cold these past few days. You should get out less. If you need something, just send a servant. I can go over to Jiaxing Garden myself.\"","\"How could I let you do that? Grandfather, your health has just recovered. You need your rest as well.\"","\"Besides, it’s fine if I’m unwell. If something were to happen to you, the other grand-uncles and uncles in the estate would surely blame me.\"","\"Who would dare? You’re my granddaughter. Not just anyone can blame you.\"","\"Grandfather...\"","The conversation was rather heartwarming, but to an outsider, it would have sounded like two patients discussing their conditions.","After a few more pleasantries,","Xiao Wan’er took out the \"Baicao Hall Expansion Charter\" and placed it in the Old Master’s hands. \"Grandfather, please take a look at this.\"","\"This is...\"","The Old Master looked at the booklet. He had, of course, heard of Hundred Herbs Hall and knew about the teas it sold.","And recently, due to the relationship between the Xiao Family Medicine Hall and Hundred Herbs Hall, he had even specifically sought out a few bottles to try.","Wangji Tea was refreshing. Old Platinum Tea was slightly bitter with a sweet aftertaste. Divine Bull Tea had a strange flavor, but after drinking it, Power surged through his body.","As for the Mushroom Tea and Beauty Tea, he had only looked at them and hadn’t actually tried them.","However, after trying it, he found the Old Platinum Tea truly did make him feel much more relaxed. He had been drinking a bottle every day recently.","But tea was one thing; the Old Master was still a bit puzzled about some \"expansion charter.\"","\"I heard the owner of that Hundred Herbs Hall came over today. Did he bring this?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded with a smile. \"Boss Chen is young and promising. Not only is his mastery of the Medical Dao exquisite, but he also has a sharp mind for business.\"","After a few words of praise, she continued, \"He did indeed bring this charter today. He wants to cooperate with our Xiao Family.\"","The Old Master began to flip through the booklet, saying, \"I’ve already said that you’re in charge of the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s affairs. You don’t need to specifically...\"","Before he could finish, he saw the contents of the booklet. He let out a soft sound, a hint of interest appearing on his face.","Seeing his expression, Xiao Wan’er knew her grandfather was just as stunned by the contents as she had been. She said with a smile,","\"The matters discussed in this charter are immense. I couldn’t make a decision, so I had to come and ask for your guidance, Grandfather.\"","The Old Master grunted in acknowledgment, holding the booklet far away to read the contents clearly, muttering to himself.","\"Hundred Herbs Hall wishes to use Shu State as a base, first expanding to neighboring states and counties, then developing the lands of the Nine State and Three Prefectures...\"","Seeing this, Xiao Wan’er sat quietly in her chair and waited.","She had faith in this charter, and she had a certain amount of faith in Boss Chen’s plans and ambitions.","The only uncertainty was whether the Xiao Family could support Hundred Herbs Hall’s expansion with all its might, as Boss Chen requested.","「Before long.」","The Old Master finished reading the entire charter in detail. A trace of amazement appeared on his thin, wrinkled face. \"Interesting.\"","\"Wan’er, was this charter written by that owner of Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Xiao Wan’er nodded. \"Grandfather, he was the one who brought it. Judging by the handwriting, it was written by Wang Ji on his behalf.\"","\"Oh? And what do you think of this matter?\"","\"I... I want to give it a try. It’s just that I understand the difficulty involved, and the effort it would require.\"","\"If the family decides to support Hundred Herbs Hall, I’m afraid it will affect other matters.\"","The Old Master nodded slightly. \"Your assessment is astute. This matter is not so simple.\"","\"Putting aside what’s outside Shu State, just dealing with the Noble Families in the local states and counties of Shu State is no easy task.\"","\"If Hundred Herbs Hall’s earnings were small, it would be fine. But looking at the Xiao Family Medicine Hall’s profits from the last month, those teas... the profits are enormous.\"","Having been in Shu State for many years, the Old Master knew just how troublesome those great clans could be.","This was especially true for the tribes and clans in the mountainous regions.","Even if the Xiao Family’s might alone could make them submit, it would still attract some criticism.","Once Hundred Herbs Hall started turning a profit, once the Xiao Family Medicine Hall started distributing its share, even if the members of those great clans said nothing, they would inevitably feel some resentment.","They would probably say things like, \"The Xiao Family is hogging all the profits,\" or, \"They don’t think to include their old subordinates and brothers in their money-making ventures.\"","Ultimately, the Xiao Family had cultivated its presence in Shu State for two hundred years. Its relationships with the various clans, states, and counties were deeply and intricately connected; a simple, one-size-fits-all solution was not possible.","It was just like the Mutual Market built in cooperation with the Mountain Race.","They had to bring some people in, win over some of the Noble Families, to put everyone at ease.","Xiao Wan’er thought for a moment and asked, \"Grandfather, does our family need to share some of the silver coins from this?\"","Hearing this, the Old Master teased, \"A share does indeed need to be given out. But why can’t it be Hundred Herbs Hall that gives it?\"","Xiao Wan’er froze for a second, then said hesitantly, \"But Boss Chen was the one who proposed this charter, I...\"","\"You feel bad about it?\"","\"A little.\"","Seeing her nod, the Old Master said with a smile, \"Wan’er, your nature is too kind. You’ll be at a disadvantage in the world of business.\"","A blush of shame appeared on Xiao Wan’er’s face, and she lowered her head slightly. \"I was wrong.\"","\"That was too harsh.\"","\"This isn’t about right or wrong. It’s just that you don’t understand the stakes involved. It may seem like our Xiao Family can take a fifty percent share in Shu State, but in reality, it’s thirty percent at most.\"","\"And Hundred Herbs Hall provides the charter, the formulas, the people... hmm. Taking fifty percent is actually quite reasonable.\"","Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but smile. \"Grandfather, you think so too.\"","The Old Master shook his head with a smile. \"I just think he’s making this money too easily.\"","At this point, he had finally understood the value of the charter.","Hundred Herbs Hall had the formulas, the money-making methods, and the brains. The only thing it lacked was the connections to get through to the various powers that be.","Coincidentally, the Xiao Family had close ties with all parties and possessed the connections, but lacked a profitable business.","They could complement each other’s needs.","\"That owner of Hundred Herbs Hall has a unique vision. That’s a rare and valuable quality.\"","Seeing him praise Boss Chen, Xiao Wan’er was delighted. \"Grandfather, you... you agree?\"","The Old Master raised a hand, gesturing for her to wait.","「After a moment of thought.」","The Old Master watched the rain fall outside the hall, weighed the pros and cons, and said, \"This deal can be done. I agree to it.\"","Joy bloomed in Xiao Wan’er’s heart, but she knew he had more to say, so she didn’t speak hastily.","Then she heard the Old Master continue, \"However, we cannot be hasty with this. Many things still need careful consideration. At the very least...\"","\"At the very least, we need to find out about that boss... What’s his name?\"","\"Chen Yu. I heard he’s been studying medicine with his master in the mountains.\"","The Old Master nodded. \"We must be able to trust this Chen Yu.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused, then said with understanding, \"You’re right, Grandfather.\"","\"The Xiao Family is going through troubled times. We must be careful with everything.\"","\"I understand.\"","Xiao Wan’er was naturally aware of some of her family’s circumstances and could understand the Old Master’s reasoning.","However, she had a strange, inexplicable faith in that Boss Chen and didn’t believe he was a problem.","「Before long.」","Xiao Wan’er left with a smile on her face.","The Old Master watched her walk away, only then letting out a soft sigh.","\"You heard all that, didn’t you?\"","\"Later, go and investigate that boss... Chen Yu. While you’re at it, investigate the others in Hundred Herbs Hall as well.\"","\"Our Xiao Family’s luck has been extremely poor for the last five years. To suddenly encounter such a good thing... it forces an old man like me to be suspicious.\"","As soon as his voice fell, a shadowy figure emerged from a side room, bowing in salute.","\"This subordinate will go shortly.\"","The Old Master grunted. \"Just investigate it on the side.\"","\"Your primary task recently is to keep a close watch on the Jing State Liu Family.\"","\"Since they’re acting up again, imposing a ten percent grain tax on the summer harvest in the Three Towns, they’re bound to make other moves.\"","\"Rest assured, Marquis. Their movements are all under the watch of the Hidden Guard.\"","\"It’s just that there have been strange stirrings in the black market recently.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"A newly placed Hidden Guard sent word last night that Elder Demon Fang died at the hands of Black Tooth. Also, quite a few Evil Demons have gathered at the Spring Rain Building, seemingly discussing some major deal.\"","The Old Master frowned slightly, a flash of killing intent in his cloudy eyes.","\"What kind of major deal requires clearing out all the spies in the black market?\"","\"Investigate it thoroughly. See what the Bright Moon Building is up to.\"","\"Yes, sir!\""]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192 - 177: Chess Dao Great Success, Gifting a Blade, and an Appointment","paragraphs":["Although Chen Yi didn’t know the details of Xiao Wan’er’s conversation with the Old Master, he had a general idea of how the Old Master and certain members of the Xiao Family would react when he presented the proposal.","On one hand, the expansion of the Hundred Herbs Hall could significantly alleviate the Xiao Family’s financial burdens regarding silver coins and resolve some of the pressure from the Imperial Court, the Dingyuan Army, and other Noble Families.","On the other hand, the matter itself required no significant investment from the Xiao Family.","To be precise, by leveraging the connections the Xiao Family had built in Shu State over the years, they merely had to call in a few favors and give up a portion of the profits to ensure no one would give the Hundred Herbs Hall any trouble.","It was, in a way, giving the Xiao Family a channel to monetize their \"connections.\"","Furthermore, they could use this opportunity to deepen their relationships with some of the Noble Families in the various prefectures and counties of Shu State.","It was a win-win situation for everyone involved.","Therefore, Chen Yi couldn’t think of any reason for the Old Master to refuse.","The only thing he was unsure about was what the Old Master’s intentions were for the Hundred Herbs Hall.","After all, a fifty percent cut of the profits seemed like a lot, but after accounting for all the social obligations and expenses, the Xiao Family would be left with thirty to forty percent at most.","Compared to the solid fifty percent that the Hundred Herbs Hall would be taking home.","Anyone in that position would inevitably feel a bit of an imbalance.","Additionally, the attitudes of certain other people in the Xiao Family also had to be considered.","The second branch, the third branch, and other side branches.","It was foreseeable that once the Xiao Family Medicine Hall started earning large sums of silver coins through the Hundred Herbs Hall, people like Xiao Wang and Xiao Shen would not just stand by and do nothing.","They might try to use some pretext to cause a scene, hoping to replace Xiao Wan’er as the Xiao Family’s general manager.","At the very least, they would fight for some benefits for their respective branches.","For example, increasing the monthly allowances, or planting some of their people in the Xiao Family Medicine Hall, or even the Hundred Herbs Hall.","Chen Yi had anticipated all of this and naturally had countermeasures in mind.","However, since the Hundred Herbs Hall’s expansion had not yet taken its first step, he didn’t need to worry about it for the time being.","Instead, the matter of the Bright Moon Building and the Hidden Guard \"burning the summer grain of the Three Towns\" was imminent, and he could not afford the slightest carelessness.","So, after leaving the Xiao Family, Chen Yi went directly to the residence in the West Market and instructed Wang Ji and Zhang Dabao to have Liu Lang come over after they returned.","However, he estimated it would take Liu Lang some time to investigate the Liu Family’s whereabouts, so he probably wouldn’t arrive so quickly.","Chen Yi wasn’t in a hurry. He sat quietly on the Grandmaster’s Chair in the main hall, his eyes fixed on the falling rain outside, but his mind was already focused on what was to come.","In his mind, black and white stones were placed on a Go board, then picked up again, constantly shifting and disrupting the situation on the board.","At that moment, the rain outside began to pick up.","SPLASH! The rain hammered against the roof tiles and stone slabs, creating a rapid, loud PATTER.","Mixed in were the sounds of raindrops hitting puddles, sending water splashing everywhere.","The dark clouds in the sky must have thickened, making the light inside the residence even dimmer.","A faint RUMBLE of thunder could be heard in the distance.","Then, flashes of lightning tore through the gloom, illuminating the slightly noisy main hall.","It also clearly lit up Chen Yi’s handsome profile, the face he used for his alias, \"Chen Yu.\"","Even his bright eyes seemed to be veiled in a faint fluorescent light, piercing through layers of dark clouds and mist like lightning to see the final state of the game.","「About an hour later.」","Chen Yi unconsciously tapped his fingers twice on the back of the chair and muttered under his breath:","\"Let’s do it that way, then.\"","He had sorted everything out. In the end, some people would have to pay a price, and others would have to be made fearful.","It was also a way of handing the Old Master a blade, allowing him to display the might of the Xiao Family.","This time, he not only wanted to alleviate the internal and external pressures on the Xiao Family, but more importantly, to create a comfortable environment for himself.","After all, by his count, he hadn’t gone fishing in four or five days.","Thinking of this, Chen Yi glanced outside, listened for a moment, and seeing that Liu Lang hadn’t arrived yet, he opened his status screen to take a look:","[Opportunity: 138]","In the last two days, he had witnessed Liu Wen scheming against Ma Liangcai and Black Tooth discussing important matters. One was a Yellow-level Top Grade event, the other Earth-level Middle Grade, yielding a bountiful harvest.","His Opportunity had once again surpassed one hundred, allowing him to raise one Dao to Great Success.","However, since only his Chess Dao was still at the Minor Success Realm, there was no need for other considerations.","Chen Yi immediately raised his Chess Dao to Great Success.","Before the myriad Profound Mysteries of the Chess Dao could fully settle in his mind, he lifted the red cloth from a nearby tray and picked up the long blade.","He now had a Profound Tier *Brocade Spring Saber Technique* and a *Carefree Travel* Zither Score that he could practice.","This would allow him to acquire the Saber Dao and the Zither Dao simultaneously.","Taking advantage of the free moment, Chen Yi drew the long blade and began practicing the Brocade Spring Saber Technique in the main hall.","「About fifteen minutes later.」","He finished a passable run-through of the Brocade Spring Saber Technique and immediately saw a line of large text float before his eyes:","[Successfully practiced Saber Technique: Brocade Spring Saber Technique (Profound Tier). Level: Initial Insight]","[Martial Arts: Blade - Uninitiated 0/1 (Upgradeable)]","Without pausing, Chen Yi sheathed the long blade and, repeating his previous action, picked up the Seven-Stringed Zither from another tray to play according to the *Carefree Travel* Zither Score.","However, he had overestimated his talent for music.","After all, when he practiced the Brocade Spring Saber Technique, he had a foundation in Martial Arts, so even if the moves were clumsy, his body could still perform the actions.","But when it came to zither skills, he couldn’t even read the sheet music, let alone play the corresponding notes.","A carefree and elegant zither piece became a fragmented, discordant mess in his hands, so awful that anyone who heard it would have instantly covered their ears.","After a few attempts, Chen Yi chose to give up.","Fortunately, there were no outsiders here. Otherwise, even with his thick skin, he estimated he would have blushed from embarrassment.","Chen Yi sullenly put away the Seven-Stringed Zither, muttering to himself about finding someone to teach him later, and then proceeded to raise his Saber Dao to Minor Success.","Instantly, in addition to the yet-to-be-digested Profound Mysteries of the Great Success Chess Dao, the entry-level and Minor Success Realm Profound Mysteries of the Saber Dao flooded his mind.","Even though his Cultivation had reached the Sixth Grade Realm, with his Forehead Acupoint Sea of Qi mastery and the Four Directions Divine Position to help absorb the influx, his brow still throbbed with pain from the contents of these two Daos.","Chen Yi rubbed the space between his eyebrows and rested for a moment before he started to feel better.","It had been a long time since his Medical Dao reached Great Success that he had felt this sensation of being overwhelmed by the Profound Mysteries of a Dao Realm.","「Not long after.」","Liu Lang rushed in.","Seeing Chen Yi’s appearance, he couldn’t help but ask with some confusion, \"Boss, did you not sleep all night?\"","Chen Yi ignored him, rubbing his brow as he asked, \"Have you found the Liu Family’s whereabouts?\"","Liu Lang sat down to the side and nodded. \"Found it.\"","\"Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue are currently staying on Kangning Street in North City. They aren’t living with Liu Hong.\"","\"Only Liu Yu is staying at Liu Hong’s house.\"","\"Also, in the few days since they arrived in Shu State, apart from visiting Liu Hong right at the beginning, Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue have just been wandering around the Prefecture City.\"","\"In contrast, Liu Yu has been staying at Liu Hong’s house and hasn’t gone out ever since he visited the Dingyuan Marquis’s Mansion.\"","After hearing this, Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly. \"So, you’re saying Liu Yu and the siblings Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue came to Shu State with different purposes?\"","He remembered the initial information he’d heard from Liu Wen—that they wanted to propose a marriage to the Xiao Family.","For this reason, Liu Yu, the Chief Steward of the Liu Family’s second branch, had even made a special trip to the Xiao Family to mention it to the Old Master.","But the Old Master had rejected him outright.","Now, with Liu Yu staying at Liu Hong’s house while Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue were out wandering, it was obvious they had their own separate agendas.","Chen Yi speculated internally, ’Liu Yu is probably here to coordinate with Liu Hong, or perhaps to urge him to resolve the dispute with the Xiao Family.’","’His marriage proposal to the Xiao Family might have just been a secondary objective, or maybe it was just him taking the first step on Liu Wen’s behalf.’","’As for the siblings Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue... I can’t quite see their intentions yet.’","With these thoughts in mind, Chen Yi gave an order. \"In that case, go deliver a message to Liu Wen tonight, in Black Tooth’s name.\"","Liu Lang was taken aback, pointing to himself. \"Me? In Black Tooth’s name?\"","\"Yes. You don’t need to say much. Just tell him that on the night after tomorrow, Black Tooth will pay him a visit to discuss an important matter.\"","\"But Black Tooth...\"","Seeing that he still didn’t get it, Chen Yi raised a hand to cut him off. \"I’ll be the one going, of course.\"","\"Are you thinking of sending a message to the real Black Tooth and telling him to go see Liu Wen?\"","The realization dawned on Liu Lang, and he laughed awkwardly a couple of times, though he still didn’t quite understand why Chen Yi was doing this.","\"Boss, I know what I need to do.\"","\"But can you tell me why we have to go through all this trouble to see Liu Wen, and why you’re doing it in Black Tooth’s name?\"","Chen Yi shot him a glare and said irritably, \"You’ll understand when you come with me, won’t you?\"","It wasn’t that he couldn’t tell Liu Lang.","It was just that with Liu Lang’s mind, knowing too much wouldn’t do him any good.","If he went to deliver the message to Liu Wen and someone tricked him into revealing something, that would be a huge problem.","Liu Lang thought about it and agreed, nodding his head.","\"Do you have any other instructions?\"","Chen Yi was about to say there was nothing else when he suddenly remembered something. He pointed to the long blade on the table, which was covered by a red cloth, and said, \"The thing I promised you.\"","Liu Lang went over and lifted the cloth, his eyes lighting up. \"A blade?\"","Looking at the long blade with its simple, unadorned scabbard and grand appearance, he eagerly drew it from its sheath.","A sharp gleam of light flashed from the blade.","Liu Lang’s face broke into a wide grin. He unfastened the Broken Blade from his waist and hung the new one in its place, fiddling with it fondly.","\"Thank you for the blade, Boss.\"","\"As long as you’re satisfied.\"","Seeing Liu Lang endlessly drawing and sheathing the long blade, Chen Yi waved a hand to dismiss him.","Before he left, Chen Yi didn’t forget to remind Liu Lang about his task for the night.","\"Remember not to get entangled with Liu Wen. Just deliver the message.\"","\"And remember to hide yourself well. Don’t run into any of Black Tooth’s men, or you might ruin the plan.\"","Liu Lang nodded in agreement, then walked out, still preoccupied with drawing and sheathing his new blade.","Seeing this, Chen Yi secretly shook his head. He could only hope that Liu Lang would handle tonight’s task with the same care he was showing that long blade.","If he failed to draw Liu Wen into the scheme, it would truly be a pity.","Once the residence fell quiet again, Chen Yi removed his disguise, changed back into a long robe, and headed back to the Xiao Family under an Oil Paper Umbrella.","Although it was a rainy day, his mood had lightened considerably after setting his plans in motion.","On the way back, he not only bought some food to fill his stomach,","but he also made a special trip to a zither shop to buy two zither scores, which he would use later when he found a teacher to instruct him in the Zither Dao.","After all, for someone like him with a bit of a compulsive streak, he either didn’t start something at all, or he had to do it perfectly.","He couldn’t just let that copy of *Carefree Travel* sit there unlearned.","Walking and stopping along the way, he spent two hours before finally returning to the Spring Lotus Garden.","Before he could call for Xiaodie to bring water for him to wash up and change, Shen Huatang came looking for him.","\"Young Master, the Young Miss invites you to dinner.\"","\"...\"","Chen Yi rubbed his stomach, which was already seventy or eighty percent full, and replied, \"Is it okay if I don’t go?\"","Shen Huatang paused for a second, then curtsied. \"Please forgive me, Young Master.\"","\"Fine, I’ll go after I change my clothes...\"","’If I’d known, I wouldn’t have eaten out,’ he thought. ’Now I’ll miss out on a good meal.’"]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193 - 178: I’d Be the One to Break, I...","paragraphs":["After a quick wash, Chen Yi changed into a fresh, dry long robe and made his way to Jiaxing Garden under an oil-paper umbrella.","By now, Xiao Wan’er had already laid out a sumptuous feast.","Xiao Wuge, Xie Tingyun, and Shen Huatang, along with Xiaodie, Cui’er, and Juan’er, were already seated.","Seeing Chen Yi arrive, Xiao Wan’er and Xiao Wuge smiled and beckoned for him to take a seat, while the others all rose to welcome him.","Chen Yi casually cupped his hands in greeting and sat down opposite Xiao Wuge.","To his left was Xiao Wan’er in the seat of honor, and to his right was Xiaodie.","He couldn’t help but catch faint wisps of fragrance.","Most of it came from Xiao Wan’er, while a smaller portion was the sweet scent from the young maid, Xiaodie.","After looking around the table, Chen Yi feigned ignorance and asked, \"This banquet was supposed to be for that boss from Hundred Herbs Hall, wasn’t it?\"","\"Why? Didn’t he come?\"","Xiao Wan’er gave him a look of mock reproach. \"And you have the nerve to ask. I told you this morning to come back early, but you only just got back tonight.\"","Chen Yi met her gaze and said calmly, \"Mr. Yue Ming invited me. His hospitality was hard to refuse, so I stayed at the academy for a while longer.\"","Xiao Wan’er naturally didn’t doubt him, nor was she truly blaming him. She said her piece and let it drop, then went on to explain:","\"That Boss Chen came with his people this afternoon. Although he’s a bit reserved and quiet, his speech and demeanor were quite exceptional.\"","\"Especially that Baicao Hall Expansion Charter he presented. It was truly admirable. Even Grandfather had high praise for him.\"","Chen Yi made a sound of understanding. ’He was fairly certain she had already discussed it with the Old Master. It wasn’t hard to deduce the outcome from her mention of \"high praise\"—the Old Master must have approved the charter he proposed.’","\"What charter is so impressive?\"","\"It’s a plan to expand Hundred Herbs Hall into Shu State, and even across all the Nine State and Three Prefectures of our Wei Dynasty. Grandfather and I both reviewed it and think it’s feasible.\"","\"Not only will it help Hundred Herbs Hall grow, but it will also bring considerable profits to our Xiao Family. It’s a win-win situation. Also...\"","Xiao Wan’er recounted everything in detail, completely forgetting the reminder \"Boss Chen\" had given her earlier.","So much so that Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang, who knew the real situation, couldn’t help but shoot a few extra glances at Chen Yi.","They were likely wondering what was so special about him to earn such complete trust from the Eldest Miss.","Meanwhile, Xiao Wuge and Xiaodie weren’t paying much attention to these matters; their eyes were glued to the delicious food on the table, and they were quietly salivating.","Perhaps because the two were being too obvious, Xiao Wan’er paused her explanation, invited everyone to pick up their chopsticks, and suggested they eat as they talked.","Chen Yi had already eaten while he was out, so he only took a couple of bites before falling into a casual chat with Xiao Wan’er.","\"From the sound of it, that Boss Chen is quite capable.\"","\"He is. Otherwise, he never could have produced a charter like that.\"","Xiao Wan’er paused. Thinking back to the strange thoughts she’d had during her meeting with Boss Chen, she couldn’t help but look at Chen Yi now.","She scrutinized him carefully, looking him up and down.","As she studied him, she began comparing the similarities and differences between Boss Chen and Chen Yi in her mind.","’Their brows and eyes were somewhat similar, but their gazes were different.’","’His eyes were gentle and full of spirit, making him seem warm and approachable.’","’Their face shapes were similar—in fact, they were almost identical.’","’But their facial features were slightly different.’","’Though his skin was a bit tanner, his features were softer and less sharp-edged, which was more pleasing to the eye.’","’Their builds were similar, but since he wasn’t skilled in Martial Arts, he seemed a bit more scholarly and frail.’","’But that wasn’t a bad thing; most talented scholars were like that.’","’And also...’","In just a few moments, Xiao Wan’er had mentally listed ten ways Chen Yi outshone Boss Chen.","’All in all, his superiority was obvious.’","Chen Yi noticed her staring. He glanced down at himself but found nothing out of the ordinary, so he couldn’t help but ask:","\"Eldest Sister, is there something on me...?\"","But before he could finish, Xiao Wan’er snapped back to reality, and the chopsticks in her hand fell to the floor with a CLATTER.","Her face flushed as she hurriedly bent down to pick them up, not noticing that her forehead was headed straight for the corner of the table.","Seeing this, Chen Yi forgot his question and, with lightning-fast reflexes, shot his hand out to block the corner of the table.","He perfectly caught Xiao Wan’er’s smooth forehead.","SMACK.","The crisp sound made everyone, who had already looked over when the chopsticks fell, freeze in stunned silence.","Even Xiao Wan’er, who had just bumped her head against Chen Yi’s palm, was dazed. With her forehead pressed against his warm hand, she felt her face burning as if on fire.","It wasn’t just the warmth spreading from her forehead, but also the embarrassment from her own flustered reaction that left her at a complete loss for a moment.","Seeing this, Chen Yi gently tilted her head up and asked with a smile, \"Eldest Sister, are you all right?\"","\"They’re just a pair of chopsticks. Don’t worry about picking them up. Just have Cui’er get you a new pair.\"","Hearing this, Cui’er quickly stood up, picked up the chopsticks, and said apologetically:","\"Please forgive me, milady. It was my fault. I’ll go get you a new pair of chopsticks right away.\"","The others saw what had happened and mostly understood the situation, so they didn’t say anything.","Only Xiao Wuge, ever the precocious child, couldn’t help but laugh after figuring out what just happened.","\"Sis, you should thank Brother-in-law.\"","\"If Brother-in-law hadn’t stepped in, you would have cracked your head on the table corner.\"","This made Xiao Wan’er’s face flush an even deeper red. Her eyes darted about shyly, and she feigned a light slap at him.","\"You’re talking nonsense! If anything was going to break, it would have been me... I mean... the table is quite hard.\"","She was clearly at a loss for words, and her explanation sounded rather feeble.","Stammering, Xiao Wan’er finally remembered the impropriety of the situation. She suppressed her embarrassment, lowered her head slightly, and offered her thanks.","Chen Yi just smiled. He knew she had simply been lost in thought, but he didn’t press the matter, not wanting to make the easily embarrassed Xiao Wan’er feel even more awkward."]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194 - 178: If Someone’s Going to Be the Bad Guy, It’s Me, I...","paragraphs":["After Cui’er brought Xiao Wan’er a new pair of chopsticks and she sat back down, Chen Yi continued their previous topic of conversation.","\"With Elder Master Xiao’s nod, won’t Hundred Herbs Hall soon be able to flourish all over Shu State?\"","Xiao Wan’er didn’t answer right away. She quietly let out a breath to compose herself before trying to organize her thoughts, her head still feeling a bit fuzzy.","\"Grandfather is still a bit wary. He said we should wait.\"","\"Wait?\"","\"Yes. He wants to confirm Boss Chen’s background. But I don’t think there will be any issues. I heard today that he’s been studying the Medical Dao with his master since he was a child, and he also said...\"","Chen Yi clearly wasn’t listening to the rest of what she said.","Elder Master Xiao’s caution didn’t surprise him, but it would certainly cause some trouble.","Especially since when he had ordered Wang Ji to establish Hundred Herbs Hall, he hadn’t put much thought into it, treating it as just a casual move in a larger game.","As a result, there were holes in many of the details.","For instance, the background of \"Chen Yu,\" the whereabouts of his master, and the connections to Ma Liangcai and Jishi Medicine Hall.","None of these things would hold up under close scrutiny.","’I need to find a way to fix this,’ Chen Yi thought. He had to get through the Xiao Family’s investigation somehow.","If his identity were exposed, he could forget about expanding Hundred Herbs Hall. It would only bring a host of unnecessary problems.","Perhaps sensing that he wasn’t really listening, Xiao Wan’er trailed off. Still hesitant to meet his gaze after what had happened earlier, she glanced in his direction.","\"Brother-in-law, do you think there’s a problem with Hundred Herbs Hall?\"","Chen Yi snapped out of his thoughts and met her gaze, smiling as he shook his head.","\"My apologies, Sister-in-law. I was just lost in thought about something.\"","Xiao Wan’er turned her head, feigning a casual air as she picked up a piece of pastry and nibbled on it. \"What was it?\"","\"If Elder Master Xiao is so concerned and needs to spend time and silver coins maintaining all these relationships, why not just have Hundred Herbs Hall offer a larger share of the profits?\"","\"Grandfather had a similar idea, but I turned it down.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"After all, Boss Chen was the one who proposed the arrangement. And his Hundred Herbs Hall helped us before. It wouldn’t be right to put him in a difficult position now.\"","After hearing Xiao Wan’er’s explanation, Chen Yi understood. She didn’t want to be ungrateful and cast someone aside after they had been helpful.","A warmth spread through his chest, but he couldn’t help but sigh.","’She’s just like Elder Master Xiao.’","Xiao Wan’er was too kind-hearted. Whether with family or outsiders, in business or in her personal life, she always put others first.","It was an admirable quality, but...","without others looking out for her, she was bound to be taken advantage of.","They chatted for a little while longer before finishing dinner.","Seeing a lot of food still left on the table, Xiao Wan’er belatedly asked, \"Brother-in-law, did you not have much of an appetite today?\"","Chen Yi made up an excuse to brush off her question.","’It wasn’t that he didn’t want to eat more; he was simply stuffed.’","Besides, with Xie Tingyun and Shen Huatang present, he couldn’t very well use his Four Symbols Skill to aid his digestion.","He had already forced himself to eat as much as Xiao Wuge; that was a feat in itself.","After a short rest, Chen Yi took Xiaodie and Xiao Wuge back to Spring Lotus Garden. From a distance, he waved, gesturing for Xiao Wan’er not to stay out in the cold.","Xiao Wan’er smiled and waved back, watching until their figures disappeared into Spring Lotus Garden before she returned to her wooden house.","When she saw the chopsticks still in Cui’er’s hand, her mind drifted back to what had happened earlier, and she couldn’t help but touch her smooth, fair forehead.","Her hand was cool, but for some reason, her forehead felt warm to the touch.","’My brother-in-law... he really is... far more remarkable than Boss Chen.’","「Inside Spring Lotus Garden.」","Chen Yi, of course, had no idea that Xiao Wan’er was comparing him with himself.","After washing up and changing his clothes, he, Xiao Wuge, and Xiaodie each went back to their own rooms to rest.","It had been a long day, and only now could he finally, truly relax.","By now, the rain had eased slightly.","The thunder and lightning had stopped, and the wind had died down considerably.","Still, the sound of drizzling rain and the croaking of frogs in the pond filled Spring Lotus Garden, adding a little life to the quiet, rainy night.","Chen Yi stood by the window for a moment before sitting cross-legged on his bed to begin his Cultivation of the Four Symbols Skill.","’Judging by the time, Liu Lang probably hasn’t set out for Liu Wen’s location yet.’","’I hope everything goes smoothly for him.’","...","「Just past ten o’clock at night.」","The downpour over Shu State City had ceased.","Only a sparse drizzle remained, carried by a cool wind that chilled the faces of the few pedestrians out on the streets.","Liu Lang, however, didn’t feel the chill. He was focused only on concealing his movements as he hurried toward Kangning Street in North City.","He had left early, so he was still wearing a Raincoat and a bamboo hat. The straw rustled softly whenever he moved.","He had also just acquired a fine new Blade, and he couldn’t resist drawing it for a look every so often, the CLANG of steel mixing with the rustle of his Raincoat.","If the streets hadn’t been mostly empty, and if he hadn’t known to avoid the patrolling City Guard and Imprisonment Officers, he would have been stopped long ago.","Luckily, he made it without incident. After more than half an hour, he finally arrived outside the residence where Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue were staying, having come from Hundred Herbs Hall.","Liu Lang scanned the area, noting the guards at the entrance. He curled his lip in disdain, then circled around to the side and slipped into the compound.","Even if the Noble Families had money and men, when it came to Martial Arts, their guards and Nursing Homes were mostly just Lower Three Grades Martial Artists.","The few powerful ones were personal bodyguards to the young masters and ladies of the family; they would never be posted on simple guard duty outside.","As a result, Liu Lang managed to sneak deep into the residence without encountering a single Guard he considered worthy of a second glance.","However, even though this was just a temporary residence for Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue, the estate was still quite large.","It had three courtyards on both the left and right sides, with a rear garden set apart by a covered walkway."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195 - 178: If Someone’s Going to Be Bad, It’s Me...","paragraphs":["It was nothing short of luxurious.","So much so that it took Liu Lang a considerable amount of time to figure out where Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue were staying.","’Liu Wen in the west, Liu Zhaoxue in the east... I can’t be wrong.’","Liu Lang lay prone on a surrounding wall, surveying the area for a moment before flipping over into the western rear residence and quietly making his way toward the wing.","As he drew near, he abruptly stopped, then ducked behind a nearby tree.","The next moment, he heard a CREAK.","A hundred feet away, the door to a wooden building opened, and a figure emerged.","It wasn’t the slender Liu Wen, but Liu Zhaoxue, dressed in a long red gown.","Liu Lang glanced over. ’What kind of strange customs does the Liu Family have?’ he cursed inwardly. Just as he was about to head for the other rear residence, he heard a voice from behind him:","\"Come out.\"","’Hm?’","Liu Lang froze. ’Have I been discovered?’","Before he could investigate further, he heard another voice from behind him:","\"Miss Zhaoxue, I trust you’ve been well.\"","The voice belonged to a man, low and tinged with malice.","\"It’s you?\"","Unable to contain his curiosity, Liu Lang tilted his head, sneaking a peek out of the corner of his eye.","He saw a figure dressed in black, only their eyes visible, crouching on the eaves of the wooden building and staring down at Liu Zhaoxue.","’How strange. There’s someone else hiding here?’","Liu Lang thought to himself, worried he might be seen. At the same time, he couldn’t help but suspect the man was one of Black Tooth’s people.","After all, Chen Yi had warned him to watch out for Black Tooth sending someone to the Liu Family to verify the marriage alliance with the Xiao Family.","Just as he was mulling this over, he heard Liu Zhaoxue speak.","\"You came looking for me at this hour. Aren’t you afraid my Second Brother will find you?\"","The man in black said in a low voice, \"What’s there to be afraid of?\"","\"That bastard Liu Wen has Wen Yu with him right now. Why would he care about his paternal half-sister?\"","\"Instead of worrying about him, Miss Zhaoxue, you should be worrying about yourself.\"","\"What do I have to worry about?\"","\"Heh. Do you even believe that yourself?\"","\"...\"","Liu Zhaoxue’s delicate brows knitted together. She looked up at him and said, \"Why don’t you just say what you came here for.\"","The man in black let out a hoarse laugh. \"I’m here to help you, Miss Zhaoxue. Why do you even have to ask?\"","\"Help me?\"","\"You said you’d help me last time, but in the end, Liu Wen is still responsible for Xinglin Hall’s expansion into Shu State.\"","\"I’m sure Miss Zhaoxue is aware that the Liu Family’s Sixth Young Master accomplished nothing and ended up dead in Shu State... That was an accident. It had nothing to do with us.\"","Liu Zhaoxue let out a noncommittal snort, clearly unconvinced.","After a moment of silence,","she asked, \"Tell me. How does your Five Poison Sect plan to help me this time?\"","Hearing this, the man in black chuckled. \"Now that’s more like it.\"","\"Miss Zhaoxue, you should be well aware that you can’t even protect yourself right now. Without outside help, you’ll end up worse off than Xiao Jinghong.\"","\"She, at least, is the commander of the Dingyuan Army and holds military power. As for you...\"","\"I reckon you’ll just be married off by the Liu Family to another family for an alliance.\"","Liu Zhaoxue ignored him and pressed on, \"If you’re only here to spout nonsense, you can leave now.\"","\"Don’t be in such a hurry.\"","After a pause, the man in black quickened his speech. \"Someone’s coming. It’s inconvenient today. I’ll come find you again tomorrow night, same time.\"","\"When I do, I hope Miss Zhaoxue won’t be as cold and distant as you were tonight.\"","Before the man’s voice had faded, Liu Lang heard a faint whoosh through the air.","Apparently, the man in black had already left.","Liu Lang’s expression was a little strange, and he couldn’t help but mutter to himself.","’The Five Poison Sect?’","’Weren’t they wiped out decades ago by the Mountain Race Matriarch and her people?’","’To think they’d reappear in the Jianghu now... Tsk, it seems the Jianghu of Shu State is about to get turbulent.’","Despite these thoughts, Liu Lang didn’t dwell on it.","After all, he wasn’t of the Mountain Race and had no conflict with the Five Poison Sect. He couldn’t be bothered with the affairs of those Evil Demons.","’Still,’ he thought, ’it seems this Third Miss of the Liu Family from Jing State is more than she appears.’","Cooperating with the Five Poison Sect was akin to making a deal with the devil.","The fact that she dared to do it meant her courage alone surpassed that of many others.","「Not long after.」","Two figures walked in from outside the residence. One was a tall, slender man whose handsome face had a sinister cast to it.","The other was a woman, and judging by her attire, she was no mere maid.","Liu Zhaoxue saw them. \"It’s so late. Second Brother, why aren’t you resting in your wing? What brings you here?\"","’Second Brother, Liu Wen?’","Liu Lang took a look, memorized the man’s face, and remained carefully hidden.","Then he heard Liu Wen say, \"Second Uncle sent someone over just now. He told us to get ready.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Father sent a letter. He said this conflict with the Xiao Family must come to an end. He’s ordered us to take his letter to Old Marquis Xiao and go to the Xiao Family estate tomorrow.\"","Liu Zhaoxue was taken aback. \"Is Father trying to provoke the Old Marquis?\"","\"The letter doesn’t say, and Second Uncle didn’t mention its contents. I reckon Father wants us to assess the situation and act accordingly when we get there.\"","\"I see. And here I was, thinking Father would grant Second Brother’s wish and send a letter to propose marriage to the Xiao Family.\"","\"Heh... you never know...\""]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196 - 179: Dao Realm True Intent","paragraphs":["’A marriage proposal?’","’The Jing State Liu Family really wants to form a marriage alliance with the Xiao Family?’","Liu Lang recalled what Chen Yi had said at the Spring Rain Building and couldn’t help but feel amazed.","’Looks like the Boss is even more capable than I imagined.’","’He even knows about something as secret as the dealings between the Liu Family and the Xiao Family.’","’Now the Boss’s cover as a retainer for the Liu Family is solid. No one will be able to see through it.’","Just as Liu Lang was mulling this over, he heard Liu Zhaoxue ask, \"What time are we going tomorrow?\"","Liu Wen smiled. \"Naturally, we’ll go at noon, when the most people are out.\"","\"Aren’t you worried the Xiao Mansion won’t open its main gates for us, Second Brother?\"","\"Heh heh, whether I’m worried or not, Second Uncle is there to take the lead.\"","\"Our generation is too far removed from the Old Marquis. If he’s truly that rude, it’s the Xiao Family that will lose face when word gets out.\"","As Liu Wen spoke, he seemed to have just remembered something and pointed to the woman beside him, saying:","\"I forgot to introduce you.\"","\"This is Lady Yu Zhen. Second Uncle specially sought her out from Third Uncle to be your Maid.\"","The woman named Yu Zhen gracefully stepped forward and curtsied. \"This servant, Yu Zhen, greets the Third Young Miss.\"","Liu Zhaoxue sized her up briefly and nodded. \"Thank you, Second Brother.\"","Liu Wen chuckled. \"You’re thanking the wrong person. You should be thanking Second Uncle.\"","\"Oh, then Zhaoxue misunderstood. I thought it was Second Brother who asked Second Uncle to send someone to protect me.\"","\"You could see it that way, I suppose. Heh heh.\"","\"Yu Zhen, hurry up and go to Zhaoxue’s side.\"","\"This servant obeys...\"","Listening to the two of them trade veiled barbs, even someone as unobservant as Liu Lang could tell that the relationship between these Liu Family siblings was not harmonious.","When he also recalled the members of the Five Poison Sect who had come looking for Liu Zhaoxue earlier, a playful smile touched his lips.","’I wonder if the Boss would be interested in this news.’","’He probably would be.’","Not long after, Liu Wen smiled and took his leave. Liu Zhaoxue stood silently in the courtyard for a moment before leading Yu Zhen back to the wooden building without a word.","Without hesitation, Liu Lang silently followed Liu Wen all the way back to a rear residence in the eastern part of the estate.","He followed him until Liu Wen entered a wooden building.","After checking the surroundings and confirming that the guards were only posted outside, Liu Lang finally approached the building.","He pressed his ear against the wall and listened for a moment.","He could faintly hear bursts of delicate laughter, which made it clear that Liu Wen was not alone inside.","’Looks like this Liu Wen is quite the womanizer.’","’Just like me... Tsk.’","After some thought, Liu Lang gently knocked on the door three times.","KNOCK, KNOCK-KNOCK.","The soft sound carried clearly into the building.","The delicate laughter stopped abruptly, followed by Liu Wen’s slightly displeased voice, \"Who’s out there?\"","\"I... am Liu Er. My apologies for disturbing you so late at night, Young Master Liu.\"","\"Who are you? What are you here for?\"","\"I’ve come specifically to relay a message to Young Master Liu on behalf of my master.\"","\"Oh?\"","As soon as the words were out, Liu Lang heard the sound of light footsteps from within. He simply pulled his bamboo hat lower and stood quietly under the eaves.","The door creaked open.","Just as Liu Lang was about to look up, he suddenly felt a sinister, icy aura wash over him.","Without a second thought, his hand was already gripping the long blade at his waist.","SHIING.","The blade was drawn three inches.","Its cold gleam cut through the darkness, illuminating the area in front of the wooden building.","It also shone on Liu Wen, who was charging forward with his sword raised.","\"Great Success?\"","Liu Wen stopped in his tracks, then took three steps back, a hint of apprehension on his sinisterly delicate face.","Liu Lang tilted his head up slightly, his eyes staring at him from under the brim of his bamboo hat.","\"Young Master Liu, I meant no offense. I hope you will forgive me.\"","With that, he sheathed his long blade.","Even so, Liu Wen still watched him for a moment before a smile finally appeared on his grim face.","Although the smile wasn’t exactly warm, his aura finally calmed down.","\"Brother Liu Er, what an impressive Saber Technique. This young master is truly impressed.\"","\"Come, this is no place to talk. Follow me to the study.\"","Liu Lang bowed his head slightly and refused in a calm tone, \"There’s no need. I will leave once I’ve said my piece.\"","A flash of displeasure crossed Liu Wen’s eyes, but he kept the smile on his face as he asked, \"You just said you came to deliver a message for your master? Might I ask who your master is?\"","\"My master is Black Tooth of the Bright Moon Building.\"","To prove his identity, Liu Lang deliberately took out his Bright Moon Building Identity Token and showed it to him.","\"I was sent this time only to relay a single message to Young Master Liu—my master will visit you tomorrow evening at the hour of Xu to discuss a matter.\"","\"Oh, Black Tooth... No wonder Brother Liu Er possesses such a Sword Realm.\"","Liu Wen’s gaze swept over the Token, and he nodded slightly.","He had, of course, heard the name Black Tooth. He knew Black Tooth was an Elder of the Bright Moon Building and the person in charge of the black market in the Shu State region.","At the same time, he also knew that his sixth brother, Liu Jing, had previously cooperated with Black Tooth to plot against the Xiao Family.","Unfortunately, they ultimately failed.","After a moment of silence, Liu Wen sheathed his Long Sword and asked with a smile, \"And what matter does your master wish to discuss with this young master?\"","Liu Lang paused. Recalling Chen Yi’s instructions, he bowed slightly and said, \"You will find out tomorrow night.\"","With that, he tapped his toes lightly, his entire body turning into a black shadow as he flashed out of the residence and fled into the distance.","Seeing that he had vanished without a trace, the smile on Liu Wen’s face gradually disappeared, and a frigid, biting aura emanated from him.","\"Black Tooth, Bright Moon Building...\"","The words had barely left his lips when two voluptuous women in revealing clothes walked over.","\"Young Master, that man was so scary.\"","Liu Wen glanced at them and grinned. \"Did you... hear what he just said?\"","One of the women nodded timidly and pouted, \"Something about Black Tooth, Bright Moon Building...\"","Before she could finish, the tip of a sword suddenly appeared through her back. It was slowly withdrawn as she stood there, stunned.","Seeing this, the other woman immediately cowered in fear.","\"Y-Young Master, you... I, I-I-I don’t know anything.\"","Liu Wen sheathed his Long Sword, the coldness on his face vanishing instantly. He smiled, walked over, and wrapped his arm around her, leading her toward the side room.","As they walked, he comforted her with a smile, \"This young master prefers girls who are a little stupid and a little obedient, don’t you think?\"","\"Yes, yes, I’m stupid...\"","’Black Tooth, I’d like to see just what tricks you have up your sleeve.’","’I hope whatever you have to say is worth the life of that beauty.’","...","The night passed without incident.","The rain stopped at midnight, and the gloomy clouds dispersed.","After dawn broke in the east, the skies above Shu State Prefecture City were clear and vast.","The area was already known for its beautiful mountains and clear waters, the air filled with the fragrance of plants and trees.","After being nourished by the rain, that faint fragrance was now mingled with a fresh, natural scent.","This was especially true in the lush Spring Lotus Garden.","At least, that’s how the courtyard would be before the sun was high in the sky and revealed the oppressive summer heat.","Early in the morning, Xiaodie was bustling about.","She swept the fallen leaves from the courtyard, cleared the weeds from the pond, washed and hung the clothes of Xiao Wuge and Chen Yi to dry, and deftly cleaned the two wooden buildings...","After busying herself for more than an hour, Xiaodie finally wiped the fine beads of sweat from her forehead, but she didn’t feel tired in the slightest.","She stood with her hands on her hips, looking at the clean and tidy courtyard, a smile gracing her pretty face.","\"Time to call the Young Master and the Young Master-in-law for breakfast.\"","This morning, the kitchen had made her favorite griddle cakes, served with chili sauce from Guangyuan and dried fish from Jiao State. They were delicious.","Every time she thought about it, her mouth would start to water.","Xiaodie glanced at the neatly arranged breakfast on the table, swallowed unconsciously, and then quickened her pace, jogging up the stairs.","As was her routine, she first went to help Xiao Wuge wash up and get dressed before heading to Chen Yi’s room.","She carried a basin of warm water in her hands with a towel draped over her shoulder, yet she still moved with a light and quick gait.","She carefully pushed open the door, poked her head in, and saw Chen Yi sitting cross-legged on the bed.","’Is the Young Master-in-law meditating?’","Xiaodie looked at the calm-faced Chen Yi with a vague understanding, then gently placed the warm water next to the washstand.","CLICK.","A soft sound rang out.","Chen Yi’s eyes twitched slightly. He slowly opened them, met Xiaodie’s gaze, and asked with a smile, \"What time is it?\"","Seeing that she had woken him up after all, Xiaodie stuck out her tongue sheepishly and said, \"Young Master-in-law, it’s already past the middle of the hour of Yin.\"","Chen Yi said, \"Oh,\" got out of bed, stretched his limbs, and then let her help him get dressed.","Xiaodie nodded with a smile, went to the wardrobe, and asked him about his plans for the day as she rummaged through it.","She was probably trying to figure out if he was going out so she could decide whether he needed to dress more formally.","Chen Yi was just about to reply that he was staying in the mansion when a few lines of text floated across the light screen that had just appeared before him:","[Daily Intelligence · Profound-rank Lower Grade: At noon, in the Qingjing Residence of the Xiao Mansion, a group from the Jing State Liu Family will come to visit Duke Dingyuan, Xiao Yuan. A small amount of Opportunity may be obtained.]","After a quick scan, Chen Yi paused and then instructed, \"Get me a slightly more formal long robe. I’m going to Qingjing Residence to pay my respects to the Old Master today.\"","Xiaodie replied with a \"Yes,\" and took out a light blue brocade robe from the wardrobe, also finding a Jade Belt, a sachet, and other accessories to help him dress.","\"Young Master-in-law, it really has been a while since you’ve been to Qingjing Residence.\"","\"A while back, some people in the mansion were gossiping, saying that now that you’re an Academy Master and have gained great fame, you’ve become a bit arrogant.\"","\"Is that so?\"","While cooperating by raising his arms and legs, Chen Yi pondered who from the Jing State Liu Family was coming and what their purpose was.","’If it’s Liu Yu, it’s likely related to the summer grain tax of the Three Towns.’","’If Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue are among them, then the Jing State Liu Family probably hasn’t given up on the marriage alliance.’","However, Chen Yi actually hoped it would be Liu Wen.","’That way, I can go have a look and a listen. It’ll be good preparation for tonight’s meeting.’","After a simple breakfast, Chen Yi thought for a moment, then went to his study and wrote a piece of calligraphy for the Old Master.","From the look Sun Fu gave him before leaving yesterday, the Old Master already knew that his Calligraphy Dao had improved.","Sending over a piece of calligraphy now was a perfect opportunity.","However, compared to the birthday verse he wrote for the Old Master’s grand birthday last time, Chen Yi only wrote four words this time:","\"Tranquility and foresight.\"","As the brush fell, the ink turned to gold, and a Mental Realm emerged—amidst continuous mountains and waters, ripples flowed around the mountains, serenely drifting toward the horizon.","There were no people, no voices.","This was the second time Chen Yi had displayed his Calligraphy Dao after reaching Perfection.","Compared to the poem he wrote for Sun Fu, \"Farewell to Duke Changming in Shu State,\" these four words, \"Tranquility and foresight,\" were what truly matched his free-spirited and casual state of mind.","When the Mental Realm manifested, any observer would feel as if they were physically there.","Furthermore, under the influence of the Heaven and Earth Spiritual Qi, they would also feel their minds calm and pacify, which could be considered a form of enlightenment.","Chen Yi held the Yunsong Paper and examined it carefully. As understanding dawned on him, a smile couldn’t help but appear on his face:","\"So the Calligraphy Dao has such a marvelous effect.\"","Just a few words, when written, possessed the power to influence the minds of others, a clear demonstration of Dao Realm True Intent.","’Perhaps after achieving Perfection in the Martial Arts Fist, spear, and blade, I’ll gain a similar power.’","’When the Mental Realm unfolds, I could use \"True Martial Intent\" to overwhelm the minds of others.’","Mulling over these things, Chen Yi waited for the ink on the paper to dry, then rolled it up and placed it in a brocade box.","He then tidied up a bit, called for Xiao Wuge, and instructed Xiaodie to remain at Spring Lotus Garden. Then, holding the brocade box, he headed for Qingjing Residence.","At this moment, the hour of Mao had just passed, so it was still a long time until noon.","Chen Yi chose to go at this time because he planned to stay at Qingjing Residence for a while.","This would also fulfill Sun Fu’s advice—to interact more with the Old Master.","Beyond that, he also intended to probe some of the Old Master’s thoughts.","For instance, his opinion of him, or his future plans for the Xiao Family.","Xiao Wuge didn’t know about any of this. Seeing Chen Yi holding the brocade box, he thought he should also bring a gift for the Old Master, so he first pulled him on a detour to Jiaxing Garden.","Naturally, Chen Yi didn’t refuse.","Who would have thought that upon arriving at Jiaxing Garden, he would see Xiao Wan’er looking somewhat exasperated.","\"A lot of invitation cards were delivered to the mansion today. They’re all for you.\"","\"Who are they from?\"","\"Are you going to see them?\"","Chen Yi replied as if it were the most natural thing in the world, \"Of course not.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wan’er couldn’t help but chide him playfully, \"You’re asking for a beating.\""]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197 - 180: Brother-in-law, Don’t Get Any Funny Ideas","paragraphs":["Fighting them was, of course, out of the question.","But Xiao Wan’er did have a bit of a headache dealing with the young ladies and madams from the noble families who tried every trick in the book to pay her a visit.","Although their status, family background, and prestige were no match for the Xiao Family’s, they all had connections of some sort and were tied to the Xiao Family by a complex web of relationships.","Among them, only Madam Tang came to the Xiao residence simply to foster a closer relationship, as her son was already studying under Chen Yi.","The rest mostly wanted to pull some strings, hoping that one of the Xiao Family’s influential figures would put in a good word and persuade Chen Yi to let their children study the Calligraphy Dao under him.","That, at least, was manageable. Xiao Wan’er could always find a way to tactfully refuse them.","At worst, she could use Chen Yi as an excuse, saying his energy was limited.","Or she could bring up Xiao Jinghong, explaining that with her second sister not yet having returned, her brother-in-law rarely socialized.","But every time these people came to visit, they would bring gifts.","Those from less wealthy families would bring inexpensive items, like blankets or ivory from Poshisu Country.","The wealthier ones would often bring cartloads of rare trinkets, with no shortage of gold and silver jewelry.","Accepting these items was awkward, but so was refusing them.","Xiao Wan’er had even specifically sought out the Old Marquis about this. Only after he told her to accept everything did she know what to do.","She briefly explained the situation.","Xiao Wan’er looked at Chen Yi and asked softly, \"This can’t go on, don’t you think?\"","Chen Yi met her gaze and, after a moment of thought, said, \"You’re right. We need a permanent solution.\"","Her heart stirred, and she couldn’t help but remind him, \"Most of the people who come to visit are close to the Xiao Family.\"","\"Some are old subordinates of Grandfather and Father, others are close to the second and third branches of the family, and many are just the womenfolk. Perhaps...\"","\"Perhaps their methods are inappropriate, but their intentions are for the sake of their children. They’re not wicked people.\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Yi was exasperated. \"What are you worried about?\"","\"Do I look like the kind of person who would bully them?\"","’He does.’","Xiao Wan’er supplied the thought in her mind, inevitably recalling a few things Chen Yi had done in the past.","Running away on his wedding day.","Visiting Yanhua Lane after being confined.","Pretending to abduct a commoner’s daughter to help the Third Place Scholar.","And writing that poem for her...","Each and every one of those incidents could be considered scandalous and unconventional.","It made Xiao Wan’er worry that Chen Yi might come up with some bizarre scheme that would put his visitors in an impossible situation.","\"It’s best not to offend them too much, to avoid giving people something to gossip about.\"","\"Don’t worry, don’t worry.\"","Chen Yi readily agreed. Seeing it was getting late, he took Xiao Wuge and left Jiaxing Garden, heading straight for Qingjing Residence.","Xiao Wan’er watched them until they were out of sight before pulling back her gaze, a faint smile gracing her lips.","Beside her, Cui’er and Juan’er exchanged a glance before asking, \"Miss, should we accept all these visiting cards?\"","Xiao Wan’er hummed in affirmation, then collected herself and instructed, \"Accept them all.\"","\"But stagger the times. Some people will need to be separated.\"","\"Schedule Miss Wan and Miss Li for the same time. Madam Tang and Madam Xie are of similar status, so put them together as well...\"","Until Chen Yi came up with a solution, she had to handle things carefully to prevent people from gossiping about him.","After all, they wouldn’t dare say anything against the Xiao Family.","「Meanwhile.」","Chen Yi had a rough idea of what Xiao Wan’er was thinking. He felt a sense of gratification, along with a touch of gratitude toward her.","He was the one who had caused this situation, after all.","He couldn’t just keep letting the Xiao Family and people like Mr. Yue Ming of Guiyun Academy take the heat for him.","But some matters were more urgent than others.","Right now, his priority was dealing with Black Tooth and his men. Refusing the visits from the various nobles of Shu State could wait a few days.","「Not long after.」","Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge passed through the gatehouse into the central courtyard, then turned into a long, covered corridor.","Glancing around, he saw Uncle Gui sweeping fallen leaves in an open area of the courtyard.","Come to think of it, Chen Yi hadn’t seen Uncle Gui in some time.","The same went for Ge the Third and Liu Si’er. It was as if they had been deliberately avoiding him; he hadn’t seen them in ages.","But upon careful reflection...","Chen Yi knew in his heart—these Hidden Guards each had their own missions.","Ge the Third was coordinating with Xiao Dongchen and Lou Yuxue on the plan to burn the summer grain supply of the Three Towns.","Liu Si’er, having just recovered from his injuries, was now inspecting the Xiao Family’s five Medicine Halls with Wang Lixing.","Xiao Dongchen was at the Governor’s Office, handling the collection of the summer grain tax from all over Shu State, just like Chen Yunfan and Li Huai’gu.","Only Uncle Gui remained at the residence.","As Chen Yi pondered this, he couldn’t help but glance over again, just in time to meet the eyes of Uncle Gui, who had straightened up to look his way.","The man seemed surprised, as if not expecting to see Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge, and only lowered his head after a brief pause.","Noting the man’s reaction, Chen Yi continued nonchalantly through the corridor.","Soon, he and Xiao Wuge arrived at Qingjing Residence.","The Armored Warriors guarding the gate hesitated for a moment, then bowed. \"Greetings, Young Master, Master Yi.\"","Seeing that Xiao Wuge didn’t slow down, Chen Yi gently pulled him back and asked with a smile,","\"Is the Old Marquis free?\"","One of the Armored Warriors didn’t answer immediately, instead glancing at Xiao Wuge before speaking.","\"Someone from the Governor’s Office came to visit early this morning. The Marquis is meeting with him now.\"","\"Oh? Who is it?\"","\"The Right Minister of the Governor’s Office, Yang Ye, and Assistant Governor Chen Yunfan.\"","Chen Yi raised an eyebrow slightly, not having expected these two.","’For the Three Towns’ grain tax?’","’It must be.’","Li Huai’gu had mentioned in his letter yesterday that the Governor’s Office’s new order was to have him collect the summer grain from the Three Towns at a one-tenth tax rate.","He reckoned that Yang Ye and Chen Yunfan’s visit to the Old Marquis today was to explain this matter.","’So Governor Liu Hong has washed his hands of this completely.’","The thought stirred something in Chen Yi.","If Yang Ye and Chen Yunfan were here for the Three Towns’ grain tax, then the people from the Jing State Liu Family who were coming later must be here for something else.","’A marriage proposal?’","’Heh.’","Xiao Wuge, however, paid no mind to these things. Hearing that it was someone from the Governor’s Office, he simply stood quietly outside the gate with Chen Yi to wait.","But he was fidgeting restlessly, occasionally shifting the brocade box in his hands. He was clearly eager to present the gift he had chosen for the Old Marquis as soon as possible.","After waiting for about an hour, just past mid-morning, two sets of footsteps could be heard from within Qingjing Residence.","Faintly, Chen Yi could hear his brother, Chen Yunfan, muttering and complaining.","\"...I knew this would be the result.\"","\"Lord Left Envoy Liu forcing us to deliver that kind of message... The fact that the Old Marquis didn’t just throw us out already shows how magnanimous he is.\"","\"Yunfan, calm down. Whatever arrangements Lord Liu makes, you just have to carry them out.\"","\"Lord Yang, it’s easy for you to say! You have nothing to worry about, but I’m just a newcomer here. I have to spend the next few years in Shu State. How can I afford to offend the Old Marquis?\"","\"Heh, you just need to deliver the message. I’m sure Marquis Xiao won’t hold it against you.\"","\"I hope... Hmm? Brother Yi?\"","Catching sight of Chen Yi around the corner, Chen Yunfan’s impatient tone vanished, replaced by a smile.","Luckily, he remembered Xiao Wuge was also present. While winking and making faces at Chen Yi, he properly bowed to Xiao Wuge.","\"This subordinate greets the Young Master.\"","Xiao Wuge put on a serious expression and replied, \"Assistant Governor Chen.\"","He then bowed to Yang Ye along with Chen Yi, greeting him.","After they straightened up, Chen Yi glanced around, then patted Xiao Wuge on the shoulder, signaling for him to go into Qingjing Residence first.","Chen Yunfan did the same.","Except he patted Yang Ye. \"Lord Right Envoy, please excuse me. This subordinate would like a word with Qingzhou.\"","Yang Ye naturally nodded in agreement.","However, he clearly remembered Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan talking about him behind his back at Li Huai’gu’s wedding. With a stern face, he warned them,","\"You two can talk, but watch where you are and show some propriety.\"","Chen Yi and Chen Yunfan exchanged a look and smilingly agreed.","Once Yang Ye was a good distance away, Chen Yi led Chen Yunfan to a pavilion by the pond outside Qingjing Residence to sit for a moment, and inevitably asked about his brother’s recent situation.","At the mention of this, Chen Yunfan let out a bellyful of complaints.","\"This damned Assistant Governor job is so boring. Every day, I’m either in the east of the city collecting grain taxes or in the west.\"","\"Not only do I have to collect them on time, but I can’t afford the slightest mistake.\"","\"If there’s even the slightest error, the two Governors come down on you. You have no idea how miserable it is.\"","Seeing his brother’s gloomy face, Chen Yi couldn’t help but laugh. \"Brother, you’re complaining about a position others couldn’t get even if they begged.\"","But taking a closer look, he did notice that in the few days since they’d last met, Chen Yunfan had gotten quite tan.","Clearly, he really had been rushing about outdoors lately.","Chen Yunfan pouted. \"I’d be thrilled if one of those ’others’ would push me out.\"","He paused, then turned to Chen Yi with a grin. \"Then again, I forgot how impressive Brother Yi has been lately.\"","\"How so?\"","\"Now that you’ve achieved Great Success in the Calligraphy Dao and even taught several accomplished students at Guiyun Academy, your fame is second to none right now.\"","\"I’ve heard that countless students from both inside and outside Shu State are already on their way here, all hoping to study under you.\"","Chen Yi chuckled and shook his head. \"That’s just distorted rumors. It’s not that exaggerated.\"","Chen Yunfan, of course, didn’t believe him.","He chattered on about how enviable Chen Yi’s life was now and how he’d trade places if he could.","Chen Yi selectively agreed here and there, and their conversation was no longer as tit-for-tat as it had been before.","After a bit more small talk, the smile on Chen Yunfan’s face faded. He glanced around, then leaned closer and lowered his voice.","\"Don’t say I didn’t warn you, but you should spend more time at Guiyun Academy these days.\"","\"If possible, it would be best for you to stay at the academy.\"","Chen Yi knew there was a hidden meaning in his words. \"Does this have to do with your visit to the Old Marquis today?\"","Chen Yunfan nodded without hesitation. \"The Governor’s Office is dead set on collecting the summer grain tax from the Three Towns this time.\"","\"I’m sure I don’t need to tell you what the stakes are.\"","Chen Yi murmured an \"oh.\" He was well aware that the root of this issue wasn’t the Governor’s Office, but the Jing State Liu Family wanting to test their strength against the Xiao Family.","\"Are you in a difficult position, Brother?\"","\"Not really. This matter has nothing to do with me. If that old bastard tries to drag me into it, at worst I’ll just throw down my Official Seal and walk away.\"","Hearing Chen Yunfan’s cavalier words, Chen Yi just smiled and shook his head.","\"Thank you for the warning, Brother. I know what to do.\"","\"That’s the spirit. You’re an Instructor at the academy now. The affairs inside and outside the residence have nothing to do with you. Just focus on teaching. That’s for the best.\"","Seeing it was getting late, Chen Yunfan didn’t linger and rose to take his leave.","Just then, they saw several figures enter from the central courtyard. Leading them was none other than the second son of the Jing State Liu Family, Liu Yu.","Chen Yunfan let out a surprised \"Huh?\" \"What’s that bastard doing here in Shu State?\""]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198 - 181: Serenity, Vision, and an Examination","paragraphs":["’Bastard?’","Chen Yi’s interest was piqued. Judging from Chen Yunfan’s curse, he clearly knew Liu Wen and was somewhat familiar with him.","’Ah, I’d forgotten about that.’","The Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family and the Jing State Liu Family were both prominent Noble Families of the current era, so it was only natural that they knew of each other.","Moreover, with elders from both the Chen and Liu Families serving as officials in the same imperial court, it was perfectly normal for the younger generation to associate with one another.","He figured they had probably met on a few occasions.","As Chen Yi mulled this over, he knew it wasn’t the time for idle chatter, so he held his tongue.","As Chen Yunfan looked toward Liu Wen’s group, Liu Wen, Liu Zhaoxue, and the others naturally spotted them as well.","He saw them pause in their tracks.","Liu Wen seemed a little surprised, a grin spreading across his face. \"Chen Yunfan?\"","After a moment’s hesitation, Liu Wen gestured to the people behind him and walked straight toward them, a faintly sinister smile appearing on his handsome face.","His narrow eyes, however, completely ignored Chen Yi, fixing solely on Chen Yunfan.","While still a good distance away, he smiled and spread his arms wide. \"Brother Yunfan, it’s been too long! I’ve missed you dearly.\"","Chen Yunfan shot him a sidelong glance and snorted. \"This young—ahem. This official is not familiar with you.\"","With that, he seemed to recall something. He straightened up, clasped his hands behind his back, lifted his chin, and drawled:","\"You audacious commoner! Why do you not kneel upon seeing this official?\"","The smile on Liu Wen’s face froze. He slowed his pace, and his raised hands trembled slightly.","\"Brother Yunfan, surely that’s not necessary?\"","\"What? You, Liu Wen, don’t even have the rank of a Scholar. You’re just a commoner. You are required to perform the proper ceremony upon seeing an official. Or does this official need to teach you etiquette on behalf of your Jing State Liu Family?\"","Liu Wen’s anger flared at these words, and a cold glint flashed in his narrow eyes.","\"Chen Yunfan, don’t think that just because you became the top scholar, you can disrespect my Liu Family!\"","Chen Yunfan pursed his lips. \"You are mistaken. This official simply doesn’t respect *you*.\"","\"You...\"","Now Liu Wen was utterly enraged. His previously feigned magnanimity and warmth vanished without a trace.","The disgusted look on his face, as if he’d just swallowed a fly, was so amusing that Chen Yi couldn’t help but give Chen Yunfan a mental thumbs-up.","’When it came to having a sharp tongue and infuriating people, if Chen Yunfan claimed to be second best, probably no one would dare claim first.’","Just then, Liu Zhaoxue, who was waiting in the distance, bowed gracefully in their direction.","\"Zhaoxue greets you, Lord Chen. I hope Your Lordship will not make things difficult for my second brother, for the sake of the generations of friendship between the Chen and Liu Families.\"","Hearing her voice, Chen Yunfan’s gaze fell upon Liu Zhaoxue, and his eyes immediately brightened.","He then dropped his haughty act and said with a cheerful laugh:","\"Zhaoxue, you worry too much. I was merely joking with your second brother just now.\"","\"Isn’t that right, Liming?\"","Liu Wen, however, was not having any of it. He shot Chen Yunfan a glare and turned to leave.","Moreover, after rejoining the rest of the Liu Family’s group, he even snapped at Liu Zhaoxue, \"Did I ask you to speak up?\"","\"...My apologies, Second Brother.\"","\"Hmph. I’ll teach you a lesson about your place when we get back.\"","With that, Liu Wen, his face dark, followed the Xiao Mansion’s second steward toward Qingjing Residence.","Seeing this, Liu Zhaoxue hesitated for a moment. She gave Chen Yunfan and Chen Yi another apologetic bow before hurrying to catch up.","As he watched them walk away, the smile on Chen Yunfan’s face faded, and he said with a slight frown:","\"That Liu Wen is a real piece of work. He’s definitely up to no good coming to Shu State.\"","Upon hearing this, Chen Yi thought for a moment and asked, \"How does he compare to Liu Jing?\"","\"Who’s Liu Jing?\"","\"...\"","Chen Yunfan clearly had no memory of the man. After wracking his brain for a long moment, he gave up.","\"In any case,\" he said, \"Liu Wen is not a good person. You should stay far away from him.\"","Chen Yi smiled and nodded, but he sighed internally.","’I’d love to stay away from Liu Wen, but unfortunately, he’s not just a piece of work—he’s the type that sticks to you like glue.’","After a few more words of idle chat, Chen Yunfan decided not to stay any longer. He told Chen Yi to join him for a meal at Tingyu Pavilion when he had time, then hurried off.","Chen Yi agreed and watched him go.","He stood silently for a moment.","Seeing that it was getting late, he straightened his clothes and began walking at a leisurely pace toward Qingjing Residence.","’Since some things are unavoidable, there’s no point in trying to hide from them.’","’They just need to be dealt with.’","「A moment later.」","When Chen Yi arrived at Qingjing Residence, he immediately spotted Xiao Wuge waiting in the pavilion, which made him raise an eyebrow.","’The Liu Family is here, but the Old Master didn’t have Xiao Wuge stay in the main hall?’","As this thought crossed his mind, he glanced toward the main hall.","He was surprised to find that the doors to the hall, which should have been wide open, were now closed.","’It looks like they’re discussing something in secret.’","’Strange.’","According to the etiquette of the times, one should be open and have nothing to hide.","When guests came to call, unless they were close relatives or it was for a banquet, the host family would typically leave the main doors wide open.","This was a symbol of being open and aboveboard.","The current situation, however, naturally made him suspicious.","Just then, Xiao Wuge saw him approaching. He stood up and waved. \"Brother-in-law! Brother-in-law! Over here!\"","Chen Yi snapped out of his thoughts, smiled and nodded, then went to sit with him in the pavilion.","After a moment’s thought, he asked in a casual tone, \"Did you give the gift to the Old Master?\"","Xiao Wuge nodded and said with a smile, \"Grandpa was very happy. He even praised me for being so thoughtful.\"","But his smile quickly faded, and he pouted. \"It’s a shame some bad guys showed up right after. They kept me from talking more with Grandpa.\"","\"Bad guys?\"","\"Yeah! The same bad guy who said he wanted to marry my big sister. He had such a long face. You can tell he’s no good just by looking at him.\"","Chen Yi chuckled at his words, his eyes glancing toward the main hall.","’With Liu Wen’s Martial Arts Cultivation,’ he mused, ’he should be able to hear us from over there.’","After a moment’s consideration, Chen Yi smiled and said, \"You’re right. He certainly doesn’t seem like a good person.\""]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199 - 181: Tranquility, Reaching Far, Examination (Part 2)","paragraphs":["\"But you don’t have to worry. The Old Marquis sees everything with perfect clarity. There’s no way he’ll be fooled.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Wuge nodded with a solemn air.","\"Right. Grandpa already rejected that Uncle Liu last time. If those bad people dare to bring it up again, the result will be the same.\"","\"In any case, we can’t let them get what they want.\"","\"Right...?\"","Just as Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge were openly bad-mouthing Liu Wen...","Liu Wen, who was already sitting unhappily in the main hall, heard their voices and instinctively clenched his fists.","’How outrageous!’","’Xiao Wuge, and... his brother-in-law?’","’The brother-in-law Xiao Wuge mentioned must be Xiao Jinghong’s husband—that live-in son-in-law of the Xiao Family!’","’I think his name is Chen Yi, from the Jiangnan Prefecture Chen Family. He... Hmm?’","As the realization hit him, Liu Wen grew even more furious.","He had just been humiliated by Chen Yunfan, and now he was being insulted behind his back by this disgraceful live-in son-in-law.","’Are they treating me like a total pushover?!’","’If he didn’t have to focus on the important matter at hand, he would have made that live-in son-in-law pay!’","But while a storm raged in his heart, Liu Wen’s expression betrayed nothing.","He simply sat quietly in the hall, looking up at Old Marquis Xiao in the seat of honor with a slight smile on his lips.","At that moment, the Old Marquis was reading the letter in his hand, his expression placid.","But upon closer inspection, a flicker of surprise could be seen in his cloudy eyes.","「After a long while.」","Old Marquis Xiao set the letter down, slowly folded it away, and looked at Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue.","\"Aside from this letter, did your father have any other messages for me?\"","Liu Wen smiled, shaking his head before nodding. \"My father did not, but before I came to visit you, my Second and Third Uncles both gave me instructions.\"","\"Jing State and Shu State are neighbors. If the Xiao and Liu Families work together, both will benefit. If we are divided... while it might not lead to mutual destruction, it would be a terrible shame.\"","\"To use my Third Uncle’s own words, the Southern Barbarians are currently consumed by internal conflict and have no time to look north.\"","\"But once they resolve their internal disputes, they will likely stage a comeback. When that happens, you, Marquis, and my Third Uncle will be the first to bear the brunt.\"","At this, Liu Wen paused. Seeing that the Old Marquis’s expression was unreadable, he continued.","\"If you and my Third Uncle are dragged into it, that means both the Xiao and Liu Families will be swept up in war.\"","\"If we can join forces, our chances of repelling the Barbarian Race when they invade will surely be much greater.\"","His words were not without reason.","And they did, in fact, strike at the heart of the Xiao Family’s concerns.","Or more precisely, the concerns of Old Marquis Xiao and the main branch of the Xiao Family.","However, the Old Marquis was well aware of the intention behind Liu Hong’s words and knew full well what the Jing State Liu Family was planning.","After a moment of thought, a smile appeared on the Old Marquis’s face. Shaking his head, he said, \"There’s no fighting old age, I’m afraid.\"","Just as Liu Wen thought the marquis was about to offer some praise, he heard him continue, \"I should take my afternoon nap now. I won’t keep you for a meal. Please, be on your way.\"","\"Er...\"","Liu Wen was taken aback. He exchanged a look with Liu Zhaoxue, then hesitantly rose and bowed.","\"Does the Marquis have a message for me to take back?\"","But the Old Marquis merely waved a hand and, with the help of the second steward, rose and started walking toward a side chamber.","As he walked, he muttered to himself, \"Getting old, getting old.\"","Seeing this, Liu Wen felt a surge of displeasure. Gritting his teeth, he bowed and said:","\"My apologies, Marquis, but my elders instructed me before I came that I absolutely must bring back your reply.\"","\"I implore you, Marquis, for the sake of my father and my aunt, do not make things difficult for me.\"","The moment he said this, Liu Zhaoxue thought to herself, ’This is bad.’","Before she could salvage the situation, Old Marquis Xiao stopped in his tracks. With his back still to them, he said:","\"And why would I make things difficult for you?\"","\"Even if your elders came here themselves, I would still eat when it is time to eat and sleep when it is time to sleep. What could they possibly say to change that?\"","As angry as he was, Liu Wen knew he had misspoken and hurriedly bowed.","\"Forgive me, Marquis. In my anxiety, I lost my composure...\"","Before he could finish, the Old Marquis resumed walking.","\"Go back and tell Liu Hong to think carefully about whether his official duties are to Shu State or to Jing State.\"","Just as Liu Wen was about to speak, two more words drifted over:","\"Get out.\"","\"...\"","Two simple, flat words, yet they struck like a clap of thunder.","Liu Wen, his head still bowed, shot his eyes wide open, his expression shifting erratically.","This time, he had clearly and truly lost his composure.","Liu Zhaoxue, standing beside him, knew that when news of this outcome reached the Liu Family, it would undoubtedly displease their elders.","But she also knew this was not the right time for her to speak.","A person in the grip of anger won’t listen to reason.","Especially when the angered person was none other than the current Duke Dingyuan of the Great Wei Dynasty.","A man who had spent his life at war was not one to be swayed by mere words.","Seeing that things had come to this, Liu Zhaoxue could only step forward and say softly, \"Second Brother, let’s discuss this back home.\"","Liu Wen snapped back to his senses at the sound of her voice. With a slight shift, he lifted his head, his expression having already returned to a state of calm.","He said nothing more, simply turning and striding out.","The others followed close behind.","CREAK.","The moment the door opened, Chen Yi and Xiao Wuge glanced over.","They saw Liu Wen, Liu Zhaoxue, and their entourage file out with unreadable expressions, so they couldn’t tell what had happened.","But when the group reached the courtyard, Liu Wen’s gaze fell upon them.","The look in his narrow eyes instantly turned sinister, and he seemed to squeeze the words from between his teeth.","\"Liu Wen greets the Young Master, and... this fine gentleman here!\"","Chen Yi arched an eyebrow. He had a good idea of how their visit went, and a smile couldn’t help but touch his lips.","\"Chen Yi.\"","\"Chen Yi... We’ll be seeing each other again very soon.\"","After saying this, Liu Wen shot him one last, deep look before leading his group out of Qingjing Residence.","Liu Zhaoxue hesitated for a moment, but this time she didn’t offer an apologetic bow as she had before, simply following the others out.","Once Qingjing Residence was quiet again, Xiao Wuge’s brows were tightly furrowed. Young as he was, he could tell something was wrong with Liu Wen’s expression just now.","\"Brother-in-law, see? I told you he was a bad guy.\"","\"He just glared at me. His face was so scary.\"","\"And a guy like that wants to be my brother-in-law? He can forget about it.\"","Chen Yi smiled, nodded, and patted the boy’s head.","He didn’t know the details of the Old Marquis’s discussion with the Liu Family, but given the result, the process no longer mattered.","Just then, two lines of text appeared before his eyes:","[Opportunity +4.]","[Evaluation: The people were here, yet you did not hear their words or witness the scene. To let a heaven-sent Opportunity pass you by is the mark of a truly lazy individual.]","Chen Yi glanced at the text and put it out of his mind, then led Xiao Wuge into the main hall.","Just then, the Old Marquis, having heard their voices, emerged from the side chamber with a smile.","\"Wuge, Qingzhou, you’re here. Have a seat.\"","Xiao Wuge chirped a response and ran over with a smile to help him sit down, all the while recounting what he’d just witnessed—which mostly consisted of bad-mouthing Liu Wen.","The Old Marquis naturally placated him with a few words but said nothing about Liu Wen himself.","Chen Yi followed suit and sat down, remaining silent as he placed the brocade box in his hand beside the Old Marquis.","\"What’s this?\"","\"Just something I created in my leisure time. I hope you won’t mind it.\"","The Old Marquis shook his head and praised him with a laugh. \"Two days ago, when Sun Fu came to me clutching that piece of calligraphy like it was his most precious treasure, I had the chance to witness your Calligraphy Dao, Qingzhou.\"","\"Now that your Calligraphy Dao has reached the Realm of Perfection, even a few words casually written by you would have people outside fighting tooth and nail for them.\"","As he spoke, he opened the brocade box, took out the scroll inside, and slowly unfurled it.","Instantly, a hazy glow emanated from the Yunsong Paper.","The same Mental Realm Chen Yi had revealed while writing it now unfolded completely before the Old Marquis’s eyes.","\"Serenity... reaching far...\"","As the Old Marquis looked at the words on the scroll and the tranquil, distant scene they conjured, the displeasure in his heart from the Liu Family’s visit began to dissipate.","Beside him, Xiao Wuge couldn’t discern the different Realms of the Calligraphy Dao, but he too was influenced by the Mental Realm in the artwork. His pout softened, and a small smile appeared on his face.","\"Brother-in-law’s writing is the best.\"","Hearing this, the Old Marquis nodded instinctively, his eyes fixed on the scroll in admiration. \"It truly is fine work.\"","\"Even I, who am no great enthusiast of the Calligraphy Dao, can feel its influence. It’s clear that your skill, Qingzhou, has truly reached the Realm of Perfection.\"","Chen Yi simply smiled and said, \"You praise me too highly.\"","Just as he was about to say something else, the Old Marquis looked up at him, his expression growing uncharacteristically serious.","\"Speaking of which, Qingzhou, you are a man of letters. There is a matter I do not understand, and I was hoping you might enlighten me.\"","Chen Yi paused, slightly taken aback. \"Please, Old Marquis, feel free to ask.\"","\"Tell me, what is your assessment of the current situation in Shu State?\"","\"In what respect, sir?\"","\"Say whatever comes to mind.\""]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200 - 182: That Would Be Utterly Shameless","paragraphs":["’Was this a test?’","’Or did he have some other motive?’","Chen Yi had no way of knowing.","But seeing the Old Marquis’s serious expression, he knew he had to respond with proper decorum.","’It’s just... Shu State’s current situation is a mess.’","’To call it a tangled mess would be an understatement.’","On the surface, the Xiao Family reigned supreme. They held significant military power, and the other Noble Families and Clans, along with all of Shu State’s officials, major and minor, followed their lead.","’But behind the scenes?’","’With the deaths of Xiao Fengchun and the others, the core strength of the Xiao Family has been fractured. This has led some of Shu State’s Noble Families and officials to constantly obstruct and test them.’","’Furthermore, some who fancy themselves powerful and influential have either developed rebellious notions or are simply looking to gain more benefits for themselves.’","’Some even harbor the idea of \"taking their place.\"’","Yet under these circumstances, there were still people fanning the flames from the shadows.","Such as the Hidden Guard and the Jing State Liu Family.","Chen Yi understood Shu State’s situation clearly, but he couldn’t reveal everything he knew.","For one, it would be difficult for him to explain the source of his information.","Secondly, he worried that saying too much would inevitably arouse the Xiao Family’s Old Marquis’s suspicion, which would do more harm than good.","With this in mind, Chen Yi carefully chose his words. \"Things seem to be somewhat turbulent.\"","Such an answer clearly did not satisfy the Old Marquis. \"And what makes you say Shu State is turbulent?\"","It wasn’t just a scholar accomplished in the Calligraphy Dao like Chen Yi; any student of current affairs could have said as much.","But this was not the answer the Old Marquis wanted to hear.","Or rather, he wanted to hear some unconventional insights.","Chen Yi glanced at him and replied with a smile, \"By looking at the small, one can see the great.\"","\"Some time ago, there were several murders in the Prefecture City, and medicinal herbs from the Xiao Family Medicine Hall were stolen. I heard it was the work of the Illusory Sound Sect and other Evil Demons.\"","\"I believe such incidents should be rare, especially in and around the Shu State Prefecture City.\"","\"If this were Jiangnan Prefecture—not even mentioning Jinling, but just in places like Suzhou and Hangzhou—those Evil Demons wouldn’t dare show their faces within the city walls.\"","He couldn’t reveal the secrets he had discovered, so he could only make logical deductions from the known facts.","But the Old Marquis was still not satisfied. \"These are just isolated incidents. They don’t prove that Shu State is turbulent.\"","This time, however, Chen Yi smiled and shook his head. \"It is often said, ’When a nation is about to perish, monsters will appear.’ The same applies to Shu State.\"","\"If Shu State were truly at peace, I imagine the likes of the Illusory Sound Sect wouldn’t dare appear in or around the Prefecture City, let alone cause trouble. Wouldn’t you agree?\"","The Old Marquis’s expression flickered. He instantly understood the meaning of \"looking at the small to see the great\" that Chen Yi had mentioned earlier.","At the same time, he recalled the state of Shu State when Xiao Fengchun and the others were still alive.","Comparing the before and after, it was not difficult to see—five or ten years ago, Evil Demons had never caused trouble in Shu State, at least not in or around the Prefecture City.","It was mostly in the Wumeng Mountain or upper Chishui River areas.","And it was mostly Jianghu conflicts between the Mountain Race and the Evil Demonic Dao.","\"And what do you believe is the reason for these incidents, Qingzhou?\"","Hearing this, a peculiar expression flashed across Chen Yi’s face. ’The Old Marquis is asking a question he already knows the answer to.’","’But I obviously can’t point to the Xiao Family as the cause.’","After a moment’s thought, he replied, \"Many factors.\"","\"For example, after the war with the Barbarian Race, Shu State is weakened internally. The army, the City Guard, the Imprisonment Department, and even the common people need time to rest and recuperate.\"","\"Then there are outsiders stirring up trouble.\"","\"The Poshisu Country, the Barbarian Race, or the sea bandits from the Southeast Coastal Region—they all want to see chaos erupt so they can reap the benefits.\"","\"But I believe it’s only temporary. Once Shu State returns to its former glory, these petty criminals will certainly have nowhere to hide.\"","A smile appeared on the Old Marquis’s face. \"And what if I don’t want to wait?\"","\"Qingzhou, what do you think should be done to pacify Shu State?\"","Chen Yi answered without hesitation, \"Kill one to warn a hundred.\"","\"Kill one to warn a hundred, kill one to warn a hundred... Heh heh.\"","Although the Old Marquis was somewhat disappointed, feeling that Chen Yi’s words were too broad, he considered it a passing answer.","According to his own judgment, the situation in Shu State indeed showed signs of impending chaos.","It wasn’t just the meddling of the Evil Demonic Dao; many Noble Families and court officials were making moves behind the scenes, to varying degrees.","Even from outside Shu State, ill winds were blowing.","The Imperial Court, Jing State, and even places like Guangyue Prefecture and Jiao State, where Duke Qian’s Zhang Family resides, had seen developments unfavorable to Shu State and the Xiao Family.","Not to mention the restless Poshisu Country and the Barbarian Race.","Under these circumstances, if the Old Marquis wanted to \"kill one to warn a hundred\"...","...the choice of target required careful consideration.","A Noble Family like the Jing State Liu Family was a possibility.","But the commotion would be too great, inevitably attracting the attention of the Imperial Court and various other powers, and the matter would likely end unresolved.","If the target were too small, the effect would be greatly diminished.","That was why the Old Marquis held his trump card but had yet to find a suitable opportunity to play it.","After a momentary daze, he glanced at the calligraphy in his hand that read \"Tranquility Yields Foresight\" and said:","\"Qingzhou, it’s not too late for you to have lunch here before you go back. And Wuge, you as well, of course.\"","Chen Yi had no objections.","Neither did Xiao Wuge.","But the two were in different moods.","Chen Yi let out a sigh of relief; he had managed to muddle his way through the Old Marquis’s test after all.","’But it seems I won’t be able to follow Sun Fu’s advice. I should probably visit Qingjing Residence less often in the future.’","’And then there was what the Old Marquis told Xiao Wan’er earlier—about having someone investigate Chen Yu, the owner of Hundred Herbs Hall.’","’From now on, I’ll have to be more cautious and keep a low profile.’","With laughter and conversation, the meal was quite harmonious.","But for some reason, Chen Yi couldn’t shake the feeling that many of the Old Marquis’s words during the meal held hidden meanings.","\"When Jinghong returns, I’ll welcome her back with you.\"","\"Qingzhou was born at the end of the first year of the Anhe era. You’re not getting any younger.\"","\"Whether you go to Guiyun Academy or not is up to you. That old bastard Yue Ming is up to no good. Just look at the commotion in the prefecture now.\"","\"You might as well spend more time in Spring Lotus Garden, especially at night.\"","\"And also...\"","Words like these left Chen Yi unable to grasp his true meaning.","’Is he telling me to go to the academy less to avoid causing trouble for the family?’","’But why did he differentiate between day and night?’","In the end, he could only assume the Old Marquis was old and just saying whatever came to mind.","’It couldn’t possibly be him urging me and Xiao Jinghong to consummate our marriage, could it?’","’That would be far too shameless for an old man.’","...","「As evening approached.」","Over the just-cleared skies of Shu State, dark clouds gathered once more.","The puddles that had been baked by the sun for most of the day evaporated, and the rising water vapor instantly turned into a blanket of heat, making it incredibly muggy both inside and outside the Prefecture City.","Even the occasional breeze was laden with moisture and scorching heat, causing those walking through the city to sweat endlessly.","Even in Yanhua Lane in the South City, dotted with dense vegetation, the patrons and the girls were much the same.","Especially the women who took the stage to perform.","Whether it was the Cultured Courtesans who played instruments and sang, or the scantily-clad girls who twirled and leaped in their dances, sweat beaded on all their foreheads.","After finishing a performance, they would have to drink a bottle of Mushroom Tea to cool down.","In just half a day, a single Qin Building would go through a cartload of Mushroom Tea.","The Madams didn’t find it a painful expense.","Although Mushroom Tea was expensive, compared to the Divine Bull Tea and Wangji Tea they sold, this small loss was just a drop in the bucket.","You see, while the girls drank one cartload of Mushroom Tea, the patrons would drink two or three cartloads of Divine Bull Tea.","Silver coins flowed like water over the counters of the Qin Buildings, and after being counted, were hauled away to the Xiao Family’s World Relief Medicine Hall or to Hundred Herbs Hall.","After all, over this period, these tea drinks had become all the rage in Yanhua Lane.","These Qin Buildings were clearly very familiar with the whole process.","If it was like this for the other Qin Buildings, it went without saying for Spring Rain Building, which had the most booming business and the most top-ranking women in all of Yanhua Lane.","Night had not yet fallen, but the place was already bustling with people.","Patrons came and went in an endless stream.","Some were led to seats in the main hall by the Pimps and Madams in charge of greeting, while others were taken by the maids of Cultured Courtesans they knew to private rooms in the back, or to even more luxurious and expensive courtyards.","The top floor of the Qin Building, facing the street, was a stark contrast to the lively scene below.","Most of those coming and going within were tall Jianghu People, each one either masked or wearing a bamboo hat, moving without a single sound.","Even the clamor from below did not reach this place; it was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Coupled with the tightly shut doors and windows on all sides, the place was dim and silent even during the day, illuminated only by scattered lamps and lanterns.","The dim yellow halos of light bordered one another, like guards on duty, each protecting its own territory.","This caused the light and shadows to flicker and shift in the top-floor corridor.","And in a quiet room deep within the corridor, Black Tooth sat upright at a low table, a paper slip unfolded in his hand.","By the light of the oil lamp on the table, he read it carefully three times before putting the slip away and speaking:","\"So, the visitors from the Jing State Liu Family did indeed want a marriage alliance with the Xiao Family, but the Old Marquis rejected them?\"","Sitting opposite him was none other than Lou Yuxue, wearing a white jade mask.","She nodded slightly, her tone no longer the flirtatious, soft whisper from before, but much calmer and colder.","\"That is correct.\"","\"According to the spy hidden in the Xiao Family, Liu Yu from the Liu Family’s second branch first paid a visit and brought up the marriage alliance with the Old Marquis face-to-face.\"","\"Afterward... which is to say, at noon today, Liu Wen and Liu Zhaoxue went together to the Xiao Family to visit the Old Marquis. They must have gone for the same reason.\"","The eyes of Black Tooth, hidden behind his iron mask, twitched. \"And the result?\"","Lou Yuxue let out a light laugh. \"I heard that when Liu Wen left, his face was ashen.\"","\"Before he had even left the Xiao Family estate, he cursed more than once—sometimes at Liu Zhaoxue, and other times indirectly at the Xiao Family.\"","Black Tooth chuckled. \"In that case, the Medical Saint Hand from the night before last is indeed from the Liu Family.\"","Hearing this, Lou Yuxue shook her head. \"We can’t be certain yet.\"","After a pause, she continued, \"At the very least, we must rule out the possibility that he’s from the Xiao Family.\"","\"After all, the stakes of this venture are enormous. If he’s a spy sent by the Xiao Family, then forget about those few from the Evil Demonic Dao—even you and I would be in danger.\"","Black Tooth said dismissively, \"Even if the Xiao Family doesn’t know now, they’ll know it was us after the event.\"","\"At that time, you and I will both have to go into hiding to avoid being killed by the Xiao Family in their fury.\"","Just as Lou Yuxue was about to agree, she heard Black Tooth continue, \"However, your concern does have some merit.\"","\"It would be good to be absolutely sure about that Medical Saint Hand’s background.\"","Lou Yuxue glanced at him. \"Since you agree, I’ll send someone to probe Liu Wen tonight.\"","\"Probing the Liu Family is no problem, but I want to know when you plan to make your move.\"","\"Once I confirm Liu Wu’s identity, I will begin my preparations.\"","\"Good. I will fully cooperate with your actions on this matter. I hope you won’t disappoint me.\"","Seeing Black Tooth looking straight at her, Lou Yuxue laughed. \"As it should be.\"","\"However, I’m afraid my spies will all be lost after this. I’ll have to trouble you with the matter of silver coins.\"","\"Say no more. I’ll go get the silver tomorrow night.\"","As Black Tooth spoke, he glanced to the side and, with a slight exertion of force, crushed the paper in his hand to dust.","\"In any case, I won’t break the rules of Bright Moon Building.\""]}]);
